"//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\"},{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"pub static GAMES: &[Entry] =\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"/// One line of [`GAMES`]: made with [`entry`].\"},{\"line_number\":95,\"content\":\"/// A [`GAMES`] line for the game type `G`.\"},{\"line_number\":120,\"content\":\"    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.key == key)\"},{\"line_number\":185,\"content\":\"            let known: Vec<&str> = GAMES.iter().map(|g| g.key).collect();\"},{\"line_number\":244,\"content\":\"    /// The running game from [`GAMES`], if this scene is one.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/pavilion-lite/src/games/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"//! The game registry: add your game's module and one line to `GAMES`.\"},{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"pub static GAMES: &[GameDef] = &[\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.name == name).expect(\\\"registered game\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"        for g in GAMES {\"},{\"line_number\":76,\"content\":\"        for g in GAMES {\"},{\"line_number\":114,\"content\":\"        let mut s = Session::new(GAMES);\"},{\"line_number\":116,\"content\":\"        assert_eq!(call(&mut s, \\\"games\\\").as_array().unwrap().len(), GAMES.len());\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/pavilion-lite/src/games/template.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2,\"content\":\"//! to start a new game (then add it to `GAMES` in `mod.rs`).\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/pavilion-lite/src/main.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"    pavlite::tools::main(games::GAMES);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/pavilion-lite/src/character.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":174,\"content\":\"    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/scenes.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"/// The scenes a menu offers: the built-in ones, then the games (`crate::games::GAMES`).\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"    SCENES.iter().copied().chain(crate::games::GAMES.iter().map(|g| (g.key, g.about))).collect()\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"    v.extend(crate::games::GAMES.iter().map(|g| g.key.to_string()));\"},{\"line_number\":155,\"content\":\"                    crate::games::GAMES.iter().map(|g| g.key).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\\\", \\\"),\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"pub struct InputFrame {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"use pav_core::games::{GAMES, Outcome};\"},{\"line_number\":65,\"content\":\"    for g in GAMES {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/lib.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"pub mod games;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2609ef02-ad42-4478-bb30-ae445df66125"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_10","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I am identifying the minimum integration points for this large engine.\n\nSix integration points are now mapped: game registration, MercSim wrapper, camera, web page, audio, and UI. The next step is to read the engine source files to understand how games tick, scenes build, and audio feeds in.\n\nDeep engine changes to camera, input, terrain, and vehicles are too risky. A lighter architecture is better: a custom deterministic sim lives inside the Game struct, updated via post each tick. Rendering spawns visual entities for nearby things. The default third-person camera conflicts with the required first-person view and eye-height tests.\n\nThe first-person look and movement are validated by native simulation tests, not by inspecting the browser camera matrix. This means the engine can keep its third-person chase camera while the custom sim handles player stance, yaw, and pitch internally.\n\nThe browser test specifically checks that pointer-lock mousemove changes yaw, so the published status yaw must update. A first-person camera is still required for a realistic launch screenshot. I will read camera.rs to gauge the difficulty of this change. The scene should be minimal: a room with terrain, sky color, and a weapon in view.\n\nI will read camera, input, starter build, web index, and fog flags in chunks before writing code. The visual scene will be a minimal level TOML with ground and a player marker. The MercSim will run the real 2048 world. The visual layer will sync only the player's local area.\n\nRendering the full 2048-meter map at one-meter resolution would require four million vertices and likely exhaust memory. A large flat ground mesh with vertex-colored biomes is the safer fallback. It uses only about four thousand vertices and still conveys the map layout.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff6163db-cd3f-427b-baa3-2238b5be975a-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/mod.rs","limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff6163db-cd3f-427b-baa3-2238b5be975a-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs","limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff6163db-cd3f-427b-baa3-2238b5be975a-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs","limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff6163db-cd3f-427b-baa3-2238b5be975a-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/starter.rs","limit":150}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9054,"output_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":66560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"37e68ea0-c29e-4b0c-9e27-95c836f978fd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ff6163db-cd3f-427b-baa3-2238b5be975a-14","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\n10→use std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n20→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod starter;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] =\\n    &[entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build)];\\n\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n30→#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n    Won,\\n    Lost,\\n}\\n\\n/// A game's rules. Every method has a default, so a game implements only what it uses.\\n///\\n40→/// The engine calls `pre` and `post` once per tick (60 a second) from `Sim::step`; everything\\n/// else is read-only. While `pre` or `post` runs, the game is out of `sim.state.play`, so use\\n/// `self` for the game's own state and `sim` for the world.\\npub trait Game: Clone + Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send + Sync + 'static {\\n    /// The scene key that starts the game: `load scene=<KEY>`, `--scene <KEY>`, `?scene=<KEY>`.\\n    const KEY: &'static str;\\n\\n    /// Before characters move: read the player's input and decide what the characters the\\n    /// game drives do this tick. A returned input replaces that character's own (its `ai`\\n    /// brain, or the player's keys for the player).\\n50→    fn pre(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _sim: &mut Sim,\\n        _input: &InputFrame,\\n        _dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        BTreeMap::new()\\n    }\\n\\n60→    /// After physics: the rules (pickups, damage, score, win and loss). Push `SimEvent`s for\\n    /// sounds and effects (`Coin`, `Pickup`, `Hit`, `Explosion`...).\\n    fn post(&mut self, _sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {}\\n\\n    /// HUD lines: drawn at the top left of the window, returned by the `play` tool.\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        Vec::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game's state for tools and tests (`play`), as JSON.\\n70→    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::Value::Null\\n    }\\n\\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        Outcome::Playing\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The input a good player would give this tick. `play bot=true` and the tests drive the\\n    /// player with it; teach it every new rule, and keep a test that it wins.\\n80→    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        InputFrame::default()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// One line of [`GAMES`]: made with [`entry`].\\npub struct Entry {\\n    pub key: &'static str,\\n    pub about: &'static str,\\n    /// Builds the scene and sets `sim.state.play`. The `&str` is the rest of the scene name\\n90→    /// after `<key>/` (a level number, say), if any.\\n    pub build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>,\\n    load: fn(ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String>,\\n}\\n\\n/// A [`GAMES`] line for the game type `G`.\\npub const fn entry<G: Game>(about: &'static str, build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>) -> Entry {\\n    Entry { key: G::KEY, about, build, load: load_as::<G> }\\n}\\n\\n100→fn load_as<G: Game>(v: ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String> {\\n    v.deserialized::<G>().map(GameBox::new).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\\n}\\n\\n/// A game's level text: `crates/pav_core/src/games/<key>.toml` read from disk when the program\\n/// runs from the repository's root (`pav`, `cargo run`), so an edit shows at the next `load`\\n/// with no rebuild; else `built_in`, the copy embedded with `include_str!` (tests, the browser,\\n/// a shipped executable).\\npub fn level_text(key: &str, built_in: &'static str) -> std::borrow::Cow<'static, str> {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n110→    if let Ok(text) = std::fs::read_to_string(format!(\\\"crates/pav_core/src/games/{key}.toml\\\")) {\\n        return text.into();\\n    }\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let _ = key; // the browser has no files\\n    built_in.into()\\n}\\n\\n/// The game registered under `key`.\\npub fn find(key: &str) -> Option<&'static Entry> {\\n120→    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.key == key)\\n}\\n\\n/// A running game in `SimState::play`: clones (rewind, snapshots) and serializes (snapshot\\n/// files, the state hash) through the game's own derives.\\npub struct GameBox(Box<dyn DynGame>);\\n\\nimpl GameBox {\\n    pub fn new<G: Game>(game: G) -> Self {\\n        Self(Box::new(game))\\n130→    }\\n\\n    pub fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        self.0.key()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game as its own type (None for another game).\\n    pub fn get<G: Game>(&self) -> Option<&G> {\\n        self.0.as_any().downcast_ref()\\n    }\\n140→\\n    pub fn get_mut<G: Game>(&mut self) -> Option<&mut G> {\\n        self.0.as_any_mut().downcast_mut()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn hud(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        self.0.hud(sim)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn status(&self, sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n150→        self.0.status(sim)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        self.0.outcome()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn bot(&self, sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        self.0.bot(sim)\\n    }\\n160→}\\n\\nimpl Clone for GameBox {\\n    fn clone(&self) -> Self {\\n        Self(self.0.clone_box())\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]\\nstruct Saved {\\n170→    key: String,\\n    state: ciborium::Value,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Serialize for GameBox {\\n    fn serialize<S: Serializer>(&self, s: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error> {\\n        let state = self.0.save().map_err(serde::ser::Error::custom)?;\\n        Saved { key: self.key().to_string(), state }.serialize(s)\\n    }\\n}\\n180→\\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for GameBox {\\n    fn deserialize<D: Deserializer<'de>>(d: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error> {\\n        let saved = Saved::deserialize(d)?;\\n        let Some(entry) = find(&saved.key) else {\\n            let known: Vec<&str> = GAMES.iter().map(|g| g.key).collect();\\n            return Err(D::Error::custom(format!(\\\"unknown game '{}' (known: {})\\\", saved.key, known.join(\\\", \\\"))));\\n        };\\n        (entry.load)(saved.state).map_err(D::Error::custom)\\n    }\\n190→}\\n\\n/// [`Game`] as an object (the trait itself isn't one: `Clone` and serde).\\ntrait DynGame: Send + Sync {\\n    fn key(&self) -> &'static str;\\n    fn clone_box(&self) -> Box<dyn DynGame>;\\n    fn save(&self) -> Result<ciborium::Value, String>;\\n    fn pre(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame>;\\n    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>);\\n    fn hud(&self, sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String>;\\n200→    fn status(&self, sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value;\\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome;\\n    fn bot(&self, sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame;\\n    fn as_any(&self) -> &dyn Any;\\n    fn as_any_mut(&mut self) -> &mut dyn Any;\\n}\\n\\nimpl<G: Game> DynGame for G {\\n    fn key(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        G::KEY\\n210→    }\\n    fn clone_box(&self) -> Box<dyn DynGame> {\\n        Box::new(self.clone())\\n    }\\n    fn save(&self) -> Result<ciborium::Value, String> {\\n        ciborium::Value::serialized(self).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\\n    }\\n    fn pre(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        Game::pre(self, sim, input, dt, events)\\n    }\\n220→    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Games built on the engine: the hook a new game implements, and the list of games.\\n//!\\n//! A game is a struct holding its rules' state (`Clone` and serde, like everything in\\n//! `SimState`) that implements [`Game`], plus a `build` function that makes its scene. One\\n//! line in [`GAMES`] and `load scene=<key>` starts it in the tools, the window\\n//! (`shardfall --scene <key>`) and the browser (`?scene=<key>`). `starter.rs` is the template\\n//! to copy; `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` is the guide. Shardfall (`crate::arpg`) predates this hook and\\n//! keeps its own.\\n\\n10→use std::any::Any;\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\nuse serde::de::{DeserializeOwned, Error as _};\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Deserializer, Serialize, Serializer};\\n\\nuse crate::entity::EntityId;\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n20→use crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub mod starter;\\n\\n/// Every game the engine knows. `load scene=<key>` (or `<key>/<rest>`) builds it.\\npub static GAMES: &[Entry] =\\n    &[entry::<starter::Starter>(\\\"Starter: collect every shard while slimes chase you (the template to copy).\\\", starter::build)];\\n\\n/// Still playing, won or lost.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n30→#[serde(rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Outcome {\\n    #[default]\\n    Playing,\\n    Won,\\n    Lost,\\n}\\n\\n/// A game's rules. Every method has a default, so a game implements only what it uses.\\n///\\n40→/// The engine calls `pre` and `post` once per tick (60 a second) from `Sim::step`; everything\\n/// else is read-only. While `pre` or `post` runs, the game is out of `sim.state.play`, so use\\n/// `self` for the game's own state and `sim` for the world.\\npub trait Game: Clone + Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send + Sync + 'static {\\n    /// The scene key that starts the game: `load scene=<KEY>`, `--scene <KEY>`, `?scene=<KEY>`.\\n    const KEY: &'static str;\\n\\n    /// Before characters move: read the player's input and decide what the characters the\\n    /// game drives do this tick. A returned input replaces that character's own (its `ai`\\n    /// brain, or the player's keys for the player).\\n50→    fn pre(\\n        &mut self,\\n        _sim: &mut Sim,\\n        _input: &InputFrame,\\n        _dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        BTreeMap::new()\\n    }\\n\\n60→    /// After physics: the rules (pickups, damage, score, win and loss). Push `SimEvent`s for\\n    /// sounds and effects (`Coin`, `Pickup`, `Hit`, `Explosion`...).\\n    fn post(&mut self, _sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {}\\n\\n    /// HUD lines: drawn at the top left of the window, returned by the `play` tool.\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        Vec::new()\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The game's state for tools and tests (`play`), as JSON.\\n70→    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        serde_json::Value::Null\\n    }\\n\\n    fn outcome(&self) -> Outcome {\\n        Outcome::Playing\\n    }\\n\\n    /// The input a good player would give this tick. `play bot=true` and the tests drive the\\n    /// player with it; teach it every new rule, and keep a test that it wins.\\n80→    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        InputFrame::default()\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// One line of [`GAMES`]: made with [`entry`].\\npub struct Entry {\\n    pub key: &'static str,\\n    pub about: &'static str,\\n    /// Builds the scene and sets `sim.state.play`. The `&str` is the rest of the scene name\\n90→    /// after `<key>/` (a level number, say), if any.\\n    pub build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>,\\n    load: fn(ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String>,\\n}\\n\\n/// A [`GAMES`] line for the game type `G`.\\npub const fn entry<G: Game>(about: &'static str, build: fn(&mut Sim, Option<&str>) -> Result<()>) -> Entry {\\n    Entry { key: G::KEY, about, build, load: load_as::<G> }\\n}\\n\\n100→fn load_as<G: Game>(v: ciborium::Value) -> Result<GameBox, String> {\\n    v.deserialized::<G>().map(GameBox::new).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\\n}\\n\\n/// A game's level text: `crates/pav_core/src/games/<key>.toml` read from disk when the program\\n/// runs from the repository's root (`pav`, `cargo run`), so an edit shows at the next `load`\\n/// with no rebuild; else `built_in`, the copy embedded with `include_str!` (tests, the browser,\\n/// a shipped executable).\\npub fn level_text(key: &str, built_in: &'static str) -> std::borrow::Cow<'static, str> {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n110→    if let Ok(text) = std::fs::read_to_string(format!(\\\"crates/pav_core/src/games/{key}.toml\\\")) {\\n        return text.into();\\n    }\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let _ = key; // the browser has no files\\n    built_in.into()\\n}\\n\\n/// The game registered under `key`.\\npub fn find(key: &str) -> Option<&'static Entry> {\\n120→    GAMES.iter().find(|g| g.key == key)\\n}\\n\\n/// A running game in `SimState::play`: clones (rewind, snapshots) and serializes (snapshot\\n/// files, the state hash) through the game's own derives.\\npub struct GameBox(Box<dyn DynGame>);\\n\\nimpl GameBox {\\n    pub fn new<G: Game>(g