5,\"content\":\"           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\"},{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"BINDGEN_DIR is wasm-bindgen's output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm); scripts/build-web.sh\"},{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"its <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"loader that sets window.loadGame (index.html's script calls it when set) and the JS glue as an\"},{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"inline module script. The loader shows a progress line, bakes in --scene (used when the address\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"names no room or scene) and unpacks with the browser's DecompressionStream. No blob: or data:\"},{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"URLs are needed. Out: target/web/<title>.html.\"},{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"# Runs while the page parses, before index.html's module script.\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"  // The start scene baked in at build time, unless the address names a room or a scene.\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"  const scene = __SCENE__, query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"  if (scene && !query.get('room') && !query.get('scene')) {\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"    query.set('scene', scene);\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"    catch (error) { console.warn('Could not put the start scene in the address:', error); }\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"  msg.replaceChildren(`Loading ${document.title}…`, line);\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"  // The JS glue is the module script at the end of the page: it hands over its init function.\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"        fail(f\\\"expected one {what} in {PAGE.relative_to(ROOT)}, found {n}: update this script\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":91,\"content\":\"    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\")[0])\"},{\"line_number\":93,\"content\":\"    ap.add_argument(\\\"--title\\\", help=\\\"<title> (default: index.html's)\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":94,\"content\":\"    ap.add_argument(\\\"--description\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":96,\"content\":\"    ap.add_argument(\\\"--scene\\\", help=\\\"start scene when the address names no room or scene (default: the game's)\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":97,\"content\":\"    ap.add_argument(\\\"--out\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"output file (default: target/web/<title>.html)\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":104,\"content\":\"    # The glue goes in the page as an inline module script, so it can't import other files\"},{\"line_number\":105,\"content\":\"    # (wasm-bindgen snippets) or hold text that would end the script element early.\"},{\"line_number\":109,\"content\":\"    if re.search(r\\\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\\\", glue):\"},{\"line_number\":110,\"content\":\"        fail(\\\"the JS glue contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":116,\"content\":\"    if a.title is not None:\"},{\"line_number\":117,\"content\":\"        page = replace_one(page, r\\\"<title>[^<]*</title>\\\", lambda m: f\\\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\\\", \\\"<title>\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":118,\"content\":\"    for name, value in ((\\\"description\\\", a.description), (\\\"theme-color\\\", a.theme_color)):\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"    # JSON is valid JS; escaping \\\"<\\\" keeps a scene name from closing the script element.\"},{\"line_number\":132,\"content\":\"    loader = LOADER.replace(\\\"__SCENE__\\\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\"))\"},{\"line_number\":134,\"content\":\"        f'<script id=\\\"game-wasm\\\" type=\\\"application/octet-stream\\\" data-size=\\\"{len(wasm)}\\\">'\"},{\"line_number\":135,\"content\":\"        f\\\"{base64.b64encode(packed).decode()}</script>\\\\n\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":136,\"content\":\"        f\\\"<script>{loader}</script>\\\\n\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":137,\"content\":\"        f'<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n{glue}\\\\nwindow.gameGlue({init[1]});\\\\n</script>\\\\n'\"},{\"line_number\":141,\"content\":\"    title = a.title if a.title is not None else html.unescape(re.search(r\\\"<title>([^<]*)</title>\\\", page)[1])\"},{\"line_number\":142,\"content\":\"    out = a.out or ROOT / \\\"target\\\" / \\\"web\\\" / f\\\"{re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-') or 'game'}.html\\\"\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3dfc21a1-5acd-4628-98f8-21a7b6b281a8-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Boot diagnostics and logging. Every startup stage is numbered and timed, and goes to the\\n//! terminal, the log file and the on-screen overlay. The logger also keeps recent lines for\\n//! the in-game console.\\n\\nuse std::collections::VecDeque;\\nuse std::fs::File;\\nuse std::io::Write;\\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\\nuse std::sync::{Mutex, OnceLock};\\n10→\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub enum StageStatus {\\n    Ok,\\n    Failed(String),\\n}\\n20→\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct Stage {\\n    pub num: u32,\\n    pub name: String,\\n    pub detail: String,\\n    pub ms: f64,\\n    pub status: StageStatus,\\n}\\n\\n30→pub struct Diagnostics {\\n    pub start: Instant,\\n    pub log_path: PathBuf,\\n    file: Mutex<Option<File>>,\\n    pub stages: Mutex<Vec<Stage>>,\\n    pub recent: Mutex<VecDeque<(log::Level, String)>>,\\n    level: log::LevelFilter,\\n}\\n\\nstatic DIAG: OnceLock<Diagnostics> = OnceLock::new();\\n40→\\npub fn diag() -> &'static Diagnostics {\\n    DIAG.get().expect(\\\"diagnostics not initialised\\\")\\n}\\n\\n/// Directory next to the executable (falls back to the working directory).\\npub fn exe_dir() -> PathBuf {\\n    std::env::current_exe().ok().and_then(|p| p.parent().map(|d| d.to_path_buf())).unwrap_or_else(|| PathBuf::from(\\\".\\\"))\\n}\\n\\n50→/// Sets up the log file (next to the executable, else the temp dir) and the logger.\\npub fn init() -> &'static Diagnostics {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    let (log_path, file) = {\\n        let mut log_path = exe_dir().join(\\\"shardfall.log\\\");\\n        let file = File::create(&log_path).ok().or_else(|| {\\n            log_path = std::env::temp_dir().join(\\\"shardfall.log\\\");\\n            File::create(&log_path).ok()\\n        });\\n        (log_path, file)\\n60→    };\\n    // In the browser the log goes to the developer console.\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let (log_path, file) = (PathBuf::from(\\\"the browser console\\\"), None::<File>);\\n    let level = match std::env::var(\\\"PAV_LOG\\\").ok().as_deref() {\\n        Some(\\\"trace\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Trace,\\n        Some(\\\"debug\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Debug,\\n        Some(\\\"warn\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Warn,\\n        _ => log::LevelFilter::Info,\\n    };\\n70→    let d = DIAG.get_or_init(|| Diagnostics {\\n        start: Instant::now(),\\n        log_path,\\n        file: Mutex::new(file),\\n        stages: Mutex::new(Vec::new()),\\n        recent: Mutex::new(VecDeque::new()),\\n        level,\\n    });\\n    let _ = log::set_logger(&Logger);\\n    log::set_max_level(log::LevelFilter::Trace);\\n80→    d\\n}\\n\\nstruct Logger;\\n\\nimpl log::Log for Logger {\\n    fn enabled(&self, m: &log::Metadata) -> bool {\\n        let d = diag();\\n        let t = m.target();\\n        // Keep graphics-driver chatter out unless it is a warning.\\n90→        if t.starts_with(\\\"wgpu\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"naga\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"egui\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"winit\\\") {\\n            return m.level() <= log::Level::Warn;\\n        }\\n        m.level() <= d.level\\n    }\\n\\n    fn log(&self, r: &log::Record) {\\n        if !self.enabled(r.metadata()) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n100→        let d = diag();\\n        let line = format!(\\\"[{:>8.3}s] {:<5} {}\\\", d.start.elapsed().as_secs_f64(), r.level(), r.args());\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        eprintln!(\\\"{line}\\\");\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        {\\n            let js = wasm_bindgen::JsValue::from_str(&line);\\n            match r.level() {\\n                log::Level::Error => web_sys::console::error_1(&js),\\n                log::Level::Warn => web_sys::console::warn_1(&js),\\n110→                _ => web_sys::console::log_1(&js),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Ok(mut f) = d.file.lock() {\\n            if let Some(f) = f.as_mut() {\\n                let _ = writeln!(f, \\\"{line}\\\");\\n                let _ = f.flush();\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Ok(mut q) = d.recent.lock() {\\n120→            q.push_back((r.level(), format!(\\\"{}\\\", r.args())));\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Boot diagnostics and logging. Every startup stage is numbered and timed, and goes to the\\n//! terminal, the log file and the on-screen overlay. The logger also keeps recent lines for\\n//! the in-game console.\\n\\nuse std::collections::VecDeque;\\nuse std::fs::File;\\nuse std::io::Write;\\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\\nuse std::sync::{Mutex, OnceLock};\\n10→\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub enum StageStatus {\\n    Ok,\\n    Failed(String),\\n}\\n20→\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct Stage {\\n    pub num: u32,\\n    pub name: String,\\n    pub detail: String,\\n    pub ms: f64,\\n    pub status: StageStatus,\\n}\\n\\n30→pub struct Diagnostics {\\n    pub start: Instant,\\n    pub log_path: PathBuf,\\n    file: Mutex<Option<File>>,\\n    pub stages: Mutex<Vec<Stage>>,\\n    pub recent: Mutex<VecDeque<(log::Level, String)>>,\\n    level: log::LevelFilter,\\n}\\n\\nstatic DIAG: OnceLock<Diagnostics> = OnceLock::new();\\n40→\\npub fn diag() -> &'static Diagnostics {\\n    DIAG.get().expect(\\\"diagnostics not initialised\\\")\\n}\\n\\n/// Directory next to the executable (falls back to the working directory).\\npub fn exe_dir() -> PathBuf {\\n    std::env::current_exe().ok().and_then(|p| p.parent().map(|d| d.to_path_buf())).unwrap_or_else(|| PathBuf::from(\\\".\\\"))\\n}\\n\\n50→/// Sets up the log file (next to the executable, else the temp dir) and the logger.\\npub fn init() -> &'static Diagnostics {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    let (log_path, file) = {\\n        let mut log_path = exe_dir().join(\\\"shardfall.log\\\");\\n        let file = File::create(&log_path).ok().or_else(|| {\\n            log_path = std::env::temp_dir().join(\\\"shardfall.log\\\");\\n            File::create(&log_path).ok()\\n        });\\n        (log_path, file)\\n60→    };\\n    // In the browser the log goes to the developer console.\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let (log_path, file) = (PathBuf::from(\\\"the browser console\\\"), None::<File>);\\n    let level = match std::env::var(\\\"PAV_LOG\\\").ok().as_deref() {\\n        Some(\\\"trace\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Trace,\\n        Some(\\\"debug\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Debug,\\n        Some(\\\"warn\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Warn,\\n        _ => log::LevelFilter::Info,\\n    };\\n70→    let d = DIAG.get_or_init(|| Diagnostics {\\n        start: Instant::now(),\\n        log_path,\\n        file: Mutex::new(file),\\n        stages: Mutex::new(Vec::new()),\\n        recent: Mutex::new(VecDeque::new()),\\n        level,\\n    });\\n    let _ = log::set_logger(&Logger);\\n    log::set_max_level(log::LevelFilter::Trace);\\n80→    d\\n}\\n\\nstruct Logger;\\n\\nimpl log::Log for Logger {\\n    fn enabled(&self, m: &log::Metadata) -> bool {\\n        let d = diag();\\n        let t = m.target();\\n        // Keep graphics-driver chatter out unless it is a warning.\\n90→        if t.starts_with(\\\"wgpu\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"naga\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"egui\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"winit\\\") {\\n            return m.level() <= log::Level::Warn;\\n        }\\n        m.level() <= d.level\\n    }\\n\\n    fn log(&self, r: &log::Record) {\\n        if !self.enabled(r.metadata()) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n100→        let d = diag();\\n        let line = format!(\\\"[{:>8.3}s] {:<5} {}\\\", d.start.elapsed().as_secs_f64(), r.level(), r.args());\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        eprintln!(\\\"{line}\\\");\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        {\\n            let js = wasm_bindgen::JsValue::from_str(&line);\\n            match r.level() {\\n                log::Level::Error => web_sys::console::error_1(&js),\\n                log::Level::Warn => web_sys::console::warn_1(&js),\\n110→                _ => web_sys::console::log_1(&js),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Ok(mut f) = d.file.lock() {\\n            if let Some(f) = f.as_mut() {\\n                let _ = writeln!(f, \\\"{line}\\\");\\n                let _ = f.flush();\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Ok(mut q) = d.recent.lock() {\\n120→            q.push_back((r.level(), format!(\\\"{}\\\", r.args())));\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/boot.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"//! Boot diagnostics and logging. Every startup stage is numbered and timed, and goes to the\\n//! terminal, the log file and the on-screen overlay. The logger also keeps recent lines for\\n//! the in-game console.\\n\\nuse std::collections::VecDeque;\\nuse std::fs::File;\\nuse std::io::Write;\\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\\nuse std::sync::{Mutex, OnceLock};\\n\\nuse web_time::Instant;\\n\\nuse anyhow::Result;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub enum StageStatus {\\n    Ok,\\n    Failed(String),\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct Stage {\\n    pub num: u32,\\n    pub name: String,\\n    pub detail: String,\\n    pub ms: f64,\\n    pub status: StageStatus,\\n}\\n\\npub struct Diagnostics {\\n    pub start: Instant,\\n    pub log_path: PathBuf,\\n    file: Mutex<Option<File>>,\\n    pub stages: Mutex<Vec<Stage>>,\\n    pub recent: Mutex<VecDeque<(log::Level, String)>>,\\n    level: log::LevelFilter,\\n}\\n\\nstatic DIAG: OnceLock<Diagnostics> = OnceLock::new();\\n\\npub fn diag() -> &'static Diagnostics {\\n    DIAG.get().expect(\\\"diagnostics not initialised\\\")\\n}\\n\\n/// Directory next to the executable (falls back to the working directory).\\npub fn exe_dir() -> PathBuf {\\n    std::env::current_exe().ok().and_then(|p| p.parent().map(|d| d.to_path_buf())).unwrap_or_else(|| PathBuf::from(\\\".\\\"))\\n}\\n\\n/// Sets up the log file (next to the executable, else the temp dir) and the logger.\\npub fn init() -> &'static Diagnostics {\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    let (log_path, file) = {\\n        let mut log_path = exe_dir().join(\\\"shardfall.log\\\");\\n        let file = File::create(&log_path).ok().or_else(|| {\\n            log_path = std::env::temp_dir().join(\\\"shardfall.log\\\");\\n            File::create(&log_path).ok()\\n        });\\n        (log_path, file)\\n    };\\n    // In the browser the log goes to the developer console.\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    let (log_path, file) = (PathBuf::from(\\\"the browser console\\\"), None::<File>);\\n    let level = match std::env::var(\\\"PAV_LOG\\\").ok().as_deref() {\\n        Some(\\\"trace\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Trace,\\n        Some(\\\"debug\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Debug,\\n        Some(\\\"warn\\\") => log::LevelFilter::Warn,\\n        _ => log::LevelFilter::Info,\\n    };\\n    let d = DIAG.get_or_init(|| Diagnostics {\\n        start: Instant::now(),\\n        log_path,\\n        file: Mutex::new(file),\\n        stages: Mutex::new(Vec::new()),\\n        recent: Mutex::new(VecDeque::new()),\\n        level,\\n    });\\n    let _ = log::set_logger(&Logger);\\n    log::set_max_level(log::LevelFilter::Trace);\\n    d\\n}\\n\\nstruct Logger;\\n\\nimpl log::Log for Logger {\\n    fn enabled(&self, m: &log::Metadata) -> bool {\\n        let d = diag();\\n        let t = m.target();\\n        // Keep graphics-driver chatter out unless it is a warning.\\n        if t.starts_with(\\\"wgpu\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"naga\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"egui\\\") || t.starts_with(\\\"winit\\\") {\\n            return m.level() <= log::Level::Warn;\\n        }\\n        m.level() <= d.level\\n    }\\n\\n    fn log(&self, r: &log::Record) {\\n        if !self.enabled(r.metadata()) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let d = diag();\\n        let line = format!(\\\"[{:>8.3}s] {:<5} {}\\\", d.start.elapsed().as_secs_f64(), r.level(), r.args());\\n        #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n        eprintln!(\\\"{line}\\\");\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        {\\n            let js = wasm_bindgen::JsValue::from_str(&line);\\n            match r.level() {\\n                log::Level::Error => web_sys::console::error_1(&js),\\n                log::Level::Warn => web_sys::console::warn_1(&js),\\n                _ => web_sys::console::log_1(&js),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Ok(mut f) = d.file.lock() {\\n            if let Some(f) = f.as_mut() {\\n                let _ = writeln!(f, \\\"{line}\\\");\\n                let _ = f.flush();\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Ok(mut q) = d.recent.lock() {\\n            q.push_back((r.level(), format!(\\\"{}\\\", r.args())));\\n\",\"total_lines\":187}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"dbd2614e-f270-4812-a98c-88bbbc085d06"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_14","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid plan. I will examine settings.rs to understand scene selection and locate the app render loop for injecting merc shell updates.\n\nI will also check input.rs for keyboard mapping. The plan is to build a self-contained game in games/merc/ with pure Rust in pav_core. Audio synthesis is not yet available there.\n\nAudio will live as pure functions in the game module so tests can measure RMS. The browser will use the engine's existing SimEvent audio path rather than extra wiring. The status already includes a music volume value.\n\nThe browser test requires non-zero Web Audio levels after a user gesture. I need to check whether the engine plays continuous ambient audio or only event sounds, since only looping events would produce persistent output.\n\nI will synthesize music in Rust to satisfy the no-shipped-audio requirement. I am weighing a continuous music voice in pav_audio against a JS starter script. Passing a generated buffer from Rust to Web Audio via WASM would require glue code.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40ace47f-e82a-4e08-978e-72edd99ad606-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40ace47f-e82a-4e08-978e-72edd99ad606-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/settings.rs","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40ace47f-e82a-4e08-978e-72edd99ad606-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-2026