{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_21","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the rooms/_template.toml view section and a reference outdoor room.\n\nPlanning the merc module game world as a large savannah room. Adding a first-person camera override to CameraRig with eye position, yaw, pitch, roll, and FOV fields.\n\nPlanning to query the simulation status from the render thread before each rig update. The status JSON will carry mode and UI state for the first-person camera override.\n\nThe status JSON will also carry player pose, stance, health, audio, and dev flags. Browser mouse look will use synthetic MouseEvent movementX/Y dispatched by tests; the JS shim accumulates these values for Rust to read via window.gameInput.\n\nThe JS shim will live in index.html. Rust will read window.gameInput.lookX each frame.\n\nThe JS shim accumulates mouse movementX and movementY while pointer lock is active. It exposes a take() method to read and clear the deltas each frame. A pointerlockchange listener updates the locked state. Rust will read these values via web_sys in the frame loop. gameTest.queue will handle commands.\n\nThe engine's gilrs library on WASM already reads navigator.getGamepads, so the gamepad stub injected before page load will be detected automatically. The shell must detect this gamepad state to switch UI prompts to PlayStation glyphs.\n\nThe gamepad prompt glyph must flip as soon as the stub connects, not only when buttons are pressed. The JS shim will poll navigator.getGamepads and expose a pad flag to Rust, which the shell reads to switch to PlayStation glyphs. An Xbox glyph set will be selectable through a command or settings menu.\n\nThe verifier audits committed tests and saved logs rather than rebuilding them. Browser tests must be written, executed, and their output preserved as evidence.\n\nThe browser test script must match verification steps 6 and 7. Enter and Space key events need to reach the game shell even when winit captures them on WASM. The default bindings map Space to DODGE and omit Enter entirely, so the shell must explicitly handle these keys.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e92f525e-7a9a-4258-807f-a6bc827eaa1f-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1040,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e92f525e-7a9a-4258-807f-a6bc827eaa1f-55","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/rooms/_template.toml","offset":40,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e92f525e-7a9a-4258-807f-a6bc827eaa1f-56","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"KEY\\.buttons|struct Keys|pub buttons","glob":"**/pav_app/src/input.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1894,"output_tokens":1649,"cache_read_input_tokens":117376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"4c994ad8-6d5b-414c-93ab-b2b88a5946b6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e92f525e-7a9a-4258-807f-a6bc827eaa1f-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1040→                if !room.is_empty() || !pads.is_empty() {\\n                    self.view_base = Some(self.view.clone());\\n                    for u in self.view.apply(&room).into_iter().chain(self.view.apply(&pads)) {\\n                        log::warn!(\\\"unknown view setting '{u}'\\\");\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id) != room_id_before {\\n                // Rooms can open HUD overlays (feel metrics) while you are inside.\\n                let wants = self.hud.current.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.def.overlays.iter().any(|o| o == \\\"feel\\\"));\\n1050→                if wants && !self.feel.open {\\n                    self.feel.open = true;\\n                    self.feel.auto = true;\\n                } else if !wants && self.feel.auto {\\n                    self.feel.open = false;\\n                    self.feel.auto = false;\\n                }\\n                let wants = self.hud.current.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.def.overlays.iter().any(|o| o == \\\"physics\\\"));\\n                if wants && !self.physics.open {\\n                    self.physics.open = true;\\n1060→                    self.physics.auto = true;\\n                } else if !wants && self.physics.auto {\\n                    self.physics.open = false;\\n                    self.physics.auto = false;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.feel.record(curr.tick, curr.hud.feel.speed);\\n            if self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| (r.id, std::sync::Arc::as_ptr(&r.def))) != room_before {\\n                // Input switching: the room's key overrides apply while inside.\\n                let (b, errs) = match &self.hud.current {\\n1070→                    Some(r) => crate::input::Bindings::with_overrides(&r.def.keys),\\n                    None if curr.game.is_some() => (crate::input::Bindings::game(), Vec::new()),\\n                    None => (crate::input::Bindings::default(), Vec::new()),\\n                };\\n                self.input.bindings = b;\\n                for e in errs {\\n                    log::warn!(\\\"room keys: {e}\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if *curr.config != self.sim_config && curr.tick > self.config_push_tick + 3 {\\n1080→                // The simulation changed its configuration (room overrides): adopt it.\\n                self.sim_config = (*curr.config).clone();\\n            }\\n            // Entering or leaving Shardfall: its controls, camera and look.\\n            let game_mode = curr.game.is_some();\\n            if game_mode != self.input.game {\\n                self.input.game = game_mode;\\n                self.input.bindings = if game_mode { crate::input::Bindings::game() } else { crate::input::Bindings::default() };\\n                self.rig.blend_from_current(0.5);\\n                if game_mode {\\n1090→                    self.game_saved = Some((self.rig.params.clone(), self.view.clone()));\\n                    self.rig.params = CameraParams {\\n                        tilt: 56.0,\\n                        yaw: 0.0,\\n                        distance: 15.5,\\n                        fov: 40.0,\\n                        ortho: false,\\n                        follow_lag: 0.06,\\n                        height_offset: 0.8,\\n                    };\\n1100→                    let v = &mut self.view;\\n                    v.bloom = 0.55;\\n                    v.bloom_threshold = 1.0;\\n                    v.sky = \\\"#14161c\\\".into();\\n                    v.light.sun_elevation = 52.0;\\n                    v.light.sun_azimuth = 35.0;\\n                    v.light.sun_intensity = 0.95;\\n                    v.light.ambient = 0.5;\\n                    v.saturation = 1.08;\\n                    v.fog = false;\\n1110→                } else if let Some((cam, view)) = self.game_saved.take() {\\n                    self.rig.params = cam;\\n                    self.view = view;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.game_frame = curr.game.clone();\\n            if !game_mode {\\n                self.game_ui.close_all();\\n                self.game_place = None;\\n            }\",\"content_concise\":\"1040→                if !room.is_empty() || !pads.is_empty() {\\n                    self.view_base = Some(self.view.clone());\\n                    for u in self.view.apply(&room).into_iter().chain(self.view.apply(&pads)) {\\n                        log::warn!(\\\"unknown view setting '{u}'\\\");\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id) != room_id_before {\\n                // Rooms can open HUD overlays (feel metrics) while you are inside.\\n                let wants = self.hud.current.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.def.overlays.iter().any(|o| o == \\\"feel\\\"));\\n1050→                if wants && !self.feel.open {\\n                    self.feel.open = true;\\n                    self.feel.auto = true;\\n                } else if !wants && self.feel.auto {\\n                    self.feel.open = false;\\n                    self.feel.auto = false;\\n                }\\n                let wants = self.hud.current.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.def.overlays.iter().any(|o| o == \\\"physics\\\"));\\n                if wants && !self.physics.open {\\n                    self.physics.open = true;\\n1060→                    self.physics.auto = true;\\n                } else if !wants && self.physics.auto {\\n                    self.physics.open = false;\\n                    self.physics.auto = false;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.feel.record(curr.tick, curr.hud.feel.speed);\\n            if self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| (r.id, std::sync::Arc::as_ptr(&r.def))) != room_before {\\n                // Input switching: the room's key overrides apply while inside.\\n                let (b, errs) = match &self.hud.current {\\n1070→                    Some(r) => crate::input::Bindings::with_overrides(&r.def.keys),\\n                    None if curr.game.is_some() => (crate::input::Bindings::game(), Vec::new()),\\n                    None => (crate::input::Bindings::default(), Vec::new()),\\n                };\\n                self.input.bindings = b;\\n                for e in errs {\\n                    log::warn!(\\\"room keys: {e}\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if *curr.config != self.sim_config && curr.tick > self.config_push_tick + 3 {\\n1080→                // The simulation changed its configuration (room overrides): adopt it.\\n                self.sim_config = (*curr.config).clone();\\n            }\\n            // Entering or leaving Shardfall: its controls, camera and look.\\n            let game_mode = curr.game.is_some();\\n            if game_mode != self.input.game {\\n                self.input.game = game_mode;\\n                self.input.bindings = if game_mode { crate::input::Bindings::game() } else { crate::input::Bindings::default() };\\n                self.rig.blend_from_current(0.5);\\n                if game_mode {\\n1090→                    self.game_saved = Some((self.rig.params.clone(), self.view.clone()));\\n                    self.rig.params = CameraParams {\\n                        tilt: 56.0,\\n                        yaw: 0.0,\\n                        distance: 15.5,\\n                        fov: 40.0,\\n                        ortho: false,\\n                        follow_lag: 0.06,\\n                        height_offset: 0.8,\\n                    };\\n1100→                    let v = &mut self.view;\\n                    v.bloom = 0.55;\\n                    v.bloom_threshold = 1.0;\\n                    v.sky = \\\"#14161c\\\".into();\\n                    v.light.sun_elevation = 52.0;\\n                    v.light.sun_azimuth = 35.0;\\n                    v.light.sun_intensity = 0.95;\\n                    v.light.ambient = 0.5;\\n                    v.saturation = 1.08;\\n                    v.fog = false;\\n1110→                } else if let Some((cam, view)) = self.game_saved.take() {\\n                    self.rig.params = cam;\\n                    self.view = view;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.game_frame = curr.game.clone();\\n            if !game_mode {\\n                self.game_ui.close_all();\\n                self.game_place = None;\\n            }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"offset\":1040,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"                if !room.is_empty() || !pads.is_empty() {\\n                    self.view_base = Some(self.view.clone());\\n                    for u in self.view.apply(&room).into_iter().chain(self.view.apply(&pads)) {\\n                        log::warn!(\\\"unknown view setting '{u}'\\\");\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| r.id) != room_id_before {\\n                // Rooms can open HUD overlays (feel metrics) while you are inside.\\n                let wants = self.hud.current.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.def.overlays.iter().any(|o| o == \\\"feel\\\"));\\n                if wants && !self.feel.open {\\n                    self.feel.open = true;\\n                    self.feel.auto = true;\\n                } else if !wants && self.feel.auto {\\n                    self.feel.open = false;\\n                    self.feel.auto = false;\\n                }\\n                let wants = self.hud.current.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.def.overlays.iter().any(|o| o == \\\"physics\\\"));\\n                if wants && !self.physics.open {\\n                    self.physics.open = true;\\n                    self.physics.auto = true;\\n                } else if !wants && self.physics.auto {\\n                    self.physics.open = false;\\n                    self.physics.auto = false;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.feel.record(curr.tick, curr.hud.feel.speed);\\n            if self.hud.current.as_ref().map(|r| (r.id, std::sync::Arc::as_ptr(&r.def))) != room_before {\\n                // Input switching: the room's key overrides apply while inside.\\n                let (b, errs) = match &self.hud.current {\\n                    Some(r) => crate::input::Bindings::with_overrides(&r.def.keys),\\n                    None if curr.game.is_some() => (crate::input::Bindings::game(), Vec::new()),\\n                    None => (crate::input::Bindings::default(), Vec::new()),\\n                };\\n                self.input.bindings = b;\\n                for e in errs {\\n                    log::warn!(\\\"room keys: {e}\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if *curr.config != self.sim_config && curr.tick > self.config_push_tick + 3 {\\n                // The simulation changed its configuration (room overrides): adopt it.\\n                self.sim_config = (*curr.config).clone();\\n            }\\n            // Entering or leaving Shardfall: its controls, camera and look.\\n            let game_mode = curr.game.is_some();\\n            if game_mode != self.input.game {\\n                self.input.game = game_mode;\\n                self.input.bindings = if game_mode { crate::input::Bindings::game() } else { crate::input::Bindings::default() };\\n                self.rig.blend_from_current(0.5);\\n                if game_mode {\\n                    self.game_saved = Some((self.rig.params.clone(), self.view.clone()));\\n                    self.rig.params = CameraParams {\\n                        tilt: 56.0,\\n                        yaw: 0.0,\\n                        distance: 15.5,\\n                        fov: 40.0,\\n                        ortho: false,\\n                        follow_lag: 0.06,\\n                        height_offset: 0.8,\\n                    };\\n                    let v = &mut self.view;\\n                    v.bloom = 0.55;\\n                    v.bloom_threshold = 1.0;\\n                    v.sky = \\\"#14161c\\\".into();\\n                    v.light.sun_elevation = 52.0;\\n                    v.light.sun_azimuth = 35.0;\\n                    v.light.sun_intensity = 0.95;\\n                    v.light.ambient = 0.5;\\n                    v.saturation = 1.08;\\n                    v.fog = false;\\n                } else if let Some((cam, view)) = self.game_saved.take() {\\n                    self.rig.params = cam;\\n                    self.view = view;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.game_frame = curr.game.clone();\\n            if !game_mode {\\n                self.game_ui.close_all();\\n                self.game_place = None;\\n            }\\n\",\"total_lines\":2266}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e92f525e-7a9a-4258-807f-a6bc827eaa1f-55","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→# Optional: view settings while inside (`pav params prefix=view`, without \\\"view.\\\"), e.g. night:\\n# \\\"light.sun_intensity\\\" = 0.06, \\\"light.ambient\\\" = 0.25, sky = \\\"#0e1424\\\", bloom = 0.6, gi = 1.0,\\n# \\\"light.sun_elevation\\\" = 20, distortion = true, particles = true, exposure = 1.2\\n# Filters can aim at a part of the scene: \\\"filter.pixel_target\\\" = \\\"objects\\\" (characters & objects)\\n# or \\\"environment\\\", \\\"filter.color_on\\\" / \\\"grade_on\\\" / \\\"scanlines_on\\\" / \\\"grain_on\\\" / \\\"chroma_on\\\",\\n# outlines_on = \\\"objects\\\", style_objects = \\\"lit\\\", style_environment = \\\"flat\\\" (see rooms/mix_match.toml)\\n# Painterly and print styles: \\\"filter.stylize\\\" = \\\"paint\\\" | \\\"halftone\\\" | \\\"ascii\\\" | \\\"sketch\\\",\\n# \\\"filter.stylize_on\\\", \\\"filter.stylize_size\\\" (px), \\\"filter.stylize_color\\\" (rooms/paint_print.toml).\\n# Hazy air: haze, haze_height, shafts, shafts_forward, halos (rooms/light_shafts.toml).\\n# Wind and water: wind, wind_angle, wind_gusts, grass_push, water_ripples, water_speed,\\n50→# water_fade, water_rain (rooms/wind_water.toml). Transitions: \\\"filter.transition\\\" = \\\"iris\\\",\\n# \\\"filter.transition_demo\\\" = true loops it (rooms/transitions.toml).\\n# Rooms without roofs can keep tall things whole near the player: \\\"cutaway.height_cut\\\" = false\\n[view]\\n\\n# Optional: simulation parameter overrides while inside (full paths, see `pav params`).\\n[params]\\n# \\\"movement.jump_height\\\" = 2.0\\n# \\\"movement.ledge_grab\\\" = true     # off by default: a jump reaches ledges up to ~3.4 m, so keep\\n#                                   # walls you must not climb at 4 m or more in such rooms\\n60→# \\\"movement.lock_axis\\\" = \\\"z\\\"       # side-view rooms (axis in the room's own frame)\\n\\n# Optional: keyboard remapping while inside (action = [physical key names]).\\n[keys]\\n# jump = [\\\"KeyW\\\", \\\"Space\\\"]\\n# move_up = [\\\"ArrowUp\\\"]\\n\\n[layout]\\n# origin is only used when the room is loaded on its own (`pav load scene=<key>`).\\norigin = [-5.0, 0.0, -5.0]\\n70→\\n[[layout.layer]]\\ny = 0                         # more layers = more floors (add at = [col, row] to offset one)\\nmap = '''\\n###########\\n#.........#\\n#....B....#\\n#.........#\\n#.........#\\n#.........#\\n80→#.........#\\n#.........#\\n#.........#\\n#####..####\\n'''\\n\\n# Each map character: blocks (y0/y1 relative to the layer), ladder, prop or marker.\\n[layout.legend.'.']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \\\"#c8c8c8\\\" }]\\n\\n90→[layout.legend.'#']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \\\"#c8c8c8\\\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 2.0, color = \\\"#9aa5b1\\\" }]\\n\\n[layout.legend.'B']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \\\"#c8c8c8\\\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 1.0, color = \\\"#c9a27a\\\", rounded = true }]\\n# Other options: destructible = true, ghost = true (no collision), inset = 0.3 (thinner),\\n# crumble = 0.8 (falls 0.8 s after being stepped on), regrow = 4 (comes back after 4 s),\\n# strength = 40 (breaks when hit with more than this contact force, e.g. glass),\\n# look = \\\"flat\\\" | \\\"cel\\\" | \\\"lit\\\" | \\\"unlit\\\",\\n# ladder = { facing = \\\"north\\\", height = 3.0 },\\n100→# prop = { shape = { type = \\\"box\\\", half = [0.35, 0.35, 0.35] }, color = \\\"#e8704a\\\" },\\n# marker = \\\"player\\\"\\n# label = { text = \\\"HELLO\\\", size = 0.5, color = \\\"#2b2d35\\\", mode = \\\"floor\\\" }   (text on the tile)\\n# grass = { density = 4, height = 0.55, color = \\\"#7cbf5a\\\" }   tufts per cell that sway in the wind\\n#                   and part around the player (drawing only)\\n# prop = { ..., sway = \\\"leaves\\\" }   props (and [[object]]s) can sway: \\\"leaves\\\" | \\\"grass\\\"\\n#\\n# zone = { kind = \\\"...\\\", ... } makes the tile a trigger (identical neighbours merge):\\n#   kind = \\\"start\\\" | \\\"finish\\\" | \\\"gate\\\" | \\\"checkpoint\\\" | \\\"kill\\\" | \\\"water\\\" | \\\"pad\\\" | \\\"camera\\\" |\\n#          \\\"conveyor\\\" (facing = direction, speed = m/s; carries characters and props) |\\n110→#          \\\"bounce\\\" (speed = launch m/s; trampolines for characters and props)\\n#   course = \\\"name\\\"   start/finish/gates of one course share it; leaving START starts the timer,\\n#                     gates must be passed in `index` order (missed gate = +2 s), FINISH stops it\\n#   index = 1         gate order\\n#   y0 = 0, y1 = 3    height range relative to the layer (kill zones in pits: e.g. y0 = -3, y1 = -1)\\n#   label = \\\"TEXT\\\"    drawn on the floor (label_size = 0.5 to override the auto fit);\\n#                     color = \\\"#rrggbb\\\" or \\\"none\\\"; facing = \\\"east\\\" (respawn direction)\\n#   Zones are half-open boxes, so touching zones never overlap. A respawn point that lies in a\\n#   zone does not trigger it (respawning onto START keeps the timer running).\\n#   params = { \\\"movement.model\\\" = \\\"momentum\\\" }       pads: parameter changes until you leave\",\"content_concise\":\"40→# Optional: view settings while inside (`pav params prefix=view`, without \\\"view.\\\"), e.g. night:\\n# \\\"light.sun_intensity\\\" = 0.06, \\\"light.ambient\\\" = 0.25, sky = \\\"#0e1424\\\", bloom = 0.6, gi = 1.0,\\n# \\\"light.sun_elevation\\\" = 20, distortion = true, particles = true, exposure = 1.2\\n# Filters can aim at a part of the scene: \\\"filter.pixel_target\\\" = \\\"objects\\\" (characters & objects)\\n# or \\\"environment\\\", \\\"filter.color_on\\\" / \\\"grade_on\\\" / \\\"scanlines_on\\\" / \\\"grain_on\\\" / \\\"chroma_on\\\",\\n# outlines_on = \\\"objects\\\", style_objects = \\\"lit\\\", style_environment = \\\"flat\\\" (see rooms/mix_match.toml)\\n# Painterly and print styles: \\\"filter.stylize\\\" = \\\"paint\\\" | \\\"halftone\\\" | \\\"ascii\\\" | \\\"sketch\\\",\\n# \\\"filter.stylize_on\\\", \\\"filter.stylize_size\\\" (px), \\\"filter.stylize_color\\\" (rooms/paint_print.toml).\\n# Hazy air: haze, haze_height, shafts, shafts_forward, halos (rooms/light_shafts.toml).\\n# Wind and water: wind, wind_angle, wind_gusts, grass_push, water_ripples, water_speed,\\n50→# water_fade, water_rain (rooms/wind_water.toml). Transitions: \\\"filter.transition\\\" = \\\"iris\\\",\\n# \\\"filter.transition_demo\\\" = true loops it (rooms/transitions.toml).\\n# Rooms without roofs can keep tall things whole near the player: \\\"cutaway.height_cut\\\" = false\\n[view]\\n\\n# Optional: simulation parameter overrides while inside (full paths, see `pav params`).\\n[params]\\n# \\\"movement.jump_height\\\" = 2.0\\n# \\\"movement.ledge_grab\\\" = true     # off by default: a jump reaches ledges up to ~3.4 m, so keep\\n#                                   # walls you must not climb at 4 m or more in such rooms\\n60→# \\\"movement.lock_axis\\\" = \\\"z\\\"       # side-view rooms (axis in the room's own frame)\\n\\n# Optional: keyboard remapping while inside (action = [physical key names]).\\n[keys]\\n# jump = [\\\"KeyW\\\", \\\"Space\\\"]\\n# move_up = [\\\"ArrowUp\\\"]\\n\\n[layout]\\n# origin is only used when the room is loaded on its own (`pav load scene=<key>`).\\norigin = [-5.0, 0.0, -5.0]\\n70→\\n[[layout.layer]]\\ny = 0                         # more layers = more floors (add at = [col, row] to offset one)\\nmap = '''\\n###########\\n#.........#\\n#....B....#\\n#.........#\\n#.........#\\n#.........#\\n80→#.........#\\n#.........#\\n#.........#\\n#####..####\\n'''\\n\\n# Each map character: blocks (y0/y1 relative to the layer), ladder, prop or marker.\\n[layout.legend.'.']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \\\"#c8c8c8\\\" }]\\n\\n90→[layout.legend.'#']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \\\"#c8c8c8\\\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 2.0, color = \\\"#9aa5b1\\\" }]\\n\\n[layout.legend.'B']\\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \\\"#c8c8c8\\\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 1.0, color = \\\"#c9a27a\\\", rounded = true }]\\n# Other options: destructible = true, ghost = true (no collision), inset = 0.3 (thinner),\\n# crumble = 0.8 (falls 0.8 s after being stepped on), regrow = 4 (comes back after 4 s),\\n# strength = 40 (breaks when hit with more than this contact force, e.g. glass),\\n# look = \\\"flat\\\" | \\\"cel\\\" | \\\"lit\\\" | \\\"unlit\\\",\\n# ladder = { facing = \\\"north\\\", height = 3.0 },\\n100→# prop = { shape = { type = \\\"box\\\", half = [0.35, 0.35, 0.35] }, color = \\\"#e8704a\\\" },\\n# marker = \\\"player\\\"\\n# label = { text = \\\"HELLO\\\", size = 0.5, color = \\\"#2b2d35\\\", mode = \\\"floor\\\" }   (text on the tile)\\n# grass = { density = 4, height = 0.55, color = \\\"#7cbf5a\\\" }   tufts per cell that sway in the wind\\n#                   and par