{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_33","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine draws a lot of HUD chrome.\n\nThe merc scene should skip all engine HUD overlays. The egui closure will return early for merc to draw only the 10-foot DOM overlay. Accessing the scene name from root is uncertain.\n\n`scene_name` is available in scope before the egui closure. A `merc` flag will be set to skip all engine UI and touch controls. The nodraw mode only affects speed tests.\n\nThe hub protocol should be implemented entirely in the JS shim. This removes dependency on the Rust simulator's frame rate. The shim will connect immediately and call ready() as soon as the connection resolves.\n\nThe JS shim will send messages at 10 Hz from a timer after start. This avoids waiting for Rust to initialize. Both host and client will broadcast snapshots independently.\n\nThe JS shim will send pose updates and snapshots at 10 Hz. It counts received messages to confirm bidirectional traffic. The host finishes the match when time expires. The 20 per second rate limit is safe for small JSON payloads.\n\nThe hub must not call finish() when the host leaves. The harness expects a void result for host-left, not a played match. If the host exits before time-up, the round should simply end without a finish signal.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-46acc94c-ab90-4483-877b-5ccd05e8d973-77","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"cardSent","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3057,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":151040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"b0901c64-5296-42d5-94fd-26ca895dded4"}
