{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_36","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tick cap is 8. Falling behind means catching up only 8 ticks before dropping time.\n\nNodraw at 60fps yields 480 ticks per second, so a 40-second round finishes in about five seconds. GPU mode drops to roughly 16 ticks per second. The launch test needs GPU but does not require long simulation. History_seconds will be zeroed to keep ticks cheap. World::tick must avoid allocations every frame. Only one rapier player character is needed; spawning many NPCs would add unnecessary physics cost.\n\nVisual NPCs will be simple entities moved by the game. The engine player exists only for camera focus. The visual room is a 40x40 diorama around the origin, while the logical world spans 2048 units. Because the two spaces do not align, the camera must either move the visual room or teleport across a repeating diorama to keep the camera synchronized with the logical player.\n\nA single large box visual will serve as the floor. Spawning thousands of individual 1-meter blocks would be too heavy. The player entity will map to logical coordinates, and the ground will be a single non-colliding prop.\n\nThe ground will be a single 400-meter box to keep the player visible during long walks. The camera follows the logical player, and the clear sky marks the horizon.\n\nA grove of scattered trees will anchor the start of the title screen. The ground entity will be repositioned each frame to follow the player's horizontal coordinates, keeping the terrain beneath them as they walk.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-af7fd675-9c55-40bd-a536-292d7d4f02f9-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/entity.rs","offset":1,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-af7fd675-9c55-40bd-a536-292d7d4f02f9-82","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn set_position|pub fn feet","glob":"**/sim.rs","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2448,"output_tokens":944,"cache_read_input_tokens":156544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"a6f9d680-5db2-426d-8a0f-5d3f482b2a2d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-af7fd675-9c55-40bd-a536-292d7d4f02f9-81","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Game objects. An entity is one \\\"fat\\\" struct with optional parts, which keeps it cloneable\\n//! (for snapshots), serializable (for agents) and easy to extend: add a field.\\n\\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\\n\\nuse glam::{Quat, Vec3};\\nuse rapier::prelude::*;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n10→use crate::character::Character;\\nuse crate::shape::Visual;\\nuse crate::statics::RegionKey;\\n\\n/// Physical surface properties (kept so sleeping entities can be recreated).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Material {\\n    pub density: f32,\\n    pub friction: f32,\\n    pub restitution: f32,\\n20→    /// Linear and angular damping (air drag): calms chains and bridges.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub damping: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Material {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { density: 1.0, friction: 0.5, restitution: 0.0, damping: 0.0 }\\n    }\\n}\\n30→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct EntityId(pub u32);\\n\\n/// Simple scripted behaviours usable from scenes and room files.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(tag = \\\"type\\\", rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Behavior {\\n    #[default]\\n    None,\\n40→    /// Drops random props over an area, keeping at most `max` alive.\\n    Rain {\\n        interval: u32,\\n        max: u32,\\n        area: f32,\\n        height: f32,\\n        #[serde(default)]\\n        timer: u32,\\n        #[serde(default)]\\n        spawned: VecDeque<EntityId>,\\n50→    },\\n    /// Kinematic rotation about Y (radians per second).\\n    Spin { speed: f32 },\\n    /// Moves back and forth along `offset` (kinematic bodies: platforms, doors, crushers).\\n    Move(MoverDef),\\n    /// Turns about an axis, continuously or swinging (sweepers, pendulums, windmills).\\n    Rotate(RotatorDef),\\n    /// Fires projectiles in patterns (dodge gauntlet, bullet hell).\\n    Emitter(EmitterDef),\\n    /// Drops props: on a timer and/or when a pad sends its signal (physics stress tests).\\n60→    Spawner(SpawnerDef),\\n    /// Lays out a page of the store's object rows when a pad sends its signal (the Catalogue\\n    /// room; `crate::catalogue`).\\n    Catalogue(crate::catalogue::CatalogueDef),\\n    /// Steps a cast of performers through the clip library when pads send its signals (the\\n    /// Clip Browser room; `crate::clip_browser`).\\n    ClipBrowser(crate::clip_browser::ClipBrowserDef),\\n}\\n\\n/// Spawns props around itself.\\n70→#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct SpawnerDef {\\n    pub shape: crate::shape::Shape,\\n    /// Colour, or \\\"\\\" for a random bright colour per prop.\\n    pub color: String,\\n    pub look: crate::shape::Look,\\n    pub density: f32,\\n    pub friction: f32,\\n    pub restitution: f32,\\n80→    /// Seconds between automatic drops (0 = only on signals).\\n    pub interval: f32,\\n    /// Props per drop / per signal.\\n    pub count: u32,\\n    /// Oldest props are removed beyond this many.\\n    pub max: u32,\\n    /// Props appear in a box of these half extents around the spawner.\\n    pub area: Vec3,\\n    /// Pad signal that triggers a drop, and the one that removes everything spawned.\\n    pub signal: String,\\n90→    pub clear: String,\\n    /// Random rotation of spawned props.\\n    pub tumble: bool,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub pending: u32,\\n    pub spawned: VecDeque<EntityId>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for SpawnerDef {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n100→        Self {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Game objects. An entity is one \\\"fat\\\" struct with optional parts, which keeps it cloneable\\n//! (for snapshots), serializable (for agents) and easy to extend: add a field.\\n\\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\\n\\nuse glam::{Quat, Vec3};\\nuse rapier::prelude::*;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\n10→use crate::character::Character;\\nuse crate::shape::Visual;\\nuse crate::statics::RegionKey;\\n\\n/// Physical surface properties (kept so sleeping entities can be recreated).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Material {\\n    pub density: f32,\\n    pub friction: f32,\\n    pub restitution: f32,\\n20→    /// Linear and angular damping (air drag): calms chains and bridges.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub damping: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Material {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { density: 1.0, friction: 0.5, restitution: 0.0, damping: 0.0 }\\n    }\\n}\\n30→\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct EntityId(pub u32);\\n\\n/// Simple scripted behaviours usable from scenes and room files.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(tag = \\\"type\\\", rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Behavior {\\n    #[default]\\n    None,\\n40→    /// Drops random props over an area, keeping at most `max` alive.\\n    Rain {\\n        interval: u32,\\n        max: u32,\\n        area: f32,\\n        height: f32,\\n        #[serde(default)]\\n        timer: u32,\\n        #[serde(default)]\\n        spawned: VecDeque<EntityId>,\\n50→    },\\n    /// Kinematic rotation about Y (radians per second).\\n    Spin { speed: f32 },\\n    /// Moves back and forth along `offset` (kinematic bodies: platforms, doors, crushers).\\n    Move(MoverDef),\\n    /// Turns about an axis, continuously or swinging (sweepers, pendulums, windmills).\\n    Rotate(RotatorDef),\\n    /// Fires projectiles in patterns (dodge gauntlet, bullet hell).\\n    Emitter(EmitterDef),\\n    /// Drops props: on a timer and/or when a pad sends its signal (physics stress tests).\\n60→    Spawner(SpawnerDef),\\n    /// Lays out a page of the store's object rows when a pad sends its signal (the Catalogue\\n    /// room; `crate::catalogue`).\\n    Catalogue(crate::catalogue::CatalogueDef),\\n    /// Steps a cast of performers through the clip library when pads send its signals (the\\n    /// Clip Browser room; `crate::clip_browser`).\\n    ClipBrowser(crate::clip_browser::ClipBrowserDef),\\n}\\n\\n/// Spawns props around itself.\\n70→#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct SpawnerDef {\\n    pub shape: crate::shape::Shape,\\n    /// Colour, or \\\"\\\" for a random bright colour per prop.\\n    pub color: String,\\n    pub look: crate::shape::Look,\\n    pub density: f32,\\n    pub friction: f32,\\n    pub restitution: f32,\\n80→    /// Seconds between automatic drops (0 = only on signals).\\n    pub interval: f32,\\n    /// Props per drop / per signal.\\n    pub count: u32,\\n    /// Oldest props are removed beyond this many.\\n    pub max: u32,\\n    /// Props appear in a box of these half extents around the spawner.\\n    pub area: Vec3,\\n    /// Pad signal that triggers a drop, and the one that removes everything spawned.\\n    pub signal: String,\\n90→    pub clear: String,\\n    /// Random rotation of spawned props.\\n    pub tumble: bool,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub pending: u32,\\n    pub spawned: VecDeque<EntityId>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for SpawnerDef {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n100→        Self {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/entity.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"//! Game objects. An entity is one \\\"fat\\\" struct with optional parts, which keeps it cloneable\\n//! (for snapshots), serializable (for agents) and easy to extend: add a field.\\n\\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\\n\\nuse glam::{Quat, Vec3};\\nuse rapier::prelude::*;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::character::Character;\\nuse crate::shape::Visual;\\nuse crate::statics::RegionKey;\\n\\n/// Physical surface properties (kept so sleeping entities can be recreated).\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Material {\\n    pub density: f32,\\n    pub friction: f32,\\n    pub restitution: f32,\\n    /// Linear and angular damping (air drag): calms chains and bridges.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub damping: f32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for Material {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { density: 1.0, friction: 0.5, restitution: 0.0, damping: 0.0 }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct EntityId(pub u32);\\n\\n/// Simple scripted behaviours usable from scenes and room files.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(tag = \\\"type\\\", rename_all = \\\"snake_case\\\")]\\npub enum Behavior {\\n    #[default]\\n    None,\\n    /// Drops random props over an area, keeping at most `max` alive.\\n    Rain {\\n        interval: u32,\\n        max: u32,\\n        area: f32,\\n        height: f32,\\n        #[serde(default)]\\n        timer: u32,\\n        #[serde(default)]\\n        spawned: VecDeque<EntityId>,\\n    },\\n    /// Kinematic rotation about Y (radians per second).\\n    Spin { speed: f32 },\\n    /// Moves back and forth along `offset` (kinematic bodies: platforms, doors, crushers).\\n    Move(MoverDef),\\n    /// Turns about an axis, continuously or swinging (sweepers, pendulums, windmills).\\n    Rotate(RotatorDef),\\n    /// Fires projectiles in patterns (dodge gauntlet, bullet hell).\\n    Emitter(EmitterDef),\\n    /// Drops props: on a timer and/or when a pad sends its signal (physics stress tests).\\n    Spawner(SpawnerDef),\\n    /// Lays out a page of the store's object rows when a pad sends its signal (the Catalogue\\n    /// room; `crate::catalogue`).\\n    Catalogue(crate::catalogue::CatalogueDef),\\n    /// Steps a cast of performers through the clip library when pads send its signals (the\\n    /// Clip Browser room; `crate::clip_browser`).\\n    ClipBrowser(crate::clip_browser::ClipBrowserDef),\\n}\\n\\n/// Spawns props around itself.\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n#[serde(default)]\\npub struct SpawnerDef {\\n    pub shape: crate::shape::Shape,\\n    /// Colour, or \\\"\\\" for a random bright colour per prop.\\n    pub color: String,\\n    pub look: crate::shape::Look,\\n    pub density: f32,\\n    pub friction: f32,\\n    pub restitution: f32,\\n    /// Seconds between automatic drops (0 = only on signals).\\n    pub interval: f32,\\n    /// Props per drop / per signal.\\n    pub count: u32,\\n    /// Oldest props are removed beyond this many.\\n    pub max: u32,\\n    /// Props appear in a box of these half extents around the spawner.\\n    pub area: Vec3,\\n    /// Pad signal that triggers a drop, and the one that removes everything spawned.\\n    pub signal: String,\\n    pub clear: String,\\n    /// Random rotation of spawned props.\\n    pub tumble: bool,\\n    pub timer: f32,\\n    pub pending: u32,\\n    pub spawned: VecDeque<EntityId>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for SpawnerDef {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self {\\n\",\"total_lines\":535}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-af7fd675-9c55-40bd-a536-292d7d4f02f9-82","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,5