{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_42","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pointer lock movement on web typically arrives as DeviceEvent::MouseMotion rather than CursorMoved.\n\nNative tests drive look directly via World::tick, so they do not need mouse input. Browser tests require a JS shim because MouseEvent movementX bypasses winit reliably. The Rust code will read JavaScript each frame on wasm to feed browser movement into the game. I am now designing the JavaScript API.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e8d9d569-1be9-49b6-b8a2-1d337029053d-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/Cargo.toml","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4293,"output_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":172160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2544020a-d340-4c2d-b621-f3b6870f4fcb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e8d9d569-1be9-49b6-b8a2-1d337029053d-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_app\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"shardfall\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\n10→\\n[dependencies]\\npav_core.workspace = true\\npav_render.workspace = true\\npav_view.workspace = true\\npav_tools.workspace = true\\npav_ui.workspace = true\\npav_audio.workspace = true\\nglam.workspace = true\\nwinit.workspace = true\\n20→egui.workspace = true\\negui-wgpu = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"winit\\\"] }\\ngilrs.workspace = true\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\nweb-time.workspace = true\\n\\n[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))'.dependencies]\\n30→notify.workspace = true\\negui-winit = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"clipboard\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")'.dependencies]\\nwasm-bindgen.workspace = true\\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true\\nweb-sys = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"Window\\\", \\\"Document\\\", \\\"Element\\\", \\\"HtmlElement\\\", \\\"Location\\\", \\\"UrlSearchParams\\\", \\\"console\\\", \\\"Storage\\\", \\\"MediaQueryList\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]\\nwindows-sys = { version = \\\"0.61\\\", features = [\\\"Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging\\\", \\\"Win32_System_Console\\\", \\\"Win32_Foundation\\\"] }\\n40→\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_app\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"shardfall\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\n10→\\n[dependencies]\\npav_core.workspace = true\\npav_render.workspace = true\\npav_view.workspace = true\\npav_tools.workspace = true\\npav_ui.workspace = true\\npav_audio.workspace = true\\nglam.workspace = true\\nwinit.workspace = true\\n20→egui.workspace = true\\negui-wgpu = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"winit\\\"] }\\ngilrs.workspace = true\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\nweb-time.workspace = true\\n\\n[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))'.dependencies]\\n30→notify.workspace = true\\negui-winit = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"clipboard\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")'.dependencies]\\nwasm-bindgen.workspace = true\\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true\\nweb-sys = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"Window\\\", \\\"Document\\\", \\\"Element\\\", \\\"HtmlElement\\\", \\\"Location\\\", \\\"UrlSearchParams\\\", \\\"console\\\", \\\"Storage\\\", \\\"MediaQueryList\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]\\nwindows-sys = { version = \\\"0.61\\\", features = [\\\"Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging\\\", \\\"Win32_System_Console\\\", \\\"Win32_Foundation\\\"] }\\n40→\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"[package]\\nname = \\\"pav_app\\\"\\nversion.workspace = true\\nedition.workspace = true\\npublish.workspace = true\\n\\n[[bin]]\\nname = \\\"shardfall\\\"\\npath = \\\"src/main.rs\\\"\\n\\n[dependencies]\\npav_core.workspace = true\\npav_render.workspace = true\\npav_view.workspace = true\\npav_tools.workspace = true\\npav_ui.workspace = true\\npav_audio.workspace = true\\nglam.workspace = true\\nwinit.workspace = true\\negui.workspace = true\\negui-wgpu = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"winit\\\"] }\\ngilrs.workspace = true\\nserde.workspace = true\\nserde_json.workspace = true\\nanyhow.workspace = true\\nlog.workspace = true\\nweb-time.workspace = true\\n\\n[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))'.dependencies]\\nnotify.workspace = true\\negui-winit = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"clipboard\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")'.dependencies]\\nwasm-bindgen.workspace = true\\nwasm-bindgen-futures.workspace = true\\nweb-sys = { workspace = true, features = [\\\"Window\\\", \\\"Document\\\", \\\"Element\\\", \\\"HtmlElement\\\", \\\"Location\\\", \\\"UrlSearchParams\\\", \\\"console\\\", \\\"Storage\\\", \\\"MediaQueryList\\\"] }\\n\\n[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]\\nwindows-sys = { version = \\\"0.61\\\", features = [\\\"Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging\\\", \\\"Win32_System_Console\\\", \\\"Win32_Foundation\\\"] }\\n\\n[lints]\\nworkspace = true\\n\",\"total_lines\":42}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"fee359e6-7f91-4261-87c8-66a6cb580c39"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_43","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"web-sys does not include Function or eval.\n\nI'll use js_sys::Reflect::get to access window.gameInput. I may add js-sys as a direct dependency and run cargo check to update the lockfile.\n\nI'll use #[wasm_bindgen] with js_namespace to call gameBridge functions directly. I'll define gameBridge in index.html before the WASM module script loads.\n\ngameBridge will be a classic script in the HTML head, running before the WASM module. Its take() method reads gameInput and the command queue, resets input deltas, and returns a JSON payload. publish() stores status and UI state on window.__game.\n\ngameBridge will also expose localStorage helpers and AIHub status getters. Calling these from WASM requires a cfg guard, since wasm_bindgen extern \"C\" functions panic if the JavaScript object is missing.\n\nThe HTML script order is fixed: session.js runs first as an IIFE, followed by the gameBridge and hub connect scripts. The hub connect script will use a boot function with state flags to manage startup and shutdown.\n\nThe hub connect script calls AIHub.connect with shared-world mode, seats [1, 4], and card enabled. It stores the returned info on window.__mercHub, marks the hub ready, and sets gameTest.server when the server flag is present. It listens for start and end events to update internal state flags. On end it mutes audio by zeroing the gain node.\n\nThe hub connect script also handles time-up events. When the host receives a time-up signal, it finishes the game with all players tied at 100 points and marks the host as winner. It listens for leave events to stop sending updates if the host disconnects. It tracks incoming messages in window.__mercGot.\n\nA 100ms interval sends snapshot updates to the hub. Hosts broadcast snaps unreliably. Clients broadcast poses reliably.\n\nEnter key sends a ready signal when the hub is active and the game has not started. Space or Enter toggles the game menu.\n\nThe hub connect script will call boot immediately, since it sits at the end of the head and AIHub may already be available before DOMContentLoaded fires. A flag will prevent duplicate connections.\n\nThe time-up finish logic is now validated: standings must be arrays of player IDs, the host finishes the game with won set to true, and the call is skipped if the game has already ended.\n\nWhen a host leaves, the script stops sending updates but does not trigger a finish.\n\nThe time-up finish is safely gated by the ended flag, so a host-leave event that ends the round first prevents an override. The hub update rate of 10 per second is below the 20 limit. No scripts use Math.random.\n\nTouch detection uses CSS media queries to identify coarse-pointer devices without fine pointers. A pressed key disables touch-only mode. The shell triggers attract mode on touch-only title screens, and a notice appears in the DOM overlay. A single focusable settings button is tappable; clicking it sets a command.\n\nThe HTML overlay will display the title in large text so screenshots clearly show \"Jam Cry\". The canvas CSS spans the full viewport, but its drawing buffer may differ from the CSS size due to devicePixelRatio. The test requires the canvas drawing size to match the requested viewport, and Playwright screenshots use a 1280x720 viewport.\n\nThe engine sets the canvas size from the window. The CSS forces 100vw and 100vh with !important. This may stretch the drawing buffer. The viewport criterion depends on the framebuffer matching the requested size. Overflow hidden should prevent scrollbar discrepancies. On SwiftShader devicePixelRatio is likely 1. I will verify this when running.\n\nI will write the Playwright script for two launch runs. I am adding a fast-tick cap to simhost when the scene is merc and the query string contains test=1. The cap will be 240 instead of 8. I will avoid calling status() every tick because it allocates JSON. A dedicated method on the game object will handle this.\n\nThe fast-tick cap will be read from the Merc game state before each tick, since `play()` borrows the simulation and cannot be called during `advance()`. The code will use `sim.play().and_then(|p| p.get::<games::merc::Merc>())` to check the `fast` flag and cap ticks at 240 instead of 8.\n\nThe fast-tick cap will be read once per advance() call to avoid borrow conflicts. The app will set world.fast to true on the host's first frame if the URL query contains test=1. The nodraw flag is not used in launch tests.\n\nThe browser music will use a JavaScript oscillator node. A triangle wave at 196 Hz will be routed through a gain node set to 0.10 and connected to the audio context destination.\n\nThe browser script stores the gain node and audio context on window. It resumes the context on any keydown or pointerdown via capture listeners. The native test uses a Rust synthesizer instead of this JavaScript oscillator. The browser analyser will detect the same bus gain level as the Rust settings.\n\nI will write a small drum pattern in JavaScript using a counter instead of Math.random. Both the browser and Rust versions will play the same generative piece. The test will check audio levels to confirm the browser is producing real music.\n\nI will export nothing from the Rust engine and rely on engine audio events plus JavaScript. The live page will use a JavaScript Web Audio performance of the same piece to avoid cpal WASM quirks. I will document this in engine feedback: the measured synth is the Rust one, and the live page uses a matching JS performance. I am also considering whether to add a WASM export so the page can play the actual Rust-generated buffer.\n\nPushing samples directly from the frame loop is too heavy. I will add a looping `MusicBus` voice to `pav_audio` so the Rust synthesizer can play through the mixer. The same function will live in `pav_core::games::merc::audio`, letting both tests and the live app share one honest audio path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-adc4c313-793d-4b6f-b670-ca1ff96333da-93","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"wasm|web-sys","glob":"**/cpal-0.18*/**/*.rs","path":"/home/micha/.cargo/registry/src","head_limit":5}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-adc4c313-793d-4b6f-b670-ca1ff96333da-94","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"cpal.*wasm|target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"","glob":"**/pav_audio/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":914,"output_tokens":3371,"cache_read_input_tokens":176384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"6f679c4c-aaea-42c2-8134-cb62fb223eff"}
