558","uuid":"4b0ef22d-779f-4878-9f62-01a81e7ac381"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_46","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write merc.toml based on the starter.\n\nConfirmed the room spawns the player via build_standalone_room. I will write all code now and iterate on compilation errors. A debug_goal string will be added to status for debugging. Integration tests will call World functions directly and avoid Sim.\n\nA test will instantiate Sim and step frames to verify the hook updates world state and status title. InputFrame gains look, axes, and act fields. Game::pre converts these into Act. The from_frame mapping will translate stick space into movement and map look input to yaw.\n\nButton mappings are finalized. Space maps to JUMP, E to INTERACT, C to CROUCH, and Z to CRAWL prone. FOCUS serves as sprint. F maps to USE for seat changes. Native tests will use direct Act values, while the sim hook test uses InputFrame.\n\nMouse primary fire and right mouse button secondary aim are mapped. The room configuration defines additional keys for reload, map, heal, pills, tracker, melee, throw, monocular, next, and confirm. These keys apply automatically because build_standalone_room sets the room as current. Button constants and names must be added so with_overrides works.\n\nThe `act` field will carry menu command codes. The shell processes these even in the browser when the queue injects them. Codes cover confirm, back, direction, pause, god toggle, slider adjustments, save, continue, and dev open. Enter maps to confirm through the room key bindings.\n\nThe app writes mouse look into the shared input buffer before the sim thread reads it. Because pump() runs before that write, the sim consumes the previous frame's look input, creating a one-frame delay. This is acceptable for tests.\n\nThe test dispatches a mousemove and waits for the status yaw to change. The input mutex write block will include look updates. When pointer lock is lost, the app will set `input.act = 10` once to pause.\n\nJavaScript polls `navigator.getGamepads` every 200 milliseconds to detect connected gamepads. The engine also tracks the last device used, but the JavaScript flag is more reliable for stub detection. This polling does not use `Math.random`.\n\nI will verify the Xbox setting by driving the title menu with keyboard commands. The test will navigate from the title screen down to Settings, then through the controls tab and prompts row to toggle the switch.\n\nThe test will use arrow keys to reach Settings, Enter to open it, and the E key to cycle through tabs until reaching Controls. Toggling the Xbox prompt requires moving right from there. I am considering binding E to tab navigation in menus, though this conflicts with its existing interact function.\n\nI will not use E as a menu tab because it already serves as the interact button. The browser test can instead push an \"xbox\" command into the shipped `gameTest.queue` hook to toggle the Xbox setting directly.\n\nBoth the keyboard menu and the queue hook will be supported for toggling the Xbox setting. The test will use the menu first, falling back to the queue if it proves flaky.\n\nA save-and-continue flow is being planned. The test will queue a save command, reload the page, and then load the saved state. Rust will call gameBridge.storeSet to write the localStorage key `jamcry-save` during the save step.\n\nThe save-and-continue test will place a \"test-mark\" discovery via queue command, save the state, reload the page, and confirm the Continue option restores it. A dev mode test will pause the game, open the dev menu, toggle god mode, adjust a slider, and reset. Escape is handled to avoid swallowing the pause key. The launch test only verifies initial state changes before the world becomes fully playable.\n\nThe WebKit fallback will keep the message div visible for tests that check its text. The phone profile overlay displays \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button and no touch controls. The attract timer runs in simulation time, so a 10-second wait may not advance fast enough on a capped tick rate.\n\nThe attract timer advances by simulation ticks, so 10 seconds of idle time takes about 37 wall-clock seconds at the current capped tick rate. The test will wait up to 45 seconds for this case.\n\nA dynamic tick cap will fix the slow attract timer. The simulation will run at 120 ticks per second when the shell is in a menu or attract mode, and at 8 ticks per second during active play. This lets idle time catch up quickly without wasting resources on gameplay. A helper function will determine the current state to set the cap.\n\nThe tick cap helper will borrow the simulation immutably to check the Merc component and screen state. It returns 120 ticks per second when the shell is in a menu or attract mode, and 8 during active gameplay. This lets attract segments advance much faster than idle time.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b026e78-80d0-45d9-ab0e-2b617b811c17-98","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":120,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8138,"output_tokens":2893,"cache_read_input_tokens":187008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3634dac1-784f-499b-bdc9-6787adaa48cf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9b026e78-80d0-45d9-ab0e-2b617b811c17-98","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→}\\n\\npub struct App {\\n    settings: Settings,\\n    gfx: Option<Gfx>,\\n    egui_ctx: egui::Context,\\n    egui_state: Option<UiInput>,\\n    host: Option<SimHost>,\\n    rig: CameraRig,\\n    view: ViewSettings,\\n130→    /// View settings before the room's `[view]` table and pad overrides were applied, and\\n    /// which room / pad state they belong to.\\n    view_base: Option<ViewSettings>,\\n    view_key: (Option<u16>, u64),\\n    sim_config: SimConfig,\\n    app_settings: AppSettings,\\n    builder: ViewBuilder,\\n    input: Input,\\n    panel: Panel,\\n    menu_open: bool,\\n140→    paused_before_menu: bool,\\n    show_boot: bool,\\n    boot_done_at: Option<Instant>,\\n    started: Instant,\\n    last: Instant,\\n    fps: Fps,\\n    mouse: Mouse,\\n    screenshot_requested: bool,\\n    scene_name: String,\\n    toast: Option<(String, Instant)>,\\n150→    hud: RoomHud,\\n    watcher: Option<RoomWatcher>,\\n    editor: Editor,\\n    audio: Option<pav_audio::AudioOut>,\\n    audio_settings: AudioSettings,\\n    /// Tick at which the app last pushed its config (the sim's copy is adopted after that).\\n    config_push_tick: u64,\\n    latency: Latency,\\n    director: CameraDirector,\\n    feel: FeelOverlay,\\n160→    physics: PhysicsOverlay,\\n    quit: bool,\\n    /// Camera and look from before the game started (restored when leaving it).\\n    game_saved: Option<(CameraParams, ViewSettings)>,\\n    /// The Look & Filters window and the look layer over `view`.\\n    look_ui: crate::look_ui::LookUi,\\n    animation_ui: crate::animation_ui::AnimationUi,\\n    studio_mode: StudioMode,\\n    studio_navigation: bool,\\n    asset_ui: crate::asset_ui::AssetUi,\\n170→    asset_watcher: crate::asset_watch::AssetWatcher,\\n    creature_ui: crate::creature_ui::CreatureUi,\\n    creature_watcher: crate::creature_watch::CreatureWatcher,\\n    animation_watcher: Option<crate::animation_watch::AnimationWatcher>,\\n    animation_watch_attempted: bool,\\n    /// Station guide (H) and field guide.\\n    guide: crate::guide_ui::GuideUi,\\n    /// When the player last arrived somewhere new (another place, a teleport): the screen\\n    /// transition opens from then.\\n    arrival: Option<Instant>,\\n180→    /// Shardfall windows (inventory, vendor...), the latest game frame and the place whose\\n    /// look is applied.\\n    game_ui: crate::arpg_items::GameUi,\\n    /// When the hero was last saved.\\n    last_save: Instant,\\n    /// The gamepad's menu cursor (egui points) and the pointer events it makes this frame.\\n    pad_cursor: Option<Vec2>,\\n    pad_events: Vec<egui::Event>,\\n    pad_buttons: (bool, bool, bool),\\n    game_frame: Option<std::sync::Arc<pav_core::arpg::GameFrame>>,\\n190→    game_place: Option<pav_core::arpg::Place>,\\n    /// Phones and tablets: fingers, the on-screen controls and swipes (touch.rs).\\n    touch: crate::touch::Touch,\\n    /// The browser says this is a touch screen (or a finger has touched it).\\n    touch_screen: bool,\\n    /// The egui style has the touch sizes.\\n    touch_styled: bool,\\n    /// Touch screens draw at most 60 frames a second: when the next one is due.\\n    next_draw: Instant,\\n    /// Auto-attack, graphics quality, tips seen (saved).\\n200→    prefs: crate::save::Prefs,\\n    scaler: crate::quality::Scaler,\\n    #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n    bridge: Option<crate::bridge::Bridge>,\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    pending_gfx: Option<std::rc::Rc<std::cell::RefCell<Option<Result<Gfx>>>>>,\\n    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    audio_resumed: bool,\\n    init_started: bool,\\n    pub fatal: Option<String>,\\n210→}\\n\\nimpl App {\\n    fn new(settings: Settings) -> Self {\\n        let scene_name = settings.scene.clone();\\n        let touch_screen = crate::platform::touch_screen();\\n        let mut app = Self {\\n            gfx: None,\\n            egui_ctx: egui::Context::default(),\\n            egui_state: None,\\n220→            host: None,\\n            rig: CameraRig::default(),\\n            view: ViewSettings::default(),\\n            view_base: None,\\n            view_key: (None, 0),\\n            sim_config: SimConfig::default(),\\n            app_settings: AppSettings {\\n                vsync: settings.vsync,\\n                smoothing: true,\\n                show_stats: true,\\n230→                show_guide: true,\\n                aim_marker: true,\\n            },\\n            builder: ViewBuilder::new(),\\n            input: Input::new(),\\n            panel: Panel::new(),\\n            menu_open: false,\\n            paused_before_menu: false,\\n            show_boot: true,\\n            boot_done_at: None,\\n240→            started: Instant::now(),\\n            last: Instant::now(),\\n            fps: Fps { frames: 0, since: Instant::now(), fps: 0.0, frame_ms: 0.0 },\\n            mouse: Mouse::default(),\\n            screenshot_requested: false,\\n            scene_name,\\n            toast: None,\\n            hud: RoomHud::default(),\\n            watcher: None,\\n            editor: Editor::default(),\\n250→            audio: None,\\n            audio_settings: AudioSettings { master: 0.8, sfx: 1.0, footsteps: true },\\n            config_push_tick: 0,\\n            latency: Latency::default(),\\n            director: CameraDirector::default(),\\n            feel: FeelOverlay::default(),\\n            physics: PhysicsOverlay::default(),\\n            quit: false,\\n            game_saved: None,\\n            look_ui: crate::look_ui::LookUi::load(),\",\"content_concise\":\"120→}\\n\\npub struct App {\\n    settings: Settings,\\n    gfx: Option<Gfx>,\\n    egui_ctx: egui::Context,\\n    egui_state: Option<UiInput>,\\n    host: Option<SimHost>,\\n    rig: CameraRig,\\n    view: ViewSettings,\\n130→    /// View settings before the room's `[view]` table and pad overrides were applied, and\\n    /// which room / pad state they belong to.\\n    view_base: Option<ViewSettings>,\\n    view_key: (Option<u16>, u64),\\n    sim_config: SimConfig,\\n    app_settings: AppSettings,\\n    builder: ViewBuilder,\\n    input: Input,\\n    panel: Panel,\\n    menu_open: bool,\\n140→    paused_before_menu: bool,\\n    show_boot: bool,\\n    boot_done_at: Option<Instant>,\\n    started: Instant,\\n    last: Instant,\\n    fps: Fps,\\n    mouse: Mouse,\\n    screenshot_requested: bool,\\n    scene_name: String,\\n    toast: Option<(String, Instant)>,\\n150→    hud: RoomHud,\\n    watcher: Option<RoomWatcher>,\\n    editor: Editor,\\n    audio: Option<pav_audio::AudioOut>,\\n    audio_settings: AudioSettings,\\n    /// Tick at which the app last pushed its config (the sim's copy is adopted after that).\\n    config_push_tick: u64,\\n    latency: Latency,\\n    director: CameraDirector,\\n    feel: FeelOverlay,\\n160→    physics: PhysicsOverlay,\\n    quit: bool,\\n    /// Camera and look from before the game started (restored when leaving it).\\n    game_saved: Option<(CameraParams, ViewSettings)>,\\n    /// The Look & Filters window and the look layer over `view`.\\n    look_ui: crate::look_ui::LookUi,\\n    animation_ui: crate::animation_ui::AnimationUi,\\n    studio_mode: StudioMode,\\n    studio_navigation: bool,\\n    asset_ui: crate::asset_ui::AssetUi,\\n170→    asset_watcher: crate::asset_watch::AssetWatcher,\\n    creature_ui: crate::creature_ui::CreatureUi,\\n    creature_watcher: crate::creature_watch::CreatureWatcher,\\n    animation_watcher: Option<crate::animation_watch::AnimationWatcher>,\\n    animation_watch_attempted: bool,\\n    /// Station guide (H) and field guide.\\n    guide: crate::guide_ui::GuideUi,\\n    /// When the player last arrived somewhere new (another place, a teleport): the screen\\n    /// transition opens from t