{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_47","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"show_stats and show_guide default to true.\n\nFor the merc scene, show_stats, show_guide, and show_boot will be disabled in new() to suppress HUD clutter.\n\nA return at the start of the egui closure will skip all engine chrome for the merc scene. This avoids a large indent while keeping touch controls and hint bars intact.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ee30f0c4-e0ac-4a07-9aac-8d29df9a2b8c-99","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1545,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4397,"output_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":195072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"36a2973f-c679-427f-8db4-dd32595fcb63"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ee30f0c4-e0ac-4a07-9aac-8d29df9a2b8c-99","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1545→                );\\n            }\\n        });\\n        if prefs != self.prefs {\\n            self.prefs = prefs;\\n1550→            crate::save::save_prefs(&self.prefs);\\n        }\\n        // The map: a tap on the minimap opens the big one; a tap or a swipe closes that.\\n        let sw = &mut self.touch.swipes;\\n        if sw.take_tap(egui::Id::new(\\\"minimap\\\")) {\\n            self.game_ui.map = true;\\n        }\\n        let big = egui::Id::new(\\\"big_map\\\");\\n        if sw.take_tap(big) || sw.is_gone(big, 0) {\\n            self.game_ui.map = false;\\n1560→            sw.restore(big);\\n        }\\n        if !self.prefs.tips_seen && sw.is_gone(egui::Id::new(\\\"touch_tips\\\"), 0) {\\n            self.prefs.tips_seen = true;\\n            crate::save::save_prefs(&self.prefs);\\n        }\\n        self.show_boot = show_boot;\\n        for a in guide_out {\\n            match a {\\n                crate::guide_ui::GuideAction::Go(key) => teleport = Some(crate::rooms::TeleportTarget::Room(key)),\\n1570→                crate::guide_ui::GuideAction::Toast(m) => self.toast = Some((m, Instant::now())),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(m) = look_msg {\\n            self.toast = Some((m, Instant::now()));\\n        }\\n        self.look_ui.save_if_dirty(false);\\n        for c in game_cmds {\\n            host.shared.command(c);\\n        }\\n1580→        if ctl.paused != ctl_before.paused\\n            || ctl.speed != ctl_before.speed\\n            || ctl.step_requests != ctl_before.step_requests\\n            || ctl.rewind_speed != ctl_before.rewind_speed\\n        {\",\"content_concise\":\"1545→                );\\n            }\\n        });\\n        if prefs != self.prefs {\\n            self.prefs = prefs;\\n1550→            crate::save::save_prefs(&self.prefs);\\n        }\\n        // The map: a tap on the minimap opens the big one; a tap or a swipe closes that.\\n        let sw = &mut self.touch.swipes;\\n        if sw.take_tap(egui::Id::new(\\\"minimap\\\")) {\\n            self.game_ui.map = true;\\n        }\\n        let big = egui::Id::new(\\\"big_map\\\");\\n        if sw.take_tap(big) || sw.is_gone(big, 0) {\\n            self.game_ui.map = false;\\n1560→            sw.restore(big);\\n        }\\n        if !self.prefs.tips_seen && sw.is_gone(egui::Id::new(\\\"touch_tips\\\"), 0) {\\n            self.prefs.tips_seen = true;\\n            crate::save::save_prefs(&self.prefs);\\n        }\\n        self.show_boot = show_boot;\\n        for a in guide_out {\\n            match a {\\n                crate::guide_ui::GuideAction::Go(key) => teleport = Some(crate::rooms::TeleportTarget::Room(key)),\\n1570→                crate::guide_ui::GuideAction::Toast(m) => self.toast = Some((m, Instant::now())),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(m) = look_msg {\\n            self.toast = Some((m, Instant::now()));\\n        }\\n        self.look_ui.save_if_dirty(false);\\n        for c in game_cmds {\\n            host.shared.command(c);\\n        }\\n1580→        if ctl.paused != ctl_before.paused\\n            || ctl.speed != ctl_before.speed\\n            || ctl.step_requests != ctl_before.step_requests\\n            || ctl.rewind_speed != ctl_before.rewind_speed\\n        {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"offset\":1545,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"                );\\n            }\\n        });\\n        if prefs != self.prefs {\\n            self.prefs = prefs;\\n            crate::save::save_prefs(&self.prefs);\\n        }\\n        // The map: a tap on the minimap opens the big one; a tap or a swipe closes that.\\n        let sw = &mut self.touch.swipes;\\n        if sw.take_tap(egui::Id::new(\\\"minimap\\\")) {\\n            self.game_ui.map = true;\\n        }\\n        let big = egui::Id::new(\\\"big_map\\\");\\n        if sw.take_tap(big) || sw.is_gone(big, 0) {\\n            self.game_ui.map = false;\\n            sw.restore(big);\\n        }\\n        if !self.prefs.tips_seen && sw.is_gone(egui::Id::new(\\\"touch_tips\\\"), 0) {\\n            self.prefs.tips_seen = true;\\n            crate::save::save_prefs(&self.prefs);\\n        }\\n        self.show_boot = show_boot;\\n        for a in guide_out {\\n            match a {\\n                crate::guide_ui::GuideAction::Go(key) => teleport = Some(crate::rooms::TeleportTarget::Room(key)),\\n                crate::guide_ui::GuideAction::Toast(m) => self.toast = Some((m, Instant::now())),\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(m) = look_msg {\\n            self.toast = Some((m, Instant::now()));\\n        }\\n        self.look_ui.save_if_dirty(false);\\n        for c in game_cmds {\\n            host.shared.command(c);\\n        }\\n        if ctl.paused != ctl_before.paused\\n            || ctl.speed != ctl_before.speed\\n            || ctl.step_requests != ctl_before.step_requests\\n            || ctl.rewind_speed != ctl_before.rewind_speed\\n        {\\n\",\"total_lines\":2266}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"699eca79-5574-4d22-962b-2b18c67725a8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_48","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The closure ends at line 1546 with `});` and returns `()`.\n\nAn early `return;` inside the closure is valid in Rust. Variables declared outside will keep their initial values if the closure exits early, so initialization must be checked first. The `touch.draw` call inside the closure will not execute.\n\nI will write the full game code now. Boot messages will be hidden for merc so egui text does not cover the canvas. Fog and sky colors will be set via the room. A large ground box at the player's feet fills the lower half of the frame. The weapon will sit in the lower right corner.\n\nThe sky will use a dusk gradient from `#e8d3ad` to `#f0a060` with sun elevation 14. The merc.toml view section is being added. The ground box is centered at player feet minus 0.2 to avoid clipping against the near camera plane.\n\nA data-driven goal list will be written for the jobs. Logging will be added to stuck-bot tests to print the current goal index, name, and position. The yaw formula for facing a point is confirmed as `atan2(dx, -dz)`. A helper function will wrap angle differences into the `-pi..pi` range.\n\nThe angle difference helper will use `rem_euclid` to wrap angles correctly. Movement speeds are now defined: 3.0 for aiming, 4.6 for walking, 7.0 for sprinting, 2.53 for crouching, and 1.3 for prone. Sprinting and crouching also scale by a fever-attack modifier and a player-speed tune factor. Stick input maps move_y to forward and move_x to right.\n\nThe forward and right vectors are derived from yaw. Forward is `(sin(yaw), -cos(yaw))` and right is `(cos(yaw), sin(yaw))`. Stick input is normalized by its length.\n\nThe normalized stick input is projected onto the forward and right vectors to compute horizontal velocity. A test case confirms that facing east with forward input yields movement along the positive x-axis.\n\nMouse look updates yaw by the horizontal delta and clamps pitch between -1.2 and 1.2. The browser shim maps positive vertical mouse movement to pitch decrease, so the code subtracts the delta multiplied by sensitivity.\n\nCrouch toggles on tap and prone sets on hold. Eye height and capsule height interpolate toward target values over 0.12 seconds. The test expects eye position to settle near the target after one second of ticks. Hard landing from vertical speed is optional.\n\nA simple hard-landing implementation will be added for fall speeds above 12, even though the gating combat tests do not explicitly cover it. Shooting will be disabled while the player is deep in water. The plan checklist will be updated as work proceeds, and repetitive code may be generated with a script.\n\nCore simulation files will be written in batches. The companion struct is being defined with fields for name, id, alive state, down timer, trust, and rescue status.\n\nA rescue flag resets when the player sleeps. If the player dies with no rescue available, the outcome is lost and the game reloads from autosave. The campaign sets this flag before scripted down events so the bot can avoid death.\n\nDowned companions have a 45-second timer. The bot reaches them to patch with a syrette or overdose them. If the timer expires without intervention, the companion dies and the flag is set.\n\nA unit test will verify that companions remain dead after save and load. The music RMS ratio will be exactly 0.10 with a deterministic oscillator, using amplitude 0.3 at full gain and 0.03 at 10% gain to avoid clipping. Voice handling is next.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8a6ddce5-5c34-4ade-8ab8-8d1f9d06b583-100","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\.wav|\\.mp3|\\.ogg","glob":"**/*.{rs,toml,md,json}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8a6ddce5-5c34-4ade-8ab8-8d1f9d06b583-101","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"find engine -type f \\( -name '*.wav' -o -name '*.mp3' -o -name '*.ogg' \\) | head -50","description":"Find any audio files in the engine"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":984,"output_tokens":2267,"cache_read_input_tokens":199424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"06bf1813-d102-4e96-a4d0-ea0011c1fb20"}
