{\\n    let mv = vec_arg(a, \\\"move\\\")?.unwrap_or_default();\\n    let dir = glam::Vec2::new(mv.first().copied().unwrap_or(0.0), mv.get(1).copied().unwrap_or(0.0));\\n    let held = buttons_arg(a, \\\"hold\\\")?;\\n    let press = buttons_arg(a, \\\"press\\\")?;\\n    let aim = vec_arg(a, \\\"aim\\\")?.filter(|v| v.len() == 3).map(|v| glam::Vec3::new(v[0], v[1], v[2]));\\n    let n = get_u64(a, \\\"ticks\\\", 1)?.max(1);\\n    for i in 0..n {\\n        let f = pav_core::InputFrame {\\n            move_dir: dir.clamp_length_max(1.0),\\n            vertical: 0.0,\\n            aim,\\n            held: held | if i == 0 { press } else { 0 },\\n            pressed: if i == 0 { press } else { 0 },\\n            cmd: None,\\n        };\\n        s.sim.step(&f);\\n        s.sync_camera();\\n    }\\n    s.keep_events();\\n    Ok(Output::Json(player_json(s)))\\n}\\n\\nfn t_spawn(s: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\\n    use pav_core::{BodyKind, Color, Shape, Spawn, Visual};\\n    let size = vec_arg(a, \\\"size\\\")?.unwrap_or_default();\\n    let g = |i: usize, d: f32| size.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(d);\\n    let shape = match get_str(a, \\\"shape\\\").unwrap_or(\\\"box\\\") {\\n        \\\"box\\\" => Shape::Box { half: glam::Vec3::new(g(0, 0.4), g(1, g(0, 0.4)), g(2, g(0, 0.4))) },\\n        \\\"rounded_box\\\" => Shape::RoundedBox { half: glam::Vec3::new(g(0, 0.4), g(1, g(0, 0.4)), g(2, g(0, 0.4))), radius: 0.1 },\\n        \\\"sphere\\\" => Shape::Sphere { radius: g(0, 0.4) },\\n        \\\"capsule\\\" => Shape::Capsule { half_height: g(0, 0.3), radius: g(1, 0.25) },\\n\",\"total_lines\":1861}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d2687907-3b33-4909-88f5-8f0c6c778e62"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_53","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Camera data() and forward() are needed to add FpCam.\n\nI will read the remaining camera methods, SimEvent variants, and audio functions. PLAN.md sections 8 and 15 need exact numbers. The simulation will be built as a testable module first. Then camera, app, and HTML will be wired in. World design will prioritize testability.\n\nWorld will hold seed, RNG, real time, game minutes, screen, plan, player, guns, companions, enemies, fire, wind, and flags. PLAN sections 8, 14, and 15 need exact numbers. Status() usage and bot returns also need review.\n\nWorld will also hold contracts, goal, tune, dev, saves_written, ui, net, and an audio events queue. Ticks run at 60 Hz. Playthroughs require roughly 108,000 ticks across three routes. Each tick must stay under 50 microseconds.\n\nGoals will be an enum the bot understands. Tick advances goals when conditions are met. The bot supplies input only. A `play` helper will run campaigns for tests. Title flow is UI testing, not playthrough logic.\n\nWorld::campaign begins at the title screen. The bot will confirm through menus to start the playthrough. This is more honest than skipping the UI, and the few ticks spent are negligible for speed. Plan variants will set the branch choices at B4 and the ending.\n\nBurn, Read, and Chair each map to specific pills, patch, or companion deaths plus their unique endings. The bot reads world.plan to choose its path. Tests construct the plan directly for each route.\n\nCampaigns will be structured as deterministic goal step lists built from the plan at startup. The bot simply executes each current goal in sequence. The human choice is encoded in the plan itself, so tests can spawn three separate campaigns for each route. A human player would instead see those choices presented in the UI.\n\nA shared `apply_choice` function will handle B4 decisions for both the shell and the scripted route. Playthrough tests will assert flags after the bot drives movement and combat goals.\n\nTests must exercise the real systems, not shortcuts. Jam rate tests will call the genuine jam function repeatedly. Fire spread and hitscan resolution will run through their actual code paths. Playthrough tests will tick World with bot_input rather than setting flags directly. Flag assertions must reflect genuine system behavior.\n\nFlag assertions must reflect genuine system behavior. A jam flag requires an actual jam and reload. Weapon breakage needs condition below eight with shots until break. Syrette healing must increase health by the correct amount.\n\nThe bot may set up encounters through mission scripting inside World::tick. This is legitimate game logic, not a cheat. Dev teleport is forbidden for the bot.\n\nMission scripting will advance inside World::tick as the campaign itself.\n\nThe simulation will stay lightweight. Enemies will be a small Vec, fire a sparse BTreeMap, and spatial checks will remain simple. I will patch FpCam in the camera data method, review the audio API and app structure, compile the simulation first, then wire it into the application. I also need to add RELOAD and MAP button bits to the existing u32 input mask.\n\nI added HEAL, PILLS, TRACKER, MELEE, THROW, MONOCULAR, NEXT, and CONFIRM to the input bit mask. InputFrame will hold look, axes, and act. The game rotates stick-space move_dir by yaw for merc. Tests calling World::tick directly must pass the same InputFrame the native app uses.\n\nThe bot will supply move_dir in stick space. It computes desired yaw from the target world direction and clamps look to a small delta. Movement velocity blends right and forward vectors using the current yaw.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9256d012-a6ec-4b98-a875-7ca507d123bb-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs","offset":120,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9256d012-a6ec-4b98-a875-7ca507d123bb-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn sounds_for|fn render_events|pub struct Patch|pub fn render","glob":"**/pav_audio/src/lib.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9256d012-a6ec-4b98-a875-7ca507d123bb-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^## |^### |jam|syrette|wind_factor|8\\.7|coverage|sliders","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9256d012-a6ec-4b98-a875-7ca507d123bb-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/frame.rs","offset":60,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4775,"output_tokens":2283,"cache_read_input_tokens":50688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"372c52cf-8267-4b5a-9bb4-1506acaa2f56"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9256d012-a6ec-4b98-a875-7ca507d123bb-13","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→        }\\n        if !self.initialized || self.params.follow_lag <= 0.0 {\\n            self.target = focus;\\n            self.initialized = true;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let k = 1.0 - (-dt / self.current().follow_lag.max(1e-3)).exp();\\n        self.target += (focus - self.target) * k;\\n    }\\n\\n130→    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\\n        self.target = focus;\\n        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n140→        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n150→        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n160→        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n170→            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides are not cut down to a sliver.\\n            fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n        }\\n        let far = (p.distance * 4.0 + 200.0).max(300.0);\\n        let proj = if p.ortho {\\n            let half_h = p.distance * (fov * 0.5).tan();\\n            let half_w = half_h * aspect;\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::orthographic(-half_w, half_w, -half_h, half_h, 0.05, far)\\n        } else {\\n180→            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect, 0.1, far)\\n        };\\n        CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: p.ortho }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// World-space ray through a pixel (origin, direction).\\n    pub fn screen_ray(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        let cam = self.data(size.x / size.y.max(1.0));\\n        let inv = (cam.proj * cam.view).inverse();\\n        let ndc = Vec2::new(px.x / size.x * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0 - px.y / size.y * 2.0);\\n190→        let near = inv.project_point3(ndc.extend(0.0));\\n        let far = inv.project_point3(ndc.extend(1.0));\\n        (near, (far - near).normalize())\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Where a pixel's ray hits the horizontal plane at `height`.\\n    pub fn ground_point(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2, height: f32) -> Option<Vec3> {\\n        let (o, d) = self.screen_ray(px, size);\\n        if d.y.abs() < 1e-5 {\\n            return None;\\n200→        }\\n        let t = (height - o.y) / d.y;\\n        (t > 0.0).then(|| o + d * t)\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Converts stick/WASD input (x right, y up) into a world direction on the ground plane.\\n    pub fn relative_move(&self, input: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\\n        let (f, r) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let w = r * input.x + f * input.y;\\n        Vec2::new(w.x, w.z)\\n210→    }\\n\\n    pub fn view_proj(&self, aspect: f32) -> Mat4 {\\n        let d = self.data(aspect);\\n        d.proj * d.view\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"120→        }\\n        if !self.initialized || self.params.follow_lag <= 0.0 {\\n            self.target = focus;\\n            self.initialized = true;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let k = 1.0 - (-dt / self.current().follow_lag.max(1e-3)).exp();\\n        self.target += (focus - self.target) * k;\\n    }\\n\\n130→    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\\n        self.target = focus;\\n        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n140→        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n150→        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n160→        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n170→            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides