{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6a5ffdd1-05bc-40d7-a3fb-51d05b224663-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"30→# months old (doctrine 9); no default features, so no dependencies.\\ntobj = { version = \\\"4.0.3\\\", default-features = false }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\", \\\"rc\\\"] }\\nserde_json = \\\"1\\\"\\ntoml = \\\"1\\\"\\nnotify = \\\"8\\\"\\nciborium = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nanyhow = \\\"1\\\"\\n# The motion importer (pav_tools): fdlibm's trigonometry, as JavaScript engines use it, and\\n# inflate for single files out of zip archives on the web.\\n40→libm = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nminiz_oxide = \\\"0.8\\\"\\nlog = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nbytemuck = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\npollster = \\\"1\\\"\\nweb-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n50→\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n60→# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\n70→debug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\ndebug = false\\nstrip = \\\"debuginfo\\\"\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"30→# months old (doctrine 9); no default features, so no dependencies.\\ntobj = { version = \\\"4.0.3\\\", default-features = false }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\", \\\"rc\\\"] }\\nserde_json = \\\"1\\\"\\ntoml = \\\"1\\\"\\nnotify = \\\"8\\\"\\nciborium = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nanyhow = \\\"1\\\"\\n# The motion importer (pav_tools): fdlibm's trigonometry, as JavaScript engines use it, and\\n# inflate for single files out of zip archives on the web.\\n40→libm = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nminiz_oxide = \\\"0.8\\\"\\nlog = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nbytemuck = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\npollster = \\\"1\\\"\\nweb-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n50→\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n60→# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\n70→debug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\ndebug = false\\nstrip = \\\"debuginfo\\\"\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/Cargo.toml\",\"offset\":30,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"# months old (doctrine 9); no default features, so no dependencies.\\ntobj = { version = \\\"4.0.3\\\", default-features = false }\\nserde = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\", \\\"rc\\\"] }\\nserde_json = \\\"1\\\"\\ntoml = \\\"1\\\"\\nnotify = \\\"8\\\"\\nciborium = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nanyhow = \\\"1\\\"\\n# The motion importer (pav_tools): fdlibm's trigonometry, as JavaScript engines use it, and\\n# inflate for single files out of zip archives on the web.\\nlibm = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nminiz_oxide = \\\"0.8\\\"\\nlog = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nbytemuck = { version = \\\"1\\\", features = [\\\"derive\\\"] }\\npollster = \\\"1\\\"\\nweb-time = \\\"1\\\"\\n# Browser build only.\\nwasm-bindgen = \\\"0.2\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen-futures = \\\"0.4\\\"\\nweb-sys = \\\"0.3\\\"\\n\\n[workspace.lints.clippy]\\n# Style lints that fight readable game code.\\ncollapsible_if = \\\"allow\\\"\\ncollapsible_match = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntype_complexity = \\\"allow\\\"\\ntoo_many_arguments = \\\"allow\\\"\\n\\n[profile.dev]\\nopt-level = 1\\n# Keeps the target folder small (cloud containers have a fixed disk allowance); backtraces\\n# still show file:line.\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\nincremental = false\\n\\n[profile.dev.package.\\\"*\\\"]\\nopt-level = 3\\ndebug = false\\n\\n[profile.release]\\ndebug = \\\"line-tables-only\\\"\\n\\n# Distribution build (what gets sent to the user): smaller, still has function names in crash reports.\\n[profile.dist]\\ninherits = \\\"release\\\"\\ndebug = false\\nstrip = \\\"debuginfo\\\"\\n\",\"total_lines\":76}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"fdcee5f0-8451-4611-bea3-f4fbf9338858"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_64","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Warnings won't fail the build unless explicitly denied.\n\nDrafting the bot movement code. The plan uses yaw-relative stick space with clamped look.x to snap quickly. Sprint activates once angle error drops below 0.35 radians.\n\nSprint is held whenever stamina remains above zero, switching to 7 speed while active and 4.6 otherwise. Stamina regenerates when not sprinting, causing oscillation over long walks.\n\nEnemies spawn 8 meters ahead. The bot aims at their heads and kills them in two hitscan shots.\n\nEnemies will miss most shots and deal low damage. The bot will use syrettes when health drops below 40. Health regenerates at 5 per second outside critical segments, capped at 100. Scripted down states will bypass regeneration.\n\nCritical health below 20 disables regeneration until treatment completes. The syrette restores 60 health over 1.5 seconds and applies a flag. A 60-second blackout without a pill wakes at the nearest safe house with 50 health and 80% diamonds; a unit test expects 32 diamonds from 40.\n\nThe nearest safe house is the closest of the three buildings even if unclaimed. The 20% diamond fee rounds down.\n\nAfter the post is cleared, a 24-hour in-game timer begins. One real minute equals one in-game hour. Sleep at SH2 advances the clock past the deadline and away from GP1. The bot then remans the post and sets a flag.\n\nThe bot will not reman the post while the player can see it, even if the timer has elapsed.\n\nTown shots will not harm civilians during a ceasefire. The campaign sniper ends that ceasefire.\n\nA stealth exposure function will be used by the AI.\n\nDetection probability is calculated from base chance multiplied by distance falloff, posture, tall-grass cover, light, and movement. Crouched in grass at night yields roughly 0.04725. Standing on road at noon is still being computed.\n\nStanding on road at noon yields roughly 0.5 detection probability, about ten times higher than crouched in grass at night. The AI will call `merc::detection_rate` directly, and a simulation test will verify that time-to-alert varies correctly.\n\nSmoke from burning cells blocks line of sight entirely. Rifle noise reaches 160 meters; enemies suspicious at 100 meters but not at 200.\n\nA squad of four enemies will include a flanker that moves sideways during combat while the others hold position. At most four enemies may shoot at once. If half are dead, they panic and flee unless on fire.\n\nA `Ride` struct is being defined for vehicles with kind, position, yaw, speed, roll, pitch, health, and stage.\n\nVehicle entry uses the USE key. Throttle comes from vertical axes or move_dir.y, capped at 16 times a vehicle speed tune. Height derives from terrain and pitch from slope; roll above 1 recovers toward zero.\n\nDamage thresholds are 70 for steam, 40 for smoke, and 15 for fire. Fire triggers an 8-second fuse before explosion. Repair requires leaving the vehicle, standing near it, holding interact for six seconds, and restoring health to 70.\n\nBoats stop when not on water within twelve meters of a river. An NPC driver follows a road polyline. USE cycles between driver and gunner roles; the mounted gun fires only when the player is the gunner and primary is pressed.\n\nA `Wire` struct will simulate network propagation between two Worlds in net.rs. A host world ignites fire, and a client receives the delta through a `Link` that applies latency, jitter, and loss. The Link queues messages by delivery time and drops unreliable packets at random. Each message stays under 1200 bytes, with fewer than 20 sends per second. The test runs once.\n\nA simplified depot round will serve as the hub round. The host destroys tanks, picks a ledger, and reaches the boat.\n\n`World::hub_round` and `fn net_step(host, client, link, dt)` will be added for the unit test.\n\nA `fingerprint` method will hash position, yaw, flags, and tick to verify deterministic behavior across two 100-tick runs.\n\nWorld serialization via serde_json round-trip is confirmed to work because serde handles private fields. The code will be split into focused modules: types.rs for enums and constants, fire.rs for the fire grid, world.rs for player logic and goals, shell.rs for menus, plus net.rs and mod.rs for network and game glue.\n\nA `title.md` file is being added. Game strings will live in `shell.rs` inside a `all_strings()` function for test scanning, plus world place names, contract names, and the About text. Forbidden checks will be case-insensitive for proper nouns. The About text will list all source fields, but testing counts will be filled after the tests run rather than using placeholders.\n\nThe camera struct will gain a first-person field. When active, forward, up, eye, and relative movement will use the first-person basis instead of the chase camera. A helper will compute yaw, pitch, and roll together.\n\nThe first-person camera basis is being derived from yaw, pitch, and roll. Forward is computed from yaw and pitch, right from world_up crossed with forward, and up from forward crossed with right. Roll is then applied around the forward axis to complete the orientation.\n\nThe first-person camera basis is being derived from yaw, pitch, and roll. Forward is computed from yaw and pitch, right from forward crossed with world_up, and up from right crossed with forward.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e06a107-7f9b-45da-9258-c3aa4984f688-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"CameraRig \\{","glob":"**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":622,"output_tokens":2954,"cache_read_input_tokens":108160,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"71b31de6-32b2-446f-96f0-b8cedab87afc"}
