(fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\",\"new_string\":\"    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (sy, cy) = fp.yaw.sin_cos();\\n            return (Vec3::new(sy, 0.0, -cy), Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy));\\n        }\\n        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).0;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).2;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\",\"old_line\":174,\"new_string\":\"    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (sy, cy) = fp.yaw.sin_cos();\\n            return (Vec3::new(sy, 0.0, -cy), Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy));\\n        }\\n        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).0;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).2;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\",\"new_line\":174,\"context_before\":\"        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1feb916c-31a7-4979-abdf-62f053521d0e-56","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides are not cut down to a sliver.\\n            fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n        }\\n        let far = (p.distance * 4.0 + 200.0).max(300.0);\\n        let proj = if p.ortho {\\n            let half_h = p.distance * (fov * 0.5).tan();\\n            let half_w = half_h * aspect;\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::orthographic(-half_w, half_w, -half_h, half_h, 0.05, far)\\n        } else {\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect, 0.1, far)\\n        };\\n        CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: p.ortho }\\n    }\",\"new_string\":\"    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp.eye;\\n        }\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (fwd, _, up) = fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll);\\n            let eye = fp.eye;\\n            let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, up);\\n            let mut fov = fp.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n            if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n                fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n            }\\n            let near = if fp.near > 0.0 { fp.near } else { 0.08 };\\n            let far = if fp.far > near { fp.far } else { 3000.0 };\\n            let proj = glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect.max(0.01), near, far);\\n            return CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: false };\\n        }\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides are not cut down to a sliver.\\n            fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n        }\\n        let far = (p.distance * 4.0 + 200.0).max(300.0);\\n        let proj = if p.ortho {\\n            let half_h = p.distance * (fov * 0.5).tan();\\n            let half_w = half_h * aspect;\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::orthographic(-half_w, half_w, -half_h, half_h, 0.05, far)\\n        } else {\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect, 0.1, far)\\n        };\\n        CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: p.ortho }\\n    }\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides are not cut down to a sliver.\\n            fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n        }\\n        let far = (p.distance * 4.0 + 200.0).max(300.0);\\n        let proj = if p.ortho {\\n            let half_h = p.distance * (fov * 0.5).tan();\\n            let half_w = half_h * aspect;\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::orthographic(-half_w, half_w, -half_h, half_h, 0.05, far)\\n        } else {\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect, 0.1, far)\\n        };\\n        CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: p.ortho }\\n    }\",\"old_line\":208,\"new_string\":\"    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp.eye;\\n        }\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (fwd, _, up) = fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll);\\n            let eye = fp.eye;\\n            let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, up);\\n            let mut fov = fp.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n            if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n                fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n            }\\n            let near = if fp.near > 0.0 { fp.near } else { 0.08 };\\n            let far = if fp.far > near { fp.far } else { 3000.0 };\\n            let proj = glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect.max(0.01), near, far);\\n            return CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: false };\\n        }\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides are not cut down to a sliver.\\n            fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n        }\\n        let far = (p.distance * 4.0 + 200.0).max(300.0);\\n        let proj = if p.ortho {\\n            let half_h = p.distance * (fov * 0.5).tan();\\n            let half_w = half_h * aspect;\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::orthographic(-half_w, half_w, -half_h, half_h, 0.05, far)\\n        } else {\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect, 0.1, far)\\n        };\\n        CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: p.ortho }\\n    }\",\"new_line\":208,\"context_before\":\"        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n    /// World-space ray through a pixel (origin, direction).\\n    pub fn screen_ray(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"aae73983-7e58-49b7-8278-b250fa7ed27f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_68","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found in `ground_axes` when `fp` is `Some`.\n\nThe `ground_axes` logic is confirmed correct for both `fp` states. Now drafting the Merc module across multiple files: geometry, weapons, fire, world, shell, and networking.\n\nAudio and module registration are planned for later. Geometry, weapons, and fire will be written first as they are self-contained. World.rs will hold the Spec type and comprehensive logic. Action constants are being defined for input handling.\n\nAdditional action constants for Xbox, save, continue, and dev are defined. Shell logic will use these alongside button states. Gun.rs will contain the jam formula and shot resolution. World will import the geometry, weapons, and fire modules to avoid circular dependencies. Shell methods will be implemented as an `impl super::world::World` block in shell.rs.\n\nThe fire grid will be a `FireMap` struct on `World`, holding a `BTreeMap` of `(i32, i32)` cells and an `acc` float. Screen state fields will live directly on `World` in `world.rs`, with shell methods implemented in `shell.rs`.\n\ngeom.rs will contain spatial queries. Road segments are defined as line segments with half-widths. The town area is not fully road. Water has a half-width of 12. A rock circle marks the hotel kopje. Trees generate from a hash and burn at fuel 3 unless blocked by zero fuel.\n\nTree fuel is 3.0, bush 1.5, and grass 1.0. Roads, water, and rocks block fire spread entirely. A ridge height function rises from 0 to 42 across the town area.\n\nVehicle test drives will run from x=200 to x=500 along z=-520 with increasing height. A town center check is added at the origin. Tall grass is defined as non-road, non-town, non-water terrain with a hash above 0.4. The AI uses a `cover_at` function for this.\n\nTall grass is generated by hashing grid coordinates and requiring the value to exceed 0.35. An `exposure` function will be exported to compute detection probability from posture, grass cover, light level, and movement. The AI will call this with 0.35 for crouched NPCs in tall grass, 0.6 for standing ones, or 1.0 otherwise.\n\nA scripted test will verify NPC detection in grass at night: a crouched still player stays hidden for two seconds, while a standing player on the road is spotted quickly. Detection logic will be added to the world tick for NPCs. The script steps are now ordered with budgets: boot 8s, raise map 2s, waypoint 2s, reach town 150s, fever 5s, pill or blackout 90s, reach GP1 -40,640 80s, fight post 30s, and enemy jam 8s.\n\nThe remaining script steps are now ordered with budgets. These cover clearing jam, breaking weapons, rescue, wounds, loot, reaching SH1, claiming, shopping, locker access, syrette use, sleep, depot driving with wind generation, monocular use, igniting targets, mounted combat, panic, animal encounters, and a boat trip to the pump.\n\nThe script now includes steps 53 through 70. These cover contract b2 through d2, vehicle repair, rain, better way setup, patch/overdose/let die, tape, ceasefire sniper, convoy, town burn, and reaching the cement cache at (-760, 620). A tracker will be placed near a cache by the town after shopping. The bus departs from the junction area.\n\nThe bus will depart from the depot after contract B1. It stops at the junction near the depot and then heads toward town, saving a drive leg to SH2. A flag `bus_taken` will track this. The tracker cache is placed at (90, 500) between the town and SH1.\n\nWind rag is set during the depot drive when wind speed becomes 9. GPS updates once the player moves 25 meters toward the town waypoint. The player starts at the airstrip (-120, 900) after boot completes. Fever warning lasts 40 seconds before the attack phase begins; the pill step holds pills for 2.5 seconds, while blackout waits through the full 60-second attack. The total fever budget is 110 seconds.\n\nCampaign diamonds start at 40, making the fee visible. The rescue step sets player HP to zero while the companion stays alive; the bot waits three seconds, then restores fifty HP and sets a flag. Wounds set HP to fifteen, and the bot holds healing; treatment restores forty over four seconds without interference from regeneration, which only activates above twenty HP. The syrette step sets HP to forty, applies a sixty-point heal over one point five seconds, and flags completion when the dose ends.\n\nShop logic checks the player has enough diamonds before buying the weapon. The locker step switches to the purchased weapon. Breaking a weapon sets its condition to five, wear to zero, ammo to nine hundred ninety-nine, and clears the jam flag so the bot can fire and reload until the weapon breaks. Enemy jamming spawns a soldier with high RPM and low gun condition; when that soldier jams, the enemy_jam flag is set and it stops firing. Clearing jam forces the player's next shot to jam, then reloads. The fight post spawns four soldiers at thirty health twelve meters away; once they are all dead, the post_cleared flag is set and the reman timer begins at twenty-four hours.\n\nSleep advances the game by 26 hours by adding 1560 minutes directly. The player faces south after waking, so the northward GP1 mission is out of view. If the post reman timer has expired while the player looks elsewhere, the bot remans the post and sets `post_remanned`. Unit tests will not use this sleep step.\n\nStealth spawns an unaware enemy for the player to melee behind. Dart equips a dart and poisons an enemy at fifteen meters within three seconds without alerting them. Night sets the hour to twenty-three before stealth. Monocular holds half a second aiming at an enemy. Mounted fires from the technical gunner seat. Panic ignites a cell under an enemy to make it flee.\n\nAnimal encounters spawn a zebra and flag when the player fires nearby. Vehicle repair sets health to thirty, exits, holds interact for six seconds, then restores seventy and flags completion. Rain ignites a cell, sets weather to rain, and flags once the fire tick extinguishes it. Town burn ignites cells inside the town area after ceasefire ends, then flags completion. The ceasefire sniper step explicitly clears the ceasefire flag. Tape play requires holding interact at the hotel for two seconds and flags playback with subtitles. Convoy spawns a truck NPC and rocket-launches it for an explosion. The burn ending ignites the ledger at the cement cache and flags the burn outcome.\n\nThe read ending requires holding position for 180 seconds while enemies miss, then flags `ending_read`. The chair ending is triggered by interacting with a chair and flags `ending_chair`. Contract flags are marked via `Spec::Mark` on their respective steps. Wind rag is set whenever wind speed exceeds six, checked once per tick. Technical vehicle movement over twenty meters during the drive step sets a flag. Boat travel is detected when moving more than fifteen meters on the river; the pump at (-420, -30) is being checked against the river segment from (-200, -40) to (-560, 60).\n\nThe pump at (-420, -30) is not on the river. The boat will drive to the nearest river point first, then follow the segment from (-200, -40) to (-560, 60). I will add `on_water` and `river_point_near` helpers and test the boat on both grass and water.\n\nThe script is being implemented as a `Vec<Spec>` where each variant represents a step. The enum covers every ordered action from boot and map to waypoint, reach, fever, pill, blackout, fight, enemy jam, clear jam, break weapon, rescue, wound, loot, claim, shop, locker, syrette, sleep, drive, monocular, ignite, tanks, mounted combat, panic, animals, boat, stealth, dart, repair, rain, patch, overdose, die, tape, ceasefire, convoy, and town burn.\n\nThe `Spec` enum now includes `Bus`, `Tracker`, `Ending(u8)`, and `Flag(&'static str)` variants. A `budget` function will return seconds per step so the test can fail if a step exceeds its time limit. Budgets are set to 100 seconds for depot driving, 140 seconds for foot reach, and 180 seconds for the long cement cache run.\n\nThe bot will sprint during reach steps by holding FOCUS. It will use the technical vehicle for long drives to the cement cache, with a 120-second budget. Budgets are set at 200 seconds for the read ending, 120 for blackout, and 45 for break. The bot regenerates stamina quickly so it can sprint for 12 seconds.\n\nStamina drains at 7 m/s during sprint and regenerates at 4.6 m/s when idle, capped at 12. The bot releases sprint once stamina drops below 0.5 and re-engages when it rises above 8.\n\nThe bot walks at 3.0 m/s while aiming and only enters ADS when shooting. Crouch speed is 0.55 of run and prone is 0.28. Eye height smoothly interpolates to 1.58 m standing, 1.02 m crouched, or 0.42 m prone using a 0.12 second tau. Look input updates yaw and clamps pitch between -1.2 and 1.2. Movement stick vectors are built from yaw sine and cosine to drive position.\n\nThe movement stick will be tested against yaw to confirm forward and right directions. Coordinates will be clamped to the -1024..1024 map bounds. A full menu system is being implemented to replace shell screens, with a Screen enum covering Title, Difficulty, Merc, Prologue, Playing, Pause, Settings, About, Dev, Mp, Touch, Attract, Shop, SleepPick, and Ending.\n\nTouch is an overlay flag rather than a screen replacement. The UI JSON will include a notice for touch-only mode. The Attract screen remains a full-screen state. Settings, Dev, and About each use tabs with row counts limited to seven. A `rows()` method computes enabled labels per screen. A test helper will build the world and verify that no screen exceeds seven rows.\n\nA `max_rows` method will be added to validate row counts per screen. A pure `rows_for` helper is also being considered so row computation needs minimal state. The menu input struct now includes pointer coordinates, click, and device fields.\n\nMenu rows will be 64 pixels tall and spaced 80 pixels apart, centered horizontally between 160 and 800. The pointer input will set the active focus index when it lands inside a row. A `glyph` helper will return the correct control icon for a given action based on device type. The dev settings page will display seven sliders per page, with left and right controls to switch pages and act or NEXT to move between them.\n\nThe test will drive inputs to reach the fire spread slider on the balance page. It will pause from playing, select Dev mode at index three, then navigate through the five dev pages to reach Balance. The slider will be placed first on that page so focus zero targets it directly.\n\nThe Balance page will hold 21 sliders across three pages of seven each. The first slider on that page is enemy accuracy, not fire spread. The test will loop down through the rows until it finds a label containing \"Fire spread\", then press right to adjust the value and verify the status tune. A Reset row was considered but rejected because it would exceed the seven-row limit; instead, Reset is triggered by act 13 from any slider position.\n\nThe Balance page will be split into four pages of seven rows each. The first three pages hold six sliders plus a Reset row, and the last page holds three sliders plus a Reset row. This keeps every page under the seven-row limit and gives the test a real UI row to navigate to for resetting.\n\nFire spread is the ninth slider on the Balance page, so it sits at index 8. That places it on page one at row two. The test will drive inputs to reach that position rather than directly setting `dev_page` and `focus`, which would be state poking.\n\nLeft and right on a slider will change its value, while the NEXT button switches pages. The test will drive inputs through `InputFrame` only, with tick handling act and button mappings into `MenuInput` via a single shared function.\n\n`apply_menu` will handle hover, focus movement, confirm, and slider adjustments. During gameplay `tick` builds `MenuInput` from `InputFrame`, but only when the screen is not `Playing`; otherwise gameplay runs unless the user presses pause. The attract idle timer counts time spent on Title, Difficulty, Merc, Prologue, Pause, Settings, About, or Mp without menu input, look, or buttons; after ten seconds it switches to Attract while saving the return screen, and any input resets the timer and returns to Title.\n\nThe attract idle timer counts time spent on the title, any shell menu, and pause. It does not count gameplay. During attract, the segment cycles through ten states every 16 seconds and loops every 160 seconds. The test will advance time in one-second steps to reach five full loops without writing saves. Any input during attract exits it immediately. Empty MenuInput counts as no input, but look on InputFrame does.\n\nThe Title screen shows New contract, Multiplayer, Settings, and About. Continue is hidden without a save and defaults to New contract. The boot sequence moves from Title to Difficulty, then Merc, then Prologue, and finally Playing. The bot confirms at each step using Enter or Space. The test repeats this four times.\n\nThe confirm action now accepts both the CONFIRM button and JUMP. The test sends a single press per frame because `just()` only triggers on the first frame of a press. The bot will send act=1 every tick during boot to skip through the menu screens quickly.\n\nThe boot sequence will complete in four ticks. Focus will be set to Normal on the Difficulty screen and Ada on the Merc screen. Confirming the Prologue row will start the game at the airstrip and finish the boot step.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd42bb6c-ad0f-452f-9929-636fe570a398-57","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs","offset":640,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3340,"output_tokens":6844,"cache_read_input_tokens":133376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"030710ed-991b-4b50-a237-f06c18daf4b2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dd42bb6c-ad0f-452f-9929-636fe570a398-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"640→fn build<T>(device: &cpal::Device, config: cpal::StreamConfig, rx: Receiver<Cmd>, channels: usize) -> anyhow::Result<cpal::Stream>\\nwhere\\n    T: cpal::SizedSample + cpal::FromSample<f32>,\\n{\\n    use cpal::traits::DeviceTrait;\\n    let mut mixer = Mixer::new(config.sample_rate as f32);\\n    let mut buf: Vec<f32> = Vec::new();\\n    let stream = device.build_output_stream::<T, _, _>(\\n        config,\\n        move |data: &mut [T], _| {\\n650→            while let Ok(c) = rx.try_recv() {\\n                match c {\\n                    Cmd::Play(p, pan, gain, delay) => mixer.play(p, pan, gain, delay),\\n                    Cmd::Master(v) => mixer.master = v,\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let frames = data.len() / channels.max(1);\\n            buf.resize(frames * 2, 0.0);\\n            mixer.render(&mut buf);\\n            for (i, frame) in data.chunks_mut(channels.max(1)).enumerate() {\\n660→                for (c, s) in frame.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n                    *s = T::from_sample(buf[i * 2 + c.min(1)]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        |e| log::warn!(\\\"audio stream error: {e}\\\"),\\n        None,\\n    )?;\\n    Ok(stream)\\n}\\n670→\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\\n        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\",\"content_concise\":\"640→fn build<T>(device: &cpal::Device, config: cpal::StreamConfig, rx: Receiver<Cmd>, channels: usize) -> anyhow::Result<cpal::Stream>\\nwhere\\n    T: cpal::SizedSample + cpal::FromSample<f32>,\\n{\\n    use cpal::traits::DeviceTrait;\\n    let mut mixer = Mixer::new(config.sample_rate as f32);\\n    let mut buf: Vec<f32> = Vec::new();\\n    let stream = device.build_output_stream::<T, _, _>(\\n        config,\\n        move |data: &mut [T], _| {\\n650→            while let Ok(c) = rx.try_recv() {\\n                match c {\\n                    Cmd::Play(p, pan, gain, delay) => mixer.play(p, pan, gain, delay),\\n                    Cmd::Master(v) => mixer.master = v,\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let frames = data.len() / channels.max(1);\\n            buf.resize(frames * 2, 0.0);\\n            mixer.render(&mut buf);\\n            for (i, frame) in data.chunks_mut(channels.max(1)).enumerate() {\\n660→                for (c, s) in frame.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n                    *s = T::from_sample(buf[i * 2 + c.min(1)]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        |e| log::warn!(\\\"audio stream error: {e}\\\"),\\n        None,\\n    )?;\\n    Ok(stream)\\n}\\n670→\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\\n        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs\",\"offset\":640,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"fn build<T>(device: &cpal::Device, config: cpal::StreamConfig, rx: Receiver<Cmd>, channels: usize) -> anyhow::Result<cpal::Stream>\\nwhere\\n    T: cpal::SizedSample + cpal::FromSample<f32>,\\n{\\n    use cpal::traits::DeviceTrait;\\n    let mut mixer = Mixer::new(config.sample_rate as f32);\\n    let mut buf: Vec<f32> = Vec::new();\\n    let stream = device.build_output_stream::<T, _, _>(\\n        config,\\n        move |data: &mut [T], _| {\\n            while let Ok(c) = rx.try_recv() {\\n                match c {\\n                    Cmd::Play(p, pan, gain, delay) => mixer.play(p, pan, gain, delay),\\n                    Cmd::Master(v) => mixer.master = v,\\n                }\\n            }\\n            let frames = data.len() / channels.max(1);\\n            buf.resize(frames * 2, 0.0);\\n            mixer.render(&mut buf);\\n            for (i, frame) in data.chunks_mut(channels.max(1)).enumerate() {\\n                for (c, s) in frame.iter_mut().enumerate() {\\n                    *s = T::from_sample(buf[i * 2 + c.min(1)]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        },\\n        |e| log::warn!(\\\"audio stream error: {e}\\\"),\\n        None,\\n    )?;\\n    Ok(stream)\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\\n        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n\",\"total_lines\":684}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"0770eb4a-4341-4452-a272-50cf314c0e72"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_69","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Music and voice functions will be inserted before the #[cfg(test)] block.\n\nMerc files will be written compactly. The game will be registered in mod.rs. A small room will go in merc.toml. world.rs will be written in one pass. Vec2 keys are Ord. f32 fields will avoid Eq derives. The Route enum will derive Copy. A world hash function will fold player state and RNG bits.\n\nThe fingerprint method will use serde_json and fnv to hash a JSON string of the world. Private RNG fields are excluded. Non-deterministic scratch data is skipped. BTreeMap keys ensure deterministic JSON ordering.\n\nRng is Clone, so deriving Clone for World is straightforward. The Gun struct will use a WeaponId enum instead of a string slice for proper serde support. A WeaponId variant will be added for each weapon type.\n\nThe Gun struct now tracks condition, wear, jammed and broken states, ammo counts, cooldown timers, clearing progress, slap status, and shot statistics. Pull_trigger will return Jammed or Dry if the weapon is broken, jammed, out of ammo, or still cooling down.\n\nPull_trigger now returns Waiting while the weapon cools down. Jamming is probabilistic: condition below 70 or a forced jam triggers it, incrementing jams and setting the flag. After firing, ammo drops, cooldown resets to 60.0 divided by RPM, and condition degrades by wear multiplied by a tune factor. If condition falls below the break threshold with a 3% chance, the weapon breaks. A jam_probability helper returns zero for condition above 70, otherwise it scales with the square of the damage ratio.\n\nClearing a jam now takes 1.2 to 2.5 seconds, scaling with weapon condition. A second reload input shortens the remaining clear time by 40% if the weapon is still jammed. Once the timer expires, the jam flag clears automatically. The reload logic also handles magazine refills when ammo is low but reserve remains.\n\nA test will verify that the second reload tap reduces the remaining clear time to about sixty percent of the pre-slap value. Break tests will tick the world. A `resolve_shot` function will handle firing hit detection.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b214079a-2a29-4f0f-afd5-568b22fd326e-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn build_standalone_room","glob":"**/scenes.rs","-A":35}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7327,"output_tokens":2238,"cache_read_input_tokens":136704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d39e5092-8fce-4970-9d52-4b30badcec19"}
