{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_98","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to fix compile errors surgically.\n\nThe surgical fixes are:\n- Rename `campaign` to `advance_campaign` and update the call at line 602.\n- Clone `tune0` in shell.rs at line 316.\n- Use `&names` in shell.rs at line 402.\n- Split the `Reach | Tracker` arms in bot_spec.\n- Split the outer pattern for `Drive | Bus` in bot_spec.\n- Copy flags before `gun_mut` in `handle_gun`, then split the RNG pull.\n\nThe `handle_gun` fix will use `std::mem::replace` to temporarily move `self.rng` out, call `gun_mut().pull()` with the moved RNG, and restore it.\n\nA cleaner `handle_gun` fix avoids `std::mem::replace`. I'll add a `gun_index()` helper to compute the slot index, then borrow the gun and RNG directly from `self` without calling `gun_mut()`.\n\nThe `handle_gun` fix is confirmed: `self.guns[i].pull(&mut self.rng, ...)` compiles because the borrow checker allows disjoint field borrows.\n\nFor `stealth_kill`, I will collect stealth targets first, then mark them. This avoids borrowing `self.stance` while iterating over `bodies`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-734136ce-36a5-47c0-8730-54e1e74e5cd9-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1465,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-734136ce-36a5-47c0-8730-54e1e74e5cd9-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","offset":380,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-734136ce-36a5-47c0-8730-54e1e74e5cd9-55","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build