01,115,32,98,121,32,121,111,117,114,32,109,101,114,99,121,59,32,100,105,97,109,111,110,100,115,32,97,115,32,99,117,114,114,101,110,99,121,32,119,105,116,104,32,97,32,116,114,97,99,107,101,114,59,32,115,97,102,101,32,104,111,117,115,101,115,59,32,118,105,115,99,101,114,97,108,32,102,105,114,115,116,45,112,101,114,115,111,110,32,104,101,97,108,105,110,103,59,32,99,97,114,32,114,101,112,97,105,114,32,97,110,105,109,97,116,105,111,110,115,59,32,103,117,97,114,100,32,112,111,115,116,115,32,111,110,32,101,118,101,114,121,32,114,111,97,100,59,32,114,101,99,111,114,100,101,100,32,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,115,32,119,105,116,104,32,105,116,115,32,118,105,108,108,97,105,110,59,32,97,32,114,101,102,117,115,97,108,32,116,111,32,111,102,102,101,114,32,97,32,103,111,111,100,32,115,105,100,101,46,32,67,111,109,109,111,110,32,99,111,109,112,108,97,105,110,116,115,32,119,101,32,100,101,115,105,103,110,32,97,114,111,117,110,100,58,32,103,117,97,114,100,32,112,111,115,116,115,32,114,101,45,109,97,110,110,105,110,103,32,116,111,111,32,102,97,115,116,44,32,108,111,110,103,32,101,109,112,116,121,32,100,114,105,118,101,115,44,32,97,110,100,32,114,101,112,101,116,105,116,105,118,101,32,109,105,115,115,105,111,110,32,115,116,114,117,99,116,117,114,101,46,32,85,115,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,97,115,32,97,32,108,105,115,116,32,111,102,32,42,107,105,110,100,115,32,111,102,32,116,104,105,110,103,115,42,44,32,110,111,116,32,97,32,115,111,117,114,99,101,32,111,102,32,99,111,110,116,101,110,116,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":18,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"# PLAN: an original first-person survival shooter inspired by Far Cry 2\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"- **Genre:** open-world first-person shooter with survival and systemic-sandbox rules (fire, wind, wear, fever, permadeath companions).\"},{\"line_number\":148,\"content\":\"- **Rafael Quintero:** tracker. Chain-smokes. Superstitious about nothing.\"},{\"line_number\":149,\"content\":\"- **Mirela Dragan:** sharpshooter, ex-Legion. Says very little.\"},{\"line_number\":283,\"content\":\"- **Visible state:** the procedural material shifts with condition (bluing, then scratched, then rust), smoke curls from the muzzle below 25, and pieces rattle. No condition number during play. The monocular and locker use words: *New, Used, Worn, Rusted, Dying.*\"},{\"line_number\":329,\"content\":\"- Dense smoke blocks AI sight (LOS check through smoke cells) and makes the player cough.\"},{\"line_number\":332,\"content\":\"- Near cells get emissive flame cones that flicker, plus GPU particles (fire, smoke, embers presets, tuned), heat distortion and flickering point lights grouped per burning patch (up to the renderer's limit of 64, nearest first).\"},{\"line_number\":335,\"content\":\"- Far fires appear as an orange glow on the smoke.\"},{\"line_number\":341,\"content\":\"- **Readable three ways:** grass sway (engine `view.wind`, `wind_angle`, `wind_gusts`, driven by the sim's wind), smoke lean, and the **red rag on your front sight**: a verlet strip (engine `rig.rs` follows-the-leader chain) that streams downwind on every weapon. This is the signature detail, so make it readable from the couch.\"},{\"line_number\":348,\"content\":\"Each NPC has a 0–1 meter. Rate = `base × distance falloff × posture (1 / 0.6 / 0.3) × tall-grass cover (0.35 when crouched in it, 0.6 standing) × light (day 1, night 0.45, beside fire 1.5, in headlights 2) × camo suit 0.7 × movement (still 0.5, sprint 1.3)`, only inside a 120° cone with line of sight (terrain, solid objects, dense smoke).\"},{\"line_number\":350,\"content\":\"Noise from `noise m` in the table creates investigations. States: *Unaware → Suspicious (walk to the spot) → Combat → Search (20 s at the last known position) → Unaware.* Radios share alerts within 80 m. A found body makes them Suspicious. Night dart missions must really work this way. **Test:** crouched in tall grass at 30 m at night stays hidden far longer than standing on a road at noon. Grass density comes from the same function the view uses, so what you see is what hides you.\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"- **Damage stages:** healthy → white steam → black smoke (−40% speed, misfires) → on fire (8 s fuse) → explodes and ignites the grass.\"},{\"line_number\":382,\"content\":\"- **Combat:** pick cover from nodes authored in stamps and from rocks and trees near them; bound while others fire; one or two flank; at most 4 enemies aim at the player at once; accuracy falls with range and with the player's speed, rises while tracking.\"},{\"line_number\":417,\"content\":\"- Zebra herds and a few antelope (quadruped body plan, engine rig) graze and flee from shots and fire. Vultures circle over corpses and smoke, so they can betray a fight or lead you to a cache.\"},{\"line_number\":581,\"content\":\"**Title (live world behind it, dusk, smoke on the horizon):** Continue, New contract, Multiplayer, Settings, About.\"},{\"line_number\":798,\"content\":\"| **M4** | Fire, wind, smoke, burn visuals, explosions, weather, AI reactions | Fire tests (§14.1). Depot fire screenshot makes you want to play |\"},{\"line_number\":818,\"content\":\"- **AI:** squad takes cover and at least one flanker repositions. Max 4 shooters at once. Morale break. Post re-mans after its timer and never in the player's sight.\"},{\"line_number\":907,\"content\":\"Far Cry 2 (Ubisoft Montreal, 2008): first-person open-world shooter in an unnamed African civil war, inspired by *Heart of Darkness*. Known for: dynamic wind-driven grass fire; weapons that degrade, jam and break; malaria managed with pills; a hand-held map and GPS instead of a HUD map; buddies who rescue you and can die permanently, sometimes by your mercy; diamonds as currency with a tracker; safe houses; visceral first-person healing; car repair animations; guard posts on every road; recorded interviews with its villain; a refusal to offer a good side. Common complaints we design around: guard posts re-manning too fast, long empty drives, and repetitive mission structure. Use this as a list of *kinds of things*, not a source of content.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d1dc7616-f9b6-43b3-a30a-95e43bb4caa1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_117","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Plan line 818 requires the AI squad to take cover and reposition at least one flanker.\n\nOnly four bodies with alert>=2 will shoot per tick. The fifth body will flank sideways instead. No morale flag exists, so survivors will simply flee.\n\nThe test will spawn six alert soldiers and verify that at most four fire per cooldown window. The update_bodies logic will cap shooters at four and move any fifth body sideways by three units per tick.\n\nMorale will be calculated by comparing alive and dead kind 1 bodies. If dead outnumber alive, survivors flee and stop shooting. The post re-mans test will check that bodies clear and re-mans after their timers expire. The flank test will run in a fresh sandbox with six bodies.\n\nSmoke will block line-of-sight. If a burning cell sits between the player and an enemy, the see value will not increase. The fire cap, smoke check, and test file are being implemented now.\n\nI will make modules public in mod.rs. I need to edit the fire section in update_bodies for the shooter cap, add water_ahead in geom, fix the boat bot, and add ceasefire on kill. The Die companion logic is fine as-is. I will write tests in focused chunks so failures are easy to diagnose. The game_keys test should run via cargo test -p pav_core.\n\nI will run only the merc and audio tests to avoid the slow starter bot suite. A camera test will be added too. The playthrough test will be named `bot_playthrough_endings`. I noticed a boot bug where `bot_input` returns confirm every tick, which could cause double-confirm issues. I am checking the startup tick order to fix this.\n\nThe boot sequence is confirmed correct: shell_tick sets Playing on the Begin tick, then advance_script runs immediately after. The map bot will hold MAP for over 0.35 seconds before moving on. Combat tests will use fresh() to skip the campaign route. A hit test was designed with the player at (200,-200) and a dummy at (200,-210), facing -z.\n\nA wall at z=-215 will block the line of sight to a dummy at z=-220. Headshot damage is 66, torso 78, and limb 86.8. The test will fire many shots at close range without ads and verify health drops. A pitch aimed at y=1.70 should target the head, though jitter may still hit the torso.\n\nThe hit test will be deterministic by setting a fixed RNG seed and firing with ads. The vertical jitter at ten meters is only about 0.025 meters, which is smaller than the head radius, so the dummy should reliably take headshot damage. The test will simply assert that health drops when the wall is absent and stays unchanged when it is present.\n\nThe exact pitch for a headshot is 0.012 radians, which should reliably hit the dummy's head at y=1.70 and deal about 66 damage. For a limb shot, the pitch is -0.112 radians, which lands on the dummy's limb at y=0.45 instead of the torso. The ray intersects the limb sphere rather than the torso sphere.\n\nThe jam test will pull a gun with condition 35 and zero wear, expecting roughly 275 jams out of 5000 shots. Each pull resets the cooldown to zero so the test drives real firing rather than skipping the cooldown check.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ffc2f5b6-1baf-4b4a-8921-c03d0101b44b-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":167,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6226,"output_tokens":2148,"cache_read_input_tokens":144640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"8ec54fd2-39a2-40ec-a814-fb2559ecadf8"}
