{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_125","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the complete merc.rs test file.\n\nPlanning audio tests and verifying module paths for buttons, World, Route, and Screen. The playthrough will be a single test. Analyzing fire spread logic: wind speed 8 should not cross the NS road boundary at x=4, while embers require speed above 8. Checking whether Screen uses debug formatting.\n\nThe origin is water, so it cannot be used for fire ignition. The test will instead place a fire at (200, -440) with wind (0, -8), sending smoke north toward the road at z=-420.\n\nThe fire front will halt at the road boundary because road cells have zero fuel. At wind speed 8, embers cannot cross the road, but speed 9 allows a 6–15 meter hop across it. For the calm test, a single ignition cell will be ticked for 30 seconds; a roughly circular spread is expected with a bounding box aspect ratio near 1.\n\nPlanning tests for fire expiration, rain suppression, and barrel ignition. The playthrough will verify tank spawning. Direct cell counts via FireMap will be used alongside World fire.\n\nThe playthrough alone will verify the cells_500 flag, so no extra test is needed for that. The test file will be kept compact. A forbidden-string check is being added to reject placeholder or placeholder-like text.\n\nThe forbidden-string check will allow \"Far Cry 2\" only when it appears on a line prefixed with \"Source:\". The scan targets fiction lines and merc source files.\n\nThe forbidden-string scan will walk the merc directory. A run.sh script and a COVERAGE constant are planned. The playthrough panic message will list missing flags against the expected set. The union of all three routes must contain every flag, including route-specific ones like ending_burn, ending_read, and ending_chair.\n\nMapping flags to their routes: pill_taken is human and chair, blackout and companion_overdosed are read, companion_patched is human, and companion_died is chair. All other flags are shared across every route.\n\nEach route must finish with its ending flag. The union of all flags across every run must equal the full set, and any missing flag will panic with its name. Both seeds are required to complete. The play() function will return the set of flags it collected. The total workload is roughly 144,000 ticks, so the test should finish in about ten to sixty seconds.\n\nThe test will be a single cargo test run with no explicit timeout; any stalled route will panic. Vehicle yaw rate fixes are deferred until the test runs. Helpers will be placed at the top of the file. Sandbox mode correctly skips campaign logic. Movement tests will verify forward speed, yaw rotation, crouch eye height, and stamina decay.\n\nThe jam-clear test will verify that a jammed pistol reloads within 1.2 to 2.5 seconds, with the second tap reducing remaining clear time by roughly sixty percent. The enemy will be tested in World to confirm it stops firing after jamming. A syrette-heal test will restore about fifty health over two seconds, capped at one hundred, and assert the syrette flag.\n\nThe syrette test will restore fifty health over one and a half seconds, capped at one hundred, and assert the syrette flag when the dose hits zero. A wound-heal test will restore forty health over four seconds from fifteen, asserting the wound_gunshot flag. The rescue test will verify that companion.rescue_spent becomes true after a companion dies and is revived, but second death leaves health at zero because sleep cannot reset the spent flag in sandbox mode.\n\nThe blackout test will set pills to zero, fever_state to two, fever_attack to fifty-nine, diamonds to forty, and place the player away from the safe house. After two ticks the player should have fifty health and thirty-two diamonds at the nearest safe location.\n\nFever warning will trigger at one-tenth of the interval before attack, setting the warned flag without entering blackout. The tracker test compares rates at ten and fifty meters from a cache. A zero-diamond purchase attempt must fail and leave gun counts unchanged. Vehicle tests include slope climbing on a ridge, pitch increase during throttle, and roll decay. Stage damage reduces speed to smoke at stage two. Exploding a vehicle sets health to zero, starts an eight-second fuse, and ignites. Repairing a seat requires holding interact for six seconds near the vehicle.\n\nBoat tests will verify speed zero on grass and movement on water. NPC movement along the road and seat cycling are also planned. Mounting a primary weapon at seat two will set the mounted_gun flag. A save/load roundtrip test will compare diamonds, position, flags, and fingerprints after JSON serialization.\n\nA Sim::new boot test will verify the key and zero history_seconds. The music gain test computes RMS to confirm the gain ratio.\n\nThe music gain test asserts the quiet track's RMS is exactly ten percent of the full track's RMS. A new test verifies that different gun patches and different voice actors produce distinct audio output.\n\nA crackle test will verify that higher crackle counts produce more energy. The suite is complete and ready to write. A flanker test will place six soldiers with high ammo and full condition, tick for one second, and assert that at most four guns fire.\n\nThe flanker test will place six soldiers so the first four shoot and the last two flank. A morale test will place three dead bodies and one alive, tick for one second, and assert that the alive body moves forward while its gun stays idle. A post_reman test will position the player south of the post facing north; because the dot product exceeds 0.4 and distance is under 180, maybe_reman should not mark.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-189a4c99-0192-4de1-9174-43a84abc212c-122","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":250,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1387,"output_tokens":3592,"cache_read_input_tokens":159744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"09e24cae-0203-4903-9244-d86d6219ad79"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-189a4c99-0192-4de1-9174-43a84abc212c-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→pub fn safe_houses() -> [(f32, f32); 3] {\\n    [place(\\\"Pump House\\\"), place(\\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\"), place(\\\"Boat Shed\\\")]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_safe(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    safe_houses().into_iter().min_by(|a, b| dist(x, z, a.0, a.1).total_cmp(&dist(x, z, b.0, b.1))).unwrap_or((170.0, 470.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Detection multiplier from posture, grass, light and motion. Distance falloff is separate.\\n/// Crouched in tall grass at night, still: 0.6 * 0.35 * 0.45 * 0.5.\\n260→/// Standing on a road at noon, still: 1 * 1 * 1 * 0.5.\\npub fn exposure(posture: f32, grass: f32, light: f32, motion: f32) -> f32 {\\n    posture * grass * light * motion\\n}\\n\\npub fn grass_factor(x: f32, z: f32, crouched: bool) -> f32 {\\n    if !tall_grass(x, z) {\\n        1.0\\n    } else if crouched {\\n        0.35\\n270→    } else {\\n        0.6\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn wrap_angle(a: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let pi = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    (a + pi).rem_euclid(pi * 2.0) - pi\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"250→pub fn safe_houses() -> [(f32, f32); 3] {\\n    [place(\\\"Pump House\\\"), place(\\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\"), place(\\\"Boat Shed\\\")]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_safe(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    safe_houses().into_iter().min_by(|a, b| dist(x, z, a.0, a.1).total_cmp(&dist(x, z, b.0, b.1))).unwrap_or((170.0, 470.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Detection multiplier from posture, grass, light and motion. Distance falloff is separate.\\n/// Crouched in tall grass at night, still: 0.6 * 0.35 * 0.45 * 0.5.\\n260→/// Standing on a road at noon, still: 1 * 1 * 1 * 0.5.\\npub fn exposure(posture: f32, grass: f32, light: f32, motion: f32) -> f32 {\\n    posture * grass * light * motion\\n}\\n\\npub fn grass_factor(x: f32, z: f32, crouched: bool) -> f32 {\\n    if !tall_grass(x, z) {\\n        1.0\\n    } else if crouched {\\n        0.35\\n270→    } else {\\n        0.6\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn wrap_angle(a: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let pi = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    (a + pi).rem_euclid(pi * 2.0) - pi\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs\",\"offset\":250,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"pub fn safe_houses() -> [(f32, f32); 3] {\\n    [place(\\\"Pump House\\\"), place(\\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\"), place(\\\"Boat Shed\\\")]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_safe(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    safe_houses().into_iter().min_by(|a, b| dist(x, z, a.0, a.1).total_cmp(&dist(x, z, b.0, b.1))).unwrap_or((170.0, 470.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Detection multiplier from posture, grass, light and motion. Distance falloff is separate.\\n/// Crouched in tall grass at night, still: 0.6 * 0.35 * 0.45 * 0.5.\\n/// Standing on a road at noon, still: 1 * 1 * 1 * 0.5.\\npub fn exposure(posture: f32, grass: f32, light: f32, motion: f32) -> f32 {\\n    posture * grass * light * motion\\n}\\n\\npub fn grass_factor(x: f32, z: f32, crouched: bool) -> f32 {\\n    if !tall_grass(x, z) {\\n        1.0\\n    } else if crouched {\\n        0.35\\n    } else {\\n        0.6\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn wrap_angle(a: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let pi = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    (a + pi).rem_euclid(pi * 2.0) - pi\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":284}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3ff75531-b37a-4a81-9b2e-f1ca15bc5a7e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_126","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The standing road noon value is 0.\n\nSmoke and noise tests are planned. A body at 50m with AR noise should trigger an alert. A body at 20m near a grass midpoint should show no smoke rise versus normal visibility increase. The soldier helper will use Gun::new.\n\nA same-seed prefix hash test will verify deterministic campaign fingerprints. The playthrough test will run last so other failures surface first. Parallel test threads are acceptable since the long simulation should not exhaust memory.\n\nThe water_ahead function's RIVER indexing and backward branch are verified safe. The forward path returns correctly on loop exit or at the start. Tests will be written next.\n\nThe full test file will be written with write(). Audio tests will be added via search_replace. The playthrough test will print progress to stderr on each goal change so hangs are easier to debug. Drive seat logic is being double-checked: begin sets seat=1 for kind==0, and use_vehicle cycles the seat before bot_drive runs.\n\nThe Drive seat logic is confirmed. If the seat is already 1, bot_drive runs immediately. Otherwise the bot presses USE to cycle to seat 1 and snaps the player to the vehicle at the junction. After the Bus teleports the player to town with seat 0, the next Drive task begins at the junction and drives toward SH2.\n\nA bug was found in the Sleep task. When the player is already seated in a vehicle, the bot presses USE every tick to cycle through seats. This oscillates forever and prevents the task from ever exiting to interact with the safe house.\n\nThe Sleep task bug is resolved by pressing USE only once per tick while the seat is not zero. This cycles the seat through 1 and 2 before settling at 0, where the bot then holds INTERACT to trigger sleep.\n\nThe Sleep task fix is confirmed. Pressing USE only once per tick while the seat is not zero cycles through seats 1 and 2 before settling at 0, where the bot holds INTERACT to trigger sleep. The repair sets the seat to 0 in begin so the bot can hold INTERACT without oscillating. The Mounted task also behaves correctly: when transitioning from Drive, the bot presses USE and PRIMARY every tick, cycling the seat and holding primary on the way to seat 2.\n\nClaim is confirmed on foot at SH1 before any vehicle. Map step logic is verified: holding MAP for over 0.35 seconds triggers the menu, and INTERACT or act==1 sets a waypoint while the map is raised. Reach GPS requires moving more than 25 meters from the step origin and arriving within 10 meters of the target; the origin is set to the airstrip, so walking to the town gate satisfies both conditions. The test file will be written next, with fixes applied if the playthrough fails.\n\nFever could trigger during long drives because the interval is 900 seconds and routes take roughly 400–700 seconds. The human takes a pill to reset the timer, but the remaining travel plus ending time may still exceed 900 seconds of real time.\n\nIf fever strikes during the ending read, the bot will not take pills and the player remains in attack mode. The step timer continues counting, so the ending still completes normally. A blackout would teleport the player but would not reset the step counter.\n\nIf fever triggers during a drive, the player teleports to the safe house and leaves the vehicle behind, which causes the drive task to fail.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim compiles. Next I’ll lock the boat to the channel, then add tests that drive the real `World` and `Gun` code."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8c030c91-886e-43f4-9f68-4321fd94239c-123","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs","old_string":"    #[test]\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {","new_string":"    fn rms(samples: &[f32]) -> f32 {\n        let n = samples.len().max(1) as f32;\n        (samples.iter().map(|s| s * s).sum::<f32>() / n).sqrt()\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn music_bus_tracks_the_gain() {\n        let quiet = render_music(MUSIC_GAIN, 1.0, 8_000.0);\n        let full = render_music(1.0, 1.0, 8_000.0);\n        assert!(quiet.iter().all(|s| s.is_finite()));\n        let ratio = rms(&quiet) / rms(&full);\n        assert!((ratio - 0.10).abs() < 0.01, \"rms ratio {ratio}\");\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn gun_families_voices_and_crackle_differ() {\n        let pistol = render_patch(gun_patch(\"pistol\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\n        let shotgun = render_patch(gun_patch(\"shotgun\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\n        let rifle = render_patch(gun_patch(\"rifle\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\n        assert_ne!(pistol, shotgun);\n        assert_ne!(pistol, rifle);\n        let ada = render_voice(\"Ada Okoro\", \"The grass burns anyway\", 8_000.0);\n        let tomek = render_voice(\"Tomek Wrona\", \"The grass burns anyway\", 8_000.0);\n        assert_ne!(ada, tomek);\n        assert!(ada.iter().any(|s| s.abs() > 0.01));\n        assert!(rms(&render_crackle(400, 8_000.0)) > rms(&render_crackle(1, 8_000.0)));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8c030c91-886e-43f4-9f68-4321fd94239c-124","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs","new_string":"//! Jam Cry. These tests call the shipped simulation: `World::tick`, `Gun::pull`, `FireMap::tick`.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\nuse std::path::Path;\n\nuse pav_core::games::merc::fire::FireMap;\nuse pav_core::games::merc::geom::{self, exposure};\nuse pav_core::games::merc::gun::{Gun, WeaponId, clear_seconds};\nuse pav_core::games::merc::net::{Link, client_apply, host_publish};\nuse pav_core::games::merc::shell::{Device, MenuInput, glyph};\nuse pav_core::games::merc::world::{Body, Route, Screen, World, fiction_lines};\nuse pav_core::games::merc::Merc;\nuse pav_core::input::buttons;\nuse pav_core::rng::Rng;\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\n\nconst DT: f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;\n\nfn press(bit: u32) -> InputFrame {\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n    f.held = bit;\n    f.pressed = bit;\n    f\n}\n\nfn hold(bit: u32) -> InputFrame {\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n    f.held = bit;\n    f\n}\n\nfn soldier(x: f32, z: f32, alert: u8) -> Body {\n    let mut gun = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\n    gun.ammo = 400;\n    gun.reserve = 400;\n    gun.condition = 100.0;\n    Body {\n        kind: 1,\n        x,\n        z,\n        yaw: 0.0,\n        hp: 80.0,\n        alive: true,\n        alert,\n        gun,\n        see: 0.0,\n        poison: 0.0,\n        burn: 0.0,\n        doomed: false,\n        flee: 0.0,\n    }\n}\n\nfn run(w: &mut World, input: &InputFrame, seconds: f32) {\n    let n = (seconds / DT) as i32;\n    for _ in 0..n {\n        w.tick(input, DT);\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn scene_boots_and_history_is_off() {\n    for seed in [1u64, 2, 9] {\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(Merc::KEY, seed).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(sim.play().unwrap().key(), \"merc\");\n        assert_eq!(sim.config.history_seconds, 0.0);\n        for _ in 0..8 {\n            sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\n        }\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\n        assert_eq!(status[\"title\"], \"Jam Cry\");\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn same_seed_matches_across_a_save() {\n    let mut a = World::fresh(11);\n    let mut b = World::fresh(11);\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\n    f.look.x = 0.01;\n    for _ in 0..90 {\n        a.tick(&f, DT);\n        b.tick(&f, DT);\n    }\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), b.fingerprint());\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&a.save_json()).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(loaded.fingerprint(), a.fingerprint());\n    a.tick(&f, DT);\n    let mut loaded = loaded;\n    loaded.tick(&f, DT);\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), loaded.fingerprint());\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn look_and_stick_follow_yaw() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\n    let z0 = w.z;\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\n    run(&mut w, &f, 1.0);\n    assert!(w.z < z0 - 3.0, \"forward at yaw 0 moves north, z {z0} -> {}\", w.z);\n    w.yaw = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;\n    let x0 = w.x;\n    run(&mut w, &f, 1.0);\n    assert!(w.x > x0 + 3.0, \"yaw east, x {x0} -> {}\", w.x);\n    let mut look = InputFrame::default();\n    look.look.y = 5.0;\n    w.tick(&look, DT);\n    assert!(w.pitch <= 1.15 + 1e-3);\n    look.look.y = -5.0;\n    w.tick(&look, DT);\n    assert!(w.pitch >= -1.15 - 1e-3);\n    let mut crouch = hold(buttons::CROUCH);\n    crouch.move_dir.y = 0.0;\n    run(&mut w, &crouch, 1.0);\n    assert!(w.stance == 1 && (w.eye - 1.02).abs() < 0.08, \"eye {}\", w.eye);\n    let mut prone = hold(buttons::CRAWL);\n    run(&mut w, &prone, 1.0);\n    assert!(w.stance == 2 && w.eye < 0.6, \"eye {}\", w.eye);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn hits_use_zones_and_walls_block() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\n    w.yaw = 0.0;\n    w.pitch = ((1.70 - w.eye) / 10.0).atan();\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 10.0, 100.0);\n    let mut f = hold(buttons::PRIMARY | buttons::SECONDARY);\n    f.pressed = buttons::PRIMARY;\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\n    let hp = w.bodies[0].hp;\n    assert!(hp < 100.0 - 50.0, \"headshot damage, hp {hp}\");\n    w.bodies.clear();\n    w.guns[0].cooldown = 0.0;\n    w.pitch = ((0.45 - w.eye) / 10.0).atan();\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 10.0, 100.0);\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\n    let limb = w.bodies[0].hp;\n    assert!(limb > 80.0 && limb < 90.0, \"limb damage, hp {limb}\");\n    w.bodies.clear();\n    w.guns[0].cooldown = 0.0;\n    w.pitch = 0.0;\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 20.0, 100.0);\n    w.add_wall([w.x - 2.0, 0.0, w.z - 16.0], [w.x + 2.0, 3.0, w.z - 14.0]);\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].hp, 100.0, \"wall blocks the ray\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear() {\n    let mut gun = Gun::new(WeaponId::Pistol);\n    gun.condition = 35.0;\n    gun.wear = 0.0;\n    gun.ammo = 100_000;\n    gun.reserve = 100_000;\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(35);\n    let mut jams = 0u32;\n    for _ in 0..5000 {\n        gun.cooldown = 0.0;\n        gun.jammed = false;\n        if gun.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0) == pav_core::games::merc::gun::Pull::Jammed {\n            jams += 1;\n            gun.ammo += 1;\n        }\n    }\n    assert!(jams > 5000 / 30 && jams < 5000 / 12, \"jams {jams}\");\n    let mut stuck = Gun::new(WeaponId::Pistol);\n    stuck.condition = 40.0;\n    stuck.force_jam = true;\n    stuck.ammo = 10;\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(1);\n    assert_eq!(stuck.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 1.0, 8.0), pav_core::games::merc::gun::Pull::Jammed);\n    let before = stuck.ammo;\n    stuck.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 1.0, 8.0);\n    assert_eq!(stuck.ammo, before, \"a jam spends no round\");\n    stuck.tap_reload();\n    let clear = stuck.clear_left;\n    let expect = clear_seconds(40.0);\n    assert!((clear - expect).abs() < 0.01 && clear >= 1.2 && clear <= 2.5, \"{clear}\");\n    stuck.tap_reload();\n    assert!((stuck.clear_left - clear * 0.6).abs() < 0.02, \"{}\", stuck.clear_left);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(8);\n    w.guns[0] = Gun::new(WeaponId::Smg);\n    w.guns[0].condition = 5.0;\n    w.guns[0].wear = 0.0;\n    w.guns[0].ammo = 9_999;\n    w.guns[0].reserve = 9_999;\n    let fire = hold(buttons::PRIMARY | buttons::SECONDARY);\n    let mut broke = false;\n    for _ in 0..(90.0 / DT) as i32 {\n        if w.guns[0].jammed {\n            w.tick(&press(buttons::RELOAD), DT);\n        } else {\n            w.tick(&fire, DT);\n        }\n        if w.guns[0].broken || w.flags.contains(\"weapon_broke\") {\n            broke = true;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    assert!(broke, \"condition 5 should break inside 90s\");\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(9);\n    let mut g = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\n    g.condition = 5.0;\n    g.wear = 0.0;\n    g.ammo = 400;\n    let mut body = soldier(w.x, w.z - 8.0, 2);\n    body.gun = g;\n    w.bodies.push(body);\n    let mut saw_jam = false;\n    let mut shots_at_jam = 0u32;\n    for _ in 0..(20.0 / DT) as i32 {\n        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\n        if w.flags.contains(\"enemy_jam\") {\n            saw_jam = true;\n            shots_at_jam = w.bodies[0].gun.shots;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    assert!(saw_jam, \"soldier should jam\");\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].gun.shots, shots_at_jam, \"a jammed soldier stops firing\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks() {\n    let mut map = FireMap::default();\n    let origin = (200.0f32, -200.0f32);\n    assert!(map.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 30.0, 0.0));\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(2);\n    let wind = pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(8.0, 0.0);\n    for _ in 0..60 {\n        map.tick(1.0, wind, 0.9, 30.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\n    }\n    let (down, up) = map.reach(origin, wind);\n    assert!(up > 0.0, \"upwind reach {up}, down {down}\");\n    assert!(down >= up * 3.0, \"down {down} up {up}\");\n\n    let mut calm = FireMap::default();\n    calm.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 40.0, 0.0);\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(3);\n    for _ in 0..40 {\n        calm.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::ZERO, 0.9, 40.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\n    }\n    let mut min_x = i32::MAX;\n    let mut max_x = i32::MIN;\n    let mut min_z = i32::MAX;\n    let mut max_z = i32::MIN;\n    for c in calm.cells.keys() {\n        min_x = min_x.min(c.0);\n        max_x = max_x.max(c.0);\n        min_z = min_z.min(c.1);\n        max_z = max_z.max(c.1);\n    }\n    let dx = (max_x - min_x).max(1) as f32;\n    let dz = (max_z - min_z).max(1) as f32;\n    let aspect = dx.max(dz) / dx.min(dz);\n    assert!(aspect < 2.5, \"calm scar aspect {aspect} dx {dx} dz {dz}\");\n\n    let mut blocked = FireMap::default();\n    let south = (200.0f32, -440.0f32);\n    assert!(!geom::on_road(south.0, south.1));\n    blocked.ignite_at(south.0, south.1, 20.0, 0.0);\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(4);\n    for _ in 0..30 {\n        blocked.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(0.0, -8.0), 0.9, 20.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\n    }\n    let crossed = blocked.cells.keys().any(|c| {\n        let (x, z) = geom::cell_center(*c);\n        z < -416.0 && (z + 420.0).abs() > 4.0 && x > 180.0 && x < 220.0\n    });\n    assert!(!crossed, \"speed 8 does not jump the road\");\n\n    let mut ember = FireMap::default();\n    ember.ignite_at(south.0, south.1, 20.0, 0.0);\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(5);\n    for _ in 0..20 {\n        ember.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(0.0, -12.0), 0.9, 20.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\n    }\n    let hopped = ember.cells.keys().any(|c| geom::cell_center(*c).1 < -410.0);\n    assert!(hopped, \"wind above 8 can throw an ember across the road\");\n\n    let mut ash = FireMap::default();\n    ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 1.0, 0.0);\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(6);\n    ash.tick(2.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::ZERO, 0.0, 1.0, 10.0, false, &mut rng);\n    assert!(!ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 5.0, 10.0), \"burnt ground refuses a new fire\");\n    assert!(ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 5.0, 10.0 + 2880.0));\n\n    let mut wet = FireMap::default();\n    wet.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 10.0, 0.0);\n    let n = wet.tick(0.1, wind, 0.9, 10.0, 0.0, true, &mut rng);\n    assert!(n > 0 && wet.burning_count() == 0);\n\n    let mut disk = FireMap::default();\n    let lit = disk.ignite_disk(origin.0, origin.1, 6.0, 10.0, 0.0);\n    assert!(lit > 8, \"barrel disk lit {lit}\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn exposure_smoke_and_noise() {\n    let night = exposure(0.6, 0.35, 0.45, 0.5);\n    let noon = exposure(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5);\n    assert!((night - 0.04725).abs() < 1e-5);\n    assert!((noon - 0.5).abs() < 1e-5);\n    assert!(noon / night > 10.0);\n\n    let mut quiet = World::fresh(1);\n    quiet.bodies.push(soldier(quiet.x, quiet.z - 20.0, 0));\n    let mut loud = quiet.clone();\n    let mid = ((quiet.x + quiet.bodies[0].x) * 0.5, (quiet.z + quiet.bodies[0].z) * 0.5);\n    assert!(quiet.fire.ignite_at(mid.0, mid.1, 30.0, quiet.minutes));\n    run(&mut quiet, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\n    run(&mut loud, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\n    assert!(loud.bodies[0].see > quiet.bodies[0].see + 0.05, \"smoke {} open {}\", quiet.bodies[0].see, loud.bodies[0].see);\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\n    w.guns[0] = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\n    w.bodies.push(soldier(w.x + 50.0, w.z, 0));\n    w.tick(&press(buttons::PRIMARY), DT);\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].alert, 1, \"a loud shot makes them suspicious\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\n    for i in 0..6 {\n        w.bodies.push(soldier(w.x + i as f32 * 3.0, w.z - 12.0, 2));\n    }\n    let x5 = w.bodies[5].x;\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\n    let firing = w.bodies.iter().filter(|b| b.gun.shots > 0).count();\n    assert!(firing <= 4, \"shooters {firing}\");\n    assert!(w.bodies[5].x > x5 + 1.0, \"the extra soldier flanks\");\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\n    for i in 0..4 {\n        let mut b = soldier(w.x + i as f32, w.z - 8.0, 2);\n        if i < 3 {\n            b.alive = false;\n            b.hp = 0.0;\n        }\n        w.bodies.push(b);\n    }\n    let x = w.bodies[3].x;\n    let shots = w.bodies[3].gun.shots;\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\n    assert!(w.bodies[3].x > x + 2.0, \"morale sends the last soldier away\");\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[3].gun.shots, shots);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\n    let (px, pz) = geom::place(\"Kilo 38\");\n    w.post_clear = true;\n    w.post_reman_at = w.minutes - 1.0;\n    w.x = px;\n    w.z = pz + 30.0;\n    w.yaw = 0.0;\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\n    assert!(!w.flags.contains(\"post_remanned\"), \"looking at the post holds it\");\n    w.yaw = std::f32::consts::PI;\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"post_remanned\"));\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn fever_pills_blackout_and_healing() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\n    w.fever_t = w.tune.fever_interval - 0.05;\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"fever_warned\") && w.fever_state == 1);\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::PILLS), 3.0);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"pill_taken\") && w.fever_state == 0);\n    assert_eq!(w.pills, 2);\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\n    w.pills = 0;\n    w.fever_state = 2;\n    w.fever_attack = 59.0;\n    w.diamonds = 40;\n    w.x = 200.0;\n    w.z = -200.0;\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"blackout\"));\n    assert_eq!(w.hp, 50.0);\n    assert_eq!(w.diamonds, 32);\n    let safe = geom::nearest_safe(200.0, -200.0);\n    assert!(geom::dist(w.x, w.z, safe.0, safe.1) < 1.0);\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\n    w.hp = 40.0;\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::HEAL), 2.0);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"syrette\"));\n    assert!(w.hp > 90.0, \"hp {}\", w.hp);\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\n    w.hp = 15.0;\n    w.wound = 1;\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::HEAL), 4.2);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"wound_gunshot\"));\n    assert!((w.hp - 40.0).abs() < 1.0, \"hp {}\", w.hp);\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(5);\n    w.hp = 0.0;\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 4.0);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"player_rescued\") && w.hp >= 50.0);\n    assert!(w.companions.iter().any(|c| c.rescue_spent));\n    let blob = w.save_json();\n    w.hp = 0.0;\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 4.0);\n    assert!(!w.companions.iter().any(|c| c.alive && !c.rescue_spent && !c.down) || w.hp < 10.0);\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&blob).unwrap();\n    assert!(loaded.flags.contains(\"player_rescued\"));\n    assert!(loaded.companions.iter().any(|c| c.rescue_spent));\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn vehicles_climb_break_and_float() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\n    w.ride.kind = 1;\n    w.ride.seat = 1;\n    w.ride.x = 200.0;\n    w.ride.z = -520.0;\n    w.x = 200.0;\n    w.z = -520.0;\n    w.ride.health = 100.0;\n    let mut drive = InputFrame::default();\n    drive.axes.y = 1.0;\n    drive.axes.x = 0.0;\n    w.ride.yaw = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;\n    run(&mut w, &drive, 2.0);\n    assert!(w.ride.pitch > 0.01, \"pitch {}\", w.ride.pitch);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"technical_driven\"));\n    w.ride.roll = 0.3;\n    w.tick(&drive, DT);\n    assert!(w.ride.roll < 0.3);\n\n    w.ride.health = 100.0;\n    w.ride.stage = 0;\n    w.hurt_vehicle(50.0);\n    assert!(w.ride.stage >= 1, \"stage {}\", w.ride.stage);\n    w.hurt_vehicle(80.0);\n    assert_eq!(w.ride.stage, 3);\n    run(&mut w, &drive, 9.0);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"ignite_vehicle\") || w.ride.stage == 4);\n\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\n    w.ride.kind = 1;\n    w.ride.seat = 0;\n    w.ride.health = 30.0;\n    w.ride.stage = 2;\n    w.ride.x = w.x;\n    w.ride.z = w.z;\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::INTERACT), 6.5);\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\"repair_done\"));\n    assert!(w.ride.health >= 70.0);\n\n    let mut dry = World::fresh(3);\n    dry.ride.kind = 2;\n    dry.ride.seat = 1;\n    dry.ride.x = 200.0;\n    dry.ride.z = -200.0;\n    dry.x = 200.0;\n    dry.z = -200.0;\n    assert!(!geom::deep_water(200.0, -200.0));\n    let mut throttle = InputFrame::default();\n    throttle.axes.y = 1.0;\n    run(&mut dry, &throttle, 1.0);\n    assert!(dry.ride.speed.abs() < 0.2, \"boat on grass {}\", dry.ride.speed);\n\n    let (wx, wz) = geom::nearest_water(0.0, 0.0);\n    let mut wet = World::fresh(4);\n    wet.ride.kind = 2;\n    wet.ride.seat = 1;\n    wet.ride.x = wx;\n    wet.ride.z = wz;\n    wet.x = wx;\n    wet.z = wz;\n    let (tx, tz) = geom::water_ahead(wx, wz, 40.0);\n    wet.ride.yaw = geom::yaw_toward(wx, wz, tx, tz);\n    run(&mut wet, &throttle, 2.0);\n    assert!(wet.flags.contains(\"boat_driven\"), \"dist {} deep {}\", wet.ride.dist, geom::deep_water(wet.ride.x, wet.ride.z));\n\n    wet.ride.npc = true;\n    let z0 = wet.ride.z;\n    run(&mut wet, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\n    assert!((wet.ride.x - wx).abs() > 0.5 || (wet.ride.z - z0).abs() > 0.5);\n\n    let seat = wet.ride.seat;\n    wet.tick(&press(buttons::USE), DT);\n    assert_ne!(wet.ride.seat, seat);\n    wet.ride.seat = 2;\n    wet.tick(&hold(buttons::PRIMARY), DT);\n    assert!(wet.flags.contains(\"mounted_gun\"));\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn shop_tracker_and_shell() {\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\n    w.diamonds = 0;\n    let guns = w.guns.len();\n    assert!(!w.try_buy());\n    assert_eq!(w.guns.len(), guns);\n    assert_eq!(w.diamonds, 0);\n\n    w.tracker_cache = (w.x + 10.0, w.z);\n    let near = w.tracker_rate();\n    w.tracker_cache = (w.x + 50.0, w.z);\n    let far = w.tracker_rate();\n    assert!(near > far && far > 0.0, \"{near} vs {far}\");\n\n    let mut w = World::campaign(2, Route::Human);\n    assert!(w.rows().len() <= 7);\n    let screens = [\n        Screen::Title, Screen::Difficulty, Screen::Merc, Screen::Prologue, Screen::Pause, Screen::Settings, Screen::About,\n        Screen::Dev, Screen::Mp, Screen::Attract,\n    ];\n    for screen in screens {\n        w.screen = screen;\n        for tab in 0..6 {\n            w.tab = tab;\n            for page in 0..6 {\n                w.page = page;\n                assert!(w.rows().len() <= 7, \"{screen:?} tab {tab} page {page} {:?}\", w.rows());\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    w.screen = Screen::Difficulty;\n    w.focus = 0;\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { up: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\n    assert_eq!(w.focus, 2);\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { back: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Title);\n\n    w.focus = 0;\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { pointer: Some((400.0, 300.0)), ..MenuInput::default() });\n    assert_eq!(w.focus, 1);\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { pointer: Some((400.0, 230.0)), click: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Difficulty);\n\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\"confirm\", Device::Gamepad, false), \"Cross\");\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\"confirm\", Device::Gamepad, true), \"A\");\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\"fire\", Device::Keyboard, false), \"LMB\");\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\"reload\", Device::Gamepad, false), \"Square\");\n\n    w.screen = Screen::Dev;\n    w.tab = 5;\n    w.page = 1;\n    w.focus = 2;\n    let before = w.tune.fire_spread;\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { right: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\n    assert!(w.tune.fire_spread > before, \"{} -> {}\", before, w.tune.fire_spread);\n    w.page = 3;\n    w.focus = 3;\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { confirm: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\n    assert!((w.tune.fire_spread - w.tune0.fire_spread).abs() < 1e-4);\n\n    let mut w = World::campaign(3, Route::Human);\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 9.0);\n    assert_ne!(w.screen, Screen::Attract);\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.2);\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Attract);\n    let saves = w.saves_written;\n    for _ in 0..800 {\n        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\n    }\n    assert!(w.attract_loops >= 5, \"loops {}\", w.attract_loops);\n    assert_eq!(w.attract_seen, (1u16 << 10) - 1, \"seen {:b}\", w.attract_seen);\n    assert_eq!(w.saves_written, saves);\n\n    let mut w = World::campaign(4, Route::Human);\n    let mut seen = vec![format!(\"{:?}\", w.screen)];\n    for bit in [buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP, buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP] {\n        w.tick(&press(bit), DT);\n        seen.push(format!(\"{:?}\", w.screen));\n    }\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Playing, \"{seen:?}\");\n    assert!(seen.windows(2).all(|p| p[0] != p[1]), \"{seen:?}\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn fiction_has_no_source_names_and_no_audio_files() {\n    let banned = [\n        \"jackal\", \"ufll\", \"apr\", \"pala\", \"mosate\", \"bowa\", \"leboa\", \"oluwagembi\", \"mike's bar\", \"marty\", \"alencar\",\n        \"warren clyde\", \"paul ferenc\", \"hyppolite\", \"xianyong\", \"josip\", \"hakim\", \"bilders\", \"quarbani\", \"voorhees\",\n        \"todo\", \"tbd\", \"placeholder\", \"lorem\",\n    ];\n    for line in fiction_lines() {\n        let low = line.to_lowercase();\n        if low.contains(\"far cry 2\") {\n            assert!(line.contains(\"Source:\"), \"{line}\");\n        }\n        for word in banned {\n            assert!(!low.contains(word), \"{word} in {line}\");\n        }\n    }\n    let root = Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"src/games/merc\");\n    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(&root).unwrap() {\n        let path = entry.unwrap().path();\n        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(&path).unwrap_or_default().to_lowercase();\n        for word in banned {\n            assert!(!text.contains(word), \"{word} in {}\", path.display());\n        }\n    }\n    let engine = Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../..\");\n    let mut audio = Vec::new();\n    walk_audio(&engine, &mut audio);\n    assert!(audio.is_empty(), \"shipped audio files: {audio:?}\");\n}\n\nfn walk_audio(dir: &Path, out: &mut Vec<String>) {\n    let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(dir) else { return };\n    for entry in rd.flatten() {\n        let path = entry.path();\n        if path.file_name().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\"target\") {\n            continue;\n        }\n        if path.is_dir() {\n            walk_audio(&path, out);\n        } else if let Some(ext) = path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) {\n            if matches!(ext, \"wav\" | \"mp3\" | \"ogg\") {\n                out.push(path.display().to_string());\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn net_loopback_shares_one_fire_cell() {\n    let mut host = World::fresh(1);\n    let mut client = World::fresh(2);\n    assert!(host.fire.ignite_at(200.0, -200.0, 10.0, host.minutes));\n    let mut link = Link::new(7, 0.15, 0.0, 0.0);\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, false);\n    assert!(link.max_bytes < 1200);\n    for _ in 0..10 {\n        link.advance(0.1);\n    }\n    let bodies = link.poll();\n    assert!(bodies.iter().any(|b| b.contains(\"\\\"t\\\":\\\"fire\\\"\")));\n    client_apply(&mut client, &bodies);\n    let shared = host.fire.cells.keys().any(|c| client.fire.cells.get(c).is_some_and(|cell| cell.burning));\n    assert!(shared, \"host and client should share a burning cell within 1s\");\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, true);\n    assert_eq!(link.finishes, 1);\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, true);\n    assert_eq!(link.finishes, 1);\n\n    let mut lossy = Link::new(1, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n    lossy.send(false, \"{\\\"t\\\":\\\"ping\\\"}\".into());\n    lossy.advance(0.1);\n    assert!(lossy.poll().is_empty());\n    lossy.send(true, \"{\\\"t\\\":\\\"ping\\\"}\".into());\n    lossy.advance(0.1);\n    assert_eq!(lossy.poll().len(), 1);\n}\n\nconst COVERAGE: &[&str] = &[\n    \"map_raised\", \"waypoint_set\", \"gps_followed\", \"monocular_tag\", \"wind_rag\", \"jam_cleared\", \"enemy_jam\", \"weapon_broke\",\n    \"weapon_bought\", \"locker_used\", \"syrette\", \"wound_gunshot\", \"wound_shrapnel\", \"wound_burn\", \"wound_fall\", \"wound_tourniquet\",\n    \"wound_graze\", \"fever_warned\", \"pill_taken\", \"blackout\", \"player_rescued\", \"companion_patched\", \"companion_overdosed\",\n    \"companion_died\", \"better_way\", \"ignite_flare\", \"ignite_rocket\", \"ignite_flamer\", \"ignite_mortar\", \"ignite_molotov\",\n    \"ignite_frag\", \"ignite_barrel\", \"ignite_vehicle\", \"ignite_person\", \"ignite_lightning\", \"ignite_tracer\", \"ignite_cigarette\",\n    \"cells_500\", \"enemy_panicked\", \"animals_fled\", \"explosion_chain\", \"rain_extinguished\", \"stealth_kill\", \"dart_kill\",\n    \"night_contract\", \"sleep_used\", \"safe_house_claimed\", \"post_cleared\", \"post_remanned\", \"technical_driven\", \"mounted_gun\",\n    \"repair_done\", \"boat_driven\", \"bus_taken\", \"tape_played\", \"cache_tracker\", \"diamonds_spent\", \"contract_a0\", \"contract_a1\",\n    \"contract_b1\", \"contract_b2\", \"contract_b3\", \"contract_b4\", \"contract_c1\", \"contract_c2\", \"contract_c3\", \"contract_d1\",\n    \"contract_d2\", \"ceasefire_ended\", \"town_burned\", \"ending_burn\", \"ending_read\", \"ending_chair\",\n];\n\nfn play_route(route: Route, seed: u64) -> BTreeSet<String> {\n    let mut w = World::campaign(seed, route);\n    let mut goal = String::new();\n    let mut stuck = 0.0f32;\n    let cap = 60.0 * 900.0;\n    let mut t = 0.0f32;\n    while t < cap && !w.finished {\n        let input = w.bot_input();\n        let before = w.goal_name();\n        w.tick(&input, DT);\n        t += DT;\n        let now = w.goal_name();\n        if now != before {\n            if goal != before {\n                eprintln!(\"{route:?} seed {seed}: {before} -> {now} at ({:.0},{:.0}) t={t:.0}\", w.x, w.z);\n            }\n            goal = now;\n            stuck = 0.0;\n        } else {\n            stuck += DT;\n            let budget = w.goal_budget();\n            if stuck > budget && !w.finished {\n                panic!(\n                    \"{route:?} seed {seed} stuck on {now} for {stuck:.0}s (budget {budget:.0}) at ({:.1},{:.1}) step {} flags {}\",\n                    w.x, w.z, w.step, w.flags.len()\n                );\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    assert!(w.finished, \"{route:?} seed {seed} did not finish by {t:.0}s goal {} at ({:.0},{:.0})\", w.goal_name(), w.x, w.z);\n    let end = match route {\n        Route::Read => \"ending_read\",\n        Route::Chair => \"ending_chair\",\n        _ => \"ending_burn\",\n    };\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(end), \"{route:?} missing {end}\");\n    w.flags\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn bot_plays_all_three_endings() {\n    let mut union = BTreeSet::new();\n    for seed in [1u64, 2] {\n        let mut prefix_a = World::campaign(seed, Route::Human);\n        let mut prefix_b = World::campaign(seed, Route::Human);\n        for _ in 0..40 {\n            let a = prefix_a.bot_input();\n            let b = prefix_b.bot_input();\n            prefix_a.tick(&a, DT);\n            prefix_b.tick(&b, DT);\n        }\n        assert_eq!(prefix_a.fingerprint(), prefix_b.fingerprint());\n        for route in [Route::Human, Route::Read, Route::Chair] {\n            union.extend(play_route(route, seed));\n        }\n    }\n    let missing: Vec<_> = COVERAGE.iter().copied().filter(|f| !union.contains(*f)).collect();\n    assert!(missing.is_empty(), \"coverage missing {missing:?}\");\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4069,"output_tokens":11961,"cache_read_input_tokens":161024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"a3016ec0-d6b0-4f92-a4e2-a1854bdd88f7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8c030c91-886e-43f4-9f68-4321fd94239c-123","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\",\"new_string\":\"    fn rms(samples: &[f32]) -> f32 {\\n        let n = samples.len().max(1) as f32;\\n        (samples.iter().map(|s| s * s).sum::<f32>() / n).sqrt()\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn music_bus_tracks_the_gain() {\\n        let quiet = render_music(MUSIC_GAIN, 1.0, 8_000.0);\\n        let full = render_music(1.0, 1.0, 8_000.0);\\n        assert!(quiet.iter().all(|s| s.is_finite()));\\n        let ratio = rms(&quiet) / rms(&full);\\n        assert!((ratio - 0.10).abs() < 0.01, \\\"rms ratio {ratio}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn gun_families_voices_and_crackle_differ() {\\n        let pistol = render_patch(gun_patch(\\\"pistol\\\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\\n        let shotgun = render_patch(gun_patch(\\\"shotgun\\\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\\n        let rifle = render_patch(gun_patch(\\\"rifle\\\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\\n        assert_ne!(pistol, shotgun);\\n        assert_ne!(pistol, rifle);\\n        let ada = render_voice(\\\"Ada Okoro\\\", \\\"The grass burns anyway\\\", 8_000.0);\\n        let tomek = render_voice(\\\"Tomek Wrona\\\", \\\"The grass burns anyway\\\", 8_000.0);\\n        assert_ne!(ada, tomek);\\n        assert!(ada.iter().any(|s| s.abs() > 0.01));\\n        assert!(rms(&render_crackle(400, 8_000.0)) > rms(&render_crackle(1, 8_000.0)));\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\",\"old_line\":751,\"new_string\":\"    fn rms(samples: &[f32]) -> f32 {\\n        let n = samples.len().max(1) as f32;\\n        (samples.iter().map(|s| s * s).sum::<f32>() / n).sqrt()\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn music_bus_tracks_the_gain() {\\n        let quiet = render_music(MUSIC_GAIN, 1.0, 8_000.0);\\n        let full = render_music(1.0, 1.0, 8_000.0);\\n        assert!(quiet.iter().all(|s| s.is_finite()));\\n        let ratio = rms(&quiet) / rms(&full);\\n        assert!((ratio - 0.10).abs() < 0.01, \\\"rms ratio {ratio}\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn gun_families_voices_and_crackle_differ() {\\n        let pistol = render_patch(gun_patch(\\\"pistol\\\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\\n        let shotgun = render_patch(gun_patch(\\\"shotgun\\\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\\n        let rifle = render_patch(gun_patch(\\\"rifle\\\"), 0.25, 8_000.0);\\n        assert_ne!(pistol, shotgun);\\n        assert_ne!(pistol, rifle);\\n        let ada = render_voice(\\\"Ada Okoro\\\", \\\"The grass burns anyway\\\", 8_000.0);\\n        let tomek = render_voice(\\\"Tomek Wrona\\\", \\\"The grass burns anyway\\\", 8_000.0);\\n        assert_ne!(ada, tomek);\\n        assert!(ada.iter().any(|s| s.abs() > 0.01));\\n        assert!(rms(&render_crackle(400, 8_000.0)) > rms(&render_crackle(1, 8_000.0)));\\n    }\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn explosion_is_loud_then_silent() {\",\"new_line\":751,\"context_before\":\"mod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"        let ev = SimEvent::Explosion { pos: Vec3::ZERO, radius: 1.35 };\\n        let out = render_events(&[(0.0, ev)], 2.0, 22050.0, &Listener::default());\\n        let peak_early = out[..22050].iter().fold(0.0f32, |m, s| m.max(s.abs()));\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8c030c91-886e-43f4-9f68-4321fd94239c-124","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"//! Jam Cry. These tests call the shipped simulation: `World::tick`, `Gun::pull`, `FireMap::tick`.\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\\nuse std::path::Path;\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::fire::FireMap;\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::geom::{self, exposure};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::gun::{Gun, WeaponId, clear_seconds};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::net::{Link, client_apply, host_publish};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::shell::{Device, MenuInput, glyph};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::world::{Body, Route, Screen, World, fiction_lines};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::Merc;\\nuse pav_core::input::buttons;\\nuse pav_core::rng::Rng;\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\nconst DT: f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;\\n\\nfn press(bit: u32) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.held = bit;\\n    f.pressed = bit;\\n    f\\n}\\n\\nfn hold(bit: u32) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.held = bit;\\n    f\\n}\\n\\nfn soldier(x: f32, z: f32, alert: u8) -> Body {\\n    let mut gun = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n    gun.ammo = 400;\\n    gun.reserve = 400;\\n    gun.condition = 100.0;\\n    Body {\\n        kind: 1,\\n        x,\\n        z,\\n        yaw: 0.0,\\n        hp: 80.0,\\n        alive: true,\\n        alert,\\n        gun,\\n        see: 0.0,\\n        poison: 0.0,\\n        burn: 0.0,\\n        doomed: false,\\n        flee: 0.0,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn run(w: &mut World, input: &InputFrame, seconds: f32) {\\n    let n = (seconds / DT) as i32;\\n    for _ in 0..n {\\n        w.tick(input, DT);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn scene_boots_and_history_is_off() {\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2, 9] {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(Merc::KEY, seed).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(sim.play().unwrap().key(), \\\"merc\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(sim.config.history_seconds, 0.0);\\n        for _ in 0..8 {\\n            sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(status[\\\"title\\\"], \\\"Jam Cry\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn same_seed_matches_across_a_save() {\\n    let mut a = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut b = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    f.look.x = 0.01;\\n    for _ in 0..90 {\\n        a.tick(&f, DT);\\n        b.tick(&f, DT);\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), b.fingerprint());\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&a.save_json()).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(loaded.fingerprint(), a.fingerprint());\\n    a.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let mut loaded = loaded;\\n    loaded.tick(&f, DT);\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), loaded.fingerprint());\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn look_and_stick_follow_yaw() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\\n    let z0 = w.z;\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &f, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.z < z0 - 3.0, \\\"forward at yaw 0 moves north, z {z0} -> {}\\\", w.z);\\n    w.yaw = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;\\n    let x0 = w.x;\\n    run(&mut w, &f, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.x > x0 + 3.0, \\\"yaw east, x {x0} -> {}\\\", w.x);\\n    let mut look = InputFrame::default();\\n    look.look.y = 5.0;\\n    w.tick(&look, DT);\\n    assert!(w.pitch <= 1.15 + 1e-3);\\n    look.look.y = -5.0;\\n    w.tick(&look, DT);\\n    assert!(w.pitch >= -1.15 - 1e-3);\\n    let mut crouch = hold(buttons::CROUCH);\\n    crouch.move_dir.y = 0.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &crouch, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.stance == 1 && (w.eye - 1.02).abs() < 0.08, \\\"eye {}\\\", w.eye);\\n    let mut prone = hold(buttons::CRAWL);\\n    run(&mut w, &prone, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.stance == 2 && w.eye < 0.6, \\\"eye {}\\\", w.eye);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn hits_use_zones_and_walls_block() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\\n    w.yaw = 0.0;\\n    w.pitch = ((1.70 - w.eye) / 10.0).atan();\\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 10.0, 100.0);\\n    let mut f = hold(buttons::PRIMARY | buttons::SECONDARY);\\n    f.pressed = buttons::PRIMARY;\\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let hp = w.bodies[0].hp;\\n    assert!(hp < 100.0 - 50.0, \\\"headshot damage, hp {hp}\\\");\\n    w.bodies.clear();\\n    w.guns[0].cooldown = 0.0;\\n    w.pitch = ((0.45 - w.eye) / 10.0).atan();\\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 10.0, 100.0);\\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let limb = w.bodies[0].hp;\\n    assert!(limb > 80.0 && limb < 90.0, \\\"limb damage, hp {limb}\\\");\\n    w.bodies.clear();\\n    w.guns[0].cooldown = 0.0;\\n    w.pitch = 0.0;\\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 20.0, 100.0);\\n    w.add_wall([w.x - 2.0, 0.0, w.z - 16.0], [w.x + 2.0, 3.0, w.z - 14.0]);\\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].hp, 100.0, \\\"wall blocks the ray\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear() {\\n    let mut gun = Gun::new(WeaponId::Pistol);\\n    gun.condition = 35.0;\\n    gun.wear = 0.0;\\n    gun.ammo = 100_000;\\n    gun.reserve = 100_000;\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(35);\\n    let mut jams = 0u32;\\n    for _ in 0..5000 {\\n        gun.cooldown = 0.0;\\n        gun.jammed = false;\\n        if gun.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0) == pav_core::games::merc::gun::Pull::Jammed {\\n            jams += 1;\\n            gun.ammo += 1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(jams > 5000 / 30 && jams < 5000 / 12, \\\"jams {jams}\\\");\\n    let mut stuck = Gun::new(WeaponId::Pistol);\\n    stuck.condition = 40.0;\\n    stuck.force_jam = true;\\n    stuck.ammo = 10;\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(1);\\n    assert_eq!(stuck.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 1.0, 8.0), pav_core::games::merc::gun::Pull::Jammed);\\n    let before = stuck.ammo;\\n    stuck.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 1.0, 8.0);\\n    assert_eq!(stuck.ammo, before, \\\"a jam spends no round\\\");\\n    stuck.tap_reload();\\n    let clear = stuck.clear_left;\\n    let expect = clear_seconds(40.0);\\n    assert!((clear - expect).abs() < 0.01 && clear >= 1.2 && clear <= 2.5, \\\"{clear}\\\");\\n    stuck.tap_reload();\\n    assert!((stuck.clear_left - clear * 0.6).abs() < 0.02, \\\"{}\\\", stuck.clear_left);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(8);\\n    w.guns[0] = Gun::new(WeaponId::Smg);\\n    w.guns[0].condition = 5.0;\\n    w.guns[0].wear = 0.0;\\n    w.guns[0].ammo = 9_999;\\n    w.guns[0].reserve = 9_999;\\n    let fire = hold(buttons::PRIMARY | buttons::SECONDARY);\\n    let mut broke = false;\\n    for _ in 0..(90.0 / DT) as i32 {\\n        if w.guns[0].jammed {\\n            w.tick(&press(buttons::RELOAD), DT);\\n        } else {\\n            w.tick(&fire, DT);\\n        }\\n        if w.guns[0].broken || w.flags.contains(\\\"weapon_broke\\\") {\\n            broke = true;\\n            break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(broke, \\\"condition 5 should break inside 90s\\\");\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(9);\\n    let mut g = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n    g.condition = 5.0;\\n    g.wear = 0.0;\\n    g.ammo = 400;\\n    let mut body = soldier(w.x, w.z - 8.0, 2);\\n    body.gun = g;\\n    w.bodies.push(body);\\n    let mut saw_jam = false;\\n    let mut shots_at_jam = 0u32;\\n    for _ in 0..(20.0 / DT) as i32 {\\n        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n        if w.flags.contains(\\\"enemy_jam\\\") {\\n            saw_jam = true;\\n            shots_at_jam = w.bodies[0].gun.shots;\\n            break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(saw_jam, \\\"soldier should jam\\\");\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].gun.shots, shots_at_jam, \\\"a jammed soldier stops firing\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks() {\\n    let mut map = FireMap::default();\\n    let origin = (200.0f32, -200.0f32);\\n    assert!(map.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 30.0, 0.0));\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(2);\\n    let wind = pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(8.0, 0.0);\\n    for _ in 0..60 {\\n        map.tick(1.0, wind, 0.9, 30.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let (down, up) = map.reach(origin, wind);\\n    assert!(up > 0.0, \\\"upwind reach {up}, down {down}\\\");\\n    assert!(down >= up * 3.0, \\\"down {down} up {up}\\\");\\n\\n    let mut calm = FireMap::default();\\n    calm.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 40.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(3);\\n    for _ in 0..40 {\\n        calm.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::ZERO, 0.9, 40.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let mut min_x = i32::MAX;\\n    let mut max_x = i32::MIN;\\n    let mut min_z = i32::MAX;\\n    let mut max_z = i32::MIN;\\n    for c in calm.cells.keys() {\\n        min_x = min_x.min(c.0);\\n        max_x = max_x.max(c.0);\\n        min_z = min_z.min(c.1);\\n        max_z = max_z.max(c.1);\\n    }\\n    let dx = (max_x - min_x).max(1) as f32;\\n    let dz = (max_z - min_z).max(1) as f32;\\n    let aspect = dx.max(dz) / dx.min(dz);\\n    assert!(aspect < 2.5, \\\"calm scar aspect {aspect} dx {dx} dz {dz}\\\");\\n\\n    let mut blocked = FireMap::default();\\n    let south = (200.0f32, -440.0f32);\\n    assert!(!geom::on_road(south.0, south.1));\\n    blocked.ignite_at(south.0, south.1, 20.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(4);\\n    for _ in 0..30 {\\n        blocked.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(0.0, -8.0), 0.9, 20.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let crossed = blocked.cells.keys().any(|c| {\\n        let (x, z) = geom::cell_center(*c);\\n        z < -416.0 && (z + 420.0).abs() > 4.0 && x > 180.0 && x < 220.0\\n    });\\n    assert!(!crossed, \\\"speed 8 does not jump the road\\\");\\n\\n    let mut ember = FireMap::default();\\n    ember.ignite_at(south.0, south.1, 20.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(5);\\n    for _ in 0..20 {\\n        ember.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(0.0, -12.0), 0.9, 20.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let hopped = ember.cells.keys().any(|c| geom::cell_center(*c).1 < -410.0);\\n    assert!(hopped, \\\"wind above 8 can throw an ember across the road\\\");\\n\\n    let mut ash = FireMap::default();\\n    ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 1.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(6);\\n    ash.tick(2.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::ZERO, 0.0, 1.0, 10.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    assert!(!ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 5.0, 10.0), \\\"burnt ground refuses a new fire\\\");\\n    assert!(ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 5.0, 10.0 + 2880.0));\\n\\n    let mut wet = FireMap::default();\\n    wet.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 10.0, 0.0);\\n    let n = wet.tick(0.1, wind, 0.9, 10.0, 0.0, true, &mut rng);\\n    assert!(n > 0 && wet.burning_count() == 0);\\n\\n    let mut disk = FireMap::default();\\n    let lit = disk.ignite_disk(origin.0, origin.1, 6.0, 10.0, 0.0);\\n    assert!(lit > 8, \\\"barrel disk lit {lit}\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn exposure_smoke_and_noise() {\\n    let night = exposure(0.6, 0.35, 0.45, 0.5);\\n    let noon = exposure(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5);\\n    assert!((night - 0.04725).abs() < 1e-5);\\n    assert!((noon - 0.5).abs() < 1e-5);\\n    assert!(noon / night > 10.0);\\n\\n    let mut quiet = World::fresh(1);\\n    quiet.bodies.push(soldier(quiet.x, quiet.z - 20.0, 0));\\n    let mut loud = quiet.clone();\\n    let mid = ((quiet.x + quiet.bodies[0].x) * 0.5, (quiet.z + quiet.bodies[0].z) * 0.5);\\n    assert!(quiet.fire.ignite_at(mid.0, mid.1, 30.0, quiet.minutes));\\n    run(&mut quiet, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\\n    run(&mut loud, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\\n    assert!(loud.bodies[0].see > quiet.bodies[0].see + 0.05, \\\"smoke {} open {}\\\", quiet.bodies[0].see, loud.bodies[0].see);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\\n    w.guns[0] = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n    w.bodies.push(soldier(w.x + 50.0, w.z, 0));\\n    w.tick(&press(buttons::PRIMARY), DT);\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].alert, 1, \\\"a loud shot makes them suspicious\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\\n    for i in 0..6 {\\n        w.bodies.push(soldier(w.x + i as f32 * 3.0, w.z - 12.0, 2));\\n    }\\n    let x5 = w.bodies[5].x;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    let firing = w.bodies.iter().filter(|b| b.gun.shots > 0).count();\\n    assert!(firing <= 4, \\\"shooters {firing}\\\");\\n    assert!(w.bodies[5].x > x5 + 1.0, \\\"the extra soldier flanks\\\");\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\\n    for i in 0..4 {\\n        let mut b = soldier(w.x + i as f32, w.z - 8.0, 2);\\n        if i < 3 {\\n            b.alive = false;\\n            b.hp = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        w.bodies.push(b);\\n    }\\n    let x = w.bodies[3].x;\\n    let shots = w.bodies[3].gun.shots;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.bodies[3].x > x + 2.0, \\\"morale sends the last soldier away\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[3].gun.shots, shots);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    let (px, pz) = geom::place(\\\"Kilo 38\\\");\\n    w.post_clear = true;\\n    w.post_reman_at = w.minutes - 1.0;\\n    w.x = px;\\n    w.z = pz + 30.0;\\n    w.yaw = 0.0;\\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n    assert!(!w.flags.contains(\\\"post_remanned\\\"), \\\"looking at the post holds it\\\");\\n    w.yaw = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"post_remanned\\\"));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fever_pills_blackout_and_healing() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    w.fever_t = w.tune.fever_interval - 0.05;\\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"fever_warned\\\") && w.fever_state == 1);\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::PILLS), 3.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"pill_taken\\\") && w.fever_state == 0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.pills, 2);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\\n    w.pills = 0;\\n    w.fever_state = 2;\\n    w.fever_attack = 59.0;\\n    w.diamonds = 40;\\n    w.x = 200.0;\\n    w.z = -200.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"blackout\\\"));\\n    assert_eq!(w.hp, 50.0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.diamonds, 32);\\n    let safe = geom::nearest_safe(200.0, -200.0);\\n    assert!(geom::dist(w.x, w.z, safe.0, safe.1) < 1.0);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\\n    w.hp = 40.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::HEAL), 2.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"syrette\\\"));\\n    assert!(w.hp > 90.0, \\\"hp {}\\\", w.hp);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\\n    w.hp = 15.0;\\n    w.wound = 1;\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::HEAL), 4.2);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"wound_gunshot\\\"));\\n    assert!((w.hp - 40.0).abs() < 1.0, \\\"hp {}\\\", w.hp);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(5);\\n    w.hp = 0.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 4.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"player_rescued\\\") && w.hp >= 50.0);\\n    assert!(w.companions.iter().any(|c| c.rescue_spent));\\n    let blob = w.save_json();\\n    w.hp = 0.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 4.0);\\n    assert!(!w.companions.iter().any(|c| c.alive && !c.rescue_spent && !c.down) || w.hp < 10.0);\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&blob).unwrap();\\n    assert!(loaded.flags.contains(\\\"player_rescued\\\"));\\n    assert!(loaded.companions.iter().any(|c| c.rescue_spent));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn vehicles_climb_break_and_float() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    w.ride.kind = 1;\\n    w.ride.seat = 1;\\n    w.ride.x = 200.0;\\n    w.ride.z = -520.0;\\n    w.x = 200.0;\\n    w.z = -520.0;\\n    w.ride.health = 100.0;\\n    let mut drive = InputFrame::default();\\n    drive.axes.y = 1.0;\\n    drive.axes.x = 0.0;\\n    w.ride.yaw = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;\\n    run(&mut w, &drive, 2.0);\\n    assert!(w.ride.pitch > 0.01, \\\"pitch {}\\\", w.ride.pitch);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"technical_driven\\\"));\\n    w.ride.roll = 0.3;\\n    w.tick(&drive, DT);\\n    assert!(w.ride.roll < 0.3);\\n\\n    w.ride.health = 100.0;\\n    w.ride.stage = 0;\\n    w.hurt_vehicle(50.0);\\n    assert!(w.ride.stage >= 1, \\\"stage {}\\\", w.ride.stage);\\n    w.hurt_vehicle(80.0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.ride.stage, 3);\\n    run(&mut w, &drive, 9.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"ignite_vehicle\\\") || w.ride.stage == 4);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\\n    w.ride.kind = 1;\\n    w.ride.seat = 0;\\n    w.ride.health = 30.0;\\n    w.ride.stage = 2;\\n    w.ride.x = w.x;\\n    w.ride.z = w.z;\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::INTERACT), 6.5);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"repair_done\\\"));\\n    assert!(w.ride.health >= 70.0);\\n\\n    let mut dry = World::fresh(3);\\n    dry.ride.kind = 2;\\n    dry.ride.seat = 1;\\n    dry.ride.x = 200.0;\\n    dry.ride.z = -200.0;\\n    dry.x = 200.0;\\n    dry.z = -200.0;\\n    assert!(!geom::deep_water(200.0, -200.0));\\n    let mut throttle = InputFrame::default();\\n    throttle.axes.y = 1.0;\\n    run(&mut dry, &throttle, 1.0);\\n    assert!(dry.ride.speed.abs() < 0.2, \\\"boat on grass {}\\\", dry.ride.speed);\\n\\n    let (wx, wz) = geom::nearest_water(0.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut wet = World::fresh(4);\\n    wet.ride.kind = 2;\\n    wet.ride.seat = 1;\\n    wet.ride.x = wx;\\n    wet.ride.z = wz;\\n    wet.x = wx;\\n    wet.z = wz;\\n    let (tx, tz) = geom::water_ahead(wx, wz, 40.0);\\n    wet.ride.yaw = geom::yaw_toward(wx, wz, tx, tz);\\n    run(&mut wet, &throttle, 2.0);\\n    assert!(wet.flags.contains(\\\"boat_driven\\\"), \\\"dist {} deep {}\\\", wet.ride.dist, geom::deep_water(wet.ride.x, wet.ride.z));\\n\\n    wet.ride.npc = true;\\n    let z0 = wet.ride.z;\\n    run(&mut wet, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    assert!((wet.ride.x - wx).abs() > 0.5 || (wet.ride.z - z0).abs() > 0.5);\\n\\n    let seat = wet.ride.seat;\\n    wet.tick(&press(buttons::USE), DT);\\n    assert_ne!(wet.ride.seat, seat);\\n    wet.ride.seat = 2;\\n    wet.tick(&hold(buttons::PRIMARY), DT);\\n    assert!(wet.flags.contains(\\\"mounted_gun\\\"));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn shop_tracker_and_shell() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    w.diamonds = 0;\\n    let guns = w.guns.len();\\n    assert!(!w.try_buy());\\n    assert_eq!(w.guns.len(), guns);\\n    assert_eq!(w.diamonds, 0);\\n\\n    w.tracker_cache = (w.x + 10.0, w.z);\\n    let near = w.tracker_rate();\\n    w.tracker_cache = (w.x + 50.0, w.z);\\n    let far = w.tracker_rate();\\n    assert!(near > far && far > 0.0, \\\"{near} vs {far}\\\");\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(2, Route::Human);\\n    assert!(w.rows().len() <= 7);\\n    let screens = [\\n        Screen::Title, Screen::Difficulty, Screen::Merc, Screen::Prologue, Screen::Pause, Screen::Settings, Screen::About,\\n        Screen::Dev, Screen::Mp, Screen::Attract,\\n    ];\\n    for screen in screens {\\n        w.screen = screen;\\n        for tab in 0..6 {\\n            w.tab = tab;\\n            for page in 0..6 {\\n                w.page = page;\\n                assert!(w.rows().len() <= 7, \\\"{screen:?} tab {tab} page {page} {:?}\\\", w.rows());\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    w.screen = Screen::Difficulty;\\n    w.focus = 0;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { up: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.focus, 2);\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { back: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Title);\\n\\n    w.focus = 0;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { pointer: Some((400.0, 300.0)), ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.focus, 1);\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { pointer: Some((400.0, 230.0)), click: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Difficulty);\\n\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", Device::Gamepad, false), \\\"Cross\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", Device::Gamepad, true), \\\"A\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"fire\\\", Device::Keyboard, false), \\\"LMB\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"reload\\\", Device::Gamepad, false), \\\"Square\\\");\\n\\n    w.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n    w.tab = 5;\\n    w.page = 1;\\n    w.focus = 2;\\n    let before = w.tune.fire_spread;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { right: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert!(w.tune.fire_spread > before, \\\"{} -> {}\\\", before, w.tune.fire_spread);\\n    w.page = 3;\\n    w.focus = 3;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { confirm: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert!((w.tune.fire_spread - w.tune0.fire_spread).abs() < 1e-4);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(3, Route::Human);\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 9.0);\\n    assert_ne!(w.screen, Screen::Attract);\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.2);\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Attract);\\n    let saves = w.saves_written;\\n    for _ in 0..800 {\\n        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    }\\n    assert!(w.attract_loops >= 5, \\\"loops {}\\\", w.attract_loops);\\n    assert_eq!(w.attract_seen, (1u16 << 10) - 1, \\\"seen {:b}\\\", w.attract_seen);\\n    assert_eq!(w.saves_written, saves);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(4, Route::Human);\\n    let mut seen = vec![format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", w.screen)];\\n    for bit in [buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP, buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP] {\\n        w.tick(&press(bit), DT);\\n        seen.push(format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", w.screen));\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Playing, \\\"{seen:?}\\\");\\n    assert!(seen.windows(2).all(|p| p[0] != p[1]), \\\"{seen:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fiction_has_no_source_names_and_no_audio_files() {\\n    let banned = [\\n        \\\"jackal\\\", \\\"ufll\\\", \\\"apr\\\", \\\"pala\\\", \\\"mosate\\\", \\\"bowa\\\", \\\"leboa\\\", \\\"oluwagembi\\\", \\\"mike's bar\\\", \\\"marty\\\", \\\"alencar\\\",\\n        \\\"warren clyde\\\", \\\"paul ferenc\\\", \\\"hyppolite\\\", \\\"xianyong\\\", \\\"josip\\\", \\\"hakim\\\", \\\"bilders\\\", \\\"quarbani\\\", \\\"voorhees\\\",\\n        \\\"todo\\\", \\\"tbd\\\", \\\"placeholder\\\", \\\"lorem\\\",\\n    ];\\n    for line in fiction_lines() {\\n        let low = line.to_lowercase();\\n        if low.contains(\\\"far cry 2\\\") {\\n            assert!(line.contains(\\\"Source:\\\"), \\\"{line}\\\");\\n        }\\n        for word in banned {\\n            assert!(!low.contains(word), \\\"{word} in {line}\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let root = Path::new(env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\")).join(\\\"src/games/merc\\\");\\n    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(&root).unwrap() {\\n        let path = entry.unwrap().path();\\n        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(&path).unwrap_or_default().to_lowercase();\\n        for word in banned {\\n            assert!(!text.contains(word), \\\"{word} in {}\\\", path.display());\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let engine = Path::new(env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\")).join(\\\"../..\\\");\\n    let mut audio = Vec::new();\\n    walk_audio(&engine, &mut audio);\\n    assert!(audio.is_empty(), \\\"shipped audio files: {audio:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\\nfn walk_audio(dir: &Path, out: &mut Vec<String>) {\\n    let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(dir) else { return };\\n    for entry in rd.flatten() {\\n        let path = entry.path();\\n        if path.file_name().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\\\"target\\\") {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if path.is_dir() {\\n            walk_audio(&path, out);\\n        } else if let Some(ext) = path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) {\\n            if matches!(ext, \\\"wav\\\" | \\\"mp3\\\" | \\\"ogg\\\") {\\n                out.push(path.display().to_string());\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn net_loopback_shares_one_fire_cell() {\\n    let mut host = World::fresh(1);\\n    let mut client = World::fresh(2);\\n    assert!(host.fire.ignite_at(200.0, -200.0, 10.0, host.minutes));\\n    let mut link = Link::new(7, 0.15, 0.0, 0.0);\\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, false);\\n    assert!(link.max_bytes < 1200);\\n    for _ in 0..10 {\\n        link.advance(0.1);\\n    }\\n    let bodies = link.poll();\\n    assert!(bodies.iter().any(|b| b.contains(\\\"\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fire\\\\\\\"\\\")));\\n    client_apply(&mut client, &bodies);\\n    let shared = host.fire.cells.keys().any(|c| client.fire.cells.get(c).is_some_and(|cell| cell.burning));\\n    assert!(shared, \\\"host and client should share a burning cell within 1s\\\");\\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, true);\\n    assert_eq!(link.finishes, 1);\\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, true);\\n    assert_eq!(link.finishes, 1);\\n\\n    let mut lossy = Link::new(1, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\\n    lossy.send(false, \\\"{\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ping\\\\\\\"}\\\".into());\\n    lossy.advance(0.1);\\n    assert!(lossy.poll().is_empty());\\n    lossy.send(true, \\\"{\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ping\\\\\\\"}\\\".into());\\n    lossy.advance(0.1);\\n    assert_eq!(lossy.poll().len(), 1);\\n}\\n\\nconst COVERAGE: &[&str] = &[\\n    \\\"map_raised\\\", \\\"waypoint_set\\\", \\\"gps_followed\\\", \\\"monocular_tag\\\", \\\"wind_rag\\\", \\\"jam_cleared\\\", \\\"enemy_jam\\\", \\\"weapon_broke\\\",\\n    \\\"weapon_bought\\\", \\\"locker_used\\\", \\\"syrette\\\", \\\"wound_gunshot\\\", \\\"wound_shrapnel\\\", \\\"wound_burn\\\", \\\"wound_fall\\\", \\\"wound_tourniquet\\\",\\n    \\\"wound_graze\\\", \\\"fever_warned\\\", \\\"pill_taken\\\", \\\"blackout\\\", \\\"player_rescued\\\", \\\"companion_patched\\\", \\\"companion_overdosed\\\",\\n    \\\"companion_died\\\", \\\"better_way\\\", \\\"ignite_flare\\\", \\\"ignite_rocket\\\", \\\"ignite_flamer\\\", \\\"ignite_mortar\\\", \\\"ignite_molotov\\\",\\n    \\\"ignite_frag\\\", \\\"ignite_barrel\\\", \\\"ignite_vehicle\\\", \\\"ignite_person\\\", \\\"ignite_lightning\\\", \\\"ignite_tracer\\\", \\\"ignite_cigarette\\\",\\n    \\\"cells_500\\\", \\\"enemy_panicked\\\", \\\"animals_fled\\\", \\\"explosion_chain\\\", \\\"rain_extinguished\\\", \\\"stealth_kill\\\", \\\"dart_kill\\\",\\n    \\\"night_contract\\\", \\\"sleep_used\\\", \\\"safe_house_claimed\\\", \\\"post_cleared\\\", \\\"post_remanned\\\", \\\"technical_driven\\\", \\\"mounted_gun\\\",\\n    \\\"repair_done\\\", \\\"boat_driven\\\", \\\"bus_taken\\\", \\\"tape_played\\\", \\\"cache_tracker\\\", \\\"diamonds_spent\\\", \\\"contract_a0\\\", \\\"contract_a1\\\",\\n    \\\"contract_b1\\\", \\\"contract_b2\\\", \\\"contract_b3\\\", \\\"contract_b4\\\", \\\"contract_c1\\\", \\\"contract_c2\\\", \\\"contract_c3\\\", \\\"contract_d1\\\",\\n    \\\"contract_d2\\\", \\\"ceasefire_ended\\\", \\\"town_burned\\\", \\\"ending_burn\\\", \\\"ending_read\\\", \\\"ending_chair\\\",\\n];\\n\\nfn play_route(route: Route, seed: u64) -> BTreeSet<String> {\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(seed, route);\\n    let mut goal = String::new();\\n    let mut stuck = 0.0f32;\\n    let cap = 60.0 * 900.0;\\n    let mut t = 0.0f32;\\n    while t < cap && !w.finished {\\n        let input = w.bot_input();\\n        let before = w.goal_name();\\n        w.tick(&input, DT);\\n        t += DT;\\n        let now = w.goal_name();\\n        if now != before {\\n            if goal != before {\\n                eprintln!(\\\"{route:?} seed {seed}: {before} -> {now} at ({:.0},{:.0}) t={t:.0}\\\", w.x, w.z);\\n            }\\n            goal = now;\\n            stuck = 0.0;\\n        } else {\\n            stuck += DT;\\n            let budget = w.goal_budget();\\n            if stuck > budget && !w.finished {\\n                panic!(\\n                    \\\"{route:?} seed {seed} stuck on {now} for {stuck:.0}s (budget {budget:.0}) at ({:.1},{:.1}) step {} flags {}\\\",\\n                    w.x, w.z, w.step, w.flags.len()\\n                );\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(w.finished, \\\"{route:?} seed {seed} did not finish by {t:.0}s goal {} at ({:.0},{:.0})\\\", w.goal_name(), w.x, w.z);\\n    let end = match route {\\n        Route::Read => \\\"ending_read\\\",\\n        Route::Chair => \\\"ending_chair\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"ending_burn\\\",\\n    };\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(end), \\\"{route:?} missing {end}\\\");\\n    w.flags\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn bot_plays_all_three_endings() {\\n    let mut union = BTreeSet::new();\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2] {\\n        let mut prefix_a = World::campaign(seed, Route::Human);\\n        let mut prefix_b = World::campaign(seed, Route::Human);\\n        for _ in 0..40 {\\n            let a = prefix_a.bot_input();\\n            let b = prefix_b.bot_input();\\n            prefix_a.tick(&a, DT);\\n            prefix_b.tick(&b, DT);\\n        }\\n        assert_eq!(prefix_a.fingerprint(), prefix_b.fingerprint());\\n        for route in [Route::Human, Route::Read, Route::Chair] {\\n            union.extend(play_route(route, seed));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let missing: Vec<_> = COVERAGE.iter().copied().filter(|f| !union.contains(*f)).collect();\\n    assert!(missing.is_empty(), \\\"coverage missing {missing:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"//! Jam Cry. These tests call the shipped simulation: `World::tick`, `Gun::pull`, `FireMap::tick`.\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\\nuse std::path::Path;\\n\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::fire::FireMap;\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::geom::{self, exposure};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::gun::{Gun, WeaponId, clear_seconds};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::net::{Link, client_apply, host_publish};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::shell::{Device, MenuInput, glyph};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::world::{Body, Route, Screen, World, fiction_lines};\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::Merc;\\nuse pav_core::input::buttons;\\nuse pav_core::rng::Rng;\\nuse pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\nconst DT: f32 = 1.0 / 60.0;\\n\\nfn press(bit: u32) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.held = bit;\\n    f.pressed = bit;\\n    f\\n}\\n\\nfn hold(bit: u32) -> InputFrame {\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.held = bit;\\n    f\\n}\\n\\nfn soldier(x: f32, z: f32, alert: u8) -> Body {\\n    let mut gun = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n    gun.ammo = 400;\\n    gun.reserve = 400;\\n    gun.condition = 100.0;\\n    Body {\\n        kind: 1,\\n        x,\\n        z,\\n        yaw: 0.0,\\n        hp: 80.0,\\n        alive: true,\\n        alert,\\n        gun,\\n        see: 0.0,\\n        poison: 0.0,\\n        burn: 0.0,\\n        doomed: false,\\n        flee: 0.0,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn run(w: &mut World, input: &InputFrame, seconds: f32) {\\n    let n = (seconds / DT) as i32;\\n    for _ in 0..n {\\n        w.tick(input, DT);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn scene_boots_and_history_is_off() {\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2, 9] {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(Merc::KEY, seed).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(sim.play().unwrap().key(), \\\"merc\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(sim.config.history_seconds, 0.0);\\n        for _ in 0..8 {\\n            sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(status[\\\"title\\\"], \\\"Jam Cry\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn same_seed_matches_across_a_save() {\\n    let mut a = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut b = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    f.look.x = 0.01;\\n    for _ in 0..90 {\\n        a.tick(&f, DT);\\n        b.tick(&f, DT);\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), b.fingerprint());\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&a.save_json()).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(loaded.fingerprint(), a.fingerprint());\\n    a.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let mut loaded = loaded;\\n    loaded.tick(&f, DT);\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), loaded.fingerprint());\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn look_and_stick_follow_yaw() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\\n    let z0 = w.z;\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &f, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.z < z0 - 3.0, \\\"forward at yaw 0 moves north, z {z0} -> {}\\\", w.z);\\n    w.yaw = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;\\n    let x0 = w.x;\\n    run(&mut w, &f, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.x > x0 + 3.0, \\\"yaw east, x {x0} -> {}\\\", w.x);\\n    let mut look = InputFrame::default();\\n    look.look.y = 5.0;\\n    w.tick(&look, DT);\\n    assert!(w.pitch <= 1.15 + 1e-3);\\n    look.look.y = -5.0;\\n    w.tick(&look, DT);\\n    assert!(w.pitch >= -1.15 - 1e-3);\\n    let mut crouch = hold(buttons::CROUCH);\\n    crouch.move_dir.y = 0.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &crouch, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.stance == 1 && (w.eye - 1.02).abs() < 0.08, \\\"eye {}\\\", w.eye);\\n    let mut prone = hold(buttons::CRAWL);\\n    run(&mut w, &prone, 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.stance == 2 && w.eye < 0.6, \\\"eye {}\\\", w.eye);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn hits_use_zones_and_walls_block() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\\n    w.yaw = 0.0;\\n    w.pitch = ((1.70 - w.eye) / 10.0).atan();\\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 10.0, 100.0);\\n    let mut f = hold(buttons::PRIMARY | buttons::SECONDARY);\\n    f.pressed = buttons::PRIMARY;\\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let hp = w.bodies[0].hp;\\n    assert!(hp < 100.0 - 50.0, \\\"headshot damage, hp {hp}\\\");\\n    w.bodies.clear();\\n    w.guns[0].cooldown = 0.0;\\n    w.pitch = ((0.45 - w.eye) / 10.0).atan();\\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 10.0, 100.0);\\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let limb = w.bodies[0].hp;\\n    assert!(limb > 80.0 && limb < 90.0, \\\"limb damage, hp {limb}\\\");\\n    w.bodies.clear();\\n    w.guns[0].cooldown = 0.0;\\n    w.pitch = 0.0;\\n    w.spawn_dummy(w.x, w.z - 20.0, 100.0);\\n    w.add_wall([w.x - 2.0, 0.0, w.z - 16.0], [w.x + 2.0, 3.0, w.z - 14.0]);\\n    w.tick(&f, DT);\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].hp, 100.0, \\\"wall blocks the ray\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear() {\\n    let mut gun = Gun::new(WeaponId::Pistol);\\n    gun.condition = 35.0;\\n    gun.wear = 0.0;\\n    gun.ammo = 100_000;\\n    gun.reserve = 100_000;\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(35);\\n    let mut jams = 0u32;\\n    for _ in 0..5000 {\\n        gun.cooldown = 0.0;\\n        gun.jammed = false;\\n        if gun.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0) == pav_core::games::merc::gun::Pull::Jammed {\\n            jams += 1;\\n            gun.ammo += 1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(jams > 5000 / 30 && jams < 5000 / 12, \\\"jams {jams}\\\");\\n    let mut stuck = Gun::new(WeaponId::Pistol);\\n    stuck.condition = 40.0;\\n    stuck.force_jam = true;\\n    stuck.ammo = 10;\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(1);\\n    assert_eq!(stuck.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 1.0, 8.0), pav_core::games::merc::gun::Pull::Jammed);\\n    let before = stuck.ammo;\\n    stuck.pull(&mut rng, 1.0, 1.0, 8.0);\\n    assert_eq!(stuck.ammo, before, \\\"a jam spends no round\\\");\\n    stuck.tap_reload();\\n    let clear = stuck.clear_left;\\n    let expect = clear_seconds(40.0);\\n    assert!((clear - expect).abs() < 0.01 && clear >= 1.2 && clear <= 2.5, \\\"{clear}\\\");\\n    stuck.tap_reload();\\n    assert!((stuck.clear_left - clear * 0.6).abs() < 0.02, \\\"{}\\\", stuck.clear_left);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(8);\\n    w.guns[0] = Gun::new(WeaponId::Smg);\\n    w.guns[0].condition = 5.0;\\n    w.guns[0].wear = 0.0;\\n    w.guns[0].ammo = 9_999;\\n    w.guns[0].reserve = 9_999;\\n    let fire = hold(buttons::PRIMARY | buttons::SECONDARY);\\n    let mut broke = false;\\n    for _ in 0..(90.0 / DT) as i32 {\\n        if w.guns[0].jammed {\\n            w.tick(&press(buttons::RELOAD), DT);\\n        } else {\\n            w.tick(&fire, DT);\\n        }\\n        if w.guns[0].broken || w.flags.contains(\\\"weapon_broke\\\") {\\n            broke = true;\\n            break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(broke, \\\"condition 5 should break inside 90s\\\");\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(9);\\n    let mut g = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n    g.condition = 5.0;\\n    g.wear = 0.0;\\n    g.ammo = 400;\\n    let mut body = soldier(w.x, w.z - 8.0, 2);\\n    body.gun = g;\\n    w.bodies.push(body);\\n    let mut saw_jam = false;\\n    let mut shots_at_jam = 0u32;\\n    for _ in 0..(20.0 / DT) as i32 {\\n        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n        if w.flags.contains(\\\"enemy_jam\\\") {\\n            saw_jam = true;\\n            shots_at_jam = w.bodies[0].gun.shots;\\n            break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(saw_jam, \\\"soldier should jam\\\");\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].gun.shots, shots_at_jam, \\\"a jammed soldier stops firing\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks() {\\n    let mut map = FireMap::default();\\n    let origin = (200.0f32, -200.0f32);\\n    assert!(map.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 30.0, 0.0));\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(2);\\n    let wind = pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(8.0, 0.0);\\n    for _ in 0..60 {\\n        map.tick(1.0, wind, 0.9, 30.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let (down, up) = map.reach(origin, wind);\\n    assert!(up > 0.0, \\\"upwind reach {up}, down {down}\\\");\\n    assert!(down >= up * 3.0, \\\"down {down} up {up}\\\");\\n\\n    let mut calm = FireMap::default();\\n    calm.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 40.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(3);\\n    for _ in 0..40 {\\n        calm.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::ZERO, 0.9, 40.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let mut min_x = i32::MAX;\\n    let mut max_x = i32::MIN;\\n    let mut min_z = i32::MAX;\\n    let mut max_z = i32::MIN;\\n    for c in calm.cells.keys() {\\n        min_x = min_x.min(c.0);\\n        max_x = max_x.max(c.0);\\n        min_z = min_z.min(c.1);\\n        max_z = max_z.max(c.1);\\n    }\\n    let dx = (max_x - min_x).max(1) as f32;\\n    let dz = (max_z - min_z).max(1) as f32;\\n    let aspect = dx.max(dz) / dx.min(dz);\\n    assert!(aspect < 2.5, \\\"calm scar aspect {aspect} dx {dx} dz {dz}\\\");\\n\\n    let mut blocked = FireMap::default();\\n    let south = (200.0f32, -440.0f32);\\n    assert!(!geom::on_road(south.0, south.1));\\n    blocked.ignite_at(south.0, south.1, 20.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(4);\\n    for _ in 0..30 {\\n        blocked.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(0.0, -8.0), 0.9, 20.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let crossed = blocked.cells.keys().any(|c| {\\n        let (x, z) = geom::cell_center(*c);\\n        z < -416.0 && (z + 420.0).abs() > 4.0 && x > 180.0 && x < 220.0\\n    });\\n    assert!(!crossed, \\\"speed 8 does not jump the road\\\");\\n\\n    let mut ember = FireMap::default();\\n    ember.ignite_at(south.0, south.1, 20.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(5);\\n    for _ in 0..20 {\\n        ember.tick(1.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::new(0.0, -12.0), 0.9, 20.0, 0.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    }\\n    let hopped = ember.cells.keys().any(|c| geom::cell_center(*c).1 < -410.0);\\n    assert!(hopped, \\\"wind above 8 can throw an ember across the road\\\");\\n\\n    let mut ash = FireMap::default();\\n    ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 1.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(6);\\n    ash.tick(2.0, pav_core::glam::Vec2::ZERO, 0.0, 1.0, 10.0, false, &mut rng);\\n    assert!(!ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 5.0, 10.0), \\\"burnt ground refuses a new fire\\\");\\n    assert!(ash.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 5.0, 10.0 + 2880.0));\\n\\n    let mut wet = FireMap::default();\\n    wet.ignite_at(origin.0, origin.1, 10.0, 0.0);\\n    let n = wet.tick(0.1, wind, 0.9, 10.0, 0.0, true, &mut rng);\\n    assert!(n > 0 && wet.burning_count() == 0);\\n\\n    let mut disk = FireMap::default();\\n    let lit = disk.ignite_disk(origin.0, origin.1, 6.0, 10.0, 0.0);\\n    assert!(lit > 8, \\\"barrel disk lit {lit}\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn exposure_smoke_and_noise() {\\n    let night = exposure(0.6, 0.35, 0.45, 0.5);\\n    let noon = exposure(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5);\\n    assert!((night - 0.04725).abs() < 1e-5);\\n    assert!((noon - 0.5).abs() < 1e-5);\\n    assert!(noon / night > 10.0);\\n\\n    let mut quiet = World::fresh(1);\\n    quiet.bodies.push(soldier(quiet.x, quiet.z - 20.0, 0));\\n    let mut loud = quiet.clone();\\n    let mid = ((quiet.x + quiet.bodies[0].x) * 0.5, (quiet.z + quiet.bodies[0].z) * 0.5);\\n    assert!(quiet.fire.ignite_at(mid.0, mid.1, 30.0, quiet.minutes));\\n    run(&mut quiet, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\\n    run(&mut loud, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\\n    assert!(loud.bodies[0].see > quiet.bodies[0].see + 0.05, \\\"smoke {} open {}\\\", quiet.bodies[0].see, loud.bodies[0].see);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\\n    w.guns[0] = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n    w.bodies.push(soldier(w.x + 50.0, w.z, 0));\\n    w.tick(&press(buttons::PRIMARY), DT);\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[0].alert, 1, \\\"a loud shot makes them suspicious\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\\n    for i in 0..6 {\\n        w.bodies.push(soldier(w.x + i as f32 * 3.0, w.z - 12.0, 2));\\n    }\\n    let x5 = w.bodies[5].x;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    let firing = w.bodies.iter().filter(|b| b.gun.shots > 0).count();\\n    assert!(firing <= 4, \\\"shooters {firing}\\\");\\n    assert!(w.bodies[5].x > x5 + 1.0, \\\"the extra soldier flanks\\\");\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\\n    for i in 0..4 {\\n        let mut b = soldier(w.x + i as f32, w.z - 8.0, 2);\\n        if i < 3 {\\n            b.alive = false;\\n            b.hp = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        w.bodies.push(b);\\n    }\\n    let x = w.bodies[3].x;\\n    let shots = w.bodies[3].gun.shots;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    assert!(w.bodies[3].x > x + 2.0, \\\"morale sends the last soldier away\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(w.bodies[3].gun.shots, shots);\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    let (px, pz) = geom::place(\\\"Kilo 38\\\");\\n    w.post_clear = true;\\n    w.post_reman_at = w.minutes - 1.0;\\n    w.x = px;\\n    w.z = pz + 30.0;\\n    w.yaw = 0.0;\\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n    assert!(!w.flags.contains(\\\"post_remanned\\\"), \\\"looking at the post holds it\\\");\\n    w.yaw = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"post_remanned\\\"));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fever_pills_blackout_and_healing() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    w.fever_t = w.tune.fever_interval - 0.05;\\n    w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), DT);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"fever_warned\\\") && w.fever_state == 1);\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::PILLS), 3.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"pill_taken\\\") && w.fever_state == 0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.pills, 2);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\\n    w.pills = 0;\\n    w.fever_state = 2;\\n    w.fever_attack = 59.0;\\n    w.diamonds = 40;\\n    w.x = 200.0;\\n    w.z = -200.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 2.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"blackout\\\"));\\n    assert_eq!(w.hp, 50.0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.diamonds, 32);\\n    let safe = geom::nearest_safe(200.0, -200.0);\\n    assert!(geom::dist(w.x, w.z, safe.0, safe.1) < 1.0);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(3);\\n    w.hp = 40.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::HEAL), 2.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"syrette\\\"));\\n    assert!(w.hp > 90.0, \\\"hp {}\\\", w.hp);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(4);\\n    w.hp = 15.0;\\n    w.wound = 1;\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::HEAL), 4.2);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"wound_gunshot\\\"));\\n    assert!((w.hp - 40.0).abs() < 1.0, \\\"hp {}\\\", w.hp);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(5);\\n    w.hp = 0.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 4.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"player_rescued\\\") && w.hp >= 50.0);\\n    assert!(w.companions.iter().any(|c| c.rescue_spent));\\n    let blob = w.save_json();\\n    w.hp = 0.0;\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 4.0);\\n    assert!(!w.companions.iter().any(|c| c.alive && !c.rescue_spent && !c.down) || w.hp < 10.0);\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&blob).unwrap();\\n    assert!(loaded.flags.contains(\\\"player_rescued\\\"));\\n    assert!(loaded.companions.iter().any(|c| c.rescue_spent));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn vehicles_climb_break_and_float() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    w.ride.kind = 1;\\n    w.ride.seat = 1;\\n    w.ride.x = 200.0;\\n    w.ride.z = -520.0;\\n    w.x = 200.0;\\n    w.z = -520.0;\\n    w.ride.health = 100.0;\\n    let mut drive = InputFrame::default();\\n    drive.axes.y = 1.0;\\n    drive.axes.x = 0.0;\\n    w.ride.yaw = std::f32::consts::FRAC_PI_2;\\n    run(&mut w, &drive, 2.0);\\n    assert!(w.ride.pitch > 0.01, \\\"pitch {}\\\", w.ride.pitch);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"technical_driven\\\"));\\n    w.ride.roll = 0.3;\\n    w.tick(&drive, DT);\\n    assert!(w.ride.roll < 0.3);\\n\\n    w.ride.health = 100.0;\\n    w.ride.stage = 0;\\n    w.hurt_vehicle(50.0);\\n    assert!(w.ride.stage >= 1, \\\"stage {}\\\", w.ride.stage);\\n    w.hurt_vehicle(80.0);\\n    assert_eq!(w.ride.stage, 3);\\n    run(&mut w, &drive, 9.0);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"ignite_vehicle\\\") || w.ride.stage == 4);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(2);\\n    w.ride.kind = 1;\\n    w.ride.seat = 0;\\n    w.ride.health = 30.0;\\n    w.ride.stage = 2;\\n    w.ride.x = w.x;\\n    w.ride.z = w.z;\\n    run(&mut w, &hold(buttons::INTERACT), 6.5);\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(\\\"repair_done\\\"));\\n    assert!(w.ride.health >= 70.0);\\n\\n    let mut dry = World::fresh(3);\\n    dry.ride.kind = 2;\\n    dry.ride.seat = 1;\\n    dry.ride.x = 200.0;\\n    dry.ride.z = -200.0;\\n    dry.x = 200.0;\\n    dry.z = -200.0;\\n    assert!(!geom::deep_water(200.0, -200.0));\\n    let mut throttle = InputFrame::default();\\n    throttle.axes.y = 1.0;\\n    run(&mut dry, &throttle, 1.0);\\n    assert!(dry.ride.speed.abs() < 0.2, \\\"boat on grass {}\\\", dry.ride.speed);\\n\\n    let (wx, wz) = geom::nearest_water(0.0, 0.0);\\n    let mut wet = World::fresh(4);\\n    wet.ride.kind = 2;\\n    wet.ride.seat = 1;\\n    wet.ride.x = wx;\\n    wet.ride.z = wz;\\n    wet.x = wx;\\n    wet.z = wz;\\n    let (tx, tz) = geom::water_ahead(wx, wz, 40.0);\\n    wet.ride.yaw = geom::yaw_toward(wx, wz, tx, tz);\\n    run(&mut wet, &throttle, 2.0);\\n    assert!(wet.flags.contains(\\\"boat_driven\\\"), \\\"dist {} deep {}\\\", wet.ride.dist, geom::deep_water(wet.ride.x, wet.ride.z));\\n\\n    wet.ride.npc = true;\\n    let z0 = wet.ride.z;\\n    run(&mut wet, &InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    assert!((wet.ride.x - wx).abs() > 0.5 || (wet.ride.z - z0).abs() > 0.5);\\n\\n    let seat = wet.ride.seat;\\n    wet.tick(&press(buttons::USE), DT);\\n    assert_ne!(wet.ride.seat, seat);\\n    wet.ride.seat = 2;\\n    wet.tick(&hold(buttons::PRIMARY), DT);\\n    assert!(wet.flags.contains(\\\"mounted_gun\\\"));\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn shop_tracker_and_shell() {\\n    let mut w = World::fresh(1);\\n    w.diamonds = 0;\\n    let guns = w.guns.len();\\n    assert!(!w.try_buy());\\n    assert_eq!(w.guns.len(), guns);\\n    assert_eq!(w.diamonds, 0);\\n\\n    w.tracker_cache = (w.x + 10.0, w.z);\\n    let near = w.tracker_rate();\\n    w.tracker_cache = (w.x + 50.0, w.z);\\n    let far = w.tracker_rate();\\n    assert!(near > far && far > 0.0, \\\"{near} vs {far}\\\");\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(2, Route::Human);\\n    assert!(w.rows().len() <= 7);\\n    let screens = [\\n        Screen::Title, Screen::Difficulty, Screen::Merc, Screen::Prologue, Screen::Pause, Screen::Settings, Screen::About,\\n        Screen::Dev, Screen::Mp, Screen::Attract,\\n    ];\\n    for screen in screens {\\n        w.screen = screen;\\n        for tab in 0..6 {\\n            w.tab = tab;\\n            for page in 0..6 {\\n                w.page = page;\\n                assert!(w.rows().len() <= 7, \\\"{screen:?} tab {tab} page {page} {:?}\\\", w.rows());\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    w.screen = Screen::Difficulty;\\n    w.focus = 0;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { up: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.focus, 2);\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { back: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Title);\\n\\n    w.focus = 0;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { pointer: Some((400.0, 300.0)), ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.focus, 1);\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { pointer: Some((400.0, 230.0)), click: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Difficulty);\\n\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", Device::Gamepad, false), \\\"Cross\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", Device::Gamepad, true), \\\"A\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"fire\\\", Device::Keyboard, false), \\\"LMB\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(glyph(\\\"reload\\\", Device::Gamepad, false), \\\"Square\\\");\\n\\n    w.screen = Screen::Dev;\\n    w.tab = 5;\\n    w.page = 1;\\n    w.focus = 2;\\n    let before = w.tune.fire_spread;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { right: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert!(w.tune.fire_spread > before, \\\"{} -> {}\\\", before, w.tune.fire_spread);\\n    w.page = 3;\\n    w.focus = 3;\\n    w.apply_menu(MenuInput { confirm: true, ..MenuInput::default() });\\n    assert!((w.tune.fire_spread - w.tune0.fire_spread).abs() < 1e-4);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(3, Route::Human);\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 9.0);\\n    assert_ne!(w.screen, Screen::Attract);\\n    run(&mut w, &InputFrame::default(), 1.2);\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Attract);\\n    let saves = w.saves_written;\\n    for _ in 0..800 {\\n        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), 1.0);\\n    }\\n    assert!(w.attract_loops >= 5, \\\"loops {}\\\", w.attract_loops);\\n    assert_eq!(w.attract_seen, (1u16 << 10) - 1, \\\"seen {:b}\\\", w.attract_seen);\\n    assert_eq!(w.saves_written, saves);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(4, Route::Human);\\n    let mut seen = vec![format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", w.screen)];\\n    for bit in [buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP, buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP] {\\n        w.tick(&press(bit), DT);\\n        seen.push(format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", w.screen));\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Playing, \\\"{seen:?}\\\");\\n    assert!(seen.windows(2).all(|p| p[0] != p[1]), \\\"{seen:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fiction_has_no_source_names_and_no_audio_files() {\\n    let banned = [\\n        \\\"jackal\\\", \\\"ufll\\\", \\\"apr\\\", \\\"pala\\\", \\\"mosate\\\", \\\"bowa\\\", \\\"leboa\\\", \\\"oluwagembi\\\", \\\"mike's bar\\\", \\\"marty\\\", \\\"alencar\\\",\\n        \\\"warren clyde\\\", \\\"paul ferenc\\\", \\\"hyppolite\\\", \\\"xianyong\\\", \\\"josip\\\", \\\"hakim\\\", \\\"bilders\\\", \\\"quarbani\\\", \\\"voorhees\\\",\\n        \\\"todo\\\", \\\"tbd\\\", \\\"placeholder\\\", \\\"lorem\\\",\\n    ];\\n    for line in fiction_lines() {\\n        let low = line.to_lowercase();\\n        if low.contains(\\\"far cry 2\\\") {\\n            assert!(line.contains(\\\"Source:\\\"), \\\"{line}\\\");\\n        }\\n        for word in banned {\\n            assert!(!low.contains(word), \\\"{word} in {line}\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let root = Path::new(env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\")).join(\\\"src/games/merc\\\");\\n    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(&root).unwrap() {\\n        let path = entry.unwrap().path();\\n        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(&path).unwrap_or_default().to_lowercase();\\n        for word in banned {\\n            assert!(!text.contains(word), \\\"{word} in {}\\\", path.display());\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let engine = Path::new(env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\")).join(\\\"../..\\\");\\n    let mut audio = Vec::new();\\n    walk_audio(&engine, &mut audio);\\n    assert!(audio.is_empty(), \\\"shipped audio files: {audio:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\\nfn walk_audio(dir: &Path, out: &mut Vec<String>) {\\n    let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(dir) else { return };\\n    for entry in rd.flatten() {\\n        let path = entry.path();\\n        if path.file_name().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\\\"target\\\") {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if path.is_dir() {\\n            walk_audio(&path, out);\\n        } else if let Some(ext) = path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) {\\n            if matches!(ext, \\\"wav\\\" | \\\"mp3\\\" | \\\"ogg\\\") {\\n                out.push(path.display().to_string());\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn net_loopback_shares_one_fire_cell() {\\n    let mut host = World::fresh(1);\\n    let mut client = World::fresh(2);\\n    assert!(host.fire.ignite_at(200.0, -200.0, 10.0, host.minutes));\\n    let mut link = Link::new(7, 0.15, 0.0, 0.0);\\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, false);\\n    assert!(link.max_bytes < 1200);\\n    for _ in 0..10 {\\n        link.advance(0.1);\\n    }\\n    let bodies = link.poll();\\n    assert!(bodies.iter().any(|b| b.contains(\\\"\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fire\\\\\\\"\\\")));\\n    client_apply(&mut client, &bodies);\\n    let shared = host.fire.cells.keys().any(|c| client.fire.cells.get(c).is_some_and(|cell| cell.burning));\\n    assert!(shared, \\\"host and client should share a burning cell within 1s\\\");\\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, true);\\n    assert_eq!(link.finishes, 1);\\n    host_publish(&host, &mut link, true);\\n    assert_eq!(link.finishes, 1);\\n\\n    let mut lossy = Link::new(1, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\\n    lossy.send(false, \\\"{\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ping\\\\\\\"}\\\".into());\\n    lossy.advance(0.1);\\n    assert!(lossy.poll().is_empty());\\n    lossy.send(true, \\\"{\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ping\\\\\\\"}\\\".into());\\n    lossy.advance(0.1);\\n    assert_eq!(lossy.poll().len(), 1);\\n}\\n\\nconst COVERAGE: &[&str] = &[\\n    \\\"map_raised\\\", \\\"waypoint_set\\\", \\\"gps_followed\\\", \\\"monocular_tag\\\", \\\"wind_rag\\\", \\\"jam_cleared\\\", \\\"enemy_jam\\\", \\\"weapon_broke\\\",\\n    \\\"weapon_bought\\\", \\\"locker_used\\\", \\\"syrette\\\", \\\"wound_gunshot\\\", \\\"wound_shrapnel\\\", \\\"wound_burn\\\", \\\"wound_fall\\\", \\\"wound_tourniquet\\\",\\n    \\\"wound_graze\\\", \\\"fever_warned\\\", \\\"pill_taken\\\", \\\"blackout\\\", \\\"player_rescued\\\", \\\"companion_patched\\\", \\\"companion_overdosed\\\",\\n    \\\"companion_died\\\", \\\"better_way\\\", \\\"ignite_flare\\\", \\\"ignite_rocket\\\", \\\"ignite_flamer\\\", \\\"ignite_mortar\\\", \\\"ignite_molotov\\\",\\n    \\\"ignite_frag\\\", \\\"ignite_barrel\\\", \\\"ignite_vehicle\\\", \\\"ignite_person\\\", \\\"ignite_lightning\\\", \\\"ignite_tracer\\\", \\\"ignite_cigarette\\\",\\n    \\\"cells_500\\\", \\\"enemy_panicked\\\", \\\"animals_fled\\\", \\\"explosion_chain\\\", \\\"rain_extinguished\\\", \\\"stealth_kill\\\", \\\"dart_kill\\\",\\n    \\\"night_contract\\\", \\\"sleep_used\\\", \\\"safe_house_claimed\\\", \\\"post_cleared\\\", \\\"post_remanned\\\", \\\"technical_driven\\\", \\\"mounted_gun\\\",\\n    \\\"repair_done\\\", \\\"boat_driven\\\", \\\"bus_taken\\\", \\\"tape_played\\\", \\\"cache_tracker\\\", \\\"diamonds_spent\\\", \\\"contract_a0\\\", \\\"contract_a1\\\",\\n    \\\"contract_b1\\\", \\\"contract_b2\\\", \\\"contract_b3\\\", \\\"contract_b4\\\", \\\"contract_c1\\\", \\\"contract_c2\\\", \\\"contract_c3\\\", \\\"contract_d1\\\",\\n    \\\"contract_d2\\\", \\\"ceasefire_ended\\\", \\\"town_burned\\\", \\\"ending_burn\\\", \\\"ending_read\\\", \\\"ending_chair\\\",\\n];\\n\\nfn play_route(route: Route, seed: u64) -> BTreeSet<String> {\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(seed, route);\\n    let mut goal = String::new();\\n    let mut stuck = 0.0f32;\\n    let cap = 60.0 * 900.0;\\n    let mut t = 0.0f32;\\n    while t < cap && !w.finished {\\n        let input = w.bot_input();\\n        let before = w.goal_name();\\n        w.tick(&input, DT);\\n        t += DT;\\n        let now = w.goal_name();\\n        if now != before {\\n            if goal != before {\\n                eprintln!(\\\"{route:?} seed {seed}: {before} -> {now} at ({:.0},{:.0}) t={t:.0}\\\", w.x, w.z);\\n            }\\n            goal = now;\\n            stuck = 0.0;\\n        } else {\\n            stuck += DT;\\n            let budget = w.goal_budget();\\n            if stuck > budget && !w.finished {\\n                panic!(\\n                    \\\"{route:?} seed {seed} stuck on {now} for {stuck:.0}s (budget {budget:.0}) at ({:.1},{:.1}) step {} flags {}\\\",\\n                    w.x, w.z, w.step, w.flags.len()\\n                );\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    assert!(w.finished, \\\"{route:?} seed {seed} did not finish by {t:.0}s goal {} at ({:.0},{:.0})\\\", w.goal_name(), w.x, w.z);\\n    let end = match route {\\n        Route::Read => \\\"ending_read\\\",\\n        Route::Chair => \\\"ending_chair\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"ending_burn\\\",\\n    };\\n    assert!(w.flags.contains(end), \\\"{route:?} missing {end}\\\");\\n    w.flags\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn bot_plays_all_three_endings() {\\n    let mut union = BTreeSet::new();\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2] {\\n        let mut prefix_a = World::campaign(seed, Route::Human);\\n        let mut prefix_b = World::campaign(seed, Route::Human);\\n        for _ in 0..40 {\\n            let a = prefix_a.bot_input();\\n            let b = prefix_b.bot_input();\\n            prefix_a.tick(&a, DT);\\n            prefix_b.tick(&b, DT);\\n        }\\n        assert_eq!(prefix_a.fingerprint(), prefix_b.fingerprint());\\n        for route in [Route::Human, Route::Read, Route::Chair] {\\n            union.extend(play_route(route, seed));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let missing: Vec<_> = COVERAGE.iter().copied().filter(|f| !union.contains(*f)).collect();\\n    assert!(missing.is_empty(), \\\"coverage missing {missing:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"b4be13a7-0576-4195-8b8b-4dd15424287e"}
