{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_165","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading the river, nearest_water, and rain tick order carefully.\n\nBoat passage confirmed water logic works. Rain at x+3 lands on the river centerline, so ignite fails and no new burning cells spawn there. Earlier fires should still be burning after 71 seconds, but rain clears all burning cells globally. The question is why any fire remains.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1644fdd0-fd17-4a03-879b-8918e421074e-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":1,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1406,"output_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":86272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"649028b6-c3b2-4cc4-a340-0ffd7dc2efa4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1644fdd0-fd17-4a03-879b-8918e421074e-31","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Map queries for the Republic of Kwelara. Coordinates: x east, z south, origin at the map centre.\\n//! The playable square is 2048 m on a side.\\n\\nuse crate::rng::hash_f32;\\n\\npub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\\n\\npub struct Place {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n10→    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\\n    Place { name: \\\"Airstrip\\\", x: -120.0, z: 900.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilo 38\\\", x: -40.0, z: 640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilometre 40\\\", x: 0.0, z: 380.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump House\\\", x: 170.0, z: 470.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Bridge\\\", x: 40.0, z: 40.0 },\\n20→    Place { name: \\\"North Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: 110.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"South Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ste-Odile\\\", x: 720.0, z: 420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ferry\\\", x: 640.0, z: 170.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Boat Shed\\\", x: 830.0, z: 255.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump Station\\\", x: -420.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ombe Flats\\\", x: -520.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Junction\\\", x: 20.0, z: -420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Flats Post\\\", x: 60.0, z: -460.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\", x: -260.0, z: -700.0 },\\n30→    Place { name: \\\"Ridge Post\\\", x: 360.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Hotel Splendide\\\", x: 620.0, z: -640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Quarry Post\\\", x: -420.0, z: 480.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Cement Works\\\", x: -760.0, z: 620.0 },\\n];\\n\\nconst RIVER: &[(f32, f32)] = &[\\n    (1024.0, 120.0),\\n    (760.0, 260.0),\\n    (420.0, 90.0),\\n40→    (120.0, 40.0),\\n    (-200.0, -40.0),\\n    (-560.0, 60.0),\\n    (-820.0, 220.0),\\n    (-1024.0, 180.0),\\n];\\n\\npub fn place(name: &str) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    PLACES.iter().find(|p| p.name == name).map(|p| (p.x, p.z)).unwrap_or((0.0, 380.0))\\n}\\n50→\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n60→\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n70→}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\n80→pub fn on_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 12.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Deep enough for the outboard. The edges of the channel are shallows.\\npub fn deep_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 7.0\\n}\\n\\n/// A point `metres` further along the channel from the closest point on the centre line.\\n90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n140→        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\\n        i += 1;\\n        t = 0.0;\\n        if i + 1 >= RIVER.len() {\\n            return RIVER[RIVER.len() - 1];\\n        }\\n150→    }\\n    RIVER[best_i]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best = (x, z);\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n160→        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = (px, pz);\\n        }\\n    }\\n170→    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n180→    }\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Map queries for the Republic of Kwelara. Coordinates: x east, z south, origin at the map centre.\\n//! The playable square is 2048 m on a side.\\n\\nuse crate::rng::hash_f32;\\n\\npub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\\n\\npub struct Place {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n10→    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\\n    Place { name: \\\"Airstrip\\\", x: -120.0, z: 900.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilo 38\\\", x: -40.0, z: 640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilometre 40\\\", x: 0.0, z: 380.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump House\\\", x: 170.0, z: 470.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Bridge\\\", x: 40.0, z: 40.0 },\\n20→    Place { name: \\\"North Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: 110.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"South Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ste-Odile\\\", x: 720.0, z: 420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ferry\\\", x: 640.0, z: 170.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Boat Shed\\\", x: 830.0, z: 255.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump Station\\\", x: -420.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ombe Flats\\\", x: -520.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Junction\\\", x: 20.0, z: -420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Flats Post\\\", x: 60.0, z: -460.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\", x: -260.0, z: -700.0 },\\n30→    Place { name: \\\"Ridge Post\\\", x: 360.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Hotel Splendide\\\", x: 620.0, z: -640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Quarry Post\\\", x: -420.0, z: 480.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Cement Works\\\", x: -760.0, z: 620.0 },\\n];\\n\\nconst RIVER: &[(f32, f32)] = &[\\n    (1024.0, 120.0),\\n    (760.0, 260.0),\\n    (420.0, 90.0),\\n40→    (120.0, 40.0),\\n    (-200.0, -40.0),\\n    (-560.0, 60.0),\\n    (-820.0, 220.0),\\n    (-1024.0, 180.0),\\n];\\n\\npub fn place(name: &str) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    PLACES.iter().find(|p| p.name == name).map(|p| (p.x, p.z)).unwrap_or((0.0, 380.0))\\n}\\n50→\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n60→\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n70→}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\n80→pub fn on_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 12.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Deep enough for the outboard. The edges of the channel are shallows.\\npub fn deep_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 7.0\\n}\\n\\n/// A point `metres` further along the channel from the closest point on the centre line.\\n90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n140→        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\\n        i += 1;\\n        t = 0.0;\\n        if i + 1 >= RIVER.len() {\\n            return RIVER[RIVER.len() - 1];\\n        }\\n150→    }\\n    RIVER[best_i]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best = (x, z);\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n160→        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = (px, pz);\\n        }\\n    }\\n170→    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n180→    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":180,\"raw_output\":\"//! Map queries for the Republic of Kwelara. Coordinates: x east, z south, origin at the map centre.\\n//! The playable square is 2048 m on a side.\\n\\nuse crate::rng::hash_f32;\\n\\npub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\\n\\npub struct Place {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\\n    Place { name: \\\"Airstrip\\\", x: -120.0, z: 900.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilo 38\\\", x: -40.0, z: 640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilometre 40\\\", x: 0.0, z: 380.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump House\\\", x: 170.0, z: 470.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Bridge\\\", x: 40.0, z: 40.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"North Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: 110.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"South Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ste-Odile\\\", x: 720.0, z: 420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ferry\\\", x: 640.0, z: 170.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Boat Shed\\\", x: 830.0, z: 255.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump Station\\\", x: -420.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ombe Flats\\\", x: -520.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Junction\\\", x: 20.0, z: -420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Flats Post\\\", x: 60.0, z: -460.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\", x: -260.0, z: -700.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ridge Post\\\", x: 360.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Hotel Splendide\\\", x: 620.0, z: -640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Quarry Post\\\", x: -420.0, z: 480.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Cement Works\\\", x: -760.0, z: 620.0 },\\n];\\n\\nconst RIVER: &[(f32, f32)] = &[\\n    (1024.0, 120.0),\\n    (760.0, 260.0),\\n    (420.0, 90.0),\\n    (120.0, 40.0),\\n    (-200.0, -40.0),\\n    (-560.0, 60.0),\\n    (-820.0, 220.0),\\n    (-1024.0, 180.0),\\n];\\n\\npub fn place(name: &str) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    PLACES.iter().find(|p| p.name == name).map(|p| (p.x, p.z)).unwrap_or((0.0, 380.0))\\n}\\n\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 12.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Deep enough for the outboard. The edges of the channel are shallows.\\npub fn deep_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 7.0\\n}\\n\\n/// A point `metres` further along the channel from the closest point on the centre line.\\npub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\\n        i += 1;\\n        t = 0.0;\\n        if i + 1 >= RIVER.len() {\\n            return RIVER[RIVER.len() - 1];\\n        }\\n    }\\n    RIVER[best_i]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best = (x, z);\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = (px, pz);\\n        }\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":284}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d1810e15-577a-4ae3-bea1-0f1804a2053c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_166","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The player is exactly on a river vertex at (-200, -40).\n\nThe player's half-width of 12 keeps the fire at +3 x in water. The rain fix will search concentric rings for a grassy cell to ignite.\n\nThe ring search at radius 14 lands on grass at (-186, -40). Rain ticks before script advancement. The repair tick leaves weather at zero. The next tick applies rain and extinguishes the fire. This only fails if ignition and rain coincide in one tick.\n\nThe 30-second budget is more than enough. The ring search also fixes a bug where extinguished stays zero when no cells are burning. Weather is set to rain even if ignition fails, but the search should prevent that. Rain cannot strike the same tick as fire.tick. The repair-completion tick triggers begin(Rain) after simulate, so the next player tick sees weather==1 and clears the fire.\n\nThe Better step's begin handler is a no-op. It never marks better_way or downgrades the companion, so done(Better) can never pass.\n\nBetter stalls forever because its begin handler never sets better_way or downgrades the companion. Patch only marks that flag after Better is already done. The fix is to mark better_way in begin(Better) or at the choice entry point.\n\nThe Better step will mark better_way in its begin handler. It will also downgrade a companion so done(Better) can pass.\n\nThe Better step will downgrade the nearest alive companion by setting down to true and offsetting them 1.5 units east. Patch begin will also mark better_way and set down, but this is harmless.\n\nCeasefire spawns a soldier 30 meters north and equips a sniper. The bot aims and fires. Sniper damage is 110 against 30 health, so one shot should kill it. Range is 400, so the target should be hit.\n\nCeasefire completion depends on either the soldier dying during shots_tick or the player pressing interact while the Ceasefire step is active. The bot may not press interact after firing, so a miss would stall the step. I need to check whether try_interact runs unconditionally each tick.\n\nThe bot does not press the interact button during ceasefire, so the soldier must be killed by the sniper shot itself. Convoy should one-shot the truck with an RPG. Town completes immediately because begin marks town_burned before done is checked in the same loop. Driving to cement from town takes roughly fifty seconds, well within the one-hundred-forty-second budget.\n\nEnding(0) completes in one tick because script_ignite marks ending_burn on the next tick after the step begins. The read-ending route needs 180 seconds under fire, which fits within the 200-second budget; the bot will crouch and wait. Soldiers spawn at 40 meters and may shoot, so the player could still die.\n\nThe read-ending timer continues even if the player dies, because simulate still runs and script_ignite marks the flag. The Die route places a companion 40 meters away and sets its down timer to 45 seconds; the bot must rescue them within the 55-second budget.\n\nThe Die route is safe because the bot never holds interact, so patch_or_dose cannot heal the companion and the 45-second down timer expires before the 55-second budget. Better now downs the companion and moves them 40 meters away, which Die begin resets to zero.\n\nOverdose requires syrettes. The bot used one in the syrette step, so it may have none left. Overdose begin will ensure at least one syrette remains.\n\nPatch begin also marks better_way and resets the companion down timer to zero. The bot must hold interact for three seconds while syrettes remain above zero, so Patch will also ensure at least one syrette is available. The rain bug is the only remaining real staller; Better and syrette stock are just code-level gates that will not block progress.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cc3a3d6-05c9-4ac1-916d-3f6ffe5881ed-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"syrettes","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2872,"output_tokens":2424,"cache_read_input_tokens":87552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5ad77b32-58a9-4d2a-b447-cd91bc8d93df"}
