\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"test bot_plays_all_three_endings ... Human seed 1: boot -> map at (-120,900) t=0\"},{\"line_number\":81,\"content\":\"Human seed 1: drive -> ending0 at (-749,616) t=411\"},{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"Human seed 1: ending0 -> done at (-749,616) t=411\"},{\"line_number\":138,\"content\":\"Read seed 1: drive -> ending1 at (-749,616) t=490\"},{\"line_number\":139,\"content\":\"Read seed 1: ending1 -> done at (-754,618) t=670\"},{\"line_number\":196,\"content\":\"Chair seed 1: drive -> ending2 at (-749,616) t=453\"},{\"line_number\":197,\"content\":\"Chair seed 1: ending2 -> done at (-749,616) t=453\"},{\"line_number\":207,\"content\":\"thread 'bot_plays_all_three_endings' (479733) panicked at crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs:707:17:\"},{\"line_number\":208,\"content\":\"Human seed 2 stuck on enemy_jam for 25s (budget 25) at (-37.9,630.3) step 9 flags 7\"},{\"line_number\":210,\"content\":\"FAILED\"},{\"line_number\":215,\"content\":\"    bot_plays_all_three_endings\"},{\"line_number\":217,\"content\":\"test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 15 filtered out; finished in 0.63s\"},{\"line_number\":220,\"content\":\"EXIT:101\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3b33fd06-695b-428c-8d63-660091fe5aaf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_174","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All three endings for seed 1 are complete.\n\nSeed 2 is stuck on enemy_jam. The soldier with condition 5 never jams within the 25-second budget. Seed 1 passed this step in the same second.\n\nThe jam probability is only about 19% per shot. At the enemy's 600 RPM, the soldier should jam within a second if it fires. The stall likely means the soldier never alerts or never opens fire.\n\nThe soldier only fires when alert reaches 1 and the gun is not jammed. Alert starts at zero and rises from vision or nearby noise. The bot script for EnemyJam holds crouch during that phase.\n\nThe bot does not shoot during the enemy jam phase, so the soldier can only alert through vision. At default settings, the alert rate is roughly 0.5 per second from 8 meters away. It would take about 1.3 seconds to reach the threshold of 1.0, which is well within the 25-second budget. The stall on seed 2 therefore points to a different cause than slow alert buildup.\n\nThe soldier spawns almost exactly the same coordinates in both seeds, so position is not the cause. The hash-based tall_grass check may differ slightly between positions, blocking vision and preventing the alert threshold from rising.\n\nEven tall grass would still allow the soldier to alert within about two seconds, so that is not the cause. The real issue may be the time of day: at t=100 the simulation has advanced roughly 100 minutes, which could push the in-game hour into the night range.\n\nThe panic message shows the soldier is stuck at a fixed position, not merely delayed by time. If the soldier were firing, it should have jammed roughly 47 times within 25 seconds given the 19% probability, so the stall likely means it never opened fire.\n\nThe soldier never fires, so alert stays at zero. Vision only accumulates when the line of sight is clear. If fire spread from an earlier fight left a burning cell blocking the midpoint between player and soldier, vision would never reach the threshold. Seed 2 may have this smoke or fire cell in its RNG path.\n\nFire spread is ruled out. The player and enemy weapons do not ignite fire, and no smoke or flares are present at t=100. The soldier is likely still alive, since the enemy jam phase spawns a fresh soldier after the fight. The real cause of the stall remains unclear.\n\nThe soldier's initial jam state and the test's timestep are being checked. Morale is ruled out because clear_bodies() resets the dead count to zero. The spawn and enemy shoot code around the jam mark will be re-examined, possibly with a debug print.\n\nThe player is on foot, not prone or in a vehicle, so those states are ruled out. The difference between the two seeds likely comes from RNG during the fight itself, such as the player dying or their gun breaking. If the player is dead and rescue time has expired, they remain on the ground.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e17e83b6-ae9b-4b6c-8b4a-a296171bf97a-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/gun.rs","offset":120,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e17e83b6-ae9b-4b6c-8b4a-a296171bf97a-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1630,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e17e83b6-ae9b-4b6c-8b4a-a296171bf97a-43","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn play_route|DT|seed","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":660,"output_tokens":2154,"cache_read_input_tokens":98432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d09de8fc-c968-47c9-a695-f41d13ab8e94"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e17e83b6-ae9b-4b6c-8b4a-a296171bf97a-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→            shots: 0,\\n            jams: 0,\\n            force_jam: false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn family(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        stats(self.id).family\\n    }\\n\\n130→    /// One trigger pull. Jam is rolled before the bullet. A break is rolled on a real shot when\\n    /// condition is under the threshold (default 8) at 3 percent.\\n    pub fn pull(&mut self, rng: &mut Rng, jam_mul: f32, wear_mul: f32, break_at: f32) -> Pull {\\n        if self.cooldown > 0.0 {\\n            return Pull::Waiting;\\n        }\\n        if self.jammed {\\n            return Pull::Jammed;\\n        }\\n        if self.broken || self.ammo == 0 {\\n140→            return Pull::Dry;\\n        }\\n        let p = jam_probability(self.condition) * jam_mul.max(0.0);\\n        if self.force_jam || (p > 0.0 && rng.f32() < p) {\\n            self.jammed = true;\\n            self.force_jam = false;\\n            self.jams += 1;\\n            self.cooldown = 0.15;\\n            return Pull::Jammed;\\n        }\\n150→        self.ammo -= 1;\\n        self.shots += 1;\\n        let rpm = stats(self.id).rpm.max(1.0);\\n        self.cooldown = 60.0 / rpm;\\n        self.condition = (self.condition - self.wear * wear_mul.max(0.0)).max(0.0);\\n        if self.condition < break_at && rng.f32() < 0.03 {\\n            self.broken = true;\\n            return Pull::Broke;\\n        }\\n        Pull::Fired\\n160→    }\\n\\n    /// Start clearing a jam, or slap the bolt. A second tap shortens the remaining time by 40%.\\n    pub fn tap_reload(&mut self) {\\n        if self.jammed && self.clear_left <= 0.0 {\\n            self.clear_left = clear_seconds(self.condition);\\n            self.slapped = false;\\n        } else if self.jammed && self.clear_left > 0.0 && !self.slapped {\\n            self.clear_left *= 0.6;\\n            self.slapped = true;\\n170→        } else if !self.jammed && !self.broken {\\n            let s = stats(self.id);\\n            let need = s.mag.saturating_sub(self.ammo);\\n            let take = need.min(self.reserve);\\n            self.ammo += take;\\n            self.reserve -= take;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn tick_clear(&mut self, dt: f32) {\\n180→        if self.clear_left > 0.0 {\\n            self.clear_left = (self.clear_left - dt).max(0.0);\\n            if self.clear_left == 0.0 {\\n                self.jammed = false;\\n                self.slapped = false;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.cooldown > 0.0 {\\n            self.cooldown = (self.cooldown - dt).max(0.0);\\n        }\\n190→    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"120→            shots: 0,\\n            jams: 0,\\n            force_jam: false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn family(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        stats(self.id).family\\n    }\\n\\n130→    /// One trigger pull. Jam is rolled before the bullet. A break is rolled on a real shot when\\n    /// condition is under the threshold (default 8) at 3 percent.\\n    pub fn pull(&mut self, rng: &mut Rng, jam_mul: f32, wear_mul: f32, break_at: f32) -> Pull {\\n        if self.cooldown > 0.0 {\\n            return Pull::Waiting;\\n        }\\n        if self.jammed {\\n            return Pull::Jammed;\\n        }\\n        if self.broken || self.ammo == 0 {\\n140→            return Pull::Dry;\\n        }\\n        let p = jam_probability(self.condition) * jam_mul.max(0.0);\\n        if self.force_jam || (p > 0.0 && rng.f32() < p) {\\n            self.jammed = true;\\n            self.force_jam = false;\\n            self.jams += 1;\\n            self.cooldown = 0.15;\\n            return Pull::Jammed;\\n        }\\n150→        self.ammo -= 1;\\n        self.shots += 1;\\n        let rpm = stats(self.id).rpm.max(1.0);\\n        self.cooldown = 60.0 / rpm;\\n        self.condition = (self.condition - self.wear * wear_mul.max(0.0)).max(0.0);\\n        if self.condition < break_at && rng.f32() < 0.03 {\\n            self.broken = true;\\n            return Pull::Broke;\\n        }\\n        Pull::Fired\\n160→    }\\n\\n    /// Start clearing a jam, or slap the bolt. A second tap shortens the remaining time by 40%.\\n    pub fn tap_reload(&mut self) {\\n        if self.jammed && self.clear_left <= 0.0 {\\n            self.clear_left = clear_seconds(self.condition);\\n            self.slapped = false;\\n        } else if self.jammed && self.clear_left > 0.0 && !self.slapped {\\n            self.clear_left *= 0.6;\\n            self.slapped = true;\\n170→        } else if !self.jammed && !self.broken {\\n            let s = stats(self.id);\\n            let need = s.mag.saturating_sub(self.ammo);\\n            let take = need.min(self.reserve);\\n            self.ammo += take;\\n            self.reserve -= take;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn tick_clear(&mut self, dt: f32) {\\n180→        if self.clear_left > 0.0 {\\n            self.clear_left = (self.clear_left - dt).max(0.0);\\n            if self.clear_left == 0.0 {\\n                self.jammed = false;\\n                self.slapped = false;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.cooldown > 0.0 {\\n            self.cooldown = (self.cooldown - dt).max(0.0);\\n        }\\n190→    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/gun.rs\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"            shots: 0,\\n            jams: 0,\\n            force_jam: false,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn family(&self) -> &'static str {\\n        stats(self.id).family\\n    }\\n\\n    /// One trigger pull. Jam is rolled before the bullet. A break is rolled on a real shot when\\n    /// condition is under the threshold (default 8) at 3 percent.\\n    pub fn pull(&mut self, rng: &mut Rng, jam_mul: f32, wear_mul: f32, break_at: f32) -> Pull {\\n        if self.cooldown > 0.0 {\\n            return Pull::Waiting;\\n        }\\n        if self.jammed {\\n            return Pull::Jammed;\\n        }\\n        if self.broken || self.ammo == 0 {\\n            return Pull::Dry;\\n        }\\n        let p = jam_probability(self.condition) * jam_mul.max(0.0);\\n        if self.force_jam || (p > 0.0 && rng.f32() < p) {\\n            self.jammed = true;\\n            self.force_jam = false;\\n            self.jams += 1;\\n            self.cooldown = 0.15;\\n            return Pull::Jammed;\\n        }\\n        self.ammo -= 1;\\n        self.shots += 1;\\n        let rpm = stats(self.id).rpm.max(1.0);\\n        self.cooldown = 60.0 / rpm;\\n        self.condition = (self.condition - self.wear * wear_mul.max(0.0)).max(0.0);\\n        if self.condition < break_at && rng.f32() < 0.03 {\\n            self.broken = true;\\n            return Pull::Broke;\\n        }\\n        Pull::Fired\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Start clearing a jam, or slap the bolt. A second tap shortens the remaining time by 40%.\\n    pub fn tap_reload(&mut self) {\\n        if self.jammed && self.clear_left <= 0.0 {\\n            self.clear_left = clear_seconds(self.condition);\\n            self.slapped = false;\\n        } else if self.jammed && self.clear_left > 0.0 && !self.slapped {\\n            self.clear_left *= 0.6;\\n            self.slapped = true;\\n        } else if !self.jammed && !self.broken {\\n            let s = stats(self.id);\\n            let need = s.mag.saturating_sub(self.ammo);\\n            let take = need.min(self.reserve);\\n            self.ammo += take;\\n            self.reserve -= take;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn tick_clear(&mut self, dt: f32) {\\n        if self.clear_left > 0.0 {\\n            self.clear_left = (self.clear_left - dt).max(0.0);\\n            if self.clear_left == 0.0 {\\n                self.jammed = false;\\n                self.slapped = false;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.cooldown > 0.0 {\\n            self.cooldown = (self.cooldown - dt).max(0.0);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":191}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e17e83b6-ae9b-4b6c-8b4a-a296171bf97a-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1630→            let crouched = stance == 1;\\n            let grass = grass_factor(px, pz, crouched);\\n            let posture = match stance {\\n                2 => 0.3,\\n                1 => 0.6,\\n                _ => 1.0,\\n            };\\n            let motion = 0.5;\\n            let rate = exposure(posture, grass, light, motion) * self.tune.detection;\\n            let dist = geom::dist(px, pz, self.bodies[i].x, self.bodies[i].z).max(1.0);\\n1640→            let falloff = (30.0 / dist).clamp(0.0, 1.5);\\n            let (mx, mz) = ((px + self.bodies[i].x) * 0.5, (pz + self.bodies[i].z) * 0.5);\\n            let smoked = self.fire.cells.get(&geom::cell_of(mx, mz)).is_some_and(|c| c.burning);\\n            if morale_broken && self.bodies[i].kind == 1 {\\n                self.bodies[i].x += 5.0 * dt;\\n                self.bodies[i].flee += 5.0 * dt;\\n                self.bodies[i].alert = 3;\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n            if !self.dev.invisible && !smoked && self.bodies[i].alert < 2 {\\n1650→                self.bodies[i].see += rate * falloff * dt;\\n                if self.bodies[i].see > 1.0 {\\n                    self.bodies[i].alert = 2;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            // Fire under an enemy makes them run.\\n            let (cx, cz) = (self.bodies[i].x, self.bodies[i].z);\\n            let cell = geom::cell_of(cx, cz);\\n            if self.fire.cells.get(&cell).map(|c| c.burning).unwrap_or(false) {\\n                self.bodies[i].alert = 4;\\n1660→                self.bodies[i].x += 4.0 * dt;\\n                self.bodies[i].flee += 4.0 * dt;\\n                if self.bodies[i].flee > 3.0 {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"enemy_panicked\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if self.bodies[i].kind == 1 && self.bodies[i].alert >= 1 && !self.bodies[i].gun.jammed {\\n                if shooters >= 4 {\\n                    // One extra soldier peels off to the side instead of adding a fifth gun.\\n                    self.bodies[i].x += 3.0 * dt;\\n1670→                    self.bodies[i].z += 1.5 * dt;\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                shooters += 1;\\n                let gpull = {\\n                    let jam = self.tune.jam_chance;\\n                    let wear = self.tune.weapon_wear;\\n                    let br = self.tune.break_threshold;\\n                    self.bodies[i].gun.pull(&mut self.rng, jam, wear, br)\\n                };\\n1680→                if gpull == Pull::Jammed {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"enemy_jam\\\");\\n                }\\n                if gpull == Pull::Fired && self.rng.f32() < self.tune.enemy_accuracy * 0.15 {\\n                    let diff = match self.difficulty {\\n                        0 => 0.7,\\n                        2 => 1.3,\\n                        _ => 1.0,\\n                    };\\n                    if !self.dev.god && self.rescue_t <= 0.0 {\\n1690→                        self.hp -= self.tune.enemy_damage * 0.15 * diff * dt.max(0.05) * 10.0;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            self.bodies[i].gun.tick_clear(dt);\\n            if self.bodies[i].hp <= 0.0 {\\n                self.bodies[i].alive = false;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n1700→\\n    fn update_fever(&mut self, dt: f32) {\\n        if self.dev.no_fever {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if self.fever_state == 0 {\\n            self.fever_t += dt;\\n            if self.fever_t >= self.tune.fever_interval {\\n                self.fever_s