102,105,110,105,115,104,101,100,32,105,110,32,49,46,48,53,115,10,51,56,54,58,69,88,73,84,58,49,48,49,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/play5.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":373,\"content\":\"thread 'bot_plays_all_three_endings' (486943) panicked at crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs:742:5:\"},{\"line_number\":374,\"content\":\"coverage missing [\\\"post_remanned\\\", \\\"contract_d2\\\"]\"},{\"line_number\":376,\"content\":\"FAILED\"},{\"line_number\":383,\"content\":\"test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 15 filtered out; finished in 1.05s\"},{\"line_number\":386,\"content\":\"EXIT:101\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d7d3ebf3-65d3-44e0-9cf7-41bee3b7b22e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_181","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All six routes finished. Missing flags: post_remanned and contract_d2.\n\ncontract_d2 is a Flag step that follows the Ending. The Ending sets finished to true, which causes advance_script to return early before the flag step ever runs.\n\nThe cleanest fix is to mark the ending flag in script_ignite without setting finished yet. The ending step's done() will check that flag and advance normally, letting the Flag step mark contract_d2 before finished is set.\n\nRemoving `self.finished = true` from the ending script_ignite arms is safe. The campaign end logic will set finished once the script exhausts after the flag step completes. Need to check if `play_route` asserts on `w.finished`.\n\nThe 26-hour sleep at SH2 completed, but the post_remanned flag never fired. The sleep begin path only marks it when the player is near a safe house, hold_t exceeds 0.8, and the current spec is Sleep. The conditions were likely not met.\n\nThe 26-hour sleep completed at the boat teleport. The post_remanned flag likely failed because post_clear was false. The maybe_reman step sets looking_at_post and clears post_clear when the player is not looking at the post.\n\nThe 26-hour sleep check should have marked post_remanned if post_clear was true. Since it did not, post_clear was likely false when the sleep began. The fight step that sets post_clear is not in the missing flags list, so it probably ran and cleared the flag before the sleep began.\n\nThe 8-hour sleep likely set `sleep_used`, which makes the 26-hour sleep step's `done()` return true immediately after it begins. This would skip the post-remanned check entirely. Also need to find what else clears `post_clear` without marking reman.\n\nThe 26-hour sleep step's `done()` returns true immediately on its first tick because `step_t` resets to zero at the start of `begin()`, and `done()` requires `step_t > 0.2`. Since `sleep_used` is already true from the earlier 8-hour sleep, the step completes before the post-remanned check can run.\n\nThe 26-hour sleep step is skipped because `sleep_used` is a sticky flag from the earlier 8-hour sleep. The fix should make `done(Sleep)` require an actual sleep during this step, not a stale flag. One approach is to clear a step-local \"slept_this_step\" flag on `begin` and set it when the sleep interact fires. Another is to remove `sleep_used` from the world flags on `begin`, though that may conflict with the union recording.\n\nThe fix is to use a step-local boolean for the sleep check instead of the sticky `sleep_used` flag. This prevents the 26-hour sleep from completing immediately while still allowing the post-remanned flag to be set during the actual sleep interact.\n\nThe fix adds a `slept_step` boolean to the World struct. `begin()` resets it to false, and the sleep step's `done()` now requires both this flag and `step_t > 0.2`. The sleep interact branch sets the flag alongside marking `sleep_used`. A new serde field is acceptable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-750825fe-3e9a-4083-a1ab-c2c162a72167-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":350,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-750825fe-3e9a-4083-a1ab-c2c162a72167-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"post_clear","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":438,"output_tokens":2189,"cache_read_input_tokens":109696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d97e301