{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_183","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Night sets minutes to 1320.\n\nThe script runs 26-hour sleep before Night. After the sleep, minutes reach ~1540. Night then sets minutes to 1320. The 26-hour sleep adds another ~1560 minutes. Total becomes ~2880. This is above the post-clear threshold. The interaction logic should mark reman correctly.\n\nThe reman mark during sleep interact is safe because post_clear remains true before Night. Even if minutes start at 480, the total after sleep still exceeds the post-clear threshold. The next concern is whether the bot can reach the lodge and hold interact within the 50-second budget.\n\nWalking to the lodge takes about one second, so the 50-second sleep budget is easily covered.\n\nAfter arrival, the bot presses USE to exit the seat. When the seat cycles back to zero, move_body works and the bot walks to the nearest safe spot. If that distance exceeds eight meters, it walks there before holding interact.\n\nWhile the seat is occupied, the bot only presses USE with zero axes, which causes the vehicle to slow down.\n\nDrift during the two-frame seat cycle is negligible, so the bot stays within the 16-meter radius. The concern is whether `just(USE)` evaluates to true every tick when the pressed flag is set continuously, or if it only triggers on the initial press edge.\n\nIf `just(USE)` evaluates to true every tick, the bot would press USE continuously. The seat would cycle endlessly between 0, 1, and 2. The bot would never hold INTERACT at seat zero.\n\nThe seat cycles cleanly through 1, 2, and 0. The bot presses USE while occupied and holds INTERACT once the seat returns to zero. This completes the exit sequence without getting stuck in an infinite loop.\n\nThe first eight-hour sleep succeeded, confirming the exit logic works. The 26-hour sleep was skipped only because the flag was already set; removing that flag should allow it to run. I will run the test and apply the contract_d2 fix. The read ending now takes roughly two seconds instead of one, which is acceptable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3ab2834-7cba-400a-bf4b-33a2f46d0a51-55","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine\" && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/target\" cargo test -p pav_core --test merc --offline bot_plays_all_three_endings -- --nocapture --test-threads=1 > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/play6.log\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$? >> \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/play6.log\"","description":"Re-run playthrough for reman and contract flags","block_until_ms":180000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2481,"output_tokens":1546,"cache_read_input_tokens":113536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"735d9557-c23f-42fd-b015-a50444dd2916"}
