5,116,32,98,121,32,80,73,68,46,10,53,56,58,45,32,84,104,101,32,104,117,98,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,110,101,101,100,115,32,97,32,108,111,99,97,108,32,115,101,114,118,101,114,46,32,83,111,108,111,32,112,108,97,121,32,109,117,115,116,32,115,116,105,108,108,32,119,111,114,107,32,102,114,111,109,32,96,102,105,108,101,58,47,47,96,46,32,68,111,32,110,111,116,32,116,114,101,97,116,32,97,32,115,101,114,118,101,114,45,111,110,108,121,32,112,97,103,101,32,97,115,32,109,101,101,116,105,110,103,32,99,114,105,116,101,114,105,111,110,32,49,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":22,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"## Goal kind\"},{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"5. **10-foot shell, code-only audio, attract, dev mode, and multiplayer.** Keyboard and mouse use the same screens as a standard-mapping gamepad, with prompts for the last device (PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox A B X Y in Settings). Mouse hover moves focus and click confirms. No screen has more than 7 focusable rows or a dense table. Touch-only shows the exact notice \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button, shows no touch controls, and still runs attract mode. After 10 seconds without input on the title or shell menus, a looping attract demo starts in the real world, reaches every scripted segment, writes no save, and any input exits it. Dev mode, opened from the pause menu and absent in a hub session, includes cheats, teleport, spawn, world controls, and live sliders for the balance variables in PLAN.md §8.7, each with reset to defaults. All music, sound effects, and voices are synthesized in code (no shipped wav, mp3, or ogg). Voices are syllable gibberish, not r [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"2. **gating:** Run the shipped native simulation tests (the game's own test binary, starting each case from a fresh boot) for look and movement, hitscan zones and wall blocking, jam rate, jam clear, weapon break, enemy jam, syrette and wound types, fever warning, pill clear, and no-pill blackout with a diamond fee. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/sim-combat.log`. Pass only if those assertions pass and the log shows zero failures for this group.\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"3. **gating:** Run the shipped native tests for fire (8 m/s downwind ≥ 3× upwind at 60 s, breaks, regrowth, rain, chain ignition, sparse snapshot), vehicles (slope, boat shallows, repair, explode-and-ignite, NPC driver), detection (grass, night, posture, smoke, noise), and guard-post re-man rules including \\\"not while visible\\\" and town holster. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/sim-world.log`. Pass only if each of those outcomes is asserted by the run, not by a re-implementation.\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"4. **gating:** Run the shipped bot from a new game through each of the three endings on normal difficulty, then assert the PLAN.md §15 coverage-flag union, companion rescue, patch, overdose, permadeath across save and load, and a file-backed save round trip of the §5.21 fields. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/playthrough.log`. Pass only if the log shows all three endings reached and zero failures. This run must be deterministic enough that a second run of the same seeds also passes.\"},{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"5. **gating:** Run the shipped UI and offline-audio tests: focus wrap and a max of 7 rows, glyphs follow device and the Xbox setting, attract starts at 10 s of idle and not before, any input exits, dev sliders change tunables and reset restores defaults, music RMS ratio 0.10 ± 0.01, voice output non-silent and different per speaker, no NaNs. Also search the dev tree for wav, mp3, and ogg files belonging to the game. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/ui-audio.log`. Pass only if those checks pass and no game audio files are found.\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"6. **gating:** Launch the real HTML from `file://` with Playwright Chromium more than once (two separate runs), using the engine WebGPU flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` (do not use `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`). Each run: zero page errors; the canvas drawing size equals the viewport requested for that run; the frame is substantially filled (painted fraction high or a painted bbox covering most of the surface, not a clear buffer); the visible title or the published UI state equals `{GameTitle}`; keyboard input (the Enter, Space, Enter, Space solo path) changes that state. Save screenshots and console logs to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must succeed. A readback that returns a blank image is a failure to fix. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-fail.log` and treat criteria 2–5's native tests plus a static check that [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"7. **gating:** On that same page, drive the shipped browser hooks: gamepad stub flips prompts to PlayStation glyphs, the Xbox setting changes them, pointer-lock mousemove changes yaw, losing the lock opens pause, a phone profile shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and Settings with attract running and no touch controls, WebKit (no WebGPU) shows a clear message instead of a blank page, dev mode toggles a cheat and a slider visible in published status, save then Continue works from `file://`, published music gain is 0.10, and About text contains the Source Information fields and all three feedback sections. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"8. **gating:** Serve the real page with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the fetched `<title>` is this game, run PLAN.md §14.4's four harness URLs, and stop only that server PID. Pass only if `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true for each case. Then play the standalone round on two pages through BroadcastChannel and through a pasted WebRTC code to the results screen, and assert the solo page does not mark the hub client active and does not use `Math.random` for shared-world state. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"- Dev subfolder `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/`, containing a shardfall engine clone (https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall) and the new game, plus downloaded ai-hub files from https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub (`session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`).\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"Follow PLAN.md as the design (milestones M0–M11, data in TOML, pure seeded simulation separate from rendering, UI, and the page). Verifiers judge the criteria above, not a matching directory tree or identical type names. Keep rules `Clone`-able and free of hashmap iteration order and wall-clock randomness so two runs of the same seed agree. Build the campaign bot beside each contract so the playthrough test stays cheap. Put numbers in data files. Expose game status and a test-command queue on the page for browser checks, and a no-draw switch so browser tests are not limited by software-rendered frame rate. Pack one HTML that runs from `file://` and still loads the unmodified session client first. Track answers for the feedback questions while working so About and `exit-interview.json` are filled from real notes, not blanks.\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"- [ ] Add companions, every PLAN.md §11 contract, three endings, saves, and a seeded bot playthrough that sets every §15 coverage flag.\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"- [ ] Add the hub depot round and standalone two-page play; pass the four harness cases and the solo check.\"},{\"line_number\":54,\"content\":\"## Risks / Contradictions\"},{\"line_number\":55,\"content\":\"- Software WebGPU on this host is slow, and the wrong Chromium flags (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`) leave a blank canvas that still reports frames. Use the flags in verification step 6. A blank screenshot from a successful readback is an app failure. If the browser process cannot start, step 6's written fallback applies. earlyoom kills the largest browser under memory pressure; keep a single browser and stop it by PID.\"},{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"- The hub harness needs a local server. Solo play must still work from `file://`. Do not treat a server-only page as meeting criterion 1.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-317f2b74-8acf-4f86-9d52-f0cf5c795dc7-60","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine\\\" && T=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/target\\\" && S=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer\\\" && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$T\\\" cargo test -p pav_core --test merc --offline > \\\"$S/sim-all.log\\\" 2>&1; echo MERC:$? >> \\\"$S/sim-all.log\\\"; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$T\\\" cargo test -p pav_audio --offline >> \\\"$S/sim-all.log\\\" 2>&1; echo AUDIO:$? >> \\\"$S/sim-all.log\\\"; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$T\\\" cargo test -p pav_view --lib --offline first_person >> \\\"$S/sim-all.log\\\" 2>&1; echo VIEW:$? >> \\\"$S/sim-all.log\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Re-run merc, audio, and camera tests\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/terminal/call-317f2b74-8acf-4f86-9d52-f0cf5c795dc7-60.log\",\"total_bytes\":0}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"22d495c5-a12f-43de-8ad8-7ad14f43e129"}
