0,59,32,48,32,105,103,110,111,114,101,100,59,32,48,32,109,101,97,115,117,114,101,100,59,32,48,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,101,100,32,111,117,116,59,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,101,100,32,105,110,32,48,46,48,48,115,10,54,49,58,65,85,68,73,79,58,48,10,55,48,58,116,101,115,116,32,114,101,115,117,108,116,58,32,111,107,46,32,49,32,112,97,115,115,101,100,59,32,48,32,102,97,105,108,101,100,59,32,48,32,105,103,110,111,114,101,100,59,32,48,32,109,101,97,115,117,114,101,100,59,32,49,56,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,101,100,32,111,117,116,59,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,101,100,32,105,110,32,48,46,48,48,115,10,55,50,58,86,73,69,87,58,48,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":7,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/sim-all.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 16 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.81s\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"MERC:0\"},{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"AUDIO:0\"},{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 18 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":72,\"content\":\"VIEW:0\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-97516ae6-d895-444b-bf66-4ad372ff8eb3-62","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"45→## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Clone the engine into the dev subfolder, pick the title with 50 names plus a real RNG, save the notes, register the game scene, place unmodified `session.js` first, and make the single test command print a one-line count.\\n- [ ] Add first-person look and movement, the controller and keyboard layouts, a held weapon with the wind rag, hitscan, and a sky, and pass the combat sim tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 2048 m country, wind-driven fire, weapon condition and jams, healing and fever, stealth and guard posts, and drivable vehicles and the boat; pass the world sim tests.\\n- [ ] Add companions, every PLAN.md §11 contract, three endings, saves, and a seeded bot playthrough that sets every §15 coverage flag.\\n50→- [ ] Add code-only music, effects, and gibberish voices with music at 10%, plus the 10-foot shell, dev-mode sliders, attract mode, touch-only notice, and About/Credits.\\n- [ ] Add the hub depot round and standalone two-page play; pass the four harness cases and the solo check.\\n- [ ] Pack `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` into the work root, write `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md`, run the full test command and the file:// launch twice, and store the captured logs.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- Software WebGPU on this host is slow, and the wrong Chromium flags (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`) leave a blank canvas that still reports frames. Use the flags in verification step 6. A blank screenshot from a successful readback is an app failure. If the browser process cannot start, step 6's written fallback applies. earlyoom kills the largest browser under memory pressure; keep a single browser and stop it by PID.\\n- PLAN.md §1.5 allows cutting instance counts, never systems. Criterion 4 follows that. It is not a license to drop fire, jams, fever, companions, a contract row, or an ending.\\n- TASK.md also asks for the Source Information and the three feedback sections in the implementer's chat reply. The checkable copies are About/Credits and `exit-interview.json`; the reply must repeat them, and verifiers do not fail the goal only because they cannot see the chat.\\n- The hub harness needs a local server. Solo play must still work from `file://`. Do not treat a server-only page as meeting criterion 1.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"45→## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Clone the engine into the dev subfolder, pick the title with 50 names plus a real RNG, save the notes, register the game scene, place unmodified `session.js` first, and make the single test command print a one-line count.\\n- [ ] Add first-person look and movement, the controller and keyboard layouts, a held weapon with the wind rag, hitscan, and a sky, and pass the combat sim tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 2048 m country, wind-driven fire, weapon condition and jams, healing and fever, stealth and guard posts, and drivable vehicles and the boat; pass the world sim tests.\\n- [ ] Add companions, every PLAN.md §11 contract, three endings, saves, and a seeded bot playthrough that sets every §15 coverage flag.\\n50→- [ ] Add code-only music, effects, and gibberish voices with music at 10%, plus the 10-foot shell, dev-mode sliders, attract mode, touch-only notice, and About/Credits.\\n- [ ] Add the hub depot round and standalone two-page play; pass the four harness cases and the solo check.\\n- [ ] Pack `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` into the work root, write `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md`, run the full test command and the file:// launch twice, and store the captured logs.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- Software WebGPU on this host is slow, and the wrong Chromium flags (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`) leave a blank canvas that still reports frames. Use the flags in verification step 6. A blank screenshot from a successful readback is an app failure. If the browser process cannot start, step 6's written fallback applies. earlyoom kills the largest browser under memory pressure; keep a single browser and stop it by PID.\\n- PLAN.md §1.5 allows cutting instance counts, never systems. Criterion 4 follows that. It is not a license to drop fire, jams, fever, companions, a contract row, or an ending.\\n- TASK.md also asks for the Source Information and the three feedback sections in the implementer's chat reply. The checkable copies are About/Credits and `exit-interview.json`; the reply must repeat them, and verifiers do not fail the goal only because they cannot see the chat.\\n- The hub harness needs a local server. Solo play must still work from `file://`. Do not treat a server-only page as meeting criterion 1.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":45,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Clone the engine into the dev subfolder, pick the title with 50 names plus a real RNG, save the notes, register the game scene, place unmodified `session.js` first, and make the single test command print a one-line count.\\n- [ ] Add first-person look and movement, the controller and keyboard layouts, a held weapon with the wind rag, hitscan, and a sky, and pass the combat sim tests.\\n- [ ] Add the 2048 m country, wind-driven fire, weapon condition and jams, healing and fever, stealth and guard posts, and drivable vehicles and the boat; pass the world sim tests.\\n- [ ] Add companions, every PLAN.md §11 contract, three endings, saves, and a seeded bot playthrough that sets every §15 coverage flag.\\n- [ ] Add code-only music, effects, and gibberish voices with music at 10%, plus the 10-foot shell, dev-mode sliders, attract mode, touch-only notice, and About/Credits.\\n- [ ] Add the hub depot round and standalone two-page play; pass the four harness cases and the solo check.\\n- [ ] Pack `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` into the work root, write `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md`, run the full test command and the file:// launch twice, and store the captured logs.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- Software WebGPU on this host is slow, and the wrong Chromium flags (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`) leave a blank canvas that still reports frames. Use the flags in verification step 6. A blank screenshot from a successful readback is an app failure. If the browser process cannot start, step 6's written fallback applies. earlyoom kills the largest browser under memory pressure; keep a single browser and stop it by PID.\\n- PLAN.md §1.5 allows cutting instance counts, never systems. Criterion 4 follows that. It is not a license to drop fire, jams, fever, companions, a contract row, or an ending.\\n- TASK.md also asks for the Source Information and the three feedback sections in the implementer's chat reply. The checkable copies are About/Credits and `exit-interview.json`; the reply must repeat them, and verifiers do not fail the goal only because they cannot see the chat.\\n- The hub harness needs a local server. Solo play must still work from `file://`. Do not treat a server-only page as meeting criterion 1.\\n\",\"total_lines\":58}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-97516ae6-d895-444b-bf66-4ad372ff8eb3-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-05 01:35:03\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n120→    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\n130→Testing Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n140→- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-05 01:35:03\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n120→    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\n130→Testing Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n140→- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/TASK.md\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-05 01:35:03\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"b88a4a32-a0d8-4267-a22b-391fb8d18193"}
