{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_192","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The merc game is a Game trait on the sim, not the ARPG \"game\" mode.\n\nMerc scene needs rig.fp set from world eye/yaw/pitch. Stick input should be raw for merc since stick-space is locked. Look input comes from mouse movement. Pause and escape handling must be skipped for merc. Now reviewing InputFrame fields and game_input.\n\nA `merc_mode` check will detect the merc scene. The rig.fp will be set from the published world status snapshot. Input will map keys to merc buttons and use mouse delta for look, with Enter or Space as act confirm. The egui pause menu and HUD will be hidden. The clock cap will be 120 fps when not playing or drawing, otherwise 8.\n\nA Shared control flag will let the clock know the screen. The WASM side needs a JS hook to publish window.__game every 15 ticks via wasm_bindgen. I will check boot.rs, snapshot status, pack_single_html.py, and PLAN sections 14.4 and 15 for the HTML harness and controls.\n\nI will read InputFrame and the app input struct to find where escape opens pause. Shell screens and MenuInput must align between JS and Rust.\n\nThe browser test needs four confirmations: Title, Difficulty, Merc, Prologue, then Playing. The HTML keyboard handler sends these to the sim. Rust must receive them.\n\nWinit on wasm may not reliably receive dispatched keyboard events. A page-level keydown listener in capture phase is more reliable. It can push keys into a queue that Rust polls via gameBridge.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15a5e361-3032-4970-9f47-def3d0756ec0-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gameTest|__game|nodraw|gameBridge|14\\.4|harness|Enter, Space","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15a5e361-3032-4970-9f47-def3d0756ec0-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/mic