1,96,32,124,32,111,110,99,101,44,32,119,104,101,110,32,116,104,101,32,114,111,117,110,100,32,99,97,110,32,115,116,97,114,116,32,124,10,51,55,57,58,124,32,96,65,73,72,117,98,46,97,110,115,119,101,114,40,39,114,101,97,100,121,39,32,92,124,32,39,109,111,114,101,39,41,96,32,124,32,111,110,32,116,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,39,115,32,111,119,110,32,99,97,114,100,44,32,98,101,102,111,114,101,32,96,115,116,97,114,116,96,32,124,10,51,56,52,58,124,32,96,65,73,72,117,98,46,102,105,110,105,115,104,40,123,32,115,116,97,110,100,105,110,103,115,44,32,115,99,111,114,101,115,63,44,32,119,111,110,63,44,32,115,116,97,116,115,63,44,32,97,119,97,114,100,115,63,32,125,41,96,32,124,32,115,104,97,114,101,100,32,119,111,114,108,100,44,32,116,104,101,32,104,111,115,116,44,32,111,110,99,101,32,124,10,52,48,48,58,124,32,96,101,110,100,96,32,124,32,96,123,32,114,101,97,115,111,110,44,32,115,116,97,110,100,105,110,103,115,32,125,96,32,124,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":23,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":55,\"content\":\"2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\"},{\"line_number\":114,\"content\":\"- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\"},{\"line_number\":117,\"content\":\"  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\"},{\"line_number\":144,\"content\":\"The hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\"},{\"line_number\":161,\"content\":\"  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\"},{\"line_number\":163,\"content\":\"  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\"},{\"line_number\":196,\"content\":\"- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\"},{\"line_number\":198,\"content\":\"  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\"},{\"line_number\":208,\"content\":\"  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\"},{\"line_number\":209,\"content\":\"  `finish()` by then is void.\"},{\"line_number\":216,\"content\":\"| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\"},{\"line_number\":238,\"content\":\"- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\"},{\"line_number\":247,\"content\":\"- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\"},{\"line_number\":250,\"content\":\"Places and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\"},{\"line_number\":330,\"content\":\"`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\"},{\"line_number\":334,\"content\":\"`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\"},{\"line_number\":337,\"content\":\"- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\"},{\"line_number\":378,\"content\":\"| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\"},{\"line_number\":379,\"content\":\"| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\\\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\"},{\"line_number\":384,\"content\":\"| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\"},{\"line_number\":400,\"content\":\"| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15d9503a-5b56-454d-8f76-955f50c45218-104","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→- `engine/crates/pav_core/build.rs` already embeds `engine/game/**/*.toml`, the top-level `engine/anim/*.json`, `engine/assets/materials/*.json` and `engine/assets/props/{templates,lib/core,lib/kaykit_adventurers}`. To ship a new prop pack, add its folder to that list and to `props::store::SHIPPED`.\\n\\n### 2.2 Browser flags: TASK.md's list does not work for this engine\\n- With `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, the page logs `GPU device lost (Destroyed)` within a second. The canvas stays blank and rAF reports a misleading 60 fps.\\n- **Use `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`** (the engine's own list). It renders, and `page.screenshot` shows the canvas.\\n- Under those flags the starter game draws at **about 1.5 to 2.5 fps at 640–960 px wide**. The sim is capped at 8 ticks per frame, so it reaches 12–19 ticks/s, or roughly **0.2–0.3× real time**. So:\\n  - Play the game in `pav` (native, headless, far faster than real time).\\n  - Use the browser for UI, input, audio routing and hub checks.\\n  - Add a test switch that skips scene drawing (§14.3) when a browser test needs the sim at full speed.\\n- `pav capture` runs on llvmpipe at about 1 to 1.5 s per 960×540 frame.\\n70→\\n### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\\nI pasted `lib/hub/session.js` unmodified as the first script in the built page, right after `<meta charset>`, added the `hub:*` metas and a small connect/ready/send/finish shim, and served it with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`. **`window.__hubCheck.pass` was true** for all of these:\\n- `players=2`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server`\\n\\nEach software-rendered copy reached `ready()` in under 2.5 s. The harness gives all copies 20 s, so build the session scene small and call `ready()` before the first drawn frame.\\n\\n80→**The game's own card passes too.** With `card:true` and a capture-phase `keydown` listener in the page's JS that calls `AIHub.answer('ready')` on Enter, the harness's extra check passed at 2 and 4 players and in the server case. The harness dispatches a synthetic Enter at the focused element, so answer it in the JS shim rather than waiting for the Rust side.\\n\\n### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\\n- **Controller stub:** a plain-object stub works with gilrs on wasm (the engine logs \\\"gamepad connected\\\", the UI flips to gamepad prompts, and button 9 opens the menu):\\n  ```js\\n  window.__pad = { axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0})) };\\n  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\\n    timestamp:performance.now(), axes:window.__pad.axes.slice(), buttons:window.__pad.buttons, vibrationActuator:null }, null, null, null];\\n  ```\\n- **Pointer lock:**\\n90→  - `requestPointerLock({unadjustedMovement:true})` rejects with `NotSupportedError` here, so fall back to the plain call, which works.\\n  - While locked, `page.mouse.move` gives `movementX = 0`, so tests must dispatch `new MouseEvent('mousemove',{movementX,movementY,bubbles:true})`.\\n  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\\n  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\\n- **Two pages:**\\n  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\\n  - WebRTC with manual offer and answer (no ICE servers) opens over loopback in under 1 s. The codes are about 850 base64 characters.\\n- **Playwright** is in the user's site-packages, so `python3 -I script.py` can't import it. Keep your test scripts in `tests/` and run them without `-I`.\\n\\n### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\\n100→| Gap | Evidence | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\\n| No sky | `Scene.clear_color` is flat, and `apply_fog` (scene.wgsl) also fogs unlit meshes, so a dome would vanish | Add a `flags::NO_FOG` bit and build a sky dome (§6.2) |\\n| Terrain is 1 m terraces with a hard-coded palette, flattened to y = 0 around footprints | `terrain.rs` | New smooth generator behind the streaming code (§6.1) |\\n| The car can't pitch or roll, and only the player can drive | `set_enabled_rotations(false, true, false…)`; `drive_vehicles` uses only the player's input, steering toward a world direction | §5.11 |\\n| Nav only works on floor blocks near y = 0 | `NavGrid::build` | Outdoor nav (§5.13) |\\n| Shots are for bullet-hell | `Team::Player` shots only hit things with `health`; the `Hit` event stuns for 0.6 s | Your own hitscan (§5.2) |\\n| Sound is a closed `match` on events, with no buses, loops, music or voices | `pav_audio::sounds_for` | §10 |\\n| HUD is text lines; the only menu is a pavilion debug menu; no title screen | `pav_ui::game_lines`, `pav_app/ui.rs` | Your own 10-foot UI kit and shell (§8) |\",\"content_concise\":\"60→- `engine/crates/pav_core/build.rs` already embeds `engine/game/**/*.toml`, the top-level `engine/anim/*.json`, `engine/assets/materials/*.json` and `engine/assets/props/{templates,lib/core,lib/kaykit_adventurers}`. To ship a new prop pack, add its folder to that list and to `props::store::SHIPPED`.\\n\\n### 2.2 Browser flags: TASK.md's list does not work for this engine\\n- With `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, the page logs `GPU device lost (Destroyed)` within a second. The canvas stays blank and rAF reports a misleading 60 fps.\\n- **Use `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`** (the engine's own list). It renders, and `page.screenshot` shows the canvas.\\n- Under those flags the starter game draws at **about 1.5 to 2.5 fps at 640–960 px wide**. The sim is capped at 8 ticks per frame, so it reaches 12–19 ticks/s, or roughly **0.2–0.3× real time**. So:\\n  - Play the game in `pav` (native, headless, far faster than real time).\\n  - Use the browser for UI, input, audio routing and hub checks.\\n  - Add a test switch that skips scene drawing (§14.3) when a browser test needs the sim at full speed.\\n- `pav capture` runs on llvmpipe at about 1 to 1.5 s per 960×540 frame.\\n70→\\n### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\\nI pasted `lib/hub/session.js` unmodified as the first script in the built page, right after `<meta charset>`, added the `hub:*` metas and a small connect/ready/send/finish shim, and served it with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`. **`window.__hubCheck.pass` was true** for all of these:\\n- `players=2`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server`\\n\\nEach software-rendered copy reached `ready()` in under 2.5 s. The harness gives all copies 20 s, so build the session scene small and call `ready()` before the first drawn frame.\\n\\n80→**The game's own card passes too.** With `card:true` and a capture-phase `keydown` listener in the page's JS that calls `AIHub.answer('ready')` on Enter, the harness's extra check passed at 2 and 4 players and in the server case. The harness dispatches a synthetic Enter at the focused element, so answer it in the JS shim rather than waiting for the Rust side.\\n\\n### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\\n- **Controller stub:** a plain-object stub works with gilrs on wasm (the engine logs \\\"gamepad connected\\\", the UI flips to gamepad prompts, and button 9 opens the menu):\\n  ```js\\n  window.__pad = { axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0})) };\\n  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\\n    timestamp:performance.now(), axes:window.__pad.axes.slice(), buttons:window.__pad.buttons, vibrationActuator:null }, null, null, null];\\n  ```\\n- **Pointer lock:**\\n90→  - `requestPointerLock({unadjustedMovement:true})` rejects with `NotSupportedError` here, so fall back to the plain call, which works.\\n  - While locked, `page.mouse.move` gives `movementX = 0`, so tests must dispatch `new MouseEvent('mousemove',{movementX,movementY,bubbles:true})`.\\n  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\\n  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\\n- **Two pages:**\\n  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\\n  - WebRTC with manual offer and answer (no ICE servers) opens over loopback in under 1 s. The codes are about 850 base64 characters.\\n- **Playwright** is in the user's site-packages, so `python3 -I script.py` can't import it. Keep your test scripts in `tests/` and run them without `-I`.\\n\\n### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\\n100→| Gap | Evidence | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\\n| No sky | `Scene.clear_color` is flat, and `apply_fog` (scene.wgsl) also fogs unlit meshes, so a dome would vanish | Add a `flags::NO_FOG` bit and build a sky dome (§6.2) |\\n| Terrain is 1 m terraces with a hard-coded palette, flattened to y = 0 around footprints | `terrain.rs` | New smooth generator behind the streaming code (§6.1) |\\n| The car can't pitch or roll, and only the player can drive | `set_enabled_rotations(false, true, false…)`; `drive_vehicles` uses only the player's input, steering toward a world direction | §5.11 |\\n| Nav only works on floor blocks near y = 0 | `NavGrid::build` | Outdoor nav (§5.13) |\\n| Shots are for bullet-hell | `Team::Player` shots only hit things with `health`; the `Hit` event stuns for 0.6 s | Your own hitscan (§5.2) |\\n| Sound is a closed `match` on events, with no buses, loops, music or voices | `pav_audio::sounds_for` | §10 |\\n| HUD is text lines; the only menu is a pavilion debug menu; no title screen | `pav_ui::game_lines`, `pav_app/ui.rs` | Your own 10-foot UI kit and shell (§8) |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"- `engine/crates/pav_core/build.rs` already embeds `engine/game/**/*.toml`, the top-level `engine/anim/*.json`, `engine/assets/materials/*.json` and `engine/assets/props/{templates,lib/core,lib/kaykit_adventurers}`. To ship a new prop pack, add its folder to that list and to `props::store::SHIPPED`.\\n\\n### 2.2 Browser flags: TASK.md's list does not work for this engine\\n- With `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, the page logs `GPU device lost (Destroyed)` within a second. The canvas stays blank and rAF reports a misleading 60 fps.\\n- **Use `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`** (the engine's own list). It renders, and `page.screenshot` shows the canvas.\\n- Under those flags the starter game draws at **about 1.5 to 2.5 fps at 640–960 px wide**. The sim is capped at 8 ticks per frame, so it reaches 12–19 ticks/s, or roughly **0.2–0.3× real time**. So:\\n  - Play the game in `pav` (native, headless, far faster than real time).\\n  - Use the browser for UI, input, audio routing and hub checks.\\n  - Add a test switch that skips scene drawing (§14.3) when a browser test needs the sim at full speed.\\n- `pav capture` runs on llvmpipe at about 1 to 1.5 s per 960×540 frame.\\n\\n### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\\nI pasted `lib/hub/session.js` unmodified as the first script in the built page, right after `<meta charset>`, added the `hub:*` metas and a small connect/ready/send/finish shim, and served it with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`. **`window.__hubCheck.pass` was true** for all of these:\\n- `players=2`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server`\\n\\nEach software-rendered copy reached `ready()` in under 2.5 s. The harness gives all copies 20 s, so build the session scene small and call `ready()` before the first drawn frame.\\n\\n**The game's own card passes too.** With `card:true` and a capture-phase `keydown` listener in the page's JS that calls `AIHub.answer('ready')` on Enter, the harness's extra check passed at 2 and 4 players and in the server case. The harness dispatches a synthetic Enter at the focused element, so answer it in the JS shim rather than waiting for the Rust side.\\n\\n### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\\n- **Controller stub:** a plain-object stub works with gilrs on wasm (the engine logs \\\"gamepad connected\\\", the UI flips to gamepad prompts, and button 9 opens the menu):\\n  ```js\\n  window.__pad = { axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0})) };\\n  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\\n    timestamp:performance.now(), axes:window.__pad.axes.slice(), buttons:window.__pad.buttons, vibrationActuator:null }, null, null, null];\\n  ```\\n- **Pointer lock:**\\n  - `requestPointerLock({unadjustedMovement:true})` rejects with `NotSupportedError` here, so fall back to the plain call, which works.\\n  - While locked, `page.mouse.move` gives `movementX = 0`, so tests must dispatch `new MouseEvent('mousemove',{movementX,movementY,bubbles:true})`.\\n  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\\n  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\\n- **Two pages:**\\n  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\\n  - WebRTC with manual offer and answer (no ICE servers) opens over loopback in under 1 s. The codes are about 850 base64 characters.\\n- **Playwright** is in the user's site-packages, so `python3 -I script.py` can't import it. Keep your test scripts in `tests/` and run them without `-I`.\\n\\n### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\\n| Gap | Evidence | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\\n| No sky | `Scene.clear_color` is flat, and `apply_fog` (scene.wgsl) also fogs unlit meshes, so a dome would vanish | Add a `flags::NO_FOG` bit and build a sky dome (§6.2) |\\n| Terrain is 1 m terraces with a hard-coded palette, flattened to y = 0 around footprints | `terrain.rs` | New smooth generator behind the streaming code (§6.1) |\\n| The car can't pitch or roll, and only the player can drive | `set_enabled_rotations(false, true, false…)`; `drive_vehicles` uses only the player's input, steering toward a world direction | §5.11 |\\n| Nav only works on floor blocks near y = 0 | `NavGrid::build` | Outdoor nav (§5.13) |\\n| Shots are for bullet-hell | `Team::Player` shots only hit things with `health`; the `Hit` event stuns for 0.6 s | Your own hitscan (§5.2) |\\n| Sound is a closed `match` on events, with no buses, loops, music or voices | `pav_audio::sounds_for` | §10 |\\n| HUD is text lines; the only menu is a pavilion debug menu; no title screen | `pav_ui::game_lines`, `pav_app/ui.rs` | Your own 10-foot UI kit and shell (§8) |\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15d9503a-5b56-454d-8f76-955f50c45218-105","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,74,97,109,32,67,114,121,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,67,97,114,103,111,46,108,111,99,107,10,53,49,49,58,32,34,119,97,115,109,45,98,105,110,100,103,101,110,34,44,10,53,49,50,58,32,34,119,97,115,109,45,98,105,110,100,103,101,110,45,102,117,116,117,114,101,115,34,44,10,57,55,48,58,32,34,119,97,115,109,45,98,105,110,100,103,101,110,34,44,10,49,51,54,56,58,32,34,119,97,115,109,45,98,105,110,100,103,101,110,34,44,10,50,50,56,49,58,32,34,119,97,115,1