{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b5469932-c0a7-44c4-9507-22ebc0475420-106","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3390→]\\n\\n[[package]]\\nname = \\\"wasm-bindgen\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.2.129\\\"\\nsource = \\\"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\\\"\\nchecksum = \\\"9bb54f33acc68fd454578d9820b0bde1a1a3d17aa17bb7b6595806d02886d409\\\"\\ndependencies = [\\n \\\"cfg-if\\\",\\n \\\"once_cell\\\",\\n3400→ \\\"rustversion\\\",\\n \\\"wasm-bindgen-macro\\\",\\n \\\"wasm-bindgen-shared\\\",\\n]\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"3390→]\\n\\n[[package]]\\nname = \\\"wasm-bindgen\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.2.129\\\"\\nsource = \\\"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\\\"\\nchecksum = \\\"9bb54f33acc68fd454578d9820b0bde1a1a3d17aa17bb7b6595806d02886d409\\\"\\ndependencies = [\\n \\\"cfg-if\\\",\\n \\\"once_cell\\\",\\n3400→ \\\"rustversion\\\",\\n \\\"wasm-bindgen-macro\\\",\\n \\\"wasm-bindgen-shared\\\",\\n]\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/Cargo.lock\",\"offset\":3390,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"]\\n\\n[[package]]\\nname = \\\"wasm-bindgen\\\"\\nversion = \\\"0.2.129\\\"\\nsource = \\\"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\\\"\\nchecksum = \\\"9bb54f33acc68fd454578d9820b0bde1a1a3d17aa17bb7b6595806d02886d409\\\"\\ndependencies = [\\n \\\"cfg-if\\\",\\n \\\"once_cell\\\",\\n \\\"rustversion\\\",\\n \\\"wasm-bindgen-macro\\\",\\n \\\"wasm-bindgen-shared\\\",\\n]\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":4308}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b5469932-c0a7-44c4-9507-22ebc0475420-107","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→\\n### The start\\n\\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\\n`start`.\\n\\n### Reporting\\n\\n190→- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\\n  by the host only:\\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\\n200→    placed last.\\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\\n\\n### Time-up and the end\\n\\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\\n  `finish()` by then is void.\\n210→- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\\n  game, then removes it.\\n\\n| `end` reason | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\\n220→| `session-ended` | the session closed |\\n\\n### Leaving\\n\\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\\n230→  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\\n  that player leaving.\\n\\n### Scoring\\n\\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\\n  progress.\\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\\n  result instead of medals.\\n240→- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\\n\\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\\nresults:\\n\\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\\n\\n250→Places and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Sending data between copies\\n\\n### Parallel\\n\\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"180→\\n### The start\\n\\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\\n`start`.\\n\\n### Reporting\\n\\n190→- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\\n  by the host only:\\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\\n200→    placed last.\\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\\n\\n### Time-up and the end\\n\\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\\n  `finish()` by then is void.\\n210→- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\\n  game, then removes it.\\n\\n| `end` reason | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\\n220→| `session-ended` | the session closed |\\n\\n### Leaving\\n\\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\\n230→  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\\n  that player leaving.\\n\\n### Scoring\\n\\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\\n  progress.\\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\\n  result instead of medals.\\n240→- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\\n\\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\\nresults:\\n\\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\\n\\n250→Places and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Sending data between copies\\n\\n### Parallel\\n\\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/README.md\",\"offset\":180,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"\\n### The start\\n\\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\\n`start`.\\n\\n### Reporting\\n\\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\\n  by the host only:\\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\\n    placed last.\\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\\n\\n### Time-up and the end\\n\\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\\n  `finish()` by then is void.\\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\\n  game, then removes it.\\n\\n| `end` reason | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\\n\\n### Leaving\\n\\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\\n  that player leaving.\\n\\n### Scoring\\n\\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\\n  progress.\\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\\n  result instead of medals.\\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\\n\\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\\nresults:\\n\\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\\n\\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Sending data between copies\\n\\n### Parallel\\n\\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":410}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b5469932-c0a7-44c4-9507-22ebc0475420-108","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,74,97,109,32,67,114,121,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,97,112,112,47,115,114,99,47,97,112,112,46,114,115,10,54,49,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,115,104,111,119,95,103,117,105,100,101,58,32,98,111,111,108,44,10,55,48,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,118,46,98,111,111,108,40,34,115,104,111,119,95,103,117,105,100,101,34,44,32,38,109,117,116,32,115,101,108,102,46,115,104,111,119,95,103,117,105,100,101,44,32,34,67,111,110,116,114,111,108,32,103,117,105,100,101,32,111,118,101,114,108,97,121,34,41,59,10,49,52,49,58,32,32,32,32,115,104,111,119,95,98,111,111,116,58,32,98,111,111,108,44,10,50,51,48,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32