{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_203","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to implement a substantial but focused integration.\n\nAbout pages need source info and feedback. Forbidden names must appear only on the Source line. Feedback will be based on real log issues: 14 compile errors, KEY scope errors, unit test failures, and gameplay bugs.\n\nPlaythrough bugs include ignite overlap, panic flee, rain on water, sticky sleep flags, and missing post_remanned or contract_d2. These blocked the campaign. Compile errors were fixed before playtesting. I will count exact issues precisely when writing feedback.\n\nmerc_web.rs needs JS bindings and an apply function. simhost tick cap and apply need updates. app.rs should hide boot, guide, and stats during merc scenes. The rig.fp value should come from a shared cell or static instead of querying the simulation every frame.\n\nFor the merc scene, app.rs will set a fixed FpCam with eye at 0.0, 1.58, 0.2 and yaw 0.15 to fill the frame with trees and ground. The sky color should be dusk to avoid an empty background.\n\nThe rifle sits at (0.22, 1.15, -0.35) in front of the player looking down the negative Z axis.\n\nThe latest camera pose will live in a static Atomic or Mutex that merc_web updates and app.rs reads. On native builds merc_web is cfg wasm so app.rs can supply a default overlook.\n\nMouse look must change world yaw via look input. Published status.yaw should reflect pointer-lock mousemove events.\n\napply() will return nothing. After each step, the world yaw will be read and stored in a thread-local MercView struct protected by a Mutex. The camera pose will be drawn from that shared state so it matches the published status.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9ff32512-d2ce-4b9c-89b0-1498f560ef3a-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":840,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9ff32512-d2ce-4b9c-89b0-1498f560ef3a-110","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1320,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9ff32512-d2ce-4b9c-89b0-1498f560ef3a-111","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1480,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1879,"output_tokens":1402,"cache_read_input_tokens":170624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"f96981d0-6c73-43e9-b643-21bbd7a1c39a"}
