l-900689b3-2c4a-40c6-8b43-5ff124759617-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"69→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n70→pub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n80→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Radians of look since the previous tick (x = yaw, y = pitch). Summed and cleared like `pressed`.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n90→    pub look: Vec2,\\n    /// Analog vehicle axes: x steer, y throttle (positive) / brake (negative).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub axes: Vec2,\\n    /// Encoded menu or world action for replays and the bot (Jam Cry). 0 means none.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub act: u32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n100→    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"69→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n70→pub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n80→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Radians of look since the previous tick (x = yaw, y = pitch). Summed and cleared like `pressed`.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n90→    pub look: Vec2,\\n    /// Analog vehicle axes: x steer, y throttle (positive) / brake (negative).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub axes: Vec2,\\n    /// Encoded menu or world action for replays and the bot (Jam Cry). 0 means none.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub act: u32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n100→    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs\",\"offset\":69,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Radians of look since the previous tick (x = yaw, y = pitch). Summed and cleared like `pressed`.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub look: Vec2,\\n    /// Analog vehicle axes: x steer, y throttle (positive) / brake (negative).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub axes: Vec2,\\n    /// Encoded menu or world action for replays and the bot (Jam Cry). 0 means none.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub act: u32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":106}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5af034fd-0303-4eda-bcf8-1e22527903c7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_206","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The move_dir comment says world space, but the merc sim treats it as stick space and rotates by yaw.\n\nMerc scenes will use raw stick input instead of pre-rotated world space. Mouse look will be handled by JavaScript accumulation drained into the input frame during tick_once, overriding winit mouse motion. Keyboard actions will come from JS pushes. There is a risk of double-activation if both winit and JS confirm.\n\nConsecutive ticks could cause double activation. Menu keys on wasm will use only the JavaScript path, avoiding winit bindings for Enter and Space.\n\nDraining all pending JavaScript inputs into a single frame prevents double-activation. A comprehensive Hub JavaScript page script is being prepared, and the packer may insert session.js.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23656ec1-0f00-46b7-ab44-d5b83feeb027-116","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"</script>|<script|<!--","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/session.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23656ec1-0f00-46b7-ab44-d5b83feeb027-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py","offset":80,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":985,"output_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":178560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"a92473d5-181e-4b30-8148-de9af0c4afd4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-23656ec1-0f00-46b7-ab44-d5b83feeb027-116","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-23656ec1-0f00-46b7-ab44-d5b83feeb027-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"80→\\n\\ndef replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Replaces the one match of `pattern` in the page; anything else means index.html changed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    page, n = re.subn(pattern, make, page)\\n    if n != 1:\\n        fail(f\\\"expected one {what} in {PAGE.relative_to(ROOT)}, found {n}: update this script\\\")\\n    return page\\n\\n\\n90→def main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\")[0])\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"bindgen_dir\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"wasm-bindgen output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--title\\\", help=\\\"<title> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--description\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--theme-color\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--scene\\\", help=\\\"start scene when the address names no room or scene (default: the game's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--out\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"output file (default: target/web/<title>.html)\\\")\\n    a = ap.parse_args()\\n\\n100→    js, wasm_path = a.bindgen_dir / \\\"shardfall.js\\\", a.bindgen_dir / \\\"shardfall_bg.wasm\\\"\\n    for p in (js, wasm_path):\\n        if not p.is_file():\\n            fail(f\\\"{p} is missing: run wasm-bindgen --target web --out-name shardfall first\\\")\\n    # The glue goes in the page as an inline module script, so it can't import other files\\n    # (wasm-bindgen snippets) or hold text that would end the script element early.\\n    glue = js.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if (a.bindgen_dir / \\\"snippets\\\").exists() or re.search(r\\\"^import\\\\b\\\", glue, re.M):\\n        fail(\\\"the JS glue imports other files (wasm-bindgen snippets); inline them before packing\\\")\\n    if re.search(r\\\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\\\", glue):\\n110→        fail(\\\"the JS glue contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\\\")\\n    init = re.search(r\\\"^export \\\\{[^}]*?\\\\b([\\\\w$]+) as default\\\\b\\\", glue, re.M)\\n    if not init:\\n        fail(\\\"can't find the JS glue's default export (its init function)\\\")\\n\\n    page = PAGE.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if a.title is not None:\\n        page = replace_one(page, r\\\"<title>[^<]*</title>\\\", lambda m: f\\\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\\\", \\\"<title>\\\")\\n    for name, value in ((\\\"description\\\", a.description), (\\\"theme-color\\\", a.theme_color)):\\n        if value is not None:\\n120→            page = replace_one(\\n                page,\\n                rf'<meta name=\\\"{name}\\\" content=\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\">',\\n                lambda m, name=name, value=value: f'<meta name=\\\"{name}\\\" content=\\\"{html.escape(value)}\\\">',\\n                f\\\"<meta name={name}>\\\",\\n            )\\n    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\\n    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\\\t]*<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\"[^>]*>\\\\n', lambda m: \\\"\\\", \\\"manifest link\\\")\\n\\n    wasm = wasm_path.read_bytes()\\n130→    packed = gzip.compress(wasm, compresslevel=9, mtime=0)\\n    # JSON is valid JS; escaping \\\"<\\\" keeps a scene name from closing the script element.\\n    loader = LOADER.replace(\\\"__SCENE__\\\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\"))\\n    tail = (\\n        f'<script id=\\\"game-wasm\\\" type=\\\"application/octet-stream\\\" data-size=\\\"{len(wasm)}\\\">'\\n        f\\\"{base64.b64encode(packed).decode()}</script>\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"<script>{loader}</script>\\\\n\\\"\\n        f'<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n{glue}\\\\nwindow.gameGlue({init[1]});\\\\n</script>\\\\n'\\n    )\\n    page = replace_one(page, r\\\"</body>\\\", lambda m: tail + \\\"</body>\\\", \\\"</body>\\\")\\n140→\\n    title = a.title if a.title is not None else html.unescape(re.search(r\\\"<title>([^<]*)</title>\\\", page)[1])\\n    out = a.out or ROOT / \\\"target\\\" / \\\"web\\\" / f\\\"{re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-') or 'game'}.html\\\"\\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    out.write_text(page, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    mb = lambda n: f\\\"{n / 1e6:.1f} MB\\\"  # noqa: E731\\n    print(f\\\"{out}: {mb(out.stat().st_size)} (wasm {mb(len(wasm))}, gzipped {mb(len(packed))}; JS glue {mb(len(glue))})\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n150→    main()\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"80→\\n\\ndef replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Replaces the one match of `pattern` in the page; anything else means index.html changed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    page, n = re.subn(pattern, make, page)\\n    if n != 1:\\n        fail(f\\\"expected one {what} in {PAGE.relative_to(ROOT)}, found {n}: update this script\\\")\\n    return page\\n\\n\\n90→def main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\")[0])\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"bindgen_dir\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"wasm-bindgen output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--title\\\", help=\\\"<title> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--description\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--theme-color\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--scene\\\", help=\\\"start scene when the address names no room or scene (default: the game's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--out\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"output file (default: target/web/<title>.html)\\\")\\n    a = ap.parse_args()\\n\\n100→    js, wasm_path = a.bindgen_dir / \\\"shardfall.js\\\", a.bindgen_dir / \\\"shardfall_bg.wasm\\\"\\n    for p in (js, wasm_path):\\n        if not p.is_file():\\n            fail(f\\\"{p} is missing: run wasm-bindgen --target web --out-name shardfall first\\\")\\n    # The glue goes in the page as an inline module script, so it can't import other files\\n    # (wasm-bindgen snippets) or hold text that would end the script element early.\\n    glue = js.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if (a.bindgen_dir / \\\"snippets\\\").exists() or re.search(r\\\"^import\\\\b\\\", glue, re.M):\\n        fail(\\\"the JS glue imports other files (wasm-bindgen snippets); inline them before packing\\\")\\n    if re.search(r\\\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\\\", glue):\\n110→        fail(\\\"the JS glue contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\\\")\\n    init = re.search(r\\\"^export \\\\{[^}]*?\\\\b([\\\\w$]+) as default\\\\b\\\", glue, re.M)\\n    if not init:\\n        fail(\\\"can't find the JS glue's default export (its init function)\\\")\\n\\n    page = PAGE.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if a.title is not None:\\n        page = replace_one(page, r\\\"<title>[^<]*</title>\\\", lambda m: f\\\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\\\", \\\"<title>\\\")\\n    for name, value in ((\\\"description\\\", a.description), (\\\"theme-color\\\", a.theme_color)):\\n        if value is not None:\\n120→            page = replace_one(\\n                page,\\n                rf'<meta name=\\\"{name}\\\" content=\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\">',\\n                lambda m, name=name, value=value: f'<meta name=\\\"{name}\\\" content=\\\"{html.escape(value)}\\\">',\\n                f\\\"<meta name={name}>\\\",\\n            )\\n    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\\n    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\\\t]*<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\"[^>]*>\\\\n', lambda m: \\\"\\\", \\\"manifest link\\\")\\n\\n    wasm = wasm_path.read_bytes()\\n130→    packed = gzip.compress(wasm, compresslevel=9, mtime=0)\\n    # JSON is valid JS; escaping \\\"<\\\" keeps a scene name from closing the script element.\\n    loader = LOADER.replace(\\\"__SCENE__\\\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\"))\\n    tail = (\\n        f'<script id=\\\"game-wasm\\\" type=\\\"application/octet-stream\\\" data-size=\\\"{len(wasm)}\\\">'\\n        f\\\"{base64.b64encode(packed).decode()}</script>\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"<script>{loader}</script>\\\\n\\\"\\n        f'<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n{glue}\\\\nwindow.gameGlue({init[1]});\\\\n</script>\\\\n'\\n    )\\n    page = replace_one(page, r\\\"</body>\\\", lambda m: tail + \\\"</body>\\\", \\\"</body>\\\")\\n140→\\n    title = a.title if a.title is not None else html.unescape(re.search(r\\\"<title>([^<]*)</title>\\\", page)[1])\\n    out = a.out or ROOT / \\\"target\\\" / \\\"web\\\" / f\\\"{re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-') or 'game'}.html\\\"\\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    out.write_text(page, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    mb = lambda n: f\\\"{n / 1e6:.1f} MB\\\"  # noqa: E731\\n    print(f\\\"{out}: {mb(out.stat().st_size)} (wasm {mb(len(wasm))}, gzipped {mb(len(packed))}; JS glue {mb(len(glue))})\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n150→    main()\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py\",\"offset\":80,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"\\n\\ndef replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Replaces the one match of `pattern` in the page; anything else means index.html changed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    page, n = re.subn(pattern, make, page)\\n    if n != 1:\\n        fail(f\\\"expected one {what} in {PAGE.relative_to(ROOT)}, found {n}: update this script\\\")\\n    return page\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\")[0])\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"bindgen_dir\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"wasm-bindgen output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--title\\\", help=\\\"<title> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--description\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--theme-color\\\", help=\\\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--scene\\\", help=\\\"start scene when the address names no room or scene (default: the game's)\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--out\\\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\\\"output file (default: target/web/<title>.html)\\\")\\n    a = ap.parse_args()\\n\\n    js, wasm_path = a.bindgen_dir / \\\"shardfall.js\\\", a.bindgen_dir / \\\"shardfall_bg.wasm\\\"\\n    for p in (js, wasm_path):\\n        if not p.is_file():\\n            fail(f\\\"{p} is missing: run wasm-bindgen --target web --out-name shardfall first\\\")\\n    # The glue goes in the page as an inline module script, so it can't import other files\\n    # (wasm-bindgen snippets) or hold text that would end the script element early.\\n    glue = js.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if (a.bindgen_dir / \\\"snippets\\\").exists() or re.search(r\\\"^import\\\\b\\\", glue, re.M):\\n        fail(\\\"the JS glue imports other files (wasm-bindgen snippets); inline them before packing\\\")\\n    if re.search(r\\\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\\\", glue):\\n        fail(\\\"the JS glue contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\\\")\\n    init = re.search(r\\\"^export \\\\{[^}]*?\\\\b([\\\\w$]+) as default\\\\b\\\", glue, re.M)\\n    if not init:\\n        fail(\\\"can't find the JS glue's default export (its init function)\\\")\\n\\n    page = PAGE.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    if a.title is not None:\\n        page = replace_one(page, r\\\"<title>[^<]*</title>\\\", lambda m: f\\\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\\\", \\\"<title>\\\")\\n    for name, value in ((\\\"description\\\", a.description), (\\\"theme-color\\\", a.theme_color)):\\n        if value is not None:\\n            page = replace_one(\\n                page,\\n                rf'<meta name=\\\"{name}\\\" content=\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\">',\\n                lambda m, name=name, value=value: f'<meta name=\\\"{name}\\\" content=\\\"{html.escape(value)}\\\">',\\n                f\\\"<meta name={name}>\\\",\\n            )\\n    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\\n    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\\\t]*<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\"[^>]*>\\\\n', lambda m: \\\"\\\", \\\"manifest link\\\")\\n\\n    wasm = wasm_path.read_bytes()\\n    packed = gzip.compress(wasm, compresslevel=9, mtime=0)\\n    # JSON is valid JS; escaping \\\"<\\\" keeps a scene name from closing the script element.\\n    loader = LOADER.replace(\\\"__SCENE__\\\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\\\"<\\\", \\\"\\\\\\\\u003c\\\"))\\n    tail = (\\n        f'<script id=\\\"game-wasm\\\" type=\\\"application/octet-stream\\\" data-size=\\\"{len(wasm)}\\\">'\\n        f\\\"{base64.b64encode(packed).decode()}</script>\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"<script>{loader}</script>\\\\n\\\"\\n        f'<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n{glue}\\\\nwindow.gameGlue({init[1]});\\\\n</script>\\\\n'\\n    )\\n    page = replace_one(page, r\\\"</body>\\\", lambda m: tail + \\\"</body>\\\", \\\"</body>\\\")\\n\\n    title = a.title if a.title is not None else html.unescape(re.search(r\\\"<title>([^<]*)</title>\\\", page)[1])\\n    out = a.out or ROOT / \\\"target\\\" / \\\"web\\\" / f\\\"{re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-') or 'game'}.html\\\"\\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    out.write_text(page, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    mb = lambda n: f\\\"{n / 1e6:.1f} MB\\\"  # noqa: E731\\n    print(f\\\"{out}: {mb(out.stat().st_size)} (wasm {mb(len(wasm))}, gzipped {mb(len(packed))}; JS glue {mb(len(glue))})\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\",\"total_lines\":150}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"8b30decd-cf48-4292-9e45-7f971beeb1ab"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_207","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"session.js has no script tags, so it can be inlined.\n\nA build script will inline the 16KB session.js into index.html. This avoids duplicating the file in the repository.\n\nThe assembler will use a `SESSION_JS_PLACEHOLDER` marker in a template file. It will substitute the session.js bytes before the pack step, then restore the original template.\n\nThe packer hardcodes `web/index.html`, so the build will write the inlined session.js directly into that file. The DOM shell CSS targets a 10-foot UI with large type and at most seven rows. It reads `window.__game.ui` to paint rows and handles clicks for hover and command selection. Rust publishes this UI state every fifteen ticks.\n\nA title card will appear immediately while WASM loads, then the DOM shell takes over once `__game` is ready. The launch screenshot must show the canvas filled with the 3D scene and the title overlaid on top. An opaque DOM panel covering the entire canvas risks capturing the menu instead of the scene.\n\nThe menu will become a left panel so the 3D world remains visible on the right. The title screen will use a large title over a translucent bar. Pressing Enter twice will hide the menu and start playing.\n\nIf the device is touch-only, the DOM will show a notice reading \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. No on-screen stick will appear. The attract mode will keep running in the simulation while the user is idle. JavaScript will detect touch-only devices using `matchMedia` for coarse pointers and no hover support, then set a `touch_only` flag on the world state.\n\nThe Settings row remains clickable even when touch_only is active. The JavaScript sends a `{touch: true}` command to the engine for Playwright phone profiles. WebKit tests will see the existing \"needs WebGPU\" message without loading WASM. Gamepad support will be stubbed in the test so the engine detects a controller.\n\nThe shell device is `World.device`, not the engine's `last_device`. Glyphs come from `world.ui` using that device. The page script will poll `navigator.getGamepads` and push a `{device:\"gamepad\"}` command when a controller is detected.\n\nAn \"Xbox glyphs\" setting will be added. It can be toggled via act 14 or a `{xbox:true}` command. Browser tests will open settings to verify this.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd8970ca-a60c-4cee-8a77-6705f9c19574-118","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"act == 1[0-7]|fn toggle_cheat|act == 12","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2443,"output_tokens":1361,"cache_read_input_tokens":179456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"362c086f-79a6-43d5-99fe-dd7057bf80df"}
