{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-04234b12-436e-4dd9-9f76-03b1dcd8c074-127","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"160→        if !self.initialized || self.params.follow_lag <= 0.0 {\\n            self.target = focus;\\n            self.initialized = true;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let k = 1.0 - (-dt / self.current().follow_lag.max(1e-3)).exp();\\n        self.target += (focus - self.target) * k;\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\\n170→        self.target = focus;\\n        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (sy, cy) = fp.yaw.sin_cos();\\n            return (Vec3::new(sy, 0.0, -cy), Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy));\\n        }\\n180→        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).0;\\n        }\\n190→        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).2;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n200→        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n210→            return fp.eye;\\n        }\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (fwd, _, up) = fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll);\\n            let eye = fp.eye;\\n            let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, up);\\n220→            let mut fov = fp.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n            if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n                fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n            }\\n            let near = if fp.near > 0.0 { fp.near } else { 0.08 };\\n            let far = if fp.far > near { fp.far } else { 3000.0 };\\n            let proj = glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect.max(0.01), near, far);\\n            return CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: false };\\n        }\\n        let p = &self.current();\",\"content_concise\":\"160→        if !self.initialized || self.params.follow_lag <= 0.0 {\\n            self.target = focus;\\n            self.initialized = true;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let k = 1.0 - (-dt / self.current().follow_lag.max(1e-3)).exp();\\n        self.target += (focus - self.target) * k;\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\\n170→        self.target = focus;\\n        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (sy, cy) = fp.yaw.sin_cos();\\n            return (Vec3::new(sy, 0.0, -cy), Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy));\\n        }\\n180→        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).0;\\n        }\\n190→        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).2;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n200→        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n210→            return fp.eye;\\n        }\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (fwd, _, up) = fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll);\\n            let eye = fp.eye;\\n            let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, up);\\n220→            let mut fov = fp.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n            if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n                fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n            }\\n            let near = if fp.near > 0.0 { fp.near } else { 0.08 };\\n            let far = if fp.far > near { fp.far } else { 3000.0 };\\n            let proj = glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect.max(0.01), near, far);\\n            return CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: false };\\n        }\\n        let p = &self.current();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs\",\"offset\":160,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"        if !self.initialized || self.params.follow_lag <= 0.0 {\\n            self.target = focus;\\n            self.initialized = true;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let k = 1.0 - (-dt / self.current().follow_lag.max(1e-3)).exp();\\n        self.target += (focus - self.target) * k;\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\\n        self.target = focus;\\n        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (sy, cy) = fp.yaw.sin_cos();\\n            return (Vec3::new(sy, 0.0, -cy), Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy));\\n        }\\n        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).0;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).2;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp.eye;\\n        }\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (fwd, _, up) = fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll);\\n            let eye = fp.eye;\\n            let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, up);\\n            let mut fov = fp.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n            if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n                fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n            }\\n            let near = if fp.near > 0.0 { fp.near } else { 0.08 };\\n            let far = if fp.far > near { fp.far } else { 3000.0 };\\n            let proj = glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect.max(0.01), near, far);\\n            return CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: false };\\n        }\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n\",\"total_lines\":301}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"ae04fb6c-f87b-4931-a18d-91514a46ca1e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_213","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Setting rig.fp before builder.build is sufficient, provided it happens before rig.update and build.\n\nDress props will be placed relative to the player spawn point in `sim.state.spawn` rather than the layout origin. This ensures the camera can see them after spawning.\n\nThe dress props are positioned in front of the player spawn: 16 trees arranged in a spiral and a rifle in view. The camera eye will be set at feet plus (0, 1.58, 0) looking at negative Z. World x and z represent country position rather than room position.\n\nThe camera eye stays fixed at the room spawn. Yaw and pitch follow world rotation for mouse look. The default yaw faces the trees at negative Z.\n\nCamera pitch is offset by -0.18 to keep the view slightly downward at the title screen. Shell act codes will be added after the xbox toggle, and pause rows will hide dev controls when the hub is active.\n\nAbout page text will avoid forbidden names like Jackal and UFLL to satisfy the fiction test. \"Far Cry 2\" will appear only on the Source line. Feedback counts will be verified against logs, and compile errors and test failures will be tallied in parallel with code writing.\n\nWeb storage is available via web_sys. The gameBridge pull function is safe because the page script always defines it before WASM loads, preventing a panic.\n\nA `query_flag` helper will read URL search parameters once to check for flags like `nodraw`. Fast ticks apply when `nodraw`, `test=1`, or the screen is not `Playing`. During the launch test, the title screen triggers fast ticks at 120 per frame. At two frames per second, ten simulation seconds pass in roughly one real second.\n\nThe first key during the attract screen exits it back to the title without consuming the confirm. The next key then activates the title screen.\n\nThe test only requires the solo path to change state, not necessarily reach Playing. If the attract screen starts before keys are sent, the first Enter simply returns the player to Title, which is acceptable because the test compares the state before and after the four key presses.\n\nThe attract screen will appear at the ten-second mark as required. The DOM shell will display large text with the title, menu rows, and a focus highlight. Clicking a row should push a hover or click event, or set focus and confirm. However, the pointer is not currently passed through `menu_of` from `InputFrame`, which prevents hover-based focus movement.\n\nInputFrame currently lacks a pointer field, so hover and click events never reach MenuInput. The plan is to inject a MenuInput with pointer and click data directly into world.apply_menu inside merc_web::apply, bypassing the standard tick input path.\n\nA thread-local pointer would couple the shell to the application. Instead, hover events will be injected directly into `World::apply_menu` before `step`, while keyboard input continues through the normal tick path. This avoids double-processing and keeps focus movement separate from confirm activation.\n\nClick events must not flow through both the manual apply_menu injection and shell_tick, or a single keypress would trigger two screen transitions. A cross-crate static pointer is too messy. Instead, shell_tick will read extra input from existing World fields set by apply.\n\nThe chosen approach adds `pointer` and `pointer_click` fields to the World struct. These will be set from `apply` before `step`, then read by `shell_tick` to drive menu focus and clicks. The fields require `#[serde(default)]` so old save files deserialize correctly, and every struct literal must include them.\n\nDOM hover and click events will target menu rows at fixed pixel coordinates calculated from the row index. The gamepad device path sets the world device to Gamepad and locks it, preventing the keyboard from overriding the selection.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6fe4b556-f042-4ac2-89a8-548d1b31796f-128","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn notice","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","-A":25}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1019,"output_tokens":2487,"cache_read_input_tokens":194176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"bc89549a-bfcc-46c6-9141-c89527f394c5"}
