{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_215","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The device defaults to Gamepad. Glyphs start as PlayStation.\n\nKeyboard input switches the device to Keyboard on confirmation. The launch test uses keyboard, so glyphs become keyboard after the first keypress. The gamepad test locks the device to Gamepad. Keyboard mode only activates on keyboard buttons.\n\nThe device will be set to Gamepad whenever a pad is detected via getGamepads. This prevents keyboard input from overriding the gamepad stub. Actions 11 through 16 in shell_tick must also run during the Playing state, not only in the shell.\n\nshell_tick only runs when the screen is not Playing. Action 15 save must be handled in the Playing branch instead.\n\nAction 11 toggles god mode. Action 12 adjusts the eighth audio parameter. Action 13 resets the audio to its initial state. Action 15 writes a save file. Action 16 will use a new resume_save method to load a saved game from the title screen.\n\nPointer lock loss pauses the game. Rust handles act 10 during the Playing state.\n\nSave files will be written to localStorage after each step. A static tracks the last saved count to avoid redundant writes.\n\nOn boot, if a save exists in localStorage, the app sets the save flag and blob without replacing the world. This lets the title screen appear first; continue loads the saved game.\n\nThe dress() function will be updated for a richer overlook. Several small edits are planned for app.rs. Both simhost loops will use cap instead of 8.\n\nThe normal playing loop will use a tick cap of 120 for merc, while preview stays at 8. The cap function checks the simulation state and returns 120 when the play key is merc and the screen is not Playing. Nodraw mode applies only on wasm.\n\nThe tick_cap function will return 120 for merc when the screen is Playing and nodraw is active, otherwise 8. The Game trait must be in scope for the Merc lookup. apply will run inside tick_once before step.\n\napply will take a mutable Sim and a mutable InputFrame. It borrows the Merc component mutably to update the world and frame before step runs.\n\nA counter will track publish ticks instead of sim.state.tick, since holding a mutable borrow on the play component prevents reading the tick field. Publish calls must happen before dropping that borrow.\n\nThe room camera eye and yaw will be derived from world eye and yaw. World x and z are country coordinates, not room coordinates. The spawn point should be stored in Merc during dress, but Merc currently does not persist it.\n\nThe camera will use a fixed overlook position matching dress, with yaw and pitch taken from the world. The spawn point and tick will be read before mutably borrowing the play component. The eye will sit at the spawn height plus the world eye offset, yaw will match the world yaw, and pitch will subtract 0.2 to look slightly downward. The player body mesh may occupy the camera space.\n\nThe camera eye will sit 0.45 meters in front of the body using the yaw angle, keeping it just outside the head mesh. The publish strings will be raw JSON strings assigned to `window.__game.status` and `window.__game.ui`.\n\nThe Rust side will deserialize the JavaScript input bridge into a Pull struct using serde_json. It will skip empty or null responses.\n\nJavaScript strings must not contain the sequence `</script>` to avoid breaking HTML tags. The large session.js file will be embedded inline by replacing a placeholder in index.html during the build step.\n\nThe build script copies index.html to a backup, then uses Python to swap the `/*__SESSION_JS__*/` placeholder for the session.js contents before packing. The packed HTML is the final deliverable.\n\nThe packed HTML must be byte-identical to the session.js file. The placeholder script tag will be the first element, and the replacement text must match the file exactly with no extra whitespace.\n\nThe packed HTML will place the session script immediately after the charset meta tag, followed by a hub:session meta tag. A Python check will verify that the first script element's content matches the session.js file exactly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1d5bfde-c8de-4669-bcb4-12d5cfa5a917-130","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn settings_rows|Xbox|fn dev_rows","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1174,"output_tokens":2689,"cache_read_input_tokens":197760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"a2156d54-70df-431f-9f50-71667ed6c364"}
