1,32,99,104,101,99,107,97,98,108,101,32,99,111,112,105,101,115,32,97,114,101,32,65,98,111,117,116,47,67,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,97,110,100,32,96,101,120,105,116,45,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,106,115,111,110,96,59,32,116,104,101,32,114,101,112,108,121,32,109,117,115,116,32,114,101,112,101,97,116,32,116,104,101,109,44,32,97,110,100,32,118,101,114,105,102,105,101,114,115,32,100,111,32,110,111,116,32,102,97,105,108,32,116,104,101,32,103,111,97,108,32,111,110,108,121,32,98,101,99,97,117,115,101,32,116,104,101,121,32,99,97,110,110,111,116,32,115,101,101,32,116,104,101,32,99,104,97,116,46,10,53,56,58,45,32,84,104,101,32,104,117,98,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,110,101,101,100,115,32,97,32,108,111,99,97,108,32,115,101,114,118,101,114,46,32,83,111,108,111,32,112,108,97,121,32,109,117,115,116,32,115,116,105,108,108,32,119,111,114,107,32,102,114,111,109,32,96,102,105,108,101,58,47,47,96,46,32,68,111,32,110,111,116,32,116,114,101,97,116,32,97,32,115,101,114,118,101,114,45,111,110,108,121,32,112,97,103,101,32,97,115,32,109,101,101,116,105,110,103,32,99,114,105,116,101,114,105,111,110,32,49,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":12,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"1. **Hand-in and original identity.** The work folder (the one that holds `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, and `TASK.md`) contains `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json` beside the game HTML, and exactly one self-contained game page named `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html`. `{GameTitle}` is the title picked by brainstorming 50 playful riffs and then a real RNG (the 50 names and the RNG output are saved). A dev subfolder with that same stem holds the project. The page opens from `file://` (no silent blank from module CORS). The title screen shows that title. In-fiction names, places, factions, and dialogue do not copy the source: the strings Jackal, UFLL, APR, Pala, Mosate, Bowa-Seko, Leboa-Sako, Reuben Oluwagembi, and Mike's Bar, and the source's playable mercs or buddies, do not appear, and the words \\\"Far Cry 2\\\" appear only in the title-riff notes, the About/Credits source line, and the exit-interview source fields. Shipped text and behavior have no TODOs, TBDs, placehold [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"4. **Vertical slice, companions, three endings, saves, coverage.** Every contract row in PLAN.md §11 is playable, including both paymasters' jobs, a companion's alternate approach, the ceasefire breaking, the town burning, and the finale. The player chooses among three endings: burn the ledger, hold the mast while the names are read, or take the chair. A seeded bot, from a new game on normal difficulty, using only normal inputs and actions (bus travel allowed; no cheats and no teleport), reaches each ending. Across those runs, every coverage flag named in PLAN.md §15 is set by real play (union across runs is enough where one run cannot both save and lose the same companion or see every ending). A living companion rescues the downed player once per rest and the player stands at about half health; a downed companion can be patched or given a mercy overdose; a death stays dead across save and load. A save written from `file://` restores contract state, inventory and condition, discoveries [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"2. **gating:** Run the shipped native simulation tests (the game's own test binary, starting each case from a fresh boot) for look and movement, hitscan zones and wall blocking, jam rate, jam clear, weapon break, enemy jam, syrette and wound types, fever warning, pill clear, and no-pill blackout with a diamond fee. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/sim-combat.log`. Pass only if those assertions pass and the log shows zero failures for this group.\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"6. **gating:** Launch the real HTML from `file://` with Playwright Chromium more than once (two separate runs), using the engine WebGPU flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` (do not use `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`). Each run: zero page errors; the canvas drawing size equals the viewport requested for that run; the frame is substantially filled (painted fraction high or a painted bbox covering most of the surface, not a clear buffer); the visible title or the published UI state equals `{GameTitle}`; keyboard input (the Enter, Space, Enter, Space solo path) changes that state. Save screenshots and console logs to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must succeed. A readback that returns a blank image is a failure to fix. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-fail.log` and treat criteria 2–5's native tests plus a static check that [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"7. **gating:** On that same page, drive the shipped browser hooks: gamepad stub flips prompts to PlayStation glyphs, the Xbox setting changes them, pointer-lock mousemove changes yaw, losing the lock opens pause, a phone profile shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and Settings with attract running and no touch controls, WebKit (no WebGPU) shows a clear message instead of a blank page, dev mode toggles a cheat and a slider visible in published status, save then Continue works from `file://`, published music gain is 0.10, and About text contains the Source Information fields and all three feedback sections. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"Follow PLAN.md as the design (milestones M0–M11, data in TOML, pure seeded simulation separate from rendering, UI, and the page). Verifiers judge the criteria above, not a matching directory tree or identical type names. Keep rules `Clone`-able and free of hashmap iteration order and wall-clock randomness so two runs of the same seed agree. Build the campaign bot beside each contract so the playthrough test stays cheap. Put numbers in data files. Expose game status and a test-command queue on the page for browser checks, and a no-draw switch so browser tests are not limited by software-rendered frame rate. Pack one HTML that runs from `file://` and still loads the unmodified session client first. Track answers for the feedback questions while working so About and `exit-interview.json` are filled from real notes, not blanks.\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"- [ ] Add code-only music, effects, and gibberish voices with music at 10%, plus the 10-foot shell, dev-mode sliders, attract mode, touch-only notice, and About/Credits.\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"- [ ] Pack `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` into the work root, write `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md`, run the full test command and the file:// launch twice, and store the captured logs.\"},{\"line_number\":57,\"content\":\"- TASK.md also asks for the Source Information and the three feedback sections in the implementer's chat reply. The checkable copies are About/Credits and `exit-interview.json`; the reply must repeat them, and verifiers do not fail the goal only because they cannot see the chat.\"},{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"- The hub harness needs a local server. Solo play must still work from `file://`. Do not treat a server-only page as meeting criterion 1.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0bb1a3a2-d079-43c1-8736-e18b9a0ae769-13","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,11