{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_225","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large implementation.\n\nReviewing the core source files and verification requirements. The page must render a filled canvas, display the title \"Jam Cry\", and toggle UI state on Enter or Space.\n\nBrowser hooks are needed for gamepad, pointer lock, pause on unlock, touch notice, and WebGPU warnings. The hub requires four harness cases, two-page broadcast, and WebRTC. Solo mode must avoid Math.random for shared world state. The canvas fill is the hardest part because software WebGPU is slow in a small room. I will dress the scene so trees, ground, and sky fill the frame. Next I need to check how dress() spawns entities and how the renderer draws them.\n\nA uniform sky clear would fail verification. I need actual geometry covering most of the frame: trees, ground, and a rifle in view. I will check dress() and camera eye placement next.\n\nI will read app.rs sections for input, camera, escape, UI draw, and graphics setup. I also need the World struct fields, status and ui_value functions, merc mod.rs, index.html, the pack script, and the hub README protocol. I am now planning the implementation order.\n\nImplementation order is now set: Rust game-side changes first, then merc_web.rs and simhost, then index.html JavaScript, followed by native tests, Wasm build, Playwright tests, and hand-ins. World fields need serde defaults for serialization. The menu system must pass the world pointer into menu_of so shell_tick can restore it after apply_menu clears it.\n\nThe World struct will gain `pointer` and `pointer_click` fields with serde defaults. In `shell_tick`, the pointer coordinates are moved into the menu and the click flag is copied, then the local click state is reset. A single activation event fires when either confirm or click is true, so JavaScript should send one or the other. The planned act codes are 10 for pause, 11 for god mode, and 12 for slider increment.\n\nThe browser test will be written by us. We control both the command schema and the test itself. The verification only requires that the shipped hooks are actually exercised, not that they are hardcoded. We can design a clean gameTest API for this.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-161c4eba-48f7-423c-81e1-bd6ac7db47b1-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-161c4eba-48f7-423c-81e1-bd6ac7db47b1-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":360,"limit":110}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-161c4eba-48f7-423c-81e1-bd6ac7db47b1-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":2140,"limit":130}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-161c4eba-48f7-423c-81e1-bd6ac7db47b1-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":200,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-161c4eba-48f7-423c-81e1-bd6ac7db47b1-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1040,"limit":220}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9610,"output_tokens":1686,"cache_read_input_tokens":52096,"cach