{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_234","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a clear implementation plan.\n\nChecking play_pre timing and whether merc world movement uses InputFrame look. The visual camera will query the simulation host via host.query on each frame when the scene is \"merc\".\n\nRealized host.query would stall native frames for up to five seconds. The visual camera will instead read from a static mutex snapshot in pav_core::games::merc, updated by Merc::post.\n\nThe camera snapshot race is harmless. Room eye is the spawn origin plus cell position, with 1m cells and a player marker at the layout origin. The dress() function places trees in a circle around the origin and sets the ground box half extent to 6 at y=-0.2. The player body recentering happens every tick to sim.state.spawn.\n\nThe player spawn is at row 3, column 3 of the 8x8 map. The ground plane is a 12×12 box. The camera eye height is 1.58 and the pitch is -0.18, so the ground fills the lower half and the sky fills the upper half.\n\nThe verification checks for a non-uniform buffer. A sky gradient and ground geometry should pass if pixels vary, but a uniform frame would fail. Ground is #c9a24b, sky is #f0a060, and trees are green.\n\nThe camera ray at pitch -0.18 hits the ground roughly 9 meters away, but the ground plane only extends 6 meters from the origin. This means the camera would see sky through a gap unless the room floor blocks extend further. The TOML layout specifies an 8×8 floor of blocks at y0=-0.4 to y1=0.\n\nThe ground half-extent should be 40 to fill the view. Trees will be placed in front of the camera at negative Z. The eye will sit slightly forward of the body so it does not clip inside the capsule. The rifle at (0.22, 1.15, -0.35) remains visible from this position.\n\nThe ground will be enlarged to half-extent (40, 0.2, 40). A band of trees will sit at z = -4 to -12, and a ridge of laterite boxes will add surface variation. The room view sets the sky color.\n\nThe nodraw flag will skip gfx.draw when ?nodraw=1 while still creating the canvas. Launch tests must render real frames and wait for non-clear pixels because software WebGPU is slow. Browser tests can use nodraw. A tick cap of 120 on menus helps advance the simulation, but rendering remains sluggish.\n\nThe first frame after WASM initialization must paint the overlook. The camera must be set before the first draw, not waiting for the simulation status to publish. It should initialize immediately when the scene is merc with a default overlook pose. The boot screen, stats, and guide will also be hidden at startup.\n\nThe egui closure will skip all visual panels for the merc scene. This leaves the pass nearly empty so the 3D view shows through.\n\nFor the merc scene, Escape will not open the menu; JavaScript sends action 10 instead. Input handling will bypass relative mouse movement and use stick axes, mouse delta, pad axes, and actions directly. Both Rust keyboard mapping and JavaScript page capture will feed the game bridge, though this risks double input. Playwright dispatches KeyboardEvents at the page level, which may not reach winit's canvas listener depending on focus, so page-level capture is the more reliable test path.\n\nOn WASM, the merc scene will rely solely on JavaScript input. The tick_once path will replace the Rust input frame with the JS pull, so winit keyboard and mouse events are ignored for menu and movement. Native tests that call World::tick directly can still use winit look input.\n\nThe JavaScript input path will be authoritative on WASM. Each tick will overwrite look, axes, act, and buttons from the bridge. app.rs will leave move_dir at its default for the merc scene so winit cannot double-input. The frame order is: winit writes shared.input first, then tick_once reads it, merges the JS bridge values, and steps.\n\nJavaScript keydown capture will use the window capture phase to record edge-triggered actions, buttons, and look. It will call stopImmediatePropagation so winit cannot also see the event. This prevents double input for both tests and real users.\n\nPointer lock mousemove events will feed look deltas into a queue that Rust pulls each tick. A gameTest.queue will hold scripted commands.\n\nWhile the player is in the Playing state, shell_tick is skipped except for pause and save actions. Actions 11, 12, 13, 15, and 16 must therefore be handled directly inside World::tick before the screen branch. An apply_act method will dispatch these actions, starting with action 11 to toggle god mode.\n\nAction 12 increments the eighth tuning parameter. Action 13 resets all tuning values to their defaults. Action 14 toggles the Xbox controller mode. Action 15 writes a save file. Action 16 is reserved for continuing from an existing save. Action 14 will be removed from shell_tick to prevent double toggling.\n\nAction 16 will load a save and resume in the Playing state. It can be triggered from the title screen or while already playing.\n\nA browser test will verify this flow: write a save, reload the page, confirm Continue appears, and ensure the restored game matches the saved state. The save blob lives in the world, so writing from the Title screen is valid.\n\nlocalStorage persistence will be handled in merc_web. It stores the save blob whenever saves_written increases, and on first apply it restores any existing blob from localStorage into the world without replacing the live state so Continue can load it later.\n\nWorld gains pointer and pointer_click fields with serde defaults. shell_tick copies them into MenuInput and clears them each tick.\n\nNew fields added to World must use #[serde(default)] so old saves remain compatible.\n\nblank() must initialize the new fields. Dev mode will be hidden on the hub screen. The about page will list all source fields and feedback while avoiding banned substrings like \"todo\", \"tbd\", and \"lorem\". It will only mention \"Far Cry 2\" on the Source line. Feedback content must not reference Jackal or UFLL.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04d380dc-fc3f-4e5c-897c-b2ca9b1cb4a8-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs","offset":580,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04d380dc-fc3f-4e5c-897c-b2ca9b1cb4a8-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"play\\.key|state\\.play","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-04d380dc-fc3f-4e5c-897c-b2ca9b1cb4a8-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/Cargo.toml","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3656,"output_tokens":3389,"cache_read_input_tokens":107008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"28819f10-4307-4849-b537-fe092afdaa3c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-04d380dc-fc3f-4e5c-897c-b2ca9b1cb4a8-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"580→        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), 0.5);\\n        acc += 0.5;\\n    }\\n    assert!(w.attract_loops >= 5, \\\"loops {}\\\", w.attract_loops);\\n    assert_eq!(w.attract_seen, (1u16 << 10) - 1, \\\"seen {:b}\\\", w.attract_seen);\\n    assert_eq!(w.saves_written, saves);\\n\\n    let mut w = World::campaign(4, Route::Human);\\n    let mut seen = vec![format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", w.screen)];\\n    for bit in [buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP, buttons::CONFIRM, buttons::JUMP] {\\n590→        w.tick(&press(bit), DT);\\n        seen.push(format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", w.screen));\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Playing, \\\"{seen:?}\\\");\\n    assert!(seen.windows(2).all(|p| p[0] != p[1]), \\\"{seen:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn fiction_has_no_source_names_and_no_audio_files() {\\n    let banned = [\\n600→        \\\"jackal\\\", \\\"ufll\\\", \\\"apr\\\", \\\"pala\\\", \\\"mosate\\\", \\\"bowa\\\", \\\"leboa\\\", \\\"oluwagembi\\\", \\\"mike's bar\\\", \\\"marty\\\", \\\"alencar\\\",\\n        \\\"warren clyde\\\", \\\"paul ferenc\\\", \\\"hyppolite\\\", \\\"xianyong\\\", \\\"josip\\\", \\\"hakim\\\", \\\"bilders\\\", \\\"quarbani\\\", \\\"voorhees\\\",\\n        \\\"todo\\\", \\\"tbd\\\", \\\"placeholder\\\", \\\"lorem\\\",\\n    ];\\n    for line in fiction_lines() {\\n        let low = line.to_lowercase();\\n        if low.contains(\\\"far cry 2\\\") {\\n            assert!(line.contains(\\\"Source:\\\"), \\\"{line}\\\");\\n        }\\n        for word in banned {\\n610→            assert!(!low.contains(word), \\\"{word} in {line}\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let root = Path::new(env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\")).join(\\\"src/games/merc\\\");\\n    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(&root).unwrap() {\\n        let path = entry.unwrap().path();\\n        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(&path).unwrap_or_default().to_lowercase();\\n        for word in banned {\\n            assert!(!text.contains(word), \\\"{word} in {}\\\", path.display());\\n        }\\n620→    }\\n    let engine = Path::new(env!(\\\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\\\")).join(\\\"../..\\\");\\n    let mut audio = Vec::new();\\n    walk_audio(&engine, &mut audio);\\n    assert!(audio.is_empty(), \\\"shipped audio files: {audio:?}\\\");\\n}\\n\\nfn walk_audio(dir: &Path, out: &mut Vec<String>) {\\n    let Ok(rd) = std::fs::read_dir(dir) else { return };\\n    for entry in rd.flatten() {\\n630→        let path = entry.path();\\n        if path.file_name().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\\\"target\\\") {\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n        if path.is_dir() {\\n            walk_audio(&path, out);\\n        } else if let Some(ext) = path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) {\\n            if matches!(ext, \\\"wav\\\" | \\\"mp3\\\" | \\\"ogg\\\") {\\n                out.push(path.display().to_string());\\n            }\\n640→        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn net_loopback_shares_one_fire_cell() {\\n    let mut host = World::fresh(1);\\n    let mut client = World::fresh(2);\\n    assert!(host.fire.ignite_at(200.0, -200.0, 10.0, host.minutes));\\n    let mut link = Link::new(7, 0.15, 0.0, 0.0);\\n650→    host_publish(&host, &mut link, false);\\n    assert!(link.max_bytes < 1200);\\n    for _ in 0..10 {\\n        link.advance(0.1);\\n    }\\n    let bodies = link.poll();\\n    assert!(bodies.iter().any(|b| b.contains(\\\"\\\\\\\"t\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fire\\\\\\\"\\\")));\\n    client_apply(&mut client, &bodies);\\n    let shared = host.fire.cells.keys().any(|c| client.fire.cells.get(c).is_some_and(|cell| cell.burning));\\n    assert!(shared, \\\"host and client should share a burning cell within 1s\\\");\",\"content_concise\":\"580→        w.tick(&InputFrame::default(), 0.5);\\n        acc += 0.5;\\n    }\\n    assert!(w.attract_loops >= 5, \\\"loops {}\\\", w.attract_l