rror":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c3fe23e1-b719-4b1a-8171-2d4408e46a85-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"69→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n70→pub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n80→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Radians of look since the previous tick (x = yaw, y = pitch). Summed and cleared like `pressed`.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n90→    pub look: Vec2,\\n    /// Analog vehicle axes: x steer, y throttle (positive) / brake (negative).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub axes: Vec2,\\n    /// Encoded menu or world action for replays and the bot (Jam Cry). 0 means none.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub act: u32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n100→    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"69→#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n70→pub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n80→    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Radians of look since the previous tick (x = yaw, y = pitch). Summed and cleared like `pressed`.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n90→    pub look: Vec2,\\n    /// Analog vehicle axes: x steer, y throttle (positive) / brake (negative).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub axes: Vec2,\\n    /// Encoded menu or world action for replays and the bot (Jam Cry). 0 means none.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub act: u32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n100→    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs\",\"offset\":69,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct InputFrame {\\n    /// Desired movement on the ground plane: x = world +X, y = world +Z. Length <= 1.\\n    pub move_dir: Vec2,\\n    /// Vertical intent for climbing/flying/swimming (-1..1).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub vertical: f32,\\n    /// World-space aim point (mouse on the ground plane, or stick projection).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub aim: Option<Vec3>,\\n    /// Buttons held this tick.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub held: u32,\\n    /// Buttons that went down since the previous tick (never lost, even for short taps).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub pressed: u32,\\n    /// A menu action this tick (Shardfall: equip, sell, travel...), queued one per tick.\\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \\\"Option::is_none\\\")]\\n    pub cmd: Option<crate::arpg::GameCmd>,\\n    /// Radians of look since the previous tick (x = yaw, y = pitch). Summed and cleared like `pressed`.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub look: Vec2,\\n    /// Analog vehicle axes: x steer, y throttle (positive) / brake (negative).\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub axes: Vec2,\\n    /// Encoded menu or world action for replays and the bot (Jam Cry). 0 means none.\\n    #[serde(default)]\\n    pub act: u32,\\n}\\n\\nimpl InputFrame {\\n    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.held & b != 0\\n    }\\n    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\\n        self.pressed & b != 0\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":106}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"7cd63161-f07b-4a8a-b304-0742369304ee"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_238","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"look.x adds to yaw. Pointer lock mousemove changes yaw through input.\n\nPlanning world.rs changes. Adding pointer and pointer_click fields with serde defaults. Moving act 14 from shell_tick into tick(). Updating shell_tick to copy pointer state. Hiding Dev rows when the hub is active. Expanding about_pages. Considering a continue_save method.\n\nshell.rs will keep menu_of and set pointer state in shell_tick. The new pointer fields on World are accessible from shell.rs because shell_tick is an impl World method. Pause screen rows will include Resume, Settings, and Controls.\n\nThe Pause menu will include a Dev mode row when the hub is inactive, plus a Quit to title option. The about_pages content is being structured with Source Information fields including date, source, plan, genre, tech, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, and model details. Testing Feedback questions will follow in a specific order.\n\nTesting Feedback will ask four questions: total issues caught, critical issues, most helpful test, and least helpful test. Engine Feedback will ask six questions about likes, stuck points, building the game, hardest part, changes made, and one wish. Prompt Feedback will ask four questions about likes, confusion, hardest part, and desired change. Issue counts will be pulled from real log files rather than invented.\n\nTallying real log failures to answer the testing questions. Roughly 31 distinct issues were identified: about 17 post-compile and 14 compile errors.\n\nThe scratch directory will be listed in parallel with code edits to verify counts from real logs. Roughly six issues are game-breaking and prevent campaign completion: ignite, panic, rain, sleep/reman, contract_d2, and enemy jam. The remaining failures are test mismatches that are real simulation bugs.\n\nI will grep scratch logs for FAILED and error patterns to verify issue counts. I also need to write notes/feedback.md.\n\nFor merc dress, I will expand the trees and ground. I am adding a static Overlook struct in merc/mod.rs to store the camera eye position, yaw, and pitch.\n\nThe overlook() function returns a cloned Overlook struct. The merc post-render step updates yaw and pitch from the world state with a -0.18 visual pitch bias, clamping pitch between -1.0 and 0.6, while keeping the eye fixed at [0.15, 1.55, 2.6]. The app will read this overlook value before rig.update when the scene is merc. A skip_draw flag in merc_web will let the app bypass normal drawing.\n\nskip_draw is false on native builds. Nodraw tests do not check pixels, and launch tests do not set nodraw.\n\nA tick_cap function will cap simulation ticks based on whether the screen is playing. On WASM it calls merc_web::tick_cap; otherwise it caps at 8.\n\nIn simhost, the Game trait must be in scope. The tick_once function will apply merc_web::apply before stepping when targeting WASM.\n\nAfter stepping the simulation, simhost will call merc_web::publish on WASM. The app will set the merc camera from the overlook static before rig.update, using a 68-degree FOV and 0.08–3000 near/far plane. Input handling will branch by scene: merc uses the overlook yaw and pitch directly, while other scenes keep standard movement.\n\nChecking whether Input carries a look delta field. For WASM, JavaScript mouse capture should suffice without wiring winit look directly.\n\nTo prevent double speed when both JavaScript and the app send movement, merc keys will use stopImmediatePropagation on keydown so winit never receives them.\n\nEscape key handling is being added.\n\nEscape now toggles the menu in non-merc scenes and sends act 10 from the page script in merc. The UI closure will be wrapped with an early return for the merc scene to avoid error-prone per-panel guards.\n\nThe UI closure will be guarded by a `show_engine_ui` flag instead of an early return. When the scene is merc, boot, stats, and guide panels are hidden, and touch draw, hint bar, pause menu, game HUD, course HUD, and game lines are skipped.\n\nToast notifications will remain visible in the merc scene. The canvas size will be checked after the first browser run, and index.html is next.\n\nThe index.html replacement will preserve the WebGPU check and canvas observer while adding a session marker, hub metadata, DOM shell, and game scripts. The packer requires exactly one title, description, theme-color, and manifest link. The template theme color is set to #2a2420 with a build script override. The description will be one or two sentences about a first-person contract in the last dry season. The title stays as Shardfall in the template and gets replaced by the build.\n\nThe session script will be inserted immediately after the charset tag. The `/*__SESSION_JS__*/` marker must not appear inside session.js itself. The gameBridge script is placed before the closing body tag, so it loads before the WASM module and packer scripts. The script type for the game script still needs to be determined.\n\nThe game script will use classic type so it runs synchronously before the WASM module. Session.js must come first in the head to ensure AIHub is ready. Math.random will be avoided. Web Audio starts on the first keydown or pointerdown. The DOM shell paints rows via requestAnimationFrame reading window.__game, and a static title renders before wasm loads. Row clicks queue pointer and click events through the gameTest queue.\n\nShell hover coordinates are mapped to row i at [400, 220+i*80+10]. The DOM shell can also call gameInput directly. Tests live in `{dev}/tests/run.sh` and are run with `run.sh all`, which covers cargo test groups plus any separate browser tests.\n\nTest output must show only failures and a final one-line count. Cargo --quiet may still print, so filtering is needed. The full test command runs after code is finished and covers sim, ui, audio, browser, and hub tests. Steps 6-8 are separate launches that also run and save logs.\n\nTo avoid redundant browser tests, the plan is to run `run.sh` subsets for each verification step and then execute `run.sh all` once at the end. Browser tests are slow because they compile WASM first. A full dist build of the full pav_app can take five to fifteen minutes.\n\nNative tests and the WASM build cannot run concurrently because they share the same Cargo target directory. Native tests will run first, followed by the WASM build. The merc_web module must also compile on native targets using stub functions.\n\nmerc_web.rs will use cfg gates to provide stub implementations for native builds and real WASM functions. Native tick_cap always returns 8, while WASM tick_cap caps at 120 when the screen is playing. simhost can call these functions unconditionally because the native versions are no-ops. The Game trait import in simhost now includes Merc and Screen.\n\nThe apply JSON schema defines look, move, axes, buttons, pressed, act, hover, click, and device flags. pull() aggregates the queue since the last call. The save blob is stored under the localStorage key jamcry-save; on boot, a present entry sets has_save. Hub sessions replace localStorage with an empty object, so the save remains invisible to them, and write_save returns immediately in hub mode.\n\nAct 16 reloads the saved world state when a save exists, preserving the save counter and blob. Pointer fields are safe because they live in the struct and get written to the save. God mode is next.\n\nToggling the dev.god flag is sufficient for the god-mode test. The fire_spread slider is exposed in the status panel and incremented by act 12. The merc suite runs quickly, so native tests will be executed after Rust edits but before the WASM build.\n\nAbout text will be stored as separate strings in the `ui.about` array. The DOM will render them inside a hidden `#about` element using large type, making the content available before navigation. Tests will open the About screen and read the text.\n\nThe About text will be rendered visibly in the DOM at 32px when the screen is About, since hidden elements still appear in textContent. The source line must read exactly \"Source: Far Cry 2\".\n\nA notes/feedback.md file will be created in the dev folder. PROGRESS.md and an exit-interview will be written after tests so the counts are real. A deviations bullet will be added to the goal plan once the page ships. Checklist items will be flipped only after their evidence files are complete.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-540a3dfb-6654-4274-8c87-e38ae137b269-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^fn |^#\\[test\\]","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-540a3dfb-6654-4274-8c87-e38ae137b269-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^fn |#\\[test\\]","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_audio","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-540a3dfb-6654-4274-8c87-e38ae137b269-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","offset":1190,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1058,"output_tokens":4761,"cache_read_input_tokens":126080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"38d1667f-8a29-4afb-9fae-8e24dee8ec59"}
