"content\":\"        let rewinding = game_input && self.studio_mode == StudioMode::World && self.input.rewind_held();\"},{\"line_number\":1010,\"content\":\"        let game_input = game_input && !studio_active;\"},{\"line_number\":1156,\"content\":\"        let touch_game = curr.game.as_deref().filter(|_| game_input).map(|g| (g, feet, facing));\"},{\"line_number\":1159,\"content\":\"        if game_input {\"},{\"line_number\":1176,\"content\":\"        if left_tap && !self.editor.on && game_input {\"},{\"line_number\":1198,\"content\":\"            if game_input {\"},{\"line_number\":1257,\"content\":\"        if let Some(a) = intent.aiming.filter(|_| game_input) {\"},{\"line_number\":1277,\"content\":\"        if self.app_settings.aim_marker && game_input && curr.player.is_some() && !self.editor.on && curr.game.is_none() {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"f6ef94f5-eab7-4435-9ca3-0e56cc5662eb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_240","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Game input is active when the menu is closed.\n\nMerc input merging logic is being defined. JS move data should replace the frame's move_dir when provided. JS look data should overwrite the frame's look value.\n\nInput is written every frame and cleared after tick_once. JS pull runs once per tick. Key presses and pointer clicks trigger only once per keydown. Look deltas are summed until pull. The next step is implementing the JS pull function.\n\nThe JS pull function is being implemented. It returns a copy of the pending input state and resets look, pressed, and act to zero.\n\nThe JS pull function now also resets click and hover. The publish function stores both raw JSON strings and parsed objects in window.__game for convenience.\n\nThe JS pull function will drain commands from a test queue into the pending input state before returning. WASD key presses will be tracked to drive movement each pull. Enter, Space, and NumpadEnter map to act 1 for confirmation when not in a hub card. Escape maps to act 10.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb8c9b23-8ee0-4ba9-920b-f6a55dfd3e0c-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"054c|0ce6|Vendor","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":623,"output_tokens":1028,"cache_read_input_tokens":132992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5bccdbef-3bce-4728-9cad-f05dff851b99"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fb8c9b23-8ee0-4ba9-920b-f6a55dfd3e0c-65","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,56,54,58,32,32,110,97,118,105,103,97,116,111,114,46,103,101,116,71,97,109,101,112,97,100,115,32,61,32,40,41,32,61,62,32,91,123,32,105,100,58,39,83,116,117,98,32,40,83,84,65,78,68,65,82,68,32,71,65,77,69,80,65,68,32,86,101,110,100,111,114,58,32,48,53,52,99,32,80,114,111,100,117,99,116,58,32,48,99,101,54,41,39,44,32,105,110,100,101,120,58,48,44,32,99,111,110,110,101,99,116,101,100,58,116,114,117,101,44,32,109,97,112,112,105,110,103,58,39,115,116,97,110,100,97,114,100,39,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c7b746cc-cb04-4c14-9b3f-3b7efccdf83e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_241","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61e93395-f6f8-43d7-b3a5-f7b24c242419-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md","offset":70,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1290,"output_tokens":72,"cache_read_input_tokens":133504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d80fb288-b95f-4767-b0ce-8b738d3e1477"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-61e93395-f6f8-43d7-b3a5-f7b24c242419-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→\\n### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\\nI pasted `lib/hub/session.js` unmodified as the first script in the built page, right after `<meta charset>`, added the `hub:*` metas and a small connect/ready/send/finish shim, and served it with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`. **`window.__hubCheck.pass` was true** for all of these:\\n- `players=2`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server`\\n\\nEach software-rendered copy reached `ready()` in under 2.5 s. The harness gives all copies 20 s, so build the session scene small and call `ready()` before the first drawn frame.\\n\\n80→**The game's own card passes too.** With `card:true` and a capture-phase `keydown` listener in the page's JS that calls `AIHub.answer('ready')` on Enter, the harness's extra check passed at 2 and 4 players and in the server case. The harness dispatches a synthetic Enter at the focused element, so answer it in the JS shim rather than waiting for the Rust side.\\n\\n### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\\n- **Controller stub:** a plain-object stub works with gilrs on wasm (the engine logs \\\"gamepad connected\\\", the UI flips to gamepad prompts, and button 9 opens the menu):\\n  ```js\\n  window.__pad = { axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0})) };\\n  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\\n    timestamp:performance.now(), axes:window.__pad.axes.slice(), buttons:window.__pad.buttons, vibrationActuator:null }, null, null, null];\\n  ```\\n- **Pointer lock:**\\n90→  - `requestPointerLock({unadjustedMovement:true})` rejects with `NotSupportedError` here, so fall back to the plain call, which works.\\n  - While locked, `page.mouse.move` gives `movementX = 0`, so tests must dispatch `new MouseEvent('mousemove',{movementX,movementY,bubbles:true})`.\\n  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\\n  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\\n- **Two pages:**\\n  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\\n  - WebRTC with manual offer and answer (no ICE servers) opens over loopback in under 1 s. The codes are about 850 base64 characters.\\n- **Playwright** is in the user's site-packages, so `python3 -I script.py` can't import it. Keep your test scripts in `tests/` and run them without `-I`.\\n\\n### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\\n100→| Gap | Evidence | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\\n| No sky | `Scene.clear_color` is flat, and `apply_fog` (scene.wgsl) also fogs unlit meshes, so a dome would vanish | Add a `flags::NO_FOG` bit and build a sky dome (§6.2) |\\n| Terrain is 1 m terraces with a hard-coded palette, flattened to y = 0 around footprints | `terrain.rs` | New smooth generator behind the streaming code (§6.1) |\\n| The car can't pitch or roll, and only the player can drive | `set_enabled_rotations(false, true, false…)`; `drive_vehicles` uses only the player's input, steering toward a world direction | §5.11 |\\n| Nav only works on floor blocks near y = 0 | `NavGrid::build` | Outdoor nav (§5.13) |\\n| Shots are for bullet-hell | `Team::Player` shots only hit things with `health`; the `Hit` event stuns for 0.6 s | Your own hitscan (§5.2) |\\n| Sound is a closed `match` on events, with no buses, loops, music or voices | `pav_audio::sounds_for` | §10 |\\n| HUD is text lines; the only menu is a pavilion debug menu; no title screen | `pav_ui::game_lines`, `pav_app/ui.rs` | Your own 10-foot UI kit and shell (§8) |\",\"content_concise\":\"70→\\n### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\\nI pasted `lib/hub/session.js` unmodified as the first script in the built page, right after `<meta charset>`, added the `hub:*` metas and a small connect/ready/send/finish shim, and served it with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`. **`window.__hubCheck.pass` was true** for all of these:\\n- `players=2`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server`\\n\\nEach software-rendered copy reached `ready()` in under 2.5 s. The harness gives all copies 20 s, so build the session scene small and call `ready()` before the first drawn frame.\\n\\n80→**The game's own card passes too.** With `card:true` and a capture-phase `keydown` listener in the page's JS that calls `AIHub.answer('ready')` on Enter, the harness's extra check passed at 2 and 4 players and in the server case. The harness dispatches a synthetic Enter at the focused element, so answer it in the JS shim rather than waiting for the Rust side.\\n\\n### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\\n- **Controller stub:** a plain-object stub works with gilrs on wasm (the engine logs \\\"gamepad connected\\\", the UI flips to gamepad prompts, and button 9 opens the menu):\\n  ```js\\n  window.__pad = { axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0})) };\\n  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\\n    timestamp:performance.now(), axes:window.__pad.axes.slice(), buttons:window.__pad.buttons, vibrationActuator:null }, null, null, null];\\n  ```\\n- **Pointer lock:**\\n90→  - `requestPointerLock({unadjustedMovement:true})` rejects with `NotSupportedError` here, so fall back to the plain call, which works.\\n  - While locked, `page.mouse.move` gives `movementX = 0`, so tests must dispatch `new MouseEvent('mousemove',{movementX,movementY,bubbles:true})`.\\n  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\\n  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\\n- **Two pages:**\\n  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\\n  - WebRTC with manual offer and answer (no ICE servers) opens over loopback in under 1 s. The codes are about 850 base64 characters.\\n- **Playwright** is in the user's site-packages, so `python3 -I script.py` can't import it. Keep your test scripts in `tests/` and run them without `-I`.\\n\\n### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\\n100→| Gap | Evidence | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\\n| No sky | `Scene.clear_color` is flat, and `apply_fog` (scene.wgsl) also fogs unlit meshes, so a dome would vanish | Add a `flags::NO_FOG` bit and build a sky dome (§6.2) |\\n| Terrain is 1 m terraces with a hard-coded palette, flattened to y = 0 around footprints | `terrain.rs` | New smooth generator behind the streaming code (§6.1) |\\n| The car can't pitch or roll, and only the player can drive | `set_enabled_rotations(false, true, false…)`; `drive_vehicles` uses only the player's input, steering toward a world direction | §5.11 |\\n| Nav only works on floor blocks near y = 0 | `NavGrid::build` | Outdoor nav (§5.13) |\\n| Shots are for bullet-hell | `Team::Player` shots only hit things with `health`; the `Hit` event stuns for 0.6 s | Your own hitscan (§5.2) |\\n| Sound is a closed `match` on events, with no buses, loops, music or voices | `pav_audio::sounds_for` | §10 |\\n| HUD is text lines; the only menu is a pavilion debug menu; no title screen | `pav_ui::game_lines`, `pav_app/ui.rs` | Your own 10-foot UI kit and shell (§8) |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\n### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\\nI pasted `lib/hub/session.js` unmodified as the first script in the built page, right after `<meta charset>`, added the `hub:*` metas and a small connect/ready/send/finish shim, and served it with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`. **`window.__hubCheck.pass` was true** for all of these:\\n- `players=2`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server`\\n\\nEach software-rendered copy reached `ready()` in under 2.5 s. The harness gives all copies 20 s, so build the session scene small and call `ready()` before the first drawn frame.\\n\\n**The game's own card passes too.** With `card:true` and a capture-phase `keydown` listener in the page's JS that calls `AIHub.answer('ready')` on Enter, the harness's extra check passed at 2 and 4 players and in the server case. The harness dispatches a synthetic Enter at the focused element, so answer it in the JS shim rather than waiting for the Rust side.\\n\\n### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\\n- **Controller stub:** a plain-object stub works with gilrs on wasm (the engine logs \\\"gamepad connected\\\", the UI flips to gamepad prompts, and button 9 opens the menu):\\n  ```js\\n  window.__pad = { axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,touched:false,value:0})) };\\n  navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id:'Stub (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard',\\n    timestamp:performance.now(), axes:window.__pad.axes.slice(), buttons:window.__pad.buttons, vibrationActuator:null }, null, null, null];\\n  ```\\n- **Pointer lock:**\\n  - `requestPointerLock({unadjustedMovement:true})` rejects with `NotSupportedError` here, so fall back to the plain call, which works.\\n  - While locked, `page.mouse.move` gives `movementX = 0`, so tests must dispatch `new MouseEvent('mousemove',{movementX,movementY,bubbles:true})`.\\n  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\\n  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\\n- **Two pages:**\\n  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\\n  - WebRTC with manual offer and answer (no ICE servers) opens over loopback in under 1 s. The codes are about 850 base64 characters.\\n- **Playwright** is in the user's site-packages, so `python3 -I script.py` can't import it. Keep your test scripts in `tests/` and run them without `-I`.\\n\\n### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\\n| Gap | Evidence | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\\n| No sky | `Scene.clear_color` is flat, and `apply_fog` (scene.wgsl) also fogs unlit meshes, so a dome would vanish | Add a `flags::NO_FOG` bit and build a sky dome (§6.2) |\\n| Terrain is 1 m terraces with a hard-coded palette, flattened to y = 0 around footprints | `terrain.rs` | New smooth generator behind the streaming code (§6.1) |\\n| The car can't pitch or roll, and only the player can drive | `set_enabled_rotations(false, true, false…)`; `drive_vehicles` uses only the player's input, steering toward a world direction | §5.11 |\\n| Nav only works on floor blocks near y = 0 | `NavGrid::build` | Outdoor nav (§5.13) |\\n| Shots are for bullet-hell | `Team::Player` shots only hit things with `health`; the `Hit` event stuns for 0.6 s | Your own hitscan (§5.2) |\\n| Sound is a closed `match` on events, with no buses, loops, music or voices | `pav_audio::sounds_for` | §10 |\\n| HUD is text lines; the only menu is a pavilion debug menu; no title screen | `pav_ui::game_lines`, `pav_app/ui.rs` | Your own 10-foot UI kit and shell (§8) |\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"6c83f9f3-79f3-48d6-8fdb-c67559ad3ca6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_242","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The gamepad stub is installed by the test, not the page.\n\nThe page will poll getGamepads to detect the stub and lock the device as Gamepad. This prevents keyboard input from overriding the glyph. The default is already Gamepad, but the launch test uses keyboard which flips it unless locked. The glyph test installs the stub first, then checks for Cross glyphs. Polling every pull with a lock ensures reliability. The Xbox setting changes the ui.glyph to A.\n\nAct 14 toggles the Xbox glyph to A. The test can send this action or click the \"Xbox glyphs\" UI element. Toggling twice returns it to its original state.\n\nFor pointer lock yaw in headless mode, the test may request pointer lock and dispatch mouse events. The page will listen for mousemove while document.pointerLockElement is active, adding movementX to the look angle.\n\nThe mousemove listener converts pointer lock movement into yaw and pitch changes. A 100-pixel delta yields roughly 0.2 radians of rotation.\n\nIf pointer lock is lost during play, the game pauses automatically.\n\nClicking the canvas will request pointer lock while the game is active.\n\nThe click handler will call requestPointerLock on the canvas and swallow any promise rejection. Unadjusted mouse movement will be ignored.\n\nFor Playwright iPhone emulation, the page will detect coarse pointers and lack of hover via matchMedia to identify touch devices.\n\nThe phone test will use ?test=1&nodraw=1 to skip canvas drawing. The engine's touch_screen flag is ignored for merc. The test waits until the screen is Attract. On that screen only \"Press any button\" rows appear, so the Settings button may not be visible.\n\nThe touch-only criterion requires the notice, a Settings button, and attract mode to all be present. The Settings button must remain in the DOM during attract mode so it stays visible alongside the notice.\n\nThe Settings button will be a persistent DOM element separate from the menu rows. It exits attract mode and opens the settings screen via actions. The notice text must read exactly \"Controller or keyboard required\". No virtual touch controls will be added.\n\nWebKit launch without WebGPU flags should display the \"needs WebGPU\" text. The save and continue test uses nodraw=1&test=1, writes a save from the title screen, checks localStorage, reloads, confirms the Continue row appears, and resumes into Playing. Rust increments saves_written after act 15, and the next publish or apply step persists that count to localStorage.\n\nThe publish function persists saves_written after the step completes. It writes the save blob to localStorage only when saves_written exceeds the last known count and the world has no existing save. On first apply, it restores any saved blob from storage if the world is empty.\n\nMusic volume is checked via status.audio.music and Web Audio gain. The About screen must contain phrases like Date, Environment, Model, Usage, Plan, Genre, Tech, Art, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, and Testing Feedback answers. The hub connection is established at parse time before the WASM module loads, so ready() resolves within 2.5 seconds.\n\nServer mode skips local drawing and player input. The page sets a server flag on the document element. Merc_web checks this flag to skip draw calls. The host still sends world state to clients. Rust runs the simulation without applying local input.\n\nThe server harness sends world state to clients and receives poses and acknowledgments. The host page must not finish the match when it leaves, because completion only occurs on time-up while the host is still connected.\n\nNon-host players who leave are removed from the present list. The host must remain in that list so standings still include them.\n\nStandings are arrays of player IDs sorted best first. One group means a tie. Every still-present player appears exactly once.\n\nThe match finishes immediately on time-up. Sending stops once ended is set.\n\nThe card display shows the title, colored players, howto, goal, and countdown.\n\nPlayer names will be set via textContent instead of innerHTML.\n\nA capture-phase keydown listener on the window will intercept Enter and M keys while the AI hub is active and the match has not started. It will answer ready or more, prevent default behavior, and stop propagation. Other keys will queue as actions.\n\nA BroadcastChannel named jamcry-depot will connect two pages for multiplayer testing and menu communication.\n\nA `showResults` function reveals the results element with a fixed message. The `window.gameNet` object implements `startBroadcast`, which opens a `BroadcastChannel` and handles hello, ack, and done messages.\n\nThe BroadcastChannel hello message will use a fixed ID of 1 instead of a random value. Each page sends hello and receives the other's hello back as an ack, then shows results. Because BroadcastChannel does not echo own messages, both pages can safely display the result without conflict.\n\nThe WebRTC path is only used when the AI hub is inactive. It uses a loopback peer connection with no ICE servers. The offer is built by gathering candidates, creating an offer, setting the local description, waiting for ICE to complete, and encoding the SDP as base64 JSON.\n\nThe WebRTC data channel sends a 'go' message to trigger the results display on both peers. The test harness will use two pages in a single browser context, which satisfies the BroadcastChannel and WebRTC requirements.\n\nA `canRtc()` helper will block WebRTC when the AI hub is active. The test will verify that no shared-world state is generated by `Math.random` by counting calls after navigation.\n\nThe test will assert that AIHub.active and AIHub.seeded are both false in solo mode, and that the shared-world shim did not run. session.js only calls Math.random inside an active session. The results screen must be visible as a #results element. The two-page Playwright test will use file:// URLs. The harness HTML is at dev/hub/harness.html.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1048a701-d203-4c84-bbaa-13e4af003e2a-67","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function gameUrl|function metasOf","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/harness.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1251,"output_tokens":3138,"cache_read_input_tokens":134784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"17436880-205f-4259-a516-1f3c36d10a93"}
