,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":67,\"content\":\"import { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\"},{\"line_number\":76,\"content\":\"const playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\"},{\"line_number\":77,\"content\":\"const SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\"},{\"line_number\":181,\"content\":\"  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\"},{\"line_number\":429,\"content\":\"    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\"},{\"line_number\":456,\"content\":\"    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\"},{\"line_number\":465,\"content\":\"    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\"},{\"line_number\":479,\"content\":\"    await randomly(playMs / 2);\"},{\"line_number\":497,\"content\":\"    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"783c47f2-1196-4a44-89a6-b40096233509"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_245","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The play lasts about six seconds of random keys plus time-up.\n\nBoth host and clients will send reliable messages every 250ms. The server receives poses from clients and sends world snapshots to them. Clients acknowledge receipt. The harness network may drop even reliable messages despite the README guaranteeing ordered delivery.\n\nThe simulated network applies loss to all messages, so sending many reliable packets is necessary. Acks are optional; both sides can exchange data without them.\n\nMessages will be blocked before the round starts and after it ends. A `finished` flag prevents duplicate `finish` calls. The host will call `finish` with sorted player IDs when `time-up` fires, and will also handle `leave` events.\n\nThe `leave` handler removes the departing player from `present` and skips finishing if that player is the host. The `end` handler sets a flag and stops sound. Player names will be rendered as plain text content rather than HTML. The card UI must remain visible during the card phase even though the harness only checks entered answers. A countdown will run from `card.left`. The server can skip its initial draw by reading a flag set before the WASM module loads.\n\nThe server flag is set by adding `data-jam-server=\"1\"` to the document element when `info.server` is true. The server also checks for a `?nodraw=1` query parameter. It will ignore player input while running as the server. For the canvas, the room's existing dusk background will be used and the foreground will be filled densely.\n\nThe camera sits at z=2.6 above the 8×8 room floor, so the first frames may show only sky or a sliver of ground. A large ground plane will be added inside dress() on the first post-draw tick to fill the view.\n\nThe test waits for paint, so dress() will run after a few frames. The sky must not be a uniform clear color; geometry must cover most of the frame. A ground plane will fill the lower 70% while trees and sky variation occupy the upper portion. Ground covering half the frame should satisfy the requirement that the buffer is not uniformly clear.\n\nThe camera will be tilted downward to about -0.4 radians so the ground fills roughly 80% of the frame and trees rise into the sky band above it. The rifle will sit close to the camera at 0.6 meters, and fog will remain off so colors stay distinct.\n\nThe merc scene will hide the boot screen, stats, guide, and aim marker. It will use an overhead first-person camera rig. The FpCam type must be imported from the camera module.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dbeac401-15d5-42e2-b04b-7a9db7fd705c-70","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/lib.rs","limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1228,"output_tokens":1542,"cache_read_input_tokens":139904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"318c8ecd-f357-4dc8-95be-0330c9dc3446"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dbeac401-15d5-42e2-b04b-7a9db7fd705c-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Turns simulation frames into render scenes: camera rig, interpolation, style settings.\\n\\npub mod arpg;\\npub mod assets;\\npub mod build;\\npub mod camera;\\npub mod creatures;\\npub mod fx;\\npub mod look;\\n10→pub mod materials;\\npub mod vehicles;\\npub mod water;\\n\\npub use build::{ViewBuilder, ViewSettings};\\npub use camera::{CameraParams, CameraRig};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Turns simulation frames into render scenes: camera rig, interpolation, style settings.\\n\\npub mod arpg;\\npub mod assets;\\npub mod build;\\npub mod camera;\\npub mod creatures;\\npub mod fx;\\npub mod look;\\n10→pub mod materials;\\npub mod vehicles;\\npub mod water;\\n\\npub use build::{ViewBuilder, ViewSettings};\\npub use camera::{CameraParams, CameraRig};\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/lib.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"//! Turns simulation frames into render scenes: camera rig, interpolation, style settings.\\n\\npub mod arpg;\\npub mod assets;\\npub mod build;\\npub mod camera;\\npub mod creatures;\\npub mod fx;\\npub mod look;\\npub mod materials;\\npub mod vehicles;\\npub mod water;\\n\\npub use build::{ViewBuilder, ViewSettings};\\npub use camera::{CameraParams, CameraRig};\\n\",\"total_lines\":15}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"e282bfa6-751d-4751-9ce4-7ee7ca6602cd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_246","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Camera and FpCam are public.\n\nJS input is authoritative. The `apply` function pulls from JS and only overwrites the frame if data exists. If JS returns zeros, the winit frame is kept.\n\nThe `apply` function parses the JSON look and move arrays. Look values are added to the current frame. Move values replace the frame's move direction.\n\nThe `apply` function also parses the `act` field and updates the frame's action bit. JS can send `move: null` to avoid overwriting the current move direction.\n\nButton presses are OR'd into `frame.pressed` and `frame.held`.\n\nThe device field sets the world input device to gamepad when JS sends that string. It switches to keyboard only if the device lock is zero.\n\nThe `touch` and `xbox` flags are set from JSON booleans. The `xbox` flag is not cleared on every tick to avoid overwriting the act 14 toggle; it only updates when JS explicitly sends true.\n\nThe hover array sets the pointer position, and a click flag sets `pointer_click`.\n\nAct 14 double toggle is removed from `shell_tick` and handled in `world.tick` inside `apply_console` before the screen branch.\n\nContinue and save are processed at the start of every tick, even while playing.\n\nDuring attract mode, `apply_console` runs before `shell_tick`, so a save triggered by act 15 happens first. The attract screen then exits to the title because act 15 is typed input.\n\nDev mode activation is already gated by `!self.hub`, so rows filter correctly.\n\nNew act fields use serde defaults. This preserves compatibility with old saves while new saves include the fields. The same-seed test validates save and load within a single version.\n\nPointer fields default to None or false.\n\nThe same-seed test remains valid because the pointer fields are not set in that path.\n\nI am drafting about pages and scanning for banned words. I checked several common terms and none contain the forbidden substring \"apr\".","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8fe1563d-c570-42ed-a8c1-1d19872c9814-71","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ls -la /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer | head -80","description":"List scratch logs to tally real test failures"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1707,"output_tokens":1364,"cache_read_input_tokens":141056,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c5667bd1-f59d-4707-83ff-ac8a5c8f872a"}
