rok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer\\necho \\\"CHECK1 error[ count: $(rg -c 'error\\\\[' $SCR/check1.log)\\\"\\necho \\\"---- unit1 panic/error ----\\\"\\nrg -n \\\"error\\\\[|panicked|assert\\\" $SCR/unit1.log | head -20\\necho \\\"---- unit2 assert lines ----\\\"\\nrg -n \\\"panicked|assertion|left:|right:\\\" $SCR/unit2.log | head -30\\necho \\\"---- unit3 assert ----\\\"\\nrg -n -A2 \\\"panicked\\\" $SCR/unit3.log | head -20\\necho \\\"---- play messages ----\\\"\\nrg -n \\\"stuck|missing|panicked\\\" $SCR/play1.log $SCR/play2.log $SCR/play3.log $SCR/play4.log $SCR/play5.log | head -40\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Extract distinct failure messages from scratch logs\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/terminal/call-c752d19c-229d-4c4b-9a27-c14004fcb554-73.log\",\"total_bytes\":3481}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2c284bd6-7aad-4e9a-a1f0-fc2b5e0a7277"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_249","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The unit2 fire assertion message was not seen.\n\nShop assertion and unit3 blackout HP regen were noted. 26 distinct logged issues were catalogued, spanning compile errors, missing flags, stalls, and missing assets.\n\nThe total may be 27 rather than 26. Syrette, wound, and rescue fixes were applied without logged failures. Only logged failures will count as distinct issues.\n\nTesting caught 14 compile errors in a single batch. The remaining issues are a missing KEY symbol, an unlatched fever warning, unclamped attract idle dt, fire crossing the road, vehicle damage stage off by one, blackout health regenerating past the fee wake-up, ignite stalling on an already burning cell, soldiers leaving fire before the panic flag, rain failing to light river cells, a breaking gun beating the jam on seed 2, a long sleep skipping reman on the post, and the ending flag skipping the last contract flag.\n\nThe total is 26 issues caught by testing. Six are game-breaking blockers: ignite stall, panic stall, rain stall, enemy jam, post not remanned, and contract_d2 skipped.\n\nThe bot_plays_all_three_endings test was the most helpful, pinpointing stuck goals, seeds, positions, and missing flags. The attract test was least helpful because it stepped dt=1 while World::tick clamps dt to 0.5, so it measured the clamp itself. A passing audio filter test never entered the campaign. After the green run, zero failures remained.\n\nThe summary will be finalized with 26 issues and 6 game-breaking blockers. Any browser test failures will be noted before the interview ends, and placeholders are avoided.\n\nImplementation is starting now. The shell.rs pointer and click state are being wired into menu_of. World::apply_console is being updated to handle input actions.\n\nConsole action 14 is being removed from shell_tick. A `continue_save` method is being added to World to handle both the Continue button and the console path. The rows pause logic is next.\n\nThe Pause arm is being revised. The about_pages function will be replaced with full pages while preserving the first lines and source line. A substring check for \"apr\" in \"appropriate\" will be run. The dress view will be rewritten to fill the screen. Static overlook entries need fixing in mod.rs. merc_web.rs, simhost, app.rs, main.rs, index.html, tests, and notes are next.\n\n`get` requires `Game` in scope because it is a method on `GameBox`. The `tick_cap` function is being drafted to cap simulation ticks at 120 when the merc screen is not `Playing`, and to 8 otherwise. `fast_query` will read query flags such as `?test=1`.\n\n`tick_cap` will cap simulation ticks at 120 during the title screen and test launches, and at 8 while the merc screen is active. The launch screenshot occurs on the title screen, so it will use the higher tick limit. Graphics drawing will be skipped when `nodraw` or server mode is active, but the loop must still continue because the canvas exists from initialization.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b4b50236-1816-422c-978e-ec376545114a-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","offset":1,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2229,"output_tokens":3662,"cache_read_input_tokens":148992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"b9f97f6c-50da-45f3-a230-0b0e2bae8836"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b4b50236-1816-422c-978e-ec376545114a-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! 10-foot shell. Every screen has at most seven focusable rows. Hover moves focus. Click confirms.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::world::{Screen, World};\\nuse crate::input::buttons;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→pub enum Device {\\n    Gamepad,\\n    Keyboard,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct MenuInput {\\n    pub up: bool,\\n    pub down: bool,\\n    pub left: bool,\\n20→    pub right: bool,\\n    pub confirm: bool,\\n    pub back: bool,\\n    pub pointer: Option<(f32, f32)>,\\n    pub click: bool,\\n    pub device: Option<Device>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for MenuInput {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n30→        Self { up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, confirm: false, back: false, pointer: None, click: false, device: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn glyph(action: &str, device: Device, xbox: bool) -> &'static str {\\n    match (device, xbox, action) {\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Enter\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Esc\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"LMB\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"RMB\\\",\\n40→        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"R\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"M\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Space\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Circle\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"B\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"Square\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"X\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"R2\\\",\\n50→        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"RT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"L2\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"LT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"D-pad\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"Button\\\",\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n60→fn menu_of(input: &InputFrame) -> MenuInput {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! 10-foot shell. Every screen has at most seven focusable rows. Hover moves focus. Click confirms.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::world::{Screen, World};\\nuse crate::input::buttons;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→pub enum Device {\\n    Gamepad,\\n    Keyboard,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct MenuInput {\\n    pub up: bool,\\n    pub down: bool,\\n    pub left: bool,\\n20→    pub right: bool,\\n    pub confirm: bool,\\n    pub back: bool,\\n    pub pointer: Option<(f32, f32)>,\\n    pub click: bool,\\n    pub device: Option<Device>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for MenuInput {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n30→        Self { up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, confirm: false, back: false, pointer: None, click: false, device: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn glyph(action: &str, device: Device, xbox: bool) -> &'static str {\\n    match (device, xbox, action) {\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Enter\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Esc\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"LMB\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"RMB\\\",\\n40→        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"R\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"M\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Space\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Circle\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"B\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"Square\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"X\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"R2\\\",\\n50→        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"RT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"L2\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"LT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"D-pad\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"Button\\\",\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n60→fn menu_of(input: &InputFrame) -> MenuInput {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"//! 10-foot shell. Every screen has at most seven focusable rows. Hover moves focus. Click confirms.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::world::{Screen, World};\\nuse crate::input::buttons;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum Device {\\n    Gamepad,\\n    Keyboard,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct MenuInput {\\n    pub up: bool,\\n    pub down: bool,\\n    pub left: bool,\\n    pub right: bool,\\n    pub confirm: bool,\\n    pub back: bool,\\n    pub pointer: Option<(f32, f32)>,\\n    pub click: bool,\\n    pub device: Option<Device>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for MenuInput {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self { up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, confirm: false, back: false, pointer: None, click: false, device: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn glyph(action: &str, device: Device, xbox: bool) -> &'static str {\\n    match (device, xbox, action) {\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Enter\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Esc\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"LMB\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"RMB\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"R\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"M\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Space\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Circle\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"B\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"Square\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"X\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"R2\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"RT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"L2\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"LT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"D-pad\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"Button\\\",\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn menu_of(input: &InputFrame) -> MenuInput {\\n\",\"total_lines\":447}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2a62baad-96df-486e-92a4-e9d2e5860a93"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_250","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning implementation of the code changes.\n\nAdding a fire glyph to ui_value so the test can verify R2. The device lock prevents keyboard input from flipping the active device. Browser tests will install the gamepad stub before page load via addInitScript so the first ticks lock the gamepad.\n\nThe test will verify the glyph is Cross, then toggle Xbox mode via act 14 to confirm it becomes A. The gamepad stub is injected before page scripts run, so the first device poll locks the pad before keyboard events arrive. The default Gamepad/Cross state is already present without needing the stub.\n\nThe browser test will first set the device to Keyboard so the glyph reads Enter. Then it will trigger the gamepad stub and verify the prompt flips to PlayStation glyphs.\n\nThe browser test sequence is now fully defined. The stub is injected after page load via page.evaluate, not addInitScript. The glyph starts as Enter, then polls lock the gamepad to Cross, and act 14 toggles it to A.\n\nThe JavaScript `sensePad` function will detect the gamepad stub by checking `navigator.getGamepads()` for a connected pad whose ID contains both \"054c\" and \"0ce6\". When found, it sets the pending device to gamepad and locks it. The Rust side is next.\n\nRust code now handles device switching. It sets the active device to Gamepad and locks it when the pending state is gamepad with lock enabled. Keyboard input only changes the device if no lock exists yet.\n\nPointer lock tests require the game to be in Playing state first so yaw can be simulated. The test sequence is four confirms, then pointer lock, mouse movement, and reading status.yaw.\n\nLosing pointer lock happens via exitPointerLock, pointerlockchange, act 10, or screen Pause.\n\nDev mode is reached by pausing from playing, then navigating through the menu.\n\nDev mode is opened from pause with act 11, then act 12 advances the menu. Each keydown triggers one act per pull, so a 120-tick cap limits frame consumption. The test polls for the new screen before sending the next key.\n\nTest mode and nodraw are enabled for hook tests to speed up execution. The save test also uses these flags. About screen tests will verify both the joined text and the visible #about element. The fire glyph is optional; the confirm glyph suffices. The index.html rewrite must preserve exactly one title, description, theme-color, and manifest.\n\nThe session inject script will use python3 without the `-I` flag. It will modify index.html before build-web.sh runs. The session.js path is set to the current build directory.\n\nThe final HTML output path is set to the build directory. The pack description will be a plain sentence without quotes, since the packer escapes meta tags automatically.\n\nIn app.rs, the first-person camera will be enabled every frame during Merc mode and left as None otherwise. This keeps chase disabled for Merc while preserving normal behavior for other scenes. The rig update still runs normally after setting the camera.\n\nThe first-person camera will be set just before rig.update so the build frame uses it. Merc mode will suppress hint, touch, and guide UI calls to avoid noise.\n\nMerc mode will use raw axis input for movement instead of world-space intent. The aim marker is disabled in new() so it does not draw at line 1277. The ARPG HUD and touch tips are also suppressed for Merc.\n\nThe new fields need serde defaults so old save files still load. The shell module must access the pointer field directly, so it will be public or same-module visible.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eb722ca1-98e2-4c5e-b60e-27e7a912967c-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"enum Screen","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","-A":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4333,"output_tokens":2125,"cache_read_input_tokens":151168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3f5c6a9a-2354-4c53-b1fd-32b4a59c3f2a"}
