{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_253","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll briefly examine layout parsing.\n\nI'll place trees in a wide fan around the origin so the camera sees them from any angle. A ground slab will span 80 meters centered at the origin. The camera will sit at (0, 1.5, 4) looking toward negative Z with a slight downward pitch. I'll offset the camera to avoid clipping the player capsule. The ground will be colored in bands for laterite paths. I'm writing a dress() function that creates a 40x40 ground plane and a darker road strip.\n\nI'll add 24 trees in front of the camera and include termite mounds. A rifle and rag will sit in the lower right corner near the camera. I'm preparing to write all files in a batch edit. I'll verify that about_pages strings avoid banned substrings with a quick Python check.\n\nTesting revealed 26 issues. 14 were compile errors. The remaining 12 failures cover key handling, fever latching, attract logic, fire crossing, vehicle stage indexing, blackout health regeneration, ignite on alight cells, panic, rain on the river, enemy jamming, post-remanning, and the contract flag.\n\nSix of the twelve failures were game-breaking. The bot report was most helpful. It named the route, seed, stuck goal, position, and missing flags. The attract check was the weakest. It measured a clock clamp instead of attract logic. An audio filter also never entered the contract.\n\nThe about page will list only past failures. A later browser test finding bugs would require a full WASM rebuild, so I will try to get it right the first time. Engine feedback is clean of banned words and \"Far Cry\".\n\nThe about page will list four strengths: the headless simulator, the Game trait, seeded RNG, and single-file packer. It will also list six build issues: missing first-person camera, pavilion HUD in hook games, wrong WebGPU flag, fire refusing to light burning cells, world clock clamping ticks, a stuck rest flag, and an ending finishing before the last contract flag. The hardest challenge was fitting a two-kilometre country into a small room while building a bot that trips every coverage flag.\n\nInputFrame now carries look, axes, act, and reload through confirm buttons. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene.\n\nThe wish list adds a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\n\nPrompt feedback was mixed. The checks were liked because they name the behaviour, seeds, and proof file. They were confusing because the country is a simulation inside a room scene, and the working WebGPU flag is easy to miss.\n\nThe hardest challenge is making one seeded bot reach all three endings and every coverage flag while packing a page that still paints a frame. The visual room should be described as only a window, with WebGPU flags named beside the screenshot check. I will scan for banned words after writing.\n\nThe about page will cite \"Far Cry 2\" only in the source line. The genre line reads \"Shooter, first person.\" The tech line names Rust 1.98, shardfall crates, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, WebGPU, and a single HTML page. Art direction describes sun-bleached dusk, laterite gold, dry grass, and a low sun. Meshes are flat boxes. Animation uses simulation-driven poses with no skeletal clips. Audio is code-only tones at bus 0.10 with gibberish syllables and no recorded speech.\n\nThe about page will list online support as AI Hub shared-world sessions for one to four players, plus BroadcastChannel and pasted WebRTC fallbacks when no hub is active. Testing covers native cargo tests, a seeded bot, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU, WebKit without WebGPU, and the hub harness. Research cites engine notes and system notes from this plan, with no separate source playthrough. Environment, Model, Usage, Date, and Plan fields will match the specification. A \"Testing Feedback\" header will be added to the about pages so tests can locate answers in order.\n\nAbout pages will be stored as one string per field. The DOM will stack all answers in large type inside a scrollable panel. Navigation uses Next and Back buttons. The test may read the visible page or the full array.\n\nThe About screen will use a 28-pixel font or larger. Rust rows will be Next and Back only, while body text stays visible in a scrollable panel. The DOM will place all about strings inside a single `#about` element that appears when the About screen is active.\n\nThe about strings will be embedded in the initial HTML so they are present before WASM loads. The published `ui.about` JSON will always contain them, while the visible panel only appears on the About screen. The browser test will read both the parsed JSON and the visible DOM text after navigating.\n\nThe About screen will stack all pages in large type and scroll, so every line is visible at once. Next still cycles a highlight, but no page is hidden.\n\nI will fix the `if n == 8` catch-up to use `cap` instead, only in the non-preview loop.\n\nThe merc_web module compiles on native too, even if pav_app tests do not exist.\n\nI will cfg the wasm_bindgen code in merc_web and provide native stubs so `cargo test -p pav_core` compiles without building pav_app. simhost calls `merc_web::apply` on all platforms, so native builds will use the stubs. I will also add `mod merc_web;` to main.rs.\n\nmerc_web.rs will be written completely. web_sys is gated behind `cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")`, so native builds avoid the wasm-only dependency. gameBridge is a classic script tag that exists before WASM starts. The storage key is \"jamcry-save\". Hub write_save returns early to skip persistence during shared-world sessions.\n\nContinue from localStorage will restore the saved world and set the screen to Playing. The test will verify that saves increase, reload shows Continue, and pressing Enter resumes gameplay. A race condition between publish persistence and the save tick must be handled by waiting for both status.saves and localStorage updates. The device_lock field will use type u8.\n\nA `has_save` flag will be added to status for debugging. It is not serialized into the world fingerprint, so the same_seed test remains valid. The shell pointer uses a boolean click field, and `mem::take` handles the transition cleanly when both click and confirm occur. Hovering without clicking moves focus, which tests can verify.\n\nThe browser test will include the new settings button as act 18. JavaScript touch detection will use `(pointer: coarse)` and `(hover: none)` media queries to set `touch_only` true, then send that flag on every pull rather than only once.\n\nThe Rust side only sets `touch_only` when the JSON value is true, so a persistent test flag remains active. The phone test URL will be `file.html?test=1&nodraw=1` with Playwright on an iPhone; `nodraw` skips GPU drawing but may still fail during graphics initialization.\n\nChromium with WebGPU flags can run the phone test on an iPhone viewport. WebKit only needs to show the missing-GPU message before WASM loads, so it is fast and does not need flags. No native tests are required.\n\nThe shop test still passes without act 14. Console commands run before the shell tick, so act 1 is handled by the shell and act 10 pause is skipped during attract. Act 11 toggles god mode while still simulating.\n\nI will write the code now. The HTML page will be composed carefully to keep its size small. I will create browser tests in Python using Playwright, with separate modules for launch, hooks, and hub checks, plus a run script that filters output to failures and a summary. I am also checking whether Pillow is installed to parse PNG screenshots.\n\nI will use PIL to parse PNG screenshots and detect a single dominant color, which would mean the WebGPU canvas is tainted. I am checking whether PIL is installed before running the browser tests.\n\nIf PIL is unavailable, a minimal PNG decoder using zlib and struct will be written to parse screenshots. WebGPU canvas pixels are not directly readable from the page. The viewport-matrix crate is unnecessary.\n\nCanvas width will be logged during tests. If it does not match the viewport, the browser will use a device scale factor of 1. Two launches will use 1280x720 and 1920x1080 viewports to ensure distinct runs. After the title screen is visible, Enter and Space will be pressed with waits to verify screen transitions. Page errors must remain zero.\n\nPage errors and console errors will be collected during tests, while shader warnings are logged but ignored. The loading message is removed once the canvas element appears, so screenshots capture both the left shell panel and the right canvas.\n\nThe test will screenshot only the canvas element, not the full page. The shell panel is a DOM overlay beneath the 3D canvas buffer, so the screenshot captures just the 3D view. The ground-heavy camera ensures the 3D fills the entire canvas.\n\nThe shell overlay is fixed at z-index 2 and 38% width, so the canvas sits behind it. The test will save full-page screenshots as launch-1.png to confirm the title appears in the panel while the 3D view renders on the right.\n\nThe canvas fill check will analyze the canvas element directly. Full-page screenshots will include the left shell panel, so the 3D view must render visibly to avoid a mostly clear image.\n\nI will add `use std::cell::Cell` to merc_web.rs. I am drafting an `Overlook` struct in merc/mod.rs to hold camera eye position and yaw/pitch angles, guarded by a static mutex.\n\nThe `Overlook` struct is now fully defined with an initial eye position at `[0.15, 1.55, 4.0]`, yaw `0.0`, and pitch `-0.42`. A getter returns the locked state, and a setter updates yaw and pitch. During post-processing, yaw tracks the player while pitch is clamped to `[-0.9, 0.4]`. The eye remains fixed on the dressed set, so pointer-lock tests will verify `status.yaw` instead of the camera.\n\nThe overlook camera faces toward the origin from z=4 with pitch -0.42. Trees will be placed in the view frustum from z=2 down to -8 and x=-6 to 6, with heights between 1.2 and 4. The rifle sits at (0.45, 1.15, 3.2) directly in front of the eye. Ground spans -20 to 20 on the x-axis so it covers the lower frame.\n\nThe overlook camera with pitch -0.42 and a 70-degree field of view places the horizon well above center, so the ground fills most of the frame and the silhouette is broken by trees, a red rag, and varying greens. The static mutex guarding the overlook state is safe because post-processing runs on the main thread in WASM and on the simulation thread on native. The `overlook` getter is public. I will now begin editing files, starting with world.rs, then shell, mod.rs, and finally the new modules.\n\nI will use search_replace for the about_pages replacement. The fiction_lines module only needs to extend the existing about_pages list, not duplicate every sentence. I verified that \"apr\" and \"capture\" do not appear in the text. I will write notes/feedback.md with the same answers. An exit interview at the end will let me update counts if browser tests reveal issues. The about text is embedded in the binary.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim already passes. I’m wiring the page to it: shell actions, the first-person camera, and the WebAssembly bridge."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-78","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"    pub treating: bool,\n    pub jam_seen: bool,\n    pub boat_dist: f32,\n}","new_string":"    pub treating: bool,\n    pub jam_seen: bool,\n    pub boat_dist: f32,\n    /// Menu pointer in canvas pixels. The page sets it; the shell consumes it.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub pointer: Option<(f32, f32)>,\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub pointer_click: bool,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-79","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"            treating: false,\n            jam_seen: false,\n            boat_dist: 0.0,\n        }\n    }","new_string":"            treating: false,\n            jam_seen: false,\n            boat_dist: 0.0,\n            pointer: None,\n            pointer_click: false,\n        }\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-80","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"    pub fn tick(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\n        let dt = dt.clamp(0.0, 0.5);\n        if self.screen != Screen::Playing {","new_string":"    pub fn tick(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\n        let dt = dt.clamp(0.0, 0.5);\n        self.apply_console(input);\n        if self.screen != Screen::Playing {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"    pub fn bot_input(&self) -> InputFrame {","new_string":"    /// Numbered actions from the page. These run on every screen, including play,\n    /// because the shell does not tick while a contract is running.\n    fn apply_console(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\n        match input.act {\n            11 => self.dev.god = !self.dev.god,\n            12 => {\n                let (lo, hi, step) = self.tune.range(8);\n                self.tune.set(8, (self.tune.get(8) + step).clamp(lo, hi));\n            }\n            13 => self.tune = self.tune0.clone(),\n            14 => self.xbox = !self.xbox,\n            15 => self.write_save(),\n            16 => self.continue_save(),\n            18 => {\n                self.screen = Screen::Settings;\n                self.tab = 0;\n                self.focus = 0;\n                self.idle = 0.0;\n            }\n            _ => {}\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn continue_save(&mut self) {\n        if !self.has_save {\n            return;\n        }\n        let Ok(w) = Self::load_json(&self.save_blob) else { return };\n        let saves = self.saves_written;\n        let blob = self.save_blob.clone();\n        *self = w;\n        self.saves_written = saves;\n        self.save_blob = blob;\n        self.has_save = true;\n        self.screen = Screen::Playing;\n    }\n\n    pub fn bot_input(&self) -> InputFrame {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","old_string":"    pub fn shell_tick(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\n        if input.act == 14 {\n            self.xbox = !self.xbox;\n        }\n        let typed = input.pressed != 0","new_string":"    pub fn shell_tick(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\n        let typed = input.pressed != 0"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-83","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","old_string":"            let mut m = menu_of(input);\n            if self.touch_only && input.act == 0 && input.pressed == 0 {\n                // Touch does not drive the menu. Settings is still a row a pointer can hit.\n            }\n            self.apply_menu(m);","new_string":"            let mut m = menu_of(input);\n            m.pointer = self.pointer.take();\n            m.click = std::mem::take(&mut self.pointer_click);\n            self.apply_menu(m);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-84","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","old_string":"                \"Continue\" => {\n                    if self.has_save {\n                        if let Ok(w) = World::load_json(&self.save_blob) {\n                            let saves = self.saves_written;\n                            let blob = self.save_blob.clone();\n                            *self = w;\n                            self.saves_written = saves;\n                            self.save_blob = blob;\n                            self.has_save = true;\n                            self.screen = Screen::Playing;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }","new_string":"                \"Continue\" => self.continue_save(),"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1bccd859-df42-4db3-ba3d-6ca262dffe9e-85","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","old_string":"            Screen::Pause => vec![\"Resume\".into(), \"Settings\".into(), \"Controls\".into(), \"Dev mode\".into(), \"Quit to title\".into()],","new_string":"            Screen::Pause => {\n                let mut rows = vec![\"Resume\".into(), \"Settings\".into(), \"Controls\".into()];