{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_258","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A type ordering issue was found: the Flags Cell requires Copy, but the trait was implemented after the cell was already used.\n\nThe manual Copy and Clone implementations for Flags are valid. The native tick_cap function exists. A borrow issue in simhost tick_once was noted.\n\nThe borrow issue in simhost tick_once is resolved. The input variable is now properly scoped so it can be passed to sim.step on native.\n\nThe cfg block is confirmed absent. The wasm input shadowing is valid. publish accepts &Sim after step. shell.rs may have an unused World import. menu_of still has a comment. I will compile merc tests next.\n\nThe manual Copy implementation for Flags is valid because all fields are Copy. The thread_local Cell usage is safe. I will run cargo test for merc and check fiction banned words with a quick Python script.\n\nThe manual Copy implementation for Flags might conflict with merc_web. The thread_local Cell is safe because thread_local does not require Sync. Merc implements Game, so get_mut downcasting works correctly. The old act 14 console command was removed.\n\nThe shop test uses buttons rather than act 14, so it should pass. The next step is running cargo test; compilation may take 30 to 60 seconds. A banned word scan will be skipped in favor of running the suite directly.\n\nA manual scan of the about text confirmed no banned words. \"apr\" does not appear in any word.\n\nThe wasm `publish` function calls an extern `fn publish(status: &str, ui: &str)`, which risks infinite recursion. Rust allows the manual `Copy` implementation for `Flags` even when it appears after the `thread_local` cell.\n\nThe extern `publish` collides with the Rust `publish` function in the same module. I will rename the extern to `bridge_publish` using `#[wasm_bindgen(js_name = publish)]`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ae01ab52-c6ff-4656-9c9f-02f8bdec8803-105","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs","old_string":"        #[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = gameBridge, catch)]\n        fn publish(status: &str, ui: &str) -> Result<(), JsValue>;","new_string":"        #[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = gameBridge, js_name = publish, catch)]\n        fn bridge_publish(status: &str, ui: &str) -> Result<(), JsValue>;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ae01ab52-c6ff-4656-9c9f-02f8bdec8803-106","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs","old_string":"        let _ = publish(&status, &ui);","new_string":"        let _ = bridge_publish(&status, &ui);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ae01ab52-c6ff-4656-9c9f-02f8bdec8803-107","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","old_string":"pub use world::{Route, Screen, Tune, World, about_pages, fiction_lines};","new_string":"pub use world::{Route, Screen, Tune, World, about_pages, fiction_lines};\n\n// Re-export the overlook so the window crate can aim the first-person camera."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3214,"output_tokens":2509,"cache_read_input_tokens":176768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"85a097d5-5689-4fc4-bc31-2d42309becb4"}
