s_across_a_save ... ok\\ntest net_loopback_shares_one_fire_cell ... ok\\ntest shop_tracker_and_shell ... ok\\ntest look_and_stick_follow_yaw ... ok\\ntest hits_use_zones_and_walls_block ... ok\\ntest squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks ... ok\\ntest vehicles_climb_break_and_float ... ok\\ntest fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks ... ok\\ntest scene_boots_and_history_is_off ... ok\\ntest fiction_has_no_source_names_and_no_audio_files ... ok\\ntest bot_plays_all_three_endings ... ok\\n\\ntest result: ok. 16 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.97s\\n\\n\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/terminal/call-84433370-0479-4db2-b916-acccf003e0ac-109.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"truncation_hint\":\"[truncated - use read_file on output_file for full content]\",\"raw_output_bytes\":1548}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"bae01865-a3ef-4d20-ace4-7ad2452d35d9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_264","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All Merc tests passed, including the fiction and playthrough variants.\n\nStarting the long WASM build for merc_web. Also writing a pack script to inject session.js.\n\nThe pack script copies the HTML template, injects session.js via a Python script using a marker placeholder, and runs the engine's build-web.sh to compile the WASM target.\n\nThe pack script will set CARGO_BUILD_JOBS and CARGO_TARGET_DIR in the environment. The trap ensures the HTML template is restored even if the build fails. The packed output will contain the session.js bytes directly, while the source template keeps only the marker placeholder. After packing, I will verify the injected content and page metadata. The WASM build is expected to take 5–15 minutes, so I will run it in the background and monitor progress.\n\nI will write Python tests now while the WASM build runs. I am also checking merc_web for compile issues first to avoid a long wasted build. The Flags Copy implementation and Game trait import look valid.\n\nThe wasm module imports Game and other types without conflict because the native apply and publish functions are cfg-gated out. I am checking whether Cell<Flags> needs an explicit Copy or Clone derive.\n\nConfirmed that `impl Copy for Flags` is valid because `Clone` is already implemented. The `thread_local Cell::new(Flags)` call is safe. `get_mut` and `restore_save` do not reenter. `publish` and `apply` use separate calls. `wasm_bindgen` externs inside modules are allowed.\n\nThe `js_name = publish` binding correctly generates a bridge_publish wrapper. I will replace the manual `Copy` implementation with `#[derive(Copy, Clone)]` for safety, since all fields are trivially copyable. I also spotted a bug in `ensure()`: it copies flags into a local variable before mutating it, then writes that mutated copy back to the cell.\n\nThe `ensure()` bug is harmless because `Flags` implements `Copy`, so the mutated copy can be written back safely. The `restore_save` flow is also correct: it reads the current flags, modifies them, and writes them back without race conditions. I am checking whether unused imports will cause build errors under the workspace's lint settings.\n\nWarnings will not block the build unless the workspace explicitly denies them. The native stubs are cfg-gated out for WASM, so dead_code warnings on unused functions are harmless. I will not start another cargo process while the WASM build runs. I will also skip changing the about text now because it is already compiled into the Rust source.\n\nI will run the cargo build wasm directly and inject session.js only after compilation finishes. This avoids modifying the HTML template during the long build and keeps the pack step separate from the compile step.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-68bc5f7f-8547-45a0-9024-6f155d6e7056-116","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs","offset":40,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1609,"output_tokens":1908,"cache_read_input_tokens":200064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3bfe65c1-86e5-473c-89c4-2b95ac2f70a1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-68bc5f7f-8547-45a0-9024-6f155d6e7056-116","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→    }\\n\\n    struct Flags {\\n        ready: bool,\\n        test: bool,\\n        nodraw: bool,\\n        server: bool,\\n        restored: bool,\\n        saved: u32,\\n        pubs: u32,\\n50→    }\\n\\n    thread_local! {\\n        static FLAGS: Cell<Flags> = Cell::new(Flags {\\n            ready: false,\\n            test: false,\\n            nodraw: false,\\n            server: false,\\n            restored: false,\\n            saved: 0,\\n60→            pubs: 0,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    fn flags() -> Flags {\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.get())\\n    }\\n\\n    impl Copy for Flags {}\\n    impl Clone for Flags {\\n70→        fn clone(&self) -> Self {\\n            *self\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ensure() -> Flags {\\n        let mut f = flags();\\n        if f.ready {\\n            return f;\\n        }\\n80→        f.ready = true;\\n        if let Some(win) = web_sys::window() {\\n            if let Ok(search) = win.location().search() {\\n                if let Ok(q) = web_sys::UrlSearchParams::new_with_str(&search) {\\n                    f.test = q.get(\\\"test\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\");\\n                    f.nodraw = q.get(\\\"nodraw\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\") || f.test;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if let Some(doc) = win.document() {\\n                if let Some(root) = doc.document_element() {\",\"content_concise\":\"40→    }\\n\\n    struct Flags {\\n        ready: bool,\\n        test: bool,\\n        nodraw: bool,\\n        server: bool,\\n        restored: bool,\\n        saved: u32,\\n        pubs: u32,\\n50→    }\\n\\n    thread_local! {\\n        static FLAGS: Cell<Flags> = Cell::new(Flags {\\n            ready: false,\\n            test: false,\\n            nodraw: false,\\n            server: false,\\n            restored: false,\\n            saved: 0,\\n60→            pubs: 0,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    fn flags() -> Flags {\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.get())\\n    }\\n\\n    impl Copy for Flags {}\\n    impl Clone for Flags {\\n70→        fn clone(&self) -> Self {\\n            *self\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ensure() -> Flags {\\n        let mut f = flags();\\n        if f.ready {\\n            return f;\\n        }\\n80→        f.ready = true;\\n        if let Some(win) = web_sys::window() {\\n            if let Ok(search) = win.location().search() {\\n                if let Ok(q) = web_sys::UrlSearchParams::new_with_str(&search) {\\n                    f.test = q.get(\\\"test\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\");\\n                    f.nodraw = q.get(\\\"nodraw\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\") || f.test;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if let Some(doc) = win.document() {\\n                if let Some(root) = doc.document_element() {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    }\\n\\n    struct Flags {\\n        ready: bool,\\n        test: bool,\\n        nodraw: bool,\\n        server: bool,\\n        restored: bool,\\n        saved: u32,\\n        pubs: u32,\\n    }\\n\\n    thread_local! {\\n        static FLAGS: Cell<Flags> = Cell::new(Flags {\\n            ready: false,\\n            test: false,\\n            nodraw: false,\\n            server: false,\\n            restored: false,\\n            saved: 0,\\n            pubs: 0,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    fn flags() -> Flags {\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.get())\\n    }\\n\\n    impl Copy for Flags {}\\n    impl Clone for Flags {\\n        fn clone(&self) -> Self {\\n            *self\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ensure() -> Flags {\\n        let mut f = f