{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_265","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The copy implementation looks correct. Starting the WASM build and writing test scripts.\n\nVerified test flags skip drawing correctly. Launch tests draw normally. GPU launch test capped at 120 fps. Now writing tests/run.sh and Python tests in the dev folder.\n\nConfiguring WebGPU flags for SwiftShader and Vulkan. Using Playwright with headless Chromium to capture screenshots. Checking whether the `png` module is available for canvas analysis.\n\nDecided to decode PNG screenshots manually with a minimal zlib-based reader rather than relying on external tools. The test checker will sample pixels and fail if the dominant color exceeds 92% of the image while other colors are rare.\n\nRefined the screenshot checker. It will sample every 8th pixel and fail if any single color exceeds 97% of the image. A realistic dusk scene with ground, sky, and trees should pass.\n\nCanvas size will be verified against the viewport. Two separate browser launches are planned for the two runs. Page errors and console warnings will be filtered, with WebGPU type warnings ignored. The test will wait for the h1 or canvas to appear before pressing keys, using a 120-second timeout for initial load and 180 seconds for software WebGPU first frame. The title text should render even before WASM compilation begins.\n\nThe test sequence is now fully defined. It waits for the h1 and canvas, polls until the screenshot is not uniform, then waits for the __game UI to appear. Key presses are sent only after the simulation is confirmed active, with each key followed by a wait for screen change or two seconds. This prevents early WASM ticks from consuming queued inputs before the before-state screenshot is recorded.\n\nConfirmed that key presses correctly reach the Title screen when the simulation first appears. Headless mode does not require xvfb. A separate fast browser-hooks test will use `?test=1&nodraw=1` on the same HTML file. localStorage may persist across file:// origins in Chromium.\n\nThe save test will clear localStorage first. It queues an action to trigger a save, waits for the jamcry-save key to appear, reloads the page, and verifies the Continue screen loads before pressing Enter.\n\nThe dev-mode test sequence is now fully mapped. It advances from Title through Difficulty, Merc, and Prologue to Playing, then queues act 10 for Pause, three act 4s to reach the Dev mode row, act 1 to open the Dev menu, act 1 to select the Cheats tab, and finally act 1 or 11 to toggle God mode.\n\nThe dev-mode test will use act 11 to toggle God mode and act 12 to increase fire_spread. The Xbox test will queue a keyboard device first, install a stub gamepad via page.evaluate, poll for the Cross glyph, press act 14 to toggle Xbox mode, and verify the A glyph appears.\n\nThe device-switch test must handle the case where the default input is already a gamepad. It will explicitly set keyboard first, then install the stub gamepad and verify the Cross glyph appears. Pointer lock requires the Playing screen with four confirmations, but requesting it from Playwright without a user gesture is not possible.\n\nThe pointer-lock test will click the canvas while the game is playing to trigger `requestPointerLock`, then dispatch a mouse event. The canvas exists even with `nodraw` enabled because graphics initialization runs before the draw loop begins.\n\nBrowser hook tests that require the simulation still need WebGPU flags even with nodraw enabled, because the app checks navigator.gpu and cannot initialize without it. The phone test also needs the sim, so it will use an iPhone viewport with touch input alongside nodraw and test flags for fast post-init frames. The WebKit test is separate and does not wait for a canvas. The About screen test will navigate to the About page.\n\nThe About test will clear localStorage first to ensure a fresh context. It can either navigate down from the Title screen to reach the About row, or simply click the About button directly.\n\nThe About test will read the innerText of the #about element to verify Source, Date, and feedback sections. Music checks will confirm audio connects and status music is 0.10. Glyph and music tests may share one Chromium session to save startup time. The Hub test needs four sequential iframes in a separate browser. The run.sh script will be written with strict bash settings.\n\nThe run.sh script will use a quiet `run_cargo` helper that redirects output to scratch logs. It counts passes and failures, printing only failures and a final summary line. The verification expects stdout to show only the failure count, so the script itself stays silent.\n\nThe run.sh script will suppress Cargo's \"running tests\" banner so stdout contains only the final pass and failure count.\n\nThe run.sh script will accept a SCRATCH directory and write per-mode logs there. It will support subcommands for sim, ui, audio, browser, hub, and all. The full suite runs once under run.sh all, with outputs copied to the named logs afterward.\n\nTo avoid duplicate cargo runs, filtered cargo tests will be executed directly into the named scratch logs first. Browser and hub tests are excluded from run.sh all because they are slow; those will be handled separately.\n\nThe WASM build is still running, so cargo tests cannot start yet. I will write the test scripts now and run them once the build finishes. I am also reconsidering whether run.sh all should generate the scratch logs itself to avoid a second browser pass.\n\nThe run.sh script will accept the scratch directory as a runtime argument. This avoids hardcoding paths and satisfies the requirement that scratch is deleted after use.\n\nThe run.sh script will accept a scratch directory as an optional second argument. Without it, logs will default to a persistent `test-logs` folder inside the dev directory. During verification, the scratch path will be passed explicitly so the named output files land in the correct location.\n\nThe verifier will run `tests/run.sh all` without extra arguments. The script must still exit cleanly and print a final pass-and-fail summary. I will capture the step-specific logs myself using explicit redirects, while `run.sh all` performs the same checks quietly in the background.\n\nTo avoid duplicate browser time, `run.sh all` will be the only browser pass. It must write the screenshot logs directly to the scratch directory when `JAM_SCRATCH` is set, since the verifier separately checks that folder for files like `launch-1.png`.\n\nHardcoding the scratch path inside run.sh would break verification, since the verifier deletes that directory afterward. The PNG screenshots are created during my own verification run, not by run.sh itself. To avoid a second browser pass, run.sh all must both generate those screenshots and produce the final pass-and-fail summary.\n\nThe run.sh script will write all output to a persistent `test-logs/` folder inside the dev directory. After the verification run, I will copy the required files into the scratch directory so the verifier can find them.\n\nThe full run.sh suite should take about eight minutes. I will start the WASM build now with twelve parallel jobs and a custom target directory, then write the test scripts once compilation finishes.\n\nThe WASM build will redirect its output to a scratch log file using a runtime path, so the project does not persist a reference to scratch. I will write the test scripts and wait for compilation to finish before proceeding.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0ac4916-98a8-4fd2-8a0e-b682feafe659-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":265,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0ac4916-98a8-4fd2-8a0e-b682feafe659-118","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine\" && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/target\" cargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app --offline > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/wasm-build.log\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$? >> \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/wasm-build.log\"","description":"Build wasm dist of the game page","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2330,"output_tokens":4537,"cache_read_input_tokens":201600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"86279828-64b0-4899-95d1-dad2a2329dec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a0ac4916-98a8-4fd2-8a0e-b682feafe659-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"265→        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            let input = {\\n                let mut input = input;\\n                crate::merc_web::apply(sim, &mut input);\\n                input\\n            };\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            crate::merc_web::publish(sim);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n290→            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n300→            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n310→                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n320→            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\\n            if sim.rewind_to(t) {\\n                self.rewound = true;\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else if ctl.paused {\\n            if ctl.step_requests > 0 {\\n                sh.control.lock().unwrap().step_requests -= 1;\\n330→                if self.rewound {\\n                    sim.commit_rewind();\\n                    self.rewound = false;\\n                }\\n                tick_once(sim, now);\\n            }\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else {\\n            if self.rewound {\\n                // Acting after a rewind starts a new timeline.\\n340→                sim.commit_rewind();\\n                self.rewound = false;\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n            let cap = crate::merc_web::tick_cap(sim);\\n            let burst = crate::merc_web::burst();\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while (burst || now >= self.next) && n < cap {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n350→                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == cap && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now; // too far behind: drop time instead of spiralling\\n            }\",\"content_concise\":\"265→        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            let input = {\\n                let mut input = input;\\n                crate::merc_web::apply(sim, &mut input);\\n                input\\n            };\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            crate::merc_web::publish(sim);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n290→            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n300→            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n310→                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n320→            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\\n            if sim.rewind_to(t) {\\n                self.rewound = true;\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else if ctl.paused {\\n            if ctl.step_requests > 0 {\\n                sh.control.lock().unwrap().step_requests -= 1;\\n330→                if self.rewound {\\n                    sim.commit_rewind();\\n                    self.rewound = false;\\n                }\\n                tick_once(sim, now);\\n            }\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else {\\n            if self.rewound {\\n                // Acting after a rewind starts a new timeline.\\n340→                sim.commit_rewind();\\n                self.rewound = false;\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n            let cap = crate::merc_web::tick_cap(sim);\\n            let burst = crate::merc_web::burst();\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while (burst || now >= self.next) && n < cap {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n350→                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == cap && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now; // too far behind: drop time instead of spiralling\\n            }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105