{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_270","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"web-sys provides UrlSearchParams, Storage, Window, Document, and Element.\n\nConfirmed that `local_storage` needs the Storage feature, `document_element` needs Document, and `get_attribute` needs Element. The empty `impl Copy for Flags` is valid Rust 2024. `Cell::get` requires `T: Copy`, which `Flags` satisfies.\n\nThe `wasm_bindgen` catch block properly handles missing `gameBridge.pull`. The `js_namespace = gameBridge` attribute correctly resolves to the global `window.gameBridge`.\n\nNo Drop implementation exists, so the Copy trait can be safely derived. I will inspect app.rs for compile errors and review the simhost tick_once changes. I also need to read index.html and build-web.sh to write accurate browser tests and understand the packing steps.\n\nChecking PLAN.md §14.4 and §15 for harness URLs and controls. Verifying whether Device is public. The manual Copy and Clone impls in merc_web.rs are valid Rust 2024, so no immediate fix is needed.\n\n`web_sys::window()` returns `Option<Window>`. `location().search()` returns `Result<String, JsValue>`. `UrlSearchParams::new_with_str` requires the `UrlSearchParams` feature. `q.get(\"test\")` returns `Option<String>` and `is_some_and` is available in Rust 1.98. `local_storage()` returns `Result<Option<Storage>, JsValue>`.\n\n`local_storage()` returns `Result<Option<Storage>, JsValue>`, so the `let Ok(Some(store))` pattern is valid. `get_item` and `set_item` return `Result<Option<String>, JsValue>` and `Result<(), JsValue>`. `Value` implements `Display`, so `game.world.status().to_string()` compiles. The `GameBox` API for `play.get::<Merc>()` and `get_mut` still needs verification. `Device` may be re-exported from `pav_core::games::merc::Device`. `Screen`, `InputFrame`, and `Sim` are correctly imported and used in the wasm module.\n\n`Merc` and the `Game` trait are correctly imported. `use super::*` ensures `Game` is in scope for `play.key()` inside the wasm module. The borrow checker handles `restore_save` safely because it does not hold a reference to `game` after returning. Both `publish` and `apply` exist as native stubs and wasm re-exports, and simhost calls them through `merc_web`.\n\nNative stubs for `apply` and `publish` keep the native `pav_app` tests compiling even if simhost calls them unconditionally. I will read `simhost`'s tick logic and `app.rs` merc sections for compile bugs, plus `index.html` gameTest and keyboard code to write tests. The wasm build is roughly 100 of 218 steps, so I will start writing tests now.\n\nBrowser tests will target the packed HTML, which bundles session.js, game scripts, and WASM. The `?test=1&nodraw=1` hook loads WASM because `AIHub.connect` returns null on file:// URLs. Burst mode sets `burst`, `nodraw`, and a 120-tick cap; the clock loop then ticks up to 120 times per frame as fast as possible, advancing menus quickly.\n\nPublish occurs every 15 ticks, so burst mode triggers 8 publishes per frame. The title screen requires four confirmations, and tick clamps delta time to 0.5 seconds. Attract mode lasts ten seconds of idle time. Because burst can consume many frames in a single frame, the attract screen may start before the test sends input. This timing issue is a problem.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bdd44595-b372-4586-ae04-0b2daa6a4f63-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs","offset":250,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bdd44595-b372-4586-ae04-0b2daa6a4f63-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn overlook|struct FpCam|merc_scene|scene_name == \\\"merc\\\"|skip_draw|mod merc_web","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bdd44595-b372-4586-ae04-0b2daa6a4f63-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gameTest|gameBridge|function pull|startMusic|AIHub|__jamSkipGpu|requestPointerLock|coarse|settings-btn|notice","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7572,"output_tokens":1786,"cache_read_input_tokens":52224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"a383b91c-8b75-4853-a950-06dbe9146d3f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bdd44595-b372-4586-ae04-0b2daa6a4f63-13","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n260→            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            let input = {\\n                let mut input = input;\\n                crate::merc_web::apply(sim, &mut input);\\n                input\\n            };\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            crate::merc_web::publish(sim);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n290→            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n300→            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n310→                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n320→            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\\n            if sim.rewind_to(t) {\\n                self.rewound = true;\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else if ctl.paused {\\n            if ctl.step_requests > 0 {\\n                sh.control.lock().unwrap().step_requests -= 1;\\n330→                if self.rewound {\\n                    sim.commit_rewind();\\n                    self.rewound = false;\\n                }\\n                tick_once(sim, now);\\n            }\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else {\\n            if self.rewound {\\n                // Acting after a rewind starts a new timeline.\\n340→                sim.commit_rewind();\\n                self.rewound = false;\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n            let cap = crate::merc_web::tick_cap(sim);\\n            let burst = crate::merc_web::burst();\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while (burst || now >= self.next) && n < cap {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n350→                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == cap && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now; // too far behind: drop time instead of spiralling\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        let elapsed = self.window_start.elapsed();\\n        if elapsed >= Duration::from_millis(500) {\\n            let mut s = sh.stats.lock().unwrap();\\n360→            s.tps = self.window_ticks as f32 / elapsed.as_secs_f32();\\n            s.tick_ms = if self.window_ticks > 0 { self.busy.as_secs_f32() * 1000.0 / self.window_ticks as f32 } else { 0.0 };\\n            s.tick = sim.state.tick;\\n            s.entities = sim.state.entities.len();\\n            s.oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n            s.newest = sim.history.newest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick).max(sim.state.tick);\\n            s.history_mb = sim.history.approx_bytes() as f32 / 1.0e6;\\n            s.rewound = self.rewound;\\n            self.window_start = Instant::now();\\n            self.window_ticks = 0;\",\"content_concise\":\"250→            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n260→            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n270→                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n280→            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            let input = {\\n                let mut input = input;\\n                crate::merc_web::apply(sim, &mut input);\\n                input\\n            };\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            crate::merc_web::publish(sim);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n290→            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n300→            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n310→                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                    self.rewound = true;\\n                }\\n                let dt = sim.dt();\\n                publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            }\\n        } else if let Some(t) = ctl.scrub {\\n320→            sh.control.lock().unwrap().scrub = None;\\n            if sim.rewind_to(t) {\\n                self.rewound = true;\\n            }\\n            let dt = sim.dt();\\n            publish(sim, sh, dt, now);\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else if ctl.paused {\\n            if ctl.step_requests > 0 {\\n                sh.control.lock().unwrap().step_requests -= 1;\\n330→                if self.rewound {\\n                    sim.commit_rewind();\\n                    self.rewound = false;\\n                }\\n                tick_once(sim, now);\\n            }\\n            self.next = now;\\n        } else {\\n            if self.rewound {\\n                // Acting after a rewind starts a new timeline.\\n340→                sim.commit_rewind();\\n                self.rewound = false;\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n            let cap = crate::merc_web::tick_cap(sim);\\n            let burst = crate::merc_web::burst();\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while (burst || now >= self.next) && n < cap {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n350→                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == cap && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now; // too far behind: drop time instead of spiralling\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        let elapsed = self.window_start.elapsed();\\n        if elapsed >= Duration::from_millis(500) {\\n            let mut s = sh.stats.lock().unwrap();\\n360→            s.tps = self.window_ticks as f32 / elapsed.as_secs_f32();\\n            s.tick_ms = if self.window_ticks > 0 { self.busy.as_secs_f32() * 1000.0 / self.window_ticks as f32 } else { 0.0 };\\n            s.tick = sim.state.tick;\\n            s.entities = sim.state.entities.len();\\n            s.oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n            s.newest = sim.history.newest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick).max(sim.state.tick);\\n            s.history_mb = sim.history.approx_bytes() as f32 / 1.0e6;\\n            s.rewound = self.rewound;\\n            self.window_start = Instant::now();\\n            self.window_ticks = 0;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/simhost.rs\",\"offset\":250,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"            rewound: false,\\n            studio_mode: pav_core::prop_preview::StudioMode::World,\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Runs whatever is due now; returns how long until the next tick.\\n    fn advance(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, sh: &Shared) -> Duration {\\n        let previewing = sim.studio_active();\\n        let mode = sim.studio_mode();\\n        if self.studio_mode != mode {\\n            self.studio_mode = mode;\\n            self.next = Instant::now();\\n        }\\n        let ctl = *sh.control.lock().unwrap();\\n        // The animation stage has its own play, pause and speed controls. The world's time\\n        // controls stay untouched, including a paused or rewound game behind the stage.\\n        let tick_wall = if previewing { sim.dt() } else { sim.dt() / ctl.speed.clamp(0.01, 16.0) };\\n        let (busy, window_ticks) = (&mut self.busy, &mut self.window_ticks);\\n        let mut tick_once = |sim: &mut Sim, at: Instant| {\\n            let input = if previewing {\\n                InputFrame::default()\\n            } else {\\n                let mut i = sh.input.lock().unwrap();\\n                let mut frame = *i;\\n                i.pressed = 0;\\n                frame.cmd = sh.cmds.lock().unwrap().pop_front();\\n                frame\\n            };\\n            let stamp = if previewing { None } else { sh.input_stamp.lock().unwrap().take() };\\n            let t = Instant::now();\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            let input = {\\n                let mut input = input;\\n                crate::merc_web::apply(sim, &mut input);\\n                input\\n            };\\n            sim.step(&input);\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            crate::merc_web::publish(sim);\\n            *busy += t.elapsed();\\n            if let Some(s) = stamp {\\n                *sh.latency_probe.lock().unwrap() = Some((s, Instant::now(), sim.state.tick));\\n            }\\n            *window_ticks += 1;\\n            publish(sim, sh, tick_wall, at);\\n        };\\n\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        if previewing {\\n            let mut n = 0;\\n            while now >= self.next && n < 8 {\\n                self.next += Duration::from_secs_f32(tick_wall);\\n                tick_once(sim, self.next);\\n                n += 1;\\n            }\\n            if n == 8 && now > self.next {\\n                self.next = now;\\n            }\\n        } else if ctl.rewinding {\\n            if now >= self.next {\\n                self.next = now + Duration::from_secs_f32(sim.dt());\\n                let oldest = sim.history.oldest_tick().unwrap_or(sim.state.tick);\\n                let target = sim.state.tick.saturating_sub(ctl.rewind_speed.max(1) as u64).max(oldest);\\n                if target < sim.state.tick && sim.rewind_to(target) {\\n                   