\":[{\"line_number\":435,\"content\":\"    pub fn notice(&self) -> Option<&'static str> {\"},{\"line_number\":436,\"content\":\"        if self.touch_only { Some(\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\") } else { None }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c41fb82c-1d96-4ce9-84a5-07dd923b37fb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_276","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Look action only applies in simulate() during the Playing phase.\n\nThe test needs real pointer lock to verify mousemove yaw changes. I'll try Playwright's pointer lock first. If headless fails, I'll use xvfb with headed Chromium.\n\nThe test will click the canvas to request pointer lock, verify `document.pointerLockElement`, then dispatch a mousemove with movementX and wait for yaw to change.\n\nPlaywright click events are trusted, so headless Chromium should grant pointer lock. Exiting the lock pauses the simulation. Dev mode actions work without entering the pause menu.\n\nThe dev mode test will use act 11 and act 12 directly instead of navigating the pause menu. These actions toggle the god cheat and increment the fire spread slider. The pause screen still shows the Dev mode row.\n\nThe save test will write a save during Playing, reload the page, and verify the Title screen shows Continue. restore_save reads localStorage on first apply and sets has_save before the menu renders. The Continue row appears at focus 0, so act 1 or act 16 resumes to Playing.\n\nThe About screen test will queue a hover and click at coordinates 400, 470 to select the About row and activate it. localStorage needs clearing before the save test because Chromium shares one origin for file:// URLs.\n\nThe About test will use a single command that applies both hover and click in one tick. The verification requires reading the DOM paragraphs on the credits screen rather than just checking the JSON, because ui.about is always present but only visible when the About screen is active.\n\nMusic will be verified by checking that AudioNode.prototype.connect is wrapped and startMusic runs on the first keydown with gain at 0.10.\n\nLaunch tests will run without ?test=1, using two separate browser launches with WebGPU flags enabled. Screenshots will be taken at 1280x720 and 1920x1080 viewport sizes with deviceScaleFactor 1. The canvas bitmap must not be uniform, and Enter/Space input should change the simulation state.\n\nThe engine sets the canvas to window size, so a deviceScaleFactor of 1 means the drawing buffer equals CSS pixels.\n\nThe canvas width should equal the viewport width when devicePixelRatio is 1. WebGPU software rendering can take one to two minutes per launch and may OOM. The harness iframe loads session.js first, which sets AIHub before the game script runs.\n\nWhen the harness is the parent, session.js sets AIHub.active before the game script runs, so __jamSkipGpu is true and the game skips WASM. The host sends fire via a JS interval rather than Rust. In server mode, got.server sets data-jam-server and __jamSkipGpu, removes the local player, and finishes on time-up if isHost. The server itself is not included in the players list.\n\nThe host must not finish on leave. Only time-up triggers a round end. The harness expects a void result with reason host-left.\n\nPresent is seeded from info.players. Leaving removes the entry. When three or more players are present, the last player leaves before time-up and is omitted from standings.\n\nCard Enter calls AIHub.answer('ready') and stops event propagation so it does not also trigger act 1. The harness pokes Enter to activate this.\n\nsession.js must be the first script and byte-identical, since the pack step replaces a marker. build-web.sh always rebuilds Cargo, so after the background compile finishes I can either rerun it or manually run wasm-bindgen and pack. The script does not inject session.js, so that injection must happen before packing and be restored afterward. I will fix the burst spin in simhost now so the in-flight compile picks up the change.\n\nThe in-flight Cargo process has not yet started compiling the pav_app crate, so editing simhost.rs now will apply the burst spin fix. I will also replace the manual Copy implementation with `#[derive(Copy, Clone)]`.\n\nserde_json::Value::to_string produces valid JSON. Look input reaches world.tick through Merc::pre during the Playing screen, so mouse look works without shell execution. Both window.__game.status and window.__game.ui are stored as raw JSON strings; tests must parse them with JSON.parse.\n\nThe burst function will no longer be called during spinning to fix the spin bug, though it remains public for tests. Test mode always uses a tick cap of 120, including the Playing phase, so late frames may jump ahead by two seconds.\n\nThe phone attract sequence lasts ten real seconds. With nodraw enabled, requestAnimationFrame runs at 60Hz and the simulation advances one tick per frame. Ten seconds of wall-clock time equals six hundred ticks, which is exactly ten simulated seconds. Playwright headless pages are foregrounded, so background tab throttling should not affect the animation loop. The 120-tick cap catches up if frames run slower than expected, and the attract sequence tracks wall-clock simulation time.\n\nThe 120-tick cap only applies when the screen is not Playing. A long frame during launch therefore adds up to two seconds of idle time before the simulation snaps forward, preventing the attract sequence from starting until keys are pressed.\n\nI will edit the code now and write tests while waiting for the build. I also need to create notes/feedback.md. The run.sh script belongs in the dev subfolder next to the engine and hub, not inside the engine itself. The verifier expects to run `tests/run.sh all` from that dev folder.\n\nThe `all` command runs sim, ui, audio, browser, and hub tests. The harness must filter cargo output to print only failures and a final one-line summary such as `PASS n FAIL 0`.\n\nCargo output will be filtered to print only lines containing FAILED or error, plus the final summary line. The script writes logs to a dev-relative test-logs/ directory instead of hardcoding a scratch path.\n\nThe script will not reference scratch directly. It will support subset commands such as `tests/run.sh sim` and `all`. Native tests require cargo, which conflicts with the wasm build, so the script can be written now and executed after the wasm build completes. Browser tests need the packed HTML at the work root, so the script will check for it there. The script will use a bash header with strict error handling and derive the work root from its own directory.\n\nThe script derives the dev folder and engine path from its own location. Sim tests will run with 12 build jobs and a custom target directory, filtering merc test names with cargo's substring filter.\n\nCargo test passes multiple arguments after the double dash to the test binary as OR filters. The libtest harness runs any test whose name contains at least one of the specified substrings.\n\nThe ui-audio test command will run `music_bus_tracks_the_gain`, `gun_families_voices_and_crackle_differ`, and `explosion_is_loud_then_silent` from the `pav_audio` package, plus the `first_person` test from `pav_view`. The exact name of the first-person test still needs to be confirmed. The playthrough test is fast; a prior run of all sixteen tests took only 0.97 seconds after compilation.\n\nThe native and wasm builds share the same Cargo target directory. Cargo locks that directory, so the two builds cannot run concurrently.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5eb8c859-e2cc-4382-897f-2eee70e070a8-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"URLSearchParams|players|scenario|auto|game=|__hubCheck|playMs","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/harness.html","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5eb8c859-e2cc-4382-897f-2eee70e070a8-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn first_person|fn music_bus|fn gun_families|fn explosion_is","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5eb8c859-e2cc-4382-897f-2eee70e070a8-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","offset":30,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2547,"output_tokens":4109,"cache_read_input_tokens":87296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"74c773e8-3e1f-467e-be81-65aa581c2d4a"}
