,115,44,32,116,104,101,32,114,101,113,117,105,114,101,100,32,109,101,115,115,97,103,101,44,32,97,32,83,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,32,98,117,116,116,111,110,44,32,97,116,116,114,97,99,116,32,114,117,110,110,105,110,103,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":10,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":110,\"content\":\"| Pavilion overlays appear on hook games: controls card, FPS box, footer, HUD box | Seen in my screenshot of the starter | Turn all of them off for this scene |\"},{\"line_number\":355,\"content\":\"- Add vehicle-relative controls (throttle, brake, steer axes).\"},{\"line_number\":506,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · L2/RMB aim · Square/R reload or clear jam\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":524,\"content\":\"- **Own card** (`card:true`): a live scene of the truck at dusk with the title, the players in their seat colours and ready state, how to win, this player's controls and the time left from the `card` event. Enter, ✕ or tap → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △, a named key or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Handle Enter in the JS shim (§2.3). No menus or choices, and nothing done on the card changes the round. Play begins only at `start`.\"},{\"line_number\":532,\"content\":\"- **Rules:** network only through the hub. No WebRTC, sockets or `fetch` to anything else in a session. No chat, emotes or custom names. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`. No quit or restart. No dev mode. Pause opens only a sound and controls overlay, and the world keeps running. Ignore Options while Create is held (the hub's chord).\"},{\"line_number\":604,\"content\":\"Touch-only means `(any-pointer: fine)` false, `(pointer: coarse)` true and no controller connected. No touch controls at all (never show the engine's touch UI in this scene). Show **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a **Settings** button (tappable) over the running attract mode. Plugging in a controller or pressing a key brings the normal title.\"},{\"line_number\":799,\"content\":\"| **M5** | Vehicles on slopes, relative controls, boat, seats, mounted gun, damage and repair, AI pursuit | Bot drives the road end to end. Boat and repair tests pass |\"},{\"line_number\":837,\"content\":\"- **Touch-only:** Chromium with a phone profile (`has_touch`, `is_mobile`) shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a tappable Settings. No touch controls appear. Attract runs. Also check that WebKit (which has no WebGPU here) shows the page's clear message rather than a blank page.\"},{\"line_number\":866,\"content\":\"**Exit interview:** write it exactly as TASK.md's shape, beside the final HTML, and check it parses. Suggested `aiHub` values: `type` Game, `genre` Shooter, `source` Far Cry 2, `series` Far Cry, `players` 1–4, `controls` \\\"Stick or WASD move · R2 or left mouse fire · L2 or right mouse aim · Square or R reload and clear jams · D-pad or M for the map\\\", `tags` `[\\\"3d\\\",\\\"first-person\\\",\\\"co-op\\\",\\\"story\\\",\\\"vehicles\\\",\\\"exploration\\\"]`. Fill `name`, `tagline`, `description` in the game's voice.\"},{\"line_number\":883,\"content\":\"- [ ] Touch-only: no touch controls, the required message, a Settings button, attract running.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"26630e85-7709-4f96-8205-0ba1d19a62b1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_284","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Plan §14.4 requires a script to copy the final page beside hub/*.\n\nServing the work root directly is cleaner than copying the HTML beside hub. The harness game URL resolves to the same origin via a relative path from hub/.\n\nThe harness URL will use `../../Jam Cry-....html` with `players=2&auto=1`. Solo file:// loads keep the original `Math.random` because `AIHub.active` is false without `aihub=`. A test script will verify this.\n\nThe init script will save the original `Math.random` to `window.__random` before page scripts run. After loading, the harness can confirm the function is unchanged and `AIHub.active` is false. A call-count wrapper will verify no random calls occur during solo boot. WebRTC two-page testing will use a single browser context with BroadcastChannel.\n\nBoth pages must call `startBroadcast` for the BroadcastChannel handshake to complete. Page A sends a hello message, page B replies with an ack, and page A then posts done. Both pages receive these messages and display the \"BroadcastChannel\" results text.\n\nWebRTC solo testing will use a manual offer-and-answer handshake. Page A calls `offerCode()` to generate a code, page B calls `takeOffer(code)` to reply with an answer, and page A calls `takeAnswer(answer)`. The data channel opens and displays the WebRTC results text. Chromium supports RTCPeerConnection on file:// without ICE servers, so a brief delay should suffice.\n\nThe harness will not call `offerCode()`, keeping the solo test free of hub interference. The game script also skips this logic when `AIHub.active` is true. Now writing the test scripts.\n\nThe publish JSON will contain `status` and `ui` as strings. A Python helper named `push` is being drafted to queue a command and wait for a change in the published state or the screen. Because the status field does not include a tick counter, polling for a change in `ui.focus` or the screen will serve as the tick signal. For example, pressing up while on the Title screen updates focus without changing the screen itself, so the test will poll for that focus change until it appears.\n\nThe `push` helper queues a command via `page.evaluate` and waits for a predicate to pass. Glyph changes will be detected by parsing the `ui` field. Commands are safe from race conditions because the queue holds them until the WASM side pulls. The test script will wait for `window.__game.ui` to exist, with a 90-second timeout to cover WASM compilation.\n\nThe `?nodraw=1` flag only skips drawing, not GPU initialization. The WebGPU device is still created at startup, so hook tests that need the simulation will face a 20–40 second software WebGPU initialization and heavy memory use.\n\nSkipping GPU initialization entirely would require a larger refactor, so hook tests will keep the existing WebGPU flags. The first startup remains expensive, but per-frame rendering is avoided. iPhone emulation in Chromium also supports WebGPU when flags are enabled.\n\nWebKit lacks WebGPU support, so the notice and attract tests will skip WASM loading and run quickly without flags. The launch test will use full rendering with WebGPU flags and two viewports in sequence. Viewport sizes are chosen to balance memory use: 1280×720 and 800×600 for lighter runs, or 1920×1080 if needed.\n\nViewport sizes are finalized at 1280×720 and 1024×768 to reduce GPU memory pressure. Playwright screenshots will be analyzed with PIL in Python to detect blank canvas frames.\n\nCanvas screenshots will be captured via Playwright locators, and full page screenshots will be used for the title panel. A uniformity check will sample pixels from the PNG; if over 98% are the same color, the test fails. The title text will be verified through the DOM h1 element rather than OCR, alongside a check that the published status.title equals \"Jam Cry\". Keyboard input changes state. Console errors and page errors will be monitored to ensure zero failures.\n\nThe Enter-Space-Enter-Space test will record the screen state before pressing the keys and assert that it differs afterward. Playwright uses 'Space' for the spacebar. The title h1 is present in the HTML before WASM loads, so the harness can verify it immediately after page load.\n\nThe music test will intercept `AudioNode.prototype.connect` to record `GainNode` gain values, then verify that pressing a key produces a gain of 0.10. The About screen must contain the date and time, the Far Cry 2 source credit, and PLAN.md.\n\nThe About screen must also contain Shooter, first person, shardfall or Rust, sun-bleached, simulation-driven or Animation, 0.10, BroadcastChannel or AI Hub, Playwright or cargo, START_HERE or Research, Grok CLI, grok-4.7, added on import, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback.\n\nThe save test will clear localStorage before navigation, reach the Playing screen, queue an act command to trigger a save, wait for status.saves to increase, verify the jamcry-save key exists in localStorage, reload the page, and resume from the Continue option.\n\nThe dev test queues act 11 to enable god mode, then act 12 to raise fire_spread from 0.9 to 0.95.\n\nFor pointer lock, the test reaches the Playing screen, clicks the canvas, and verifies pointer lock is active on that element; if not, it retries the click. It then captures the initial yaw value into window.__yaw0.\n\nThe pointer-lock test will dispatch a synthetic mousemove event to rotate yaw, then wait for the value to change. It will exit pointer lock and verify the Pause screen appears. If pointer lock fails, the harness will fall back to a headed xvfb browser and fail with a clear message. Chromium launch arguments are set to enable unsafe WebGPU, Vulkan, and SwiftShader backends.\n\nThe SwiftShader WebGPU adapter flag is dropped; only Vulkan and SwiftShader backends will be used. Headless mode is kept, but `--disable-gpu` is avoided to preserve WebGPU support. Only one browser context will run at a time to limit memory use.\n\nA single `browser_test.py` script will accept a mode argument for launch1, launch2, hooks, webkit, phone, and net. A separate `hub_test.py`, a `run.sh` launcher, and a `notes/feedback.md` will also be created. A pack script will inject `session.js` into the HTML. The existing `pack_single_html.py` must be checked for correct output paths and title replacement before invoking it.\n\nThe run.sh launcher will filter cargo output to surface only test failures, errors, panics, and assertions. The pav_app build log will be checked to confirm the latest edits are being compiled.\n\nThe run.sh launcher will parse Cargo's test summary lines to extract the total number of tests passed and failed across all groups. It will report a single line in the format `PASS n FAIL 0` as required by the plan. The script will expose subcommands for sim, ui, audio, browser, hub, and all. Browser and hub tests require the HTML to be packed first, so run.sh will handle that step before invoking them. Sim tests compile slowly on the first run, but the native merc tests were already compiled.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30c7db1a-21cd-40b1-b23b-528fde3529de-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs","offset":40,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30c7db1a-21cd-40b1-b23b-528fde3529de-57","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md","offset":843,"limit":8}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30c7db1a-21cd-40b1-b23b-528fde3529de-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Compiling pav_app|error\\[|EXIT:|Finished","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/wasm-build.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1610,"output_tokens":3345,"cache_read_input_tokens":111616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3a41a074-6cef-4879-87f2-d2faf241f105"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30c7db1a-21cd-40b1-b23b-528fde3529de-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→    }\\n\\n    #[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\n    struct Flags {\\n        ready: bool,\\n        test: bool,\\n        nodraw: bool,\\n        server: bool,\\n        restored: bool,\\n        saved: u32,\\n50→        pubs: u32,\\n    }\\n\\n    thread_local! {\\n        static FLAGS: Cell<Flags> = Cell::new(Flags {\\n            ready: false,\\n            test: false,\\n            nodraw: false,\\n            server: false,\\n            restored: false,\\n60→            saved: 0,\\n            pubs: 0,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    fn flags() -> Flags {\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.get())\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ensure() -> Flags {\\n70→        let mut f = flags();\\n        if f.ready {\\n            return f;\\n        }\\n        f.ready = true;\\n        if let Some(win) = web_sys::window() {\\n            if let Ok(search) = win.location().search() {\\n                if let Ok(q) = web_sys::UrlSearchParams::new_with_str(&search) {\\n                    f.test = q.get(\\\"test\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\");\\n                    f.nodraw = q.get(\\\"nodraw\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\") || f.test;\",\"content_concise\":\"40→    }\\n\\n    #[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\n    struct Flags {\\n        ready: bool,\\n        test: bool,\\n        nodraw: bool,\\n        server: bool,\\n        restored: bool,\\n        saved: u32,\\n50→        pubs: u32,\\n    }\\n\\n    thread_local! {\\n        static FLAGS: Cell<Flags> = Cell::new(Flags {\\n            ready: false,\\n            test: false,\\n            nodraw: false,\\n            server: false,\\n            restored: false,\\n60→            saved: 0,\\n            pubs: 0,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    fn flags() -> Flags {\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.get())\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ensure() -> Flags {\\n70→        let mut f = flags();\\n        if f.ready {\\n            return f;\\n        }\\n        f.ready = true;\\n        if let Some(win) = web_sys::window() {\\n            if let Ok(search) = win.location().search() {\\n                if let Ok(q) = web_sys::UrlSearchParams::new_with_str(&search) {\\n                    f.test = q.get(\\\"test\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\");\\n                    f.nodraw = q.get(\\\"nodraw\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\") || f.test;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    }\\n\\n    #[derive(Clone, Copy)]\\n    struct Flags {\\n        ready: bool,\\n        test: bool,\\n        nodraw: bool,\\n        server: bool,\\n        restored: bool,\\n        saved: u32,\\n        pubs: u32,\\n    }\\n\\n    thread_local! {\\n        static FLAGS: Cell<Flags> = Cell::new(Flags {\\n            ready: false,\\n            test: false,\\n            nodraw: false,\\n            server: false,\\n            restored: false,\\n            saved: 0,\\n            pubs: 0,\\n        });\\n    }\\n\\n    fn flags() -> Flags {\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.get())\\n    }\\n\\n    fn ensure() -> Flags {\\n        let mut f = flags();\\n        if f.ready {\\n            return f;\\n        }\\n        f.ready = true;\\n        if let Some(win) = web_sys::window() {\\n            if let Ok(search) = win.location().search() {\\n                if let Ok(q) = web_sys::UrlSearchParams::new_with_str(&search) {\\n                    f.test = q.get(\\\"test\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\");\\n                    f.nodraw = q.get(\\\"nodraw\\\").is_some_and(|v| v == \\\"1\\\") || f.test;\\n\",\"total_lines\":234}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30c7db1a-21cd-40b1-b23b-528fde3529de-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"843→### 14.4 Hub\\nA script copies the final page beside `hub/*`, serves with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, parses the port the OS picked, **fetches the page and confirms its `<title>` is yours before trusting a result**, runs the cases below, and stops only the PID it started (never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k` or whatever holds a port). Other agents share this machine's ports and processes. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` for each, with the game opened as `harness.html?game=<page>&…`:\\n- `players=2&auto=1`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\\n\\n850→Also: two pages (or contexts) play the standalone round over `BroadcastChannel` and over a copy-pasted WebRTC code through to the results. Then the on-its-own check: client inactive, `Math.random` untouched.\",\"content_concise\":\"843→### 14.4 Hub\\nA script copies the final page beside `hub/*`, serves with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, parses the port the OS picked, **fetches the page and confirms its `<title>` is yours before trusting a result**, runs the cases below, and stops only the PID it started (never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k` or whatever holds a port). Other agents share this machine's ports and processes. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` for each, with the game opened as `harness.html?game=<page>&…`:\\n- `players=2&auto=1`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\\n\\n850→Also: two pages (or contexts) play the standalone round over `BroadcastChannel` and over a copy-pasted WebRTC code through to the results. Then the on-its-own check: client inactive, `Math.random` untouched.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":843,\"limit\":8,\"raw_output\":\"### 14.4 Hub\\nA script copies the final page beside `hub/*`, serves with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, parses the port the OS picked, **fetches the page and confirms its `<title>` is yours before trusting a result**, runs the cases below, and stops only the PID it started (never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k` or whatever holds a port). Other agents share this machine's ports and processes. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` for each, with the game opened as `harness.html?game=<page>&…`:\\n- `players=2&auto=1`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\\n- `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`\\n- `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\\n\\nAlso: two pages (or contexts) play the standalone round over `BroadcastChannel` and over a copy-pasted WebRTC code through to the results. Then the on-its-own check: client inactive, `Math.random` untouched.\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30c7db1a-21cd-40b1-b23b-528fde3529de-58","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,116,109,112,47,103,114,111,107,45,103,111,97,108,45,56,50,49,53,100,97,54,102,100,55,54,49,47,105,109,112,108,101