{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_288","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The parent module has an unused `use pav_core::games::Game` import. The wasm module already imports it with `use super::*`.\n\nThe compiler flags the parent import as unused despite the child module using it via `use super::*`. This is unexpected because the child should consume names from the parent namespace.\n\nThe Game trait is unnecessary because key() and get() are inherent methods on GameBox. The unused import will be removed from both the wasm and native merc_web modules.\n\nThe unused import will be removed and the wasm rebuild started. Test scripts will be written in parallel. The remaining scene_name references were checked and only one needed fixing. The workspace lints are being reviewed for dead_code on burst().\n\n`burst()` will remain public. Unused public functions in binary crates trigger dead_code warnings. The project may not deny these warnings.\n\nThe build only emitted a warning and did not fail. The unused `burst()` functions will remain as-is; the dead_code warning is acceptable.\n\nThe unused Game import will be removed from the parent module. The wasm child already imports it via `use super::*`, but key() and get() are inherent methods on GameBox, so the trait is unnecessary.\n\nNext files to write:\n- tests/run.sh\n- tests/browser.py\n- tests/hub.py\n- notes/feedback.md\n\nThe pack_single_html arguments and index.html script marker will also be checked.\n\nA `tests/pack.sh` script will automate the pack workflow: inject session, run wasm-bindgen, pack HTML, then restore the template. The pack step will wait for a successful wasm build first.\n\nThe background build will use 12 jobs and a dedicated target directory.\n\nThere is also a question about whether the `Game` trait must remain in scope for `play.get::<Merc>()`, since the method has a `G: Game` bound.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcc97260-8c83-403e-81ff-5ba8357e25a9-64","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs","old_string":"use pav_core::games::Game;\nuse pav_core::games::merc::{Merc, Screen};","new_string":"use pav_core::games::merc::{Merc, Screen};"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcc97260-8c83-403e-81ff-5ba8357e25a9-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":639,"output_tokens":1446,"cache_read_input_tokens":119424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2333fffa-78e6-4b5e-ac09-17fd11cdc38b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bcc97260-8c83-403e-81ff-5ba8357e25a9-64","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"use pav_core::games::Game;\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::{Merc, Screen};\",\"new_string\":\"use pav_core::games::merc::{Merc, Screen};\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/merc_web.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"use pav_core::games::Game;\\nuse pav_core::games::merc::{Merc, Screen};\",\"old_line\":3,\"new_string\":\"use pav_core::games::merc::{Merc, Screen};\",\"new_line\":3,\"context_before\":\"//! Browser bridge for Jam Cry. The page owns menus, look, and the hub. The sim stays authoritative.\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"use pav_core::{InputFrame, Sim};\\n\\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bcc97260-8c83-403e-81ff-5ba8357e25a9-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Packs the browser build into one self-contained HTML page: no other files, no network loads.\\n\\nusage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\\n           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\\n\\nBINDGEN_DIR is wasm-bindgen's output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm); scripts/build-web.sh\\n--single-file makes it and runs this. The page is web/index.html with the options written into\\nits <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\\n10→given), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\\nloader that sets window.loadGame (index.html's script calls it when set) and the JS glue as an\\ninline module script. The loader shows a progress line, bakes in --scene (used when the address\\nnames no room or scene) and unpacks with the browser's DecompressionStream. No blob: or data:\\nURLs are needed. Out: target/web/<title>.html.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport base64\\nimport gzip\\nimport html\\n20→import json\\nimport pathlib\\nimport re\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\\nPAGE = ROOT / \\\"web\\\" / \\\"index.html\\\"\\n\\n# Runs while the page parses, before index.html's module script.\\nLOADER = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n30→(() => {\\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\\n  // The start scene baked in at build time, unless the address names a room or a scene.\\n  const scene = __SCENE__, query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\n  if (scene && !query.get('room') && !query.get('scene')) {\\n    query.set('scene', scene);\\n    try { history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + query + location.hash); }\\n    catch (error) { console.warn('Could not put the start scene in the address:', error); }\\n  }\\n  const line = document.createElement('div');\\n40→  line.style.cssText = 'font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.7; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums';\\n  msg.style.flexDirection = 'column';\\n  msg.style.gap = '8px';\\n  msg.replaceChildren(`Loading ${document.title}…`, line);\\n  const paint = () => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 20));\\n  // The JS glue is the module script at the end of the page: it hands over its init function.\\n  const glue = new Promise((resolve) => { window.gameGlue = resolve; });\\n  window.loadGame = async () => {\\n    line.textContent = 'Unpacking…';\\n    await paint();\\n50→    // The gzipped wasm's base64 block leaves the page once read, to free its text.\\n    const block = document.getElementById('game-wasm'), size = +block.dataset.size, text = block.textContent;\\n    block.remove();\\n    let packed;\\n    if (Uint8Array.fromBase64) packed = Uint8Array.fromBase64(text);\\n    else {\\n      const bin = atob(text);\\n      packed = new Uint8Array(bin.length);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) packed[i] = bin.charCodeAt(i);\\n    }\\n60→    const wasm = new Uint8Array(size);\\n    const reader = new Blob([packed]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip')).getReader();\\n    let n = 0;\\n    for (let r = await reader.read(); !r.done; r = await reader.read()) {\\n      wasm.set(r.value, n);\\n      n += r.value.length;\\n      line.textContent = `Unpacking ${Math.floor((100 * n) / size)}%`;\\n    }\\n    if (n !== size) throw new Error(`the packed game is damaged (${n} of ${size} bytes)`);\\n    line.textContent = 'Starting…';\\n70→    await paint();\\n    const init = await glue;\\n    await init({ module_or_path: wasm });\\n  };\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef fail(text):\\n    sys.exit(f\\\"pack_single_html: {text}\\\")\\n80→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Packs the browser build into one self-contained HTML page: no other files, no network loads.\\n\\nusage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\\n           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\\n\\nBINDGEN_DIR is wasm-bindgen's output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm); scripts/build-web.sh\\n--single-file makes it and runs this. The page is web/index.html with the options written into\\nits <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\\n10→given), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\\nloader that sets window.loadGame (index.html's script calls it when set) and the JS glue as an\\ninline module script. The loader shows a progress line, bakes in --scene (used when the address\\nnames no room or scene) and unpacks with the browser's DecompressionStream. No blob: or data:\\nURLs are needed. Out: target/web/<title>.html.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport base64\\nimport gzip\\nimport html\\n20→import json\\nimport pathlib\\nimport re\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\\nPAGE = ROOT / \\\"web\\\" / \\\"index.html\\\"\\n\\n# Runs while the page parses, before index.html's module script.\\nLOADER = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n30→(() => {\\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\\n  // The start scene baked in at build time, unless the address names a room or a scene.\\n  const scene = __SCENE__, query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\n  if (scene && !query.get('room') && !query.get('scene')) {\\n    query.set('scene', scene);\\n    try { history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + query + location.hash); }\\n    catch (error) { console.warn('Could not put the start scene in the address:', error); }\\n  }\\n  const line = document.createElement('div');\\n40→  line.style.cssText = 'font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.7; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums';\\n  msg.style.flexDirection = 'column';\\n  msg.style.gap = '8px';\\n  msg.replaceChildren(`Loading ${document.title}…`, line);\\n  const paint = () => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 20));\\n  // The JS glue is the module script at the end of the page: it hands over its init function.\\n  const glue = new Promise((resolve) => { window.gameGlue = resolve; });\\n  window.loadGame = async () => {\\n    line.textContent = 'Unpacking…';\\n    await paint();\\n50→    // The gzipped wasm's base64 block leaves the page once read, to free its text.\\n    const block = document.getElementById('game-wasm'), size = +block.dataset.size, text = block.textContent;\\n    block.remove();\\n    let packed;\\n    if (Uint8Array.fromBase64) packed = Uint8Array.fromBase64(text);\\n    else {\\n      const bin = atob(text);\\n      packed = new Uint8Array(bin.length);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) packed[i] = bin.charCodeAt(i);\\n    }\\n60→    const wasm = new Uint8Array(size);\\n    const reader = new Blob([packed]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip')).getReader();\\n    let n = 0;\\n    for (let r = await reader.read(); !r.done; r = await reader.read()) {\\n      wasm.set(r.value, n);\\n      n += r.value.length;\\n      line.textContent = `Unpacking ${Math.floor((100 * n) / size)}%`;\\n    }\\n    if (n !== size) throw new Error(`the packed game is damaged (${n} of ${size} bytes)`);\\n    line.textContent = 'Starting…';\\n70→    await paint();\\n    const init = await glue;\\n    await init({ module_or_path: wasm });\\n  };\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef fail(text):\\n    sys.exit(f\\\"pack_single_html: {text}\\\")\\n80→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Packs the browser build into one self-contained HTML page: no other files, no network loads.\\n\\nusage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\\n           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\\n\\nBINDGEN_DIR is wasm-bindgen's output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm); scripts/build-web.sh\\n--single-file makes it and runs this. The page is web/index.html with the options written into\\nits <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\\ngiven), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\\nloader that sets window.loadGame (index.html's script calls it when set) and the JS glue as an\\ninline module script. The loader shows a progress line, bakes in --scene (used when the address\\nnames no room or scene) and unpacks with the browser's DecompressionStream. No blob: or data:\\nURLs are needed. Out: target/web/<title>.html.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport base64\\nimport gzip\\nimport html\\nimport json\\nimport pathlib\\nimport re\\nimport sys\\n\\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\\nPAGE = ROOT / \\\"web\\\" / \\\"index.html\\\"\\n\\n# Runs while the page parses, before index.html's module script.\\nLOADER = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n(() => {\\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\\n  // The start scene baked in at build time, unless the address names a room or a scene.\\n  const scene = __SCENE__, query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\n  if (scene && !query.get('room') && !query.get('scene')) {\\n    query.set('scene', scene);\\n    try { history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + query + location.hash); }\\n    catch (error) { console.warn('Could not put the start scene in the address:', error); }\\n  }\\n  const line = document.createElement('div');\\n  line.style.cssText = 'font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.7; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums';\\n  msg.style.flexDirection = 'column';\\n  msg.style.gap = '8px';\\n  msg.replaceChildren(`Loading ${document.title}…`, line);\\n  const paint = () => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 20));\\n  // The JS glue is the module script at the end of the page: it hands over its init function.\\n  const glue = new Promise((resolve) => { window.gameGlue = resolve; });\\n  window.loadGame = async () => {\\n    line.textContent = 'Unpacking…';\\n    await paint();\\n    // The gzipped wasm's base64 block leaves the page once read, to free its text.\\n    const block = document.getElementById('game-wasm'), size = +block.dataset.size, text = block.textContent;\\n    block.remove();\\n    let packed;\\n    if (Uint8Array.fromBase64) packed = Uint8Array.fromBase64(text);\\n    else {\\n      const bin = atob(text);\\n      packed = new Uint8Array(bin.length);\\n      for (let i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) packed[i] = bin.charCodeAt(i);\\n    }\\n    const wasm = new Uint8Array(size);\\n    const reader = new Blob([packed]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip')).getReader();\\n    let n = 0;\\n    for (let r = await reader.read(); !r.done; r = await reader.read()) {\\n      wasm.set(r.value, n);\\n      n += r.value.length;\\n      line.textContent = `Unpacking ${Math.floor((100 * n) / size)}%`;\\n    }\\n    if (n !== size) throw new Error(`the packed game is damaged (${n} of ${size} bytes)`);\\n    line.textContent = 'Starting…';\\n    await paint();\\n    const init = await glue;\\n    await init({ module_or_path: wasm });\\n  };\\n})();\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef fail(text):\\n    sys.exit(f\\\"pack_single_html: {text}\\\")\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":150}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"3f5fa46b-7504-4a05-86b8-e1167da0f3f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_289","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The loader uses history.replaceState to append query parameters.\n\nThe loader only sets scene when the query lacks it, so existing test parameters remain intact. file:// URLs may throw replaceState, but the error is caught and logged as a warning. The loader script is injected before </body>, which places it after the module script in the HTML.\n\nThe classic loader script executes during HTML parsing before deferred module scripts run. window.loadGame is therefore available when the game module calls it. Session.js runs first and initializes AIHub before the game script loads.\n\nThe loader always runs even when the GPU is skipped, because it is injected before the closing body tag. It then tries to replace children on the message element, which may fail if that element was already removed.\n\nThe classic game script does not remove the message element, so it still exists when the loader runs. The module script removes it later only after setting __jamSkipGpu, and it never calls loadGame in that case. The loader therefore sets up the progress UI safely without starting the WASM module.\n\nThe loader safely sets the message element style because it still exists when the script runs. On WebKit without GPU support, the module replaces the loader's \"Loading\" text with a needs-WebGPU notice and never calls loadGame. The final message is correct. On file:// launch, the loader appends the scene parameter, the module loads WASM via loadGame, WebGPU initializes, and the canvas appears.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-32e1d112-5dd0-4eef-adf6-9fada55c3975-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html","limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-32e1d112-5dd0-4eef-adf6-9fada55c3975-67","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"def replace_one|manifest|script","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2638,"output_tokens":944,"cache_read_input_tokens":119936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"31f2bde3-1648-4e2a-856b-2ecd6df78473"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-32e1d112-5dd0-4eef-adf6-9fada55c3975-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\n/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\">\\n<title>Jam Cry</title>\\n10→<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#2a2420\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"10\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Burn the depot, take the ledger, get out together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · L2/RMB aim · Square/R reload or clear jam\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n20→<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\\\" content=\\\"black-translucent\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\" href=\\\"manifest.webmanifest\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\">\\n<style>\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #2a2420; overscroll-behavior: none;\\n    touch-action: none; user-select: none; -webkit-user-select: none; }\\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\\n    outline: none; touch-action: none; }\\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n30→    font: 22px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #f0d8b0; text-align: center; padding: 24px; z-index: 5;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\n/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\">\\n<title>Jam Cry</title>\\n10→<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#2a2420\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"10\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Burn the depot, take the ledger, get out together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · L2/RMB aim · Square/R reload or clear jam\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n20→<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\\\" content=\\\"yes\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\\\" content=\\\"black-translucent\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"manifest\\\" href=\\\"manifest.webmanifest\\\">\\n<link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\">\\n<style>\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #2a2420; overscroll-behavior: none;\\n    touch-action: none; user-select: none; -webkit-user-select: none; }\\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\\n    outline: none; touch-action: none; }\\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\\n30→    font: 22px system-ui, sans