{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_296","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that f.test remains valid after moving f into FLAGS, since Flags is a copy.\n\nConfirmed the WASM build output path is `target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm`. Starting the background build and writing the test files.\n\nPlanning browser.py with synchronous Playwright. It will collect all failures in one log and exit with code 1. Smaller viewports are chosen to avoid OOM. The script will use the iPhone 13 device preset if available, otherwise manual options.\n\nPlaywright screenshot composites the page, so canvas pixels should appear if the compositor renders them. A blank readback is a known failure to fix, so actual painting must occur. The overlook scene uses non-uniform colors and trees, making it a good test target.\n\nThe canvas screenshot captures only the 3D bitmap, excluding the HTML shell overlay. A full page screenshot includes the title. The skip_draw flag is correctly disabled without nodraw.\n\nWriting the test files into the dev tests directory. Also creating pack.sh.\n\nThe run.sh `all` target will skip rebuilding WASM and assume HTML artifacts already exist. If they are missing, it fails immediately.\n\nNative tests must wait for the WASM build to finish first. After that, pack.sh can run in parallel with native tests because pack uses wasm-bindgen directly and does not need cargo's target directory lock.\n\nPlanning the hub harness test. The game URL will use `urllib.parse.quote` for the filename, and the relative path from `hub/harness.html` will be `../../{filename}`. The script will fetch the title before loading the harness and verify it shows \"Jam Cry\" rather than the raw filename.\n\nPack.sh will verify that session.js is the first script in the packed HTML and that the template marker remains intact. It will also check for exactly one title tag, the theme-color meta tag, and a single output file.\n\nWorking out the exact byte-level comparison for pack.sh. The script tag contains `/*__SESSION_JS__*/` with newlines around it, so the check must strip whitespace to match the injected JavaScript.\n\nThe template script tag will be collapsed to a single line containing only `/*__SESSION_JS__*/`. This ensures the injected JavaScript body is byte-identical to the session.js file, eliminating any whitespace mismatch in pack.sh.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8563e530-82ca-4056-b85c-8610861134b9-80","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html","old_string":"<script>\n/*__SESSION_JS__*/\n</script>","new_string":"<script>/*__SESSION_JS__*/</script>"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8563e530-82ca-4056-b85c-8610861134b9-81","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine\" && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/target\" cargo build --locked --profile dist --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p pav_app --offline > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/wasm-build2.log\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$? >> \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/wasm-build2.log\"","description":"Rebuild wasm pav_app after compile fix","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":634,"output_tokens":2052,"cache_read_input_tokens":139392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c