).unwrap_or_default())\\n}\\n\\nimpl Settings {\\n    /// In the browser: defaults, plus `?room=NAME&seed=N` from the page address.\",\"new_line\":60,\"context_before\":\"#[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\nconst HEADER: &str = \\\"# Shardfall startup settings. Delete this file to restore defaults.\\\\n# backend = \\\\\\\"vulkan\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"dx12\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\";\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"    #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n    pub fn load(_args: &[String]) -> (Self, String) {\\n        let mut s = Settings::default();\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-233ce1bf-49c4-4b3f-87ae-91c2f4d1e342-89","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"  var pending = { look: [0, 0], move: null, axes: null, pressed: 0, act: 0, hover: null, click: false, device: null, touch: null, xbox: null, lock: false, hub: false };\",\"new_string\":\"  var pending = { look: [0, 0], move: null, axes: null, pressed: 0, act: 0, hover: null, click: false, device: null, touch: null, xbox: null, lock: false, hub: false };\\n  window.__jamScene = 'merc';\\n  try {\\n    var q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\n    if (!q.get('scene') && !q.get('room')) {\\n      q.set('scene', 'merc');\\n      history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + q.toString() + location.hash);\\n    }\\n  } catch (e) {}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"  var pending = { look: [0, 0], move: null, axes: null, pressed: 0, act: 0, hover: null, click: false, device: null, touch: null, xbox: null, lock: false, hub: false };\",\"old_line\":68,\"new_string\":\"  var pending = { look: [0, 0], move: null, axes: null, pressed: 0, act: 0, hover: null, click: false, device: null, touch: null, xbox: null, lock: false, hub: false };\\n  window.__jamScene = 'merc';\\n  try {\\n    var q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\n    if (!q.get('scene') && !q.get('room')) {\\n      q.set('scene', 'merc');\\n      history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + q.toString() + location.hash);\\n    }\\n  } catch (e) {}\",\"new_line\":68,\"context_before\":\"</div>\\n<script>\\n(function () {\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  var held = {};\\n  var screenName = 'Title';\\n  var started = false;\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"1f392f45-5cb9-42fc-a5bc-cc522d2cec90"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_303","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking whether Rust allows nested extern declarations inside functions.\n\nWasm_bindgen proc macros likely require module-level placement. I'll write the test files and remaining scripts now while the build runs. Browser.py is the most critical file to get right.\n\nVerified that history.replaceState preserves existing query parameters when adding scene=merc. The harness iframe URL is set by the harness itself, so our script won't interfere with it. Confirmed that our test script does not call Math.random.\n\nWriting the remaining files now. run.sh and pack.sh will handle spaces in paths carefully. pack.sh will verify that session.js is the first script. browser.py helpers will stay tight. Playwright will use file:// URLs via as_uri(). The canvas paint timeout is set to 180 seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The scene has to come up as Jam Cry even when the address has no query. I’m writing the pack and browser checks while that rebuild runs."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ecdb02e4-9371-4a17-b03b-49468628c79f-90","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/notes/feedback.md","new_string":"# Jam Cry feedback notes\n\nThese are the answers copied into About and exit-interview.json. Counts come from the scratch logs: 14 compile errors, then 12 failing test runs after it compiled. Six of those stopped a contract route.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\nTesting caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\n\n6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\n\nThe most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\n\nThe least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\nThe headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\n\nThe rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\n\nThe contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\n\nThe hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\n\nInputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\n\nOne change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\nThe checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\n\nThe country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\n\nThe hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\n\nName the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ecdb02e4-9371-4a17-b03b-49468628c79f-91","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/pack.sh","new_string":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Inject unmodified session.js, bindgen the existing wasm, pack one HTML, restore the template.\nset -euo pipefail\nDEV=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nENGINE=\"$DEV/engine\"\nWORK=\"$(cd \"$DEV/..\" && pwd)\"\nNAME=\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503\"\nHTML=\"$WORK/$NAME.html\"\nPAGE=\"$ENGINE/web/index.html\"\nSESSION=\"$DEV/hub/session.js\"\nWASM=\"$ENGINE/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\"\n[[ -f \"$WASM\" ]] || { echo \"FAIL: wasm missing: $WASM\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncp \"$PAGE\" \"$PAGE.template\"\nrestore() { mv -f \"$PAGE.template\" \"$PAGE\"; }\ntrap restore EXIT\npython3 - \"$PAGE\" \"$SESSION\" <<'PY'\nimport pathlib, sys\npage, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\ntext = page.read_text()\njs = session.read_bytes()\nmarker = b\"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\"\nraw = text.encode()\nif raw.count(marker) != 1:\n    raise SystemExit(\"marker missing\")\nif b\"</script\" in js.lower() or b\"<!--\" in js or b\"<script\" in js.lower():\n    raise SystemExit(\"session.js cannot sit in a script element\")\npage.write_bytes(raw.replace(marker, js, 1))\nPY\nBINDGEN=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \"$BINDGEN\" --out-name shardfall \"$WASM\"\n(\n  cd \"$ENGINE\"\n  python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \"$BINDGEN\" \\\n    --title \"Jam Cry\" \\\n    --description \"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\" \\\n    --theme-color \"#2a2420\" \\\n    --scene merc \\\n    --out \"$HTML\"\n)\nrm -rf \"$BINDGEN\"\npython3 - \"$HTML\" \"$SESSION\" \"$PAGE\" <<'PY'\nimport pathlib, sys\nhtml, session, template = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\ntext = html.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\njs = session.read_text()\nstart = text.find(\"<script>\")\nend = text.find(\"</script>\", start)\nbody = text[start + len(\"<script>\"):end]\nif body != js:\n    raise SystemExit(f\"first script is not session.js ({len(body)} vs {len(js)})\")\nif text.count(\"<title>\") != 1 or \"<title>Jam Cry</title>\" not in text:\n    raise SystemExit(\"title\")\nif text.count('name=\"theme-color\"') != 1 or 'content=\"#2a2420\"' not in text:\n    raise SystemExit(\"theme\")\nif \"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\" not in template.read_text():\n    raise SystemExit(\"template was not restored\")\nprint(\"packed\", html.name, \"bytes\", html.stat().st_size)\nPY\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":796,"output_tokens":2026,"cache_read_input_tokens":154112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"9ebae58a-0d9e-442d-8824-3ed599bc265b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ecdb02e4-9371-4a17-b03b-49468628c79f-90","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Jam Cry feedback notes\\n\\nThese are the answers copied into About and exit-interview.json. Counts come from the scratch logs: 14 compile errors, then 12 failing test runs after it compiled. Six of those stopped a contract route.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n\\nTesting caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\n\\n6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\n\\nThe most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\n\\nThe least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n\\nThe headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\n\\nThe rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\n\\nThe contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\n\\nThe hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\n\\nInputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\n\\nOne change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n\\nThe checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\n\\nThe country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\n\\nThe hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\n\\nName the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/notes/feedback.md has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/notes/feedback.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/notes/feedback.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Jam Cry feedback notes\\n\\nThese are the answers copied into About and exit-interview.json. Counts come from the scratch logs: 14 compile errors, then 12 failing test runs after it compiled. Six of those stopped a contract route.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n\\nTesting caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\n\\n6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\n\\nThe most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\n\\nThe least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n\\nThe headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\n\\nThe rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\n\\nThe contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\n\\nThe hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\n\\nInputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\n\\nOne change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n\\nThe checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\n\\nThe country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\n\\nThe hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\n\\nName the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ecdb02e4-9371-4a17-b03b-49468628c79f-91","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Inject unmodified session.js, bindgen the existing wasm, pack one HTML, restore the template.\\nset -euo pipefail\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nWORK=\\\"$(cd \\\"$DEV/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nNAME=\\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503\\\"\\nHTML=\\\"$WORK/$NAME.html\\\"\\nPAGE=\\\"$ENGINE/web/index.html\\\"\\nSESSION=\\\"$DEV/hub/session.js\\\"\\nWASM=\\\"$ENGINE/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\\"\\n[[ -f \\\"$WASM\\\" ]] || { echo \\\"FAIL: wasm missing: $WASM\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\ncp \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$PAGE.template\\\"\\nrestore() { mv -f \\\"$PAGE.template\\\" \\\"$PAGE\\\"; }\\ntrap restore EXIT\\npython3 - \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\npage, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = page.read_text()\\njs = session.read_bytes()\\nmarker = b\\\"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\\"\\nraw = text.encode()\\nif raw.count(marker) != 1:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"marker missing\\\")\\nif b\\\"</script\\\" in js.lower() or b\\\"<!--\\\" in js or b\\\"<script\\\" in js.lower():\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"session.js cannot sit in a script element\\\")\\npage.write_bytes(raw.replace(marker, js, 1))\\nPY\\nBINDGEN=\\\"$(mktemp -d)\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$WASM\\\"\\n(\\n  cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n  python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" \\\\\\n    --title \\\"Jam Cry\\\" \\\\\\n    --description \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\" \\\\\\n    --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" \\\\\\n    --scene merc \\\\\\n    --out \\\"$HTML\\\"\\n)\\nrm -rf \\\"$BINDGEN\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$HTML\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" \\\"$PAGE\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\nhtml, session, template = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = html.read_text(errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\njs = session.read_text()\\nstart = text.find(\\\"<script>\\\")\\nend = text.find(\\\"</script>\\\", start)\\nbody = text[start + len(\\\"<script>\\\"):end]\\nif body != js:\\n    raise SystemExit(f\\\"first script is not session.js ({len(body)} vs {len(js)})\\\")\\nif text.count(\\\"<title>\\\") != 1 or \\\"<title>Jam Cry</title>\\\" not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"title\\\")\\nif text.count('name=\\\"theme-color\\\"') != 1 or 'content=\\\"#2a2420\\\"' not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"theme\\\")\\nif \\\"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\\" not in template.read_text():\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"template was not restored\\\")\\nprint(\\\"packed\\\", html.name, \\\"bytes\\\", html.stat().st_size)\\nPY\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/pack.sh has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/pack.sh has been created.\",\"a