{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_308","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The WASM build completed successfully in 1 minute and 10 seconds.\n\nThe build succeeded, but it is unclear whether the updated settings.rs was actually compiled. The log shows rapid compilation without recompiling that file, so Cargo may have used a stale fingerprint.\n\nThe successful build confirms the updated settings.rs was compiled. The file was edited before the build started, so the changes were present on disk.\n\nThe remaining scripts and shell files were written and made executable. The next step is to pack the HTML.\n\nHTML packing will use wasm-bindgen directly and skip cargo. Native tests can run in parallel with packing because they do not conflict. The native rebuild of pav_core should finish in about one minute.\n\nThe full merc test suite will run once to verify about_slice works, then filtered runs will follow. Only one cargo test process should be active at a time.\n\nI will run the full merc test suite once and pack the HTML in parallel. Browser tests will follow once packing finishes. I am estimating that both processes could take up to three minutes total.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The WebAssembly build finished. Next I’ll pack the page and re-run the native sim tests."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f9fac320-5d9e-43c0-99b0-42e137992921-98","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/pack.sh\"","description":"Pack Jam Cry into one HTML file","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f9fac320-5d9e-43c0-99b0-42e137992921-99","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine\" && CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 C