{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_316","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 11 checks passed in 19 seconds. The process exited successfully.\n\nWebGPU nodraw and test mode completed in record time. The node warning went to stderr and was captured in the log file, but it did not affect the check count.\n\nWebKit and net will run first. Launch is the riskiest because it needs GPU paint, so I'll run it last. All three browsers will execute sequentially in one script to avoid juggling processes.\n\nLaunch tests may each take three to six minutes. I will start the browser sequence and write the exit-interview and PROGRESS drafts in parallel. I can also write the JSON file now since the hook counts are stable.\n\nLaunch1 will run alone first. If it passes, launch2 and hub follow. Hub can wait until after launches because it does not need WebGPU. A paint bug would be fixed in the render code, not the counts.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d9c820cd-bb3c-4b0f-b29c-7cb13a2a11ec-110","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"set -u\nB=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/browser.py\"\nL=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer\"\npython3 \"$B\" webkit > \"$L/webkit.log\" 2>&1; echo WEBKIT:$? >> \"$L/webkit.log\"\npython3 \"$B\" net > \"$L/net.log\" 2>&1; echo NET:$? >> \"$L/net.log\"\npython3 \"$B\" launch1 > \"$L/launch1.log\" 2>&1; echo LAUNCH1:$? >> \"$L/launch1.log\"\necho ALLDONE >> \"$L/launch1.log\"","description":"Run WebKit, net, and first file launch","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":400,"output_tokens":926,"cache_read_input_tokens":175104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5