{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_326","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `guide_panel` function calls `guide(device)`, which likely refers to `crate::input::guide` imported in `ui.rs`.\n\nThe screenshot shows a dark panel on the left, but `guide_panel` is actually `LEFT_BOTTOM`. The image description may have placed it incorrectly. Since the scene is \"merc\", the guide should be hidden unless `scene_name` is wrong. The dark panel might actually be the semi-transparent shell (#shell), and the control list could be a hallucination from faint text.\n\nThe description mentions an X button, which suggests a Window rather than the guide Area. The shell text likely overlaps with the egui guide. I will search for Window::new calls in panel.rs or rooms.rs.\n\nI am checking lines 470-520 to see if `show_guide` is reset after being set false. The first-frame path might also be involved. I ruled out a wasm build issue because the successful compile included the fix. The scene name comparison might fail due to casing or a path like \"world/merc\".","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1b0e54a6-2565-4bb3-af70-110921e86590-127","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scene_name","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":831,"output_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":188288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"81a8a751-4fda-4846-be56-097af8c0c4c2"}
