{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_339","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The room card appears for merc because merc is a room scene.\n\nThe fix is to return early before any egui windows when the scene is merc. This suppresses the room card, pad notes, physics UI, feel UI, teleport menu, editor, and look window.\n\nThe early return also prevents `card_visible` from setting `guide.station`. I will rebuild the WASM binary, repack the app, and relaunch to verify the fix.\n\nNo cargo processes are running. The early return is safe because closure variables default to None or empty, and skipping egui should not break input.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The room card is the pavilion window on top of the title. I’ll skip the engine UI for this scene and repack."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7601918c-176e-4682-a9d7-b458cc87802a-145","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs","old_string":"        let out = self.egui_ctx.run_ui(raw, |ui| {\n            let ctx = ui.ctx().clone();\n            if let Some(c) = &info.crash {","new_string":"        let out = self.egui_ctx.run_ui(raw, |ui| {\n            let ctx = ui.ctx().clone();\n            if scene_name == \"merc\" {\n                // The page owns the shell. The room card and the pavilion panels stay off.\n                return;\n            }\n            if let Some(c) = &info.crash {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2091,"output_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":202368,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2aa780e9-f6c3-40e7-9cb3-8408f0115f88"}
