{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_352","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A CSS rule setting `button` elements to `display: block` overrides the `hidden` attribute on `#settings-btn`.\n\nThe Settings button appears twice: as a visible standalone element with an orange border and focus style, and as the menu row. It likely receives focus because it is the first button in the shell.\n\nThe orange focus ring matches both the button border and the focus style. Adding `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` will reliably hide hidden elements. This confirms the bug shown in the launch screenshot. The plan requires the Settings button to appear only when a touch notice is set.\n\nThe fix belongs in the template `index.html`, not the packed HTML, because `pack.sh` rebuilds from the template. The WASM does not need a rebuild for this change. I am checking whether the packer uses `engine/web/index.html` as its shell.\n\nThe invite buttons \"Make code\" and \"Join code\" are also inside a hidden `#invite` container. They likely share the same display bug, though the screenshot did not mention them.\n\nOnly `#settings-btn` is affected by the display override; the `#invite` div and `#notice` paragraph respect their `hidden` attributes correctly. Once properly hidden, focus should shift to the menu rows, which receive an `on` class from the game.\n\nThe orange border on the floating Settings button is its permanent border, not a focus ring. The game focus is already correctly on New contract, which carries the `on` class. The `#about` and `#card` divs also respect their `hidden` attributes. I will add `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` after the existing button rule.\n\nA cleaner selector `button[hidden]` would beat the default button rule without `!important`. I will also check whether the shell clips the About section at 540px.\n\nThe shell uses overflow: auto, so the About section is scrollable rather than clipped from the document. At 540px height, the menu content totals roughly 600px, exceeding the viewport and likely causing visual clipping. The duplicate Settings button consumes about 80px of that space.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e94d651f-1aac-4991-b86c-b9d052ab15d3-24","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"settings|notice|hidden","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/browser.py"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e94d651f-1aac-4991-b86c-b9d052ab15d3-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"settings-btn|hidden|notice","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2557,"output_tokens":1462,"cache_read_input_tokens":63104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c79d429d-29c5-470d-87f8-4e1f667a9395"}
