{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_363","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"hub.py is running as PID 648002 with HTTP enabled.\n\nSearching for the Chromium child of hub.py. The 7:11 runtime suggests a case is hanging or the browser is closing.\n\nThe 90-second timeout should have fired, so the hang likely stems from a stuck wait_for_function or iframe loading. If skip fails, all four players may load the full 11MB WASM game and start WebGPU, causing the harness to wait indefinitely for game logic that never finishes. I will inspect the Chromium child process and the harness page to verify expected timing.\n\nThe 10-minute game round means the harness could wait for the full session. Four cases at 90 seconds each would total about six minutes. The 7:11 runtime suggests the fourth case is hitting its timeout or the browser close is hanging. I will check the node driver's child processes and open pages to confirm.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8e19adcd-89f1-4283-8f15-0327c9676d8d-39","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ps -o pid,ppid,etime,pcpu,pmem,cmd --ppid 648002\necho '--- node/chrome under hub ---'\n# walk descendants\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, pathlib\nroot=648002\nchildren={}\nfor p in pathlib.Path('/proc').iterdir():\n    if not p.name.isdigit():\n        continue\n    try:\n        stat=(p/'stat').read_text().split()\n        ppid=int(stat[3])\n    except Exception:\n        continue\n    children.setdefault(ppid, []).append(int(p.name))\nseen=[]\nstack=[root]\nwhile stack:\n    pid=stack.pop()\n    for c in children.get(pid, []):\n        seen.append(c)\n        stack.append(c)\nprint('descendants', len(seen))\nfor pid in seen:\n    try:\n        cmd=pathlib.Path(f'/proc/{pid}/cmdline').read_bytes().replace(b'\\x00', b' ').decode()[:240]\n        et=pathlib.Path(f'/proc/{pid}/stat').read_text().split()[21]\n    except Exception as e:\n        cmd=str(e)\n   