{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_380","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The audio-bus issue is that cargo test runs both library and documentation tests.\n\nThe `take_cargo` script only checks the last `test result:` line. Documentation tests appear last with zero passes, so it fails even though unit tests passed. The fix is to sum passed and failed counts across all test result lines.\n\nThe updated `take_cargo` script now iterates over every `test result:` line. It extracts passed and failed counts with sed, sums them across all lines, and fails only if the total passed count is zero.\n\nReal failures will still be caught because `show_fail` prints FAILED lines. The browser tests are still running, so I will fix `run.sh` now and rerun the full suite once they finish. Editing the script mid-run is safe since the current bash already loaded it. I could also skip doc tests with `--doc` or a filter after `--`.\n\nThe filter does not match documentation tests, so they run with zero passes. Using `cargo test -p pav_audio --lib` would skip doc tests entirely and avoid the parsing bug. Pav_core integration tests have no doc tests. Pav_view may still have them; its log was truncated during compilation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e89a3187-7995-4dcb-a279-689f0e17585d-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs","offset":660,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e89a3187-7995-4dcb-a279-689f0e17585d-65","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/run.sh","old_string":"  local line p f\n  line=\"$(grep '^test result:' \"$log\" | tail -1)\"\n  p=\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\([0-9][0-9]*\\) passed.*/\\1/p' <<<\"$line\")\"\n  f=\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\([0-9][0-9]*\\) failed.*/\\1/p' <<<\"$line\")\"\n  p=\"${p:-0}\"\n  f=\"${f:-0}\"","new_string":"  # Sum every cargo result. Doc-tests often add a 0-passed line after the real suite.\n  local p=0 f=0 line np nf\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\n    np=\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\([0-9][0-9]*\\) passed.*/\\1/p' <<<\"$line\")\"\n    nf=\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\([0-9][0-9]*\\) failed.*/\\1/p' <<<\"$line\")\"\n    p=$((p + ${np:-0}))\n    f=$((f + ${nf:-0}))\n  done < <(grep '^test result:' \"$log\")"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2790,"output_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":101632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"f194aa94-dc00-4f1e-858d-ce586ef33f8b"}
