{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_387","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 48 tests passed. The run.sh output was a single line.\n\nNext steps include verifying the regenerated launch screenshots, copying evidence to scratch with required names, writing the handin check script and log, updating goal plan checkboxes and deviations, confirming one HTML file remains with the restored template marker and exit-interview parses correctly, and marking todos complete while keeping at least one in_progress.\n\nMarking all todos complete is correct once the goal is finished. The handin verification will check the HTML path, dev subfolder, PROGRESS.md, title notes, exit-interview.json structure, and forbidden strings in shipped game files.\n\nThe handin check will use a Python script to verify file existence, parse JSON, and scan source files while excluding the packed wasm blob. This avoids false positives from base64-encoded strings inside the HTML.\n\nThe handin check will mirror the existing fiction test's source-file scan. It will search world.rs, shell scripts, toml files, index.html text, and notes. The packed HTML contains gzip wasm so short tokens will false-positive there.\n\nThe handin bundle needs sim-combat.log, sim-world.log, playthrough.log, ui-audio.log, browser.log, hub.log, launch-1.png, launch-2.png, launch.log, run-all.log, and handin.log. launch.log should merge the two launch console outputs. The regenerated launch screenshots will be checked first to confirm they are still correct.\n\nThe plan file checkboxes are being flipped from [ ] to [x] in order as each task passes. A Deviations section is being added with one bullet.\n\nHub and pack HTML checks are now complete. The deviations bullet will be inserted at the end of the plan file.\n\nThe work root contains exactly one HTML file. The title notes exist. The pack.sh script restores the index.html template marker, so the suite does not overwrite it. The run.sh output is confirmed clean: only the PASS/FAIL summary line appears in stdout, while the Node warning was redirected to stderr and captured by the Python runner.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0aaba036-0f50-47d1-b130-947d3739a1e3-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/test-logs/launch-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0aaba036-0f50-47d1-b130-947d3739a1e3-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"BANNED|jackal|fiction_lines|fn fiction","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2340,"output_tokens":1392,"cache_read_input_tokens":115200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"1ecd1ea7-86c1-4848-b97e-33a7e8746cee"}
