ontent\":\"- **Reading:** read §1 to §3 whole before you start. Read the rest as you reach each milestone in §13.\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## 1. The game\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"### 1.1 Pitch\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"### 1.2 Genre and perspective (DECIDED)\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"### 1.3 Pillars: every feature serves one of these\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"### 1.4 Keep what makes the source distinctive, and improve it. Do not copy it.\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"### 1.5 Scope (DECIDED)\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"**In:** everything in §5 to §11. A main path of 75 to 90 minutes with an ending choice, plus side content on the map.\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"## 2. What I verified by building the engine here (2026-11-04)\"},{\"line_number\":55,\"content\":\"### 2.1 Builds\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"- `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` **refuses wasm-bindgen snippets**. Don't use `#[wasm_bindgen(inline_js)]` or `module=`. Call global functions on `window` instead (§12.5).\"},{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"### 2.2 Browser flags: TASK.md's list does not work for this engine\"},{\"line_number\":68,\"content\":\"  - Add a test switch that skips scene drawing (§14.3) when a browser test needs the sim at full speed.\"},{\"line_number\":71,\"content\":\"### 2.3 Hub harness: confirmed passing on an engine page\"},{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"### 2.4 Input in headless Chromium\"},{\"line_number\":99,\"content\":\"### 2.5 What the engine does not give you (you build it)\"},{\"line_number\":102,\"content\":\"| No first-person camera | `CameraRig::forward` clamps tilt to 0–90°, so it can't look up; `far = max(distance*4+200, 300)` | §12.2 |\"},{\"line_number\":111,\"content\":\"| `InputFrame` has no look input; `cmd` is Shardfall's type; it must stay `Copy` | `input.rs` | Add `look: Vec2`, `axes: Vec2`, `act: u32` (§12.3) |\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"### 2.6 What is in the asset store\"},{\"line_number\":126,\"content\":\"## 3. World bible and writing\"},{\"line_number\":128,\"content\":\"### 3.1 Setting\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"### 3.2 Cast\"},{\"line_number\":155,\"content\":\"### 3.3 Writing style (TASK.md: \\\"a writing style similar to the source's\\\")\"},{\"line_number\":177,\"content\":\"### 3.4 Story in one paragraph\"},{\"line_number\":187,\"content\":\"## 4. Controls (DECIDED)\"},{\"line_number\":238,\"content\":\"**Feel settings (defaults):** stick look 140°/s at full deflection with a response curve, mouse 0.12°/count, aim assist on for controller only (slowdown near targets plus light magnetism while L2 is held), invert Y off. Rendered look uses the latest input every frame, not only tick results (§12.2).\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"## 5. Systems\"},{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"### 5.1 Movement\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"### 5.2 Shooting\"},{\"line_number\":252,\"content\":\"### 5.3 Weapons (DECIDED: three slots, plus throwables and machete)\"},{\"line_number\":275,\"content\":\"### 5.4 Condition and jams (pillar 3)\"},{\"line_number\":287,\"content\":\"### 5.5 Damage and treatment\"},{\"line_number\":299,\"content\":\"### 5.6 Fever (pillar 3)\"},{\"line_number\":308,\"content\":\"### 5.7 Fire (pillar 1: the feature people will remember)\"},{\"line_number\":339,\"content\":\"### 5.8 Wind and weather\"},{\"line_number\":344,\"content\":\"### 5.9 Time of day\"},{\"line_number\":347,\"content\":\"### 5.10 Stealth and detection\"},{\"line_number\":352,\"content\":\"### 5.11 Vehicles (engine changes required)\"},{\"line_number\":371,\"content\":\"### 5.12 Companions (pillar 3)\"},{\"line_number\":379,\"content\":\"### 5.13 Enemy AI\"},{\"line_number\":389,\"content\":\"### 5.14 Guard posts and territory\"},{\"line_number\":392,\"content\":\"### 5.15 Safe houses\"},{\"line_number\":395,\"content\":\"### 5.16 Economy\"},{\"line_number\":403,\"content\":\"### 5.17 Map, GPS, monocular (pillar 2)\"},{\"line_number\":410,\"content\":\"### 5.18 Tapes\"},{\"line_number\":413,\"content\":\"### 5.19 Reputation\"},{\"line_number\":416,\"content\":\"### 5.20 Wildlife and people\"},{\"line_number\":420,\"content\":\"### 5.21 Saves\"},{\"line_number\":426,\"content\":\"### 5.22 Difficulty\"},{\"line_number\":431,\"content\":\"## 6. The world\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"### 6.1 Terrain and view distance\"},{\"line_number\":447,\"content\":\"### 6.2 Sky\"},{\"line_number\":450,\"content\":\"### 6.3 Places (positions are metres, x east, z south, origin at map centre; put them in `world.toml` and adjust freely)\"},{\"line_number\":494,\"content\":\"## 7. Multiplayer (DECIDED)\"},{\"line_number\":498,\"content\":\"### 7.1 Mode and tags\"},{\"line_number\":511,\"content\":\"### 7.2 The round: \\\"Contract Run\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":522,\"content\":\"### 7.3 Protocol checklist\"},{\"line_number\":523,\"content\":\"- JS shim `window.gameNet` (§12.5) wraps `AIHub`: call `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true})` while the page parses. When it resolves `null`, run the normal game with the title screen.\"},{\"line_number\":534,\"content\":\"### 7.4 Netcode (host-authoritative world, each copy owns its own player)\"},{\"line_number\":542,\"content\":\"- Keep the message layer in Rust (`engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/net.rs`), pure and testable: an in-memory link with seeded latency, jitter and loss runs two `Sim`s in a test (§14).\"},{\"line_number\":544,\"content\":\"### 7.5 Hidden tabs and low frame rates\"},{\"line_number\":547,\"content\":\"### 7.6 Outside a session: the same round from the title menu\"},{\"line_number\":556,\"content\":\"## 8. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\"},{\"line_number\":558,\"content\":\"### 8.1 UI kit (DECIDED: egui, drawn your way)\"},{\"line_number\":572,\"content\":\"### 8.2 Prompts\"},{\"line_number\":580,\"content\":\"### 8.3 Screens\"},{\"line_number\":598,\"content\":\"- **About/Credits:** paged, large text, §15 content\"},{\"line_number\":600,\"content\":\"### 8.4 HUD\"},{\"line_number\":603,\"content\":\"### 8.5 Touch-only devices\"},{\"line_number\":606,\"content\":\"### 8.6 Attract mode\"},{\"line_number\":623,\"content\":\"### 8.7 Dev mode (from the pause menu, not in sessions)\"},{\"line_number\":635,\"content\":\"## 9. Art and animation\"},{\"line_number\":637,\"content\":\"### 9.1 Art direction (engine's native style as the base)\"},{\"line_number\":653,\"content\":\"### 9.2 New assets (format-2 prop JSON in `engine/assets/props/lib/merc/`, §2.1 for shipping; use the engine's check loop)\"},{\"line_number\":663,\"content\":\"### 9.3 Animation (engine's native system as the base)\"},{\"line_number\":679,\"content\":\"## 10. Audio (all in code, no audio files; extend `pav_audio`)\"},{\"line_number\":693,\"content\":\"## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\"},{\"line_number\":712,\"content\":\"**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"## 12. Architecture\"},{\"line_number\":718,\"content\":\"### 12.1 Dev folder\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a05df810-a283-4768-9940-3dfe90236305-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/\\n  - engine/\\n    - AGENTS.md\\n    - anim/\\n      - 100style/\\n        - style100_back.json\\n        - style100_backrun.json\\n        - style100_idle.json\\n        - style100_run.json\\n        - style100_side.json\\n        - style100_siderun.json\\n      - catalogs/\\n        - 100style.json\\n        - 100style_back.json\\n        - 100style_backrun.json\\n        - 100style_idle.json\\n        - 100style_run.json\\n      