{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_407","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The player moves in abstract coordinates while the camera eye remains fixed in a small diorama.\n\nThe rifle and rag are static world boxes rather than a viewmodel. Stance eye height is computed in World but never copied to the camera, since aim_overlook only updates yaw and pitch. Native simulation tests for look and movement pass.\n\nThe simulation logic is correct. The visual camera failing to track the player is a rendering gap, not a code defect. The project's core purpose is a playable first-person game on the Pavilion engine.\n\nMouse look rotates the overlook camera correctly. WASD changes the player's x and z coordinates in the status JSON, but the view stays fixed. The country player has no visible capsule; the room body remains at spawn. Stance changes World.eye, yet the rendered FpCam.eye is constant. This is a real defect: the shipped first-person camera ignores both stance eye height and world position.\n\nCriterion 2 is ambiguous: it requires eye height changes, but \"eye\" could mean the rendered camera or the simulation field. The HTML page is the real entry point, and movement through the country remains invisible. A criterion whose code is present but whose integrated behavior is unreachable or unusable is refuted.\n\nThe bot director teleports the player and stamps flags, violating the no-cheats rule. Town teleportation in world.rs:971-976 marks town_burned during begin(), completing the step without actual play. Boat teleportation in world.rs:883-893 places the player on water.\n\nNight and Better also auto-set flags in begin() before any play. The contract rows are mostly script steps that stamp state without requiring actual gameplay. Criterion 2 requires every contract row to be playable.\n\nHitscan targets abstract simulation bodies rather than the visual world. Soldiers are coordinates in World, not spawned entities. The player aims at box trees while shooting invisible targets. This makes the game unplayable as a first-person shooter.\n\nThe wind rag is a static decorative box. It is marked when wind speed exceeds six regardless of visibility, so the flag is set by wind speed rather than the rag being visible.\n\nI will also check session.js for modifications, verify Math.random usage in browser tests, confirm the audio test covers music 0.10, review the about screen content, and scan for forbidden names.\n\nThe fire simulation test finished in 0.00 seconds, which is plausible for a small grid with few burning cells. The companion name \"Rafael Quintero\" is not on the forbidden list.\n\nHealth regeneration caps at 100 HP rather than the top of the current segment. Criterion 2 requires restoration amounts matching PLAN.md §5.5, but the test only checks syrette and wound treatment values.\n\nThe health regeneration cap at 100 HP is a deviation from PLAN.md §5.5, but the criterion only requires syrette and wound treatment amounts to match. The blackout fee test correctly asserts a 20% diamond deduction.\n\nThe jam formula matches. I need to verify whether the room body changes capsule height when stance changes, since the room body stays at spawn. I will also inspect the hit code to confirm hitscan multipliers are actually applied rather than faked.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ae6f18b-51b6-4380-b619-2dd16ba4fcf1-43","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"capsule|map_raised|gps|monocular|day_night|sun","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc","glob":"*.rs","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ae6f18b-51b6-4380-b619-2dd16ba4fcf1-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/web/index.html","limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ae6f18b-51b6-4380-b619-2dd16ba4fcf1-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1860,"limit":280}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5896,"output_tokens":2013,"cache_read_input_tokens":103296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"6ebff73c-dfe8-47ab-b1bf-799840949b3b"}
