1,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,109,101,114,99,47,119,111,114,108,100,46,114,115,10,49,53,56,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,110,111,99,108,105,112,58,32,98,111,111,108,44,10,49,54,52,49,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,108,101,116,32,110,105,103,104,116,32,61,32,115,101,108,102,46,104,111,117,114,40,41,32,60,32,53,46,48,32,124,124,32,115,101,108,102,46,104,111,117,114,40,41,32,62,32,50,48,46,48,59,10,50,50,54,50,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,34,104,111,117,114,34,58,32,115,101,108,102,46,104,111,117,114,40,41,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":305,\"content\":\"            let o = pav_core::games::merc::overlook();\"},{\"line_number\":1242,\"content\":\"            let o = pav_core::games::merc::overlook();\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":338,\"content\":\"            \\\"Noclip\\\" => d.noclip = !d.noclip,\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"pub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"fn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\"},{\"line_number\":135,\"content\":\"        aim_overlook(self.world.yaw, pitch);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":158,\"content\":\"    pub noclip: bool,\"},{\"line_number\":1641,\"content\":\"        let night = self.hour() < 5.0 || self.hour() > 20.0;\"},{\"line_number\":2262,\"content\":\"            \\\"hour\\\": self.hour(),\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-92cab50b-137f-4e9e-bc36-dd49cc42ded4-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"620→\\nShow the title and a pulsing \\\"Press any button\\\" prompt (the correct glyphs). Music at the normal 10% default. Never touch saves. It must loop indefinitely without getting stuck (test it).\\n\\n### 8.7 Dev mode (from the pause menu, not in sessions)\\nPages, all controller-navigable:\\n- **Cheats:** God mode, Infinite ammo, No jams, No fever, Noclip, Invisible to AI, Show AI state and detection meters, Show fire grid, Show nav, Show FPS and tick stats.\\n- **Teleport:** every place in §6.3, plus \\\"next objective\\\". **Story:** jump to any contract or ending, complete objective, kill nearby.\\n- **Spawn and give:** enemy by role, squad, vehicle, weapon at chosen condition, diamonds, pills, syrettes.\\n- **World:** time of day, clock speed, wind direction and speed, weather, ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, time scale.\\n- **Balance (live sliders with value and default tick, \\\"Reset to defaults\\\" per page and for all):** enemy accuracy, enemy damage, player damage, detection rate, enemy count multiplier, weapon wear, jam chance, weapon-break threshold, fire spread rate, burn time, wind strength, burn damage, fever interval, fever severity, syrette heal, companion rescue window, vehicle speed, vehicle toughness, contract pay, post re-man hours, player speed.\\n630→\\nEvery slider is a `Tunable`, so `pav set path=merc.fire.spread_rate value=…` does the same thing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Art and animation\\n\\n### 9.1 Art direction (engine's native style as the base)\\n**Keep the engine's cel shading, capsule puppets, primitive-built props and soft bloom.** Make it read as a **sun-bleached safari poster gone wrong**: flat planes of ochre, gold and rust, long shadows, heavy air.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"620→\\nShow the title and a pulsing \\\"Press any button\\\" prompt (the correct glyphs). Music at the normal 10% default. Never touch saves. It must loop indefinitely without getting stuck (test it).\\n\\n### 8.7 Dev mode (from the pause menu, not in sessions)\\nPages, all controller-navigable:\\n- **Cheats:** God mode, Infinite ammo, No jams, No fever, Noclip, Invisible to AI, Show AI state and detection meters, Show fire grid, Show nav, Show FPS and tick stats.\\n- **Teleport:** every place in §6.3, plus \\\"next objective\\\". **Story:** jump to any contract or ending, complete objective, kill nearby.\\n- **Spawn and give:** enemy by role, squad, vehicle, weapon at chosen condition, diamonds, pills, syrettes.\\n- **World:** time of day, clock speed, wind direction and speed, weather, ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, time scale.\\n- **Balance (live sliders with value and default tick, \\\"Reset to defaults\\\" per page and for all):** enemy accuracy, enemy damage, player damage, detection rate, enemy count multiplier, weapon wear, jam chance, weapon-break threshold, fire spread rate, burn time, wind strength, burn damage, fever interval, fever severity, syrette heal, companion rescue window, vehicle speed, vehicle toughness, contract pay, post re-man hours, player speed.\\n630→\\nEvery slider is a `Tunable`, so `pav set path=merc.fire.spread_rate value=…` does the same thing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Art and animation\\n\\n### 9.1 Art direction (engine's native style as the base)\\n**Keep the engine's cel shading, capsule puppets, primitive-built props and soft bloom.** Make it read as a **sun-bleached safari poster gone wrong**: flat planes of ochre, gold and rust, long shadows, heavy air.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":620,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"\\nShow the title and a pulsing \\\"Press any button\\\" prompt (the correct glyphs). Music at the normal 10% default. Never touch saves. It must loop indefinitely without getting stuck (test it).\\n\\n### 8.7 Dev mode (from the pause menu, not in sessions)\\nPages, all controller-navigable:\\n- **Cheats:** God mode, Infinite ammo, No jams, No fever, Noclip, Invisible to AI, Show AI state and detection meters, Show fire grid, Show nav, Show FPS and tick stats.\\n- **Teleport:** every place in §6.3, plus \\\"next objective\\\". **Story:** jump to any contract or ending, complete objective, kill nearby.\\n- **Spawn and give:** enemy by role, squad, vehicle, weapon at chosen condition, diamonds, pills, syrettes.\\n- **World:** time of day, clock speed, wind direction and speed, weather, ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, time scale.\\n- **Balance (live sliders with value and default tick, \\\"Reset to defaults\\\" per page and for all):** enemy accuracy, enemy damage, player damage, detection rate, enemy count multiplier, weapon wear, jam chance, weapon-break threshold, fire spread rate, burn time, wind strength, burn damage, fever interval, fever severity, syrette heal, companion rescue window, vehicle speed, vehicle toughness, contract pay, post re-man hours, player speed.\\n\\nEvery slider is a `Tunable`, so `pav set path=merc.fire.spread_rate value=…` does the same thing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Art and animation\\n\\n### 9.1 Art direction (engine's native style as the base)\\n**Keep the engine's cel shading, capsule puppets, primitive-built props and soft bloom.** Make it read as a **sun-bleached safari poster gone wrong**: flat planes of ochre, gold and rust, long shadows, heavy air.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-92cab50b-137f-4e9e-bc36-dd49cc42ded4-55","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-92cab50b-137f-4e9e-bc36-dd49cc42ded4-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/session.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":8,\"raw_output\":\"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c41c520b-ea82-4af8-ba62-86994313b16b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_411","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that `move_body` never reads the `noclip` field.\n\nTeleport activation does not set position. The simulation tracks hours for stealth detection, but the visual sky remains static room lighting. This disconnect will be noted as part of the overlook rather than a separate nitpick.\n\nThe overlook camera and body are pinned, so first-person movement and stance eye never reach the view. Map, GPS, and monocular are flag timers rather than props, and the rifle and rag are static boxes.\n\nEndings cannot be chosen. build() always routes to Route::Human, the shell lacks an ending choice, and script_ignite auto-marks ending_burn.\n\nRead and Chair exist only as test constructors.\n\nDev teleport, spawn, and world commands are no-ops. The shell ignores place names during activation, and tabs 3 and 4 show only Next and Reset.\n\nCampaign director teleports and stamps coverage without the action the flag names. Town teleport and flag stamping occur in world.rs:971-976. Boat teleport occurs in world.rs:883-893. Night stamps night_contract in begin at world.rs:875-877. Ignite classes stamp flags by calling ignite_at directly rather than firing weapons, as in world.rs:1889-1950.\n\nFindings 1 and 4 both satisfy the \"don't invent requirements\" rule because they are explicitly stated in acceptance criteria 2, 4, and 5.\n\nThe playthrough tests pass by driving the cheating script. They call World::campaign(route) and bot_input, which routes through begin() warps. The test suite encodes the cheat as success rather than independent theater.\n\nThe implementer must make both the bot and human paths use real movement, weapons, and choices, then assert those behaviors rather than patching tests to ignore teleports.\n\nThe plan deviations describe a seeded height field and 10-foot menus as the page shell. They do not weaken acceptance criteria to drop first-person movement or physical props.\n\nThe overlook camera is fixed in pitch and yaw. It never updates eye height or follows the player's world position. The hardcoded eye remains static while the country moves beneath it. Mouse look changes only the diorama angle.\n\nThe launch gate is valid. The title screen and state change are visible in the screenshots, satisfying criterion 6. The hand-in files exist and the exit interview parses.\n\nTests printed 48 PASS and 0 FAIL. Hub checks passed.\n\nI will write the two verdict files only. The workspace will remain untouched.\n\nConfidence is high. These are source-level defects.\n\nNo blocking issues exist. They are model-fixable.\n\nI am also looking for one decisive input/expected/actual bug to cite as a concrete refute.\n\nConcrete refutes are now identified.\n\n- Town step: the player is instantly teleported to Kilometre 40 and the town_burned flag is set before any input. The expected behavior is a journey followed by a played burn.\n- Dev teleport: selecting \"Airstrip\" leaves the player at the same coordinates because activate() does not match the label.\n- Stance change: crouching updates World.eye but leaves FpCam.eye unchanged, so the camera never lowers.\n\nThe verdict will cite four findings rather than a laundry list of every missing PLAN.md system. Missing skeletal animation or streamed terrain is explicitly covered by deviations, and the acceptance criteria do not require a mesh if the country remains playable in the simulation. The bar for first-person movement is strict. A hostile reading might claim the simulation is the game and the overlook is an accepted deviation.\n\nThe plan deviations are self-serving commentary that attempts to lower the bar without editing the acceptance criteria. They do not constitute a valid narrowing of the requirements. Criterion 5 is being verified by comparing the packed HTML header comment against hub/session.js.\n\nThe playthrough test passes Route into World::campaign, so it never exercises a real player choice. The implementer should add an actual in-game choice and drive it with normal inputs rather than special-casing routes in the test constructor.\n\nFor the camera, FpCam.eye must be driven from world position plus stance eye so the country is shown from that eye. The implementer should not merely assert World.eye.\n\nThe terminal response must be exactly `Refuted`. Findings will use game-relative paths with line numbers. The jam test bounds match the specification and are not a bug. Health regenerates at 8 HP per second up to 100, which conflicts with §5.5 requiring slow regeneration up to the current segment.\n\nThe health regeneration code climbs to 100 HP instead of stopping at the top of the current segment. For example, at 45 HP it regenerates all the way to 100 rather than halting at 60. The criterion does not specify the exact rate, but §5.5 requires the cap.\n\nThe health regeneration cap is a PLAN.md §5.5 requirement, so criterion 2 can legitimately cite it as a restore amount. The phrase \"restore the amounts\" applies to syrette and wound treatments, while the 100 HP / 5 segments display is separate.\n\nThe health regeneration cap is being reconsidered. Criterion 2's verification step lists syrette, wound types, fever warning, pill clear, and no-pill blackout, but not segment-capped regen. The instruction also warns against refuting missing edge cases that the plan did not require. This suggests the 8 HP/s climb to 100 HP may be a non-finding rather than a bug.\n\nThe segment-capped health regeneration bug will be kept as a smaller finding. The instruction limits the verdict to one item per gap, so the stronger issues take priority.\n\nThe segment-capped health regeneration bug is being dropped from the verdict. The verification plan only asserts syrette and wound treatments, so adding a segment cap would be scope creep.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim tests pass, but the shipped page never moves the camera with the player, never offers the three endings, and the campaign script teleports and stamps flags. Those are criterion failures, not polish."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7872a028-b51e-4c8e-bbd0-67a0c62fd39b-57","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-verdict-8215da6fd761-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs:52\",\n      \"detail\": \"First-person play is not wired to the view: aim_overlook copies only yaw/pitch, FpCam.eye stays [0.15, 1.55, 4.2], and post() pins the body to spawn, so WASD and stance never move the camera or eye height. Map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag are flags or static boxes, not first-person props. Drive the rendered eye from world position plus stance eye and show the country from that eye.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs:71\",\n      \"detail\": \"A human new game is always Route::Human. The shell has no burn/read/chair choice, and script_ignite marks ending_burn on the first tick of Spec::Ending(0). Read and chair exist only as World::campaign(route) in the test. Add an in-play choice and reach each ending from that choice with normal inputs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs:971\",\n      \"detail\": \"The campaign director cheats the playthrough: Spec::Town sets x/z and town_burned immediately, Spec::Boat teleports onto water, Spec::Night stamps night_contract in begin, and script_ignite stamps ignite_flare/rocket/flamer/etc. by calling ignite_at instead of firing those weapons. Criterion 4 forbids teleport and cheats and requires coverage from real play. Remove the warps and make the bot use the same actions a player uses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs:285\",\n      \"detail\": \"Dev Teleport lists places but activate() ignores those labels, so picking a place does not move the player. Spawn and World tabs only offer Next page and Reset. noclip is stored and never read in move_body. Wire teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip to real state changes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"merc/mod.rs:52-135 and app.rs:1241-1251 pin the camera; world.rs:875-976 and 1889-1958 stamp flags and teleport; shell.rs:285-416 leaves teleport/spawn/world as no-ops; playthrough.log only runs World::campaign(route).\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"See goal-classifier markdown. Native tests and the file:// title launches pass, but the playable page does not move in first person, does not let the player choose an ending, cheats the coverage bot, and leaves dev teleport/spawn/world unwired.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7872a028-b51e-4c8e-bbd0-67a0c62fd39b-58","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-classifier-8215da6fd761-1-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Verdict: Refuted\n\nThe hand-in exists (`Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html`, `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`), `tests/run.sh all` captured `PASS 48 FAIL 0`, and both file:// launches show the title **Jam Cry** over a filled overlook. Those checks do not make the game the one criteria 2, 4, and 5 describe.\n\n## First person is a fixed overlook\n\n`Overlook.eye` is initialized to `[0.15, 1.55, 4.2]` and `aim_overlook` writes only yaw and pitch (`merc/mod.rs:42-56`, `134-135`). `Game::pre` feeds the pavilion body a default input and `post` snaps it back to the room spawn (`mod.rs:118-130`). `app.rs:1241-1251` copies that same fixed eye into `FpCam` every frame.\n\nCrouch updates `World.eye` toward 1.02 or 0.42 (`world.rs:1260-1266`) and WASD updates `World.x/z` (`world.rs:1344-1350`), but neither value reaches the camera. The rifle and red rag are boxes spawned once at fixed coordinates (`mod.rs:99-102`). Map, GPS, and monocular are button timers that set flags (`world.rs:1268-1284`), not props in the hands. A player looking at the page cannot move through the 2048 m country.\n\n## Three endings are not a player choice\n\n`build` always starts `Route::Human` (`mod.rs:71`). The shell goes Title → Difficulty → Merc → Prologue → Playing and never offers burn / read the names / take the chair (`shell.rs:204-250`). `script_ignite` marks `ending_burn` on the first tick of `Spec::Ending(0)` (`world.rs:1956-1958`). `bot_plays_all_three_endings` only reaches the other two endings by constructing `World::campaign(seed, Route::Read|Chair)` (`tests/merc.rs:737`). That is not the player choosing.\n\n## Coverage bot teleports and stamps flags\n\nCriterion 4 allows bus travel and forbids other teleports and cheats. The director does both before the bot acts:\n\n- `Spec::Town` sets `x/z` to Kilometre 40 and marks `town_burned` (`world.rs:971-976`).\n- `Spec::Boat` moves the player onto the nearest water (`world.rs:883-893`).\n- `Spec::Night` sets the clock and marks `night_contract` inside `begin` (`world.rs:875-877`).\n- `script_ignite` marks `ignite_flare`, `ignite_rocket`, `ignite_flamer`, `ignite_mortar`, `ignite_molotov`, `ignite_frag`, `ignite_barrel`, `ignite_vehicle`, `ignite_person`, `ignite_lightning`, and `ignite_cigarette` by calling `ignite_at` / `ignite_disk`, ignoring the input (`world.rs:1889-1950`). The matching weapons are not fired.\n\n`Spec::Flag` marks each contract id as soon as the step begins (`world.rs:986`). The playthrough log is green because it asserts those stamps, not because a normal-input run lit each weapon class or walked into the burning town.\n\n## Dev teleport, spawn, and world do nothing\n\n`activate` on the dev screen handles the tab menu, reset, next page, and cheat toggles (`shell.rs:285-310`). A place name on the Teleport tab is not handled, so the player does not move. Spawn (`tab == 3`) and World (`tab == 4`) only render \"Next page\" and \"Reset to defaults\" (`shell.rs:416`). `noclip` is toggled (`shell.rs:338`) and never read in `move_body`.\n\n## What did hold\n\nJSON shape and `usage == \"added on import\"`, title notes, packed page opening from `file://` with a non-flat canvas (launch-1.png, launch-2.png), hub harness `CHECKS 5`, and the native jam / hitscan / fire-ratio tests on the headless `World`. Those do not cover the missing player-facing paths above.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2346,"output_tokens":4575,"cache_read_input_tokens":126080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"03b06719-bc18-46e9-a29d-d63c58dd4550"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7872a028-b51e-4c8e-bbd0-67a0c62fd39b-57","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs:52\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"First-person play is not wired to the view: aim_overlook copies only yaw/pitch, FpCam.eye stays [0.15, 1.55, 4.2], and post() pins the body to spawn, so WASD and stance never move the camera or eye height. Map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag are flags or static boxes, not first-person props. Drive the rendered eye from world position plus stance eye and show the country from that eye.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs:71\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"A human new game is always Route::Human. The shell has no burn/read/chair choice, and script_ignite marks ending_burn on the first tick of Spec::Ending(0). Read and chair exist only as World::campaign(route) in the test. Add an in-play choice and reach each ending from that choice with normal inputs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs:971\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"The campaign director cheats the playthrough: Spec::Town sets x/z and town_burned immediately, Spec::Boat teleports onto water, Spec::Night stamps night_contract in begin, and script_ignite stamps ignite_flare/rocket/flamer/etc. by calling ignite_at instead of firing those weapons. Criterion 4 forbids teleport and cheats and requires coverage from real play. Remove the warps and make the bot use the same actions a player uses.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs:285\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Dev Teleport lists places but activate() ignores those labels, so picking a place does not move the player. Spawn and World tabs only offer Next page and Reset. noclip is stored and never read in move_body. Wire teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip to real state changes.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"merc/mod.rs:52-135 and app.rs:1241-1251 pin the camera; world.rs:875-976 and 1889-1958 stamp flags and teleport; shell.rs:285-416 leaves teleport/spawn/world as no-ops; playthrough.log only runs World::campaign(route).\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"See goal-classifier markdown. Native tests and the file:// title launches pass, but the playable page does not move in first person, does not let the player choose an ending, cheats the coverage bot, and leaves dev teleport/spawn/world unwired.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-verdict-8215da6fd761-1-0.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-verdict-8215da6fd761-1-0.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-verdict-8215da6fd761-1-0.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs:52\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"First-person play is not wired to the view: aim_overlook copies only yaw/pitch, FpCam.eye stays [0.15, 1.55, 4.2], and post() pins the body to spawn, so WASD and stance never move the camera or eye height. Map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag are flags or static boxes, not first-person props. Drive the rendered eye from world position plus stance eye and show the country from that eye.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs:71\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"A human new game is always Route::Human. The shell has no burn/read/chair choice, and script_ignite marks ending_burn on the first tick of Spec::Ending(0). Read and chair exist only as World::campaign(route) in the test. Add an in-play choice and reach each ending from that choice with normal inputs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs:971\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"The campaign director cheats the playthrough: Spec::Town sets x/z and town_burned immediately, Spec::Boat teleports onto water, Spec::Night stamps night_contract in begin, and script_ignite stamps ignite_flare/rocket/flamer/etc. by calling ignite_at instead of firing those weapons. Criterion 4 forbids teleport and cheats and requires coverage from real play. Remove the warps and make the bot use the same actions a player uses.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs:285\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Dev Teleport lists places but activate() ignores those labels, so picking a place does not move the player. Spawn and World tabs only offer Next page and Reset. noclip is stored and never read in move_body. Wire teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip to real state changes.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"merc/mod.rs:52-135 and app.rs:1241-1251 pin the camera; world.rs:875-976 and 1889-1958 stamp flags and teleport; shell.rs:285-416 leaves teleport/spawn/world as no-ops; playthrough.log only runs World::campaign(route).\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"See goal-classifier markdown. Native tests and the file:// title launches pass, but the playable page does not move in first person, does not let the player choose an ending, cheats the coverage bot, and leaves dev teleport/spawn/world unwired.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7872a028-b51e-4c8e-bbd0-67a0c62fd39b-58","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe hand-in exists (`Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html`, `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`), `tests/run.sh all` captured `PASS 48 FAIL 0`, and both file:// launches show the title **Jam Cry** over a filled overlook. Those checks do not make the game the one criteria 2, 4, and 5 describe.\\n\\n## First person is a fixed overlook\\n\\n`Overlook.eye` is initialized to `[0.15, 1.55, 4.2]` and `aim_overlook` writes only yaw and pitch (`merc/mod.rs:42-56`, `134-135`). `Game::pre` feeds the pavilion body a default input and `post` snaps it back to the room spawn (`mod.rs:118-130`). `app.rs:1241-1251` copies that same fixed eye into `FpCam` every frame.\\n\\nCrouch updates `World.eye` toward 1.02 or 0.42 (`world.rs:1260-1266`) and WASD updates `World.x/z` (`world.rs:1344-1350`), but neither value reaches the camera. The rifle and red rag are boxes spawned once at fixed coordinates (`mod.rs:99-102`). Map, GPS, and monocular are button timers that set flags (`world.rs:1268-1284`), not props in the hands. A player looking at the page cannot move through the 2048 m country.\\n\\n## Three endings are not a player choice\\n\\n`build` always starts `Route::Human` (`mod.rs:71`). The shell goes Title → Difficulty → Merc → Prologue → Playing and never offers burn / read the names / take the chair (`shell.rs:204-250`). `script_ignite` marks `ending_burn` on the first tick of `Spec::Ending(0)` (`world.rs:1956-1958`). `bot_plays_all_three_endings` only reaches the other two endings by constructing `World::campaign(seed, Route::Read|Chair)` (`tests/merc.rs:737`). That is not the player choosing.\\n\\n## Coverage bot teleports and stamps flags\\n\\nCriterion 4 allows bus travel and forbids other teleports and cheats. The director does both before the bot acts:\\n\\n- `Spec::Town` sets `x/z` to Kilometre 40 and marks `town_burned` (`world.rs:971-976`).\\n- `Spec::Boat` moves the player onto the nearest water (`world.rs:883-893`).\\n- `Spec::Night` sets the clock and marks `night_contract` inside `begin` (`world.rs:875-877`).\\n- `script_ignite` marks `ignite_flare`, `ignite_rocket`, `ignite_flamer`, `ignite_mortar`, `ignite_molotov`, `ignite_frag`, `ignite_barrel`, `ignite_vehicle`, `ignite_person`, `ignite_lightning`, and `ignite_cigarette` by calling `ignite_at` / `ignite_disk`, ignoring the input (`world.rs:1889-1950`). The matching weapons are not fired.\\n\\n`Spec::Flag` marks each contract id as soon as the step begins (`world.rs:986`). The playthrough log is green because it asserts those stamps, not because a normal-input run lit each weapon class or walked into the burning town.\\n\\n## Dev teleport, spawn, and world do nothing\\n\\n`activate` on the dev screen handles the tab menu, reset, next page, and cheat toggles (`shell.rs:285-310`). A place name on the Teleport tab is not handled, so the player does not move. Spawn (`tab == 3`) and World (`tab == 4`) only render \\\"Next page\\\" and \\\"Reset to defaults\\\" (`shell.rs:416`). `noclip` is toggled (`shell.rs:338`) and never read in `move_body`.\\n\\n## What did hold\\n\\nJSON shape and `usage == \\\"added on import\\\"`, title notes, packed page opening from `file://` with a non-flat canvas (launch-1.png, launch-2.png), hub harness `CHECKS 5`, and the native jam / hitscan / fire-ratio tests on the headless `World`. Those do not cover the missing player-facing paths above.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-classifier-8215da6fd761-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-classifier-8215da6fd761-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-classifier-8215da6fd761-1-skeptic-0.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe hand-in exists (`Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html`, `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json`), `tests/run.sh all` captured `PASS 48 FAIL 0`, and both file:// launches show the title **Jam Cry** over a filled overlook. Those checks do not make the game the one criteria 2, 4, and 5 describe.\\n\\n## First person is a fixed overlook\\n\\n`Overlook.eye` is initialized to `[0.15, 1.55, 4.2]` and `aim_overlook` writes only yaw and pitch (`merc/mod.rs:42-56`, `134-135`). `Game::pre` feeds the pavilion body a default input and `post` snaps it back to the room spawn (`mod.rs:118-130`). `app.rs:1241-1251` copies that same fixed eye into `FpCam` every frame.\\n\\nCrouch updates `World.eye` toward 1.02 or 0.42 (`world.rs:1260-1266`) and WASD updates `World.x/z` (`world.rs:1344-1350`), but neither value reaches the camera. The rifle and red rag are boxes spawned once at fixed coordinates (`mod.rs:99-102`). Map, GPS, and monocular are button timers that set flags (`world.rs:1268-1284`), not props in the hands. A player looking at the page cannot move through the 2048 m country.\\n\\n## Three endings are not a player choice\\n\\n`build` always starts `Route::Human` (`mod.rs:71`). The shell goes Title → Difficulty → Merc → Prologue → Playing and never offers burn / read the names / take the chair (`shell.rs:204-250`). `script_ignite` marks `ending_burn` on the first tick of `Spec::Ending(0)` (`world.rs:1956-1958`). `bot_plays_all_three_endings` only reaches the other two endings by constructing `World::campaign(seed, Route::Read|Chair)` (`tests/merc.rs:737`). That is not the player choosing.\\n\\n## Coverage bot teleports and stamps flags\\n\\nCriterion 4 allows bus travel and forbids other teleports and cheats. The director does both before the bot acts:\\n\\n- `Spec::Town` sets `x/z` to Kilometre 40 and marks `town_burned` (`world.rs:971-976`).\\n- `Spec::Boat` moves the player onto the nearest water (`world.rs:883-893`).\\n- `Spec::Night` sets the clock and marks `night_contract` inside `begin` (`world.rs:875-877`).\\n- `script_ignite` marks `ignite_flare`, `ignite_rocket`, `ignite_flamer`, `ignite_mortar`, `ignite_molotov`, `ignite_frag`, `ignite_barrel`, `ignite_vehicle`, `ignite_person`, `ignite_lightning`, and `ignite_cigarette` by calling `ignite_at` / `ignite_disk`, ignoring the input (`world.rs:1889-1950`). The matching weapons are not fired.\\n\\n`Spec::Flag` marks each contract id as soon as the step begins (`world.rs:986`). The playthrough log is green because it asserts those stamps, not because a normal-input run lit each weapon class or walked into the burning town.\\n\\n## Dev teleport, spawn, and world do nothing\\n\\n`activate` on the dev screen handles the tab menu, reset, next page, and cheat toggles (`shell.rs:285-310`). A place name on the Teleport tab is not handled, so the player does not move. Spawn (`tab == 3`) and World (`tab == 4`) only render \\\"Next page\\\" and \\\"Reset to defaults\\\" (`shell.rs:416`). `noclip` is toggled (`shell.rs:338`) and never read in `move_body`.\\n\\n## What did hold\\n\\nJSON shape and `usage == \\\"added on import\\\"`, title notes, packed page opening from `file://` with a non-flat canvas (launch-1.png, launch-2.png), hub harness `CHECKS 5`, and the native jam / hitscan / fire-ratio tests on the headless `World`. Those do not cover the missing player-facing paths above.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"22504d8a-ba0a-4162-88c8-739e94178d6e"}
