{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_413","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Continuing work on the Jam Cry game.\n\nVerification was rejected due to high-priority bugs. First-person play is not wired to the view: `aim_overlook` only copies yaw and pitch, `FpCam.eye` stays fixed, and `post()` pins the body to spawn, so WASD and stance never move the camera or eye height. Map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag are flags or static boxes rather than first-person props. The rendered eye must be driven from world position plus stance eye, and the country shown from that eye.\n\nNew games always start as Route::Human because the shell lacks burn, read, and chair choices. Read and chair exist only in test code. An in-play choice must be added so each ending is reached with normal inputs.\n\nThe campaign director also cheats the playthrough. Spec::Town sets position and burned flags immediately. Spec::Boat teleports onto water. Spec::Night stamps the contract flag at startup. script_ignite marks ignite flags by calling ignite_at instead of firing weapons.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The review found four real gaps: the camera never leaves the overlook, endings are test-only, the campaign script teleports and stamps flags, and dev mode does not change the world. I’ll wire those to the same actions a player uses."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e8e5c53-2895-4784-8efb-d8b2a1d858d7-93","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"fp","content":"Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"endings","content":"Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs","status":"pending"},{"id":"bot","content":"Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions","status":"pending"},{"id":"dev","content":"Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip","status":"pending"},{"id":"verify","content":"Re-run sim, playthrough, and the plan verification checks","status":"pending"}],"merge":false}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e8e5c53-2895-4784-8efb-d8b2a1d858d7-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4e8e5c53-2895-4784-8efb-d8b2a1d858d7-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn aim_overlook|fn post\\(|FpCam|overlook|stance|eye_height|Spec::Town|Spec::Boat|Spec::Night|Spec::Ending|script_ignite|fn bot_input|noclip|Teleport|fn activate","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":120866,"output_tokens":1062,"cache_read_input_tokens":10112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"63deeebe-b653-4271-ba81-5c0e6652e6e9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4e8e5c53-2895-4784-8efb-d8b2a1d858d7-93","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [in_progress] fp: Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props\\n- [pending] endings: Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs\\n- [pending] bot: Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions\\n- [pending] dev: Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip\\n- [pending] verify: Re-run sim, playthrough, and the plan verification checks\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Re-run sim, playthrough, and the plan verification checks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"fp\":{\"content\":\"Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},\"endings\":{\"content\":\"Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"bot\":{\"content\":\"Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"dev\":{\"content\":\"Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"Re-run sim, playthrough, and the plan verification checks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4e8e5c53-2895-4784-8efb-d8b2a1d858d7-94","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Jam Cry. The country is [`world::World`]; the pavilion room is a dusk overlook the body stands in.\\n\\npub mod fire;\\npub mod geom;\\npub mod gun;\\npub mod net;\\npub mod shell;\\npub mod world;\\n\\n10→use std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::{Game, GameBox, level_text};\\nuse crate::color::Color;\\nuse crate::entity::{EntityId, Spawn};\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\n20→use crate::input::InputFrame;\\nuse crate::room::RoomDef;\\nuse crate::shape::{Shape, Visual};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub use fire::FireMap;\\npub use geom::exposure;\\npub use gun::{Gun, WeaponId, clear_seconds, jam_probability, spread_mul};\\npub use net::{Link, client_apply, host_publish};\\npub use shell::{Device, MenuInput, glyph};\\n30→pub use world::{Route, Screen, Tune, World, about_pages, fiction_lines};\\n\\nconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\\\"../merc.toml\\\");\\n\\n/// Where the window looks. The country yaw is copied; the eye stays in the overlook.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n40→}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n50→}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n}\\n\\n/// Rules state. Visual entity ids are not part of the save: they are rebuilt in `post`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n60→pub struct Merc {\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    dressed: bool,\\n}\\n\\n/// Builds the overlook and starts a human-route contract. History stays off: the save is the world.\\npub fn build(sim: &mut Sim, _rest: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {\\n    let def = RoomDef::parse(&level_text(Merc::KEY, LEVEL)).map_err(|e| anyhow!(\\\"merc.toml: {e}\\\"))?;\\n    crate::scenes::build_standalone_room(sim, Merc::KEY, def);\\n70→    sim.config.history_seconds = 0.0;\\n    let game = Merc { world: World::campaign(sim.state.seed, Route::Human), dressed: false };\\n    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(game));\\n    Ok(())\\n}\\n\\nimpl Merc {\\n    fn dress(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim) {\\n        if self.dressed {\\n            return;\\n80→        }\\n        self.dressed = true;\\n        let ground = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(48.0, 0.2, 48.0) }, Color::hex(\\\"#c9a24b\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"ground\\\", Vec3::new(0.0, -0.2, 0.0)).visual(ground));\\n        let road = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(3.2, 0.08, 40.0) }, Color::hex(\\\"#8a5a32\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"road\\\", Vec3::new(-1.2, 0.02, -6.0)).visual(road));\\n        let greens = [\\\"#3d5a32\\\", \\\"#2f4a28\\\", \\\"#4a6a38\\\", \\\"#243820\\\", \\\"#6a5030\\\"];\\n        for i in 0..28 {\\n            let col = (i % 7) as f32 - 3.0;\\n            let row = (i / 7) as f32;\\n90→            let h = 1.4 + (i % 5) as f32 * 0.55;\\n            let at = Vec3::new(col * 1.7, h, 1.2 - row * 2.4);\\n            let trunk = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.22, h, 0.22) }, Color::hex(greens[i % 5]));\\n            sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"tree\\\", at).visual(trunk));\\n            let crown = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.7, 0.45, 0.7) }, Color::hex(greens[(i + 2) % 5]));\\n            sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"crown\\\", at + Vec3::new(0.0, h * 0.65, 0.0)).visual(crown));\\n        }\\n        let mound = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(1.4, 0.7, 1.1) }, Color::hex(\\\"#a86838\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"mound\\\", Vec3::new(2.4, 0.7, -1.5)).visual(mound));\\n        let rifle = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.05, 0.05, 0.42) }, Color::hex(\\\"#2a2420\\\"));\\n100→        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"rifle\\\", Vec3::new(0.42, 1.18, 3.15)).visual(rifle));\\n        let rag = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.08, 0.16, 0.02) }, Color::hex(\\\"#9a2a22\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"rag\\\", Vec3::new(0.62, 1.42, 2.6)).visual(rag));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Game for Merc {\\n    const KEY: &'static str = \\\"merc\\\";\\n\\n    fn pre(\\n110→        &mut self,\\n        sim: &mut Sim,\\n        input: &InputFrame,\\n        dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        self.world.tick(input, dt);\\n        let mut out = BTreeMap::new();\\n        if let Some(id) = sim.state.player {\\n            // The country moves inside `World`. The room body stays put so the controller does not fight it.\\n120→            out.insert(id, InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        out\\n    }\\n\\n    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n        self.dress(sim);\\n        if let Some(id) = sim.state.player {\\n            let feet = sim.state.spawn;\\n            sim.set_position(id, feet);\\n130→        }\\n        if self.world.guns.first().is_some_and(|g| g.shots > 0) {\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Impact { pos: Vec3::new(0.0, 1.2, -1.0), strength: 0.4 });\\n        }\\n        let pitch = (self.world.pitch - 0.40).clamp(-0.95, 0.35);\\n        aim_overlook(self.world.yaw, pitch);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        vec![format!(\\\"HP {:.0}\\\", self.world.hp), self.world.goal_name()]\\n140→    }\\n\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        self.world.status()\\n    }\\n\\n    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        self.world.bot_input()\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Jam Cry. The country is [`world::World`]; the pavilion room is a dusk overlook the body stands in.\\n\\npub mod fire;\\npub mod geom;\\npub mod gun;\\npub mod net;\\npub mod shell;\\npub mod world;\\n\\n10→use std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::{Game, GameBox, level_text};\\nuse crate::color::Color;\\nuse crate::entity::{EntityId, Spawn};\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\n20→use crate::input::InputFrame;\\nuse crate::room::RoomDef;\\nuse crate::shape::{Shape, Visual};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub use fire::FireMap;\\npub use geom::exposure;\\npub use gun::{Gun, WeaponId, clear_seconds, jam_probability, spread_mul};\\npub use net::{Link, client_apply, host_publish};\\npub use shell::{Device, MenuInput, glyph};\\n30→pub use world::{Route, Screen, Tune, World, about_pages, fiction_lines};\\n\\nconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\\\"../merc.toml\\\");\\n\\n/// Where the window looks. The country yaw is copied; the eye stays in the overlook.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n40→}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n50→}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n}\\n\\n/// Rules state. Visual entity ids are not part of the save: they are rebuilt in `post`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n60→pub struct Merc {\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    dressed: bool,\\n}\\n\\n/// Builds the overlook and starts a human-route contract. History stays off: the save is the world.\\npub fn build(sim: &mut Sim, _rest: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {\\n    let def = RoomDef::parse(&level_text(Merc::KEY, LEVEL)).map_err(|e| anyhow!(\\\"merc.toml: {e}\\\"))?;\\n    crate::scenes::build_standalone_room(sim, Merc::KEY, def);\\n70→    sim.config.history_seconds = 0.0;\\n    let game = Merc { world: World::campaign(sim.state.seed, Route::Human), dressed: false };\\n    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(game));\\n    Ok(())\\n}\\n\\nimpl Merc {\\n    fn dress(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim) {\\n        if self.dressed {\\n            return;\\n80→        }\\n        self.dressed = true;\\n        let ground = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(48.0, 0.2, 48.0) }, Color::hex(\\\"#c9a24b\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"ground\\\", Vec3::new(0.0, -0.2, 0.0)).visual(ground));\\n        let road = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(3.2, 0.08, 40.0) }, Color::hex(\\\"#8a5a32\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"road\\\", Vec3::new(-1.2, 0.02, -6.0)).visual(road));\\n        let greens = [\\\"#3d5a32\\\", \\\"#2f4a28\\\", \\\"#4a6a38\\\", \\\"#243820\\\", \\\"#6a5030\\\"];\\n        for i in 0..28 {\\n            let col = (i % 7) as f32 - 3.0;\\n            let row = (i / 7) as f32;\\n90→            let h = 1.4 + (i % 5) as f32 * 0.55;\\n            let at = Vec3::new(col * 1.7, h, 1.2 - row * 2.4);\\n            let trunk = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.22, h, 0.22) }, Color::hex(greens[i % 5]));\\n            sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"tree\\\", at).visual(trunk));\\n            let crown = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.7, 0.45, 0.7) }, Color::hex(greens[(i + 2) % 5]));\\n            sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"crown\\\", at + Vec3::new(0.0, h * 0.65, 0.0)).visual(crown));\\n        }\\n        let mound = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(1.4, 0.7, 1.1) }, Color::hex(\\\"#a86838\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"mound\\\", Vec3::new(2.4, 0.7, -1.5)).visual(mound));\\n        let rifle = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.05, 0.05, 0.42) }, Color::hex(\\\"#2a2420\\\"));\\n100→        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"rifle\\\", Vec3::new(0.42, 1.18, 3.15)).visual(rifle));\\n        let rag = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.08, 0.16, 0.02) }, Color::hex(\\\"#9a2a22\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"rag\\\", Vec3::new(0.62, 1.42, 2.6)).visual(rag));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Game for Merc {\\n    const KEY: &'static str = \\\"merc\\\";\\n\\n    fn pre(\\n110→        &mut self,\\n        sim: &mut Sim,\\n        input: &InputFrame,\\n        dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        self.world.tick(input, dt);\\n        let mut out = BTreeMap::new();\\n        if let Some(id) = sim.state.player {\\n            // The country moves inside `World`. The room body stays put so the controller does not fight it.\\n120→            out.insert(id, InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        out\\n    }\\n\\n    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n        self.dress(sim);\\n        if let Some(id) = sim.state.player {\\n            let feet = sim.state.spawn;\\n            sim.set_position(id, feet);\\n130→        }\\n        if self.world.guns.first().is_some_and(|g| g.shots > 0) {\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Impact { pos: Vec3::new(0.0, 1.2, -1.0), strength: 0.4 });\\n        }\\n        let pitch = (self.world.pitch - 0.40).clamp(-0.95, 0.35);\\n        aim_overlook(self.world.yaw, pitch);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        vec![format!(\\\"HP {:.0}\\\", self.world.hp), self.world.goal_name()]\\n140→    }\\n\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        self.world.status()\\n    }\\n\\n    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        self.world.bot_input()\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"//! Jam Cry. The country is [`world::World`]; the pavilion room is a dusk overlook the body stands in.\\n\\npub mod fire;\\npub mod geom;\\npub mod gun;\\npub mod net;\\npub mod shell;\\npub mod world;\\n\\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\\nuse glam::Vec3;\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::{Game, GameBox, level_text};\\nuse crate::color::Color;\\nuse crate::entity::{EntityId, Spawn};\\nuse crate::frame::SimEvent;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\nuse crate::room::RoomDef;\\nuse crate::shape::{Shape, Visual};\\nuse crate::sim::Sim;\\n\\npub use fire::FireMap;\\npub use geom::exposure;\\npub use gun::{Gun, WeaponId, clear_seconds, jam_probability, spread_mul};\\npub use net::{Link, client_apply, host_publish};\\npub use shell::{Device, MenuInput, glyph};\\npub use world::{Route, Screen, Tune, World, about_pages, fiction_lines};\\n\\nconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\\\"../merc.toml\\\");\\n\\n/// Where the window looks. The country yaw is copied; the eye stays in the overlook.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n}\\n\\n/// Rules state. Visual entity ids are not part of the save: they are rebuilt in `post`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct Merc {\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    dressed: bool,\\n}\\n\\n/// Builds the overlook and starts a human-route contract. History stays off: the save is the world.\\npub fn build(sim: &mut Sim, _rest: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {\\n    let def = RoomDef::parse(&level_text(Merc::KEY, LEVEL)).map_err(|e| anyhow!(\\\"merc.toml: {e}\\\"))?;\\n    crate::scenes::build_standalone_room(sim, Merc::KEY, def);\\n    sim.config.history_seconds = 0.0;\\n    let game = Merc { world: World::campaign(sim.state.seed, Route::Human), dressed: false };\\n    sim.state.play = Some(GameBox::new(game));\\n    Ok(())\\n}\\n\\nimpl Merc {\\n    fn dress(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim) {\\n        if self.dressed {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        self.dressed = true;\\n        let ground = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(48.0, 0.2, 48.0) }, Color::hex(\\\"#c9a24b\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"ground\\\", Vec3::new(0.0, -0.2, 0.0)).visual(ground));\\n        let road = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(3.2, 0.08, 40.0) }, Color::hex(\\\"#8a5a32\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"road\\\", Vec3::new(-1.2, 0.02, -6.0)).visual(road));\\n        let greens = [\\\"#3d5a32\\\", \\\"#2f4a28\\\", \\\"#4a6a38\\\", \\\"#243820\\\", \\\"#6a5030\\\"];\\n        for i in 0..28 {\\n            let col = (i % 7) as f32 - 3.0;\\n            let row = (i / 7) as f32;\\n            let h = 1.4 + (i % 5) as f32 * 0.55;\\n            let at = Vec3::new(col * 1.7, h, 1.2 - row * 2.4);\\n            let trunk = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.22, h, 0.22) }, Color::hex(greens[i % 5]));\\n            sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"tree\\\", at).visual(trunk));\\n            let crown = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.7, 0.45, 0.7) }, Color::hex(greens[(i + 2) % 5]));\\n            sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"crown\\\", at + Vec3::new(0.0, h * 0.65, 0.0)).visual(crown));\\n        }\\n        let mound = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(1.4, 0.7, 1.1) }, Color::hex(\\\"#a86838\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"mound\\\", Vec3::new(2.4, 0.7, -1.5)).visual(mound));\\n        let rifle = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.05, 0.05, 0.42) }, Color::hex(\\\"#2a2420\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"rifle\\\", Vec3::new(0.42, 1.18, 3.15)).visual(rifle));\\n        let rag = Visual::new(Shape::Box { half: Vec3::new(0.08, 0.16, 0.02) }, Color::hex(\\\"#9a2a22\\\"));\\n        sim.spawn(Spawn::new(\\\"rag\\\", Vec3::new(0.62, 1.42, 2.6)).visual(rag));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl Game for Merc {\\n    const KEY: &'static str = \\\"merc\\\";\\n\\n    fn pre(\\n        &mut self,\\n        sim: &mut Sim,\\n        input: &InputFrame,\\n        dt: f32,\\n        _events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>,\\n    ) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\\n        self.world.tick(input, dt);\\n        let mut out = BTreeMap::new();\\n        if let Some(id) = sim.state.player {\\n            // The country moves inside `World`. The room body stays put so the controller does not fight it.\\n            out.insert(id, InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        out\\n    }\\n\\n    fn post(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, _dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) {\\n        self.dress(sim);\\n        if let Some(id) = sim.state.player {\\n            let feet = sim.state.spawn;\\n            sim.set_position(id, feet);\\n        }\\n        if self.world.guns.first().is_some_and(|g| g.shots > 0) {\\n            events.push(SimEvent::Impact { pos: Vec3::new(0.0, 1.2, -1.0), strength: 0.4 });\\n        }\\n        let pitch = (self.world.pitch - 0.40).clamp(-0.95, 0.35);\\n        aim_overlook(self.world.yaw, pitch);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn hud(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> Vec<String> {\\n        vec![format!(\\\"HP {:.0}\\\", self.world.hp), self.world.goal_name()]\\n    }\\n\\n    fn status(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        self.world.status()\\n    }\\n\\n    fn bot(&self, _sim: &Sim) -> InputFrame {\\n        self.world.bot_input()\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":149}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4e8e5c53-2895-4784-8efb-d8b2a1d858d7-95","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,1