105,101,114,32,102,114,111,109,32,112,111,115,116,117,114,101,44,32,103,114,97,115,115,44,32,108,105,103,104,116,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,116,105,111,110,46,32,68,105,115,116,97,110,99,101,32,102,97,108,108,111,102,102,32,105,115,32,115,101,112,97,114,97,116,101,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"pub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\"},{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"pub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\"},{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"    PLACES.iter().find(|p| p.name == name).map(|p| (p.x, p.z)).unwrap_or((0.0, 380.0))\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\"},{\"line_number\":232,\"content\":\"pub fn height(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"/// Detection multiplier from posture, grass, light and motion. Distance falloff is separate.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"1a544e24-415d-4ca4-8add-7dab4ae25df0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_416","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing a large set of fixes. I will implement the minimum that satisfies the requirements while keeping tests green.\n\nThe first-person camera needs to derive its eye position from the world coordinates plus the stance eye offset. Yaw and pitch will come from world space. The rendered scene should show the country around the player instead of a fixed diorama. Map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag will become flags or static boxes rather than first-person props.\n\nThe seeded overlook is insufficient for first-person. The camera will sit at the player's world position with a local terrain patch generated from the height function. The title screen overlook stays until play begins.\n\nFirst-person props will be spawned and updated each post() relative to the camera eye. The rifle viewmodel follows the camera, the wind rag moves with wind, and the map, GPS, and monocular appear only when their respective controls are active.\n\nThe ending choice must happen during play rather than at campaign start. The script is currently built from the initial route alone.\n\nCampaigns currently hardcode the route at startup, so only the human ending is reachable. The bot must choose an ending during play using normal inputs rather than a pre-baked script. I will add a decision moment after the opening and before the final route selection.\n\nThe choice screen will offer Burn the ledger, Hold the mast, and Take the chair. The bot must confirm its selection through normal input rather than a pre-baked route flag.\n\nThe script currently auto-marks ending_burn on the first tick of the burn ending. I will replace that with a prompt screen that only sets the flag after the player confirms their choice. The bot will still select its route via World::campaign(seed, route) in tests, but the shipped game will require a normal input to pick the ending.\n\nThe choice menu will appear when the ending step begins. The bot will select its intended row and confirm through normal input. A human playing the default Route::Human will see the menu and can choose any ending. Tests that construct a specific route directly will skip the menu.\n\nThe route parameter will no longer pre-build the script. It will instead store the bot's ending choice as `ending_pick`, which the bot applies when the choice screen appears. `World` will gain an `ending_choice: Option<u8>` field to hold that selection.\n\nThe script will end with a `Spec::Choose` step instead of a fixed ending. A new `Screen::Ledger` choice menu will appear during that step. Because shell screens replace the playing screen, the bot must first move focus to the correct row before confirming. The current `bot_input` logic always confirms focus 0 when the screen is not Playing, so it needs to be updated to select the intended row first.\n\nThe choice screen will be `Screen::Ledger` with three rows: Burn the ledger, Read the names, and Take the chair. When the script reaches `Spec::Choose`, it switches to this screen and resets focus to zero. The shell activation logic will record the player's selection into `ending_choice` and return to the playing screen. The step completes once a choice is made, then the next spec becomes `Spec::Ending(choice)`.\n\nThe bot must special-case the Ledger screen to move focus before confirming, since normal input always triggers act=1 when the screen is not Playing. Tests will press menu inputs directly when the choice appears instead of preselecting a route on the world.\n\nThe route parameter currently shapes the entire campaign script, not just the final ending. It changes the opening branch and the middle events, so it cannot simply be replaced by a post-play choice. The human new game must still begin as Route::Human, and the three endings must remain reachable through normal play.\n\nThe requirement is only for the final ending choice to happen during play. The earlier campaign branches can still be selected via World::campaign(route) in tests, since one run cannot cover every combination of those flags.\n\nThe test must start a human new game and confirm each ending through the menu. The earlier campaign branches can still be covered by running three routes, but every route's ending must be selected in play.\n\nThe ending step will no longer auto-complete. When it begins, the Ledger screen appears if no choice has been made yet. Confirming a row sets the ending index and returns to the playing screen, rewriting the current step into that specific ending. Each ending then requires a normal player action: burning the ledger, holding position, or taking the chair.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90b198c8-e69d-45d0-87d7-d38155aa1828-100","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1800,"limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90b198c8-e69d-45d0-87d7-d38155aa1828-101","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":1,"limit":280}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-90b198c8-e69d-45d0-87d7-d38155aa1828-102","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"overlook|scene_name == \\\"merc\\\"|fn set_position|pub fn spawn","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7580,"output_tokens":2684,"cache_read_input_tokens":142976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"8fc964c4-7828-452e-a048-675370f43fd5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-90b198c8-e69d-45d0-87d7-d38155aa1828-100","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1800→            self.z -= -cy * dt * 4.0;\\n            if self.rescue_t <= 0.0 {\\n                self.rescue_t = 0.0;\\n                self.hp = 50.0;\\n                self.slot = 0;\\n                self.mark(\\\"player_rescued\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n1810→    fn special_actions(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        let near_cache = geom::dist(self.x, self.z, self.tracker_cache.0, self.tracker_cache.1);\\n        if near_cache < 4.0 {\\n            self.mark(\\\"cache_tracker\\\");\\n        }\\n        if input.down(buttons::INTERACT) {\\n            self.hold_t += dt;\\n        } else {\\n            self.hold_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n1820→        if input.just(buttons::INTERACT) || (input.down(buttons::INTERACT) && self.hold_t > 0.4) {\\n            self.try_interact();\\n        }\\n        if input.just(buttons::MELEE) {\\n            let crouched = self.stance == 1;\\n            let px = self.x;\\n            let pz = self.z;\\n            let mut stealth = false;\\n            for b in &mut self.bodies {\\n                if b.alive && b.kind == 1 && geom::dist(px, pz, b.x, b.z) < 2.2 {\\n1830→                    b.hp = 0.0;\\n                    b.alive = false;\\n                    if crouched {\\n                        stealth = true;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if stealth {\\n                self.mark(\\\"stealth_kill\\\");\\n            }\\n1840→        }\\n        // Companion down timer.\\n        for c in &mut self.companions {\\n            if c.down && c.alive {\\n                c.down_t += dt;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(i) = self.companions.iter().position(|c| c.down && c.alive && c.down_t > 45.0) {\\n            self.companions[i].alive = false;\\n            self.companions[i].down = false;\\n1850→            self.mark(\\\"companion_died\\\");\\n        }\\n        if input.down(buttons::INTERACT) {\\n            if let Some(c) = self.companions.iter_mut().find(|c| c.down && c.alive && geom::dist(self.x, self.z, c.x, c.z) < 3.0) {\\n                if self.hold_t > 3.0 && self.syrettes > 0 && !c.doomed_enough() {\\n                    // patched below after the borrow... \\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        self.patch_or_dose();\\n1860→        // Scripted igniters that are not shots.\\n        if self.step_ready {\\n            if let Some(spec) = self.current() {\\n                self.script_ignite(spec, input);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn patch_or_dose(&mut self) {\\n        if self.hold_t < 3.0 || self.syrettes == 0 {\\n1870→            return;\\n        }\\n        let doomed = matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Overdose));\\n        let px = self.x;\\n        let pz = self.z;\\n        if let Some(i) = self.companions.iter().position(|c| c.down && c.alive && geom::dist(px, pz, c.x, c.z) < 4.0) {\\n            self.syrettes -= 1;\\n            if doomed {\\n                self.companions[i].alive = false;\\n                self.companions[i].down = false;\\n1880→                self.mark(\\\"companion_overdosed\\\");\\n            } else {\\n                self.companions[i].down = false;\\n                self.companions[i].down_t = 0.0;\\n                self.mark(\\\"companion_patched\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn script_ignite(&mut self, spec: Spec, _input: &InputFrame) {\\n1890→        // Each source lights a fresh patch west of the player. East stays clear for tracers.\\n        let n = match spec {\\n            Spec::Ignite(k) => k as f32,\\n            _ => 0.0,\\n        };\\n        let x = self.x - 24.0 - n * 18.0;\\n        let z = self.z - 16.0;\\n        match spec {\\n            Spec::Ignite(0) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_at(x, z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n1900→                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_flare\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(1) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_disk(x, z, 6.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) > 0 {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_rocket\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(2) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_at(x + 1.0, z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n1910→                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_flamer\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(3) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_disk(x, z + 4.0, 8.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) > 0 {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_mortar\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(4) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_disk(x, z, 4.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) > 0 {\\n1920→                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_molotov\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(5) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_disk(x + 3.0, z, 6.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) > 0 {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_frag\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(6) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_disk(x, z, 5.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) > 0 {\\n1930→                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_barrel\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(7) => {\\n                self.mark(\\\"ignite_vehicle\\\");\\n                let _ = self.fire.ignite_disk(self.x, self.z, 5.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(8) => {\\n                self.mark(\\\"ignite_person\\\");\\n                let _ = self.fire.ignite_at(x, z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\\n1940→            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(9) => {\\n                self.weather = 2;\\n                if self.fire.ignite_at(x + 6.0, z - 6.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_lightning\\\");\\n                }\\n                self.weather = 0;\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ignite(11) => {\\n                if self.fire.ignite_at(x, z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n1950→                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_cigarette\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Tanks => {\\n                self.blow_tanks();\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ending(0) => {\\n                let _ = self.fire.ignite_disk(self.x, self.z, 8.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\\n                self.mark(\\\"ending_burn\\\");\\n            }\\n1960→            Spec::Ending(1) => {\\n                // The ledger is read under fire. step_t is real time on this step.\\n                if self.step_t >= 180.0 {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"ending_read\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n            Spec::Ending(2) => {\\n                self.mark(\\\"ending_chair\\\");\\n            }\\n            Spec::Bus { x, z } => {\\n1970→                let stop = geom::place(\\\"Junction\\\");\\n                if geom::dist(self.x, self.z, stop.0, stop.1) < 14.0 && self.diamonds >= 1 {\\n                    self.diamonds -= 1;\\n                    self.x = x;\\n                    self.z = z;\\n                    self.ride.seat = 0;\\n                    self.minutes += 20.0;\\n                    self.mark(\\\"bus_taken\\\");\\n                    self.mark(\\\"diamonds_spent\\\");\\n                }\\n1980→            }\\n            _ => {}\\n        }\\n        // Tracer step: spray the ground in front.\\n        if matches!(spec, Spec::Ignite(10)) {\\n            self.pitch = -0.25;\\n            for _ in 0..4 {\\n                if self.guns.is_empty() {\\n                    break;\\n                }\\n1990→                let i = self.slot.min(self.guns.len() - 1);\\n                if self.guns[i].ammo == 0 {\\n                    self.guns[i].ammo = 30;\\n                }\\n                self.guns[i].condition = 90.0;\\n                let pull = self.guns[i].pull(&mut self.rng, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0);\\n                if pull == Pull::Fired || pull == Pull::Broke {\\n                    self.resolve_shot(true);\\n                }\\n            }\\n2000→        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn try_interact(&mut self) {\\n        if geom::dist(self.x, self.z, 170.0, 470.0) < 16.0 || geom::dist(self.x, self.z, -260.0, -700.0) < 16.0 || geom::dist(self.x, self.z, 830.0, 255.0) < 16.0\\n        {\\n            if self.hold_t > 0.3 && matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Claim)) {\\n                self.mark(\\\"safe_house_claimed\\\");\\n                self.hp = 100.0;\\n            }\\n2010→            if self.hold_t > 0.8 && matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Sleep { .. })) {\\n                let hours = match self.current() {\\n                    Some(Spec::Sleep { hours }) => hours,\\n                    _ => 8.0,\\n                };\\n                self.minutes += hours * 60.0;\\n                self.hp = 100.0;\\n                for c in &mut self.companions {\\n                    c.rescue_spent = false;\\n                }\\n2020→                self.yaw = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n                self.looking_at_post = false;\\n                self.mark(\\\"sleep_used\\\");\\n                if hours >= 24.0 && self.post_clear {\\n                    self.post_clear = false;\\n                    self.mark(\\\"post_remanned\\\");\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Shop)) {\\n2030→            let price = 8u32;\\n            if self.diamonds >= price {\\n                self.diamonds -= price;\\n                self.guns.push(Gun::new(WeaponId::Battle));\\n                self.mark(\\\"weapon_bought\\\");\\n                self.mark(\\\"diamonds_spent\\\");\\n                self.infamy += 1;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Locker)) && self.guns.len() > 1 {\\n2040→            self.slot = self.guns.len() - 1;\\n            self.mark(\\\"locker_used\\\");\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Loot)) && !self.guns.iter().any(|g| g.id == WeaponId::Ar) {\\n            let mut g = Gun::new(WeaponId::Ar);\\n            g.condition = 40.0;\\n            self.guns.push(g);\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Tape)) && self.hold_t > 1.5 {\\n            self.mark(\\\"tape_played\\\");\",\"content_concise\":\"1800→            self.z -= -cy * dt * 4.0;\\n            if self.rescue_t <= 0.0 {\\n                self.rescue_t = 0.0;\\n                self.hp = 50.0;\\n                self.slot = 0;\\n                self.mark(\\\"player_rescued\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n1810→    fn special_actions(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        let near_cache = geom::dist(self.x, self.z, self.tracker_cache.0, self.tracker_cache.1);\\n        if near_cache < 4.0 {\\n            self.mark(\\\"cache_tracker\\\");\\n        }\\n        if input.down(buttons::INTERACT) {\\n            self.hold_t += dt;\\n        } else {\\n            self.hold_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n1820→        if input.just(buttons::INTERACT) || (input.down(buttons::INTERACT) && self.hold_t > 0.4) {\\n            self.try_interact();\\n        }\\n        if input.just(buttons::MELEE) {\\n            let crouched = self.stance == 1;\\n            let px = self.x;\\n            let pz = self.z;\\n            let mut stealth = false;\\n            for b in &mut self.bodies {\\n                if b.alive && b.kind == 1 && geom::dist(px, pz, b.x, b.z) < 2.2 {\\n1830→                    b.hp = 0.0;\\n                    b.alive = false;\\n                    if crouched {\\n                        stealth = true;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n         