{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_417","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A large set of fixes is ahead. Care and focus are needed.\n\nThe first-person camera must be set from world coordinates instead of the fixed overlook position. The player body should not be pinned to spawn; it can follow the camera or move to the world position. The country at 2048m must remain visible from that eye.\n\nRendering the entire country every frame is too heavy. A local patch around the player is feasible instead.\n\nThe camera eye will be set to world coordinates with yaw and pitch. Terrain such as ground tiles, trees, water, and roads must move with the player so it remains visible.\n\nFirst-person props including the rifle, wind rag, map, GPS, and monocular should appear in front of the camera when used.\n\nThe title screen must keep the dressed overlook. The camera will only switch to world coordinates once playing begins. This preserves the launch screenshot requirement.\n\nThe `post()` function will set the overlook eye to world coordinates plus stance height during play. The player body will follow that position.\n\nA local terrain patch of 256 four-meter boxes will be updated each frame relative to the player. First-person props will be placed in view space: the rifle in front-right, the rag offset by wind, and the map as a flat box when raised.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-52f9ba5a-b9f0-4a81-91e3-40793d9b615c-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn set_position|fn spawn\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-52f9ba5a-b9f0-4a81-91e3-40793d9b615c-104","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-202611