{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_418","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will implement a focused set of fixes.\n\nI will read move_body and the Screen enum to understand weapon firing. This lets ignite use real shots.\n\nThe four bugs are:\n- Camera eye position must derive from world position plus stance eye. Show the country from that eye. Add FP props for map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag.\n- Ending choice must be in-play burn, read, or chair. Do not auto-mark ending_burn. Reach each ending with normal inputs.\n- Campaign cheats must remove warp in Spec::Town. Set x and z immediately but only stamp town_burned after the player ignites.\n\nSpec::Boat must no longer teleport onto water. The player or bot must travel there and board normally.\n\nSpec::Night must only stamp night_contract when the player is actually at night performing the contract action.\n\nscript_ignite must equip and fire real weapons instead of stamping flags directly.\n\nDev mode needs real controls for Spawn and World tabs. noclip must affect move_body.\n\nThe playthrough test must still pass and set all coverage flags.\n\nRemoving cheats means the bot must perform actions within the time budget. The current playthrough finishes in 0.69 seconds despite simulating up to 54,000 ticks, so real movement should still be fast enough. I will check move_body speeds and weapon firing to confirm honest play can complete. Spec::Bus also teleports the player via script_ignite.\n\nBus travel is explicitly allowed, so the bus position setting is fine. Town warp and Boat teleport are the two actual cheats to remove.\n\nThe camera plan is now concrete. During play, the overlook eye will derive from world position plus stance eye, with yaw and pitch taken from the world. The title screen will keep its dressed overlook so the launch screenshot remains intact.\n\npost() must not pin the body to spawn during play. The capsule should move to the world feet position instead.\n\nA local terrain patch around the eye will replace the fixed origin diorama. It will sample height, fuel, roads, and water within a small radius and recenter on the player as they move. This gives the illusion of viewing the country from that eye without drawing the full 2048-meter map.\n\nFirst-person props will sit in view space. The rifle box sits at eye plus forward 0.45, right 0.22, and minus up 0.18. The wind rag offsets from the muzzle by wind. A map card appears when the map is held. A small GPS box appears when a waypoint is set. A scope tube appears when the monocular is held.\n\nProp entity IDs will be stored on Merc and updated each post. The terrain patch will use a 12-by-12 grid of 4-meter cells, roughly 144 entities plus trees. Each frame the grid repositions around the player based on height, water, road, and tree data. Colors can be set at spawn or respawned when the player crosses a cell, though despawning is needed to avoid leaks.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f4c04b1a-7f01-44bf-8078-c2d9ddbc280d-107","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":240,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f4c04b1a-7f01-44bf-8078-c2d9ddbc280d-108","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":430,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f4c04b1a-7f01-44bf-8078-c2d9ddbc280d-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1288,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f4c04b1a-7f0