_xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/gun.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"pub enum WeaponId {\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"    Flare,\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"    Flamer,\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"    Molotov,\"},{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"        Flare => Stats { name: \\\"Flare pistol\\\", family: \\\"launcher\\\", mag: 1, reserve: 8, rpm: 40.0, damage: 10.0, range: 60.0, wear: 0.5, noise: 60.0, pellets: 1, ignites: true, silent: false },\"},{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"        Rpg => Stats { name: \\\"Rocket tube\\\", family: \\\"launcher\\\", mag: 1, reserve: 6, rpm: 15.0, damage: 300.0, range: 150.0, wear: 1.2, noise: 260.0, pellets: 1, ignites: true, silent: false },\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"        Flamer => Stats { name: \\\"Flamethrower\\\", family: \\\"flame\\\", mag: 100, reserve: 300, rpm: 600.0, damage: 30.0, range: 14.0, wear: 0.05, noise: 40.0, pellets: 1, ignites: true, silent: false },\"},{\"line_number\":62,\"content\":\"        Molotov => Stats { name: \\\"Petrol bottle\\\", family: \\\"flame\\\", mag: 1, reserve: 4, rpm: 60.0, damage: 15.0, range: 24.0, wear: 0.0, noise: 30.0, pellets: 1, ignites: true, silent: false },\"},{\"line_number\":132,\"content\":\"    pub fn pull(&mut self, rng: &mut Rng, jam_mul: f32, wear_mul: f32, break_at: f32) -> Pull {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"pub enum Screen {\"},{\"line_number\":226,\"content\":\"enum Spec {\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"    Ignite(u8),\"},{\"line_number\":321,\"content\":\"        v.push(Spec::Ignite(ig));\"},{\"line_number\":700,\"content\":\"            Some(Spec::Ignite(n)) => return format!(\\\"ignite{n}\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":1034,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(n) => self.flags.contains(ignite_flag(n)),\"},{\"line_number\":1080,\"content\":\"            Spec::Fight | Spec::Ceasefire | Spec::Convoy | Spec::Ignite(10) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1145,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(k) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1618,\"content\":\"        if ignites || id == WeaponId::Flare || id == WeaponId::Rpg || id == WeaponId::Flamer || id == WeaponId::Mortar || id == WeaponId::Molotov || id == WeaponId::Frag {\"},{\"line_number\":1892,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(k) => k as f32,\"},{\"line_number\":1898,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(0) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1903,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(1) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1908,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(2) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1913,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(3) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1918,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(4) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1923,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(5) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1928,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(6) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1933,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(7) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1937,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(8) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1941,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(9) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1948,\"content\":\"            Spec::Ignite(11) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1984,\"content\":\"        if matches!(spec, Spec::Ignite(10)) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"42dc482e-510c-48ac-90f3-c3b72653116f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_419","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large change. I need to implement it carefully so the playthrough still finishes.\n\nThe 900-minute playthrough budget allows 54,000 ticks. Walking the first 450 meters would consume roughly 3,840 ticks. The script currently uses instant begin() cheats.\n\nRemoving the begin() cheats means the bot must perform actions itself. The existing bot_spec already tries many actions. The Town, Night, and ignite flags are currently forced to true instantly. For ignites, the bot should equip the correct weapon and fire instead of calling script_ignite directly. Shot resolution already handles the actual ignition if the weapon has that property.\n\nThe Ignite script covers twelve weapon types. The skeptic notes that script_ignite currently bypasses firing by calling ignite_at directly. I will give the player the correct weapon and select it during the Ignite beat. This may still be a cheat, since equipping is an action the player normally performs.\n\nThe bot should pick up and fire the weapon rather than merely equip it. resolve_shot will then set the ignite flag when the shot hits grass. Barrel, vehicle, person, lightning, and cigarette may not be guns, so WeaponId and resolve_shot need review. Town and Boat must also stop teleporting; the bot will drive or walk to Kilometre 40 and ignite the town with fire or a molotov. town_burned is marked by internal fire burning, not begin().\n\nThe boat must be spawned at the nearest water. The player will travel there, enter the boat, and drive it. The boat_driven flag should trigger when the bot drives on water.\n\nFor Night, begin() should set the clock to night rather than stamping the contract flag immediately. The flag should instead be set when the player performs an action at night, such as crouching, moving, or firing.\n\nThe Night contract will require the player to move or act while the clock is set to night, with the flag marked during simulation once both conditions are met.\n\nFor the Ending step, a three-row menu will appear: Burn the ledger, Read the names, and Take the chair. The human game remains Route::Human until a choice is made. The bot will navigate this menu using down and confirm inputs to select the row matching its assigned route.\n\nThe burn ending must not be forced by script_ignite. The player should ignite the ledger with an igniting weapon or hold position for the read. The read lasts 180 seconds, which is 10,800 ticks and fits within budget. The chair ending requires an interact to sit.\n\nThe test currently selects the route via World::campaign(seed, route). The skeptic wants an in-play choice that the test can also use.\n\nThe test will start a new game and play until the ending menu. The bot will select burn, read, or chair via inputs. The earlier route branches still determine mid-campaign content such as blackout versus pill or companion fate. The ending choice will override those branches at the end.\n\nThe bug is that World::campaign with a fixed route auto-completes the ending step. Spec::Ending must stop auto-completing and instead open the choice menu. The bot then selects the row matching its assigned route, while a human on Route::Human can pick any option.\n\nThe burn ending must remain an action, not an instant flag. I will add a Screen::Finale with the three rows. When the script reaches Spec::Ending, it will switch to this screen if no choice has been made yet. The step stays incomplete until the player selects an option and performs the corresponding action.\n\nThe script currently hardcodes `Spec::Ending(n)` for each route. This forces the ending before the player can choose. I will replace that final step with `Spec::Choose` so the script never pre-bakes the ending. The route still determines earlier steps, but the final choice is made in play.\n\nThe bot will select the finale row matching its assigned route. A human on Route::Human can pick any row instead.\n\nThe bot will select the Read ending by focusing and confirming. Burn requires firing a flare at the player's feet to light the ledger; ending_burn is set only when fire ignites nearby during the ending. Read requires crouching still for 180 seconds; ending_read is set once that duration passes. Chair requires interacting to sit; ending_chair is set on that interaction.\n\nThe bot must move the Finale menu focus to the row matching its assigned route before confirming, rather than always selecting the first option. The done check will verify the flag set by the chosen ending instead of the spec number.\n\nThe test does not need changes. The bot will handle the Finale menu automatically. The read ending adds roughly 21,600 ticks across both seeds. That is about one to two seconds. Burn and chair should be quick. Town will no longer teleport.\n\nThe player is at the convoy location before town. Kilometre 40 is roughly 1,100 meters from the ranger's lodge. Walking would take about 157 seconds. The bot should drive or walk to reach it.\n\nThe default Town budget is 30 seconds. Walking from the ranger's lodge to Kilometre 40 requires roughly 159 seconds, so the budget must be raised to about 200 seconds. That adds approximately 60,000 ticks across all six runs.\n\nThe boat step occurs after the player reaches the ranger's lodge, which is far from the nearest water. The bot must therefore travel to the river before boarding the boat.\n\nThe nearest water is roughly 660 meters from the ranger's lodge. The bot will walk there, spawn the boat at that location without teleporting the player, board it with USE, and drive. A 160-second budget should cover the walk plus driving.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0480d63-5355-43e3-94f4-5a6120d662e5-111","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1354,"limit":280}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0480d63-5355-43e3-94f4-5a6120d662e5-112","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0480d63-5355-43e3-94f4-5a6120d662e5-113","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/gun.rs","offset":1,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a0480d63-5355-43e3-94f4-5a6120d662e5-114","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1540,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4333,"output_tokens":3475,"cache_read_input_tokens":162432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"47765cfb-c846-4f33-b55c-6f888cbb3bf6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a0480d63-5355-43e3-94f4-5a6120d662e5-111","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1354→    fn use_vehicle(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        if input.just(buttons::USE) && self.ride.kind != 0 {\\n            self.ride.seat = (self.ride.seat + 1) % 3;\\n            if self.ride.seat == 2 {\\n                // gunner\\n            }\\n1360→        }\\n        if self.ride.seat == 0 {\\n            if self.ride.kind != 0 && geom::dist(self.x, self.z, self.ride.x, self.ride.z) < 5.0 && input.down(buttons::INTERACT) {\\n                self.ride.repair += dt;\\n                if self.ride.repair >= 6.0 && self.ride.health < 70.0 {\\n                    self.ride.health = 70.0;\\n                    self.ride.stage = 1;\\n                    self.ride.fuse = 0.0;\\n                    self.ride.repair = 0.0;\\n                    self.mark(\\\"repair_done\\\");\\n1370→                }\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let steer = input.axes.x;\\n        self.ride.yaw = geom::wrap_angle(self.ride.yaw + steer * dt * 1.6);\\n        let mut max_s = 16.0 * self.tune.vehicle_speed;\\n        if self.ride.stage == 2 {\\n            max_s *= 0.6;\\n        }\\n1380→        if self.ride.stage >= 3 {\\n            max_s *= 0.2;\\n        }\\n        if self.ride.kind == 2 && !geom::deep_water(self.ride.x, self.ride.z) {\\n            max_s = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        let throttle = input.axes.y;\\n        self.ride.speed += (throttle.clamp(-0.4, 1.0) * max_s - self.ride.speed) * (dt * 2.5).min(1.0);\\n        let (sy, cy) = self.ride.yaw.sin_cos();\\n        let before = (self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n1390→        self.ride.x += sy * self.ride.speed * dt;\\n        self.ride.z += -cy * self.ride.speed * dt;\\n        let (x, z) = geom::clamp_map(self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n        self.ride.x = x;\\n        self.ride.z = z;\\n        self.ride.dist += geom::dist(before.0, before.1, self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n        let h = geom::height(self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n        let h2 = geom::height(self.ride.x + sy * 2.0, self.ride.z - cy * 2.0);\\n        self.ride.pitch = (h2 - h).atan();\\n        if self.ride.roll.abs() > 0.02 {\\n1400→            self.ride.roll *= (1.0 - dt * 3.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n        }\\n        self.x = self.ride.x;\\n        self.z = self.ride.z;\\n        if self.ride.kind == 1 && self.ride.dist > 20.0 {\\n            self.mark(\\\"technical_driven\\\");\\n        }\\n        if self.ride.kind == 2 && self.ride.dist > 15.0 && geom::deep_water(self.ride.x, self.ride.z) {\\n            self.mark(\\\"boat_driven\\\");\\n            self.boat_dist = self.ride.dist;\\n1410→        }\\n        if self.ride.seat == 2 && input.down(buttons::PRIMARY) {\\n            self.mark(\\\"mounted_gun\\\");\\n        }\\n        if self.ride.stage == 3 {\\n            self.ride.fuse -= dt;\\n            if self.ride.fuse <= 0.0 {\\n                self.ride.stage = 4;\\n                self.ride.health = 0.0;\\n                let _ = self.fire.ignite_disk(self.ride.x, self.ride.z, 6.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\\n1420→                self.mark(\\\"ignite_vehicle\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.ride.npc {\\n            let points = [(0.0, 800.0), (0.0, 400.0), (0.0, 0.0), (0.0, -400.0)];\\n            let target = points[self.ride.npc_i % points.len()];\\n            if geom::dist(self.ride.x, self.ride.z, target.0, target.1) < 8.0 {\\n                self.ride.npc_i += 1;\\n            }\\n            let desired = geom::yaw_toward(self.ride.x, self.ride.z, target.0, target.1);\\n1430→            let err = geom::wrap_angle(desired - self.ride.yaw);\\n            self.ride.yaw = geom::wrap_angle(self.ride.yaw + err.clamp(-1.0, 1.0) * dt * 2.0);\\n            self.ride.speed = 10.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn hurt_vehicle(&mut self, dmg: f32) {\\n        if self.ride.kind == 0 || self.ride.stage == 4 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n1440→        self.ride.health -= dmg / self.tune.vehicle_tough.max(0.2);\\n        if self.ride.health > 70.0 {\\n            self.ride.stage = 0;\\n        } else if self.ride.health > 40.0 {\\n            self.ride.stage = 1;\\n        } else if self.ride.health > 15.0 {\\n            self.ride.stage = 2;\\n        } else if self.ride.health > 0.0 {\\n            if self.ride.stage < 3 {\\n                self.ride.fuse = 8.0;\\n1450→            }\\n            self.ride.stage = 3;\\n        } else {\\n            self.ride.stage = 4;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn handle_items(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        if input.just(buttons::HEAL) && self.hp >= 20.0 && self.hp < 100.0 && self.syrettes > 0 && self.syrette_t <= 0.0 {\\n            self.syrettes -= 1;\\n1460→            self.syrette_t = 1.5;\\n        }\\n        if self.syrette_t > 0.0 {\\n            let step = dt.min(self.syrette_t);\\n            self.hp = (self.hp + self.tune.syrette_heal / 1.5 * step).min(100.0);\\n            self.syrette_t -= step;\\n            if self.syrette_t <= 0.0 {\\n                self.syrette_t = 0.0;\\n                self.mark(\\\"syrette\\\");\\n            }\\n1470→        }\\n        if self.hp < 20.0 && self.hp > 0.0 && input.down(buttons::HEAL) {\\n            self.treating = true;\\n            self.heal_t += dt;\\n            if self.heal_t >= 4.0 {\\n                self.hp = 40.0;\\n                self.heal_t = 0.0;\\n                self.treating = false;\\n                self.mark(wound_flag(self.wound.max(1)));\\n                self.wound = 0;\\n1480→            }\\n        } else if self.hp >= 20.0 {\\n            self.treating = false;\\n            self.heal_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        if self.fever_state > 0 && input.down(buttons::PILLS) && self.pills > 0 {\\n            self.pill_t += dt;\\n            if self.pill_t >= 2.5 {\\n                self.pills -= 1;\\n                self.pill_t = 0.0;\\n1490→                self.fever_state = 0;\\n                self.fever_t = 0.0;\\n                self.fever_attack = 0.0;\\n                self.mark(\\\"pill_taken\\\");\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            self.pill_t = 0.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n1500→    fn handle_gun(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        if self.guns.is_empty() {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let infinite = self.dev.infinite;\\n        let no_jams = self.dev.no_jams;\\n        let i = self.slot.min(self.guns.len() - 1);\\n        {\\n            let g = &mut self.guns[i];\\n            if input.just(buttons::RELOAD) {\\n1510→                g.tap_reload();\\n            }\\n            g.tick_clear(dt);\\n            if infinite {\\n                g.ammo = g.ammo.max(30);\\n            }\\n            if no_jams {\\n                g.jammed = false;\\n                g.force_jam = false;\\n            }\\n1520→        }\\n        if self.guns[i].jammed {\\n            self.jam_seen = true;\\n        } else if self.jam_seen {\\n            self.mark(\\\"jam_cleared\\\");\\n        }\\n        let holster = self.ceasefire && geom::in_town(self.x, self.z);\\n        let want = input.down(buttons::PRIMARY) && !self.treating && !holster && self.rescue_t <= 0.0;\\n        if !want {\\n            return;\\n1530→        }\\n        let ads = input.down(buttons::SECONDARY);\\n        let jam = self.tune.jam_chance;\\n        let wear = self.tune.weapon_wear;\\n        let br = self.tune.break_threshold;\\n        let pull = self.guns[i].pull(&mut self.rng, jam, wear, br);\\n        if pull != Pull::Fired && pull != Pull::Broke {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        self.resolve_shot(ads);\\n1540→        if pull == Pull::Broke {\\n            self.mark(\\\"weapon_broke\\\");\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn resolve_shot(&mut self, ads: bool) {\\n        let st = gun::stats(self.gun().id);\\n        let spread = 0.02 * gun::spread_mul(self.gun().condition) * if ads { 0.25 } else { 1.0 };\\n        let jitter = (self.rng.f32() - 0.5) * spread;\\n        let yaw = self.yaw + jitter;\\n1550→        let pitch = self.pitch + jitter * 0.5;\\n        let (sy, cy) = yaw.sin_cos();\\n        let (sp, cp) = pitch.sin_cos();\\n        let dir = (sy * cp, sp, -cy * cp);\\n        let origin = (self.x, self.eye, self.z);\\n        self.shots_tick(origin, dir, st.damage * self.tune.player_damage, st.range, st.noise, st.ignites, st.silent, self.gun().id, self.gun().shots);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn shots_tick(&mut self, origin: (f32, f32, f32), dir: (f32, f32, f32), damage: f32, range: f32, noise: f32, ignites: bool, silent: bool, id: WeaponId, shot_n: u32) {\\n        let mut best_t = range;\\n1560→        let mut best_zone = 0u8;\\n        let mut best_i: Option<usize> = None;\\n        let mut blocked = false;\\n        for w in &self.walls {\\n            if let Some(t) = ray_aabb(origin, dir, w.min, w.max) {\\n                if t < best_t {\\n                    best_t = t;\\n                    blocked = true;\\n                    best_i = None;\\n                }\\n1570→            }\\n        }\\n        if !blocked {\\n            for (i, b) in self.bodies.iter().enumerate() {\\n                if !b.alive {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                let zones = [(1.70, 0.18, 3u8), (1.15, 0.28, 1u8), (0.45, 0.20, 2u8)];\\n                for (y, r, zone) in zones {\\n                    if let Some(t) = ray_sphere(origin, dir, (b.x, y, b.z), r) {\\n1580→                        if t < best_t {\\n                            best_t = t;\\n                            best_zone = zone;\\n                            best_i = Some(i);\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let hit_x = origin.0 + dir.0 * best_t;\\n1590→        let hit_z = origin.2 + dir.2 * best_t;\\n        if let Some(i) = best_i {\\n            let mul = match best_zone {\\n                3 => 3.0,\\n                2 => 0.6,\\n                _ => 1.0,\\n            };\\n            let dmg = damage * mul;\\n            let kind = self.bodies[i].kind;\\n            let in_town = geom::in_town(self.bodies[i].x, self.bodies[i].z);\\n1600→            if self.ceasefire && in_town && kind == 2 {\\n                // Civilians are safe while the ceasefire holds.\\n            } else if id == WeaponId::Dart {\\n                self.bodies[i].poison = 3.0;\\n            } else {\\n                self.bodies[i].hp -= dmg;\\n                if self.bodies[i].hp <= 0.0 {\\n                    self.bodies[i].alive = false;\\n                    if kind == 1 && self.stance == 1 && silent {\\n                        self.mark(\\\"stealth_kill\\\");\\n1610→                    }\\n                    if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ceasefire)) {\\n                        self.ceasefire = false;\\n                        self.mark(\\\"ceasefire_ended\\\");\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if ignites || id == WeaponId::Flare || id == WeaponId::Rpg || id == WeaponId::Flamer || id == WeaponId::Mortar || id == WeaponId::Molotov || id == WeaponId::Frag {\\n            let _ = self.fire.ignite_at(hit_x, hit_z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\\n1620→        }\\n        // Tracers: every third round, a quarter of them light dry grass.\\n        if shot_n > 0 && shot_n % 3 == 0 && self.rng.f32() < 0.25 {\\n            if self.fire.ignite_at(hit_x, hit_z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n                self.mark(\\\"ignite_tracer\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if !silent {\\n            for b in &mut self.bodies {\\n                if b.alive && b.alert == 0 && geom::dist(self.x, self.z, b.x, b.z) < noise {\\n1630→                    b.alert = 1;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\",\"content_concise\":\"1354→    fn use_vehicle(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        if input.just(buttons::USE) && self.ride.kind != 0 {\\n            self.ride.seat = (self.ride.seat + 1) % 3;\\n            if self.ride.seat == 2 {\\n                // gunner\\n            }\\n1360→        }\\n        if self.ride.seat == 0 {\\n            if self.ride.kind != 0 && geom::dist(self.x, self.z, self.ride.x, self.ride.z) < 5.0 && input.down(buttons::INTERACT) {\\n                self.ride.repair += dt;\\n                if self.ride.repair >= 6.0 && self.ride.health < 70.0 {\\n                    self.ride.health = 70.0;\\n                    self.ride.stage = 1;\\n                    self.ride.fuse = 0.0;\\n                    self.ride.repair = 0.0;\\n                    self.mark(\\\"repair_done\\\");\\n1370→                }\\n            }\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let steer = input.axes.x;\\n        self.ride.yaw = geom::wrap_angle(self.ride.yaw + steer * dt * 1.6);\\n        let mut max_s = 16.0 * self.tune.vehicle_speed;\\n        if self.ride.stage == 2 {\\n            max_s *= 0.6;\\n        }\\n1380→        if self.ride.stage >= 3 {\\n            max_s *= 0.2;\\n        }\\n        if self.ride.kind == 2 && !geom::deep_water(self.ride.x, self.ride.z) {\\n            max_s = 0.0;\\n        }\\n        let throttle = input.axes.y;\\n        self.ride.speed += (throttle.clamp(-0.4, 1.0) * max_s - self.ride.speed) * (dt * 2.5).min(1.0);\\n        let (sy, cy) = self.ride.yaw.sin_cos();\\n        let before = (self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n1390→        self.ride.x += sy * self.ride.speed * dt;\\n        self.ride.z += -cy * self.ride.speed * dt;\\n        let (x, z) = geom::clamp_map(self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n        self.ride.x = x;\\n        self.ride.z = z;\\n        self.ride.dist += geom::dist(before.0, before.1, self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n        let h = geom::height(self.ride.x, self.ride.z);\\n        let h2 = geom: