oison <= 0.0 && self.bodies[i].hp > 0.0 {\\n                    self.bodies[i].hp = 0.0;\\n                    self.bodies[i].alive = false;\\n                    self.mark(\\\"dart_kill\\\");\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n\",\"total_lines\":2449}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d6a082d5-393a-4be4-b4ac-7bf717eee5e2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_420","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large change. I need to implement it carefully so tests still pass.\n\nThe country view will use a first-person camera driven by world position and stance eye. The pavilion room stays a small dressed scene. Map, GPS, monocular, rifle, and wind rag become flags or static boxes rather than first-person props.\n\nThe title overlook stays when the screen is not playing so launch screenshots remain valid. During play, the camera will render a local patch of country around the player rather than the full world.\n\nThe camera eye will be the player's world position plus stance eye height. Each post() updates a 9x9 local terrain patch centered on the player, placing first-person props in view space: rifle in front-right, rag offset by wind, map board when raised, GPS unit when a waypoint is set, and monocular when active. Entity IDs are stored on Merc and moved each frame with set_position instead of respawning. The grid covers roughly 72 meters and about eighty entities.\n\nTerrain colors are set by surface type: water blue-gray, road laterite dark, rock gray, grass gold, and trees green. First-person props are positioned using yaw and pitch vectors relative to the eye point. The rifle sits 0.55 meters forward, 0.22 meters right, and 0.18 meters down. The rag sits 0.08 meters right and 0.12 meters up from the rifle plus a wind offset. A flat box appears in front of the face when the map is raised. The monocular becomes a tube. The GPS unit is a small box on the left wrist when a waypoint is set.\n\nThe camera will jump to the airstrip when play begins. The player body will be moved to world feet each frame so it is no longer pinned. Input to the room body stays zero so physics does not fight the controller.\n\nThe `aim_view` function will drive the overlook camera. During play it sets the eye position and orientation to the player's world coordinates and stance angles. When not playing it preserves the title overlook but still copies yaw and clamps pitch so the title screen can glance around.\n\nThe overlook camera will use a stored title constant. It only overwrites the eye position when playing. This keeps the title view stable when exiting to the menu.\n\nA new ending screen will appear at Spec::Ending if the player has not yet chosen. It offers three options: burn the ledger, read the names, or take the chair.\n\nThe ending screen must be reachable from every route, including the human new game. Currently campaign() bakes a fixed ending into the script at build time, so tests that pass a specific route will fail if the player can choose later. The plan is to either share one script until the choice point, or make the final spec depend on the player's selection.\n\nThe bot must move the Ledger screen focus before confirming. Route::Read targets row 1, Route::Chair targets row 2, and all other routes default to row 0. The bot will use act 4 to move down and act 3 to move up until the correct row is selected.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-286d5de7-4c3a-4e35-9666-c6f0a47ad59c-115","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","offset":1,"limit":160}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-286d5de7-4c3a-4e35-9666-c6f0a47ad59c-116","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn shell_tick|act ==","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-286d5de7-4c3a-4e35-9666-c6f0a47ad59c-117","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ignite_flag|fn blow_tanks|WeaponId::","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10994,"output_tokens":1745,"cache_read_input_tokens":166656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"e1201bc6-4473-4945-b819-b3ed9dbdddbf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-286d5de7-4c3a-4e35-9666-c6f0a47ad59c-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! 10-foot shell. Every screen has at most seven focusable rows. Hover moves focus. Click confirms.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::world::{Screen, World};\\nuse crate::input::buttons;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→pub enum Device {\\n    Gamepad,\\n    Keyboard,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct MenuInput {\\n    pub up: bool,\\n    pub down: bool,\\n    pub left: bool,\\n20→    pub right: bool,\\n    pub confirm: bool,\\n    pub back: bool,\\n    pub pointer: Option<(f32, f32)>,\\n    pub click: bool,\\n    pub device: Option<Device>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for MenuInput {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n30→        Self { up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, confirm: false, back: false, pointer: None, click: false, device: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn glyph(action: &str, device: Device, xbox: bool) -> &'static str {\\n    match (device, xbox, action) {\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Enter\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Esc\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"LMB\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"RMB\\\",\\n40→        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"R\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"M\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Space\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Circle\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"B\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"Square\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"X\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"R2\\\",\\n50→        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"RT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"L2\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"LT\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"D-pad\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"Button\\\",\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n60→fn menu_of(input: &InputFrame) -> MenuInput {\\n    MenuInput {\\n        up: input.act == 3,\\n        down: input.act == 4,\\n        left: input.act == 5,\\n        right: input.act == 6,\\n        confirm: input.act == 1 || input.just(buttons::CONFIRM) || input.just(buttons::JUMP),\\n        back: input.act == 2,\\n        pointer: None,\\n        click: false,\\n70→        device: None,\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nimpl World {\\n    pub fn shell_tick(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\\n        let typed = input.pressed != 0\\n            || input.act != 0\\n            || input.look.length_squared() > 1e-8\\n            || input.move_dir.length_squared() > 1e-8;\\n80→        if typed && self.device_lock == 0 {\\n            // A pointer-only hover does not arrive through InputFrame. Keyboard buttons do.\\n            if input.pressed & (buttons::CONFIRM | buttons::JUMP | buttons::MAP | buttons::RELOAD) != 0 || input.act != 0 {\\n                self.device = Device::Keyboard;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n            if typed {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                self.focus = 0;\\n90→                self.idle = 0.0;\\n                self.attract_t = 0.0;\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            self.attract_t += dt;\\n            let seg = ((self.attract_t / 16.0) as u32) % 10;\\n            self.attract_seen |= 1u16 << seg;\\n            self.attract_loops = (self.attract_t / 160.0) as u32;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n100→        let shell = self.screen != Screen::Playing;\\n        if shell {\\n            if typed {\\n                self.idle = 0.0;\\n            } else if !self.hub {\\n                self.idle += dt;\\n            }\\n            if self.idle >= 10.0 && !self.hub {\\n                self.screen = Screen::Attract;\\n                return;\\n110→            }\\n            let mut m = menu_of(input);\\n            m.pointer = self.pointer.take();\\n            m.click = std::mem::take(&mut self.pointer_click);\\n            self.apply_menu(m);\\n            let _ = &mut m;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn apply_menu(&mut self, m: MenuInput) {\\n120→        if let Some(d) = m.device {\\n            self.device = d;\\n        }\\n        if self.screen == Screen::Playing || self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n            if m.confirm || m.back || m.up || m.down || m.click || m.pointer.is_some() {\\n                if self.screen == Screen::Attract {\\n                    self.screen = Screen::Title;\\n                    self.focus = 0;\\n                    self.idle = 0.0;\\n                    self.attract_t = 0.0;\\n130→                }\\n            }\\n            if self.screen != Screen::Title {\\n                return;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let n = self.rows().len();\\n        if n == 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n140→        if let Some((px, py)) = m.pointer {\\n            for i in 0..n {\\n                let y0 = 220.0 + i as f32 * 80.0;\\n                if px >= 160.0 && px <= 900.0 && py >= y0 && py <= y0 + 64.0 {\\n                    self.focus = i;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if m.up {\\n            self.focus = if self.focus == 0 { n - 1 } else { self.focus - 1 };\\n150→        }\\n        if m.down {\\n            self.focus = (self.focus + 1) % n;\\n        }\\n        self.focus = self.focus.min(n - 1);\\n        let activate = m.confirm || m.click;\\n        if m.left || m.right {\\n            self.nudge_slider(if m.right { 1.0 } else { -1.0 });\\n        }\\n        if m.back {\\n160→            self.go_back();\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! 10-foot shell. Every screen has at most seven focusable rows. Hover moves focus. Click confirms.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::world::{Screen, World};\\nuse crate::input::buttons;\\nuse crate::input::InputFrame;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n10→pub enum Device {\\n    Gamepad,\\n    Keyboard,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct MenuInput {\\n    pub up: bool,\\n    pub down: bool,\\n    pub left: bool,\\n20→    pub right: bool,\\n    pub confirm: bool,\\n    pub back: bool,\\n    pub pointer: Option<(f32, f32)>,\\n    pub click: bool,\\n    pub device: Option<Device>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for MenuInput {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n30→        Self { up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, confirm: false, back: false, pointer: None, click: false, device: None }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn glyph(action: &str, device: Device, xbox: bool) -> &'static str {\\n    match (device, xbox, action) {\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Enter\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Esc\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"fire\\\") => \\\"LMB\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"aim\\\") => \\\"RMB\\\",\\n40→        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"reload\\\") => \\\"R\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"map\\\") => \\\"M\\\",\\n        (Device::Keyboard, _, \\\"jump\\\") => \\\"Space\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"Cross\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"confirm\\\") => \\\"A\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"Circle\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, true, \\\"back\\\") => \\\"B\\\",\\n        (Device::Gamepad, false, 