{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_422","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`eye_pos()` already computes world position, height, and stance eye.\n\nThe camera ignores `eye_pos()`. I'll wire aim to it during play. The country view patch will update in `post()` when playing. I need to check if entity visuals are mutable. If not, I'll despawn and respawn the patch on cell moves. Colors rebuild only when the anchor cell changes. Positions update every frame. The `Screen` enum is in `world.rs`.\n\nAdding `Screen::Ledger` requires `rows()`, `activate()`, and `go_back()`. It only appears during endings. Debug formatting and dev tests are unaffected. The Ignite(k) bot currently presses PRIMARY for all keys except k==11 and k==10, since k==10 already fires in `script_ignite`.\n\n`begin(Spec::Ignite(k))` will equip the correct weapon for that beat. The flag must come from the shot, not `ignite_at` in `script_ignite`. Mapping: 0 flare, 1 rocket, 2 flamer, 3 mortar, 4 molotov, 5 frag, 6 barrel.\n\nThe barrel (kind 5) will be spawned for Ignite(6). It must be destroyed by a shot to trigger `ignite_barrel`. `blow_tanks` currently sets this flag when tanks die, so it should be removed from there. `Ignite(6)` will set the flag directly when a barrel is destroyed.\n\nVehicle ignition will damage the vehicle to stage 3 so the fuse counts down and marks `ignite_vehicle`. The bot fires at it. A burning person will be spawned for person ignition. The flag marks when a shot from an igniting weapon hits a body.\n\nLightning and cigarette ignitions are environmental, not weapon-based. Lightning requires the player to stand in open air for a step before striking, and only ignites if they are not on water. Cigarette is already handled by the bot pressing interact.\n\nLightning will be triggered by firing a flare into a storm. The bot holds PRIMARY for Ignite(10). The automatic tracer loop in script_ignite will be removed so the bot can fire manually instead.\n\nThe tracer ignition flag will be set whenever a rifle shot ignites the cell during Ignite(10), bypassing the 25% random chance. This ensures the test reliably triggers the flag without relying on repeated bot fire.\n\nThe 25% random chance for tracer ignitions is too risky for a deterministic test. The bot will fire manually at grassy cells during Ignite(10), marking the flag on every third shot that hits fuel. If the seeded RNG still misses, the bot will keep firing until the flag appears or the 30-second budget expires.\n\nThe tracer step will no longer force `ignite_at` at a dry spot. The bot fires manually instead, and every third shot during the step attempts ignition. If the random chance fails, the test will bump the probability only when the player has fired three or more rounds on that step.\n\nI need to inspect `Gun::pull` and the shots counter.\n\nFor Town, `begin` does not set position or mark `town_burned`. The bot drives or walks to Kilometre 40 and fires an igniting weapon. `town_burned` is set when a cell inside the town burns. The player's position after the convoy step must be checked, since the boat currently teleports them to water.\n\nIf the boat no longer teleports, the player will walk from the lodge at (-260, -700) to the nearest water. The closest river point is roughly 663 meters away. At 7 m/s this takes about 95 seconds. That leaves enough time within the 160-second boat budget. Town follows many steps.\n\nWithout boat teleportation, the player must walk from the airstrip to reach the town at (0, 380). The nearest reachable cell is (-40, 640), roughly 450 meters away and about 64 seconds at 7 m/s. Driving to (-520, -520) would take another 75 seconds. Bus travel to Junction (20, -420) then to (0, 380) is permitted. The Town budget should be raised to accommodate these longer journeys.\n\nBus travel will remain allowed. Night will simply set the clock and mark the flag when the player acts at night. Boat will spawn at the nearest water from the lodge, requiring a 95-second walk to board and drive 15 meters on deep water. The remaining steps are stealth, dart, repair, rain, better, companion, tape, ceasefire, and convoy.\n\nAfter the boat step, the player remains in the vehicle and does not disembark. Subsequent steps such as stealth therefore cannot move them off the boat, since `move_body` returns when `seat != 0`. The Town budget should be raised from 30 seconds to 120 seconds to cover the 64-second walk from the river to the town.\n\nThe Town step currently teleports the player to the town. If boat teleportation is removed, the player stays in the boat and never reaches the town. The Town bot spec uses interact, which does not move the player. I need to fix the Town bot so it can reach the town without teleporting.\n\nThe Town bot will exit the vehicle with USE if needed, walk to the town, and fire an igniting weapon inside the town radius. The town_burned flag is only set once fire actually burns within that radius.\n\nFor Night, begin will set the clock to 22:00 but not mark the night_contract flag. The bot will perform a small action such as moving or raising the map during the step so the flag is triggered by actual player behavior.\n\nThe previous Sleep step already advances time by 26 hours, so the Night step will naturally trigger the contract flag once the clock reaches night. This removes the need for a manual action during the Night step.\n\nThe Night step will force the clock to 22:00, but the night_contract flag will only be set after the player moves more than one meter. The Boat step will place the boat at the nearest water without moving the player; the bot will walk to it, use USE to enter, and then drive.\n\nThe USE key will only board a vehicle when the player is within six meters of it. Once already seated, switching seats or exiting remains unrestricted.\n\nThe Boat bot will walk to the boat when not already in it, then press USE to board. Once seated, it drives toward the next deep-water waypoint. The boat spawns on the river centerline, which is always deep enough for movement. When driving begins, the ride is replaced with a technical vehicle at the player's position.\n\nThe Boat begin logic will set the player's seat to 0 and spawn the boat at the nearest water cell. This forces the bot to walk to the boat rather than teleporting, since a technical vehicle from the Drive step would otherwise leave the player in seat 1.\n\nThe Town step will ensure the player has a Molotov by spawning one if they lack it, then fire it inside the town radius to trigger the burning flag.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e17899ff-5c1e-4397-ba97-c3d27173a340-121","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"self\\.slot|buttons::","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e17899ff-5c1e-4397-ba97-c3d27173a340-122","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub const","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e17899ff-5c1e-4397-ba97-c3d27173a340-123","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/gun.rs","offset":100,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4070,"output_tokens":3844,"cache_read_input_tokens":181760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"e3ae7737-c400-4e06-82dc-e1efb74879e0"}
