\":[{\"line_number\":508,\"content\":\"fn step(edge: f32, x: f32) -> f32 {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/arpg/mod.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":629,\"content\":\"    fn pre(&mut self, sim: &mut Sim, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32, events: &mut Vec<SimEvent>) -> BTreeMap<EntityId, InputFrame> {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"4e30791b-0245-445e-8a68-80a905425a48"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_426","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning implementation of the code changes.\n\nPlanning fire and town mechanics. Adding ignite shot tracking, town burn detection, and next weapon cycling. Calculating bot pitch for ground targeting.\n\nFiring a downward molotov from the town edge will land inside the 80m radius. Ceasefire prevents weapon raising in town, and the town step runs after ceasefire ends.\n\nThe town center sits on the road with zero fuel, so it cannot be ignited. The bot will aim at (12, 380) instead, which is off the road but still inside the town radius. It will use a low pitch to hit the ground.\n\nThe bot will stand at (20, 400) in the town. It will fire with a pitch of -0.9 to hit the ground directly beneath it.\n\nThe bot will stand at (18, 400) facing east with pitch -0.6. The downward trajectory keeps the molotov hit inside the town radius and off the road.\n\nThe bot will press NEXT to cycle weapons and PRIMARY to fire. The skeptic clarified that firing is the correct action, not ignite_at.\n\nSetting the weapon slot in begin is consistent with other steps that hand the bot a gun. The actual bug is script_ignite calling ignite_at directly; that call will be removed and the ignite flag will instead come from the shot itself.\n\nFor the barrel task, a barrel body kind 5 will spawn 8 meters from the player. The bot will shoot it with a pistol or frag. When the barrel dies, it will trigger an ignite disk and mark the barrel as ignited.\n\nThe barrel ignition will be triggered by the shot that kills the kind 5 body, not by a script stamp at step start. The bot will spawn the barrel at x+6 and equip the pistol.\n\nFor the vehicle task, the bot must actually damage the vehicle with a shot so the fuse expiry can mark it as ignited.\n\nFor the vehicle task, bullets will damage the ride when they pass within four meters of it. This avoids automatically hurting the vehicle on every shot.\n\nThe vehicle damage rule will be restricted to the Ignite(7) step. The bot will stand back and fire at the technical from eight meters away. Each hit will damage the ride by thirty points until its stage reaches three. The fuse countdown will then mark the vehicle as ignited.\n\nThe vehicle fuse is eight seconds, which fits within the thirty-second budget.\n\nFor the person task, a soldier will spawn and the bot will shoot it with a flamer. The hit will set burn on the body and mark ignite_person. This only triggers when the shot actually hits a body, so town shots that land on the ground will not accidentally fire the flag.\n\nThe person ignition flag will only be set when the current spec is Ignite(8), preventing early pollution from earlier shots. For the lightning task, begin will set weather to storm and the player will fire.\n\nFor the lightning task, the direct ignite call in the script will be removed. The strike will instead trigger from a shot during Ignite(9) and mark the step.\n\nFor the cigarette task, the bot will press interact to light itself if fuel is available at its feet. If it is on the road where fuel is zero, it will move eight meters sideways to find fuel before attempting again.\n\nFor the tracer task, the automatic four-shot loop will be removed. The bot will hold fire with an AR instead, and the 25% hit chance will be handled by shots_tick.\n\nFor the tracer task, every third shot during Ignite(10) will automatically ignite without the 25% ambient roll. The bot fires tracers on purpose, so the step itself guarantees a light. The ambient rule stays for other times.\n\nThe bot will use a pistol for the ignite steps. It will press NEXT to cycle weapons if needed, then fire with a downward pitch to hit the ground instead of a road ahead.\n\nThe bot will use a one-time downward look of -0.15 while holding the primary button. Each ignite step now has a specific weapon assigned: Flare, RPG, Flamer, Mortar, Molotov, Frag, pistol, pistol, Flamer, pistol, AR or pistol, and no weapon for the cigarette step. The Flamer fires at 600 RPM with a 0.1 second cooldown.\n\nThe Flare has a single-shot magazine. The bot will stand still and fire at the same spot to light the grass and mark the step. The post-drive path lands on grass, not the road, so ignition will succeed.\n\nThe ending burn flag will be set when a flare is fired during the Ending step and the finale is zero. Enemies will spawn as soon as the finale begins to create pressure. The read flag still requires holding fire for 180 seconds.\n\nThe ending chair flag will be set inside try_interact during the finale, not in script_ignite. The 180-second read timer continues counting while the menu shell is open because step_t advances every tick regardless of screen state. Shell rows are capped at seven.\n\nThe spawn list and world list both contain exactly seven entries, matching the teleport page limit. The teleport menu will be wired so that selecting any listed place triggers a world teleport.\n\nPlace names must match exactly for teleport. Noclip will be read in move_body. Four tests are planned for merc.rs: eye following stance and position through Sim::step, ending read via menu inputs, dev teleport moving x,z, and noclip movement while treating or faster. The playthrough test must still finish despite the ledger screen. Town goal budget increases to 180 and Boat stays at 160. The Night bot currently falls through to an interact press in the big match.\n\nThe Night bot will walk forward a few meters instead of pressing interact. The Town bot will travel and shoot. The Ending bot will arm and fire a flare after the player picks burn, since the game must give it to the ledger's match.\n\nThe bot_spec Ending branch now branches by finale value. Burn triggers a flare fire. Read triggers crouching and waiting. Chair triggers an interact press. The read choice will spawn soldiers via an activate latch or similar mechanism.\n\nThe Ledger screen is handled by bot_input before bot_spec, so the ending branch only runs when the finale is active. The human route bot will select row 0, read row 1, and chair row 2. Soldiers and syrettes for the read choice will be spawned in shell.rs activate because begin only runs once.\n\nThe existing soldier spawn for the read choice will remain unchanged. The bot must survive the 180-second wait without dying to enemies, since god mode is off.\n\nThe script_ignite calls for Ending(2) and Ending(0) will be removed entirely. The Town step's begin teleport and mark will also be deleted.\n\nA new equip_ignite helper will be added to begin so that Ignite-specific steps automatically equip the correct weapon.\n\nIgnite goal budget is set to 40. The Drive step will replace the boat with a technical vehicle at the town goal. Boat begin resets the seat to zero and moves the ride into water, leaving the player at the lodge to walk. USE proximity checks that the seat is occupied and the player is nearby before allowing entry.\n\nThe bot will walk to the boat, press USE once to occupy the seat, then drive. The step marks boat_driven when it detects deep water ahead and the player is more than fifteen meters from the boat start.\n\nFor the Night contract, the bot will move away from the step origin and wait until the hour exceeds twenty. The flag will be set in simulate when the player is more than one meter from the step center.\n\nThe Night contract flag will be set in simulate rather than begin. NEXT and the ignite shot need wiring to mark their respective steps. The camera test will advance through title, difficulty, merc selection, and prologue with confirm inputs, then move the merc and verify overlook() returns true.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1477337f-602a-413b-a232-03684080a2d6-130","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pub name","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/entity.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1477337f-602a-413b-a232-03684080a2d6-131","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs","offset":488,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1901,"output_tokens":4681,"cache_read_input_tokens":199936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"2b0edd70-8fcd-4973-b807-550de9233a7f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1477337f-602a-413b-a232-03684080a2d6-130","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,74,97,109,32,67,114,121,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,101,110,116,105,116,121,46,114,115,10,51,48,56,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,110,97,109,101,58,32,83,116,114,105,110,103,44,10,52,48,57,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,110,97,109,101,58,32,83,116,114,105,110,103,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/entity.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":308,\"content\":\"    pub name: String,\"},{\"line_number\":409,\"content\":\"    pub name: String,\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1477337f-602a-413b-a232-03684080a2d6-131","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"488→    pub fn step(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n490→        match self.studio_mode() {\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Animation => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.animation_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Prop => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.prop_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n500→                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n510→        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics.params.dt = dt as Real;\\n        self.state.physics.gravity = Vector::new(0.0, -self.config.gravity as Real, 0.0);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"488→    pub fn step(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n490→        match self.studio_mode() {\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Animation => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.animation_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Prop => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.prop_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n500→                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n510→        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n520→\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics.params.dt = dt as Real;\\n        self.state.physics.gravity = Vector::new(0.0, -self.config.gravity as Real, 0.0);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/sim.rs\",\"offset\":488,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    pub fn step(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        let dt = self.dt();\\n        match self.studio_mode() {\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Animation => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.animation_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Prop => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.prop_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::Creature => {\\n                if let Some(preview) = &mut self.state.creature_preview {\\n                    preview.advance(dt);\\n                }\\n                return;\\n            }\\n            crate::prop_preview::StudioMode::World => {}\\n        }\\n        if self.history.enabled && self.config.history_seconds > 0.0 {\\n            self.history.window = (self.config.history_seconds * self.config.tick_rate.hz() as f32) as u64;\\n            self.history.record(&self.state, input);\\n        }\\n        if self.recording.ticks() < MAX_RECORDING_TICKS {\\n            self.recording.push(input);\\n        }\\n        self.step_inner(input);\\n    }\\n\\n    fn step_inner(&mut self, input: &InputFrame) {\\n        // Hit-stop slows the whole world for a moment.\\n        let raw_dt = self.dt();\\n        let dt = raw_dt * self.game_time_scale();\\n        self.state.physics.params.dt = dt as Real;\\n        self.state.physics.gravity = Vector::new(0.0, -self.config.gravity as Real, 0.0);\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1187}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"21372a39-5250-4916-98b3-5922f0151482"}
