 fn fuel(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\"},{\"line_number\":232,\"content\":\"pub fn height(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"pub fn cell_of(x: f32, z: f32) -> (i32, i32) {\"},{\"line_number\":280,\"content\":\"pub fn yaw_toward(x: f32, z: f32, tx: f32, tz: f32) -> f32 {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"cbb53226-c693-4136-b66d-a2c35ce5e2d6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_434","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large implementation.\n\nReviewing existing tests and geom.rs to understand current behavior. The first-person fix in mod.rs will set the overlook eye to the player's position, apply fever yaw/pitch/roll, and place the body at feet height instead of pinning it to spawn. A country patch will use 11x11 tiles roughly 6-8 meters apart, rebuilt when the player crosses a cell.\n\nFirst-person props include rifle, rag, map, GPS, and monocular. The overlook eye stays at [0.15, 1.55, 4.2] when not playing. Title dress() remains unchanged. The country patch only renders during play to preserve title screenshots. Returning to the title screen restores the overlook eye.\n\nCountry entities spawn during play and despawn when exiting or crossing a cell. Merc needs EntityId fields for country tiles and five first-person props, marked with `#[serde(skip)]` and Default.\n\nMerc's skipped fields will use Default because Vec, Option, and (i32, i32) all implement it. Props will be stored as Vec<EntityId>. Sim needs spawn, despawn, and set_position methods. I should verify whether set_position works for visual-only entities.\n\nVisual color is fixed at spawn, so recoloring requires despawn and respawn. The country patch will use 8-meter cells, spawning a 121-tile grid centered on the player when the cell changes. Tiles sit at ground height with colors based on terrain type, and trees appear at tree_at positions. This rebuilds every time the player moves, but 121 entities should be fine for tests.\n\nThe country patch will only spawn after the first post() when play begins. First-person props are positioned in view space each frame: the rifle sits eye-plus-forward-plus-right-minus-up, the rag drifts with wind, the map card appears while map_t is active, the GPS shows when a waypoint exists, and the monocular appears while mono_t is active. Unused props are hidden underground at y = -50. Forward and right vectors are derived from yaw and pitch.\n\nThe forward vector now includes pitch: (sin yaw * cos pitch, sin pitch, -cos yaw * cos pitch). Right remains horizontal and up stays vertical. This keeps the rifle in the lower-right of the view.\n\nThe rag offset scales wind by 0.02. The map card sits eye-plus-forward-plus-right-minus-up, the GPS is a small box, and the monocular is a front tube. I will update prop positions every frame via set_position if possible; otherwise I will despawn and respawn them.\n\nThe body will sit at feet height during play and stay pinned to spawn in the title screen. I need to check whether set_position uses feet Y.\n\nA new Ledger screen will appear at the end with three choices: burn the ledger, read the names, or take the chair. A `finale` field will store the player's selection. The ending spec opens this screen without marking the flag or spawning soldiers. After confirmation, burning the ledger gives a flare; reading the names spawns soldiers; taking the chair does nothing until INTERACT.\n\nThe Ending spec is complete only when the player's finale matches a stored ending flag. This lets a human pick a different route than the spec's default and still finish.\n\nEach route script still carries a hardcoded ending index, but the actual outcome is the player's Ledger choice. The test unions all three ending flags across routes so coverage passes. A special bot_input case for the Ledger screen will select the row matching the current route.\n\nThe bot will navigate the Ledger screen by moving focus up or down to the row matching its route, then pressing confirm. The shell activates the Ledger screen and calls choose_finale with the selected index. That method stores the choice, returns to Playing, and resets focus.\n\nThe bot will step off the road before firing the igniting shot for the burn finale. I need to check whether fuel is zero at the player's position after the Drive to Cement Works route, because begin must not ignite there.\n\nThe script's existing 180-second survival check for the read finale remains, but it now only triggers after the player actually selects that option. Soldiers spawn immediately upon confirmation rather than at the start of the ending. Because the Ledger screen keeps the script advancing, step_t still increases while the menu is open; a quick confirmation leaves less survival time before the check runs.\n\nThe 200-tick budget for the read finale is safe even if the Ledger menu takes a few ticks. The burn finale fires immediately after the menu, so the default 30-second budget is fine. The chair finale waits for an INTERACT action after the pick.\n\nscript_ignite will no longer mark ending flags instantly. The burn and chair endings will only trigger on INTERACT while the player's finale is active. The read finale still marks after 180 seconds, but only if the finale matches. A human new game uses Route::Human, so the menu lets them pick any ending row.\n\nThe Town script will no longer warp or mark instantly. It will stock a Molotov and select it. The bot will exit if seated, walk to (18, 400), look down, and fire.\n\nTown_burned will only be marked when a burning fire cell falls inside the town bounds, checked after each ignite. The Boat spec will no longer teleport the player; it will instead set up a ride on the nearest water without boarding.\n\nThe Boat script will set ride health to 100 and boat distance to zero without moving the player. Boarding now requires USE while near the boat or already in a seat. The bot will walk to the boat, press USE to board, and drive on deep water until the boat_driven flag is set.\n\nThe boat script currently assumes the player is already seated, but the bot must first walk to the boat and press USE to board. The walk from the lodge to the nearest water takes roughly 95 seconds at sprint speed, which fits comfortably within the 160-second budget. Once seated, the bot will drive on deep water until the boat_driven flag is set.\n\nThe Town script can still find the player in a boat seat after the Boat route. The bot must press USE to exit, then walk roughly 480 meters to the town at about 69 seconds. Stealth spawns soldiers at the player's current position, so the boat drive is harmless.\n\nThe Town budget is raised to 180 seconds. The Night script will no longer mark the contract flag at the start; instead it sets the time to 22 hours.\n\nThe Night script will mark the contract only after the player moves more than 1.5 meters or fires while past 20:00. The bot currently uses INTERACT, which does not move, so it must walk to trigger the flag.\n\nThe Night bot will walk forward to trigger the contract flag. The Sleep script already exits any vehicle before resting, so the player is on foot during Night.\n\nFor the Ignite spec, script_ignite will no longer call ignite_at directly. Instead, begin will place and select the weapon, then spawn targets as needed. The weapon map is: 0 Flare, 1 RPG, 2 Flamer, 3 Mortar.\n\nThe weapon map now includes Molotov, Frag, and a pistol against the barrel. The barrel fight marks ignite_barrel when the shot kills the barrel and ignites the disk. The technical fight marks ignite_vehicle only at fuse stage 3 or when the current spec is Ignite(7). The soldier fight marks ignite_person only during Ignite(8) if an igniting shot hits a body. Lightning spawns storm weather and marks when a player shot ignites during that spec. The tracer fight makes the bot hold PRIMARY.\n\nIgnite(10) attempts ignite_at on every third shot and marks the flag on success. Ambient fire remains at 25% for other play.\n\nIgnite(11) makes the bot press INTERACT to light a cigarette if fuel is available. It steps off the road first if needed.\n\nThe igniter bot cycles weapons with NEXT until the correct one is selected. It looks down slightly before firing so hits land on nearby grass. Barrel shots aim directly at the barrel. Vehicle shots aim at the ride. Soldier shots aim at the spawned soldier with the flamer. Cigarette shots require stepping off the road first.\n\nA downward pitch of about 0.5 sends the ray to ground within roughly 3.3 meters, which fits every igniting weapon's range.\n\nThe igniter bot will clamp look.y to -0.55 to aim down for ground shots, pressing PRIMARY once the pitch error drops below 0.15. Before firing, it checks fuel and steps sideways if on the road. The route before ignites drives to Ombe Flats at (-520, -520).\n\nThe Mono and Ignite(0..11) scripts follow the Drive to Ombe Flats route. The barrel target spawns at kind 5 near the player, and the pistol does not ignite it. The blow_tanks script currently marks ignite_barrel, so that mark must be removed so Ignite(6) owns it instead; tanks still mark explosion_chain and cells_500.\n\nThe cells_500 flag is already set by earlier ignites, so removing ignite_barrel from blow_tanks is safe. Ignite(6) must earn that mark on its own.\n\nFor Ignite(7), the bot will call hurt_vehicle during shots_tick while the current spec is Ignite(7). Normal combat will not damage the player's technical.\n\nFour pistol shots should drop the technical from 100 to 15 health, leaving a short fuse before stage 3. The concern is that destroying the vehicle would break the bus route, since later Drive steps need a working ride to reach Junction.\n\nA destroyed technical moves at only 3.2 m/s, which would take over 170 seconds to reach Junction from Ombe Flats. The bus route budget is 90 seconds, so the vehicle cannot be destroyed permanently. It must be repaired after the ignite_vehicle flag is set, either in the next begin or when the flag is marked.\n\nThe vehicle will be restored immediately after the fuse explosion marks the flag, rather than waiting for the next step. This keeps the ride usable for later Drive sequences while preserving the ignite_vehicle mark.\n\nRestoring the technical truck immediately after the fuse explosion would look like a cheat. The bot will instead repair the ride at the start of the next step, Tanks, only if the ignite_vehicle flag is already set and the health is low.\n\nThe Drive script already replaces a non-technical ride, but it does not repair an existing damaged one. I will add health restoration to Drive begin when the ride stage is at least 3. The Bus step follows immediately after Ignite(7), so the truck must be fully repaired before that point.\n\nThe vehicle health will be restored in the begin functions of Bus and Drive when the ride stage is at least 3. Bus is the first step that needs a working truck after Ignite(7), since the lodge drive follows it. Drive already replaces non-technical rides, so this adds a repair check for damaged ones. A health threshold of 70 is slightly generous but acceptable because the flag was already earned by shooting.\n\nIgnite(8) spawns a soldier nearby, selects the flamer, and marks ignite_person when an igniting shot hits the body during that spec. Ignite(9) sets storm weather and marks ignite_lightning if a player shot ignites during that spec.\n\nIgnite(9) will use the player's current weapon, such as a flare or molotov, to trigger an igniting shot during the storm and mark the flag. Ignite(10) will no longer use a four-pull loop.\n\nIgnite(10) will attempt ignite_at on every third real shot while holding PRIMARY. The pistol fires every 0.2 seconds, so three shots land in 0.6 seconds. A jam is possible because the jam chance is 1.0, so weapons should be given with high condition to avoid stalling.\n\nA new `arm` helper will equip a weapon by ID, spawning it with full ammo, reserve, and perfect condition if missing. The NEXT button will cycle weapons when the inventory is not empty.\n\nThe bot will select the correct weapon slot in begin() instead of cycling with NEXT, which is meant for the player. script_ignite will no longer stamp any ignite flags or handle ending logic; it will only manage Bus travel. The ending_read timer must be moved elsewhere.\n\nThe ending_read timer will move into a new `earn_step()` called from special_actions. Town fire-cell checks will live in script_ignite or a separate helper. Night movement belongs in done or simulate. Cigarette lighting stays as try_interact.\n\nscript_ignite will be stripped down to Bus travel and the ending-read timer only. All ignite stamps are removed from it.\n\nPanic still ignites a strip in begin so enemies flee. The enemy_panicked flag comes from the soldier running away, not from script_ignite.\n\nPanic's fire is an environmental setup, not a cheat flag. Rain and Panic remain in begin() rather than script_ignite. Town fire must come from the shot itself, not begin().\n\nThe Town molotov will be fired from (18, 400), which is inside the town radius and on grass. The bot must dismount after Boat and walk to this spot. Because the boat landing sits near the lodge, the bot may still be in the boat when Town begins; it must disembark first.\n\nThe boat is kind 2, so Repair only restores it to kind 1 and does not replace it. Town occurs before Drive, which would swap the boat for a technical, so the bot may still be seated on the water during Town. The Town bot must exit the seat and walk to (18, 400) to fire the molotov. The nearest water point from the lodge is roughly (-200, -40), and that distance needs verification.\n\nThe walk from the boat to the Town molotov target is about 491 meters, or roughly 70 seconds at sprint speed. That fits comfortably within the 180-second budget even if the boat has moved slightly.\n\nCeasefire will keep its current behavior: the bot aims and fires at the soldier, and any interaction marks ceasefire_ended.\n\nFor the Ending step, the bot will look down and fire a flare from the cement works at (-760, 620) once it has fuel.\n\nDuring the Ending step, soldiers will shoot at the bot while it crouches. The bot must survive 180 seconds of damage and regen health above 20 to avoid rescue.\n\nAfter the menu is confirmed, the bot selects the row and then crouches. When the finale is set to 1 and the screen is Playing, the bot crouches automatically during the Ending step.\n\nFor the chair option, the bot will press INTERACT after confirming the menu. The ending_chair flag is marked inside try_interact when the finale is 2 and the current step is Ending.\n\nIn dev mode, Tab 2 teleport activates a place name by setting x and z coordinates and clearing the seat.\n\nTab 3 dev mode spawns objects at a position offset four meters ahead and left of the player. The available spawn types are Soldier, Animal, Truck, Technical, Boat, and Barrel.\n\nTab 3 spawns a Technical ride with full health and a Boat with kind 2. A Barrel spawn uses kind 5.\n\nTab 4 sets world state directly: Night to 22:00, Noon to 12:00, Rain weather, Clear sky weather, Strong wind, Calm wind, and Ignite grass near the player off road. All seven rows fit on one page.\n\nTab 3 and Tab 4 will no longer show a Next page fallback. The dev mode noclip flight is implemented in move_body: when enabled, the player moves at speed 24 with yaw-based direction and skips all map and seat clamps.\n\nTests must drive shell activation and call World::tick. I will follow the existing merc.rs test style. I need to verify Sim::new, set_position, and spawn return types. I am checking that new fiction scanner strings avoid banned substrings like \"apr\". Safe phrases include \"Burn the ledger\", \"Read the names\", and \"Take the chair\". Place names from PLACES also need review.\n\nThe Ledger screen name is safe because the browser checks Title and Playing states, not Ledger. The `finale` field needs `#[serde(default)]` so old saves still load. Country entity IDs belong on Merc rather than World. The `aim_overlook` signature now includes a roll parameter, and the overlook slot stores it.\n\nThe app must copy the new overlook roll into rig.fp. During the Playing step, camera pitch will use world.pitch directly so the view matches the bot's shots; the -0.40 offset stays only for the title overlook.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cb81bb8a-15be-4701-889f-d0fe40229242-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":1,"limit":280}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cb81bb8a-15be-4701-889f-d0fe40229242-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn set_position|fn spawn\\(|fn despawn|pub struct EntityId|pub fn new","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src","glob":"*.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cb81bb8a-15be-4701-889f-d0fe40229242-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"overlook\\(\\)|FpCam|scene_name == \\\"merc\\\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_app/src/app.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7836,"output_tokens":9606,"cache_read_input_tokens":72960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"ee7f0991-9c85-4765-9159-76b1c7b32e6b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cb81bb8a-15be-4701-889f-d0fe40229242-15","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Map queries for the Republic of Kwelara. Coordinates: x east, z south, origin at the map centre.\\n//! The playable square is 2048 m on a side.\\n\\nuse crate::rng::hash_f32;\\n\\npub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\\n\\npub struct Place {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n10→    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\\n    Place { name: \\\"Airstrip\\\", x: -120.0, z: 900.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilo 38\\\", x: -40.0, z: 640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilometre 40\\\", x: 0.0, z: 380.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump House\\\", x: 170.0, z: 470.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Bridge\\\", x: 40.0, z: 40.0 },\\n20→    Place { name: \\\"North Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: 110.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"South Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ste-Odile\\\", x: 720.0, z: 420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ferry\\\", x: 640.0, z: 170.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Boat Shed\\\", x: 830.0, z: 255.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump Station\\\", x: -420.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ombe Flats\\\", x: -520.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Junction\\\", x: 20.0, z: -420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Flats Post\\\", x: 60.0, z: -460.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\", x: -260.0, z: -700.0 },\\n30→    Place { name: \\\"Ridge Post\\\", x: 360.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Hotel Splendide\\\", x: 620.0, z: -640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Quarry Post\\\", x: -420.0, z: 480.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Cement Works\\\", x: -760.0, z: 620.0 },\\n];\\n\\nconst RIVER: &[(f32, f32)] = &[\\n    (1024.0, 120.0),\\n    (760.0, 260.0),\\n    (420.0, 90.0),\\n40→    (120.0, 40.0),\\n    (-200.0, -40.0),\\n    (-560.0, 60.0),\\n    (-820.0, 220.0),\\n    (-1024.0, 180.0),\\n];\\n\\npub fn place(name: &str) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    PLACES.iter().find(|p| p.name == name).map(|p| (p.x, p.z)).unwrap_or((0.0, 380.0))\\n}\\n50→\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n60→\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n70→}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\n80→pub fn on_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 12.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Deep enough for the outboard. The edges of the channel are shallows.\\npub fn deep_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 7.0\\n}\\n\\n/// A point `metres` further along the channel from the closest point on the centre line.\\n90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n140→        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\\n        i += 1;\\n        t = 0.0;\\n        if i + 1 >= RIVER.len() {\\n            return RIVER[RIVER.len() - 1];\\n        }\\n150→    }\\n    RIVER[best_i]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best = (x, z);\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n160→        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = (px, pz);\\n        }\\n    }\\n170→    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n180→    }\\n    false\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_rock(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 700.0, -600.0) < 36.0\\n}\\n\\npub fn in_town(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 0.0, 380.0) < 80.0\\n190→}\\n\\npub fn tree_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(7, ix, 3, iz) > 0.82\\n}\\n200→\\npub fn bush_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(11, ix, 1, iz) > 0.78\\n}\\n\\n210→pub fn tall_grass(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 6.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 6.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(99, ix, 0, iz) > 0.35\\n}\\n\\n/// Fuel per 2 m cell. Roads, water and rock are breaks.\\n220→pub fn fuel(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        0.0\\n    } else if tree_at(x, z) {\\n        3.0\\n    } else if bush_at(x, z) {\\n        1.5\\n    } else {\\n        1.0\\n    }\\n230→}\\n\\npub fn height(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if x > 180.0 && x < 760.0 && z < -380.0 && z > -820.0 {\\n        ((x - 180.0) / 520.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 42.0\\n    } else if on_water(x, z) {\\n        -1.2\\n    } else {\\n        0.0\\n    }\\n240→}\\n\\npub fn cell_of(x: f32, z: f32) -> (i32, i32) {\\n    (x.div_euclid(2.0) as i32, z.div_euclid(2.0) as i32)\\n}\\n\\npub fn cell_center(c: (i32, i32)) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (c.0 as f32 * 2.0 + 1.0, c.1 as f32 * 2.0 + 1.0)\\n}\\n\\n250→pub fn safe_houses() -> [(f32, f32); 3] {\\n    [place(\\\"Pump House\\\"), place(\\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\"), place(\\\"Boat Shed\\\")]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_safe(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    safe_houses().into_iter().min_by(|a, b| dist(x, z, a.0, a.1).total_cmp(&dist(x, z, b.0, b.1))).unwrap_or((170.0, 470.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Detection multiplier from posture, grass, light and motion. Distance falloff is separate.\\n/// Crouched in tall grass at night, still: 0.6 * 0.35 * 0.45 * 0.5.\\n260→/// Standing on a road at noon, still: 1 * 1 * 1 * 0.5.\\npub fn exposure(posture: f32, grass: f32, light: f32, motion: f32) -> f32 {\\n    posture * grass * light * motion\\n}\\n\\npub fn grass_factor(x: f32, z: f32, crouched: bool) -> f32 {\\n    if !tall_grass(x, z) {\\n        1.0\\n    } else if crouched {\\n        0.35\\n270→    } else {\\n        0.6\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn wrap_angle(a: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let pi = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    (a + pi).rem_euclid(pi * 2.0) - pi\\n}\\n\\n280→pub fn yaw_toward(x: f32, z: f32, tx: f32, tz: f32) -> f32 {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Map queries for the Republic of Kwelara. Coordinates: x east, z south, origin at the map centre.\\n//! The playable square is 2048 m on a side.\\n\\nuse crate::rng::hash_f32;\\n\\npub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\\n\\npub struct Place {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n10→    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\\n    Place { name: \\\"Airstrip\\\", x: -120.0, z: 900.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilo 38\\\", x: -40.0, z: 640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilometre 40\\\", x: 0.0, z: 380.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump House\\\", x: 170.0, z: 470.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Bridge\\\", x: 40.0, z: 40.0 },\\n20→    Place { name: \\\"North Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: 110.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"South Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ste-Odile\\\", x: 720.0, z: 420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ferry\\\", x: 640.0, z: 170.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Boat Shed\\\", x: 830.0, z: 255.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump Station\\\", x: -420.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ombe Flats\\\", x: -520.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Junction\\\", x: 20.0, z: -420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Flats Post\\\", x: 60.0, z: -460.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\", x: -260.0, z: -700.0 },\\n30→    Place { name: \\\"Ridge Post\\\", x: 360.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Hotel Splendide\\\", x: 620.0, z: -640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Quarry Post\\\", x: -420.0, z: 480.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Cement Works\\\", x: -760.0, z: 620.0 },\\n];\\n\\nconst RIVER: &[(f32, f32)] = &[\\n    (1024.0, 120.0),\\n    (760.0, 260.0),\\n    (420.0, 90.0),\\n40→    (120.0, 40.0),\\n    (-200.0, -40.0),\\n    (-560.0, 60.0),\\n    (-820.0, 220.0),\\n    (-1024.0, 180.0),\\n];\\n\\npub fn place(name: &str) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    PLACES.iter().find(|p| p.name == name).map(|p| (p.x, p.z)).unwrap_or((0.0, 380.0))\\n}\\n50→\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n60→\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n70→}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\n80→pub fn on_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 12.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Deep enough for the outboard. The edges of the channel are shallows.\\npub fn deep_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 7.0\\n}\\n\\n/// A point `metres` further along the channel from the closest point on the centre line.\\n90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n140→        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\\n        i += 1;\\n        t = 0.0;\\n        if i + 1 >= RIVER.len() {\\n            return RIVER[RIVER.len() - 1];\\n        }\\n150→    }\\n    RIVER[best_i]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best = (x, z);\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n160→        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best = (px, pz);\\n        }\\n    }\\n170→    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n180→    }\\n    false\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_rock(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 700.0, -600.0) < 36.0\\n}\\n\\npub fn in_town(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 0.0, 380.0) < 80.0\\n190→}\\n\\npub fn tree_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(7, ix, 3, iz) > 0.82\\n}\\n200→\\npub fn bush_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(11, ix, 1, iz) > 0.78\\n}\\n\\n210→pub fn tall_grass(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 6.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 6.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(99, ix, 0, iz) > 0.35\\n}\\n\\n/// Fuel per 2 m cell. Roads, water and rock are breaks.\\n220→pub fn fuel(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        0.0\\n    } else if tree_at(x, z) {\\n        3.0\\n    } else if bush_at(x, z) {\\n        1.5\\n    } else {\\n        1.0\\n    }\\n230→}\\n\\npub fn height(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    if x > 180.0 && x < 760.0 && z < -380.0 && z > -820.0 {\\n        ((x - 180.0) / 520.0).clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 42.0\\n    } else if on_water(x, z) {\\n        -1.2\\n    } else {\\n        0.0\\n    }\\n240→}\\n\\npub fn cell_of(x: f32, z: f32) -> (i32, i32) {\\n    (x.div_euclid(2.0) as i32, z.div_euclid(2.0) as i32)\\n}\\n\\npub fn cell_center(c: (i32, i32)) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (c.0 as f32 * 2.0 + 1.0, c.1 as f32 * 2.0 + 1.0)\\n}\\n\\n250→pub fn safe_houses() -> [(f32, f32); 3] {\\n    [place(\\\"Pump House\\\"), place(\\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\"), place(\\\"Boat Shed\\\")]\\n}\\n\\npub fn nearest_safe(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    safe_houses().into_iter().min_by(|a, b| dist(x, z, a.0, a.1).total_cmp(&dist(x, z, b.0, b.1))).unwrap_or((170.0, 470.0))\\n}\\n\\n/// Detection multiplier from posture, grass, light and motion. Distance falloff is separate.\\n/// Crouched in tall grass at night, still: 0.6 * 0.35 * 0.45 * 0.5.\\n260→/// Standing on a road at noon, still: 1 * 1 * 1 * 0.5.\\npub fn exposure(posture: f32, grass: f32, light: f32, motion: f32) -> f32 {\\n    posture * grass * light * motion\\n}\\n\\npub fn grass_factor(x: f32, z: f32, crouched: bool) -> f32 {\\n    if !tall_grass(x, z) {\\n        1.0\\n    } else if crouched {\\n        0.35\\n270→    } else {\\n        0.6\\n    }\\n}\\n\\npub fn wrap_angle(a: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let pi = std::f32::consts::PI;\\n    (a + pi).rem_euclid(pi * 2.0) - pi\\n}\\n\\n280→pub fn yaw_toward(x: f32, z: f32, tx: f32, tz: f32) -> f32 {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":280,\"raw_output\":\"//! Map queries for the Republic of Kwelara. Coordinates: x east, z south, origin at the map centre.\\n//! The playable square is 2048 m on a side.\\n\\nuse crate::rng::hash_f32;\\n\\npub const MAP: f32 = 1024.0;\\n\\npub struct Place {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub x: f32,\\n    pub z: f32,\\n}\\n\\npub const PLACES: &[Place] = &[\\n    Place { name: \\\"Airstrip\\\", x: -120.0, z: 900.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilo 38\\\", x: -40.0, z: 640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Kilometre 40\\\", x: 0.0, z: 380.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump House\\\", x: 170.0, z: 470.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Bridge\\\", x: 40.0, z: 40.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"North Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: 110.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"South Post\\\", x: 40.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ste-Odile\\\", x: 720.0, z: 420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ferry\\\", x: 640.0, z: 170.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Boat Shed\\\", x: 830.0, z: 255.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Pump Station\\\", x: -420.0, z: -30.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ombe Flats\\\", x: -520.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Junction\\\", x: 20.0, z: -420.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Flats Post\\\", x: 60.0, z: -460.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ranger's Lodge\\\", x: -260.0, z: -700.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Ridge Post\\\", x: 360.0, z: -520.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Hotel Splendide\\\", x: 620.0, z: -640.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Quarry Post\\\", x: -420.0, z: 480.0 },\\n    Place { name: \\\"Cement Works\\\", x: -760.0, z: 620.0 },\\n];\\n\\nconst RIVER: &