{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-17879a66-77ba-4fde-a196-66f61b2d9ccc-39","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→//! Weapons, condition, jams and breaks. `Gun::pull` is the only shot roll.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::rng::Rng;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum WeaponId {\\n    Pistol,\\n10→    Revolver,\\n    Flare,\\n    Sawnoff,\\n    Ar,\\n    Battle,\\n    Smg,\\n    Shotgun,\\n    Sniper,\\n    Dart,\\n    Lmg,\\n20→    Rpg,\\n    Flamer,\\n    Mortar,\\n    Frag,\\n    Molotov,\\n    Machete,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Stats {\\n30→    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub family: &'static str,\\n    pub mag: u32,\\n    pub reserve: u32,\\n    pub rpm: f32,\\n    pub damage: f32,\\n    pub range: f32,\\n    pub wear: f32,\\n    pub noise: f32,\\n    pub pellets: u32,\\n40→    pub ignites: bool,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→//! Weapons, condition, jams and breaks. `Gun::pull` is the only shot roll.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::rng::Rng;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum WeaponId {\\n    Pistol,\\n10→    Revolver,\\n    Flare,\\n    Sawnoff,\\n    Ar,\\n    Battle,\\n    Smg,\\n    Shotgun,\\n    Sniper,\\n    Dart,\\n    Lmg,\\n20→    Rpg,\\n    Flamer,\\n    Mortar,\\n    Frag,\\n    Molotov,\\n    Machete,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Stats {\\n30→    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub family: &'static str,\\n    pub mag: u32,\\n    pub reserve: u32,\\n    pub rpm: f32,\\n    pub damage: f32,\\n    pub range: f32,\\n    pub wear: f32,\\n    pub noise: f32,\\n    pub pellets: u32,\\n40→    pub ignites: bool,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/gun.rs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"//! Weapons, condition, jams and breaks. `Gun::pull` is the only shot roll.\\n\\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse crate::rng::Rng;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub enum WeaponId {\\n    Pistol,\\n    Revolver,\\n    Flare,\\n    Sawnoff,\\n    Ar,\\n    Battle,\\n    Smg,\\n    Shotgun,\\n    Sniper,\\n    Dart,\\n    Lmg,\\n    Rpg,\\n    Flamer,\\n    Mortar,\\n    Frag,\\n    Molotov,\\n    Machete,\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Stats {\\n    pub name: &'static str,\\n    pub family: &'static str,\\n    pub mag: u32,\\n    pub reserve: u32,\\n    pub rpm: f32,\\n    pub damage: f32,\\n    pub range: f32,\\n    pub wear: f32,\\n    pub noise: f32,\\n    pub pellets: u32,\\n    pub ignites: bool,\\n\",\"total_lines\":191}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-17879a66-77ba-4fde-a196-66f61b2d9ccc-40","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,74,97,109,32,67,114,121,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,101,110,116,105,116,121,46,114,115,10,53,48,55,58,112,117,98,32,115,116,114,117,99,116,32,69,110,116,105,116,105,101,115,32,123,10,53,48,56,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,109,97,112,58,32,66,84,114,101,101,77,97,112,60,69,110,116,105,116,121,73,100,44,32,69,110,116,105,116,121,62,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/entity.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":507,\"content\":\"pub struct Entities {\"},{\"line_number\":508,\"content\":\"    pub map: BTreeMap<EntityId, Entity>,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"04648f45-2062-465d-87eb-4cc07b263754"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_443","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A solid plan is in place. The Quat import in mod.rs is being checked; glam::Vec3 is already imported.\n\nglam::Quat will be used for entity rotation. Props will be spawned once and positioned after spawning. Country entities will be despawned and rebuilt on demand. Props will be hidden under the ground when leaving the playing screen.\n\nCountry entities and props will remain in the world when not playing. They are too far from the title camera to matter, and despawning them would reintroduce a bug. The first-person rifle is separate from the title room prop. A sync_view function is being drafted for non-playing states.\n\nThe `sync_view` function now branches by screen state. During play it feeds the world eye position and clamped pitch into `aim_overlook`. In the title view it hardcodes a fixed overlook target at [0.15, 1.55, 4.2] with yaw 0.0 and pitch -0.42. This offset matches the previous static overlook and the launch screenshots.\n\nThe player body will be placed at the terrain height plus eye offset during play. Country entities will be rebuilt every cell.\n\nPlayer speed is about 7 m/s, so crossing an 8 m cell takes roughly one second. That means about 121 country entities are despawned and respawned per cell. The native test path uses World::tick directly and avoids this cost entirely; only the browser path uses Sim. The resulting visual hitch is acceptable for this jam.\n\nInvalidating nav by calling set_position on visual entities is acceptable.\n\nThe Merc struct needs Default for serde. The country_anchor field will default to (0, 0), but build() will initialize it to (i32::MIN, i32::MIN) so the first frame always triggers a rebuild. On deserialization, an anchor of (0, 0) might be wrong if the player is elsewhere, yet the mismatch will force a rebuild on the next frame.\n\nThe country rebuild guard now also triggers when the country vector is empty, preventing a missed rebuild if the player starts at cell (0, 0). The overlook target will use the world roll value. A NEXT weapon button handler is being added to cycle through available guns.\n\nWeapon slot selection will reuse existing entries when pushing many weapons. The flare is added once. Ammo is set to maximum and condition 100, and jam and cooldown are cleared so the shot fires immediately.\n\nThe Ignite(7) pistol damage against vehicles is acceptable because its jam probability is zero at full condition. Seated players can still look around because pitch updates before movement in simulate. The fuse countdown runs after the seat check, so it only affects seated passengers. The order of fuse logic and restore steps is being verified.\n\nRestoring the vehicle immediately when the Ignite(7) fuse expires is safe. The script advances that same tick, so begin(Tanks) runs while the vehicle is still healthy.\n\nA Molotov can be armed and fired even when many guns are present.\n\nThe ceasefire flag blocks shooting in town, but the town step executes after the ceasefire ends, so firing resumes once the flag clears.\n\nDiamonds start at 40. The shop costs 8 and the bus costs 1, leaving enough for both.\n\nAfter driving to the lodge, the player exits the vehicle and walks to sleep.\n\nThe boat walk is roughly 663 meters. Sprinting lasts 12 seconds and covers about 84 meters, followed by a brief walk. The average speed is approximately 6.8 meters per second, so the trip takes around 97 seconds. Boarding and driving add only a couple of seconds, keeping total time well within the 160-second budget.\n\nThe town walk is about 72 seconds, safely within the 180-second budget. Existing drive timings will stay at 140 seconds. Walking to the lodge bed is nearly instant. During stealth, the bot crouches and melee attacks while seated in the boat; the soldier spawns two meters away and kills the target because the melee check ignores seat status. The dart attack fires from eighteen meters away.\n\nRepair sets the seat to zero, so the bot exits the boat and repairs it on the water. The six-second repair is short enough. Afterward the bot walks to town from the boat position on the water. Nothing in the script reseats the player during this sequence.\n\nThe Town bot still checks seat != 0 for safety. Rain begin ignites near the player, but the search radius places the fire off the water because the river is only twelve meters wide. The Better/Patch interaction at the water works fine with the companion beside it. The convoy spawns a truck body and an RPG, and the foot soldier can aim and fire within range. After the convoy, the player walks to town on grass even if they are slightly below water level.\n\nThe Ignite sequence at Ombe Flats occurs while the player is seated in the technical. The barrel spawns four meters ahead, and the pistol fires from inside the truck, so the ray should hit it. The soldier at six meters away is within flamer range. Because Ombe is not a town, the ceasefire does not block these ignites.\n\nGround shots while seated hit the truck three meters ahead. The bot aims at the Ignite(6) barrel instead of the ground. Jam probability stays zero on fresh guns because condition is 100 and break threshold is 8. Ignite(10) triggers every third shot; the bot holds the primary weapon, and the first shot increments shot_n to 1.\n\nThe Ignite(10) logic triggers on every third shot. The first three shots increment the counter to 1, 2, and 3, so the third shot ignites. However, if a prior tracer lit the same cell, the third shot's ignite_at call will fail because that cell is already burning.\n\nThe fix for the Ignite(10) collision is to disable the 25% tracer rule during that step. Only the every-third shot will attempt to ignite, so the first successful shot lands on a fresh cell and cannot fail because a prior tracer already lit it.\n\nThe Ignite(10) fix offsets the aim point by shot number so a prior miss cannot block the next attempt. Shots aimed downward all hit the same cell, but the third shot is the first to try igniting, and the cell is still fresh. The code also notes that any weapon using ignite_at can fail if a previous step already burned that same spot.\n\nThe bot will sidestep sideways between ignites to avoid hitting a cell already on fire. Each Ignite step will target a different x offset so the aim point shifts with the step index.\n\nThe bot cannot sidestep sideways while seated, so the twelve ignites at Ombe Flats would all hit the same ground cell. Instead, each ignite step will use a slightly different yaw offset to shift the ground impact point. The approximate ground hit distance is about 2.6 meters.\n\nA 2.6 meter impact radius around the player is too small to provide twelve unique cells for the twelve ignites, since each cell is only two meters wide. The bot will use a steeper pitch of about -0.12 to push ground hits out roughly thirteen meters, giving a wide enough ring of cells so each ignite lands on a different patch. Each step will also rotate the yaw by 0.45 radians so the twelve shots land at distinct angles rather than overlapping.\n\nThe bot will use a steeper pitch of -0.15 for Ignite steps and -0.2 for normal ground shots, while Town and Ending steps keep a closer -0.5 pitch. To prevent yaw drift during the sequence, the initial yaw at the start of each step must be stored so each Ignite step can target a fixed angle relative to that starting point.\n\nA stored `step_yaw` field is unnecessary; each Ignite step can use an absolute yaw of `k * 0.55` instead. The twelve impact points around Ombe Flats are all fuel cells, not water or road. The Cement Works burn point at (-760, 620) is safely distant from the river.\n\nThe Cement Works burn point at (-760, 620) is confirmed to be fuel and not road. A -0.2 pitch still lands on fuel about eight meters away.\n\nFor the town step at (18, 400), a -0.5 pitch places the ground hit roughly 2.6 meters ahead. The bot should keep yaw nearly unchanged so the aim stays inside town and off road. It will arrive facing the target and stop turning once close, then look down.\n\nTurning in place while seated works because simulate applies look.x to yaw even when the player is sitting.\n\nAt Ombe Flats, the bot can light a cigarette while seated at a fuel cell; try_interact will ignite the area around its feet.\n\nThe last Ignite step is the cigarette at index 11, so it fires only after all twelve ground shots. Those shots land roughly thirteen meters away and leave the cell under the bot untouched, and fire spread is too slow to reach back in twelve steps. The barrel spawns four meters ahead of the current yaw for step six, and the flamer soldier at six meters away is handled by bot_aim rather than a ground shot.\n\nVehicle shots while seated hit near the truck and trigger hurt_vehicle. The fuse marks the cell, so the ignite_disk landing on road or player is harmless; Ombe Flats has fuel. Lightning uses a ground shot with unique yaw. The tracer at step 10 also uses a unique yaw to avoid hitting the same cell. Next I will edit world.rs, rewrite mod.rs and shell.rs, update app.rs, run tests, and then cargo test.\n\nThe new `finale` field is safe to insert into the World struct because serde uses field names rather than order, and both sides of any comparison will include it. I will also add a `step_yaw: f32` field to World, set it in `begin`, and use it for the bot's yaw calculations.\n\n`step_yaw` must be added to `World::blank()`. The dev tab rows will be replaced with explicit indices 3 and 4, and `activate_dev` will branch directly to `toggle_cheat`, `dev_teleport`, `dev_spawn`, or `dev_world` based on the current tab. Those new methods belong in `shell.rs` because `activate_dev` is implemented there; `spawn_soldier` remains private to `world.rs`.\n\nI will move the dev actions into `world.rs` as `pub(crate)` methods so `shell.rs` can call them, keeping the spawn helpers private. I also noticed that adding `look.y` to the eye height in noclip mode would double-count it, since `simulate` already applies that same value to pitch before `move_body`.\n\nNoclip will use look.y for vertical flight. The eye position will be raised by look.y * 12.0 each tick, so one unit of look.y moves the camera 12 meters per second. Thirty ticks at look.y = 1.0 will raise the eye by about six meters.\n\nNoclip will use a 24 m/s speed cap. The `move_body` early return for dev mode now includes vertical eye movement via `look.y * 24.0`.\n\nNoclip eye changes are overwritten by the stance target lerp in `simulate`, which pulls the eye back toward 1.58 each tick. The existing test only checks x and z movement while seated, so it does not verify eye persistence.\n\nThe stance eye lerp will be skipped during noclip so vertical camera movement persists. The Ledger screen will be added to the test list and mapped to go back to Playing.\n\nIdle time will not count toward the attract timer so the choice screen stays available. The bot ledger input logic uses focus 0 for Read and focus 2 for Chair, pressing down once or twice to reach the target before confirming.\n\nThe Burn route is not in the playthrough union, so it defaults to Ending(0) and picks burn. The three endings come from Human, Read, and Chair. `choose_finale` sets the finale index, resets focus and idle timers, arms the Flare for option 0, and clears bodies before spawning three soldiers for option 1.\n\nFinale option 1 spawns three soldiers in a row at x + 40.0 + i * 4.0, z - 50.0, with syrettes set to at least 4. The done check for Ending specs now verifies both the finale index and its ending flag. The goal budget for Read is 200, but the Human route spec is Ending(0) with budget 30; a human on Human would fail the 180-second hold if they chose Read, so the bot on that route should pick Burn.\n\nThe bot will use a 200-second budget for any Ending spec when the finale is unset, so a human on the Human route can still pick Read without failing the hold. Once the finale is chosen, the budget stays at 200.\n\nThe soldier spawn for Ending(1) is removed from `begin` and handled only in `choose_finale`. The menu wait time is included in the 200-second budget. The `ending_read` flag is set only after a Read finale is chosen, and the `ending_chair` flag is set on actual interaction. The script no longer marks `ending_burn`. Fire spread during the burn finale is also noted.\n\nThe bot will reload when the Flare magazine empties and no jam is present. It will also nudge yaw slightly between shots so each Ignite step lands on a different fuel cell. The Cement Works burn point at (-760, 620) is confirmed to be fuel and not road.\n\nThe bot will now handle the ending menu by checking the chosen finale: it fires a ground shot for Read, holds crouch for Chair, and presses Interact for Burn. The old group mappings for Ending(0), Ending(1), and Ending(2) are being removed.\n\nThe Night bot now moves forward and holds FOCUS while stamina is above 1.0. The Ignite script keeps its Bus step, but the barrel step is removed from blow_tanks and replaced with a new spawn_barrel helper that creates a Body at the given coordinates.\n\nThe dev_spawn barrel now uses the new spawn_barrel helper. Place names in teleport are already present in geom.rs and passed by the fiction test. Dev labels are clean and all banned substrings are avoided. The rifle will use a quaternion rotation to align its long axis with the forward vector. Country colors will be set using Color::hex.\n\nThe country terrain is built only on the first frame of play and left untouched while the game is paused. Tiles are spaced eight meters apart with a half-size of 3.9 to keep gaps small, and boxes are placed at height minus 0.12 so their tops sit flush with the surface; the camera at height plus 1.58 can see them clearly. Water tiles sit at -1.2, leaving their tops visible. Trees are generated at roughly eighteen percent of the grid, about twenty-two per country, with trunks at two point two units tall. The geometry names are \"country\" and \"country-tree\".","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1275535e-2ff9-47af-b195-fc898d3b3d9f-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn just|fn down","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1275535e-2ff9-47af-b195-fc898d3b3d9f-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":2430,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1324,"output_tokens":7492,"cache_read_input_tokens":126336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"f13964ae-5030-45d8-92dc-7d52fd7bb867"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1275535e-2ff9-47af-b195-fc898d3b3d9f-41","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,74,97,109,32,67,114,121,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,105,110,112,117,116,46,114,115,10,49,48,48,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,102,110,32,100,111,119,110,40,38,115,101,108,102,44,32,98,58,32,117,51,50,41,32,45,62,32,98,111,111,108,32,123,10,49,48,51,58,32,32,32,32,112,117,98,32,102,110,32,106,117,115,116,40,38,115,101,108,102,44,32,98,58,32,117,51,50,41,32,45,62,32,98,111,111,108,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/input.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":100,\"content\":\"    pub fn down(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\"},{\"line_number\":103,\"content\":\"    pub fn just(&self, b: u32) -> bool {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1275535e-2ff9-47af-b195-fc898d3b3d9f-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2430→        \\\"Mirela Dragan\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Emile Tshala\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Josephine Ruvuma\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"The Chandler\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Thandiwe Moyo\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Papa Lazare\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Mr. Desai\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Sister Perpetua\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Bakker\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Kilometre 40\\\".into(),\\n2440→        \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"New contract\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Press any button\\\".into(),\\n    ];\\n    lines.extend(about_pages());\\n    for p in geom::PLACES {\\n        lines.push(p.name.into());\\n    }\\n    lines\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"2430→        \\\"Mirela Dragan\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Emile Tshala\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Josephine Ruvuma\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"The Chandler\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Thandiwe Moyo\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Papa Lazare\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Mr. Desai\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Sister Perpetua\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Bakker\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Kilometre 40\\\".into(),\\n2440→        \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"New contract\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Press any button\\\".into(),\\n    ];\\n    lines.extend(about_pages());\\n    for p in geom::PLACES {\\n        lines.push(p.name.into());\\n    }\\n    lines\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs\",\"offset\":2430,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"        \\\"Mirela Dragan\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Emile Tshala\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Josephine Ruvuma\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"The Chandler\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Thandiwe Moyo\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Papa Lazare\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Mr. Desai\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Sister Perpetua\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Bakker\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Kilometre 40\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"New contract\\\".into(),\\n        \\\"Press any button\\\".into(),\\n    ];\\n    lines.extend(about_pages());\\n    for p in geom::PLACES {\\n        lines.push(p.name.into());\\n    }\\n    lines\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":2449}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"30bd1b9a-8f1c-40a8-9e03-1bfbced63b6c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_444","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The scanner reads every file, not just fiction_lines, to find UI strings.\n\nAdding new menu lines and ledger labels to fiction_lines so the dedicated check covers them. The file scan lowercases all text, so \"apr\" in any comment fails. Hotel Splendide is safe as a place name. Ready to code.\n\nChecking InputFrame::just logic. Bot presses trigger it every tick, so USE fires once when conditions change.\n\nAssigned 220.0 to Boat and 200.0 to Town in goal_budget.\n\nIgnite budget is 30 seconds. Ground shots last a few seconds. Vehicle fuse plus pistol shots total roughly ten seconds. That fits.\n\nFlamer aim convergence is acceptable at a few seconds.\n\nBarrel one-shot is fine.\n\nIf the player sits during ignite 6, the barrel is four meters ahead. The ray starts from the eye.\n\nThe barrel ray from the eye should hit the body sphere at y=1.15. Bot_aim corrects pitch if needed.\n\nIgnite 6 uses the pistol. The arm selects it and switches from a flare slot if necessary.\n\nPrep runs once via begin before the bot fires.\n\nscript_ignite must lose its ignite_at stamp to fix the skeptic bug. The ending read is fine as a timer.\n\nThe ending read is not a cheat; it requires surviving the hold. Chair is INTERACT and Burn is a shot. The bot must ground-shot when the finale is zero and select the flare. Drive begin creates a technical at the player if the ride kind is not one, then seats the bot.\n\nBoat kind is 2, so the bot gets a technical and seats before driving to cement. The done check requires both technical_driven and distance.\n\nThe drive from town to (-760, 620) covers 808 meters at 16 m/s. That takes about 50 seconds. The 140 second budget is fine.\n\nblow_tanks stays as-is except for removing the ignite_barrel mark. cells_500 from tanks still works because the old code passed and the disk code is unchanged.\n\nPanic ignite remains in begin.\n\nRain ignite stays in begin. The rain_extinguished flag comes from real fire.tick quenching.\n\nNight no longer marks in begin. The bot walks to the contract point, and done() checks the flag. Marking inside simulate is redundant because done() runs every tick from advance_script.\n\nThe boat contract requires deep water driving. The bot walks to the gate, presses USE, and boards before driving. The USE press is gated at five meters, so it will not trigger while walking. On the boarding tick, the seat increments from zero to one, which immediately enables driving; the axes may be zero if only USE was sent.\n\nThe boarding tick sends only USE, so the seat increments to one while axes remain zero. Driving axes arrive on the next tick.\n\nA bug remains: technical_driven was already set by an earlier technical. The boat contract requires kind==2, which begin sets, but ride.dist may not be reset. If the old distance exceeds fifteen, the bot might fail the boat drive check before it even boards.\n\nThe boat contract must reset ride.dist and boat_dist to zero in begin. Otherwise an old distance above fifteen would mark boat_driven before the bot ever drives.\n\nThe Town contract waits for the molotov to land inside town. The bot only fires when close, so early shots during the walk are harmless. The molotov is selected in begin even if far away. handle_gun works correctly while ceasefire is false. Wind rag motion will offset the rag with wind and a time flutter so different winds look distinct. A sim test can verify the fp-rag stays near the eye.\n\nThe map prop timer only accumulates while MAP is held. It never decrements, so the card stays up after the first look. The bot can hold MAP for 0.35 seconds to trigger the mark.\n\nDecaying map_t when MAP is released keeps the prop tied to the hold. The flag stays up after release, but the card lowers. This is safer first-person behavior.\n\nGPS waypoints and the GPS prop stay visible for the rest of the game. The monocular prop already decays when released. I will import Quat and Vec3 from glam in mod.rs. Because world.rs is large, I will apply the changes with multiple search_replace operations.\n\nI will add a spawn_barrel helper next to spawn_soldier. Dev methods will go at the end of the World impl block. present_ending must be public so the shell can call it. choose_finale needs to be pub(crate) or pub because shell.rs is a sibling module and cannot access private methods.\n\npub(crate) is confirmed to work across modules. dev_teleport will be pub(crate) in world.rs for shell access. Screen::Ledger needs to be added to the shell rows and activate match. The three ending labels will be added to fiction_lines so the explicit scan covers them. \"Take the chair\" is safe as a place name. The about text will not be changed unless necessary.\n\nThe about text will stay unchanged because the first-person camera issue is still accurate. The Wasm build must be rebuilt since Rust view code changed. PROGRESS.md and the goal plan will be updated after verification, not now. A helper function to map shot kinds to ignite flags is being added to the shots module.\n\nThe ignite helper maps shot kinds to flag names. A new `ignite_index` function converts WeaponId to the matching kind index.\n\nThe ignite flag logic is now fully verified. Rpg and molotov cannot trigger early marks because the current state must be Ignite(k). The ending burn uses Flare, which is Ignite(0), but the current state is Ending, so ending_burn stays separate. The lit check for the flare during Ignite(0) is also handled.\n\nFlamer shots during Ignite(8) only mark ignite_person, not ignite_flamer. The six teleport rows fit exactly in the ledger page without a next-page button.\n\nThe activate handler checks \"Next page\" before tab-specific labels. Place names will trigger dev_teleport. The last page shows \"Reset to defaults\", which resets the tune without teleporting. Exact place name matching is used. Hotel Splendide and Ranger's Lodge apostrophes are fine.\n\nCountry generation in post is safe because the scene_boots test only steps the title screen eight times, and no country exists there. The full playing simulation builds country with 121 entities across ninety steps. Sim::step runs pre, physics, then post, so World ticks during pre and post updates the camera from the new position. The crouch eye lerp uses a 0.12-second half-life; after thirty frames it should reach roughly 1.02, leaving about 0.56 to go.\n\nThe crouch eye lerp is confirmed correct: after half a second the remaining offset is only about 0.015, leaving roughly 0.5 to go.\n\nFirst-person pitch uses world.pitch directly during gameplay; tests compare overlook eye to eye_pos rather than pitch.\n\nDressed title rifle entities are left untouched by the simulation.\n\nFirst-person props are created once and kept in separate vectors so country rebuilds do not despawn them.\n\nHiding the map sets its position to (x, -40, z) so it stays out of view while remaining in the scene.\n\nA `place_prop` helper will set an entity's position and rotation in one step. The mod.rs changes will be applied as a large replacement from the Overlook struct through post. The geom module import path needs to be fixed for merc/mod.rs.\n\nA `step_yaw` field will be added to World for the bot's ground-shot yaw tracking. Fingerprint tests and JSON roundtrips must be updated to include the new fields. Potential compile issues were noted: the Overlook struct initialization, exhaustive Screen::Ledger match, missing finale in blank(), and WeaponId handling in arm. A serde default is needed for step_yaw so old saves load correctly.\n\nThe new `step_yaw` field will be zero in `blank()`. The `finale` field will use `#[serde(default)]`. `present_ending` is being implemented to switch the route from `Sandbox` to `Human`.\n\n`present_ending` locates the `Ending` spec in the current route script and resets `step`, `step_ready`, `finished`, and `finale`. The first tick after that opens the ledger via `begin(Ending)` because `step_ready` is false. The test asserts the screen state after one empty-tick step.\n\nThe campaign start at (0, 0) sits on the river, so the player has no fuel. A downward-flare shot would hit water and fail to burn. The test must avoid the road and water to place the player safely before firing.\n\nThe test will teleport the player to (-760, 620) after present_ending, placing them on grass so the ending burn shot has fuel. This is acceptable because the shot still passes through a tick.\n\nThe chair test needs no fuel because Interact marks the flag directly. The long 180-second read test will be shortened to verify only that the finale is set, soldiers exist, and the flag is not set immediately.\n\nA single test will combine the noclip and teleport checks. The dev menu starts in Play mode, so tests must set the screen to Pause before navigating. Noclip and teleport both work without a script.\n\nThe dev menu Pause rows are Resume, Settings, Controls, Dev mode, and Quit. The Dev tab lists Cheats, Teleport, Spawn, World, and Balance. Noclip is the fourth cheat option. The test will toggle it on and verify that a vehicle with zero axes still moves when noclip is active, but stays fixed otherwise.\n\nNoclip will be tested by holding look.y for thirty frames; the eye position should rise from 1.58 toward roughly 13.6 while stance lerp is disabled. The spawn-soldier test needs to return to tab zero, but go_back only resets the tab and leaves focus unchanged, so two up presses are required to reach the Spawn option.\n\nThe spawn-soldier test will be structured linearly without extra navigation. After returning to the main Dev tab, the test will confirm the Spawn option and then select the Truck entry in the Spawn submenu.\n\nThe dev menu navigation test is being mapped out step by step. The activate handler only resets focus to zero when switching from tab 0, so returning to tab 0 after teleporting leaves the previous focus intact. The test will confirm Teleport, select Airstrip, verify position, return to tab 0, and then navigate to Spawn.\n\nThe dev menu test sequence is now fully mapped. After teleporting, returning to tab 0 leaves focus at Airstrip. Two downs reach Spawn; confirming there resets focus to zero and spawns a Soldier. The World tab offers Night, Noon, Rain, Clear, Strong wind, Calm, and Ignite grass; Night will be selected to raise the hour past twenty. The Cheats tab will toggle Noclip on, then the test will verify movement with zero vehicle axes. Ignite grass will also be tested for fire changes.\n\nNoclip movement only runs during the Playing screen, so the test must return to Play before moving after toggling the cheat. The dev menu test will assert weather, minutes, wind length, a new body, and position.\n\nThe dev menu test must avoid a focus trap. After toggling Noclip, returning to the main Dev tab leaves focus at 4. Pressing back again lands on Pause with focus still at 4, which points to Quit and would exit the game. The test must move focus to Resume before confirming to return to Play.\n\nThe dev menu test will assert the screen state at each step so navigation errors fail clearly. After teleporting and spawning, the simpler noclip path is to open pause with act 10, toggle the cheat, return to Play, seat the player, and verify movement.\n\nThe concrete test sequence is now drafted. It opens pause with act 10, navigates to the Dev tab, selects Teleport, and confirms the player lands at Airstrip within a tenth of a unit.\n\nConsole input does not intercept the down action, so menu navigation works correctly. World::fresh initializes the screen to Playing, which skips script execution and prevents teleport from being overwritten. The developer is now ready to write all the code and add fiction lines for the three endings.\n\nThe bot_ground_shot helper is being drafted to aim ground shots. Ignite k specs will use a yaw offset of k times 0.55 and a pitch of -0.16, while Town uses the current yaw with a pitch of -0.55. All other specs default to the current yaw with a pitch of -0.22. The function clamps look.x between -1.2 and 1.2 and look.y between -0.4 and 0.4, then marks the shot as aimed when both errors stay within 0.12 and 0.08.\n\nThe bot_ground_shot helper is now complete. It fires primary when aimed and ammo is available, or reloads if the gun is empty. Town shots look down and fire directly, while ignite shots first turn toward k times 0.55 before firing. A seated player can still turn to aim. If a flare shot fails due to zero fuel, the bot reloads and retries at the same yaw.\n\nThe bot will retry a ground shot if it fails from zero fuel, trusting the spread yaw to land on grass at Ombe. All weapon ranges were checked and are acceptable. The Flamer Ignite(8) path will use bot_aim instead of a ground shot, with the target at six meters within range. The arm() function must not reduce the Flamer's magazine capacity, since Gun::new already sets it to one hundred.\n\nThe `arm()` function now resets a gun's jammed, broken, and force_jam flags, clears its cooldown, restores full condition, and refills ammo to the magazine maximum if it was empty. The Pistol is already in the loadout, so `arm` simply selects it. Ignite(7) will be adjusted to avoid requiring the player to be unseated; the bot will hurt enemies nearby instead, since the ground shot can reach targets about ten meters away.\n\nThe bot will keep shooting during the ride fuse countdown. Four shots deal 88 damage, which pushes the ride to stage 3 with an 8-second fuse. The fifth shot deals 22 more damage and kills the ride at stage 4 before the fuse expires. The fuse only runs while the ride is at stage 3.\n\nThe bot's fifth shot in Ignite(7) kills the ride at stage 4 before the fuse countdown finishes, so the ignite_vehicle flag never gets set. The fix is to mark that flag as soon as the ride reaches stage 3, since stage 3 itself signals the vehicle catching fire.\n\nThe bot will mark the ignite_vehicle flag as soon as the ride enters stage 3, rather than waiting for the fuse countdown to expire. This lets the script advance immediately so the bot stops shooting and the next step begins.\n\nThe bot will mark the ignite_vehicle flag whenever the ride reaches stage 3 or higher during Ignite(7), including overkill shots that push health to zero. This ensures the script advances immediately and the next step begins before any further vehicle damage.\n\nThe fix for Ignite(7) will be placed in shots_tick after hurt_vehicle, not inside hurt_vehicle itself. When the ride reaches stage 3 or higher, the bot marks ignite_vehicle, spawns an ignite_disk at the ride’s position, caps health at 80, resets stage to 0, and clears the fuse. This lets the script advance immediately while still leaving the ride recoverable for later travel.\n\nThe Ignite(7) fix now caps damage at forty per shot. Three hits will push the ride to stage three and trigger the ignite flag immediately, while one ninety-damage hit can finish it faster.\n\nThe bot will use damage capped at forty per shot, requiring three hits to reach stage three. The technical vehicle remains available for the mounted step because its kind is set during the drive and nothing clears it before ignition. The design is now complete, so the developer will write the code, update the test screen list, add ledger rows to the fiction lines, and verify NEXT input handling.\n\nThe bot will place a cigarette fire at its current position when the fuel gauge is above zero, marking `ignite_cigarette` if the burn succeeds. If fuel is empty, it will walk to step_x plus ten. The `script_ignite` function will be reduced to Bus and ending read timer logic only. The developer is now starting to write files.\n\nThe developer will write mod.rs first, then world.rs in chunks, followed by shell, app, and tests. Merc derives Clone and Serialize, so Vec clones work correctly. The country_anchor type is also Clone. Post() events will remain. A view-basis helper will be added to mod.rs with a canonical yaw-zero comment.\n\nProp positions will use the view basis so they align with the camera. The rifle sits eye-plus-forward-0.45, right-0.18, up-0.22. The rag sits eye-plus-forward-0.7, right-0.35, up-0.05 with wind flutter driven by world.wind and minutes. The map, GPS, and mono props use similar offsets. The test rag stays within 1.5 units of the eye.\n\nThe country tile will be named \"country\" and placed within twelve meters of the player. It is spawned at the airstrip, so it does not interfere with the title camera. The launch screenshot stays on the title screen before any click, and the first frame of play shows the country near the player.\n\nThe developer is ready to code. They will update the goal budget in the match, add `step_yaw` and `finale` fields to the world struct, and insert a `Ledger` variant into the screen enum. They also plan to enable noclip at the start of `move_body` and gate `use_vehicle` by proximity.\n\nThe `Ledger` variant will be inserted after `Playing`. Existing pattern matches will fail to compile and need updating, so the shell file will be rewritten comprehensively. The world.rs screen logic already treats `Ledger` as a menu, which prevents the player from walking during the menu while still allowing input to reach it. A special case for `bot_input` will be placed before the playing check. The finale selection must return to `Playing` so the next tick can simulate the shot. On the confirm tick, `shell_tick` runs because the screen remains `Ledger`.\n\nThe activate flow sets the screen to Playing and advances the script, so the bot fires on the next tick. The read route crouches the bot and increments step_t while the menu is active; script_ignite only runs during simulate when the screen is Playing, so it triggers after the menu ends.\n\nThe 200-point budget covers the menu, which lasts under one second. The read route crouches the bot and leaves bodies intact, matching the old playthrough. The developer will set a high block-until limit before running cargo to avoid killing sibling processes.\n\nThe developer will write all code first, then run a single cargo test. Incremental compilation is disabled in the dev profile, so each rebuild takes one to three minutes. They are also checking that the fiction scan avoids restricted words like \"appropriate\", \"April\", and \"apr\".\n\nThe bot will aim at the body zone to kill the barrel with one shot. The flamer marks on hit rather than on death, and ignite_person only triggers when the body is hit.\n\nThe fuse tick runs before the shot handler, so resetting the vehicle stage to zero and marking the ignite flag in the same tick is safe. The bot’s near check uses a ten-meter threshold; at a pitch of negative zero point one six, the distance to the target is roughly ten meters.\n\nThe town fire check will use cell_center to detect in-town cells. Molotov ignites apply to a single cell, and if that cell is inside town, town_burning becomes true. The developer will also mark the town state directly inside done(Town) rather than relying on a separate call. Implementation begins with mod.rs, which requires adding EntityId to the struct.\n\nThe developer will add `use glam::Quat` and geometry helpers. Country spawns once, so it is not a performance concern. Player movement covers roughly ten meters per second, which may cross one eight-meter cell and trigger a single rebuild. They confirmed that `set_position` returns the entity and `entities.get_mut` is public. Tests will be added to merc.rs near the playthrough. Scene name lookups work even if the room already contains entities. The `Sim::new(scene, seed)` signature was verified.\n\nThe NEXT button check will be placed at the start of handle_gun so switching weapons does not also trigger a fire. Adding step_yaw to World is safe because blank() initializes it and JSON already includes the field. All fields in the test World clone must be set explicitly.\n\nThe shell test screens array will include Ledger so the row limit is checked. The dev_rows tabs are small enough to fit on one page without falling through to a Next button. A custom name list for the spawn tab will omit the Reset option, and activate will not see it. The World ledger contains seven names.\n\nThe dev-world \"Ignite grass\" action will place fire eight meters ahead of the player. Night mode sets minutes to twenty-two hours, so tests can assert the hour exceeds twenty. The teleport helper will also clear the seat field.\n\nThe developer is writing the `dev_spawn` helper. It places entities six meters ahead and four meters behind the player. Soldiers spawn with forty health. Animals and trucks spawn normally. The Technical variant sets the ride kind to one, clears the seat, and positions the vehicle at the spawn point.\n\nThe `dev_spawn` helper now fully initializes the Technical and Boat variants with health, stage, and zero speed. The `dev_world` helper is being written to handle developer world actions such as setting the time to night.\n\nThe `dev_world` helper now sets noon, toggles rain and clear sky, and adjusts wind. It also ignites grass eight meters ahead and to the side of the player. These helpers are public but the test will use the menu instead. The shell activate flow calls them. Ledger is added to the go_back logic. Everything is ready for writing.\n\nThe title ground is hidden during play because the player starts at the airstrip and the pad is only ninety-six meters across. The developer also finalized the color palette for trees, grass, water, road, and rocks.\n\nThe title pad near the origin overlaps with country tiles and the dress ground during play. The developer will name the dress boxes so they can despawn them when the game starts.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The campaign still stamps flags and the camera never leaves the overlook. I’ll wire the eye, the ending menu, real shot actions, and the dev controls into the sim next."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-43","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","old_string":"use glam::Vec3;","new_string":"use glam::{Quat, Vec3};"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-44","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","old_string":"/// Where the window looks. The country yaw is copied; the eye stays in the overlook.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct Overlook {\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\n    pub yaw: f32,\n    pub pitch: f32,\n}\n\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\n    yaw: 0.0,\n    pitch: -0.42,\n});\n\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\n}\n\nfn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\n}","new_string":"/// Where the window looks. Menus keep the dusk overlook. Play copies the body.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct Overlook {\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\n    pub yaw: f32,\n    pub pitch: f32,\n    pub roll: f32,\n}\n\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\n    yaw: 0.0,\n    pitch: -0.42,\n    roll: 0.0,\n});\n\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\n}\n\nfn aim_overlook(eye: [f32; 3], yaw: f32, pitch: f32, roll: f32) {\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\n    slot.eye = eye;\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\n    slot.roll = roll;\n}\n\n/// Same basis as `pav_view::camera::fp_basis`. Yaw 0, pitch 0, roll 0 → forward (0, 0, −1), right (1, 0, 0).\nfn view_basis(yaw: f32, pitch: f32, roll: f32) -> (Vec3, Vec3, Vec3) {\n    let (sy, cy) = yaw.sin_cos();\n    let (sp, cp) = pitch.sin_cos();\n    let mut forward = Vec3::new(sy * cp, sp, -cy * cp);\n    if forward.length_squared() < 1e-8 {\n        forward = Vec3::NEG_Z;\n    }\n    forward = forward.normalize();\n    let mut right = forward.cross(Vec3::Y);\n    if right.length_squared() < 1e-6 {\n        right = Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy);\n    }\n    right = right.normalize();\n    let up = right.cross(forward).normalize();\n    let (sr, cr) = roll.sin_cos();\n    let rolled_right = (right * cr + up * sr).normalize();\n    let rolled_up = (up * cr - right * sr).normalize();\n    (forward, rolled_right, rolled_up)\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-45","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","old_string":"pub struct Merc {\n    pub world: World,\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    dressed: bool,\n}","new_string":"pub struct Merc {\n    pub world: World,\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    dressed: bool,\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    country: Vec<EntityId>,\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    country_anchor: (i32, i32),\n    #[serde(skip)]\n    props: Vec<EntityId>,\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-46","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs","old_string":"    let game = Merc { world: World::campaign(sim.state.seed, Route::Human), dressed: false };","new_string":"    let game = Merc {\n        world: World::campaign(sim.state.seed, Route::Human),\n        dressed: false,\n        country: Vec::new(),\n        country_anchor: (i32::MIN, i32::MIN),\n        props: Vec::new(),\n    };"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7886,"output_tokens":13472,"cache_read_input_tokens":127616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"8d0093ff-b3de-45bd-8f4b-246f12f91e19"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-43","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"use glam::Vec3;\",\"new_string\":\"use glam::{Quat, Vec3};\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"use glam::Vec3;\",\"old_line\":13,\"new_string\":\"use glam::{Quat, Vec3};\",\"new_line\":13,\"context_before\":\"use std::collections::BTreeMap;\\n\\nuse anyhow::{Result, anyhow};\\n\",\"context_after\":\"use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\\n\\nuse super::{Game, GameBox, level_text};\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-44","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"/// Where the window looks. The country yaw is copied; the eye stays in the overlook.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n}\",\"new_string\":\"/// Where the window looks. Menus keep the dusk overlook. Play copies the body.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n    pub roll: f32,\\n}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n    roll: 0.0,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(eye: [f32; 3], yaw: f32, pitch: f32, roll: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.eye = eye;\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n    slot.roll = roll;\\n}\\n\\n/// Same basis as `pav_view::camera::fp_basis`. Yaw 0, pitch 0, roll 0 → forward (0, 0, −1), right (1, 0, 0).\\nfn view_basis(yaw: f32, pitch: f32, roll: f32) -> (Vec3, Vec3, Vec3) {\\n    let (sy, cy) = yaw.sin_cos();\\n    let (sp, cp) = pitch.sin_cos();\\n    let mut forward = Vec3::new(sy * cp, sp, -cy * cp);\\n    if forward.length_squared() < 1e-8 {\\n        forward = Vec3::NEG_Z;\\n    }\\n    forward = forward.normalize();\\n    let mut right = forward.cross(Vec3::Y);\\n    if right.length_squared() < 1e-6 {\\n        right = Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy);\\n    }\\n    right = right.normalize();\\n    let up = right.cross(forward).normalize();\\n    let (sr, cr) = roll.sin_cos();\\n    let rolled_right = (right * cr + up * sr).normalize();\\n    let rolled_up = (up * cr - right * sr).normalize();\\n    (forward, rolled_right, rolled_up)\\n}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"/// Where the window looks. The country yaw is copied; the eye stays in the overlook.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(yaw: f32, pitch: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n}\",\"old_line\":34,\"new_string\":\"/// Where the window looks. Menus keep the dusk overlook. Play copies the body.\\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\\npub struct Overlook {\\n    pub eye: [f32; 3],\\n    pub yaw: f32,\\n    pub pitch: f32,\\n    pub roll: f32,\\n}\\n\\nstatic OVERLOOK: std::sync::Mutex<Overlook> = std::sync::Mutex::new(Overlook {\\n    eye: [0.15, 1.55, 4.2],\\n    yaw: 0.0,\\n    pitch: -0.42,\\n    roll: 0.0,\\n});\\n\\npub fn overlook() -> Overlook {\\n    *OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\nfn aim_overlook(eye: [f32; 3], yaw: f32, pitch: f32, roll: f32) {\\n    let mut slot = OVERLOOK.lock().unwrap();\\n    slot.eye = eye;\\n    slot.yaw = yaw;\\n    slot.pitch = pitch;\\n    slot.roll = roll;\\n}\\n\\n/// Same basis as `pav_view::camera::fp_basis`. Yaw 0, pitch 0, roll 0 → forward (0, 0, −1), right (1, 0, 0).\\nfn view_basis(yaw: f32, pitch: f32, roll: f32) -> (Vec3, Vec3, Vec3) {\\n    let (sy, cy) = yaw.sin_cos();\\n    let (sp, cp) = pitch.sin_cos();\\n    let mut forward = Vec3::new(sy * cp, sp, -cy * cp);\\n    if forward.length_squared() < 1e-8 {\\n        forward = Vec3::NEG_Z;\\n    }\\n    forward = forward.normalize();\\n    let mut right = forward.cross(Vec3::Y);\\n    if right.length_squared() < 1e-6 {\\n        right = Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy);\\n    }\\n    right = right.normalize();\\n    let up = right.cross(forward).normalize();\\n    let (sr, cr) = roll.sin_cos();\\n    let rolled_right = (right * cr + up * sr).normalize();\\n    let rolled_up = (up * cr - right * sr).normalize();\\n    (forward, rolled_right, rolled_up)\\n}\",\"new_line\":34,\"context_before\":\"\\nconst LEVEL: &str = include_str!(\\\"../merc.toml\\\");\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n/// Rules state. Visual entity ids are not part of the save: they are rebuilt in `post`.\\n#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f2de2948-9ea3-4b74-94f8-84134cb8e26b-45","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"pub struct Merc {\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    dressed: bool,\\n}\",\"new_string\":\"pub struct Merc {\\n    pub world: World,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    dressed: bool,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    country: Vec<EntityId>,\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    country_anchor: (i32, i32),\\n    #[serde(skip)]\\n    props: Vec<EntityId>,\\n}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/mod.rs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-2026