{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_462","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pause has five rows. Moving up from row 4 reaches rows 3, 2, 1, and 0.\n\nFour up presses correctly land on Resume. The back navigation from cheats works as expected. Noclip test logic is sound: it sets the ride while playing, skips the seat early-out, and advances for 30 ticks.\n\nEye position increases by 12 over 30 ticks. The movement assertion passes because the z delta against the ride seat exceeds 2, satisfying the OR condition. Storing z0 would make a future failure clearer. Next step is compilation and Quat verification.\n\nMerc is public and the Game trait is in scope, so get::<Merc>() will compile. I'll run only the merc test first to avoid a long full suite. The build will use 12 jobs, offline mode, and the engine's target directory.\n\nThe playthrough test will add roughly 65,000 extra simulation ticks across six routes. That should only extend runtime by a few seconds. I'll set the test timeout to five minutes and run all merc tests together.\n\nThe Quat::from_rotation_arc signature will be verified by compiling rather than inspecting the cargo registry. A minor integer division edge case in mod.rs is harmless. Extreme pitch angles in view_basis are acceptable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-728ef052-e5c5-4a01-a929-19818128ca61-100","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn spawn_truck|fn spawn_barrel|fn prep_ignite|fn present_ending","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1026,"output_tokens":1211,"cache_read_input_tokens":181760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"d79076fd-e670-451f-a08d-9f819b73e4b4"}
