{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_466","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"FP and Ledger tests passed. The dev menu test failed because focus after two backs is not 4.\n\nThe resume test failed because focus landed on Settings (index 1) after four ups. This implies the starting focus was 0, and the up key wrapped around to the last row.\n\nTracing the back navigation shows focus should have remained at 4, so four ups from there would land on Resume. The fact that it landed on Settings instead suggests focus was not actually 4 when the menu opened, or an up press triggered an unexpected side effect.\n\nThe menu code confirms act(3) only triggers an up move. The focus mismatch likely stems from the first back navigation from tab 1 not leaving focus at 4, perhaps due to Next page logic.\n\nThe Noclip toggle succeeded and focus remained at 4. The failure is isolated to the Resume navigation after that.\n\nThe Pause screen contains five rows: Resume, Settings, Controls, Dev mode, and Quit. Focus should have remained at 4 after the two back presses, so four ups from there would land on Resume rather than Settings.\n\nThe `go_back` function resets focus to 0 on its first line. This likely explains why focus was not at 4 when the four up presses began.\n\nThe fix is to remove the four up presses. After the second back, focus resets to 0, which is Resume, so confirming directly will work.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-27f7d562-2efe-48ab-b8c5-44b76e19dde2-104","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs","old_string":"    w.tick(&act(2), DT);\n    w.tick(&act(2), DT);\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Pause, \"focus {} rows {:?}\", w.focus, w.rows());\n    for _ in 0..4 {\n        w.tick(&act(3), DT);\n    }\n    assert_eq!(w.rows().get(w.focus).map(String::as_str), Some(\"Resume\"));\n    w.tick(&act(1), DT);\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Playing);","new_string":"    w.tick(&act(2), DT);\n    w.tick(&act(2), DT);\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Pause, \"focus {} rows {:?}\", w.focus, w.rows());\n    assert_eq!(w.rows().get(w.focus).map(String::as_str), Some(\"Resume\"));\n    w.tick(&act(1), DT);\n    assert_eq!(w.screen, Screen::Playing);"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1187,"output_tokens":1631,"cache_read_input_tokens":185216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"ebdf5d93-3b32-417a-b3d5-98b8c337c1e2"}
