{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_474","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Resuming from where I left off.\n\nfp, endings, and dev tests are complete. The bot playthrough is still failing on ignite11. I will check that the uncompiled edits are present and re-run the playthrough test.\n\nI will read the long-running-background-tasks skill before starting the cargo test. I need to verify the edits exist in the engine and scratch directories before running cargo. I will not set CARGO_HOME.\n\nI will verify the test results by checking evidence rather than trusting the summary. I also want to inspect the cigarette and tracer code for correctness before compiling, since that will take about ninety seconds.\n\nI am inspecting world.rs for logic bugs before compiling. The Ignite(11) walk target might still be burning if fire spread occurs. I also need to check whether Ignite(7)'s disk of radius 5 burns cells the walk target could hit.\n\nThe step coordinates are captured at the start of ignite 11, after Ignite(7) has already burned. The walk target is roughly twenty meters away, which should sit outside a radius-five disk unless fire spread occurs during the intervening ignites.\n\nThe seat-cycling USE logic is correct. I will verify the edits are present and then run the test. The cargo build should finish within the block_until window.\n\nThe playthrough test could run for a long time if the bot completes all six routes. It is CPU-bound and runs at 60fps without rendering. Previously stuck tests finished quickly because they hit the 30-second budget panic. A full successful run would take more time.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The playthrough is still red on the cigarette and tracer steps. I’ll confirm those edits are in the source, then re-run the three-ending bot against the shipped sim."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-afa652eb-a2a5-4f8a-a545-2b1fbbfd8173-0","name":"todo_write","input":{"to