{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_488","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The blow_tanks configuration uses 7x7 tanks spaced 10 meters apart, with each tank having an ignite_disk radius of 6.\n\nThe 7x7 grid spans 60 by 60 meters. Each cell is 4 square meters. The 1296-cell bounding box exceeds the 500-cell threshold. Coverage is continuous because the 10-meter spacing leaves a 5-meter gap between centers, which falls inside the 6-meter radius.\n\nThe existing 7×7 disk will continue to mark explosion_chain and cells_500. PLAN.md appears to favor this approach over requiring player shots.\n\nThe rejection text only applies to the ignite_* flags, so blow_tanks remains unchanged.\n\nPanic mode spawns a soldier and ignites a strip. Enemies panic when the cell beneath them burns. They light disks at the soldier's position and flee at 4 m/s for 30 seconds. The soldier sits at (x+4, z-4) with a 3-meter radius disk. This should trigger panic in roughly one second.\n\nThere is a concern that the disk might not cover the soldier's exact cell if coverage is measured from cell centers.\n\nAnimals spawn at (x+6, z-6). They flee when the first gun has shots and they are within 40 meters. The bot holds secondary and does not fire to avoid scattering the herd. The first gun should already have shots from earlier pistol use. If arm() pushes a new weapon slot, guns.first() still points to the original pistol.\n\nAnimals flee at 6 m/s, so they clear the 8-unit threshold in about 1.4 seconds. They skip the fire panic code because their kind is not 3. Rain ignites fuel and marks rain_extinguished when the next fire tick hits.\n\nThe 40-meter search radius should leave the river. The tank farm is at Ombe, hundreds of meters from the rain event near the lodge. Nearby grass is unlikely to be fully burnt.\n\nFresh grass is available for the rain event.\n\nDuring Ceasefire, a soldier spawns 30 meters south with a sniper. The bot aims and fires. Killing this soldier ends the ceasefire. The sniper deals 110 damage to 30 health in one shot. The 30-meter distance is easily within range.\n\nThe ceasefire holster check only blocks firing when the player is in town. After the rain and boat events, the player is near the river, so this restriction does not apply.\n\nThe Convoy event spawns a kind 6 truck at z-16 with an RPG. The bot aims and fires. One shot deals 300 damage within 150 meters range. Kind 6 bodies are damaged by shots_tick.\n\nWalking from the river to town is long but still fits within the budget.\n\nTwo preemptive fixes remain: adding a fresh-cell search for the cigarette and making the bot board the truck if it is on foot.\n\nThe bus event should also board the player if they are on foot and far away, in case the mounted event left them unmounted.\n\nTracer offsets need to be more robust.\n\nFor the Mounted event, pressing USE every tick cycles the seat. The mark only fires when the seat reaches 2 and primary is held. Because use_vehicle runs before handle_gun in the simulation loop, the mark triggers at the end of that tick. The next step's bot input will not include that USE press.\n\nIf the player starts at seat 2, the USE press cycles the seat to 0 before the mark fires on tick 3. If the player starts at seat 0 and is far away, pressing USE does nothing because the seat never changes; walking is required instead.\n\nThe Mounted and Bus events will be updated so the bot boards the vehicle if it is on foot. The cigarette search will also treat cells with a burnt_until timestamp as unavailable.\n\nThe `cell_open` helper now rejects cells that are burning or still within their `burnt_until` window. The `nearest_open_cell` function searches concentric rings around the target point, checking only the outermost cells of each ring for an open spot.\n\nThe `bot_ignite` function for cigarette k==11 now handles three cases. If the player is not in seat 0, it presses USE to cycle the seat. Otherwise it searches for an open cell near the current position. If the nearest open cell is more than 1.2 meters away, it walks there. If no open cell exists nearby, it presses INTERACT.\n\nThe 1.2-meter threshold for the cigarette event is too small. A player standing in a corner of a 2-meter cell can be up to 1.4 meters from its center, so they would walk forever instead of interacting with their own open cell. The bot should check if the current cell is already open and interact immediately if it is.\n\nThe cigarette bot now checks the current cell first, then nearest open cell, then falls back to the step position. Sprint is enabled for faster travel. The Mounted event is next.\n\nThe Mounted event now walks to the truck when the player is on foot and the seat is 0, but only if the vehicle is more than 5 meters away. It does not press USE while walking. Once the player reaches seat 2, it holds PRIMARY.\n\nThe Bus event now walks to the Junction bus stop when the player is on foot and the vehicle is more than 5 meters away. It presses USE to board if already near. Once in seat 0, it drives to the Junction. If the player started in seat 2 from the Mounted event, the bot simply drives straight to the Junction.\n\nThe tracer shot search will be widened so one triple-shot lands. The INTERACT press for the cigarette event fires immediately on the first tick, so ignite_at should succeed. Comments must avoid banned substrings like \"apr\". After the boat event, the player is seated and then walks to town; the boat is far from the town exit.\n\nThe town bot presses USE every tick until the seat reaches 0, then walks. Walking from deep water to town may cross the map in 220 seconds, but the test will reveal any timeout. The Drive event after town might use kind 2 (boat).\n\nThe Drive event replaces the boat with a technical at the player's position and seats them. The bot then drives to the cement yard, roughly 800 meters away at 16 m/s, which takes about 50 seconds and fits within the 140-second budget. The technical_driven flag may already be set from earlier driving, so the bot only needs to arrive at the target. It is unclear whether ride.dist resets when the boat is replaced.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-44fd75ad-5211-46f0-a7fc-6181fccd9243-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1016,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-44fd75ad-5211-46f0-a7fc-6181fccd9243-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"post_cleared|fn maybe_reman","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3154,"output_tokens":3613,"cache_read_input_tokens":82688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"cab3b5d6-7c61-4b85-8463-3fc309a930b2"}
