{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_498","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The monitor started. A note indicates another background task is the same monitor.\n\nThe running background task is the monitor just started, not a duplicate. Cargo ID is e6117183. I will keep working without polling. I will examine town molotov and boat distance to prepare for test fixes. I will read geom river to estimate walk time. I will check if the old monitor 9338ce28 is still alive.\n\nThe old monitor has exited. I will not edit world.rs while the compiler is running. I will read the river data to prepare for any needed budget change.\n\nI analyzed the soldier's escape from burning cells. At 4 m/s, a 2 m cell is exited in exactly 0.75 s. That matches the 3-point flee threshold. The escape is borderline.\n\nThe soldier's escape from the single disk is barely sufficient. The six-disk strip provides a much safer path, since the disks overlap and the soldier stays inside them for the entire run. I will wait for the monitor.\n\nI checked the reach budgets. The three key paths are all well within their limits. Airstrip to (0, 460) takes about 67 seconds. The second leg from (0, 460) takes about 27 seconds. The third from (-40, 640) to safe house takes about 40 seconds. All fit comfortably inside the 160-second budget.\n\nThe remaining reach budgets are also safe. The drive from the safe house to Ombe takes about 75 seconds, and the bus leg to Junction takes roughly 41 seconds. The drive to the lodge and the boat trip both fit within their limits. I am now checking the distance from the water to town.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-67a8d85b-7f11-4a6e-9911-620be1fe47fc-55","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":90,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1124,"output_tokens":1167,"cache_read_input_tokens":108032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"15265735-8275-4190-82f3-cf0807a6bbc8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-67a8d85b-7f11-4a6e-9911-620be1fe47fc-55","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n140→        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\",\"content_concise\":\"90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n140→        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\\n        if left <= remain {\\n            let u = t + left / len;\\n            return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n        }\\n        left -= remain;\\n\",\"total_lines\":284}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"53a2560c-9dca-4449-ab43-7af1a63dff31"}
