,32,48,32,109,101,97,115,117,114,101,100,59,32,49,56,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,101,100,32,111,117,116,59,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,101,100,32,105,110,32,48,46,51,49,115,10,56,54,58,69,88,73,84,58,49,48,49,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/playthrough-try2.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"thread 'bot_plays_all_three_endings' (793826) panicked at crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs:886:17:\"},{\"line_number\":74,\"content\":\"Human seed 1 stuck on boat for 240s (budget 240) at (-218.4,-42.3) step 51 flags 49\"},{\"line_number\":83,\"content\":\"test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 18 filtered out; finished in 0.31s\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"EXIT:101\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5558edeb-2bf3-4c8d-b107-5bf555b09072"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_505","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boat has been stuck for 240 seconds at coordinates (-218.\n\nThe boat is stuck near the river. The player walked to the water but never completed the boat_driven task, which requires a 15-unit deep-water ride. The bot's boat logic is being examined.\n\nThe bot's boat code checks distance to the ride target and presses USE. The player is already on the river at (-218.4, -42.3), so the boat should have started.\n\nThe 240-second stall suggests the boat is either stuck trying to board or has zero speed because the water is not deep enough. The code caps boat speed at zero when kind 2 is active but deep_water returns false.\n\nThe boat is likely stuck in a USE-cycling loop. The bot presses USE while within 5 meters of the ride target, which toggles the seat from 0 to 1. Once the seat changes, the bot drives toward water_ahead, but that target is the current position, so the boat never moves. The distance never exceeds 15 units, preventing the boat_driven task from completing. The location should be deep water, so the stall is probably caused by the seat cycling rather than a lack of deep water.\n\nThe stuck coordinates match the boat's ride position exactly, so the player is already snapped into the boat seat. The stall is therefore not caused by a USE-cycling loop or boarding delay; the boat is simply unable to move.\n\nThe exact distance from the river segment endpoint to the stuck position is being calculated. The point lies roughly 18.5 meters along the segment, which determines whether deep_water evaluates to true.\n\nThe point is roughly 19 meters along the river segment, so deep_water should be true. The stall may instead mean the player never boarded and is standing beside the boat.\n\nThe USE button logic is being re-examined. If the player is near the boat, USE should advance the seat to 1 and start driving. The stall suggests ride.kind may be reverting from 2 back to 1 elsewhere in the code.\n\nThe seat is not cycling because the bot only presses USE while the seat is 0. Once the player boards, the bot drives and never re-presses USE. The stall is therefore not a USE-cycling loop. The boat may be yawing in place or moving in circles without gaining distance. The deep_water check and shallow-water behavior are being examined.\n\nThe deep_water check may be using a coarse river-width approximation that misses the polyline centerline. The nearest_water function might also return the wrong point from the lodge spawn, so the boat position is not recognized as deep water.\n\nThe boat spawn point was set to the nearest water at the start of the step. The player walked from the lodge to the boat, arriving with roughly 140 seconds remaining in the 240-second budget. This confirms the boat was reached and the stall is not caused by a late arrival.\n\nThe 240-second timer resets whenever the goal changes. The bot walked roughly 100 seconds to reach the boat, then spent the remaining 140 seconds stuck at that position.\n\nThe boat never reaches the 15-unit distance needed to complete the task. The stall likely occurs because the boat drives onto shallow water or the bank, where deep_water becomes false and speed drops to zero. The deep_water, on_water, and movement logic are being re-examined.\n\nThe water_ahead target may be calculated incorrectly, sending the boat toward shallow bank rather than deep water. If the boat hits the shore immediately, it stops before covering the required 15 units.\n\nThe nearest water point to the lodge spawn (-260, -700) is the river vertex (-200, -40). This confirms the boat spawned at that exact coordinate, so the stuck position matches the ride target.\n\nThe boarding tick only presses USE and leaves axes at zero, so the boat does not throttle until the next tick. The exact distance from the lodge to the river is being recalculated.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-29c0e3d1-c10a-45e2-9918-08d37db47886-61","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":50,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-29c0e3d1-c10a-45e2-9918-08d37db47886-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"-> .*ignite|stuck on","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/playthrough-try2.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":495,"output_tokens":2770,"cache_read_input_tokens":115072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"f672942c-831a-4fd7-bb47-c0b7eabd4401"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-29c0e3d1-c10a-45e2-9918-08d37db47886-61","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"50→\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n60→\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n70→}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n}\\n\\n80→pub fn on_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 12.0\\n}\\n\\n/// Deep enough for the outboard. The edges of the channel are shallows.\\npub fn deep_water(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    river_dist(x, z) < 7.0\\n}\\n\\n/// A point `metres` further along the channel from the closest point on the centre line.\\n90→pub fn water_ahead(x: f32, z: f32, metres: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    let mut best_i = 0usize;\\n    let mut best_t = 0.0f32;\\n    let mut best_d = f32::MAX;\\n    for (i, w) in RIVER.windows(2).enumerate() {\\n        let abx = w[1].0 - w[0].0;\\n        let abz = w[1].1 - w[0].1;\\n        let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n        let t = if len2 < 1e-4 { 0.0 } else { (((x - w[0].0) * abx + (z - w[0].1) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0) };\\n        let px = w[0].0 + abx * t;\\n100→        let pz = w[0].1 + abz * t;\\n        let d = dist(x, z, px, pz);\\n        if d < best_d {\\n            best_d = d;\\n            best_i = i;\\n            best_t = t;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    let mut i = best_i;\\n    let mut t = best_t;\\n110→    let mut left = metres.abs();\\n    let forward = metres >= 0.0;\\n    if !forward {\\n        // Walk back toward the upstream end of the polyline.\\n        while left > 0.0 {\\n            let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n            let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n            let abx = bx - ax;\\n            let abz = bz - az;\\n            let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n120→            let back = t * len;\\n            if left <= back {\\n                let u = t - left / len;\\n                return (ax + abx * u, az + abz * u);\\n            }\\n            left -= back;\\n            if i == 0 {\\n                return RIVER[0];\\n            }\\n            i -= 1;\\n130→            t = 1.0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    while left > 0.0 && i + 1 < RIVER.len() {\\n        let (ax, az) = RIVER[i];\\n        let (bx, bz) = RIVER[i + 1];\\n        let abx = bx - ax;\\n        let abz = bz - az;\\n        let len = (abx * abx + abz * abz).sqrt().max(0.001);\\n        let remain = (1.0 - t) * len;\",\"content_concise\":\"50→\\npub fn clamp_map(x: f32, z: f32) -> (f32, f32) {\\n    (x.clamp(-MAP, MAP), z.clamp(-MAP, MAP))\\n}\\n\\npub fn dist(ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let dx = ax - bx;\\n    let dz = az - bz;\\n    (dx * dx + dz * dz).sqrt()\\n}\\n60→\\nfn seg_dist(x: f32, z: f32, ax: f32, az: f32, bx: f32, bz: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let abx = bx - ax;\\n    let abz = bz - az;\\n    let len2 = abx * abx + abz * abz;\\n    if len2 < 1e-4 {\\n        return dist(x, z, ax, az);\\n    }\\n    let t = (((x - ax) * abx + (z - az) * abz) / len2).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n    dist(x, z, ax + abx * t, az + abz * t)\\n70→}\\n\\npub fn river_dist(x: f32, z: f32) -> f32 {\\n    let mut best = f32::MAX;\\n    for w in RIVER.windows(2) {\\n        best = best.min(seg_dist(x, z, w[0].0, w[0].1, w[1].0, w[1].1));\\n    }\\n    best\\n