{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_506","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boat step is stuck at (-218.4, -42).\n\nThe character reached the boat but never triggered boat_driven. I need to check the full log and goal transitions to find why driving failed.\n\nThe boat_driven trigger requires deep water and distance over 15 meters. The character is roughly 18.5 meters from the river vertex, so deep water should be true. I am checking whether this point lies on the river centerline.\n\nThe boat is in shallow water. The point is only about 7.2 meters from the river centerline, so deep_water is false and movement is blocked. This explains why boat_driven never triggered.\n\nThe boat should snap to the river centerline on boarding. The stuck position is 7 meters from the boat, so the player likely never boarded. I am checking whether the boat moved.\n\nThe boat may have drifted off the centerline while driving toward water_ahead. It could have hit shallow water and stopped, preventing the 15-meter distance threshold from being reached. The 240-second stall suggests it arrived there and remained.\n\nThe boat likely overshot the 7-meter deep channel. At 16 m/s, a small steering error sends it into shallow water immediately. Speed drops to zero, so the 15-meter distance threshold is never reached and the step remains stuck.\n\nThe boat starts with an undefined yaw. It was likely heading south toward the lodge, not along the river centerline. This mismatch causes it to drive off course immediately, hit shallow water, and stop before reaching the 15-meter distance threshold.\n\nThe core simulation rule is that once the boat stops in shallow water, it cannot restart. The bot drives forward in its old yaw and immediately leaves the deep channel. It hits shallow water within a few meters, stops, and never regains speed to reach the 15-meter distance threshold.\n\nThe steering rate is only 1.6 radians per second. A 90-degree turn takes one second, but the boat travels 16 meters in that time at full throttle. This confirms the bot exits the 7-meter deep channel immediately and cannot correct its course.\n\nSetting the boat's initial yaw to face along the river centerline when it spawns would fix the overshoot. The player would still walk to the boat and drive, but the boat would start aligned with the channel. This prevents the bot from immediately leaving the deep water and hitting shallow water.\n\nA real player would turn the boat in place before driving forward. The bot should reduce throttle when yaw error is large so it can correct heading before applying full speed. This prevents overshooting into shallow water.\n\nI am now drafting the `bot_drive` change. I must be careful not to reduce throttle too aggressively, since the technical needs to reach the lodge within budget despite turning in place at the start.\n\nI drafted the `bot_drive` throttle reduction. Boats now use 0.15 throttle when yaw error exceeds 0.35 radians, while land vehicles keep full speed. I am checking whether this throttle value correctly limits speed to prevent overshooting into shallow water.\n\nThe throttle reduction is safe. At 0.15 throttle the boat moves only 2.4 m/s while turning, so its path radius is about 1.5 m and it stays well inside the 7 m deep channel. Once aligned, full throttle allows a 40 m drive in deep water.\n\nThe boat's initial yaw will be set to face water_ahead when it spawns. This ensures the boat starts aligned with the river centerline rather than relying solely on the throttle reduction.\n\nBoth the initial yaw alignment and the gentle throttle reduction will be applied together for robustness. Once the boat reaches the 15-meter distance threshold, the step is marked complete even if it later beaches, since subsequent steps only require exiting to town. The player approaches the boat from the south, where the lodge is located.\n\nThe stuck position is 7.2 meters from the river centerline, not on it. The bot likely drove a few meters off course and stopped, leaving distance below 15 meters. A 5-meter boarding radius would still allow the player to reach the boat and seat.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c79a8d1c-ed41-42ec-825f-e4c8e9cd5475-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/playthrough-try2.log","offset":60,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c79a8d1c-ed41-42ec-825f-e4c8e9cd5475-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn yaw_toward","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4563,"output_tokens":2907,"cache_read_input_tokens":115456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"799a458c-7a42-4098-8e4d-37fdb0ff2b91"}
