{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_507","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The log shows a jump from `mounted` to `animals`, skipping the panic.\n\nThe panic likely completed within the same tick as mounted. The log only prints when the goal name changes between ticks, so it never recorded the transition.\n\nThe panic spec is skipped when `done(Panic)` is true immediately on the same tick. This happens if the `enemy_panicked` flag was already set earlier, so the script advances directly to the next step without ever running the panic logic.\n\nThe flag was likely set legitimately during an earlier fight. The panic step still ignites disks under the soldier even when it skips the soldier panicking.\n\nThe panic step spawns a soldier and ignites disks during `begin`, but it does not set the `enemy_panicked` flag. If that flag were already set, the step would finish immediately on the same tick without the soldier ever fleeing. The flag must have been set earlier or during that tick's `begin`/`done` cycle.\n\nThe flag was set by an earlier real fire panic, so the step auto-completes without cheating. Coverage only requires the flag to be set, and a human who already panicked an enemy would also skip this step. This is acceptable.\n\nMounted, bus, drive to lodge, and sleep all succeeded. Boat failed. The panic flag will be checked after the union check. The boat fix requires gentle throttle during turns and spawning facing along the channel.\n\nThe boat fix should prevent beaching entirely. A 40-meter ahead-of-water check may miss a bend and let the straight-line drive leave the channel.\n\nThe nearest water vertex to the lodge is (-200, -40), roughly 663 meters away. The 40-meter ahead-of-water check from that point may hit a shared vertex between two segments.\n\nThe 40-meter ahead-of-water check from the shared vertex lands on the next segment. A straight drive along that centerline stays on track for 373 meters. The boat only beaches if its yaw is misaligned.\n\nThe boat will be spawned with the correct initial yaw and driven at gentle throttle. The 240-second budget is sufficient. After reaching the river, the bot will walk to town. The `enemy_panicked` flag should be cleared at the start of the panic step so the step must earn it again.\n\nClearing the flag risks a 30-second stall if the soldier spawns without fire. The soldier sits on a burning cell and flees once it moves out of range, so the step should work. The flag will still be cleared to make the step genuine.\n\nThe animals step completed in two seconds, confirming the flag was not pre-set. The bus and technical drive logic correctly limits throttle only for the boat kind, so the truck is unaffected.\n\nThe boat throttle math checks out. At 0.05 throttle the yaw rate is 0.64 to 1.6 rad/s, giving an arc radius of 0.5 to 1.25 meters. That stays safely inside the 7-meter channel width. Once yaw error drops below 0.4, full throttle restores and the boat reaches the 15-meter mark in about one second.\n\nThe boat will be spawned with yaw aligned to the centerline, so it starts driving straight at full throttle. The `use_vehicle` steering already uses `ride.yaw`, and spawning on the centerline guarantees the boat is deep enough to avoid the zero-speed shallow-water limit.\n\nNight completed in one tick, confirming the transition was real. The finished monitor will be killed if still running. The boat should finish in roughly 100 seconds after the walk.\n\nThe remaining campaign steps fit easily within the 240-second budget. The failed test finished in only 0.31 seconds of test time, so a full six-route run should take just a few seconds. Compilation remains the main bottleneck at roughly sixty seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Ignites, the bus, and the drive to the lodge all completed. The boat reached the channel, then drove out of the deep water and stopped. I’ll point it along the river and keep the throttle low until the bow is lined up."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-932974fb-eb6e-467d-9a29-d31125e91f8c-65","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"    fn bot_drive(&self, tx: f32, tz: f32) -> InputFrame {\n        let desired = geom::yaw_toward(self.ride.x, self.ride.z, tx, tz);\n        let err = geom::wrap_angle(desired - self.ride.yaw);\n        let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n        f.axes.x = err.clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\n        f.axes.y = 1.0;\n        f\n    }","new_string":"    fn bot_drive(&self, tx: f32, tz: f32) -> InputFrame {\n        let desired = geom::yaw_toward(self.ride.x, self.ride.z, tx, tz);\n        let err = geom::wrap_angle(desired - self.ride.yaw);\n        let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n        f.axes.x = err.clamp(-1.0, 1.0);\n        // The outboard stops dead once it leaves the deep channel, so turn before opening up.\n        if self.ride.kind == 2 && err.abs() > 0.4 {\n            f.axes.y = 0.05;\n        } else {\n            f.axes.y = 1.0;\n        }\n        f\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-932974fb-eb6e-467d-9a29-d31125e91f8c-66","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"            Spec::Panic => {\n                self.clear_bodies();\n                let sx = self.x + 4.0;\n                let sz = self.z - 4.0;\n                self.spawn_soldier(sx, sz, 40.0, false);","new_string":"            Spec::Panic => {\n                // An earlier scare does not finish this job. The soldier has to run from this fire.\n                self.flags.remove(\"enemy_panicked\");\n                self.clear_bodies();\n                let sx = self.x + 4.0;\n                let sz = self.z - 4.0;\n                self.spawn_soldier(sx, sz, 40.0, false);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-932974fb-eb6e-467d-9a29-d31125e91f8c-67","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","old_string":"            Spec::Boat => {\n                let (wx, wz) = geom::nearest_water(self.x, self.z);\n                self.ride.kind = 2;\n                self.ride.seat = 0;\n                self.ride.x = wx;\n                self.ride.z = wz;\n                self.ride.speed = 0.0;\n                self.ride.health = 100.0;\n                self.ride.stage = 0;\n                self.ride.dist = 0.0;\n                self.boat_dist = 0.0;\n            }","new_string":"            Spec::Boat => {\n                let (wx, wz) = geom::nearest_water(self.x, self.z);\n                let (ax, az) = geom::water_ahead(wx, wz, 40.0);\n                self.ride.kind = 2;\n                self.ride.seat = 0;\n                self.ride.x = wx;\n                self.ride.z = wz;\n                self.ride.yaw = geom::yaw_toward(wx, wz, ax, az);\n                self.ride.speed = 0.0;\n                self.ride.health = 100.0;\n                self.ride.stage = 0;\n                self.ride.dist = 0.0;\n                self.boat_dist = 0.0;\n            }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3586,"output_tokens":4163,"cache_read_input_tokens":119936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"14100c5c-a9e1-4915-89b2-20cd194f3614"}
