{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_516","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The playthrough passed all three endings.\n\nSeed 1 finished in roughly 180 seconds. Seed 2 also completed. Boat and town travel times were realistic. The panic ending lasted one second.\n\nThe rain-to-patch sequence skipped the better-way flag because both actions completed in the same tick. Coverage tests confirmed the flags were still set correctly.\n\nThe rain-to-patch overlap likely occurred within the same one-second tick. The next steps are to run the full merc test suite, rebuild WASM, pack, and execute the verification plan.\n\nThe full merc test suite will run first to catch regressions before the WASM build. The playthrough is included again, but incremental compilation should keep it fast.\n\nThe full merc suite will run first. Then I will read pack.sh and build the WASM distribution. After packing, I will execute the browser and hub tests. Evidence will be copied to scratch, deviations and PROGRESS.md updated, and the checklist re-judged.\n\nThe verification plan is ordered: handin check, sim-combat, sim-world, playthrough, ui-audio, launch twice, browser hooks, hub, then run.sh all. Native tests do not require WASM, so the merc suite will run first. The WASM build must precede packing and browser tests because the shipping page needs the Rust fixes.\n\nThe full merc suite will run first. WASM and native tests share the target directory, so they cannot run concurrently. After packing, I will execute tests/run.sh all. I also need to verify that the fiction scan handles new comments correctly.\n\nI will avoid inflating issue counts. The final chat reply must include Source Information and feedback from exit-interview.json. I checked the playthrough comments for banned substrings and found none. The full merc suite includes the fiction scan, which the playthrough test does not cover.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ec1e0db-52d3-4cdb-bb6e-3caf512af749-77","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"bot","content":"bot: Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions","status":"completed"},{"id":"verify","content":"verify: Re-run sim, playthrough, wasm pack, and the plan verification checks","status":"in_progress"}],"merge":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ec1e0db-52d3-4cdb-bb6e-3caf512af749-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/run.sh","offset":115,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8ec1e0db-52d3-4cdb-bb6e-3caf512af749-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/pack.sh"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4655,"output_tokens":1449,"cache_read_input_tokens":133248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"856f561a-d275-4091-86e4-56c4c546f835"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8ec1e0db-52d3-4cdb-bb6e-3caf512af749-77","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] fp: fp: Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props\\n- [completed] endings: endings: Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs\\n- [completed] bot: bot: Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions\\n- [completed] dev: dev: Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip\\n- [in_progress] verify: verify: Re-run sim, playthrough, wasm pack, and the plan verification checks\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"fp: Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"endings: Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"bot: Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"dev: Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"verify: Re-run sim, playthrough, wasm pack, and the plan verification checks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"fp\":{\"content\":\"fp: Drive the rendered eye from world position and stance, and show first-person props\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"endings\":{\"content\":\"endings: Add an in-play burn/read/chair choice reached with normal inputs\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"bot\":{\"content\":\"bot: Remove campaign warps and flag stamps; bot uses player actions\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"dev\":{\"content\":\"dev: Wire dev teleport, spawn, world controls, and noclip\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"verify: Re-run sim, playthrough, wasm pack, and the plan verification checks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8ec1e0db-52d3-4cdb-bb6e-3caf512af749-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"115→  run_py \\\"$LOGS/hub.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/hub.py\\\"\\n}\\n\\ncase \\\"$mode\\\" in\\n  sim) run_sim ;;\\n120→  ui|audio) run_ui ;;\\n  browser) run_browser ;;\\n  hub) run_hub ;;\\n  all)\\n    run_sim\\n    run_ui\\n    run_browser\\n    run_hub\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n130→    echo \\\"FAIL: unknown mode $mode\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    ;;\\nesac\\n\\n# Pass count cannot go negative if a script's CHECKS was smaller than FAIL lines.\\nif [[ \\\"$pass\\\" -lt 0 ]]; then pass=0; fi\\necho \\\"PASS $pass FAIL $fail\\\"\\n[[ \\\"$fail\\\" == 0 ]]\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"115→  run_py \\\"$LOGS/hub.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/hub.py\\\"\\n}\\n\\ncase \\\"$mode\\\" in\\n  sim) run_sim ;;\\n120→  ui|audio) run_ui ;;\\n  browser) run_browser ;;\\n  hub) run_hub ;;\\n  all)\\n    run_sim\\n    run_ui\\n    run_browser\\n    run_hub\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n130→    echo \\\"FAIL: unknown mode $mode\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    ;;\\nesac\\n\\n# Pass count cannot go negative if a script's CHECKS was smaller than FAIL lines.\\nif [[ \\\"$pass\\\" -lt 0 ]]; then pass=0; fi\\necho \\\"PASS $pass FAIL $fail\\\"\\n[[ \\\"$fail\\\" == 0 ]]\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/run.sh\",\"offset\":115,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  run_py \\\"$LOGS/hub.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/hub.py\\\"\\n}\\n\\ncase \\\"$mode\\\" in\\n  sim) run_sim ;;\\n  ui|audio) run_ui ;;\\n  browser) run_browser ;;\\n  hub) run_hub ;;\\n  all)\\n    run_sim\\n    run_ui\\n    run_browser\\n    run_hub\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: unknown mode $mode\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    ;;\\nesac\\n\\n# Pass count cannot go negative if a script's CHECKS was smaller than FAIL lines.\\nif [[ \\\"$pass\\\" -lt 0 ]]; then pass=0; fi\\necho \\\"PASS $pass FAIL $fail\\\"\\n[[ \\\"$fail\\\" == 0 ]]\\n\",\"total_lines\":138}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8ec1e0db-52d3-4cdb-bb6e-3caf512af749-79","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Inject unmodified session.js, bindgen the existing wasm, pack one HTML, restore the template.\\nset -euo pipefail\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nWORK=\\\"$(cd \\\"$DEV/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nNAME=\\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503\\\"\\nHTML=\\\"$WORK/$NAME.html\\\"\\nPAGE=\\\"$ENGINE/web/index.html\\\"\\n10→SESSION=\\\"$DEV/hub/session.js\\\"\\nWASM=\\\"$ENGINE/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\\"\\n[[ -f \\\"$WASM\\\" ]] || { echo \\\"FAIL: wasm missing: $WASM\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\ncp \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$PAGE.template\\\"\\nrestore() { mv -f \\\"$PAGE.template\\\" \\\"$PAGE\\\"; }\\ntrap restore EXIT\\npython3 - \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\npage, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = page.read_text()\\n20→js = session.read_bytes()\\nmarker = b\\\"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\\"\\nraw = text.encode()\\nif raw.count(marker) != 1:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"marker missing\\\")\\nif b\\\"</script\\\" in js.lower() or b\\\"<!--\\\" in js or b\\\"<script\\\" in js.lower():\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"session.js cannot sit in a script element\\\")\\npage.write_bytes(raw.replace(marker, js, 1))\\nPY\\nBINDGEN=\\\"$(mktemp -d)\\\"\\n30→wasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$WASM\\\"\\n(\\n  cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n  python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" \\\\\\n    --title \\\"Jam Cry\\\" \\\\\\n    --description \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\" \\\\\\n    --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" \\\\\\n    --scene merc \\\\\\n    --out \\\"$HTML\\\"\\n)\\n40→rm -rf \\\"$BINDGEN\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$HTML\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\nhtml, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = html.read_text(errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\njs = session.read_text()\\nstart = text.find(\\\"<script>\\\")\\nend = text.find(\\\"</script>\\\", start)\\nbody = text[start + len(\\\"<script>\\\"):end]\\nif body != js:\\n50→    raise SystemExit(f\\\"first script is not session.js ({len(body)} vs {len(js)})\\\")\\nif text.count(\\\"<title>\\\") != 1 or \\\"<title>Jam Cry</title>\\\" not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"title\\\")\\nif text.count('name=\\\"theme-color\\\"') != 1 or 'content=\\\"#2a2420\\\"' not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"theme\\\")\\nprint(\\\"packed\\\", html.name, \\\"bytes\\\", html.stat().st_size)\\nPY\\nrestore\\ntrap - EXIT\\ngrep -q '/\\\\*__SESSION_JS__\\\\*/' \\\"$PAGE\\\"\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Inject unmodified session.js, bindgen the existing wasm, pack one HTML, restore the template.\\nset -euo pipefail\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nWORK=\\\"$(cd \\\"$DEV/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nNAME=\\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503\\\"\\nHTML=\\\"$WORK/$NAME.html\\\"\\nPAGE=\\\"$ENGINE/web/index.html\\\"\\n10→SESSION=\\\"$DEV/hub/session.js\\\"\\nWASM=\\\"$ENGINE/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\\"\\n[[ -f \\\"$WASM\\\" ]] || { echo \\\"FAIL: wasm missing: $WASM\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\ncp \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$PAGE.template\\\"\\nrestore() { mv -f \\\"$PAGE.template\\\" \\\"$PAGE\\\"; }\\ntrap restore EXIT\\npython3 - \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\npage, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = page.read_text()\\n20→js = session.read_bytes()\\nmarker = b\\\"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\\"\\nraw = text.encode()\\nif raw.count(marker) != 1:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"marker missing\\\")\\nif b\\\"</script\\\" in js.lower() or b\\\"<!--\\\" in js or b\\\"<script\\\" in js.lower():\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"session.js cannot sit in a script element\\\")\\npage.write_bytes(raw.replace(marker, js, 1))\\nPY\\nBINDGEN=\\\"$(mktemp -d)\\\"\\n30→wasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$WASM\\\"\\n(\\n  cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n  python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" \\\\\\n    --title \\\"Jam Cry\\\" \\\\\\n    --description \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\" \\\\\\n    --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" \\\\\\n    --scene merc \\\\\\n    --out \\\"$HTML\\\"\\n)\\n40→rm -rf \\\"$BINDGEN\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$HTML\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\nhtml, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = html.read_text(errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\njs = session.read_text()\\nstart = text.find(\\\"<script>\\\")\\nend = text.find(\\\"</script>\\\", start)\\nbody = text[start + len(\\\"<script>\\\"):end]\\nif body != js:\\n50→    raise SystemExit(f\\\"first script is not session.js ({len(body)} vs {len(js)})\\\")\\nif text.count(\\\"<title>\\\") != 1 or \\\"<title>Jam Cry</title>\\\" not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"title\\\")\\nif text.count('name=\\\"theme-color\\\"') != 1 or 'content=\\\"#2a2420\\\"' not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"theme\\\")\\nprint(\\\"packed\\\", html.name, \\\"bytes\\\", html.stat().st_size)\\nPY\\nrestore\\ntrap - EXIT\\ngrep -q '/\\\\*__SESSION_JS__\\\\*/' \\\"$PAGE\\\"\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/pack.sh\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Inject unmodified session.js, bindgen the existing wasm, pack one HTML, restore the template.\\nset -euo pipefail\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nWORK=\\\"$(cd \\\"$DEV/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nNAME=\\\"Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503\\\"\\nHTML=\\\"$WORK/$NAME.html\\\"\\nPAGE=\\\"$ENGINE/web/index.html\\\"\\nSESSION=\\\"$DEV/hub/session.js\\\"\\nWASM=\\\"$ENGINE/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/dist/shardfall.wasm\\\"\\n[[ -f \\\"$WASM\\\" ]] || { echo \\\"FAIL: wasm missing: $WASM\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\ncp \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$PAGE.template\\\"\\nrestore() { mv -f \\\"$PAGE.template\\\" \\\"$PAGE\\\"; }\\ntrap restore EXIT\\npython3 - \\\"$PAGE\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\npage, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = page.read_text()\\njs = session.read_bytes()\\nmarker = b\\\"/*__SESSION_JS__*/\\\"\\nraw = text.encode()\\nif raw.count(marker) != 1:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"marker missing\\\")\\nif b\\\"</script\\\" in js.lower() or b\\\"<!--\\\" in js or b\\\"<script\\\" in js.lower():\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"session.js cannot sit in a script element\\\")\\npage.write_bytes(raw.replace(marker, js, 1))\\nPY\\nBINDGEN=\\\"$(mktemp -d)\\\"\\nwasm-bindgen --target web --no-typescript --out-dir \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" --out-name shardfall \\\"$WASM\\\"\\n(\\n  cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n  python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py \\\"$BINDGEN\\\" \\\\\\n    --title \\\"Jam Cry\\\" \\\\\\n    --description \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\" \\\\\\n    --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" \\\\\\n    --scene merc \\\\\\n    --out \\\"$HTML\\\"\\n)\\nrm -rf \\\"$BINDGEN\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$HTML\\\" \\\"$SESSION\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib, sys\\nhtml, session = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])\\ntext = html.read_text(errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\njs = session.read_text()\\nstart = text.find(\\\"<script>\\\")