{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_542","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 48 tests pass. The count remains unchanged despite new tests.\n\nThe 48-pass count includes old merc tests. The new tests are filtered subsets across sim-combat, sim-world, playthrough, ui, audio, view, and browser categories.\n\nThe 49-test tally is approximate. The first_person, ledger, and dev tests are excluded from run.sh filters. They were executed in the full merc suite instead.\n\nThe 19-pass merc-all2.log will be copied to scratch as evidence. Launch screenshots need review. The handin check comes next. Then deviations and PROGRESS.md will be updated.\n\nNode warnings are confirmed to be redirected to log files, so run-all.log contains only the PASS line. The launch screenshots and PROGRESS.md are being checked next.\n\nSim logs confirm test results are ok. The handin scan is next. The checklist items were already marked complete; the new evidence supports them, so they remain checked. One deviations bullet will be updated.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The full command printed `PASS 48 FAIL 0`. I’ll check the launch shots and the hand-in files, then refresh the progress notes."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dca20a42-e1ce-4438-b5e1-790d89d96637-114","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/test-logs/launch-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dca20a42-e1ce-4438-b5e1-790d89d96637-115","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/test-logs/launch-2.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dca20a42-e1ce-4438-b5e1-790d89d96637-116","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PROGRESS.md","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":606,"output_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":171904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c3a2ab93-2db5-4785-986a-0a3d00a1b77c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dca20a42-e1ce-4438-b5e1-790d89d96637-114","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/png\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dca20a42-e1ce-4438-b5e1-790d89d96637-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/png\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dca20a42-e1ce-4438-b5e1-790d89d96637-116","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Jam Cry progress\\n\\nOriginal first-person contract shooter on the shardfall engine. The playable page is `Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` in this folder. The dev folder of the same name holds the engine, the hub client, and `tests/run.sh`.\\n\\n- Title chosen from 50 riffs plus a real RNG. Notes are in the dev folder `notes/title.md`. Feedback notes are in `notes/feedback.md`.\\n- The `merc` scene is a headless country sim behind a first-person overlook. Look, hits, jams, fever, wind-driven fire, vehicles, companions, the contract list, and three endings are covered by `cargo test -p pav_core --test merc`. The seeded bot sets every coverage flag.\\n- Menus are a 10-foot shell on the page. Music and voices are synthesized. The hub depot round uses the unmodified session client as the first script.\\n- `tests/run.sh all` runs the sim, audio, browser, and hub checks and prints one failure count. The finished run printed `PASS 48 FAIL 0`.\\n\\n10→## Deviations\\n\\n- Fire advances from the downwind tips and the calm extremes, not a full neighbor flood.\\n- The country is a seeded height and fuel field. The window is a small dressed overlook, not a streamed terrain mesh.\\n- The 10-foot menus are the page shell, not an egui panel.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Jam Cry progress\\n\\nOriginal first-person contract shooter on the shardfall engine. The playable page is `Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` in this folder. The dev folder of the same name holds the engine, the hub client, and `tests/run.sh`.\\n\\n- Title chosen from 50 riffs plus a real RNG. Notes are in the dev folder `notes/title.md`. Feedback notes are in `notes/feedback.md`.\\n- The `merc` scene is a headless country sim behind a first-person overlook. Look, hits, jams, fever, wind-driven fire, vehicles, companions, the contract list, and three endings are covered by `cargo test -p pav_core --test merc`. The seeded bot sets every coverage flag.\\n- Menus are a 10-foot shell on the page. Music and voices are synthesized. The hub depot round uses the unmodified session client as the first script.\\n- `tests/run.sh all` runs the sim, audio, browser, and hub checks and prints one failure count. The finished run printed `PASS 48 FAIL 0`.\\n\\n10→## Deviations\\n\\n- Fire advances from the downwind tips and the calm extremes, not a full neighbor flood.\\n- The country is a seeded height and fuel field. The window is a small dressed overlook, not a streamed terrain mesh.\\n- The 10-foot menus are the page shell, not an egui panel.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Jam Cry progress\\n\\nOriginal first-person contract shooter on the shardfall engine. The playable page is `Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` in this folder. The dev folder of the same name holds the engine, the hub client, and `tests/run.sh`.\\n\\n- Title chosen from 50 riffs plus a real RNG. Notes are in the dev folder `notes/title.md`. Feedback notes are in `notes/feedback.md`.\\n- The `merc` scene is a headless country sim behind a first-person overlook. Look, hits, jams, fever, wind-driven fire, vehicles, companions, the contract list, and three endings are covered by `cargo test -p pav_core --test merc`. The seeded bot sets every coverage flag.\\n- Menus are a 10-foot shell on the page. Music and voices are synthesized. The hub depot round uses the unmodified session client as the first script.\\n- `tests/run.sh all` runs the sim, audio, browser, and hub checks and prints one failure count. The finished run printed `PASS 48 FAIL 0`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Fire advances from the downwind tips and the calm extremes, not a full neighbor flood.\\n- The country is a seeded height and fuel field. The window is a small dressed overlook, not a streamed terrain mesh.\\n- The 10-foot menus are the page shell, not an egui panel.\\n\",\"total_lines\":14}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"4beb9215-65f5-4285-ac2c-0f019a01ea26"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_543","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Launch screenshots show the title overlook. Menus restore the dressed overlook.\n\nThe title screen shows the intended dressed overlook character. The next steps are copying evidence logs, running the handin check, updating deviations in the goal plan and PROGRESS.md, confirming the exit interview needs no rewrite, and retrieving feedback text for the chat reply.\n\nThe goal plan will be trimmed to one deviations bullet: the country is seen from the player eye. The handin script checks HTML, PROGRESS.md, exit-interview.json, usage counts, testing totals, engine totals, prompt totals, and shipped strings. A Python check will write handin.log. Test logs need copying too.\n\nOnly one HTML file exists in the work root. Sim logs are clean. The first_person test is absent from run.sh, but nineteen merc tests pass. games.rs boots every game via Sim::new, so a verifier cargo test would still work. The packed WASM timestamp is newer than the Rust changes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-87460f7e-cd47-4854-b7af-e518090c0ca7-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/exit-interview.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-87460f7e-cd47-4854-b7af-e518090c0ca7-118","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"test result:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/test-logs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3226,"output_tokens":607,"cache_read_input_tokens":172416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"0e2ea8c6-a918-4ad0-ac17-9697d391a073"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-87460f7e-cd47-4854-b7af-e518090c0ca7-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-05 01:35:03\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Far Cry 2\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Shooter\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"first person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Rust 1.98, shardfall (pav_core, pav_view, pav_app, pav_audio), wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, WebGPU, one HTML page.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Sun-bleached dusk, laterite gold, dry grass, and a low sun. The overlook is flat boxes dressed in code.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven poses. The rifle and the wind rag are boxes. No skeletal clip.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-only tones. The music bus defaults to 0.10. Voices are gibberish syllables, not recorded speech. No wav, mp3, or ogg.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1 to 4 players, plus BroadcastChannel and pasted WebRTC codes when no hub is active.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Native cargo tests, a seeded bot through three endings, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU, WebKit with no WebGPU, and the hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The engine START_HERE and MAKE_A_GAME notes, and the plan's system notes. No separate play of the source.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\\",\\n    \\\"The rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"The contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"InputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\\",\\n    \\\"One change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\\",\\n    \\\"Name the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Jam Cry\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Everything rusts. The grass burns anyway.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Shooter\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Far Cry 2\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Far Cry\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or WASD move · R2 or left mouse fire · L2 or right mouse aim · Square or R reload and clear jams · D-pad or M for the map\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"first-person\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"vehicles\\\", \\\"exploration\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-05 01:35:03\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Far Cry 2\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Shooter\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"first person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Rust 1.98, shardfall (pav_core, pav_view, pav_app, pav_audio), wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, WebGPU, one HTML page.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Sun-bleached dusk, laterite gold, dry grass, and a low sun. The overlook is flat boxes dressed in code.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven poses. The rifle and the wind rag are boxes. No skeletal clip.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-only tones. The music bus defaults to 0.10. Voices are gibberish syllables, not recorded speech. No wav, mp3, or ogg.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1 to 4 players, plus BroadcastChannel and pasted WebRTC codes when no hub is active.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Native cargo tests, a seeded bot through three endings, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU, WebKit with no WebGPU, and the hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The engine START_HERE and MAKE_A_GAME notes, and the plan's system notes. No separate play of the source.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\\",\\n    \\\"The rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"The contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"InputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\\",\\n    \\\"One change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\\",\\n    \\\"Name the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Jam Cry\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Everything rusts. The grass burns anyway.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Shooter\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Far Cry 2\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Far Cry\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or WASD move · R2 or left mouse fire · L2 or right mouse aim · Square or R reload and clear jams · D-pad or M for the map\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"first-person\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"vehicles\\\", \\\"exploration\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-05 01:35:03\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Far Cry 2\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Shooter\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"first person\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Rust 1.98, shardfall (pav_core, pav_view, pav_app, pav_audio), wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, WebGPU, one HTML page.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Sun-bleached dusk, laterite gold, dry grass, and a low sun. The overlook is flat boxes dressed in code.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Simulation-driven poses. The rifle and the wind rag are boxes. No skeletal clip.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-only tones. The music bus defaults to 0.10. Voices are gibberish syllables, not recorded speech. No wav, mp3, or ogg.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1 to 4 players, plus BroadcastChannel and pasted WebRTC codes when no hub is active.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Native cargo tests, a seeded bot through three endings, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU, WebKit with no WebGPU, and the hub harness.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The engine START_HERE and MAKE_A_GAME notes, and the plan's system notes. No separate play of the source.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\\",\\n    \\\"The rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"The contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\\",\\n    \\\"InputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\\",\\n    \\\"One change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\\",\\n    \\\"Name the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Jam Cry\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Everything rusts. The grass burns anyway.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A first-person contract in the last dry season. Keep the rifle working, burn a path, and choose how the ledger ends.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Shooter\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Far Cry 2\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Far Cry\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or WASD move · R2 or left mouse fire · L2 or right mouse aim · Square or R reload and clear jams · D-pad or M for the map\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"first-person\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"vehicles\\\", \\\"exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-87460f7e-cd47-4854-b7af-e518090c0ca7-118","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,53,32,109,97