ontent\":\"test result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 18 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":57,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 2 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 5 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":69,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 1 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":75,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 5 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":81,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 1 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 3 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"},{\"line_number\":93,\"content\":\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 1 filtered out; finished in 0.00s\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"55ec4e13-f10c-44a6-afd0-f8b734509d9a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_544","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test run remains green with zero failures.\n\nThe 26/6 counts are historical and unchanged. The new bugs were design fixes, not counted test failures. I will update PROGRESS deviations to mention the eye and the goal plan bullet. I will copy evidence and run the handin scanner. I will check TASK.md for forbidden name scan expectations and write a Python script in scratch.\n\nThe handin script will list HTML files, parse the exit interview, and scan fiction. It will skip packed HTML base64 for short banned substrings and search merc sources and visible page strings instead. I will write a handin.log recording file existence, JSON shape, and the passed fiction test. A Python script will also scan merc Rust sources for banned words.\n\nThe banned substring list is finalized. \"apr\" is flagged as dangerous. The existing fiction test already passed, so I will trust that result and run a careful scan. Far Cry 2 references will be restricted to lines containing \"Source\". Next I will write the handin script, copy logs, and update the plan and progress files.\n\nThe PROGRESS deviations will list four honest fixes: play driving the eye from the body, the ledger as an in-play choice, bot actions versus dev commands, and world changes. The goal plan checklist is already complete. Logs will be copied to scratch with new names.\n\nLaunch logs will be merged into scratch/launch.log. Browser, hub, and simulation logs will also be copied to scratch. The exit interview uses an en-dash. I will update files and copy evidence together. One HTML file must remain in the work root. I will keep at least one in_progress flag until the goal is fully done.\n\nI will mark verify as completed as the final step when saving evidence. The final chat reply must include all source fields and feedback in question order.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed0a55b9-65c1-4c7e-a7fb-defb6c521ab6-119","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/notes/feedback.md","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed0a55b9-65c1-4c7e-a7fb-defb6c521ab6-120","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Testing Feedback|Engine Feedback|Prompt Feedback|Source Information","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/TASK.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3294,"output_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":175616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"1f32715d-cfb5-48a3-8cc1-6d7ed7f07b6c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ed0a55b9-65c1-4c7e-a7fb-defb6c521ab6-119","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Jam Cry feedback notes\\n\\nThese are the answers copied into About and exit-interview.json. Counts come from the scratch logs: 14 compile errors, then 12 failing test runs after it compiled. Six of those stopped a contract route.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n\\nTesting caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\n\\n6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\n10→\\nThe most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\n\\nThe least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n\\nThe headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\n\\nThe rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\n20→\\nThe contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\n\\nThe hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\n\\nInputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\n\\nOne change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n30→\\nThe checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\n\\nThe country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\n\\nThe hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\n\\nName the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Jam Cry feedback notes\\n\\nThese are the answers copied into About and exit-interview.json. Counts come from the scratch logs: 14 compile errors, then 12 failing test runs after it compiled. Six of those stopped a contract route.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n\\nTesting caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\n\\n6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\n10→\\nThe most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\n\\nThe least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n\\nThe headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\n\\nThe rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\n20→\\nThe contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\n\\nThe hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\n\\nInputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\n\\nOne change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n30→\\nThe checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\n\\nThe country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\n\\nThe hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\n\\nName the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/notes/feedback.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Jam Cry feedback notes\\n\\nThese are the answers copied into About and exit-interview.json. Counts come from the scratch logs: 14 compile errors, then 12 failing test runs after it compiled. Six of those stopped a contract route.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n\\nTesting caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\\n\\n6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\\n\\nThe most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\\n\\nThe least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n\\nThe headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\\n\\nThe rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\\n\\nThe contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\\n\\nThe hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\\n\\nInputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\\n\\nOne change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n\\nThe checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\\n\\nThe country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\\n\\nThe hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\\n\\nName the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country.\\n\",\"total_lines\":37}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ed0a55b9-65c1-4c7e-a7fb-defb6c521ab6-120","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,65,83,75,46,109,100,10,57,50,58,35,35,32,83,111,117,114,99,101,32,73,