{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_553","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first-person camera fix looks solid. The eye tracks the body during play. Country tiles spawn around the player. Props follow the eye.\n\nThe test command omits the new tests. The playthrough log only ran the bot playthrough. The implementer claims tests pass, but the single command filters them out. They may still exist and pass if run separately.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule only counts new objections as defects if they are demonstrable in shipped behavior or unmet gating criteria. Gating criterion 9 requires the full test command to pass with zero failures. It does not require every test to be included in that single filter.\n\nThe missing tests create a real gap. The shipped command does not exercise the fixes. This is grounds to refute if the repository already has a way to test this change. I will check the implementer logs for the new tests.\n\nThe bot playthrough still pre-selects routes via `World::campaign(seed, route)` for Read and Chair. The new ledger test covers the choice logic, but the existing bot test does not exercise it. This means the ending choice and cheat removal may not be fully verified by the current suite.\n\nThe player choice path may only exist in unit tests. The campaign script likely still auto-assigns endings based on route. I need to check how Route::Human reaches the ledger, whether Read and Chair bypass the choice, and if the human route bot actually selects an ending via inputs.\n\nThe `present_ending()` helper may be a test-only shortcut that jumps straight to the ending. If so, the bot playthrough never exercises the actual player choice for any of the three endings. A true human new game uses `Route::Human`, so the requirement that the player chooses among three endings would remain unverified.\n\nThe prior gap explicitly required an in-play choice at the ledger, not just pre-selected routes. The bot could reach all three endings by playing three human games and choosing different ledger options, or it could keep using Route::Read and Route::Chair shortcuts.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4934e208-328b-4f61-a1f9-1251dbb3ae5e-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":286,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4934e208-328b-4f61-a1f9-1251dbb3ae5e-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":860,"limit":280}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4934e208-328b-4f61-a1f9-1251dbb3ae5e-68","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1100,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4934e208-328b-4f61-a1f9-1251dbb3ae5e-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","offset":200,"limit":230}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8476,"output_tokens":1308,"cache_read_input_tokens":146560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"47878a4a-5a2d-4bf0-9669-05fb8a629907"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4934e208-328b-4f61-a1f9-1251dbb3ae5e-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"286→\\nfn build_script(route: Route) -> Vec<Spec> {\\n    let mut v = vec![\\n        Spec::Boot,\\n290→        Spec::Map,\\n        Spec::Way,\\n        Spec::Reach { x: 0.0, z: 460.0, gps: true },\\n        Spec::Fever,\\n    ];\\n    if route == Route::Read {\\n        v.push(Spec::Blackout);\\n    } else {\\n        v.push(Spec::Pill);\\n    }\\n300→    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_a0\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Reach { x: -40.0, z: 640.0, gps: false });\\n    v.push(Spec::Fight);\\n    v.push(Spec::EnemyJam);\\n    v.push(Spec::Jam);\\n    v.push(Spec::Break);\\n    v.push(Spec::Rescue);\\n    for w in 1..=6 {\\n        v.push(Spec::Wound(w));\\n    }\\n310→    v.push(Spec::Loot);\\n    v.push(Spec::Reach { x: 170.0, z: 470.0, gps: false });\\n    v.push(Spec::Claim);\\n    v.push(Spec::Shop);\\n    v.push(Spec::Locker);\\n    v.push(Spec::Syrette);\\n    v.push(Spec::Tracker);\\n    v.push(Spec::Sleep { hours: 8.0 });\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_a1\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Drive { x: -520.0, z: -520.0 });\\n320→    v.push(Spec::Mono);\\n    for ig in 0..12 {\\n        v.push(Spec::Ignite(ig));\\n    }\\n    v.push(Spec::Tanks);\\n    v.push(Spec::Mounted);\\n    v.push(Spec::Panic);\\n    v.push(Spec::Animals);\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_b1\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Bus { x: 0.0, z: 380.0 });\\n330→    v.push(Spec::Drive { x: -260.0, z: -700.0 });\\n    v.push(Spec::Sleep { hours: 26.0 });\\n    v.push(Spec::Night);\\n    v.push(Spec::Boat);\\n    v.push(Spec::Stealth);\\n    v.push(Spec::Dart);\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_b2\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Repair);\\n    v.push(Spec::Rain);\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_b3\\\"));\\n340→    v.push(Spec::Better);\\n    match route {\\n        Route::Read => v.push(Spec::Overdose),\\n        Route::Chair => v.push(Spec::Die),\\n        _ => v.push(Spec::Patch),\\n    }\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_b4\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Tape);\\n    v.push(Spec::Ceasefire);\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_c1\\\"));\\n350→    v.push(Spec::Convoy);\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_c2\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Town);\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_c3\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Drive { x: -760.0, z: 620.0 });\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_d1\\\"));\\n    let end = match route {\\n        Route::Read => 1,\\n        Route::Chair => 2,\\n        _ => 0,\\n360→    };\\n    v.push(Spec::Ending(end));\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_d2\\\"));\\n    v\\n}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]\\npub struct World {\\n    pub seed: u64,\\n    pub rng: Rng,\\n370→    pub route: Route,\\n    pub screen: Screen,\\n    pub focus: usize,\\n    pub tab: usize,\\n    pub page: usize,\\n    pub difficulty: u8,\",\"content_concise\":\"286→\\nfn build_script(route: Route) -> Vec<Spec> {\\n    let mut v = vec![\\n        Spec::Boot,\\n290→        Spec::Map,\\n        Spec::Way,\\n        Spec::Reach { x: 0.0, z: 460.0, gps: true },\\n        Spec::Fever,\\n    ];\\n    if route == Route::Read {\\n        v.push(Spec::Blackout);\\n    } else {\\n        v.push(Spec::Pill);\\n    }\\n300→    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_a0\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Reach { x: -40.0, z: 640.0, gps: false });\\n    v.push(Spec::Fight);\\n    v.push(Spec::EnemyJam);\\n    v.push(Spec::Jam);\\n    v.push(Spec::Break);\\n    v.push(Spec::Rescue);\\n    for w in 1..=6 {\\n        v.push(Spec::Wound(w));\\n    }\\n310→    v.push(Spec::Loot);\\n    v.push(Spec::Reach { x: 170.0, z: 470.0, gps: false });\\n    v.push(Spec::Claim);\\n    v.push(Spec::Shop);\\n    v.push(Spec::Locker);\\n    v.push(Spec::Syrette);\\n    v.push(Spec::Tracker);\\n    v.push(Spec::Sleep { hours: 8.0 });\\n    v.push(Spec::Flag(\\\"contract_a1\\\"));\\n    v.push(Spec::Drive { x: -5