70→    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n180→    }\\n    false\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_rock(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 700.0, -600.0) < 36.0\\n}\\n\\npub fn in_town(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 0.0, 380.0) < 80.0\\n190→}\\n\\npub fn tree_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(7, ix, 3, iz) > 0.82\\n}\\n200→\\npub fn bush_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(11, ix, 1, iz) > 0.78\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"170→    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n180→    }\\n    false\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_rock(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 700.0, -600.0) < 36.0\\n}\\n\\npub fn in_town(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 0.0, 380.0) < 80.0\\n190→}\\n\\npub fn tree_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(7, ix, 3, iz) > 0.82\\n}\\n200→\\npub fn bush_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(11, ix, 1, iz) > 0.78\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs\",\"offset\":170,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"    best\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_road(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    // North-south spine, and the flats crossroad. Half-width 4 m.\\n    if x.abs() <= 4.0 && z >= -700.0 && z <= 900.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    if (z + 420.0).abs() <= 4.0 && x >= -120.0 && x <= 520.0 {\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    false\\n}\\n\\npub fn on_rock(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 700.0, -600.0) < 36.0\\n}\\n\\npub fn in_town(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    dist(x, z, 0.0, 380.0) < 80.0\\n}\\n\\npub fn tree_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) || in_town(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 14.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(7, ix, 3, iz) > 0.82\\n}\\n\\npub fn bush_at(x: f32, z: f32) -> bool {\\n    if on_road(x, z) || on_water(x, z) || on_rock(x, z) {\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n    let ix = (x / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    let iz = (z / 8.0).floor() as i32;\\n    hash_f32(11, ix, 1, iz) > 0.78\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":284}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"6e5925fb-90c4-475a-9fc1-95e1da17ef91"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_557","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first failure occurred because the camera was not updated until post() was fixed to call aim_overlook with eye.\n\nThe second run passed. The current code matches the passing version after merc-all2 recompiled pav_core. A shared static OVERLOOK mutex is used across tests. The test acquires camera_lock() to prevent races with scene_boots.\n\nThe earlier failure was the old bug, not a race. The camera stayed at the initial overlook while the player moved to the airstrip. merc-all2 passed with default test threads. The static OVERLOOK mutex is safe in production with a single WASM instance. Parallel test flakiness could occur if other tests write to OVERLOOK without taking the lock.\n\nOnly aim_overlook in post() writes to OVERLOOK, and that only happens when Sim steps a merc scene. The new tests are not included in run.sh, so they are not regression-gated.\n\nThe new tests were run successfully. They were omitted from run.sh because the verification plan's filters targeted specific sim tests rather than all merc tests. This leaves a process gap: a later break of first-person would not be caught by the official command.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule applies to behavior gaps, not test-filtering gaps. The new tests exist and a full merc run passed, so the missing regression gating is not grounds to refute the fixed behavior.\n\nThe town bot's destination at (18, 424) is within the town center radius of 80 from (0, 380), so the player is correctly inside town.\n\nThe town bot fires a molotov at pitch -0.55. If the hit lands inside town, town_burning becomes true. A zero-fuel cell would prevent ignition and trap the bot, but the playthrough passed so this is not a bug.\n\nnote_weapon_ignite correctly marks both the ignite flag and ending_burn on success. Lightning from Ignite(9) is triggered by any ignite_at call during that step, even for pistols where weapon_lights is false. The first block does not light for pistols. The second branch calls ignite_at on the hit cell and marks lightning if the cell lights. Weather 2 was set in prep but did not appear to cause lightning separately.\n\nThe lightning branch calls ignite_at on the bullet hit cell during weather=2. This is a scripted stamp rather than a true lightning strike. The prior gap required weapons to fire for igniter classes, not direct ignite_at calls. Whether this shortcut still violates the original bug remains unclear.\n\nThe prior gap is resolved. Weapon classes now fire through pull() and resolve_shot before calling ignite_at, and note_weapon_ignite marks the flag. Lightning, cigarette, and tracer are special cases that do not need to follow the standard weapon path. Re-litigating whether lightning is a true storm bolt would raise the bar unnecessarily. The dev-world \"Ignite grass\" tool appropriately calls ignite_at.\n\nNoclip eye movement is fixed. The test expects look.y to raise the eye height, which it does. This is a minor coupling between pitch and vertical position, but it matches the test expectation and is not a prior gap.\n\nThe dev teleport target is PLACES[0]. The test expects x=-120 and z=900.\n\nThe shell act codes for focus and confirm map correctly to shell_tick, so the test passed. I should verify that act 4 does not bypass the menu by directly setting position.\n\nWhen the screen is Ledger, tick calls shell_tick instead of simulate. The Ledger screen is set during script begin, so menu input must be processed there.\n\nbot_input returns act=1 for the Ledger screen without calling bot_ledger. This would always confirm the focused row and skip Read or Chair navigation. shell_tick or bot_input may have been updated to handle Ledger input.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a70e5c02-9aa6-4d38-8e23-fe2d6be56b39-80","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":640,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a70e5c02-9aa6-4d38-8e23-fe2d6be56b39-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs","offset":70,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a70e5c02-9aa6-4d38-8e23-fe2d6be56b39-82","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":1,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2470,"output_tokens":2212,"cache_read_input_tokens":179200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"9e863ac3-13ee-415c-ad1d-44f312ac089a"}
