   if let Some(ax) = v.get(\\\"axes\\\").filter(|x| x.is_array()) {\\n            frame.axes.x = num(ax, 0);\\n            frame.axes.y = num(ax, 1);\\n        }\\n        if let Some(bits) = v.get(\\\"pressed\\\").and_then(|n| n.as_u64()) {\\n            let bits = bits as u32;\\n            frame.pressed |= bits;\\n            frame.held |= bits;\\n        }\\n        if let Some(act) = v.get(\\\"act\\\").and_then(|n| n.as_u64()) {\\n            if act != 0 {\\n                frame.act = act as u32;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if let Some(h) = v.get(\\\"hover\\\").filter(|x| x.is_array()) {\\n            game.world.pointer = Some((num(h, 0), num(h, 1)));\\n        }\\n        if v.get(\\\"click\\\").and_then(|b| b.as_bool()) == Some(true) {\\n            game.world.pointer_click = true;\\n        }\\n        let lock = v.get(\\\"lock\\\").and_then(|b| b.as_bool()) == Some(true);\\n        if let Some(dev) = v.get(\\\"device\\\").and_then(|s| s.as_str()) {\\n            if dev == \\\"gamepad\\\" {\\n                game.world.device = pav_core::games::merc::Device::Gamepad;\\n                if lock {\\n                    game.world.device_lock = 1;\\n                }\\n            } else if dev == \\\"keyboard\\\" && game.world.device_lock == 0 {\\n                game.world.device = pav_core::games::merc::Device::Keyboard;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if v.get(\\\"touch\\\").and_then(|b| b.as_bool()) == Some(true) {\\n            game.world.touch_only = true;\\n        }\\n        if v.get(\\\"xbox\\\").and_then(|b| b.as_bool()) == Some(true) {\\n            game.world.xbox = true;\\n        }\\n        if v.get(\\\"hub\\\").and_then(|b| b.as_bool()) == Some(true) {\\n            game.world.hub = true;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    fn restore_save(world: &mut pav_core::games::merc::World) {\\n        let mut f = flags();\\n        if f.restored || world.hub {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        f.restored = true;\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.set(f));\\n        let Some(win) = web_sys::window() else { return };\\n        let Ok(Some(store)) = win.local_storage() else { return };\\n        let Ok(Some(blob)) = store.get_item(\\\"jamcry-save\\\") else { return };\\n        if blob.is_empty() || world.has_save {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        world.save_blob = blob;\\n        world.has_save = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn publish(sim: &Sim) {\\n        let Some(play) = sim.state.play.as_ref() else { return };\\n        if play.key() != \\\"merc\\\" {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let Some(game) = play.get::<Merc>() else { return };\\n        let mut f = flags();\\n        if game.world.saves_written > f.saved && !game.world.hub && !game.world.save_blob.is_empty() {\\n            f.saved = game.world.saves_written;\\n            if let Some(win) = web_sys::window() {\\n                if let Ok(Some(store)) = win.local_storage() {\\n                    let _ = store.set_item(\\\"jamcry-save\\\", &game.world.save_blob);\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let n = f.pubs;\\n        f.pubs = n.wrapping_add(1);\\n        FLAGS.with(|c| c.set(f));\\n        if !f.test && n % 15 != 0 {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let status = game.world.status().to_string();\\n        let ui = game.world.ui_value().to_string();\\n        let _ = bridge_publish(&status, &ui);\\n\",\"total_lines\":224}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"a56b08cd-efef-49b0-a63e-32ca0f610631"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_564","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The UI includes rows from self.rows(), which contains Ledger options.\n\nPointer click coordinates align with the hover y positions. Ledger clicks work because shell_tick skips apply_menu during Playing. The four gaps appear fixed. Now checking for regressions.\n\nDuring Ledger, advance_script still runs but skips the route check because shell_tick already switched the screen to Playing. This prevents premature script advancement.\n\nIdle attract is blocked during Ledger. The Ending screen only reopens the ledger when step_ready is false, so it won't clear the finale after begin. The first_person test uses CONFIRM and JUMP to start.\n\nThe first_person test sequence reached Playing correctly. Country synchronization only updates every eight minutes on anchor changes, and the camera was within twelve meters of a country tile when playing began. Static dress still spawns trees at the overlook origin.\n\nThe static dress trees are not a bug. They remain at the overlook origin while the player is elsewhere, so they only appear when walking nearby.\n\nThe player body is set to feet height. In first person, the inside of the character mesh may be visible. The test checks that country tiles exist near the eye, not that they are fully unobstructed by the body.\n\nThe camera eye sits roughly 1.58 meters above the player spawn height. The character head is about 1.6 meters above the feet. This places the camera inside the head. A large mesh could block the view. Pavilion characters are typically viewed from outside.\n\nThe camera follows the entity correctly. The prior gap required this behavior, and it is satisfied. A blocked view would be a new defect, but no gameplay screenshot is available to demonstrate it. Many first-person engines hide the player mesh; if this engine does not, the user would see their own character from inside.\n\nThe rifle prop is placed 0.46 meters in front of the eye. If the player body mesh is opaque and surrounds the camera, the rifle could be hidden inside the mesh. The post function sets the player position but does not hide the mesh, so the room character remains visible at the camera origin while the camera looks forward.\n\nThe player mesh is a capsule puppet with the head at the top. The camera sits at eye height looking forward, so it should see over the chest or through the head rather than inside the body. This is uncertain without evidence, but the structural requirement to drive the eye from position is satisfied. The wind rag flutter uses a box near the eye driven by the wind vector, which is adequate for the prior gap. The issue is not refuted.\n\nThe page_of teleport screen includes \"Next page\" and \"Reset to defaults\" rows. These are handled correctly. All screens respect the seven-row limit: dev_rows tab 4 shows exactly seven items, Ledger has three, Spawn has six, and Cheats page_of has seven. No screen exceeds this cap.\n\nDev balance pages also respect the seven-row limit. The reset row appears only on the final page, while earlier pages show six sliders plus a next-page entry.\n\nThe UI screen status uses `paint`'s `u.screen` field rather than the debug format string.\n\nA potential save regression exists: new world fields such as `finale` may lack serde defaults, which would break compatibility with old saves.\n\nThe save roundtrip test passed, confirming older saves remain compatible. The Route::Human ending script ignores its argument and lets the player choose, while the bot selects the first option. The Read route test also passed, with the bot moving focus to the second row and holding crouch for 180 seconds.\n\nThe vehicles test uses a fresh world without noclip and passed. The run.sh filter is not an unmet gating criterion because the tests were executed in merc-all2.\n\nThe ledger unit test uses present_ending to teleport directly to the ending screen for speed. This is a test-only shortcut, not shipped behavior. The full bot plays the complete route and opens the ledger through Spec::Ending begin. The choice mechanism is still verified correctly.\n\nThe first_person test passed in parallel with the full suite, so no camera lock race occurred this run. The static overlook origin could still race if another test steps the simulation.\n\nscene_boots_and_history_is_off might step the simulation and reset the camera to the menu eye if it calls post while not playing. merc-all2 passed, so either the tests do not overlap or the post call is skipped. The first_person test passed once, but a concurrent run could still cause a flake.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8c5ab1fb-1da7-4024-a1ab-56cfa0490cd4-97","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs","offset":55,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8c5ab1fb-1da7-4024-a1ab-56cfa0490cd4-98","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":2630,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2201,"output_tokens":2422,"cache_read_input_tokens":198272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"25da8708-fc36-4253-9fda-b86a40fe9c76"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8c5ab1fb-1da7-4024-a1ab-56cfa0490cd4-97","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"55→fn run(w: &mut World, input: &InputFrame, seconds: f32) {\\n    let n = (seconds / DT) as i32;\\n    for _ in 0..n {\\n        w.tick(input, DT);\\n    }\\n60→}\\n\\n/// The rendered eye is one process slot. Two merc sims must not write it at once.\\nfn camera_lock() -> std::sync::MutexGuard<'static, ()> {\\n    static LOCK: std::sync::Mutex<()> = std::sync::Mutex::new(());\\n    LOCK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn scene_boots_and_history_is_off() {\\n70→    let _cam = camera_lock();\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2, 9] {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(Merc::KEY, seed).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(sim.play().unwrap().key(), \\\"merc\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(sim.config.history_seconds, 0.0);\\n        for _ in 0..8 {\\n            sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(status[\\\"title\\\"], \\\"Jam Cry\\\");\\n80→    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn same_seed_matches_across_a_save() {\\n    let mut a = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut b = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    f.look.x = 0.01;\\n90→    for _ in 0..90 {\\n        a.tick(&f, DT);\\n        b.tick(&f, DT);\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), b.fingerprint());\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&a.save_json()).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(loaded.fingerprint(), a.fingerprint());\\n    a.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let mut loaded = loaded;\\n    loaded.tick(&f, DT);\\n100→    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), loaded.fingerprint());\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn look_and_stick_follow_yaw() {\",\"content_concise\":\"55→fn run(w: &mut World, input: &InputFrame, seconds: f32) {\\n    let n = (seconds / DT) as i32;\\n    for _ in 0..n {\\n        w.tick(input, DT);\\n    }\\n60→}\\n\\n/// The rendered eye is one process slot. Two merc sims must not write it at once.\\nfn camera_lock() -> std::sync::MutexGuard<'static, ()> {\\n    static LOCK: std::sync::Mutex<()> = std::sync::Mutex::new(());\\n    LOCK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn scene_boots_and_history_is_off() {\\n70→    let _cam = camera_lock();\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2, 9] {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(Merc::KEY, seed).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(sim.play().unwrap().key(), \\\"merc\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(sim.config.history_seconds, 0.0);\\n        for _ in 0..8 {\\n            sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(status[\\\"title\\\"], \\\"Jam Cry\\\");\\n80→    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn same_seed_matches_across_a_save() {\\n    let mut a = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut b = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    f.look.x = 0.01;\\n90→    for _ in 0..90 {\\n        a.tick(&f, DT);\\n        b.tick(&f, DT);\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), b.fingerprint());\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&a.save_json()).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(loaded.fingerprint(), a.fingerprint());\\n    a.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let mut loaded = loaded;\\n    loaded.tick(&f, DT);\\n100→    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), loaded.fingerprint());\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn look_and_stick_follow_yaw() {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs\",\"offset\":55,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"fn run(w: &mut World, input: &InputFrame, seconds: f32) {\\n    let n = (seconds / DT) as i32;\\n    for _ in 0..n {\\n        w.tick(input, DT);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/// The rendered eye is one process slot. Two merc sims must not write it at once.\\nfn camera_lock() -> std::sync::MutexGuard<'static, ()> {\\n    static LOCK: std::sync::Mutex<()> = std::sync::Mutex::new(());\\n    LOCK.lock().unwrap()\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn scene_boots_and_history_is_off() {\\n    let _cam = camera_lock();\\n    for seed in [1u64, 2, 9] {\\n        let mut sim = Sim::new(Merc::KEY, seed).unwrap();\\n        assert_eq!(sim.play().unwrap().key(), \\\"merc\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(sim.config.history_seconds, 0.0);\\n        for _ in 0..8 {\\n            sim.step(&InputFrame::default());\\n        }\\n        let status = sim.play().unwrap().status(&sim);\\n        assert_eq!(status[\\\"title\\\"], \\\"Jam Cry\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn same_seed_matches_across_a_save() {\\n    let mut a = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut b = World::fresh(11);\\n    let mut f = InputFrame::default();\\n    f.move_dir.y = 1.0;\\n    f.look.x = 0.01;\\n    for _ in 0..90 {\\n        a.tick(&f, DT);\\n        b.tick(&f, DT);\\n    }\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), b.fingerprint());\\n    let loaded = World::load_json(&a.save_json()).unwrap();\\n    assert_eq!(loaded.fingerprint(), a.fingerprint());\\n    a.tick(&f, DT);\\n    let mut loaded = loaded;\\n    loaded.tick(&f, DT);\\n    assert_eq!(a.fingerprint(), loaded.fingerprint());\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn look_and_stick_follow_yaw() {\\n\",\"total_lines\":930}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8c5ab1fb-1da7-4024-a1ab-56cfa0490cd4-98","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2630→        let pages = all.len().div_ceil(size);\\n        let p = (self.page as usize).min(pages - 1);\\n        let start = p * size;\\n        all[start..(start + size).min(all.len())].to_vec()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn ui_value(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        json!({\\n            \\\"screen\\\": format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", self.screen),\\n            \\\"rows\\\": self.rows(),\\n2640→            \\\"focus\\\": self.focus,\\n            \\\"label\\\": self.rows().get(self.focus).cloned().unwrap_or_default(),\\n            \\\"notice\\\": self.notice(),\\n            \\\"touch_controls\\\": false,\\n            \\\"glyph\\\": shell::glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", self.device, self.xbox),\\n            \\\"xbox\\\": self.xbox,\\n            \\\"device\\\": format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", self.device),\\n            \\\"about\\\": self.about_slice(),\\n        })\\n    }\\n2650→}\\n\\nfn wound_flag(n: u8) -> &'static str {\\n    match n {\\n        1 => \\\"wound_gunshot\\\",\\n        2 => \\\"wound_shrapnel\\\",\\n        3 => \\\"wound_burn\\\",\\n        4 => \\\"wound_fall\\\",\\n        5 => \\\"wound_tourniquet\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"wound_graze\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"2630→        let pages = all.len().div_ceil(size);\\n        let p = (self.page as usize).min(pages - 1);\\n        let start = p * size;\\n        all[start..(start + size).min(all.len())].to_vec()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn ui_value(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        json!({\\n            \\\"screen\\\": format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", self.screen),\\n            \\\"rows\\\": self.rows(),\\n2640→            \\\"focus\\\": self.focus,\\n            \\\"label\\\": self.rows().get(self.focus).cloned().unwrap_or_default(),\\n            \\\"notice\\\": self.notice(),\\n            \\\"touch_controls\\\": false,\\n            \\\"glyph\\\": shell::glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", self.device, self.xbox),\\n            \\\"xbox\\\": self.xbox,\\n            \\\"device\\\": format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", self.device),\\n            \\\"about\\\": self.about_slice(),\\n        })\\n    }\\n2650→}\\n\\nfn wound_flag(n: u8) -> &'static str {\\n    match n {\\n        1 => \\\"wound_gunshot\\\",\\n        2 => \\\"wound_shrapnel\\\",\\n        3 => \\\"wound_burn\\\",\\n        4 => \\\"wound_fall\\\",\\n        5 => \\\"wound_tourniquet\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"wound_graze\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs\",\"offset\":2630,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"        let pages = all.len().div_ceil(size);\\n        let p = (self.page as usize).min(pages - 1);\\n        let start = p * size;\\n        all[start..(start + size).min(all.len())].to_vec()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn ui_value(&self) -> serde_json::Value {\\n        json!({\\n            \\\"screen\\\": format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", self.screen),\\n            \\\"rows\\\": self.rows(),\\n            \\\"focus\\\": self.focus,\\n            \\\"label\\\": self.rows().get(self.focus).cloned().unwrap_or_default(),\\n            \\\"notice\\\": self.notice(),\\n            \\\"touch_controls\\\": false,\\n            \\\"glyph\\\": shell::glyph(\\\"confirm\\\", self.device, self.xbox),\\n            \\\"xbox\\\": self.xbox,\\n            \\\"device\\\": format!(\\\"{:?}\\\", self.device),\\n            \\\"about\\\": self.about_slice(),\\n        })\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nfn wound_flag(n: u8) -> &'static str {\\n    match n {\\n        1 => \\\"wound_gunshot\\\",\\n        2 => \\\"wound_shrapnel\\\",\\n        3 => \\\"wound_burn\\\",\\n        4 => \\\"wound_fall\\\",\\n        5 => \\\"wound_tourniquet\\\",\\n        _ => \\\"wound_graze\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":2806}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"7394e765-f70c-44b3-961e-786f48e2607f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_565","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both simulation tests acquire the camera lock.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb72c0ef-207c-4dfd-a5b5-f49a8aa489d6-99","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-verdict-8215da6fd761-2-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"merc-all2.log: 19 passed including first_person_eye_tracks_the_body, ledger_confirm_earns_the_chosen_ending, dev_menu_teleports_spawns_and_noclip_flies, and bot_plays_all_three_endings; mod.rs:244-262, world.rs:891-1000 and 1272-1385, shell.rs:286-325.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"All four prior gaps are fixed in the current sim and packed page. The camera eye follows the body and stance, the ledger is an in-play choice, town/boat/night/ignite no longer warp or stamp, and dev teleport, spawn, world, and noclip change state. merc-all2.log shows 19 passed; tests/run.sh all is PASS 48 FAIL 0.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fb72c0ef-207c-4dfd-a5b5-f49a8aa489d6-100","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/goal-classifier-8215da6fd761-2-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Verdict: Not Refuted\n\nThe four prior gaps are fixed in the current sources. `implementer/merc-all2.log` is a full `pav_core --test merc` run after those edits: **19 passed, 0 failed**. The packed HTML (11,548,171 bytes) is newer than `world.rs`, and `tests/run.sh all` still ends `PASS 48 FAIL 0` with both file:// launches reporting `CHECKS 4`.\n\n## Camera follows the body\n\nWhile `Screen::Playing`, `post` places the room body at `(world.x, height, world.z)`, rebuilds an 8 m country patch around that point, and copies `eye_pos()` (terrain height plus stance eye) into the overlook (`merc/mod.rs:244-262`, `world.rs:2589-2591`). The rifle, wind rag, map, GPS, and monocular are props parented to that eye (`mod.rs:183-221`). `app.rs:1241-1251` still builds `FpCam` from `overlook()`, so the published eye is what the page renders. `first_person_eye_tracks_the_body` steps a real `Sim` through New contract → play, walks, crouches, and checks the overlook eye, the rifle distance, and a country tile under the eye. That test failed once against the old pinned eye (`merc-all.log`: cam stayed `[0.15, 1.55, 4.2]`) and passed after the recompile.\n\n## Ledger is a choice\n\n`Spec::Ending` opens `Screen::Ledger` and clears `finale` (`world.rs:995-999`). The rows are Burn the ledger, Read the names, and Take the chair (`shell.rs:376`). `choose_finale` records the confirmed row; burn is marked only after a lighting shot, read only after 180 s, chair only on interact (`world.rs:1811-1812`, `2117-2119`, `2145-2146`). `bot_input` on the ledger calls `bot_ledger` (`world.rs:662-664`), so Read and Chair are menu moves, not `World::campaign` shortcuts that skip the screen. `ledger_confirm_earns_the_chosen_ending` and `bot_plays_all_three_endings` both passed.\n\n## Town, boat, night, and ignites are played\n\n- Town only arms a molotov (`world.rs:991-992`). The bot walks to the town and fires (`bot_town`, `1302-1312`). `town_burned` is set when a burning cell is inside the town (`1073-1077`, `2389-2396`).\n- The boat is left unoccupied on the water (`world.rs:901-913`). The bot walks to it, boards with Use, then drives (`bot_boat`, `1288-1299`).\n- Night sets the clock in `begin` and sets `night_contract` only after the body moves (`world.rs:894-895`, `1055-1059`).\n- Ignite steps arm the matching weapon (`prep_ignite`, `2317-2342`). Flags for flare, rocket, flamer, mortar, molotov, and frag are marked from `resolve_shot` when that weapon actually lights a cell (`note_weapon_ignite`, `2346-2357`, `1807-1810`).\n\n## Dev tools change state\n\n`activate` on the dev screen calls `dev_teleport`, `dev_spawn`, and `dev_world` (`shell.rs:309-317`). Teleport writes the named place (`world.rs:2433-2443`). Spawn adds a soldier, animal, truck, vehicle, or barrel (`2446-2473`). World sets time, weather, wind, or a grass fire (`2476-2488`). Noclip is read in `move_body` and flies at 24 m/s, including vertical eye (`1471-1483`). `dev_menu_teleports_spawns_and_noclip_flies` drives those through `tick` and passed.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3237,"output_tokens":1376,"cache_read_input_tokens":200448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"ac183a60-1fae-49b0-b241-d64ce6dfb6ec"}
