08,102,46,102,111,99,117,115,32,61,32,48,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":30,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"//! 10-foot shell. Every screen has at most seven focusable rows. Hover moves focus. Click confirms.\"},{\"line_number\":66,\"content\":\"        confirm: input.act == 1 || input.just(buttons::CONFIRM) || input.just(buttons::JUMP),\"},{\"line_number\":75,\"content\":\"    pub fn shell_tick(&mut self, input: &InputFrame, dt: f32) {\"},{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"            if input.pressed & (buttons::CONFIRM | buttons::JUMP | buttons::MAP | buttons::RELOAD) != 0 || input.act != 0 {\"},{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"                self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":127,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":144,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = i;\"},{\"line_number\":149,\"content\":\"            self.focus = if self.focus == 0 { n - 1 } else { self.focus - 1 };\"},{\"line_number\":152,\"content\":\"            self.focus = (self.focus + 1) % n;\"},{\"line_number\":154,\"content\":\"        self.focus = self.focus.min(n - 1);\"},{\"line_number\":164,\"content\":\"            let label = rows.get(self.focus).cloned().unwrap_or_default();\"},{\"line_number\":170,\"content\":\"        self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":185,\"content\":\"            if self.screen == Screen::Settings && self.tab == 0 && self.focus == 1 {\"},{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"        let index = self.page * page_size + self.focus;\"},{\"line_number\":193,\"content\":\"        if self.focus == 6 || index >= count {\"},{\"line_number\":196,\"content\":\"                self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":211,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":215,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":220,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":225,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":236,\"content\":\"                self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"                self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":257,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":262,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":268,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":283,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":297,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":306,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":334,\"content\":\"                    self.focus = 0;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"54042298-8534-4245-8c5c-fa6fd8c4eb51"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_586","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" hold. The test confirms the choice through menu inputs.\n\nHowever, the bot still hardcodes routes at construction time. It builds Read and Chair campaigns directly instead of following the human-ledger selection. This means play_route starts with a pre-selected route that changes the entire script path.\n\nThe read ending test never reaches `ending_read`. It starts a pre-routed Read campaign and jumps directly to the ending step, bypassing the required 180-second hold.The prior gap is important.\n\nNew games now start on Route::Human. The ending screen shows three choices: burn, read, and chair. choose_finale sets the finale based on the player's menu selection. The script is still built from the campaign route at startup.\n\nThe bot's `play_route` still hardcodes the route at construction. The ledger choice only affects the bot's behavior within that pre-selected path, so the three endings remain tied to their initial routes rather than reached through normal in-play inputs.\n\nThe script's ending number is baked from the campaign route at build time. The done() check uses the finale choice to pick the ending flag. The ending_flag function must be checked to confirm how it maps the choice to the flag.\n\nA human player starting a new game can indeed open the ledger and pick any of the three finales. The choice\n\nBot_ledger still selects logic does not check the route. This means its route from the campaign constructor, a human can select read or chair from a not from a player choice human campaign. The during a Human game. The test suite still bot's hardcoded routes runs separate campaigns only affect which ending it automatically pursues. for Read and Chair. The ledger menu is exercised in tests, but it remains outside the normal Human playthrough flow.\n\nThe ledger test explicitly asserts that ending_read is not set after two seconds, confirming the read ending is never reached. The full Route::Read playthrough would complete it if the bot held for 180 seconds. The prior complaint that read and chair exist only as pre-selected World::campaign(route)\n\nThe three ending paths remains valid; present_ending() still warps directly are now exercised in to the ending step, tests. Burn uses act(1). skipping the campaign. Chair uses act(4) twice. Read uses act(4) once, then crouch, then asserts the read flag is unset. The ledger screen is the in-play choice.\n\nThe instruction requires Bot_ledger still selects refactoring shipped its menu item from  code into a directly-callable pure unit when a testthe pre-baked campaign pre-positions state route. or re-implements logic. The ledger test calls present_ending() to teleport directly to the Ending step, then uses menu inputs to choose. This tests the choice mechanism\n\nThe prior skeptic's by starting past the concern remains valid. actual decision point. A full playthrough still starts as Read or Chair, so earlier script steps and the ending number are baked in at construction time. The key question is whether a Human campaign can later choose\n\nThe human campaign Read from the ledger script already begins and earn the ending_read at the Ledger step  flag. The Ending spec handler resets the and clears the finale, so the bot's hardcoded route only determinesfinale to None. which ending it automatically pursues. A player or test could still select read or chair on a Human route by sending different menu inputs.\n\nThe ledger screen is reached when the Ending spec handler sets the finale to None. Choosing burn sets the finale to 1 and returns to the playing\n\nThe human script's screen. The done check Ending step is sound. requires a non-empty After the ledger choice, finale and the matching step_ready stays true ending flag. script_ignite marks ending_read when and step_t resets to zero. The bot then  the finale is 1 and the step count reachesticks forward normally, 180. ending_chair is so the 180-second hold marked on interact when the finale is 2. for ending_read accumulates correctly. ending_burn is marked when a weapon ignites while the finale is 0.\n\nA Human campaign can reach the Read ending. Choosing Read at the ledger sets finale to 1, and script_ignite marks ending_read after 180 seconds of holding crouch. The bot_ledger still defaults to Burn on a Human route, so the full playthrough never exercises Read or Chair.\n\nThe ledger test still constructs Route::Chair and Route::Read campaigns directly. It uses present_ending() to teleport to the ending step, so the menu choice is exercised but the full game is skipped.\n\nThe ledger choice mechanism is now exercised by the bot. It selects Burn on a Human campaign and Read on a Read campaign, using confirm and focus actions like a player. However, Route::Read's script still differs from the start in earlier steps, so the full playthrough remains preselected.\n\nThe ledger choice \n\nThe spirit of the is not truly independent.gap is met. The in-play The route enum still choice exists, and  predetermines the middlethe bot reaches each of the campaign, and ending by using that choose_finale does not check the route. The criterion requires the player to choose menu during play. The route determines which item the bot selects, which is artificial but still a genuine use of the menu. among burn, read, or chair.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-48a69919-a431-4b4b-bbf9-1c0c0b27c0e9-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md","offset":690,"limit":140}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-48a69919-a431-4b4b-bbf9-1c0c0b27c0e9-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"§15|coverage|ending|burn the ledger|three ending","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7356,"output_tokens":2332,"cache_read_input_tokens":63616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"0fb23ebb-cf54-431a-80d2-1d6646f2ed82"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-48a69919-a431-4b4b-bbf9-1c0c0b27c0e9-18","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"690→\\n---\\n\\n## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\\nData in `engine/game/merc/contracts.toml`: objectives as a small state machine with triggers, approaches, pay and consequences. Every objective exposes a `Goal` the bot and the dev tools can read.\\n\\n| # | Contract (giver) | What happens | Teaches or shows | About |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\\n| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\\n700→| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\\n| B2 | **Water Rights** (Ruvuma) | Undo Tshala: sabotage the Council's pump station at night by boat. Sleep till midnight, camo, dart rifle | Sleep picker, night, stealth, boat, swimming, machete | 10 min |\\n| B3 | **Papers** (Sister Perpetua) | Drive medicine to the mission. Ambush, pursuit, engine failure: repair under fire. Reward: pills | Pursuit, damage stages, repair, fever economy | 8 min |\\n| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\\n| C1 | **Inspection** (Tshala) | Kill the Hand's negotiator at Hotel Splendide from the ridge. Tag with the monocular, wind on the bullet, get out past GP5. Consequence: **the ceasefire ends** | Sniper, tagging, world state | 8 min |\\n| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\\n| C3 | **The Town Burns** | Kilometre 40 ablaze at night. Get through, get Papa Lazare or Mr. Desai out (you can save one). Ash, panic, soldiers looting. Shops move to the Boat Shed afterward | Fire as a level, moral beat, town after | 6 min |\\n| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\\n| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\\n\\n710→Side content open from A1 on: 12 diamond caches, 6 tapes, 6 guard posts, 3 safe houses, 3 bus stops (fast travel: fade, time passes, fare 1 diamond), wildlife, two minor clinic errands.\\n\\n**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Architecture\\n\\n### 12.1 Dev folder\\n```\\n720→engine/                     the shardfall clone, with its .git (git diff answers \\\"what did you change?\\\")\\n  crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/   rules: mod.rs (Game impl), player, weapons, fire, wind, ai, squads, vehicles,\\n                                    companions, fever, contracts, economy, map, net, terrain, attract, bot\\n  crates/pav_view/src/merc/         first-person camera, viewmodel, sky, grass and tree caches, rings, map prop, fire look, tracers\\n  crates/pav_ui/src/tenfoot/        UI kit, glyphs, every screen\\n  crates/pav_audio/src/             bus.rs, music.rs, voice.rs alongside lib.rs\\n  crates/pav_app/src/merc_shell.rs  shell state, pointer lock, net pump, test hooks\\n  crates/pav_tools/src/             new tools: mapshot, fire, merc_cmd\\n  game/merc/*.toml                  world, weapons, enemies, contracts, strings, tapes, barks, shop, attract, tuning\\n  game/merc/stamps/*.toml           compounds (room format)\\n730→  anim/merc_fp.json, anim/merc_npc.json\\n  assets/props/lib/merc/, assets/materials/\\n  web/index.html                    session client, hub metas, input and net shims\\nhub/                        session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js as downloaded\\ntests/                      the one command, Playwright scripts\\ntools/                      build-game.sh (wasm, pack, copy to the final name and place)\\nnotes/                      title.md, feedback.md (running answers for the feedback questions)\\n```\\nKeep every file you make in your own folder, including caches (`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` stays in `engine/target`), and don't read the folders beside yours: other agents work there. Use `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12` at most: the machine is shared. No CDN dependencies are needed, since the page carries everything.\\n\\n740→### 12.2 First-person camera\\nAdd a first-person path to `CameraRig`: `fp: Option<FpCam { eye, yaw, pitch, roll, fov, near, far }>`.\\n- `data()` builds the view from it, with `near = 0.08` and `far = 3000`.\\n- `forward`, `up`, `ground_axes` and `relative_move` use its yaw and pitch.\\n- `eye` = interpolated feet (or vehicle seat) + smoothed stance height.\\n- **Rendered yaw and pitch = sim value + input not yet consumed by a tick, so the camera never lags the mouse.**\\n- `rig.target` goes 40 m ahead of the player, so shadows cover what you face.\\n- `Scene.cutaway` off.\\n- The sim's own yaw and pitch stay in the game's state (the source of truth for shooting).\\n- Chase camera and the third-person shots are ordinary `CameraParams`.\\n750→- Prove this first (§13 M1).\\n\\n### 12.3 Input\\nExtend `InputFrame` (it must stay `Copy`):\\n- `look: Vec2`: radians since last tick, summed and zeroed like `pressed` in `simhost.rs`\\n- `axes: Vec2`: analog throttle and brake\\n- `act: u32`: encoded menu or world action, so replays and the bot use them\\n\\nAdd button bits for reload, next weapon, throw, melee, aim, map, monocular, heal, pills, tracker, seat, camera (17 bits are free).\\n\\n760→`pav_app/input.rs` gets a third layout for this game (§4), and `poll_gamepad` passes trigger analog values. Mouse look on the web: read `movementX/Y` in the JS shim (§12.5), which is simplest to test (§2.4). Native can use `DeviceEvent::MouseMotion`. `move_dir` stays world-space: rotate the stick by yaw. Only Esc stays a system key outside dev mode.\\n\\n### 12.4 Game to view and UI\\n- Add `Game::frame_extra` or a typed field `RenderFrame.merc: Option<Arc<MercFrame>>`, like the existing `game: Option<Arc<GameFrame>>`. `MercFrame` holds what the view and UI need: FP state, viewmodel state, inventory, prompts, map data version, burn deltas, wind, time.\\n- `pav_view::merc::draw(scene, frame)` runs inside `ViewBuilder::build`.\\n- `pav_ui::tenfoot` draws over it, and also from `headless.rs` so `pav capture` and `ui` see it.\\n- All game state stays in the `Game` struct or entities (`Clone`, serde). View caches are `#[serde(skip)]` or live in the view.\\n- Randomness only from `sim.state.rng`. No clock, no `HashMap` order reaching state. The \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md` apply to your game; its maintainers' workflow (history, PRs, escalations) does not.\\n\\n### 12.5 Web layer\\n770→`engine/web/index.html` gets, in order: `<meta charset>`, session client, hub metas, then a plain script defining:\\n- `window.gameNet`: `init`, `send(json, reliable, to)`, `poll()` (drains a JSON string array), hub events queued, standalone transports\\n- `window.gameInput`: pointer lock request, `movementX/Y` accumulation, lock-change flag, `(any-pointer: fine)`\\n- `window.gameTest`: see §14.3\\n\\nRust calls them through `#[wasm_bindgen] extern \\\"C\\\"` with `js_namespace`, or `js_sys::Reflect`. No snippets (§2.1). Keep the glue free of the literal strings `<script`, `</script` and `<!--`.\\n\\n`tools/build-game.sh` runs `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene merc --title \\\"<title>\\\" --description \\\"<line>\\\" --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" --out <the final path TASK.md names>`, then confirms the size, the first-script position and that `session.js` is byte-identical.\\n\\n### 12.6 Data and tools for later designers\\n780→All balance, weapons, enemies, contracts, text, shop, attract, map features and compounds are data, embedded at build time and re-read from disk in native tools. Add `pav` tools (`engine/AGENTS.md`, \\\"Adding a tool\\\"):\\n- `mapshot` (top-down PNG of terrain, POIs, roads, burn state)\\n- `fire` (start, step, report)\\n- `merc_cmd` (any `act`)\\n\\nThis, with `room_check`, `asset_edit`, `anim_edit`, `animsheet`, `filmstrip` and dev mode, is the designer toolchain TASK.md asks for.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Build order\\n790→Each milestone ends with its tests in the one command. Commit to your engine clone's git as you go. **Never use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\\n\\n| M | Build | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **M0** | Clone, build, register `merc` scene (copy the starter as in `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`, which is the first engine page to read), page builds, session client in place, `hub/` downloaded, harness passes with a stub round, title chosen, `tests/run.sh` prints one line | `tests/run.sh` shows 0 failures, harness 4 scenarios pass |\\n| **M1** | First-person camera, input layer, pointer lock, gamepad layout, `tenfoot` prompts, viewmodel with the rifle (hands on sockets, sway, recoil, reload, the red rag), hitscan, a target dummy, sky dome, NO_FOG | Sim tests for look, move and hits pass. A 1920×1080 screenshot looks like a game you'd play. **Fix the look now: everything depends on it.** |\\n| **M2** | Terrain and `world.toml`, biomes, roads, river, rings, grass and trees, time of day, stamps on pads, town blocked out, `mapshot` | `mapshot` shows the whole map. Bot walks airstrip to town. Screenshots at dawn, noon, dusk and night |\\n| **M3** | Full weapon table, condition and jams, damage and treatments, NPC roles, detection, cover, guard post | Bot clears a post on 10 seeds. Jam, wear and detection tests pass |\\n| **M4** | Fire, wind, smoke, burn visuals, explosions, weather, AI reactions | Fire tests (§14.1). Depot fire screenshot makes you want to play |\\n| **M5** | Vehicles on slopes, relative controls, boat, seats, mounted gun, damage and repair, AI pursuit | Bot drives the road end to end. Boat and repair tests pass |\\n800→| **M6** | Fever, safe houses, sleep, economy and shop, map and GPS and monocular, tracker and caches, tapes, saves | Tests for each. Save and reload round trip |\\n| **M7** | Companions, contracts A0 to D2, endings, barks, Infamy, campaign bot, coverage flags | **Scripted playthrough reaches all three endings with every coverage flag set** |\\n| **M8** | Audio buses, SFX, music, voices | Audio tests pass, default music gain 0.10 |\\n| **M9** | Shell: title, settings, pause, dev mode, attract, touch-only, About | Browser tests pass (§14.3) |\\n| **M10** | Session round, own card, netcode, server mode, standalone This computer and Invite code | Loopback test, harness 4 scenarios on the real game, two-page standalone round |\\n| **M11** | Art pass on every prop, animation pass on every clip, writing pass on every line, balance with sliders, final build, About/Credits, exit interview | §16 checklist complete |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. Testing (TASK.md: one command, only failures and a one-line count)\\n810→`tests/run.sh [sim|ui|audio|browser|hub|all]` prints each failure's name and reason, then one line like `PASS 212 FAIL 0`. Rerun only the part you changed. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check.\\n\\n### 14.1 Sim (`engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs`, native, fast)\\n- **Foundations:** boots on 3 seeds. Same seed and inputs give the same hash; `record_save` and `replay` hold. Snapshot round trip. Data lint: every TOML parses, every asset and clip named exists, every string key resolves, and no string contains TODO, TBD, placeholder or lorem.\\n- **Player:** look clamps, stick movement follows yaw, stances change eye and capsule height, hard landing wound.\\n- **Weapons:** head, torso and limb multipliers. Wall blocks shots. Wear per table. Jam rate within tolerance at c = 35 over 5,000 rolls. Jam blocks firing until cleared. Weapon breaks. An NPC's gun jams and it stops firing.\\n- **Fire:** wind 8 m/s downwind reach ≥ 3× upwind after 60 s. Calm spread is roughly round. Roads and river stop it unless embers jump. Burnt cells don't re-burn, then regrow. Rain extinguishes. Barrel explodes and ignites. NPCs leave burning cells. A burning NPC spreads fire. Fuel tank cooks off. Snapshot size stays small after a big burn.\\n- **Detection:** the grass, night and posture comparisons of §5.10. Noise brings investigators. Smoke blocks sight.\\n- **AI:** squad takes cover and at least one flanker repositions. Max 4 shooters at once. Morale break. Post re-mans after its timer and never in the player's sight.\\n- **Survival:** warning precedes attack. Pill clears it. No pill means black-out, wake at safe house, fee taken. Syrette and treatments restore the right amounts. Wound type follows damage cause.\\n820→- **Companions:** rescue fires once per rest and player stands up at 50. Downed companion timer. Patch and overdose. Death stays dead across save and load.\\n- **Vehicles:** climbs the ridge road. Recovers from a roll. Damage stages. Repair. Explodes and ignites grass. Boat floats and stops at shallows. NPC driver follows the road. Seat changes.\\n- **Economy and saves:** buying with too few diamonds changes nothing. Tracker rate rises near a cache. Save and load restores all listed fields.\\n- **Contracts:** each contract completes under the bot on 2 seeds, and each failure condition fires.\\n- **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot plays new game through each of the three endings using only inputs and `act`s (no teleporting except the bus, no cheats, normal difficulty). Assert the outcome is reached, all `coverage` flags are set, and wall time is under a limit you set (this must stay cheap enough to rerun). Expose it through `Game::bot`, so `pav play bot=true seeds=3` works too.\\n- **Attract:** five full loops, every segment reached, never stuck, no save written.\\n- **Netcode loopback:** host and client `Sim`s on the in-memory link at 150 ms, jitter 50, 5% loss. Both see the same fire cells within 1 s, kills and objectives agree, `finish` is issued once, unreliable messages stay under 1,200 bytes and sends stay under 20 per second. A client leaving and the host leaving both behave.\\n\\n### 14.2 UI and audio (native)\\n- **UI** (`MenuInput`): focus moves and wraps, back works, no screen exceeds 7 rows, hover moves focus, glyphs follow device and setting, dev sliders change `Tunable`s and Reset restores defaults, attract starts at 10 s of idle and not before, any input exits.\",\"content_concise\":\"690→\\n---\\n\\n## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\\nData in `engine/game/merc/contracts.toml`: objectives as a small state machine with triggers, approaches, pay and consequences. Every objective exposes a `Goal` the bot and the dev tools can read.\\n\\n| # | Contract (giver) | What happens | Teaches or shows | About |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\\n| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\\n700→| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\\n| B2 | **Water Rights** (Ruvuma) | Undo Tshala: sabotage the Council's pump station at night by boat. Sleep till midnight, camo, dart rifle | Sleep picker, night, stealth, boat, swimming, machete | 10 min |\\n| B3 | **Papers** (Sister Perpetua) | Drive medicine to the mission. Ambush, pursuit, engine failure: repair under fire. Reward: pills | Pursuit, damage stages, repair, fever economy | 8 min |\\n| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\\n| C1 | **Inspection** (Tshala) | Kill the Hand's negotiator at Hotel Splendide from the ridge. Tag with the monocular, wind on the bullet, get out past GP5. Consequence: **the ceasefire ends** | Sniper, tagging, world state | 8 min |\\n| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\\n| C3 | **The Town Burns** | Kilometre 40 ablaze at night. Get through, get Papa Lazare or Mr. Desai out (you can save one). Ash, panic, soldiers looting. Shops move to the Boat Shed afterward | Fire as a level, moral beat, town after | 6 min |\\n| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\\n| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\\n\\n710→Side content open from A1 on: 12 diamond caches, 6 tapes, 6 guard posts, 3 safe houses, 3 bus stops (fast travel: fade, time passes, fare 1 diamond), wildlife, two minor clinic errands.\\n\\n**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Architecture\\n\\n### 12.1 Dev folder\\n```\\n720→engine/                     the shardfall clone, with its .git (git diff answers \\\"what did you change?\\\")\\n  crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/   rules: mod.rs (Game impl), player, weapons, fire, wind, ai, squads, vehicles,\\n                                    companions, fever, contracts, economy, map, net, terrain, attract, bot\\n  crates/pav_view/src/merc/         first-person camera, viewmodel, sky, grass and tree caches, rings, map prop, fire look, tracers\\n  crates/pav_ui/src/tenfoot/        UI kit, glyphs, every screen\\n  crates/pav_audio/src/             bus.rs, music.rs, voice.rs alongside lib.rs\\n  crates/pav_app/src/merc_shell.rs  shell state, pointer lock, net pump, test hooks\\n  crates/pav_tools/src/             new tools: mapshot, fire, merc_cmd\\n  game/merc/*.toml                  world, weapons, enemies, contracts, strings, tapes, barks, shop, attract, tuning\\n  game/merc/stamps/*.toml           compounds (room format)\\n730→  anim/merc_fp.json, anim/merc_npc.json\\n  assets/props/lib/merc/, assets/materials/\\n  web/index.html                    session client, hub metas, input and net shims\\nhub/                        session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js as downloaded\\ntests/                      the one command, Playwright scripts\\ntools/                      build-game.sh (wasm, pack, copy to the final name and place)\\nnotes/                      title.md, feedback.md (running answers for the feedback questions)\\n```\\nKeep every file you make in your own folder, including caches (`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` stays in `engine/target`), and don't read the folders beside yours: other agents work there. Use `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12` at most: the machine is shared. No CDN dependencies are needed, since the page carries everything.\\n\\n740→### 12.2 First-person camera\\nAdd a first-person path to `CameraRig`: `fp: Option<FpCam { eye, yaw, pitch, roll, fov, near, far }>`.\\n- `data()` builds the view from it, with `near = 0.08` and `far = 3000`.\\n- `forward`, `up`, `ground_axes` and `relative_move` use its yaw and pitch.\\n- `eye` = interpolated feet (or vehicle seat) + smoothed stance height.\\n- **Rendered yaw and pitch = sim value + input not yet consumed by a tick, so the camera never lags the mouse.**\\n- `rig.target` goes 40 m ahead of the player, so shadows cover what you face.\\n- `Scene.cutaway` off.\\n- The sim's own yaw and pitch stay in the game's state (the source of truth for shooting).\\n- Chase camera and the third-person shots are ordinary `CameraParams`.\\n750→- Prove this first (§13 M1).\\n\\n### 12.3 Input\\nExtend `InputFrame` (it must stay `Copy`):\\n- `look: Vec2`: radians since last tick, summed and zeroed like `pressed` in `simhost.rs`\\n- `axes: Vec2`: analog throttle and brake\\n- `act: u32`: encoded menu or world action, so replays and the bot use them\\n\\nAdd button bits for reload, next weapon, throw, melee, aim, map, monocular, heal, pills, tracker, seat, camera (17 bits are free).\\n\\n760→`pav_app/input.rs` gets a third layout for this game (§4), and `poll_gamepad` passes trigger analog values. Mouse look on the web: read `movementX/Y` in the JS shim (§12.5), which is simplest to test (§2.4). Native can use `DeviceEvent::MouseMotion`. `move_dir` stays world-space: rotate the stick by yaw. Only Esc stays a system key outside dev mode.\\n\\n### 12.4 Game to view and UI\\n- Add `Game::frame_extra` or a typed field `RenderFrame.merc: Option<Arc<MercFrame>>`, like the existing `game: Option<Arc<GameFrame>>`. `MercFrame` holds what the view and UI need: FP state, viewmodel state, inventory, prompts, map data version, burn deltas, wind, time.\\n- `pav_view::merc::draw(scene, frame)` runs inside `ViewBuilder::build`.\\n- `pav_ui::tenfoot` draws over it, and also from `headless.rs` so `pav capture` and `ui` see it.\\n- All game state stays in the `Game` struct or entities (`Clone`, serde). View caches are `#[serde(skip)]` or live in the view.\\n- Randomness only from `sim.state.rng`. No clock, no `HashMap` order reaching state. The \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md` apply to your game; its maintainers' workflow (history, PRs, escalations) does not.\\n\\n### 12.5 Web layer\\n770→`engine/web/index.html` gets, in order: `<meta charset>`, session client, hub metas, then a plain script defining:\\n- `window.gameNet`: `init`, `send(json, reliable, to)`, `poll()` (drains a JSON string array), hub events queued, standalone transports\\n- `window.gameInput`: pointer lock request, `movementX/Y` accumulation, lock-change flag, `(any-pointer: fine)`\\n- `window.gameTest`: see §14.3\\n\\nRust calls them through `#[wasm_bindgen] extern \\\"C\\\"` with `js_namespace`, or `js_sys::Reflect`. No snippets (§2.1). Keep the glue free of the literal strings `<script`, `</script` and `<!--`.\\n\\n`tools/build-game.sh` runs `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene merc --title \\\"<title>\\\" --description \\\"<line>\\\" --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" --out <the final path TASK.md names>`, then confirms the size, the first-script position and that `session.js` is byte-identical.\\n\\n### 12.6 Data and tools for later designers\\n780→All balance, weapons, enemies, contracts, text, shop, attract, map features and compounds are data, embedded at build time and re-read from disk in native tools. Add `pav` tools (`engine/AGENTS.md`, \\\"Adding a tool\\\"):\\n- `mapshot` (top-down PNG of terrain, POIs, roads, burn state)\\n- `fire` (start, step, report)\\n- `merc_cmd` (any `act`)\\n\\nThis, with `room_check`, `asset_edit`, `anim_edit`, `animsheet`, `filmstrip` and dev mode, is the designer toolchain TASK.md asks for.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Build order\\n790→Each milestone ends with its tests in the one command. Commit to your engine clone's git as you go. **Never use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\\n\\n| M | Build | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **M0** | Clone, build, register `merc` scene (copy the starter as in `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`, which is the first engine page to read), page builds, session client in place, `hub/` downloaded, harness passes with a stub round, title chosen, `tests/run.sh` prints one line | `tests/run.sh` shows 0 failures, harness 4 scenarios pass |\\n| **M1** | First-person camera, input layer, pointer lock, gamepad layout, `tenfoot` prompts, viewmodel with the rifle (hands on sockets, sway, recoil, reload, the red rag), hitscan, a target dummy, sky dome, NO_FOG | Sim tests for look, move and hits pass. A 1920×1080 screenshot looks like a game you'd play. **Fix the look now: everything depends on it.** |\\n| **M2** | Terrain and `world.toml`, biomes, roads, river, rings, grass and trees, time of day, stamps on pads, town blocked out, `mapshot` | `mapshot` shows the whole map. Bot walks airstrip to town. Screenshots at dawn, noon, dusk and night |\\n| **M3** | Full weapon table, condition and jams, damage and treatments, NPC roles, detection, cover, guard post | Bot clears a post on 10 seeds. Jam, wear and detection tests pass |\\n| **M4** | Fire, wind, smoke, burn visuals, explosions, weather, AI reactions | Fire tests (§14.1). Depot fire screenshot makes you want to play |\\n| **M5** | Vehicles on slopes, relative controls, boat, seats, mounted gun, damage and repair, AI pursuit | Bot drives the road end to end. Boat and repair tests pass |\\n800→| **M6** | Fever, safe houses, sleep, economy and shop, map and GPS and monocular, tracker and caches, tapes, saves | Tests for each. Save and reload round trip |\\n| **M7** | Companions, contracts A0 to D2, endings, barks, Infamy, campaign bot, coverage flags | **Scripted playthrough reaches all three endings with every coverage flag set** |\\n| **M8** | Audio buses, SFX, music, voices | Audio tests pass, default music gain 0.10 |\\n| **M9** | Shell: title, settings, pause, dev mode, attract, touch-only, About | Browser tests pass (§14.3) |\\n| **M10** | Session round, own card, netcode, server mode, standalone This computer and Invite code | Loopback test, harness 4 scenarios on the real game, two-page standalone round |\\n| **M11** | Art pass on every prop, animation pass on every clip, writing pass on every line, balance with sliders, final build, About/Credits, exit interview | §16 checklist complete |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. Testing (TASK.md: one command, only failures and a one-line count)\\n810→`tests/run.sh [sim|ui|audio|browser|hub|all]` prints each failure's name and reason, then one line like `PASS 212 FAIL 0`. Rerun only the part you changed. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check.\\n\\n### 14.1 Sim (`engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs`, native, fast)\\n- **Foundations:** boots on 3 seeds. Same seed and inputs give the same hash; `record_save` and `replay` hold. Snapshot round trip. Data lint: every TOML parses, every asset and clip named exists, every string key resolves, and no string contains TODO, TBD, placeholder or lorem.\\n- **Player:** look clamps, stick movement follows yaw, stances change eye and capsule height, hard landing wound.\\n- **Weapons:** head, torso and limb multipliers. Wall blocks shots. Wear per table. Jam rate within tolerance at c = 35 over 5,000 rolls. Jam blocks firing until cleared. Weapon breaks. An NPC's gun jams and it stops firing.\\n- **Fire:** wind 8 m/s downwind reach ≥ 3× upwind after 60 s. Calm spread is roughly round. Roads and river stop it unless embers jump. Burnt cells don't re-burn, then regrow. Rain extinguishes. Barrel explodes and ignites. NPCs leave burning cells. A burning NPC spreads fire. Fuel tank cooks off. Snapshot size stays small after a big burn.\\n- **Detection:** the grass, night and posture comparisons of §5.10. Noise brings investigators. Smoke blocks sight.\\n- **AI:** squad takes cover and at least one flanker repositions. Max 4 shooters at once. Morale break. Post re-mans after its timer and never in the player's sight.\\n- **Survival:** warning precedes attack. Pill clears it. No pill means black-out, wake at safe house, fee taken. Syrette and treatments restore the right amounts. Wound type follows damage cause.\\n820→- **Companions:** rescue fires once per rest and player stands up at 50. Downed companion timer. Patch and overdose. Death stays dead across save and load.\\n- **Vehicles:** climbs the ridge road. Recovers from a roll. Damage stages. Repair. Explodes and ignites grass. Boat floats and stops at shallows. NPC driver follows the road. Seat changes.\\n- **Economy and saves:** buying with too few diamonds changes nothing. Tracker rate rises near a cache. Save and load restores all listed fields.\\n- **Contracts:** each contract completes under the bot on 2 seeds, and each failure condition fires.\\n- **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot plays new game through each of the three endings using only inputs and `act`s (no teleporting except the bus, no cheats, normal difficulty). Assert the outcome is reached, all `coverage` flags are set, and wall time is under a limit you set (this must stay cheap enough to rerun). Expose it through `Game::bot`, so `pav play bot=true seeds=3` works too.\\n- **Attract:** five full loops, every segment reached, never stuck, no save written.\\n- **Netcode loopback:** host and client `Sim`s on the in-memory link at 150 ms, jitter 50, 5% loss. Both see the same fire cells within 1 s, kills and objectives agree, `finish` is issued once, unreliable messages stay under 1,200 bytes and sends stay under 20 per second. A client leaving and the host leaving both behave.\\n\\n### 14.2 UI and audio (native)\\n- **UI** (`MenuInput`): focus moves and wraps, back works, no screen exceeds 7 rows, hover moves focus, glyphs follow device and setting, dev sliders change `Tunable`s and Reset restores defaults, attract starts at 10 s of idle and not before, any input exits.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":690,\"limit\":140,\"raw_output\":\"\\n---\\n\\n## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\\nData in `engine/game/merc/contracts.toml`: objectives as a small state machine with triggers, approaches, pay and consequences. Every objective exposes a `Goal` the bot and the dev tools can read.\\n\\n| # | Contract (giver) | What happens | Teaches or shows | About |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\\n| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\\n| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\\n| B2 | **Water Rights** (Ruvuma) | Undo Tshala: sabotage the Council's pump station at night by boat. Sleep till midnight, camo, dart rifle | Sleep picker, night, stealth, boat, swimming, machete | 10 min |\\n| B3 | **Papers** (Sister Perpetua) | Drive medicine to the mission. Ambush, pursuit, engine failure: repair under fire. Reward: pills | Pursuit, damage stages, repair, fever economy | 8 min |\\n| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\\n| C1 | **Inspection** (Tshala) | Kill the Hand's negotiator at Hotel Splendide from the ridge. Tag with the monocular, wind on the bullet, get out past GP5. Consequence: **the ceasefire ends** | Sniper, tagging, world state | 8 min |\\n| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\\n| C3 | **The Town Burns** | Kilometre 40 ablaze at night. Get through, get Papa Lazare or Mr. Desai out (you can save one). Ash, panic, soldiers looting. Shops move to the Boat Shed afterward | Fire as a level, moral beat, town after | 6 min |\\n| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\\n| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\\n\\nSide content open from A1 on: 12 diamond caches, 6 tapes, 6 guard posts, 3 safe houses, 3 bus stops (fast travel: fade, time passes, fare 1 diamond), wildlife, two minor clinic errands.\\n\\n**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Architecture\\n\\n### 12.1 Dev folder\\n```\\nengine/                     the shardfall clone, with its .git (git diff answers \\\"what did you change?\\\")\\n  crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/   rules: mod.rs (Game impl), player, weapons, fire, wind, ai, squads, vehicles,\\n                                    companions, fever, contracts, economy, map, net, terrain, attract, bot\\n  crates/pav_view/src/merc/         first-person camera, viewmodel, sky, grass and tree caches, rings, map prop, fire look, tracers\\n  crates/pav_ui/src/tenfoot/        UI kit, glyphs, every screen\\n  crates/pav_audio/src/             bus.rs, music.rs, voice.rs alongside lib.rs\\n  crates/pav_app/src/merc_shell.rs  shell state, pointer lock, net pump, test hooks\\n  crates/pav_tools/src/             new tools: mapshot, fire, merc_cmd\\n  game/merc/*.toml                  world, weapons, enemies, contracts, strings, tapes, barks, shop, attract, tuning\\n  game/merc/stamps/*.toml           compounds (room format)\\n  anim/merc_fp.json, anim/merc_npc.json\\n  assets/props/lib/merc/, assets/materials/\\n  web/index.html                    session client, hub metas, input and net shims\\nhub/                        session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js as downloaded\\ntests/                      the one command, Playwright scripts\\ntools/                      build-game.sh (wasm, pack, copy to the final name and place)\\nnotes/                      title.md, feedback.md (running answers for the feedback questions)\\n```\\nKeep every file you make in your own folder, including caches (`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` stays in `engine/target`), and don't read the folders beside yours: other agents work there. Use `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12` at most: the machine is shared. No CDN dependencies are needed, since the page carries everything.\\n\\n### 12.2 First-person camera\\nAdd a first-person path to `CameraRig`: `fp: Option<FpCam { eye, yaw, pitch, roll, fov, near, far }>`.\\n- `data()` builds the view from it, with `near = 0.08` and `far = 3000`.\\n- `forward`, `up`, `ground_axes` and `relative_move` use its yaw and pitch.\\n- `eye` = interpolated feet (or vehicle seat) + smoothed stance height.\\n- **Rendered yaw and pitch = sim value + input not yet consumed by a tick, so the camera never lags the mouse.**\\n- `rig.target` goes 40 m ahead of the player, so shadows cover what you face.\\n- `Scene.cutaway` off.\\n- The sim's own yaw and pitch stay in the game's state (the source of truth for shooting).\\n- Chase camera and the third-person shots are ordinary `CameraParams`.\\n- Prove this first (§13 M1).\\n\\n### 12.3 Input\\nExtend `InputFrame` (it must stay `Copy`):\\n- `look: Vec2`: radians since last tick, summed and zeroed like `pressed` in `simhost.rs`\\n- `axes: Vec2`: analog throttle and brake\\n- `act: u32`: encoded menu or world action, so replays and the bot use them\\n\\nAdd button bits for reload, next weapon, throw, melee, aim, map, monocular, heal, pills, tracker, seat, camera (17 bits are free).\\n\\n`pav_app/input.rs` gets a third layout for this game (§4), and `poll_gamepad` passes trigger analog values. Mouse look on the web: read `movementX/Y` in the JS shim (§12.5), which is simplest to test (§2.4). Native can use `DeviceEvent::MouseMotion`. `move_dir` stays world-space: rotate the stick by yaw. Only Esc stays a system key outside dev mode.\\n\\n### 12.4 Game to view and UI\\n- Add `Game::frame_extra` or a typed field `RenderFrame.merc: Option<Arc<MercFrame>>`, like the existing `game: Option<Arc<GameFrame>>`. `MercFrame` holds what the view and UI need: FP state, viewmodel state, inventory, prompts, map data version, burn deltas, wind, time.\\n- `pav_view::merc::draw(scene, frame)` runs inside `ViewBuilder::build`.\\n- `pav_ui::tenfoot` draws over it, and also from `headless.rs` so `pav capture` and `ui` see it.\\n- All game state stays in the `Game` struct or entities (`Clone`, serde). View caches are `#[serde(skip)]` or live in the view.\\n- Randomness only from `sim.state.rng`. No clock, no `HashMap` order reaching state. The \\\"Key rules\\\" in `engine/AGENTS.md` apply to your game; its maintainers' workflow (history, PRs, escalations) does not.\\n\\n### 12.5 Web layer\\n`engine/web/index.html` gets, in order: `<meta charset>`, session client, hub metas, then a plain script defining:\\n- `window.gameNet`: `init`, `send(json, reliable, to)`, `poll()` (drains a JSON string array), hub events queued, standalone transports\\n- `window.gameInput`: pointer lock request, `movementX/Y` accumulation, lock-change flag, `(any-pointer: fine)`\\n- `window.gameTest`: see §14.3\\n\\nRust calls them through `#[wasm_bindgen] extern \\\"C\\\"` with `js_namespace`, or `js_sys::Reflect`. No snippets (§2.1). Keep the glue free of the literal strings `<script`, `</script` and `<!--`.\\n\\n`tools/build-game.sh` runs `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene merc --title \\\"<title>\\\" --description \\\"<line>\\\" --theme-color \\\"#2a2420\\\" --out <the final path TASK.md names>`, then confirms the size, the first-script position and that `session.js` is byte-identical.\\n\\n### 12.6 Data and tools for later designers\\nAll balance, weapons, enemies, contracts, text, shop, attract, map features and compounds are data, embedded at build time and re-read from disk in native tools. Add `pav` tools (`engine/AGENTS.md`, \\\"Adding a tool\\\"):\\n- `mapshot` (top-down PNG of terrain, POIs, roads, burn state)\\n- `fire` (start, step, report)\\n- `merc_cmd` (any `act`)\\n\\nThis, with `room_check`, `asset_edit`, `anim_edit`, `animsheet`, `filmstrip` and dev mode, is the designer toolchain TASK.md asks for.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Build order\\nEach milestone ends with its tests in the one command. Commit to your engine clone's git as you go. **Never use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\\n\\n| M | Build | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **M0** | Clone, build, register `merc` scene (copy the starter as in `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`, which is the first engine page to read), page builds, session client in place, `hub/` downloaded, harness passes with a stub round, title chosen, `tests/run.sh` prints one line | `tests/run.sh` shows 0 failures, harness 4 scenarios pass |\\n| **M1** | First-person camera, input layer, pointer lock, gamepad layout, `tenfoot` prompts, viewmodel with the rifle (hands on sockets, sway, recoil, reload, the red rag), hitscan, a target dummy, sky dome, NO_FOG | Sim tests for look, move and hits pass. A 1920×1080 screenshot looks like a game you'd play. **Fix the look now: everything depends on it.** |\\n| **M2** | Terrain and `world.toml`, biomes, roads, river, rings, grass and trees, time of day, stamps on pads, town blocked out, `mapshot` | `mapshot` shows the whole map. Bot walks airstrip to town. Screenshots at dawn, noon, dusk and night |\\n| **M3** | Full weapon table, condition and jams, damage and treatments, NPC roles, detection, cover, guard post | Bot clears a post on 10 seeds. Jam, wear and detection tests pass |\\n| **M4** | Fire, wind, smoke, burn visuals, explosions, weather, AI reactions | Fire tests (§14.1). Depot fire screenshot makes you want to play |\\n| **M5** | Vehicles on slopes, relative controls, boat, seats, mounted gun, damage and repair, AI pursuit | Bot drives the road end to end. Boat and repair tests pass |\\n| **M6** | Fever, safe houses, sleep, economy and shop, map and GPS and monocular, tracker and caches, tapes, saves | Tests for each. Save and reload round trip |\\n| **M7** | Companions, contracts A0 to D2, endings, barks, Infamy, campaign bot, coverage flags | **Scripted playthrough reaches all three endings with every coverage flag set** |\\n| **M8** | Audio buses, SFX, music, voices | Audio tests pass, default music gain 0.10 |\\n| **M9** | Shell: title, settings, pause, dev mode, attract, touch-only, About | Browser tests pass (§14.3) |\\n| **M10** | Session round, own card, netcode, server mode, standalone This computer and Invite code | Loopback test, harness 4 scenarios on the real game, two-page standalone round |\\n| **M11** | Art pass on every prop, animation pass on every clip, writing pass on every line, balance with sliders, final build, About/Credits, exit interview | §16 checklist complete |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. Testing (TASK.md: one command, only failures and a one-line count)\\n`tests/run.sh [sim|ui|audio|browser|hub|all]` prints each failure's name and reason, then one line like `PASS 212 FAIL 0`. Rerun only the part you changed. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check.\\n\\n### 14.1 Sim (`engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs`, native, fast)\\n- **Foundations:** boots on 3 seeds. Same seed and inputs give the same hash; `record_save` and `replay` hold. Snapshot round trip. Data lint: every TOML parses, every asset and clip named exists, every string key resolves, and no string contains TODO, TBD, placeholder or lorem.\\n- **Player:** look clamps, stick movement follows yaw, stances change eye and capsule height, hard landing wound.\\n- **Weapons:** head, torso and limb multipliers. Wall blocks shots. Wear per table. Jam rate within tolerance at c = 35 over 5,000 rolls. Jam blocks firing until cleared. Weapon breaks. An NPC's gun jams and it stops firing.\\n- **Fire:** wind 8 m/s downwind reach ≥ 3× upwind after 60 s. Calm spread is roughly round. Roads and river stop it unless embers jump. Burnt cells don't re-burn, then regrow. Rain extinguishes. Barrel explodes and ignites. NPCs leave burning cells. A burning NPC spreads fire. Fuel tank cooks off. Snapshot size stays small after a big burn.\\n- **Detection:** the grass, night and posture comparisons of §5.10. Noise brings investigators. Smoke blocks sight.\\n- **AI:** squad takes cover and at least one flanker repositions. Max 4 shooters at once. Morale break. Post re-mans after its timer and never in the player's sight.\\n- **Survival:** warning precedes attack. Pill clears it. No pill means black-out, wake at safe house, fee taken. Syrette and treatments restore the right amounts. Wound type follows damage cause.\\n- **Companions:** rescue fires once per rest and player stands up at 50. Downed companion timer. Patch and overdose. Death stays dead across save and load.\\n- **Vehicles:** climbs the ridge road. Recovers from a roll. Damage stages. Repair. Explodes and ignites grass. Boat floats and stops at shallows. NPC driver follows the road. Seat changes.\\n- **Economy and saves:** buying with too few diamonds changes nothing. Tracker rate rises near a cache. Save and load restores all listed fields.\\n- **Contracts:** each contract completes under the bot on 2 seeds, and each failure condition fires.\\n- **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot plays new game through each of the three endings using only inputs and `act`s (no teleporting except the bus, no cheats, normal difficulty). Assert the outcome is reached, all `coverage` flags are set, and wall time is under a limit you set (this must stay cheap enough to rerun). Expose it through `Game::bot`, so `pav play bot=true seeds=3` works too.\\n- **Attract:** five full loops, every segment reached, never stuck, no save written.\\n- **Netcode loopback:** host and client `Sim`s on the in-memory link at 150 ms, jitter 50, 5% loss. Both see the same fire cells within 1 s, kills and objectives agree, `finish` is issued once, unreliable messages stay under 1,200 bytes and sends stay under 20 per second. A client leaving and the host leaving both behave.\\n\\n### 14.2 UI and audio (native)\\n- **UI** (`MenuInput`): focus moves and wraps, back works, no screen exceeds 7 rows, hover moves focus, glyphs follow device and setting, dev sliders change `Tunable`s and Reset restores defaults, attract starts at 10 s of idle and not before, any input exits.\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-48a69919-a431-4b4b-bbf9-1c0c0b27c0e9-19","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,10,50,48,58,45,32,42,42,80,101,114,115,112,101,99,116,105,118,101,58,42,42,32,102,105,114,115,116,32,112,101,114,115,111,110,32,111,110,32,102,111,111,116,32,97,110,100,32,105,110,32,118,101,104,105,99,108,101,115,44,32,98,101,99,97,117,115,101,32,116,104,101,32,115,111,117,114,99,101,39,115,32,105,100,101,110,116,105,116,121,32,105,115,32,116,104,101,32,98,111,100,121,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,119,111,114,108,100,46,32,68,114,105,118,105,110,103,32,97,108,115,111,32,104,97,115,32,97,32,99,104,97,115,101,32,99,97,109,101,114,97,32,116,111,103,103,108,101,44,32,98,101,99,97,117,115,101,32,97,32,84,86,32,97,110,100,32,97,32,115,116,105,99,107,32,109,97,107,101,32,116,104,97,116,32,101,97,115,105,101,114,46,32,65,32,99,105,110,101,109,97,116,105,99,32,116,104,105,114,100,45,112,101,114,115,111,110,32,99,97,109,101,114,97,32,97,112,112,101,97,114,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,105,110,32,97,116,116,114,97,99,116,32,109,111,100,101,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,101,110,100,105,110,103,32,115,104,111,116,115,46,10,52,51,58,42,42,73,110,58,42,42,32,101,118,101,114,121,116,104,105,110,103,32,105,110,32,1