120,116,46,10,56,55,56,58,45,32,91,32,93,32,68,101,109,111,32,108,111,110,103,32,101,110,111,117,103,104,32,116,111,32,115,104,111,119,32,101,118,101,114,121,116,104,105,110,103,58,32,112,108,97,121,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,32,97,115,115,101,114,116,115,32,97,108,108,32,99,111,118,101,114,97,103,101,32,102,108,97,103,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":15,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"- **Perspective:** first person on foot and in vehicles, because the source's identity is the body in the world. Driving also has a chase camera toggle, because a TV and a stick make that easier. A cinematic third-person camera appears only in attract mode and the ending shots.\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"**In:** everything in §5 to §11. A main path of 75 to 90 minutes with an ending choice, plus side content on the map.\"},{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"The **Republic of Kwelara**, an invented landlocked country. It is the last dry season of a civil war that both sides have stopped pretending to win. Rust-red laterite roads, gold grass to the horizon, flat-topped acacias, baobabs, granite kopjes, one brown river with green forest along its banks, and everywhere the leftovers of the colonial era and of three failed governments. A ceasefire holds in exactly one town. Don't name real countries, ethnic groups or flags.\"},{\"line_number\":178,\"content\":\"You land at night on a cargo flight whose crates are stencilled for both sides. Papa Lazare finds you collapsing with fever on his doorstep, and a companion gets you on your feet. You take work from the Council and the Hand to get close to the Chandler. Each job undoes the last. Your assassination at the Hotel Splendide ends the ceasefire and the town burns. The crates, the tapes and the ledger all lead to the old Cement Works. There the Chandler, dying of the same fever, shows you the ledger: every buyer, your two employers, and the firm that hired you, paid by the Chandler himself. He hired his own killer because he wanted an ending or a successor. **Three endings (player's choice):**\"},{\"line_number\":183,\"content\":\"Every ending finishes on a final tape: **your own voice**, in gibberish with subtitles, being interviewed.\"},{\"line_number\":545,\"content\":\"The hub voids a round if the host tab stays hidden over 20 s, but a shorter stall must not kill the world. Pump the sim from a timer as well as rAF when `document.hidden`, and raise the per-frame tick cap on the host so it catches up. On a software GPU keep sending at the same rate.\"},{\"line_number\":598,\"content\":\"- **About/Credits:** paged, large text, §15 content\"},{\"line_number\":626,\"content\":\"- **Teleport:** every place in §6.3, plus \\\"next objective\\\". **Story:** jump to any contract or ending, complete objective, kill nearby.\"},{\"line_number\":712,\"content\":\"**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\"},{\"line_number\":801,\"content\":\"| **M7** | Companions, contracts A0 to D2, endings, barks, Infamy, campaign bot, coverage flags | **Scripted playthrough reaches all three endings with every coverage flag set** |\"},{\"line_number\":824,\"content\":\"- **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot plays new game through each of the three endings using only inputs and `act`s (no teleporting except the bus, no cheats, normal difficulty). Assert the outcome is reached, all `coverage` flags are set, and wall time is under a limit you set (this must stay cheap enough to rerun). Expose it through `Game::bot`, so `pav play bot=true seeds=3` works too.\"},{\"line_number\":857,\"content\":\"## 15. Feature list for the coverage flags, and what ships in About/Credits\"},{\"line_number\":859,\"content\":\"**Coverage flags (each set by real play; a test passes on the union across the three playthrough runs, since no single run can both save and lose the same companion or reach every ending):** map raised, waypoint set, GPS followed, monocular tag, wind rag visible at speed > 6, jam cleared, enemy jam seen, weapon broke, weapon bought, locker used, syrette, each wound treatment type, fever warned, pill taken, black-out (bot route), player rescued, companion patched, companion overdosed, companion died, better-way taken, fire lit by each igniter class, 500+ cells burned in one fire, enemy panicked, animals fled, explosion chain, rain extinguished, stealth kill, dart kill, night contract, sleep used, safe house claimed, post cleared, post re-manned, technical driven, mounted gun fired, repair done, boat driven, bus taken, tape played, cache found by tracker, diamonds spent, each contract, ceasefire ended, town burned, each ending.\"},{\"line_number\":877,\"content\":\"- [ ] All systems in §5 present. All contracts in §11 playable. Three endings. No TODOs, placeholders or stubs anywhere, including in text.\"},{\"line_number\":878,\"content\":\"- [ ] Demo long enough to show everything: playthrough asserts all coverage flags.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"993958ed-931b-40b6-8bd4-8402d16c54ee"}
