44,32,110,111,114,109,97,108,32,100,105,102,102,105,99,117,108,116,121,41,46,32,65,115,115,101,114,116,32,116,104,101,32,111,117,116,99,111,109,101,32,105,115,32,114,101,97,99,104,101,100,44,32,97,108,108,32,96,99,111,118,101,114,97,103,101,96,32,102,108,97,103,115,32,97,114,101,32,115,101,116,44,32,97,110,100,32,119,97,108,108,32,116,105,109,101,32,105,115,32,117,110,100,101,114,32,97,32,108,105,109,105,116,32,121,111,117,32,115,101,116,32,40,116,104,105,115,32,109,117,115,116,32,115,116,97,121,32,99,104,101,97,112,32,101,110,111,117,103,104,32,116,111,32,114,101,114,117,110,41,46,32,69,120,112,111,115,101,32,105,116,32,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,32,96,71,97,109,101,58,58,98,111,116,96,44,32,115,111,32,96,112,97,118,32,112,108,97,121,32,98,111,116,61,116,114,117,101,32,115,101,101,100,115,61,51,96,32,119,111,114,107,115,32,116,111,111,46,10,56,53,55,58,35,35,32,49,53,46,32,70,101,97,116,117,114,101,32,108,105,115,116,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,118,101,114,97,103,101,32,102,108,97,103,115,44,32,97,110,100,32,119,104,97,116,32,115,104,105,112,115,32,105,110,32,65,98,111,117,116,47,67,114,101,100,105,116,115,10,56,55,56,58,45,32,91,32,93,32,68,101,109,111,32,108,111,110,103,32,101,110,111,117,103,104,32,116,111,32,115,104,111,119,32,101,118,101,114,121,116,104,105,110,103,58,32,112,108,97,121,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,32,97,115,115,101,114,116,115,32,97,108,108,32,99,111,118,101,114,97,103,101,32,102,108,97,103,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":17,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":116,\"content\":\"- **Props:** generic only. Barrels, casks, crates, sacks, tents, market stalls, tables, chairs, cots, fences, wells, signposts, lanterns, rowboat, rocks, rubble. **No guns, modern vehicles, trees, grass, huts or sandbags.** Those are yours (§9.2).\"},{\"line_number\":159,\"content\":\"- Tshala: \\\"You will burn the depot at Ombe. If anyone asks, it was the dry season.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":178,\"content\":\"You land at night on a cargo flight whose crates are stencilled for both sides. Papa Lazare finds you collapsing with fever on his doorstep, and a companion gets you on your feet. You take work from the Council and the Hand to get close to the Chandler. Each job undoes the last. Your assassination at the Hotel Splendide ends the ceasefire and the town burns. The crates, the tapes and the ledger all lead to the old Cement Works. There the Chandler, dying of the same fever, shows you the ledger: every buyer, your two employers, and the firm that hired you, paid by the Chandler himself. He hired his own killer because he wanted an ending or a successor. **Three endings (player's choice):**\"},{\"line_number\":179,\"content\":\"1. **Burn it.** Torch the works and the ledger, and walk into the grass. The war goes on and nobody knows.\"},{\"line_number\":181,\"content\":\"3. **Take the chair.** Sit at his radio. The next order comes in, and you answer it.\"},{\"line_number\":377,\"content\":\"- At the end, the highest-trust survivor comes to the Cement Works. The ledger has their name in it too. They stay anyway, or they don't (trust threshold).\"},{\"line_number\":505,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Burn the depot, take the ledger, get out together\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":515,\"content\":\"3. One player takes the ledger case from the office (carrying it slows you and prevents sprinting; it can be dropped and picked up).\"},{\"line_number\":598,\"content\":\"- **About/Credits:** paged, large text, §15 content\"},{\"line_number\":705,\"content\":\"| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\"},{\"line_number\":707,\"content\":\"| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\"},{\"line_number\":708,\"content\":\"| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\"},{\"line_number\":712,\"content\":\"**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\"},{\"line_number\":801,\"content\":\"| **M7** | Companions, contracts A0 to D2, endings, barks, Infamy, campaign bot, coverage flags | **Scripted playthrough reaches all three endings with every coverage flag set** |\"},{\"line_number\":824,\"content\":\"- **Scripted playthrough of the whole game:** the bot plays new game through each of the three endings using only inputs and `act`s (no teleporting except the bus, no cheats, normal difficulty). Assert the outcome is reached, all `coverage` flags are set, and wall time is under a limit you set (this must stay cheap enough to rerun). Expose it through `Game::bot`, so `pav play bot=true seeds=3` works too.\"},{\"line_number\":857,\"content\":\"## 15. Feature list for the coverage flags, and what ships in About/Credits\"},{\"line_number\":878,\"content\":\"- [ ] Demo long enough to show everything: playthrough asserts all coverage flags.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-410f5a45-4953-4a25-93dc-d6c8292a04fe-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"270→            arrival: None,\\n            game_ui: Default::default(),\\n            last_save: Instant::now(),\\n            pad_cursor: None,\\n            pad_events: Vec::new(),\\n            pad_buttons: (false, false, false),\\n            game_frame: None,\\n            game_place: None,\\n            touch: Default::default(),\\n            touch_screen,\\n280→            touch_styled: false,\\n            next_draw: Instant::now(),\\n            prefs: crate::save::load_prefs(),\\n            scaler: Default::default(),\\n            #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n            bridge: None,\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            pending_gfx: None,\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            audio_resumed: false,\\n290→            init_started: false,\\n            fatal: None,\\n            settings,\\n        };\\n        if touch_screen {\\n            // Phones: touch controls from the start, none of the desktop's diagnostics.\\n            app.input.last_device = Device::Touch;\\n            app.show_boot = false;\\n            app.app_settings.show_stats = false;\\n        }\\n300→        if app.scene_name == \\\"merc\\\" {\\n            app.show_boot = false;\\n            app.app_settings.show_stats = false;\\n            app.app_settings.show_guide = false;\\n            app.app_settings.aim_marker = false;\\n            let o = pav_core::games::merc::overlook();\\n            app.rig.fp = Some(pav_view::camera::FpCam {\\n                eye: Vec3::new(o.eye[0], o.eye[1], o.eye[2]),\\n                yaw: o.yaw,\\n                pitch: o.pitch,\\n310→                roll: o.roll,\\n                fov: 70.0,\\n                near: 0.08,\\n                far: 3000.0,\\n            });\\n        }\\n        app\\n    }\\n\\n    /// A finger on the screen: the touch layer decides whether it is the stick, a control, a\\n320→    /// swipe or egui's (and then egui gets the event).\\n    fn on_touch(&mut self, t: &winit::event::Touch, event: &WindowEvent) {\\n        #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n        self.resume_audio();\\n        let Some(g) = &self.gfx else { return };\\n        let ppp = self.egui_ctx.zoom_factor() * g.window.scale_factor() as f32;\\n        let pos = egui::pos2(t.location.x as f32 / ppp, t.location.y as f32 / ppp);\\n        self.input.last_device = Device::Touch;\\n        self.touch_screen = true;\\n        use winit::event::TouchPhase as P;\\n330→        let to_egui = match t.phase {\\n            P::Started => {\\n                // (The root layer is everywhere; only windows and labels over the game count.)\\n                let under = self.egui_ctx.layer_id_at(pos).filter(|l| *l != egui::LayerId::background()).map(|l| l.order);\\n                self.touch.down(t.id, pos, under)\\n            }\\n            P::Moved => self.touch.moved(t.id, pos),\\n            P::Ended => self.touch.up(t.id, pos, false),\\n            P::Cancelled => self.touch.up(t.id, pos, true),\\n        };\\n340→        if to_egui {\\n            if let (Some(st), Some(g)) = (&mut self.egui_state, &self.gfx) {\\n                st.on_window_event(&g.window, event);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// A tap on the open game closes what is open over it, one thing at a time.\\n    fn close_on_tap(&mut self) {\\n        if self.menu_open {\",\"content_concise\":\"270→            arrival: None,\\n            game_ui: Default::default(),\\n            last_save: Instant::now(),\\n            pad_cursor: None,\\n            pad_events: Vec::new(),\\n            pad_buttons: (false, false, false),\\n            game_frame: None,\\n            game_place: None,\\n            touch: Default::default(),\\n            touch_screen,\\n280→            touch_styled: false,\\n            next_draw: Instant::now(),\\n            prefs: crate::save::load_prefs(),\\n            scaler: Default::default(),\\n            #[cfg(not(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\"))]\\n            bridge: None,\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            pending_gfx: None,\\n            #[cfg(target_arch = \\\"wasm32\\\")]\\n            audio_resumed: false,\\n290→            init_started: false,\\n        