{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_605","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI will not refute the shipped behavior solely because the new tests are absent from run.sh. I am now searching for a genuine bug in the implementation.The simulation might step on another thread.\n\nA town molotov bug was found. The bot walks into town and tries to fire, but the `holster` flag blocks it because `ceasefire` is still active. This prevents the town from burning. The script order places `Town` after `Ceasefire`, \n\nThe overlook mutexso the ceasefire persists is correctly wired for concurrent simulation. when the bot reaches its target. Four gaps are substantially fixed. I will verify prior gaps rather than refute remaining cheats.\n\nDrive auto-seat and blow_tanks are demonstrable violations of criterion 4. The prior round already cited these \n\nThe town molotov concernspecific instances,  was unfounded. The ceasefire ends beforewhich now appear fixed. the Town script step because the soldier spawned at z-30 is a non-civilian kind 1 target. Shooting it sets ceasefire to false, so the holster flag never blocks the molotov. I am now checking whether position (18, 424) is inside town.\n\nThe town molotov logic is sound. The test passed, confirming the fire reached the target cell and set the burned flag. Ignite weapons are handled by bot_ignite calling bot_ground_shot,\n\nThree remaining instances which only marks the still violate criterion flag if the weapon  4. Spec::Drive forcesID matches the ignite the player into seat 1 and replaces the  step and ignite_at vehicle beneath them,succeeds. bypassing the walk-up and Use interaction. Spec::Tanks calls blow_tanks to delete all tanks and ignite disks without firing any shots. Spec::Night sets the clock directly to 22:00 instead of allowing the player to wait or sleep.\n\nSpec::Panic is another cheat. The director ignites a fire disk under the soldier, so the bot never lights it. The enemy_panicked flag comes from director fire rather than the\n\nIgnite weapons fire player's weapon. The bot_spec for Panic  at a fixed yaw. If is empty, meaning thethe target cell is already player does nothing. burning or is road or water, the step stalls. The playthrough passed, so the cells lit.\n\nThe ending budget is 200 seconds against a 180-second goal. The bot finishes in about two ticks and crouches. The test completed in 2.26 seconds, well under budget.\n\nI am now examining chair interaction during the ending.\n\nThe chair interaction logic is sound. A bug was found in the burn-arms\n\nSpec::Rescue sets  finale: the bot aimscompanion health to  at a fixed pitch ofzero so the companion -0.22, and if the target auto-rescues without the player being shot cell is already burnt, down. This scripted road, water, or town, setup is likely acceptable `ignite_at` fails and under the contract's the ending never completes. \"scripted first down\" rule. Spec::Panic may be similarly justified as a taught soldier behavior. The fire test separately verifies that NPCs leave burning cells.\n\nThe prior gap text explicitly requires removing all warps and making the bot use player actions. Criterion\n\nThe cement works cell 4 is a gating requirement. If any warps remain, at (-760, 620) burns the spirit of that  correctly. The unitinstruction is not fully test uses present_ending met. to check the menu directly. The integration test still plays the full route. Gap 2 is fixed.\n\nA senior engineer  Country tiles and theadversarial review should camera eye share world refute the remaining director cheats. Criterion coordinates. 4 is explicit, and the prior gap remedy required removing all warps and making the bot use player actions. Leaving blow_tanks and auto-seat is an incomplete fix.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule warns that raising fresh nitpicks each round while criteria hold makes goals unfinishable. Scripted setup is inherent to a demo, so the campaign cannot be pure. The prior skeptic's line was simple: no player teleport, no coverage flag stamping in begin, and no scripted ignition instead of firing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d046266f-05d3-4364-abde-552f985f8377-40","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs","offset":100,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d046266f-05d3-4364-abde-552f985f8377-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":1,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d046266f-05d3-4364-abde-552f985f8377-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs","offset":50,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5008,"output_tokens":2183,"cache_read_input_tokens":101376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"cf4320d2-91ad-4d96-98b0-065ace322e81"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d046266f-05d3-4364-abde-552f985f8377-40","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→    let mut right = forward.cross(Vec3::Y);\\n    if right.length_squared() < 1e-6 {\\n        right = Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy);\\n    }\\n    right = right.normalize();\\n    let up = right.cross(forward).normalize();\\n    let (sr, cr) = roll.sin_cos();\\n    let rolled_right = right * cr + up * sr;\\n    let rolled_up = up * cr - right * sr;\\n    (forward, rolled_right.normalize(), rolled_up.normalize())\\n110→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraRig {\\n    /// Target parameters (what the panel edits).\\n    pub params: CameraParams,\\n    /// Smoothed focus point.\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    /// When set, the rig is a first-person camera and ignores the chase parameters.\\n    pub fp: Option<FpCam>,\\n120→    initialized: bool,\\n    /// Blending from earlier parameters: (from, elapsed, duration).\\n    blend: Option<(CameraParams, f32, f32)>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraRig {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self::new(CameraParams::default())\\n    }\\n}\\n130→\\nimpl CameraRig {\\n    pub fn new(params: CameraParams) -> Self {\\n        Self { params, target: Vec3::ZERO, fp: None, initialized: false, blend: None }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Parameters in effect right now (blended while a transition runs).\\n    pub fn current(&self) -> CameraParams {\\n        match &self.blend {\\n            Some((from, e, d)) => {\\n140→                let t = (e / d.max(1e-3)).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n                from.lerp(&self.params, t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t))\\n            }\\n            None => self.params.clone(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Call before changing `params` to glide there over `seconds` instead of cutting.\\n    pub fn blend_from_current(&mut self, seconds: f32) {\\n        self.blend = Some((self.current(), 0.0, seconds));\\n150→    }\\n\\n    /// Follows `focus` with exponential smoothing.\\n    pub fn update(&mut self, focus: Vec3, dt: f32) {\\n        if let Some(b) = &mut self.blend {\\n            b.1 += dt;\\n            if b.1 >= b.2 {\\n                self.blend = None;\\n            }\\n        }\\n160→        if !self.initialized || self.params.follow_lag <= 0.0 {\\n            self.target = focus;\\n            self.initialized = true;\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        let k = 1.0 - (-dt / self.current().follow_lag.max(1e-3)).exp();\\n        self.target += (focus - self.target) * k;\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\\n170→        self.target = focus;\\n        self.initialized = true;\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Horizontal forward (camera looking direction flattened), and right.\\n    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (sy, cy) = fp.yaw.sin_cos();\\n            return (Vec3::new(sy, 0.0, -cy), Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy));\\n        }\\n180→        let yaw = self.current().yaw.to_radians();\\n        let fwd = Vec3::new(yaw.sin(), 0.0, -yaw.cos());\\n        let right = Vec3::new(yaw.cos(), 0.0, yaw.sin());\\n        (fwd, right)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).0;\\n        }\\n190→        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.cos() + Vec3::NEG_Y * t.sin()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            return fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll).2;\\n        }\\n        let (fh, _) = self.ground_axes();\\n200→        let t = self.current().tilt.clamp(0.0, 90.0).to_radians();\\n        (fh * t.sin() + Vec3::Y * t.cos()).normalize()\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        self.target + Vec3::Y * self.current().height_offset\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n210→            return fp.eye;\\n        }\\n        self.look_at() - self.forward() * self.current().distance\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\\n        if let Some(fp) = &self.fp {\\n            let (fwd, _, up) = fp_basis(fp.yaw, fp.pitch, fp.roll);\\n            let eye = fp.eye;\\n            let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, up);\\n220→            let mut fov = fp.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n            if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n                fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n            }\\n            let near = if fp.near > 0.0 { fp.near } else { 0.08 };\\n            let far = if fp.far > near { fp.far } else { 3000.0 };\\n            let proj = glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect.max(0.01), near, far);\\n            return CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: false };\\n        }\\n        let p = &self.current();\\n230→        let fwd = self.forward();\\n        let eye = self.eye();\\n        let view = glam::camera::rh::view::look_to_mat4(eye, fwd, self.up());\\n        let mut fov = p.fov.clamp(1.0, 170.0).to_radians();\\n        if aspect < 1.0 && aspect > 0.0 {\\n            // Taller than wide (a phone held upright): the field of view is the width's, so the\\n            // sides are not cut down to a sliver.\\n            fov = (2.0 * ((fov * 0.5).tan() / aspect).atan()).min(150f32.to_radians());\\n        }\\n        let far = (p.distance * 4.0 + 200.0).max(300.0);\\n240→        let proj = if p.ortho {\\n            let half_h = p.distance * (fov * 0.5).tan();\\n            let half_w = half_h * aspect;\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::orthographic(-half_w, half_w, -half_h, half_h, 0.05, far)\\n        } else {\\n            glam::camera::rh::proj::directx::perspective(fov, aspect, 0.1, far)\\n        };\\n        CameraData { view, proj, eye, forward: fwd, ortho: p.ortho }\\n    }\\n\\n250→    /// World-space ray through a pixel (origin, direction).\\n    pub fn screen_ray(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\\n        let cam = self.data(size.x / size.y.max(1.0));\\n        let inv = (cam.proj * cam.view).inverse();\\n        let ndc = Vec2::new(px.x / size.x * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0 - px.y / size.y * 2.0);\\n        let near = inv.project_point3(ndc.extend(0.0));\\n        let far = inv.project_point3(ndc.extend(1.0));\\n        (near, (far - near).normalize())\\n    }\\n\\n260→    /// Where a pixel's ray hits the horizontal plane at `height`.\\n    pub fn ground_point(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2, height: f32) -> Option<Vec3> {\\n        let (o, d) = self.screen_ray(px, size);\\n        if d.y.abs() < 1e-5 {\\n            return None;\\n        }\\n        let t = (height - o.y) / d.y;\\n        (t > 0.0).then(|| o + d * t)\\n    }\\n\\n270→    /// Converts stick/WASD input (x right, y up) into a world direction on the ground plane.\\n    pub fn relative_move(&self, input: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\\n        let (f, r) = self.ground_axes();\\n        let w = r * input.x + f * input.y;\\n        Vec2::new(w.x, w.z)\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn view_proj(&self, aspect: f32) -> Mat4 {\\n        let d = self.data(aspect);\\n        d.proj * d.view\\n280→    }\\n}\\n\\n#[cfg(test)]\\nmod tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn first_person_yaw_zero_faces_north() {\\n        let (forward, _, _) = fp_basis(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);\\n290→        assert!(forward.z < -0.9, \\\"{forward:?}\\\");\\n        assert!(forward.x.abs() < 0.05 && forward.y.abs() < 0.05, \\\"{forward:?}\\\");\\n        let (up_look, _, _) = fp_basis(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\\n        assert!(up_look.y > 0.4, \\\"{up_look:?}\\\");\\n        let cam = FpCam::default();\\n        assert!((cam.near - 0.08).abs() < 1e-5);\\n        assert!((cam.far - 3000.0).abs() < 1.0);\\n        let mut rig = CameraRig::default();\\n        rig.fp = Some(cam);\\n        assert!(rig.forward().z < -0.9);\\n300→    }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"100→    let mut right = forward.cross(Vec3::Y);\\n    if right.length_squared() < 1e-6 {\\n        right = Vec3::new(cy, 0.0, sy);\\n    }\\n    right = right.normalize();\\n    let up = right.cross(forward).normalize();\\n    let (sr, cr) = roll.sin_cos();\\n    let rolled_right = right * cr + up * sr;\\n    let rolled_up = up * cr - right * sr;\\n    (forward, rolled_right.normalize(), rolled_up.normalize())\\n110→}\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\\npub struct CameraRig {\\n    /// Target parameters (what the panel edits).\\n    pub params: CameraParams,\\n    /// Smoothed focus point.\\n    pub target: Vec3,\\n    /// When set, the rig is a first-person camera and ignores the chase parameters.\\n    pub fp: Option<FpCam>,\\n120→    initialized: bool,\\n    /// Blending from earlier parameters: (from, elapsed, duration).\\n    blend: Option<(CameraParams, f32, f32)>,\\n}\\n\\nimpl Default for CameraRig {\\n    fn default() -> Self {\\n        Self::new(CameraParams::default())\\n    }\\n}\\n130→\\nimpl CameraRig {\\n    pub fn new(params: CameraParams) -> Self {\\n        Self { params, target: Vec3::ZERO, fp: None, initialized: false, blend: None }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Parameters in effect right now (blended while a transition runs).\\n    pub fn current(&self) -> CameraParams {\\n        match &self.blend {\\n            Some((from, e, d)) => {\\n140→                let t = (e / d.max(1e-3)).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\\n                from.lerp(&self.params, t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t))\\n            }\\n            None => self.params.clone(),\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /// Call before changing `params` to glide there over `seconds` instead of cutting.\\n    pub fn blend_from_current(&mut self, seconds: f32) {\\n        self.blend = Some((self.current(), 0.0, seconds));\\n150→    }\\n\\n    /// Follows `focus` with exponential smoothing.\\n    pub fn updat