{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_616","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nNight is fixed. The flag requires player movement, not a time warp.\n\nBoat and Town are also fixed. I will check the route logs to confirm the Town transition.\n\nThe latest playthrough log contains no eprintln output. The test should have printed on every goal change, so the missing lines are unexpected.The changes file is unrelated noise from result.json updates, not the game diff.\n\nThe test likely ran without printing goal changes. Cargo combined stdout and stderr into the log, so the missing eprintln lines are not a defect. The playthrough finished successfully.\n\nA potential bug in the first-person view is being investigated. The player entity is placed at world coordinates far from the origin, while the overlook scenery is near (0,0). This spatial mismatch could break the fixed camera view.\n\nThe Rust test harness suppresses stdout and stderr for passing tests. This explains the missing eprintln output in the captured\n\nThe camera correctly log. The test passed, targets country tiles so the coverage assertion from the airstrip during succeeded without revealing gameplay. The overlook which flags were set. view is reserved for menus. Map, GPS, and monocular props are now dynamic entities rather than static boxes. They move each frame relative to the eye position and hide when inactive.\n\nThe rifle and rag are now dynamic props\n\nA passing test does that follow the eye not prove the scripted during play. They were cheats are gone. The previously static boxes, prior skeptic's complaint so this change aligns was exactly that the with the prior gap  test passes becauserequirements. Weapon the director stamps mesh swaps were not flags without player required. The prior action. I will now  claim should not besystematically list  refuted.every coverage flag and trace its source to find any remaining director-only stamps.\n\nwind_rag is a new scripted cheat. The director sets wind speed to 9 at Drive begin, so the flag is stamped without any player \n\nAll four gaps are action. The criterionfixed. Tests passed  requires the rag toacross the first-person view, ledger, dev menu, be visible at speed and suite 19. The bot greater than 6, but successfully plays  the code only checksall three endings. The raw wind length and run-all suite shows never verifies visibility. 48 passes and zero failures.\n\nThe remaining scripted beats were removed after naming specific warps. This prevents ratcheting. Criterion 4's no-cheats rule now applies only to those named warps. The bot walks, boards, fires, and confirms ledger choices.\n\nThe systematic review of coverage flags continues. Most are valid player actions. Only jam_cleared and enemy_jam might be forced by begin. Weapon_broke, syrette, wounds, fever_warned, and pill_taken all \n\nThe ledger test neverrequire real player  earns the ending_readinput. The list is incomplete. flag. The chair and read worlds remain as Route::Chair and Route::Read. Play_route still awards endings during a full game. The bot_ledger uses the route to select menu items with act inputs. This counts as in-play choice with normal inputs. A human new game can pick any finale because choose_finale ignores the spec's ending index. The Route::Human script sets finale to None and opens the ledger. A player selecting Read works correctly.\n\nDev noclip persists and act 10 opens the pause menu. The test passed.\n\nLaunch evidence must be spot-checked. The verification plan gates on this step. The implementer claims launches passed. I need to confirm that screenshots and logs\n\nplayer_rescued is a scripted setup. The exist and are not blank. director forces the player's health to zero at step start, so the rescue beat triggers automatically rather than from real combat.\n\ncompanion_patched and companion_overdosed are valid player actions. The bot holds the interaction button while the director downs the companion.\n\ncompanion_died is a scripted death timer. The director downs the companion far away so the player cannot patch them. The bot idles and never chooses to let them die.\n\nLaunch logs, screenshots, hub log, and handin are being checked for acceptance and integrity. The 48-pass run-all result is plausible given prior suite counts.\n\nThe companion death timer is a real event. The bot simply waits","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c90869bb-44cb-4504-b308-77ef960d8630-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/launch.log","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c90869bb-44cb-4504-b308-77ef960d8630-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/launch-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c90869bb-44cb-4504-b308-77ef960d8630-55","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/hub.log","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5254,"output_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":116096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"57edf82f-271b-4586-a24b-7bb671eaf1ac"}
