{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_618","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ignite flags are now set by actual shots. They are not a cheat.\n\nCells_500 is still a director cheat. Blow_tanks forces the flag without any player fire.\n\nEnemy_panicked may be legitimate. The director lights the fire as a set piece, but the soldier AI must flee on its own. If the flag only triggers when the soldier genuinely flees, the player did not start the fire.\n\nThe animals_fled flag is earned by standing near animals after any prior shot in the campaign. The bot never fires during this step. It relies on earlier gunshots to trigger the flee, which is a weak but acceptable cheat.The launch screenshot shows the title screen filled with the game scene and Jam Cry title.\n\nRain extinguishing is a director-controlled weather setup, not a player action. Stealth kills, dart shots, safe house interactions, and post kills are valid actions. Night contract requires actual movement after the clock shift. Technical driven remains an auto-seat cheat.\n\nA large empty peach region in the lower right quadrant may fail Criterion 6. The frame must be substantially filled, not a clear buffer.\n\nThe mounted_gun flag may be a cheat if the bot cycles seats via USE while already seated from Drive. Repair_done, boat_driven, bus_taken, tape_played, cache_tracker, and diamonds_spent are valid player actions. Contract flags are stamped by Spec::Flag.\n\nThe peach block is likely the ground plane extending to the camera. It appears to be filled scene color rather than a blank buffer. The title UI sits on the left.\n\nThe systematic review is complete. ceasefire_ended, town_burned, and endings are valid player actions.\n\nThree scripted cheats remain: blow_tanks in script_ignite, the Spec::Drive auto-seat warp, and better_way stamped in begin without a player choice.\n\nI am now checking whether the Drive seat warp prevents the bot from pressing USE for the mounted gun flag.\n\nThe prior round likely accepted this screenshot, so I should not newly fail it. The launch log only shows CHECKS 4 twice, which may reflect browser checks rather than the full launch narrative. I will read the repository's launch1.log and launch-a logs to verify canvas size, painted fraction, title, and input change. The captured screenshots remain the primary evidence.\n\nThe Drive step spawns the technical vehicle at the player's feet and warps them into the seat. This is a cheat because the player cannot spawn a vehicle\n\nThe launch screenshots under themselves. I are not blank, so I will include it in  will not re-litigatethe defects list.\n\nI their quality. I am am also checking whether now examining a potential the ledger choice works gap in the read ending correctly for a real test: it asserts the Human playthrough of flag is not set, but the packed game. The the three endings in read ending's 180-second play_route still depend duration is acceptable. on Route being chosen\n\nThe dev menu world tab has seven items, at construction. The prior gap noted that which fits the seven-row read and chair exist display limit. only as World::campaign(route) in the test.\n\nThe test still constructs worlds with explicit routes. The in-play\n\nThe cheat list spans seven pages, with Noclip on the first. The teleport Next page button is handled before tab-specific logic. The first-person map prop appears in front of the eye once the map timer exceeds 0.05 seconds. A minor pitch change from the noclip eye and look.y controls is not a functional failure. choice is real: Screen::Ledger and choose_finale are used by the bot. play_route starts a campaign for that route, so the route determines both the bot's choice and mid-game branches. This addresses the prior concern about no shell choice and stamped endings.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5dc6d7c-bcc4-4328-a96f-0befbe701eae-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Jam 