0,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,101,110,100,105,110,103,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":21,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"- **Genre:** open-world first-person shooter with survival and systemic-sandbox rules (fire, wind, wear, fever, permadeath companions).\"},{\"line_number\":145,\"content\":\"**Four mercs (DECIDED: the dossier pick).** On a new game the player picks one. The other three become the recruitable companions, so write their lines to work without knowing who the player picked.\"},{\"line_number\":178,\"content\":\"You land at night on a cargo flight whose crates are stencilled for both sides. Papa Lazare finds you collapsing with fever on his doorstep, and a companion gets you on your feet. You take work from the Council and the Hand to get close to the Chandler. Each job undoes the last. Your assassination at the Hotel Splendide ends the ceasefire and the town burns. The crates, the tapes and the ledger all lead to the old Cement Works. There the Chandler, dying of the same fever, shows you the ledger: every buyer, your two employers, and the firm that hired you, paid by the Chandler himself. He hired his own killer because he wanted an ending or a successor. **Three endings (player's choice):**\"},{\"line_number\":297,\"content\":\"- **Going down at 0 HP:** if a companion is alive and their rescue isn't spent, you go to the **rescue sequence** (§5.12). Otherwise a death card, then reload the last autosave.\"},{\"line_number\":373,\"content\":\"- **Rescue:** when you go down, the best living companion (once per rest) appears out of the bush within 6 s, shooting. In first person you are dragged 10–15 m on your back, sky lurching, then a syrette to the neck and a line of dialogue. You stand at 50 HP with your sidearm.\"},{\"line_number\":374,\"content\":\"- **Down companion:** during shared jobs or their own trouble they can go down: gibberish cries, on-map marker, **45 s to reach them**. Options at their side: *Patch up* (costs a syrette), or if they are too far gone only *Overdose* (a mercy kill with a morphine syrette, a held button, and a final line). If you don't come, they die alone.\"},{\"line_number\":375,\"content\":\"- **Permadeath:** a dead companion's stool stays empty, and the map gets a pencil note. Survivors mention it.\"},{\"line_number\":376,\"content\":\"- **\\\"A better way\\\":** before each main contract a living companion may offer an alternate approach (more money, more danger, and it can leave them trapped). There are three scripted variants, one per companion, each usable with any companion. Buddy trouble happens at most 3 times in a run.\"},{\"line_number\":405,\"content\":\"  - Mesh: a 128×128 vertex-coloured grid from the biome and height data, roads and rivers as thin ribbons, place names in engine `Text3d`, handwritten marks for discoveries, posts, caches, contracts and companion notes. Burn scars update every few seconds.\"},{\"line_number\":411,\"content\":\"Six cassettes hidden on the map (hotel, mission, depot, lodge, cement works, the bar after the fire). In first person you hold a battered recorder (usable while walking): the Chandler and Thandiwe in gibberish with large subtitles. Each tape is about 8 lines, and together they are the real story. Tape 5 gives the Cement Works its meaning. The last tape is yours, written from the player's actual run (merc name, companions lost, who paid you most).\"},{\"line_number\":421,\"content\":\"- Progress JSON in `localStorage`, using `pav_app/save.rs`'s pattern. It holds contract state, inventory with conditions, discoveries, time, wind, fever timer, companions, post timers, sparse burn map, diamonds, Infamy.\"},{\"line_number\":499,\"content\":\"**`shared-world`**, seats `1-4`. Your friends are your companions. Read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md` whole, and download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `hub/`.\"},{\"line_number\":518,\"content\":\"Enemies, fire, jams and all the other systems are live, with a fixed loadout and no shop, fever on a short mild timer, and no pause. Down players can be **dragged and patched** by friends (the companion mechanic), and otherwise respawn on the truck after 45 s, up to 6 team lives.\"},{\"line_number\":629,\"content\":\"- **Balance (live sliders with value and default tick, \\\"Reset to defaults\\\" per page and for all):** enemy accuracy, enemy damage, player damage, detection rate, enemy count multiplier, weapon wear, jam chance, weapon-break threshold, fire spread rate, burn time, wind strength, burn damage, fever interval, fever severity, syrette heal, companion rescue window, vehicle speed, vehicle toughness, contract pay, post re-man hours, player speed.\"},{\"line_number\":698,\"content\":\"| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\"},{\"line_number\":699,\"content\":\"| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\"},{\"line_number\":703,\"content\":\"| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\"},{\"line_number\":707,\"content\":\"| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\"},{\"line_number\":722,\"content\":\"                                    companions, fever, contracts, economy, map, net, terrain, attract, bot\"},{\"line_number\":820,\"content\":\"- **Companions:** rescue fires once per rest and player stands up at 50. Downed companion timer. Patch and overdose. Death stays dead across save and load.\"},{\"line_number\":859,\"content\":\"**Coverage flags (each set by real play; a test passes on the union across the three playthrough runs, since no single run can both save and lose the same companion or reach every ending):** map raised, waypoint set, GPS followed, monocular tag, wind rag visible at speed > 6, jam cleared, enemy jam seen, weapon broke, weapon bought, locker used, syrette, each wound treatment type, fever warned, pill taken, black-out (bot route), player rescued, companion patched, companion overdosed, companion died, better-way taken, fire lit by each igniter class, 500+ cells burned in one fire, enemy panicked, animals fled, explosion chain, rain extinguished, stealth kill, dart kill, night contract, sleep used, safe house claimed, post cleared, post re-manned, technical driven, mounted gun fired, repair done, boat driven, bus taken, tape played, cache found by tracker, diamonds spent, each contract, ceasefire ended, town burned, each ending.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bfc89211-1565-472c-bb9e-62ecb7477911-62","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"650→\\n**Materials:** add `engine/assets/materials/{rust_tin,laterite,stained_concrete,thatch,burnt_wood,painted_steel}.json`.\\n\\n### 9.2 New assets (format-2 prop JSON in `engine/assets/props/lib/merc/`, §2.1 for shipping; use the engine's check loop)\\n- **Weapons:** the §5.3 list, each with `grip`, `fore`, `mag` and `muzzle` sockets, plus a separate magazine or shell part where reloads show it. Rust and wear through material params.\\n- **Hand props:** pliers, knife, syrette, pill bottle, lighter, wrench, map board, GPS, monocular, tape recorder, cigarette, tracker.\\n- **Vehicles:** technical, jeep, truck, river boat, plus wreck variants. Wheels drawn from `VehicleView`.\\n- **Buildings and military:** tin shack, mud-brick hut with thatch, concrete bunker, watchtower, sandbag walls, oil tanks, fuel drums, jerrycans, ammo crates, radio mast, roadside sign, hotel ruin pieces, cement silos and conveyors, church, pump machinery, cable ferry, market goods, bar interior, garage, shop shelving, tires, burnt car.\\n- **Vegetation:** flat-top acacia, baobab, thorn bush, river trees, reeds, termite mound, kopje boulders, grass clumps (custom mesh, `flags::GRASS`, dry colours, 0.5–1.2 m tall, thick enough to hide a crouching man).\\n- **Generic props:** use the store (`assets find=`).\\n660→- **Grass and burnable trees are view-side caches per chunk**, rebuilt when that chunk's burn version changes. The sim only needs the density function. Don't put them in `statics`.\\n- **Water:** carve the river into per-chunk water zone strips for swimming. Draw them with the engine's water, with ripples only near the player.\\n\\n### 9.3 Animation (engine's native system as the base)\\n**The first-person rig uses the engine's own parts:**\\n- Biped `Skel`, key-pose clips (`engine/anim/merc_fp.json` in the existing readable format), and IK.\\n- Pin hands to the held prop's sockets (a small addition), so every gun is held correctly.\\n- Transform the upper body by camera rotation so the head joint is the eye, and draw only arms and held props.\\n- Add an additive procedural layer on the weapon root: walk bob, stick and mouse sway, recoil spring, breathing, fever tremor, wall pull-back (lower the gun when a short ray hits something).\\n- Clip files carry timed events (`mag_out`, `mag_in`, `sound: click`) as data.\\n670→\\n**Author these with `anim_edit` and check with `animsheet` and `filmstrip`:**\\n- **First person (about 30):** idle and sprint per weapon class, draw, holster, reload for magazine, belt, shell, break-action, rocket; jam clear per class; bolt slap; throw; machete swing; backstab; syrette; six wound treatments; pills; map raise and lower; monocular; tracker; recorder; wheel loop; repair; overdose; pick up; gun breaking apart; being dragged (camera path plus arms); stand up after rescue.\\n- **NPC:** rifle idle, walk, run, strafe (cut from the Swat takes), crouch and fire, prone, fire upper-body (derive from `Pistol_Aim_*` and Swat), reload, jam clear, throw (existing), panic run and burning flail (new), drag someone (new), being dragged (new), wounded crawl (`MESH2MOTION/Crawl`, slower), deaths (existing), sit and bar idle, market carrying (existing). Mount weapons through the look's `weapon` field with an `asset` held by its `grip` socket (`engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`, \\\"Library assets in game code\\\", shows the form; you'll need a new `WeaponKind` for guns).\\n- **Vehicles:** wheel spin and suspension (existing), hood up, gun traverse.\\n- **Secondary motion (`rig.rs` chains):** the red rag, scarves, antenna whip.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Audio (all in code, no audio files; extend `pav_audio`)\\n680→Everything renders through the same Rust code live and offline (`render_events`), so tests can measure it.\\n- **Engine additions:** buses (Master, Music, SFX, Voice); looping voices with live gain, pitch and cutoff; a data-driven patch table instead of the closed match; a simple feedback delay for space; distance low-pass; ducking.\\n- **Music: default volume 10%** (a constant in settings, test it). Sparse, generative and code-written:\\n  - Pluck (Karplus-Strong) guitar and thumb-piano figures, hand drums, a low drone, distorted guitar in combat.\\n  - States: Title, Explore day and night, Tension, Combat, Fever (detuned pads), Town (a tinny transistor-radio highlife loop with gibberish singing, placed in the world), Ending.\\n  - Original melodies only.\\n- **SFX:** one patch set per weapon family (noise burst + low thump + tail by environment), dead click, jam clatter, bolt slap, reload parts, rag flutter on high wind, fire crackle and roar by nearby cells, explosions, engine loops by RPM and damage, tyres on dirt, boat outboard, wrench, syrette, pliers, finger snap, pills rattle, footsteps by surface, grass rustle, insects and birds by time of day, wind by speed, thunder, tracker beeps, menu ticks.\\n- **Voices: Animalese-style gibberish.** A formant synth turns each subtitle's syllables into short vowel-consonant blips at a per-character pitch and timbre, with a little contour for questions and shouting. Same system for barks (faster, louder) and tapes (through a tape-hiss, band-limited filter). Subtitles on by default.\\n- **Fever and critical states** low-pass the world and add tinnitus and heartbeat.\\n- **Web:** the browser only starts audio after a gesture (`resume_audio` exists). Attract mode is silent until the first gesture (which exits it anyway) unless the context is already running.\\n690→\\n---\\n\\n## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\\nData in `engine/game/merc/contracts.toml`: objectives as a small state machine with triggers, approaches, pay and consequences. Every objective exposes a `Goal` the bot and the dev tools can read.\\n\\n| # | Contract (giver) | What happens | Teaches or shows | About |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\\n| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\\n700→| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\\n| B2 | **Water Rights** (Ruvuma) | Undo Tshala: sabotage the Council's pump station at night by boat. Sleep till midnight, camo, dart rifle | Sleep picker, night, stealth, boat, swimming, machete | 10 min |\\n| B3 | **Papers** (Sister Perpetua) | Drive medicine to the mission. Ambush, pursuit, engine failure: repair under fire. Reward: pills | Pursuit, damage stages, repair, fever economy | 8 min |\\n| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\\n| C1 | **Inspection** (Tshala) | Kill the Hand's negotiator at Hotel Splendide from the ridge. Tag with the monocular, wind on the bullet, get out past GP5. Consequence: **the ceasefire ends** | Sniper, tagging, world state | 8 min |\\n| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\\n| C3 | **The Town Burns** | Kilometre 40 ablaze at night. Get through, get Papa Lazare or Mr. Desai out (you can save one). Ash, panic, soldiers looting. Shops move to the Boat Shed afterward | Fire as a level, moral beat, town after | 6 min |\\n| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\\n| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\\n\\n710→Side content open from A1 on: 12 diamond caches, 6 tapes, 6 guard posts, 3 safe houses, 3 bus stops (fast travel: fade, time passes, fare 1 diamond), wildlife, two minor clinic errands.\\n\\n**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Architecture\\n\\n### 12.1 Dev folder\\n```\",\"content_concise\":\"650→\\n**Materials:** add `engine/assets/materials/{rust_tin,laterite,stained_concrete,thatch,burnt_wood,painted_steel}.json`.\\n\\n### 9.2 New assets (format-2 prop JSON in `engine/assets/props/lib/merc/`, §2.1 for shipping; use the engine's check loop)\\n- **Weapons:** the §5.3 list, each with `grip`, `fore`, `mag` and `muzzle` sockets, plus a separate magazine or shell part where reloads show it. Rust and wear through material params.\\n- **Hand props:** pliers, knife, syrette, pill bottle, lighter, wrench, map board, GPS, monocular, tape recorder, cigarette, tracker.\\n- **Vehicles:** technical, jeep, truck, river boat, plus wreck variants. Wheels drawn from `VehicleView`.\\n- **Buildings and military:** tin shack, mud-brick hut with thatch, concrete bunker, watchtower, sandbag walls, oil tanks, fuel drums, jerrycans, ammo crates, radio mast, roadside sign, hotel ruin pieces, cement silos and conveyors, church, pump machinery, cable ferry, market goods, bar interior, garage, shop shelving, tires, burnt car.\\n- **Vegetation:** flat-top acacia, baobab, thorn bush, river trees, reeds, termite mound, kopje boulders, grass clumps (custom mesh, `flags::GRASS`, dry colours, 0.5–1.2 m tall, thick enough to hide a crouching man).\\n- **Generic props:** use the store (`assets find=`).\\n660→- **Grass and burnable trees are view-side caches per chunk**, rebuilt when that chunk's burn version changes. The sim only needs the density function. Don't put them in `statics`.\\n- **Water:** carve the river into per-chunk water zone strips for swimming. Draw them with the engine's water, with ripples only near the player.\\n\\n### 9.3 Animation (engine's native system as the base)\\n**The first-person rig uses the engine's own parts:**\\n- Biped `Skel`, key-pose clips (`engine/anim/merc_fp.json` in the existing readable format), and IK.\\n- Pin hands to the held prop's sockets (a small addition), so every gun is held correctly.\\n- Transform the upper body by camera rotation so the head joint is the eye, and draw only arms and held props.\\n- Add an additive procedural layer on the weapon root: walk bob, stick and mouse sway, recoil spring, breathing, fever tremor, wall pull-back (lower the gun when a short ray hits something).\\n- Clip files carry timed events (`mag_out`, `mag_in`, `sound: click`) as data.\\n670→\\n**Author these with `anim_edit` and check with `animsheet` and `filmstrip`:**\\n- **First person (about 30):** idle and sprint per weapon class, draw, holster, reload for magazine, belt, shell, break-action, rocket; jam clear per class; bolt slap; throw; machete swing; backstab; syrette; six wound treatments; pills; map raise and lower; monocular; tracker; recorder; wheel loop; repair; overdose; pick up; gun breaking apart; being dragged (camera path plus arms); stand up after rescue.\\n- **NPC:** rifle idle, walk, run, strafe (cut from the Swat takes), crouch and fire, prone, fire upper-body (derive from `Pistol_Aim_*` and Swat), reload, jam clear, throw (existing), panic run and burning flail (new), drag someone (new), being dragged (new), wounded crawl (`MESH2MOTION/Crawl`, slower), deaths (existing), sit and bar idle, market carrying (existing). Mount weapons through the look's `weapon` field with an `asset` held by its `grip` socket (`engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`, \\\"Library assets in game code\\\", shows the form; you'll need a new `WeaponKind` for guns).\\n- **Vehicles:** wheel spin and suspension (existing), hood up, gun traverse.\\n- **Secondary motion (`rig.rs` chains):** the red rag, scarves, antenna whip.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Audio (all in code, no audio files; extend `pav_audio`)\\n680→Everything renders through the same Rust code live and offline (`render_events`), so tests can measure it.\\n- **Engine additions:** buses (Master, Music, SFX, Voice); looping voices with live gain, pitch and cutoff; a data-driven patch table instead of the closed match; a simple feedback delay for space; distance low-pass; ducking.\\n- **Music: default volume 10%** (a constant in settings, test it). Sparse, generative and code-written:\\n  - Pluck (Karplus-Strong) guitar and thumb-piano figures, hand drums, a low drone, distorted guitar in combat.\\n  - States: Title, Explore day and night, Tension, Combat, Fever (detuned pads), Town (a tinny transistor-radio highlife loop with gibberish singing, placed in the world), Ending.\\n  - Original melodies only.\\n- **SFX:** one patch set per weapon family (noise burst + low thump + tail by environment), dead click, jam clatter, bolt slap, reload parts, rag flutter on high wind, fire crackle and roar by nearby cells, explosions, engine loops by RPM and damage, tyres on dirt, boat outboard, wrench, syrette, pliers, finger snap, pills rattle, footsteps by surface, grass rustle, insects and birds by time of day, wind by speed, thunder, tracker beeps, menu ticks.\\n- **Voices: Animalese-style gibberish.** A formant synth turns each subtitle's syllables into short vowel-consonant blips at a per-character pitch and timbre, with a little contour for questions and shouting. Same system for barks (faster, louder) and tapes (through a tape-hiss, band-limited filter). Subtitles on by default.\\n- **Fever and critical states** low-pass the world and add tinnitus and heartbeat.\\n- **Web:** the browser only starts audio after a gesture (`resume_audio` exists). Attract mode is silent until the first gesture (which exits it anyway) unless the context is already running.\\n690→\\n---\\n\\n## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\\nData in `engine/game/merc/contracts.toml`: objectives as a small state machine with triggers, approaches, pay and consequences. Every objective exposes a `Goal` the bot and the dev tools can read.\\n\\n| # | Contract (giver) | What happens | Teaches or shows | About |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\\n| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\\n700→| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\\n| B2 | **Water Rights** (Ruvuma) | Undo Tshala: sabotage the Council's pump station at night by boat. Sleep till midnight, camo, dart rifle | Sleep picker, night, stealth, boat, swimming, machete | 10 min |\\n| B3 | **Papers** (Sister Perpetua) | Drive medicine to the mission. Ambush, pursuit, engine failure: repair under fire. Reward: pills | Pursuit, damage stages, repair, fever economy | 8 min |\\n| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\\n| C1 | **Inspection** (Tshala) | Kill the Hand's negotiator at Hotel Splendide from the ridge. Tag with the monocular, wind on the bullet, get out past GP5. Consequence: **the ceasefire ends** | Sniper, tagging, world state | 8 min |\\n| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\\n| C3 | **The Town Burns** | Kilometre 40 ablaze at night. Get through, get Papa Lazare or Mr. Desai out (you can save one). Ash, panic, soldiers looting. Shops move to the Boat Shed afterward | Fire as a level, moral beat, town after | 6 min |\\n| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\\n| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\\n\\n710→Side content open from A1 on: 12 diamond caches, 6 tapes, 6 guard posts, 3 safe houses, 3 bus stops (fast travel: fade, time passes, fare 1 diamond), wildlife, two minor clinic errands.\\n\\n**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Architecture\\n\\n### 12.1 Dev folder\\n```\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":650,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"\\n**Materials:** add `engine/assets/materials/{rust_tin,laterite,stained_concrete,thatch,burnt_wood,painted_steel}.json`.\\n\\n### 9.2 New assets (format-2 prop JSON in `engine/assets/props/lib/merc/`, §2.1 for shipping; use the engine's check loop)\\n- **Weapons:** the §5.3 list, each with `grip`, `fore`, `mag` and `muzzle` sockets, plus a separate magazine or shell part where reloads show it. Rust and wear through material params.\\n- **Hand props:** pliers, knife, syrette, pill bottle, lighter, wrench, map board, GPS, monocular, tape recorder, cigarette, tracker.\\n- **Vehicles:** technical, jeep, truck, river boat, plus wreck variants. Wheels drawn from `VehicleView`.\\n- **Buildings and military:** tin shack, mud-brick hut with thatch, concrete bunker, watchtower, sandbag walls, oil tanks, fuel drums, jerrycans, ammo crates, radio mast, roadside sign, hotel ruin pieces, cement silos and conveyors, church, pump machinery, cable ferry, market goods, bar interior, garage, shop shelving, tires, burnt car.\\n- **Vegetation:** flat-top acacia, baobab, thorn bush, river trees, reeds, termite mound, kopje boulders, grass clumps (custom mesh, `flags::GRASS`, dry colours, 0.5–1.2 m tall, thick enough to hide a crouching man).\\n- **Generic props:** use the store (`assets find=`).\\n- **Grass and burnable trees are view-side caches per chunk**, rebuilt when that chunk's burn version changes. The sim only needs the density function. Don't put them in `statics`.\\n- **Water:** carve the river into per-chunk water zone strips for swimming. Draw them with the engine's water, with ripples only near the player.\\n\\n### 9.3 Animation (engine's native system as the base)\\n**The first-person rig uses the engine's own parts:**\\n- Biped `Skel`, key-pose clips (`engine/anim/merc_fp.json` in the existing readable format), and IK.\\n- Pin hands to the held prop's sockets (a small addition), so every gun is held correctly.\\n- Transform the upper body by camera rotation so the head joint is the eye, and draw only arms and held props.\\n- Add an additive procedural layer on the weapon root: walk bob, stick and mouse sway, recoil spring, breathing, fever tremor, wall pull-back (lower the gun when a short ray hits something).\\n- Clip files carry timed events (`mag_out`, `mag_in`, `sound: click`) as data.\\n\\n**Author these with `anim_edit` and check with `animsheet` and `filmstrip`:**\\n- **First person (about 30):** idle and sprint per weapon class, draw, holster, reload for magazine, belt, shell, break-action, rocket; jam clear per class; bolt slap; throw; machete swing; backstab; syrette; six wound treatments; pills; map raise and lower; monocular; tracker; recorder; wheel loop; repair; overdose; pick up; gun breaking apart; being dragged (camera path plus arms); stand up after rescue.\\n- **NPC:** rifle idle, walk, run, strafe (cut from the Swat takes), crouch and fire, prone, fire upper-body (derive from `Pistol_Aim_*` and Swat), reload, jam clear, throw (existing), panic run and burning flail (new), drag someone (new), being dragged (new), wounded crawl (`MESH2MOTION/Crawl`, slower), deaths (existing), sit and bar idle, market carrying (existing). Mount weapons through the look's `weapon` field with an `asset` held by its `grip` socket (`engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`, \\\"Library assets in game code\\\", shows the form; you'll need a new `WeaponKind` for guns).\\n- **Vehicles:** wheel spin and suspension (existing), hood up, gun traverse.\\n- **Secondary motion (`rig.rs` chains):** the red rag, scarves, antenna whip.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Audio (all in code, no audio files; extend `pav_audio`)\\nEverything renders through the same Rust code live and offline (`render_events`), so tests can measure it.\\n- **Engine additions:** buses (Master, Music, SFX, Voice); looping voices with live gain, pitch and cutoff; a data-driven patch table instead of the closed match; a simple feedback delay for space; distance low-pass; ducking.\\n- **Music: default volume 10%** (a constant in settings, test it). Sparse, generative and code-written:\\n  - Pluck (Karplus-Strong) guitar and thumb-piano figures, hand drums, a low drone, distorted guitar in combat.\\n  - States: Title, Explore day and night, Tension, Combat, Fever (detuned pads), Town (a tinny transistor-radio highlife loop with gibberish singing, placed in the world), Ending.\\n  - Original melodies only.\\n- **SFX:** one patch set per weapon family (noise burst + low thump + tail by environment), dead click, jam clatter, bolt slap, reload parts, rag flutter on high wind, fire crackle and roar by nearby cells, explosions, engine loops by RPM and damage, tyres on dirt, boat outboard, wrench, syrette, pliers, finger snap, pills rattle, footsteps by surface, grass rustle, insects and birds by time of day, wind by speed, thunder, tracker beeps, menu ticks.\\n- **Voices: Animalese-style gibberish.** A formant synth turns each subtitle's syllables into short vowel-consonant blips at a per-character pitch and timbre, with a little contour for questions and shouting. Same system for barks (faster, louder) and tapes (through a tape-hiss, band-limited filter). Subtitles on by default.\\n- **Fever and critical states** low-pass the world and add tinnitus and heartbeat.\\n- **Web:** the browser only starts audio after a gesture (`resume_audio` exists). Attract mode is silent until the first gesture (which exits it anyway) unless the context is already running.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. The demo: contracts and beat sheet\\nData in `engine/game/merc/contracts.toml`: objectives as a small state machine with triggers, approaches, pay and consequences. Every objective exposes a `Goal` the bot and the dev tools can read.\\n\\n| # | Contract (giver) | What happens | Teaches or shows | About |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A0 | **Landing Fees** | Night landing at the airstrip, crates stencilled for both sides, Bakker's goodbye. Walk the road with the map up. The fever hits at the bar door, and you wake in the back room with a companion and pills | Look, walk, map, GPS, fever, pills, the town | 6 min |\\n| A1 | **On the House** (Papa Lazare) | Clear Kilo 38. Scripted first jam. Scripted first down and companion rescue. Wound treatment. Loot a rusty rifle. Claim the Pump House. First shopping trip | Combat, jam, rescue, treatment, loot condition, safe house, shop, sleep | 10 min |\\n| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\\n| B2 | **Water Rights** (Ruvuma) | Undo Tshala: sabotage the Council's pump station at night by boat. Sleep till midnight, camo, dart rifle | Sleep picker, night, stealth, boat, swimming, machete | 10 min |\\n| B3 | **Papers** (Sister Perpetua) | Drive medicine to the mission. Ambush, pursuit, engine failure: repair under fire. Reward: pills | Pursuit, damage stages, repair, fever economy | 8 min |\\n| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\\n| C1 | **Inspection** (Tshala) | Kill the Hand's negotiator at Hotel Splendide from the ridge. Tag with the monocular, wind on the bullet, get out past GP5. Consequence: **the ceasefire ends** | Sniper, tagging, world state | 8 min |\\n| C2 | **Receipts** (Ruvuma) | Hijack the arms convoy from the airstrip on the quarry road. Crates are stencilled for both sides, and the ledger is mentioned. Heavy fight with rocket man and flame trooper | Special weapons, explosives, tape reveal | 8 min |\\n| C3 | **The Town Burns** | Kilometre 40 ablaze at night. Get through, get Papa Lazare or Mr. Desai out (you can save one). Ash, panic, soldiers looting. Shops move to the Boat Shed afterward | Fire as a level, moral beat, town after | 6 min |\\n| D1 | **Last Order** | Assault or infiltrate the Cement Works, both armies present, surviving companion arrives. The Chandler, the ledger | Everything together | 10 min |\\n| D2 | **Ending** | Burn it (fire finale) / Read it (hold the mast 3 min) / Take the chair. Final tape, credits, return to title | Choice | 3 min |\\n\\nSide content open from A1 on: 12 diamond caches, 6 tapes, 6 guard posts, 3 safe houses, 3 bus stops (fast travel: fade, time passes, fare 1 diamond), wildlife, two minor clinic errands.\\n\\n**Coverage rule:** the game keeps a `coverage` set in `Game::status` (one flag per row of §15's feature list). The playthrough test asserts every flag is set. That is how you prove the demo shows ALL features.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Architecture\\n\\n### 12.1 Dev folder\\n```\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"e9bbdb07-9c29-4cc6-8cfb-ba89935117db"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_627","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The prior gap concerns the director cheating.\n\nFirst-person and ledger choice fixes are confirmed. Director cheating is only partially fixed. script_ignite still calls blow_tanks without a weapon. Spec::Drive still warps the player into the seat. Spec::Better and Spec::Patch/Overdose/Die still stamp better_way in begin().\n\nSpec::Panic lights the fire in begin() and the bot does nothing. The anti-ratchet rule forbids teleport and cheats and requires real play coverage. Only blow_tanks will be flagged, since it is inside script_ignite and stamps explosion_chain and cells_500 without a weapon.\n\nThe 180-second crouch test passed, confirming ending_read is reachable. A potential bug was spotted: the ledger Route::Human bot always selects burn, while Route::Read's script uses Spec::Ending(1).\n\nThe ledger playthrough passed, confirming the bot path is fixed. The dev menu is also fixed. First-person is confirmed fixed in merc-all2. I am now considering whether to refute the remaining director cheats.\n\nSpec::Drive warps the player into the vehicle seat without a USE action. This is a warp into a vehicle, not a position teleport like Boat. The prior gap examples did not list auto-enter as a prohibited cheat.\n\nBus teleport is allowed. present_ending teleports only in unit tests, not the playthrough bot. blackout teleports to the safe house as a designed fever consequence. Spec::Bus script sets coordinates, which is permitted. begin() runs for any player, so auto-seating is not a bot-only cheat.\n\nSpec::Drive is a director cheat. It forces any player into the driver's seat at the start of every drive objective. Criterion 4 forbids teleport and warps. This was the director cheat the prior round asked to remove, but it was missed in this spec.\n\nThe Drive auto-seat is a demonstrable defect against Criterion 4 and will be included in the refutation. Spec::Better stamps the better_way flag before the player acts, so done() returns true immediately.\n\nSpec::Better auto-completes in the same advance_script iteration as it begins, with zero player input. Patch, Overdose, and Die also stamp better_way again. The companion is downed by the director, but the coverage flag is set without the alternate approach being chosen or played. Criterion 4 requires a companion's alternate approach to be playable and covered by real play. Auto-completing the step violates this gating criterion.\n\nPatch is the only step that actually requires player input. It demands holding interact to down the companion, while Better and the later specs merely stamp flags. The bot therefore completes Patch without ever choosing the alternate approach, leaving the coverage flag set without real play.\n\nThe prior round only refuted the named director cheats. It never explicitly addressed the better-way flag gap, so raising it now may be seen as a new objection rather than a genuine fix.\n\nThe prior round implicitly accepted the better-way flag gap because it never raised it. A new objection based on an unmet gating criterion is valid. The auto-complete behavior violates Criterion 4.\n\nThe prior round only explicitly refuted named director cheats. It never raised the better-way flag gap, so implicit acceptance does not apply. A real defect can still be raised.\n\nPanic will be included as a fourth director cheat. The bot performs no input and the fire is lit in begin(). Spawning enemies is too broad to flag. The prior round's distinction between setup and real play will guide the final list.\n\nSetup such as spawning enemies is acceptable, but outcome stamps and teleports that skip player action are not. blow_tanks is an outcome stamp, Drive seat is a teleport into the action, and better_way is another outcome stamp. Panic fire is borderline setup because the soldier actually runs to it; it will only be included if the player is supposed to ignite it. The panic plan is a coverage flag rather than a specific contract row.\n\nPanic is included because the B1 contract requires the player to light the fire, not the director. The animal step is dismissed as a secondary issue; the bot does not fire during the step, and the animals flee only because of prior shots.\n\nwind_rag is skipped because it would be a minor nit. The town position and ceasefire are already correct.\n\nThe 180-second crouch timer accumulates correctly during ledger menu frames. The Human route finale selection is verified as working. The first-person country visibility test is being checked against the 12-meter assertion.\n\nThe first-person country visibility test passed. The dev noclip pitch fix also passed. The refutation is now narrowed to the incomplete gap 3 director cheats.\n\nThe Drive auto-seat only triggers on the first technical leg. If the player already has a technical ride from a previous drive, the code skips re-seating and the bot must walk and press USE to enter. The flag is still earned during that initial warp.\n\nThe refutation will list three director cheats. script_ignite still calls blow_tanks without a weapon. Drive still warps the player into the driver seat. Panic still lights the fire in begin() while the bot sends no input. The better_way flag gap is included because it stamps a coverage flag with zero play, violating Criterion 4 and the prior gap's remedy.\n\nThe read ending test never asserts the flag becomes true after 180 seconds. The panic fire is lit by a trail of six disks, so the fleeing soldier stays on fire long enough for flee to pass three; the player does not start it.\n\nThe read ending test does assert the flag becomes true after 180 seconds. The first-person country visibility test is not in run.sh, so it cannot be used as a refute. The town molotov shot may land outside the 80-meter radius, but the test passed because a cell eventually burns.\n\nThe dev menu correctly limits the world tab to seven rows. The shell dev world \"Ignite grass\" is the seventh row, and the take(7) filter preserves it. The refutation is now complete.\n\nThe read ending timer advances during the ledger menu before the player makes a choice. If the player waits three minutes without shooting, step_t reaches 180 but finale remains zero, so the flag is not marked. The bot must still fire to trigger the ending.\n\nchoose_finale does not reset step_t. Time spent on the ledger menu counts toward the three-minute mast hold, so choosing Read after a long wait instantly completes the ending without the player actually holding the mast.\n\nThe read ending hold is purely theatrical. script_ignite ignores input, so any button press for 180 seconds satisfies the timer. The bot crouches during the finale, but the director never checks for actual button state or position.\n\nThe read ending is not being refuted for lacking a physical mast. The prior gap only required the flag to be non-instant and the choice to exist, and both are satisfied. Demanding an actual hold at a mast would raise the bar beyond the requested fix. The anti-ratchet rule against adding nits also applies.\n\nThe step_t bug is a real defect in the ending the gap asked to wire, so it will be included as one finding. The Human route still reaches the finale choice without present_ending, confirming gap 2 is fixed. The final verdict is REFUTE for incomplete gap 3, plus panic if it is clearly the same issue.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule against fresh nits is being weighed. Criterion 4 demands that every coverage flag be set by real play and that no teleport or cheat occur. If scripted explosion_chain counts as real play, the criterion holds; if it does not, the director cheat violates it. The final verdict hinges on this interpretation.\n\nThe verdict is now settled. Criterion 4 is violated because blow_tanks, Drive teleport, and better_way all set coverage flags without real player action. The prior round already flagged this pattern as dishonest.\n\nThe implementer should replace director stamps with real player actions. The bot must shoot the tanks, enter the technical ride, and complete the better-way choice through normal inputs. The existing playthrough test should still pass once the simulation is fixed.\n\nSpec::Flag is excluded from the findings because it is a chapter marker rather than a real play action. The final list remains three director cheats. The Drive teleport is being re-examined: if the player already occupies a technical seat, the bot sends axes and drives normally, so the missing action is boarding rather than warping.\n\nDrive should spawn the vehicle under the player and auto-seat them, matching the boat step. The bot must press USE to enter instead of teleporting. better_way should start as setup with the companion going down, but the flag must be earned through a real taken action rather than stamped in begin.\n\nThe HTML shell remains visible during the Ledger menu because its paint logic never hides it when the screen is set to Playing.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23a8472e-38d9-4e30-b24b-ef16cdd9721c-63","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"shell\\.hidden|Playing|dataset.screen|#shell","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23a8472e-38d9-4e30-b24b-ef16cdd9721c-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html","offset":800,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4336,"output_tokens":6252,"cache_read_input_tokens":134016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"1dc116d6-66d4-4d74-b266-908e42ceabb7"}
