,103,117,110,32,102,105,114,101,100,44,32,114,101,112,97,105,114,32,100,111,110,101,44,32,98,111,97,116,32,100,114,105,118,101,110,44,32,98,117,115,32,116,97,107,101,110,44,32,116,97,112,101,32,112,108,97,121,101,100,44,32,99,97,99,104,101,32,102,111,117,110,100,32,98,121,32,116,114,97,99,107,101,114,44,32,100,105,97,109,111,110,100,115,32,115,112,101,110,116,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,99,111,110,116,114,97,99,116,44,32,99,101,97,115,101,102,105,114,101,32,101,110,100,101,100,44,32,116,111,119,110,32,98,117,114,110,101,100,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,101,110,100,105,110,103,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"| Source idea to keep (as a kind of mechanic) | What we do better or differently |\"},{\"line_number\":376,\"content\":\"- **\\\"A better way\\\":** before each main contract a living companion may offer an alternate approach (more money, more danger, and it can leave them trapped). There are three scripted variants, one per companion, each usable with any companion. Buddy trouble happens at most 3 times in a run.\"},{\"line_number\":703,\"content\":\"| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\"},{\"line_number\":859,\"content\":\"**Coverage flags (each set by real play; a test passes on the union across the three playthrough runs, since no single run can both save and lose the same companion or reach every ending):** map raised, waypoint set, GPS followed, monocular tag, wind rag visible at speed > 6, jam cleared, enemy jam seen, weapon broke, weapon bought, locker used, syrette, each wound treatment type, fever warned, pill taken, black-out (bot route), player rescued, companion patched, companion overdosed, companion died, better-way taken, fire lit by each igniter class, 500+ cells burned in one fire, enemy panicked, animals fled, explosion chain, rain extinguished, stealth kill, dart kill, night contract, sleep used, safe house claimed, post cleared, post re-manned, technical driven, mounted gun fired, repair done, boat driven, bus taken, tape played, cache found by tracker, diamonds spent, each contract, ceasefire ended, town burned, each ending.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-127d8c02-62fb-4755-84bb-e2c59fa6a574-136","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"480→| SH3 Boat Shed | 830, 255 | Safe house with river boat |\\n| Pump station | -420, -30 | Night stealth contract, north bank |\\n| **Ombe Flats depot** | -520, -520 | Fuel tanks in a sea of grass: fire set piece, hub round |\\n| Flats junction, GP4 | 20, -420; 60, -460 | Crossroads, bus stop |\\n| SH2 Ranger's Lodge | -260, -700 | Safe house |\\n| GP5 Ridge road | 360, -520 | Post on the switchback |\\n| **Hotel Splendide** | 620, -640 | Ruined colonial hotel on the ridge. Sniper overlook at 760, -520 |\\n| GP6 Quarry road | -420, 480 | Post |\\n| **Cement Works** | -760, 620 | Silos, quarry, radio mast: the finale |\\n\\n490→**Compounds are stamps:** ASCII room files in the engine's own level format (`engine/game/merc/stamps/*.toml`, checked with `pav room_check`), with walls, roofs, props, markers (`cover`, `spawn_rifle`, `barrel`, `cache`, `bed`…) and `[[object]]`s placed on terrain pads. Interiors exist for the bar, shop, clinic, safe houses, hotel lobby and works control room. Doorways are open, with no door logic. Turn the engine's cutaway off for this game.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer (DECIDED)\\n\\nTASK.md asks to follow the hub protocol \\\"for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own\\\". I'm covering both readings: full hub sessions, a clean solo game when there is no hub, and the same co-op round playable outside the hub.\\n\\n### 7.1 Mode and tags\\n**`shared-world`**, seats `1-4`. Your friends are your companions. Read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md` whole, and download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `hub/`.\\n500→```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"10\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Burn the depot, take the ledger, get out together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · L2/RMB aim · Square/R reload or clear jam\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\nPaste `session.js` **unmodified** as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`, by editing `engine/web/index.html`. The packer keeps it there.\\n510→\\n### 7.2 The round: \\\"Contract Run\\\"\\nIn a session the game opens straight into this, with no title or menus. It takes place on the Ombe Flats slice of the map, 8–10 minutes.\\n1. Mercs start on a truck at the track's end, at dusk, with wind set to favour a fire.\\n2. Destroy three fuel tanks by any means. Fire is the obvious way.\\n3. One player takes the ledger case from the office (carrying it slows you and prevents sprinting; it can be dropped and picked up).\\n4. All living mercs reach the river boat, about 500 m south across the grass, so the fire you lit chases you out, and leave.\\n\\nEnemies, fire, jams and all the other systems are live, with a fixed loadout and no shop, fever on a short mild timer, and no pause. Down players can be **dragged and patched** by friends (the companion mechanic), and otherwise respawn on the truck after 45 s, up to 6 team lives.\\n\\n520→**Scoring:** +100 per objective shared, +10 per kill, +25 per rescue, −25 for friendly fire. `AIHub.finish({standings, scores, won, stats, awards})` by the host. `won` is true on extraction. Stats: kills, rescues, jams, cells ignited. Awards: *Arsonist, Field Medic, Rust Bucket, Last Out.* On `time-up`, the host finishes at once (within `graceMs`).\\n\\n### 7.3 Protocol checklist\\n- JS shim `window.gameNet` (§12.5) wraps `AIHub`: call `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true})` while the page parses. When it resolves `null`, run the normal game with the title screen.\\n- **Own card** (`card:true`): a live scene of the truck at dusk with the title, the players in their seat colours and ready state, how to win, this player's controls and the time left from the `card` event. Enter, ✕ or tap → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △, a named key or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Handle Enter in the JS shim (§2.3). No menus or choices, and nothing done on the card changes the round. Play begins only at `start`.\\n- `AIHub.ready()` once the sim is built, with no key press, before drawing the first frame.\\n- **World seed:** `info.seed` as the `Sim` seed on every copy. `Math.random` is not seeded in shared world and the Rust game doesn't use it.\\n- Countdown from `AIHub.time()` (negative for the first 3 s).\\n- `leave`: remove that merc. Host left: `end` arrives with `host-left`.\\n- `end`: no more input, nothing sent, sound off (master to 0, suspend).\",\"content_concise\":\"480→| SH3 Boat Shed | 830, 255 | Safe house with river boat |\\n| Pump station | -420, -30 | Night stealth contract, north bank |\\n| **Ombe Flats depot** | -520, -520 | Fuel tanks in a sea of grass: fire set piece, hub round |\\n| Flats junction, GP4 | 20, -420; 60, -460 | Crossroads, bus stop |\\n| SH2 Ranger's Lodge | -260, -700 | Safe house |\\n| GP5 Ridge road | 360, -520 | Post on the switchback |\\n| **Hotel Splendide** | 620, -640 | Ruined colonial hotel on the ridge. Sniper overlook at 760, -520 |\\n| GP6 Quarry road | -420, 480 | Post |\\n| **Cement Works** | -760, 620 | Silos, quarry, radio mast: the finale |\\n\\n490→**Compounds are stamps:** ASCII room files in the engine's own level format (`engine/game/merc/stamps/*.toml`, checked with `pav room_check`), with walls, roofs, props, markers (`cover`, `spawn_rifle`, `barrel`, `cache`, `bed`…) and `[[object]]`s placed on terrain pads. Interiors exist for the bar, shop, clinic, safe houses, hotel lobby and works control room. Doorways are open, with no door logic. Turn the engine's cutaway off for this game.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer (DECIDED)\\n\\nTASK.md asks to follow the hub protocol \\\"for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own\\\". I'm covering both readings: full hub sessions, a clean solo game when there is no hub, and the same co-op round playable outside the hub.\\n\\n### 7.1 Mode and tags\\n**`shared-world`**, seats `1-4`. Your friends are your companions. Read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md` whole, and download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `hub/`.\\n500→```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"10\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Burn the depot, take the ledger, get out together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · L2/RMB aim · Square/R reload or clear jam\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\nPaste `session.js` **unmodified** as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`, by editing `engine/web/index.html`. The packer keeps it there.\\n510→\\n### 7.2 The round: \\\"Contract Run\\\"\\nIn a session the game opens straight into this, with no title or menus. It takes place on the Ombe Flats slice of the map, 8–10 minutes.\\n1. Mercs start on a truck at the track's end, at dusk, with wind set to favour a fire.\\n2. Destroy three fuel tanks by any means. Fire is the obvious way.\\n3. One player takes the ledger case from the office (carrying it slows you and prevents sprinting; it can be dropped and picked up).\\n4. All living mercs reach the river boat, about 500 m south across the grass, so the fire you lit chases you out, and leave.\\n\\nEnemies, fire, jams and all the other systems are live, with a fixed loadout and no shop, fever on a short mild timer, and no pause. Down players can be **dragged and patched** by friends (the companion mechanic), and otherwise respawn on the truck after 45 s, up to 6 team lives.\\n\\n520→**Scoring:** +100 per objective shared, +10 per kill, +25 per rescue, −25 for friendly fire. `AIHub.finish({standings, scores, won, stats, awards})` by the host. `won` is true on extraction. Stats: kills, rescues, jams, cells ignited. Awards: *Arsonist, Field Medic, Rust Bucket, Last Out.* On `time-up`, the host finishes at once (within `graceMs`).\\n\\n### 7.3 Protocol checklist\\n- JS shim `window.gameNet` (§12.5) wraps `AIHub`: call `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true})` while the page parses. When it resolves `null`, run the normal game with the title screen.\\n- **Own card** (`card:true`): a live scene of the truck at dusk with the title, the players in their seat colours and ready state, how to win, this player's controls and the time left from the `card` event. Enter, ✕ or tap → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △, a named key or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Handle Enter in the JS shim (§2.3). No menus or choices, and nothing done on the card changes the round. Play begins only at `start`.\\n- `AIHub.ready()` once the sim is built, with no key press, before drawing the first frame.\\n- **World seed:** `info.seed` as the `Sim` seed on every copy. `Math.random` is not seeded in shared world and the Rust game doesn't use it.\\n- Countdown from `AIHub.time()` (negative for the first 3 s).\\n- `leave`: remove that merc. Host left: `end` arrives with `host-left`.\\n- `end`: no more input, nothing sent, sound off (master to 0, suspend).\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":480,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"| SH3 Boat Shed | 830, 255 | Safe house with river boat |\\n| Pump station | -420, -30 | Night stealth contract, north bank |\\n| **Ombe Flats depot** | -520, -520 | Fuel tanks in a sea of grass: fire set piece, hub round |\\n| Flats junction, GP4 | 20, -420; 60, -460 | Crossroads, bus stop |\\n| SH2 Ranger's Lodge | -260, -700 | Safe house |\\n| GP5 Ridge road | 360, -520 | Post on the switchback |\\n| **Hotel Splendide** | 620, -640 | Ruined colonial hotel on the ridge. Sniper overlook at 760, -520 |\\n| GP6 Quarry road | -420, 480 | Post |\\n| **Cement Works** | -760, 620 | Silos, quarry, radio mast: the finale |\\n\\n**Compounds are stamps:** ASCII room files in the engine's own level format (`engine/game/merc/stamps/*.toml`, checked with `pav room_check`), with walls, roofs, props, markers (`cover`, `spawn_rifle`, `barrel`, `cache`, `bed`…) and `[[object]]`s placed on terrain pads. Interiors exist for the bar, shop, clinic, safe houses, hotel lobby and works control room. Doorways are open, with no door logic. Turn the engine's cutaway off for this game.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer (DECIDED)\\n\\nTASK.md asks to follow the hub protocol \\\"for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own\\\". I'm covering both readings: full hub sessions, a clean solo game when there is no hub, and the same co-op round playable outside the hub.\\n\\n### 7.1 Mode and tags\\n**`shared-world`**, seats `1-4`. Your friends are your companions. Read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md` whole, and download `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `hub/`.\\n```html\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"10\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Burn the depot, take the ledger, get out together\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move · R2/LMB fire · L2/RMB aim · Square/R reload or clear jam\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\nPaste `session.js` **unmodified** as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`, by editing `engine/web/index.html`. The packer keeps it there.\\n\\n### 7.2 The round: \\\"Contract Run\\\"\\nIn a session the game opens straight into this, with no title or menus. It takes place on the Ombe Flats slice of the map, 8–10 minutes.\\n1. Mercs start on a truck at the track's end, at dusk, with wind set to favour a fire.\\n2. Destroy three fuel tanks by any means. Fire is the obvious way.\\n3. One player takes the ledger case from the office (carrying it slows you and prevents sprinting; it can be dropped and picked up).\\n4. All living mercs reach the river boat, about 500 m south across the grass, so the fire you lit chases you out, and leave.\\n\\nEnemies, fire, jams and all the other systems are live, with a fixed loadout and no shop, fever on a short mild timer, and no pause. Down players can be **dragged and patched** by friends (the companion mechanic), and otherwise respawn on the truck after 45 s, up to 6 team lives.\\n\\n**Scoring:** +100 per objective shared, +10 per kill, +25 per rescue, −25 for friendly fire. `AIHub.finish({standings, scores, won, stats, awards})` by the host. `won` is true on extraction. Stats: kills, rescues, jams, cells ignited. Awards: *Arsonist, Field Medic, Rust Bucket, Last Out.* On `time-up`, the host finishes at once (within `graceMs`).\\n\\n### 7.3 Protocol checklist\\n- JS shim `window.gameNet` (§12.5) wraps `AIHub`: call `AIHub.connect({mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true})` while the page parses. When it resolves `null`, run the normal game with the title screen.\\n- **Own card** (`card:true`): a live scene of the truck at dusk with the title, the players in their seat colours and ready state, how to win, this player's controls and the time left from the `card` event. Enter, ✕ or tap → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △, a named key or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Handle Enter in the JS shim (§2.3). No menus or choices, and nothing done on the card changes the round. Play begins only at `start`.\\n- `AIHub.ready()` once the sim is built, with no key press, before drawing the first frame.\\n- **World seed:** `info.seed` as the `Sim` seed on every copy. `Math.random` is not seeded in shared world and the Rust game doesn't use it.\\n- Countdown from `AIHub.time()` (negative for the first 3 s).\\n- `leave`: remove that merc. Host left: `end` arrives with `host-left`.\\n- `end`: no more input, nothing sent, sound off (master to 0, suspend).\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-127d8c02-62fb-4755-84bb-e2c59fa6a574-137","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1740→        let mut best_zone = 0u8;\\n        let mut best_i: Option<usize> = None;\\n        let mut blocked = false;\\n        for w in &self.walls {\\n            if let Some(t) = ray_aabb(origin, dir, w.min, w.max) {\\n                if t < best_t {\\n                    best_t = t;\\n                    blocked = true;\\n                    best_i = None;\\n                }\\n1750→            }\\n        }\\n        if !blocked {\\n            for (i, b) in self.bodies.iter().enumerate() {\\n                if !b.alive {\\n                    continue;\\n                }\\n                let zones = [(1.70, 0.18, 3u8), (1.15, 0.28, 1u8), (0.45, 0.20, 2u8)];\\n                for (y, r, zone) in zones {\\n                    if let Some(t) = ray_sphere(origin, dir, (b.x, y, b.z), r) {\\n1760→                        if t < best_t {\\n                            best_t = t;\\n                            best_zone = zone;\\n                            best_i = Some(i);\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let hit_x = origin.0 + dir.0 * best_t;\\n1770→        let hit_z = origin.2 + dir.2 * best_t;\\n        if let Some(i) = best_i {\\n            let mul = match best_zone {\\n                3 => 3.0,\\n                2 => 0.6,\\n                _ => 1.0,\\n            };\\n            let dmg = damage * mul;\\n            let kind = self.bodies[i].kind;\\n            let in_town = geom::in_town(self.bodies[i].x, self.bodies[i].z);\\n1780→            if self.ceasefire && in_town && kind == 2 {\\n                // Civilians are safe while the ceasefire holds.\\n            } else if id == WeaponId::Dart {\\n                self.bodies[i].poison = 3.0;\\n            } else {\\n                self.bodies[i].hp -= dmg;\\n                if ignites && matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ignite(8))) && kind == 1 {\\n                    self.mark(\\\"ignite_person\\\");\\n                }\\n                if self.bodies[i].hp <= 0.0 {\\n1790→                    self.bodies[i].alive = false;\\n                    if kind == 1 && self.stance == 1 && silent {\\n                        self.mark(\\\"stealth_kill\\\");\\n                    }\\n                    if kind == 5 && matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ignite(6))) {\\n                        let bx = self.bodies[i].x;\\n                        let bz = self.bodies[i].z;\\n                        let _ = self.fire.ignite_disk(bx, bz, 5.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\\n                        self.mark(\\\"ignite_barrel\\\");\\n                    }\\n1800→                    if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ceasefire)) {\\n                        self.ceasefire = false;\\n                        self.mark(\\\"ceasefire_ended\\\");\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let weapon_lights = ignites\\n            || matches!(id, WeaponId::Flare | WeaponId::Rpg | WeaponId::Flamer | WeaponId::Mortar | WeaponId::Molotov | WeaponId::Frag);\\n        if weapon_lights && self.fire.ignite_at(hit_x, hit_z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n1810→            self.note_weapon_ignite(id);\\n            if self.finale == Some(0) && matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ending(_))) {\\n                self.mark(\\\"ending_burn\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ignite(9))) && self.fire.ignite_at(hit_x, hit_z, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes) {\\n            self.mark(\\\"ignite_lightning\\\");\\n        }\\n        if matches!(self.current(), Some(Spec::Ignite(7))) && self.ride.kind != 0 {\\n            // The round starts at the eye. Score the closest point on that ray, not the far hit.\\n1820→            let rel_x = self.ride.x - origin.0;\\n            let rel_z = self.ride.z - origin.2;\\n            let along = rel_x * dir.0 + rel_z * dir.2;\\n            let t = along.clamp(0.0, best_t);\\n            let cx = origin.0 + dir.0 * t;\\n            let cz = origin.2 + dir.2 * t;\\n            if geom::dist(cx, cz, self.ride.x, self.ride.z) < 4.0 {\\n                self.hurt_vehicle(damage.max(40.0));\\n                if self.ride.stage >= 3 {\\n                    let _ = self.fire.ignite_disk(self.ride.x, self.ride.z, 5.0, self.tune.burn_time, self.minutes);\",\"content_concise\":\"1740→        let mut best_zone = 0u8;\\n        let mut best_i: Option<usize> = None;\\n        let mut blocked = false;\\n        for w in &self.walls {\\n            if let Some(t) = ray_aabb(origin, dir, w.min, w.max) {\\n                if t < best_t {\\n                  