      if self.fire.burned >= 500 {\\n                self.mark(\\\"cells_500\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn hour(&self) -> f32 {\\n        (self.minutes / 60.0) % 24.0\\n    }\\n\\n    pub fn tracker_rate(&self) -> f32 {\\n        let d = geom::dist(self.x, self.z, self.tracker_cache.0, self.tracker_cache.1).max(1.0);\\n        if d > 60.0 { 0.0 } else { 8.0 / d }\\n\",\"total_lines\":2806}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"f2a5fab6-b096-47bf-a5fa-d346e5154c3d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_634","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand the tank shooting chain.\n\nThe 7x7 barrel farm has 49 tanks. A single tank shot could trigger an explosion chain that burns over 500 cells. The challenge is to earn both flags by shooting the tanks as a player would.\n\nThe bot will shoot tanks directly instead of using script_ignite. When a tank dies from a shot, it should explode and ignite nearby neighbors to start the chain. The explosion_chain logic needs to detect when a second tank cooks off from the first explosion rather than from a direct hit.\n\nThe tank farm will use 7x7 barrels at 10m spacing with radius-6 burn disks. A new `cook_tank` method will trigger when a kind-5 barrel dies during the Tanks spec. This starts the explosion chain that spreads fire to adjacent tanks.\n\nThe `cook_tank` method ignites an 8.0 radius burn disk at the exploded tank's position. It then scans nearby alive kind-5 barrels within 14 meters and kills them instantly to trigger the chain. A \"explosion_chain\" flag is set once any neighboring tank is destroyed.\n\nA simple loop that kills only immediate neighbors would stop the chain at one ring. The revised `cook_tank` uses a queue to process each exploded tank in sequence, finding and destroying all alive kind-5 barrels within 16 meters of every blast site. This creates a true propagation chain rather than a single ring of destruction.\n\nThe queue loop marks \"explosion_chain\" whenever any neighboring tank is destroyed, then ignites a 12-meter burn disk at each victim's position and adds it to the queue. The \"cells_500\" flag is set once the total burned cells reach 500. I am now verifying whether a single shot can actually propagate through the entire 7x7 farm with 10-meter spacing and a 16-meter blast radius.\n\nThe 16-meter blast radius reaches adjacent and diagonal neighbors, so one shot can indeed chain through the entire 7x7 farm. The total burnable area covers roughly 1764 cells, which far exceeds the 500-cell threshold. Because the fire system counts only unique cells, overlapping blasts still increment the burned counter properly. I am now questioning whether destroying every tank from a single shot matches how a player would actually behave.\n\nThe bot must actually aim and shoot at a tank rather than just holding the primary button. The closest tank sits 20 meters south of the player, well within the 40-meter pistol range. Shots work while seated, so the bot does not need to exit the vehicle. A headshot deals 66 damage and a torso shot deals 22.\n\nThe bot aims at the torso zone, which is enough to kill a 20 HP tank in one shot. The pistol remains selected after the cigarette interaction, and its magazine was refilled during the prior task. I should add a reload check to the tank bot so it does not fire a dry shot if ammo runs low.\n\nThe bot will aim at the nearest alive tank and fire. The `blow_tanks` script function will be removed entirely.\n\nThe `blow_tanks` function will be deleted entirely rather than left unused, with its logic moved directly into the shot handler. Marking `cells_500` inside `cook_tank` is safe because the flag is idempotent and the fire tick path already checks the burned count. The `explosion_chain` flag should only trigger when a second tank dies from the blast itself, not from the direct shot that started it.\n\nThe 14-meter blast radius reaches orthogonal neighbors but misses diagonal ones. The chain still spreads because the grid is connected via orthogonal links. The 6-meter burn disks overlap on the 10-meter grid, so the total coverage spans about 72 meters and easily exceeds the 500-cell threshold.\n\nThe 72×72 meter burn area covers roughly 1,296 cells, comfortably above the 500-cell threshold. A radius-6 disk is chosen over radius-5 for safety. Processing 49 overlapping disks in one tick requires about 11,000 cell operations, which is acceptable. The tank bot can aim, fire, and chain through all 49 tanks in under a second, so it fits easily within the 30-second budget. I am now adding a 9 m/s east wind to the Drive spec.\n\nThe Drive spec will set the ride seat to 0 and spawn the bot nearby instead of on the feet. This matches the boat leg behavior, where the bot walks when far away and presses USE when close.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-add7b2b7-d088-4b1e-9e75-df73941ca6e5-139","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn campaign|fn blank|ride:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-add7b2b7-d088-4b1e-9e75-df73941ca6e5-140","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1188,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-add7b2b7-d088-4b1e-9e75-df73941ca6e5-141","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"better_way|Spec::Better|companion","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/shell.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4112,"output_tokens":2763,"cache_read_input_tokens":195200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5baec630-beb0-425d-a253-8c70f6fc509f"}
