{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_638","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to read STAGE.md and understand the requirements.\n\nI need to understand several mechanics before implementing:\n\n- How cells_500 is marked in simulate\n- How ignite_disk works and counts burned\n- How use_vehicle handles boarding and seat cycling\n- How companions get downed\n- Bot aim for tanks\n- Whether the pistol is selected when tanks start\n- How technical_driven is marked\n- The boat boarding pattern\n\nI will also review PLAN.md for tank, drive, and boarding sections.\n\nThe tank design is now clear. Remove the automatic `blow_tanks()` call from `script_ignite`. When a real shot kills a kind-5 tank while the current stage is `Spec::Tanks`, ignite that tank and chain-kill neighbors within 14–16 m. Mark `explosion_chain` only if a second tank dies from the blast. `cells_500` will come from the real burned count. The bot should aim at the nearest alive kind-5, fire, and reload if the pistol is dry. Arm the pistol at the start of the Tanks stage. Do not stamp any flags in `begin`.\n\nDrive mechanics are now clear. When replacing a non-technical driver, seat the new occupant in seat 0 and place the truck a few metres away instead of using seat 1 at the current position. The existing Drive bot already walks to within five metres and presses USE to board. Do not unseat a player who is already driving a kind-1 technical.\n\nThe Better stage needs cleanup. Remove every `mark(\"better_way\")` from Better, Patch, Overdose, and Die begins. Do not down the companion in Better begin. Instead, during `try_interact` while the current stage is `Spec::Better`, mark `better_way` and then down the nearby companion. `done(Better)` should only check for that flag.\n\nThe player arrives at Ombe by driving, so they are already seated in the technical when the Tanks stage begins.\n\nThe closest tank is 20 m away, well inside the 40 m pistol range. A single torso hit deals 22 damage, which kills a tank with 20 HP. The blast radius of roughly 15–16 m covers all eight neighbors in the 7×7 grid, so one shot can recursively cook the entire farm.\n\nThe old 6 m radius disks overlap heavily on the 10 m grid, so the 7×7 farm still covers well over 500 cells. Ombe is grass at (-520, -520) with fuel above zero, satisfying the condition. I also need to verify that simulate marks `cells_500` when `fire.burned` reaches 500.\n\nI need to verify that simulate auto-marks `cells_500` when burned reaches 500 around line 1460.\n\nThe `explosion_chain` flag must only be set when a neighbor dies from the blast, not from the original trigger shot. I will call `ignite_disk` on each exploded tank and carefully handle recursion to avoid double-processing.\n\nI need to verify the `ignite_disk` implementation. The 6 m radius should burn enough cells for the 500-cell threshold, but I will raise it slightly if overlap is too tight. The player standing on a burned cell is fine. After the ignites finish, the weapon may still be a flamer or molotov, so I must explicitly arm the pistol at the start of the Tanks stage.\n\nThe bot will aim at the nearest alive kind-5’s torso with pitch 1.15 and fire. One shot should chain the entire farm, so a single aimed shot is enough within the thirty-second budget.\n\nThe chain logic will live in an `explode_tank` helper. It ignites a disk at the dead tank’s position, kills neighbors within roughly fifteen meters, marks `explosion_chain` if any neighbor dies from the blast, and recurses on those neighbors. Care must be taken to avoid double-processing bodies while iterating inside `shots_tick`.\n\nKind-5 deaths during Ignite(6) must not trigger the tank chain. That step already ignites a disk and marks `ignite_barrel`, so it stays in its own branch.\n\nThe tank stage will use a separate branch: when a kind-5 dies while the current stage is `Spec::Tanks`, call `explode_tank(i)`.\n\n`explode_tank` will mark the dead tank as `alive=false` to prevent re-explosion, then recurse on neighbors that just died.\n\nI will check whether simulate auto-marks `cells_500` when burned reaches 500, since the rejection says both flags are earned by shooting. I also need to remove the now-unused `blow_tanks` function to avoid a compiler warning.\n\nI will replace the old `blow_tanks` function with `explode_tank`. For the Drive stage, I am placing a technical truck a few metres ahead of the player so they can board it with USE.\n\nThe Drive stage now resets the ride fuse and distance. The bot walks to within five metres before pressing USE to board. After the boat, the next Drive replaces it with a technical nearby and seats the occupant in seat 0. Once the bus drop-off is reached, the truck is left at that spot and no longer respawned.\n\nI need to check the script order to confirm whether the first Drive stage happens while the player is on foot or already seated. I also need to verify that spawning a technical truck eight metres ahead of the yaw will not land on water, since it is a land vehicle.\n\nThe Better stage will mark `better_way` during `try_interact` instead of in `begin`. Patch, Overdose, and Die stages will down the nearest alive companion and place them nearby. The companion is dropped at `self.x + 40.0` for Die, or `self.x + 1.5` for Patch and Overdose.\n\nThe bot presses INTERACT on the Better offer, which triggers try_interact to mark better_way. The stage is considered done when that flag is present. I need to verify that INTERACT registers as just-pressed so try_interact runs before done() checks it. I also need to check whether advance_script could process INTERACT and begin() in the same tick.\n\nThe tick order is unclear. If `advance_script` runs before input, the bot's INTERACT from the previous step could trigger `try_interact` during the same tick as `Better`'s `begin`. If input runs first, the bot presses INTERACT on the next tick after `Better` begins. Either way, a one-tick delay is acceptable.\n\nA same-frame edge case remains. If the bot's INTERACT for Better is processed after Rain's completion in the same tick, the flag would be set from the prior button press rather than from the Better stage itself. The rejection requires the flag to be set only after the player takes the offered approach, so a frame-delayed trigger could be rejected.\n\nThe green log currently shows rain and patch in the same second because better_way was stamped inside Better begin. After the fix, Better should appear as its own step. I need to read advance_script carefully to see if it chains steps together on the transition tick. If INTERACT completes the stage instantly, the step is still considered played since input was required.\n\nA single INTERACT tick might not satisfy a skeptic who wants the approach to feel played. I will add a brief spatial action so the Better stage does not complete instantly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d128e9a2-a31a-48b7-92b0-e99639c2affa-7","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"better.way|Better Way|explosion chain|cells_500|technical|USE|board","glob":"**/PLAN.md","head_limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d128e9a2-a31a-48b7-92b0-e99639c2affa-8","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn ignite_disk|burned|cells_500|fn use_vehicle|fn advance_script|technical_driven|fn arm\\(","glob":"**/merc/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11691,"output_tokens":3727,"cache_read_input_tokens":41728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"e24ece51-3eaa-420d-b89b-4ccdb7cc8442"}
