0,56,56,50,58,45,32,91,32,93,32,67,111,110,116,114,111,108,108,101,114,32,102,105,114,115,116,58,32,101,118,101,114,121,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,119,111,114,107,115,32,111,110,32,97,32,68,117,97,108,83,101,110,115,101,32,40,115,116,117,98,98,101,100,41,32,119,105,116,104,32,80,108,97,121,83,116,97,116,105,111,110,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,44,32,88,98,111,120,32,103,108,121,112,104,32,111,112,116,105,111,110,44,32,107,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,110,97,116,105,118,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,116,104,101,105,114,32,111,119,110,32,112,114,111,109,112,116,115,44,32,104,111,118,101,114,32,109,111,118,101,115,32,102,111,99,117,115,44,32,99,108,105,99,107,115,32,119,111,114,107,44,32,110,111,32,100,101,110,115,101,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":22,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"Controller first (DualSense, standard mapping). The keyboard and mouse use what PC FPS players expect. Prompts follow the last device used, and a Settings option swaps PlayStation glyphs for Xbox's A B X Y.\"},{\"line_number\":193,\"content\":\"| On foot | DualSense | Xbox prompt | Keyboard and mouse |\"},{\"line_number\":213,\"content\":\"| In a vehicle | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\"},{\"line_number\":224,\"content\":\"| Map up | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\"},{\"line_number\":231,\"content\":\"| Menus | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\"},{\"line_number\":357,\"content\":\"- Add a `Boat` kind that floats at the water height with an outboard (arcade, wake particles, stops at the shallows).\"},{\"line_number\":376,\"content\":\"- **\\\"A better way\\\":** before each main contract a living companion may offer an alternate approach (more money, more danger, and it can leave them trapped). There are three scripted variants, one per companion, each usable with any companion. Buddy trouble happens at most 3 times in a run.\"},{\"line_number\":390,\"content\":\"Six posts on the road network (§6.3), each a stamp with 4–7 soldiers, cover nodes, a barrel or two and sometimes a technical. They fire on sight outside the ceasefire. A cleared post gets a pencil X on the map and stays clear for 24 in-game hours (slider), and never re-mans while the player can see it.\"},{\"line_number\":550,\"content\":\"- **Invite code:** WebRTC star with host-created offer, joiner answer, copy and paste codes (keyboard required for this one step; say so on screen). Use one reliable and one unordered channel per peer. STUN allowed here, never in a session.\"},{\"line_number\":568,\"content\":\"- **One set of screens.** Keyboard and mouse use the same screens and layouts as the controller, with their own prompts and native behaviour, never a separate desktop layout.\"},{\"line_number\":576,\"content\":\"- Key caps and mouse-button icons for keyboard and mouse\"},{\"line_number\":604,\"content\":\"Touch-only means `(any-pointer: fine)` false, `(pointer: coarse)` true and no controller connected. No touch controls at all (never show the engine's touch UI in this scene). Show **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a **Settings** button (tappable) over the running attract mode. Plugging in a controller or pressing a key brings the normal title.\"},{\"line_number\":655,\"content\":\"- **Hand props:** pliers, knife, syrette, pill bottle, lighter, wrench, map board, GPS, monocular, tape recorder, cigarette, tracker.\"},{\"line_number\":656,\"content\":\"- **Vehicles:** technical, jeep, truck, river boat, plus wreck variants. Wheels drawn from `VehicleView`.\"},{\"line_number\":686,\"content\":\"- **SFX:** one patch set per weapon family (noise burst + low thump + tail by environment), dead click, jam clatter, bolt slap, reload parts, rag flutter on high wind, fire crackle and roar by nearby cells, explosions, engine loops by RPM and damage, tyres on dirt, boat outboard, wrench, syrette, pliers, finger snap, pills rattle, footsteps by surface, grass rustle, insects and birds by time of day, wind by speed, thunder, tracker beeps, menu ticks.\"},{\"line_number\":700,\"content\":\"| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\"},{\"line_number\":703,\"content\":\"| B4 | **A Better Way** (companion) | A companion's alternate plan on a convoy goes wrong: they go down in burning grass. Patch them or give the overdose | Companion down, mercy, permadeath, Infamy | 8 min |\"},{\"line_number\":835,\"content\":\"- **Controls:** keyboard, mouse hover and click, pad stub (§2.4). Prompts follow the device. Xbox setting changes glyphs. Synthetic mouse changes yaw under pointer lock. Lock lost opens pause.\"},{\"line_number\":837,\"content\":\"- **Touch-only:** Chromium with a phone profile (`has_touch`, `is_mobile`) shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a tappable Settings. No touch controls appear. Attract runs. Also check that WebKit (which has no WebGPU here) shows the page's clear message rather than a blank page.\"},{\"line_number\":859,\"content\":\"**Coverage flags (each set by real play; a test passes on the union across the three playthrough runs, since no single run can both save and lose the same companion or reach every ending):** map raised, waypoint set, GPS followed, monocular tag, wind rag visible at speed > 6, jam cleared, enemy jam seen, weapon broke, weapon bought, locker used, syrette, each wound treatment type, fever warned, pill taken, black-out (bot route), player rescued, companion patched, companion overdosed, companion died, better-way taken, fire lit by each igniter class, 500+ cells burned in one fire, enemy panicked, animals fled, explosion chain, rain extinguished, stealth kill, dart kill, night contract, sleep used, safe house claimed, post cleared, post re-manned, technical driven, mounted gun fired, repair done, boat driven, bus taken, tape played, cache found by tracker, diamonds spent, each contract, ceasefire ended, town burned, each ending.\"},{\"line_number\":882,\"content\":\"- [ ] Controller first: every screen works on a DualSense (stubbed) with PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyph option, keyboard and mouse native with their own prompts, hover moves focus, clicks work, no dense screens.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d128e9a2-a31a-48b7-92b0-e99639c2affa-8","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,55,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,95,95,120,98,100,55,100,57,49,47,119,111,114,107,47,74,97,109,32,67,114,121,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,53,48,51,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,99,114,97,116,101,115,47,112,97,118,95,99,111,114,101,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,115,47,109,101,114,99,47,119,111,114,108,100,46,11