01,100,95,101,110,111,117,103,104,40,41,32,123,10,50,48,57,52,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,102,32,115,101,108,102,46,104,111,108,100,95,116,32,60,32,51,46,48,32,124,124,32,115,101,108,102,46,115,121,114,101,116,116,101,115,32,61,61,32,48,32,123,10,50,49,48,49,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,115,101,108,102,46,115,121,114,101,116,116,101,115,32,45,61,32,49,59,10,50,49,48,56,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,115,101,108,102,46,99,111,109,112,97,110,105,111,110,115,91,105,93,46,100,111,119,110,95,116,32,61,32,48,46,48,59,10,50,52,49,50,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,115,101,108,102,46,115,121,114,101,116,116,101,115,32,61,32,115,101,108,102,46,115,121,114,101,116,116,101,115,46,109,97,120,40,52,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":23,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"    pub down_t: f32,\"},{\"line_number\":386,\"content\":\"    pub syrettes: u32,\"},{\"line_number\":462,\"content\":\"        w.syrettes = 3;\"},{\"line_number\":473,\"content\":\"        w.syrettes = 3;\"},{\"line_number\":499,\"content\":\"            syrettes: 3,\"},{\"line_number\":521,\"content\":\"                Companion { name: \\\"Tomek Wrona\\\".into(), alive: true, down: false, down_t: 0.0, rescue_spent: false, x: 0.0, z: 0.0 },\"},{\"line_number\":522,\"content\":\"                Companion { name: \\\"Rafael Quintero\\\".into(), alive: true, down: false, down_t: 0.0, rescue_spent: false, x: 0.0, z: 0.0 },\"},{\"line_number\":523,\"content\":\"                Companion { name: \\\"Mirela Dragan\\\".into(), alive: true, down: false, down_t: 0.0, rescue_spent: false, x: 0.0, z: 0.0 },\"},{\"line_number\":849,\"content\":\"                self.syrettes = self.syrettes.max(1);\"},{\"line_number\":961,\"content\":\"                    c.down_t = 0.0;\"},{\"line_number\":970,\"content\":\"                    c.down_t = 0.0;\"},{\"line_number\":976,\"content\":\"                        c.down_t = 0.0;\"},{\"line_number\":1069,\"content\":\"            Spec::Die => self.flags.contains(\\\"companion_died\\\"),\"},{\"line_number\":1635,\"content\":\"        if input.just(buttons::HEAL) && self.hp >= 20.0 && self.hp < 100.0 && self.syrettes > 0 && self.syrette_t <= 0.0 {\"},{\"line_number\":1636,\"content\":\"            self.syrettes -= 1;\"},{\"line_number\":2069,\"content\":\"                c.down_t += dt;\"},{\"line_number\":2072,\"content\":\"        if let Some(i) = self.companions.iter().position(|c| c.down && c.alive && c.down_t > 45.0) {\"},{\"line_number\":2075,\"content\":\"            self.mark(\\\"companion_died\\\");\"},{\"line_number\":2079,\"content\":\"                if self.hold_t > 3.0 && self.syrettes > 0 && !c.doomed_enough() {\"},{\"line_number\":2094,\"content\":\"        if self.hold_t < 3.0 || self.syrettes == 0 {\"},{\"line_number\":2101,\"content\":\"            self.syrettes -= 1;\"},{\"line_number\":2108,\"content\":\"                self.companions[i].down_t = 0.0;\"},{\"line_number\":2412,\"content\":\"                self.syrettes = self.syrettes.max(4);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"ae3be7aa-d230-4f4f-8cdd-6564c75b51de"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_642","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical order bug needs to be accounted for.\n\nThe tick function processes input before advancing the script. A step can therefore complete immediately during the same tick if its done() condition is met. In Tanks, the previous step finishes when the cigarette flag is set during simulation.\n\nThe fire button is not ignored. The bot fires during the Tanks step itself, so the next tick advances to Mounted. The only remaining concern is whether lingering primary input from a prior ignite could interfere, though the current sequence uses INTERACT and pistol shots.\n\nThe bot remains in seat 1 during Tanks, so it cannot immediately satisfy Mounted's done condition. It will use the seat change to reach seat 2 and fire. Drive completion requires arrival and technical_driven, keeping the bot seated.\n\nTank farm spawns are positioned correctly relative to the player. The nearest tank sits 20 meters south, well within pistol range. Aiming updates yaw and pitch before shots fire. The pistol will be armed at the start of Tanks so the condition is 100 and the magazine is full.\n\nA few missed shots are acceptable because the 30-second budget is ample. The ignite radius covers 49 tanks, and some cells may already be burned from earlier ignites at Ombe. The fuel at (-520, -520) and the farm extent need verification. During Drive, the truck spawns near seat 0; the bot walks to it and uses it.\n\nThe first drive spawns the technical 8 meters ahead of the pump house. The bot walks to it and boards. The ride distance is reset when spawning so the first 20 meters count toward this drive. After the bus, the kind is already 1, so no respawn occurs and the truck stays at the player's feet.\n\nThe first drive leg is handled correctly because the bot presses USE immediately once it is within five meters. After the bus, no extra boarding logic is needed. For the third drive after the boat, kind is 2 and the technical spawns near seat 0; the bot walks to it and boards. The boat step already sets the distance and technical_driven flags, so this final drive only requires reaching the cement works while seated.\n\nRepair resets the seat to 0 and spawns the truck at the player's feet when kind is 0. After the boat step, kind remains 2, so repair does not set it to 1; the Drive step later replaces the boat with a technical.\n\nIn Better, rain completes during simulation. If the bot does not mark the flag or down the companion, done() stays false and the step remains on Better. The next tick, the bot presses INTERACT during simulation to mark better_way and down the companion.\n\nPatch downs the companion at x+1.5 and holds INTERACT for three seconds.\n\nDie begins by moving the companion to x+40 and resetting the down timer. The 45-second death countdown starts fresh. The 55-second budget is sufficient.\n\nRisk triggers the same immediate down and position shift, so the death timer begins from zero.\n\nA step that begins and ends in the same tick might not appear in logs. If the goal is sampled at the end of the tick, the step could be skipped entirely. The logging behavior needs to be checked.\n\nThe test asserts the union of coverage flags rather than requiring every step name to appear in the log. The flag is set correctly during simulation before advance_script runs, so skipping the step from a same-tick end will not break coverage.\n\nThe log is only for debugging stalls. The source code confirms the flag is set during Better's INTERACT simulation, so the skeptic will see it regardless of logging behavior.\n\nPatch begin should not mark better_way again. If the companion is already down from the interact, Patch simply positions them.\n\nEdge cases are handled: try_interact fires because the bot sets the pressed bit, and if no companion is alive the flag still marks while the down action is skipped.\n\nPatch will fail to down a companion if none are alive, causing a stall. The three routes each target one companion, so the human route simply uses whichever companion is still alive. I should also light burning grass when a companion goes down to match the \"down in burning grass\" fiction.\n\nA small fire disk will be lit at the companion's position during Better to create the burning-grass consequence. This will not mark extra flags. The bot presses INTERACT during Better, and the companion starts at (0,0) until that action moves them.\n\nBetter will place the first alive companion four meters ahead in a standing, unmarked state. The bot must walk to them and press INTERACT to accept the offer. A ring of burning grass may be lit nearby.\n\nThe bot will walk to the companion if they are more than 2.5 meters away, then press INTERACT to accept the offer. During that interaction, it marks better_way, downs the companion, and lights a small fire disk at their feet. Walking four meters takes roughly one second, so the step should appear in logs. Patch distance checks are set below four meters, and the companion is positioned only 1.5 meters from the player once downed.\n\nThe companion is placed at player+1.5 meters so Patch can reach them. The bot is on foot after repair, not in a vehicle. Drive spawns will face the player. The first technical spawn resets distance to zero, forcing the full twenty-meter drive. After ignite_vehicle, the ride restores health and stage but remains occupied by the bot, so Tanks can fire while seated.\n\nThe bot can press USE in the same tick to cycle seats and trigger Mounted, because the seat check runs before the primary condition. The Animals step will keep holding secondary fire and fleeing while pistol shots are active, preserving the existing design. The pistol magazine is fully armed at the start of Tanks, so one shot should suffice.\n\nThe bot will reload during Tanks if the magazine empties. It targets the nearest alive kind-five tank at torso height 1.15. Yaw updates before movement, so the bot can aim while seated. Pitch is handled by simulate adding look.y to the current pitch. Spread jitter may cause misses, but ADS and secondary-fire hold reduce that risk.\n\nThe pistol spread is only ±0.0025, so the 0.014 angular radius of the torso target makes hits almost certain. A single hit deals 22 damage, which is enough to kill a tank with 20 health. The nearest-tank selector also keeps targets within the 40-meter range, so distant tanks cannot be hit by mistake.\n\nThe nearest tank is still the one at 20 meters, so distant east tanks cannot be hit by mistake. The chain radius of 15.5 covers all eight neighbors, meaning one kill triggers a chain across all forty-nine tanks. Igniting forty-nine small disks with radius eight checks roughly eighteen thousand cells total; the overlapping burn area spans about fourteen hundred unique cells.\n\nThe 500-cell burn threshold is cumulative, so prior fires already count toward it. The chain still needs to set the explosion_chain flag for the step to complete.\n\nThe burn radius will start at eight meters and increase if the chain fails to reach five hundred burned cells. The unused blow_tanks function will be removed, and script_ignite will no longer arm the pistol. Comments must avoid banned substrings such as jackal, ufll, apr, pala, mosate, bowa, leboa, oluwagembi, mike's bar, marty, and alencar, plus placeholders like todo, tbd, placeholder, and lorem. The word approach is safe because it does not contain apr as consecutive letters.\n\nThe mounted bot may press USE and PRIMARY in the same frame, which cycles to seat two and triggers mounted while also firing the personal weapon. The Tanks bot must not press USE; it should only aim and fire. Reload is handled when the magazine empties or the weapon jams, though a single shot is usually enough because arm() refills the magazine and clears jam. The fire condition requires both yaw error and pitch error to stay below 0.2, and look.x is clamped to 1.5 per tick.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef75bb01-37fb-4fc7-b842-7cbd96a489f5-23","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"blow_tanks|better_way|seat = 1|Spec::Tanks|explosion_chain|technical_driven","glob":"**/tests/merc.rs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef75bb01-37fb-4fc7-b842-7cbd96a489f5-24","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"deny\\(|dead_code|unused","glob":"**/pav_core/**/*.rs","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef75bb01-37fb-4fc7-b842-7cbd96a489f5-25","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/geom.rs","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9340,"output_tokens":4218,"cache_read_input_tokens":68096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"45ad204e-7382-4fce-966b-36c0f524360f"}
