WebGPU.\\n- [ ] First-person game, on the Pavilion engine, native style extended with new assets and animations.\\n- [ ] All systems in §5 present. All contracts in §11 playable. Three endings. No TODOs, placeholders or stubs anywhere, including in text.\\n- [ ] Demo long enough to show everything: playthrough asserts all coverage flags.\\n- [ ] Music defaults to 10%. All sound, music and gibberish voices are generated in code.\\n- [ ] Dev mode reachable from pause: tools, live sliders, reset to defaults.\\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s of idle on title and menus, loops, any input exits.\\n- [ ] Controller first: every screen works on a DualSense (stubbed) with PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyph option, keyboard and mouse native with their own prompts, hover moves focus, clicks work, no dense screens.\\n- [ ] Touch-only: no touch controls, the required message, a Settings button, attract running.\\n- [ ] Hub: session client unmodified and first, all four harness cases pass, the on-its-own check passes, standalone multiplayer works over two pages.\\n- [ ] `tests/run.sh all` prints 0 failures and a one-line count.\\n- [ ] Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback are in About/Credits and your chat reply. Exit interview saved and parses.\\n- [ ] Your background processes are stopped, by PID. No stray files outside your folder.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":907}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"48d520cf-e9fc-4a5c-ac09-40acf080cd31"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_655","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The playthrough passed. I will now read STAGE.md and proceed with the remaining tasks.\n\nI will run the full merc suite and grouped tests. Then I will rebuild WASM and pack. I need to read run.sh to match the verifier's expected logs. Previous session captured sim-combat, sim-world, playthrough, ui-audio, browser, hub, launch screenshots, and run-all logs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ee59043b-5ccd-4593-ad54-62dd419e6fd5-57","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/run.sh","limit":200}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8394,"output_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":112256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"61dc2d6a-db9b-46cc-8103-92108ee68f1b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ee59043b-5ccd-4593-ad54-62dd419e6fd5-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# One test command. Prints failing lines only, then PASS n FAIL f.\\nset -u\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nLOGS=\\\"$DEV/test-logs\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$LOGS\\\"\\nmode=\\\"${1:-all}\\\"\\npass=0\\n10→fail=0\\n\\nshow_fail() {\\n  grep -E 'FAILED|^error(\\\\[|:)|panicked at|^FAIL:' \\\"$1\\\" || true\\n}\\n\\ntake_py() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  local c f\\n20→  c=\\\"$(grep -E '^CHECKS ' \\\"$log\\\" | tail -1 | awk '{print $2}')\\\"\\n  f=\\\"$(grep -c '^FAIL:' \\\"$log\\\" || true)\\\"\\n  [[ -n \\\"$c\\\" ]] || c=0\\n  pass=$((pass + c - f))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n  if [[ \\\"$c\\\" == 0 && \\\"$f\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $log produced no checks\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n  fi\\n}\\n30→\\ntake_cargo() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  if ! grep -q '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\"; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect did not finish\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    return\\n  fi\\n  # Sum every cargo result. Doc-tests often add a 0-passed line after the real suite.\\n40→  local p=0 f=0 line np nf\\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\\n    np=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) passed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    nf=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) failed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    p=$((p + ${np:-0}))\\n    f=$((f + ${nf:-0}))\\n  done < <(grep '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\")\\n  if [[ \\\"$p\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect ran 0 tests\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n50→  fi\\n  pass=$((pass + p))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n}\\n\\ncargo_tests() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  shift 2\\n  (\\n    cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n60→    CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$ENGINE/target\\\" \\\\\\n      cargo test --offline --color never \\\"$@\\\"\\n  ) >\\\"$log\\\" 2>&1 || true\\n  take_cargo \\\"$log\\\" \\\"$expect\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_sim() {\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-combat.log\\\" \\\"sim-combat\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    look_and_stick_follow_yaw hits_use_zones_and_walls_block \\\\\\n    jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear \\\\\\n70→    a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops fever_pills_blackout_and_healing\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-world.log\\\" \\\"sim-world\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks exposure_smoke_and_noise \\\\\\n    squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking \\\\\\n    vehicles_climb_break_and_float\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/playthrough.log\\\" \\\"playthrough\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    bot_plays_all_three_endings\\n}\\n\\nrun_ui() {\\n80→  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/ui-shell.log\\\" \\\"ui-shell\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    shop_tracker_and_shell fiction_has_no_source_names_and_no_audio_files\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/ui-audio-bus.log\\\" \\\"audio-bus\\\" -p pav_audio -- \\\\\\n    music_bus_tracks_the_gain gun_families_voices_and_crackle_differ explosion_is_loud_then_silent\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/ui-view.log\\\" \\\"first-person\\\" -p pav_view -- first_person_yaw_zero_faces_north\\n  local audio=\\\"$LOGS/audio-files.log\\\"\\n  find \\\"$DEV\\\" -type f \\\\( -name '*.wav' -o -name '*.mp3' -o -name '*.ogg' \\\\) ! -path '*/target/*' >\\\"$audio\\\" || true\\n  if [[ -s \\\"$audio\\\" ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: audio files present\\\"\\n    cat \\\"$audio\\\"\\n90→    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n  else\\n    pass=$((pass + 1))\\n  fi\\n  # One combined log for the ui/audio group.\\n  cat \\\"$LOGS/ui-shell.log\\\" \\\"$LOGS/ui-audio-bus.log\\\" \\\"$LOGS/ui-view.log\\\" >\\\"$LOGS/ui-audio.log\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_py() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\"\\n100→  shift\\n  python3 \\\"$@\\\" >\\\"$log\\\" 2>&1 || true\\n  take_py \\\"$log\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_browser() {\\n  run_py \\\"$LOGS/launch-a.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/browser.py\\\" launch1\\n  run_py \\\"$LOGS/launch-b.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/browser.py\\\" launch2\\n  run_py \\\"$LOGS/hooks.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/browser.py\\\" hooks\\n  run_py \\\"$LOGS/webkit.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/browser.py\\\" webkit\\n110→  run_py \\\"$LOGS/net.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/browser.py\\\" net\\n  cat \\\"$LOGS/launch-a.log\\\" \\\"$LOGS/launch-b.log\\\" \\\"$LOGS/hooks.log\\\" \\\"$LOGS/webkit.log\\\" \\\"$LOGS/net.log\\\" >\\\"$LOGS/browser.log\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_hub() {\\n  run_py \\\"$LOGS/hub.log\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests/hub.py\\\"\\n}\\n\\ncase \\\"$mode\\\" in\\n  sim) run_sim ;;\\n120→  ui|audio) run_ui ;;\\n  browser) run_browser ;;\\n  hub) run_hub ;;\\n  all)\\n    run_sim\\n    run_ui\\n    run_browser\\n    run_hub\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n130→    echo \\\"FAIL: unknown mode $mode\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    ;;\\nesac\\n\\n# Pass count cannot go negative if a script's CHECKS was smaller than FAIL lines.\\nif [[ \\\"$pass\\\" -lt 0 ]]; then pass=0; fi\\necho \\\"PASS $pass FAIL $fail\\\"\\n[[ \\\"$fail\\\" == 0 ]]\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# One test command. Prints failing lines only, then PASS n FAIL f.\\nset -u\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nLOGS=\\\"$DEV/test-logs\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$LOGS\\\"\\nmode=\\\"${1:-all}\\\"\\npass=0\\n10→fail=0\\n\\nshow_fail() {\\n  grep -E 'FAILED|^error(\\\\[|:)|panicked at|^FAIL:' \\\"$1\\\" || true\\n}\\n\\ntake_py() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  local c f\\n20→  c=\\\"$(grep -E '^CHECKS ' \\\"$log\\\" | tail -1 | awk '{print $2}')\\\"\\n  f=\\\"$(grep -c '^FAIL:' \\\"$log\\\" || true)\\\"\\n  [[ -n \\\"$c\\\" ]] || c=0\\n  pass=$((pass + c - f))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n  if [[ \