{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_681","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The http.server processes visible in the system are from other agent folders, not from this run.\n\nPASS 48 is confirmed. The goal plan checklist is complete. PROGRESS.md needs updating to reflect honest behaviors. One deviation remains. The verify task stays in progress until the reply is finished.\n\nThe verify task is now marked complete. PROGRESS.md will be updated with a precise sentence about the three fixes, without inflating issue counts.\n\nThe merc test suite covers hits, jams, fever, wind-driven fire, vehicles, companions, the contract list, and three endings. The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives to set every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice. Dev teleport, spawn, world, and noclip change the world. The bot sentence will be updated to include boarding, shooting the tanks, and taking the offer.\n\nhandin.py is safely in scratch and does not persist references to it. The exit-interview will remain unchanged.\n\nThe final reply must include Source Information and the three feedback sections in question order, copied from their files.\n\nSource Information fields are being pulled from TASK.md: Date 2026-11-05 01:35:03, Source Far Cry 2, Plan PLAN.md, Genre and Perspective Shooter / first person, Tech Rust 1.98 / shardfall, and Environment Grok CLI (headless) on Linux.\n\nModel xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh, and usage added on import are being pulled from TASK.md.\n\nEngine Feedback has six answers and Prompt Feedback has four. The reply will state points directly and avoid contrastive negation, but the stored answers will be repeated verbatim.\n\nThe monitor process already printed DONE and exited.\n\nThe goal plan file will remain untouched because no new deviation exists. The work root contains exactly one HTML file. I am now writing the PROGRESS update and marking the verify task complete.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d95bfd55-9197-4777-977b-f286d60887ba-94","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PROGRESS.md","old_string":"The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives, and the union of those runs sets every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice.","new_string":"The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives. It boards the technical with the use key, lights the tank farm with a shot, and takes the companion's offer on the ground. The union of those runs sets every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d95bfd55-9197-4777-977b-f286d60887ba-95","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"verify","content":"Re-run playthrough, wasm pack, and verification checks","status":"completed"}],"merge":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2440,"output_tokens":1109,"cache_read_input_tokens":154880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5b18e672-74fb-4bc2-8601-6fe60a43e269"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d95bfd55-9197-4777-977b-f286d60887ba-94","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives, and the union of those runs sets every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice.\",\"new_string\":\"The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives. It boards the technical with the use key, lights the tank farm with a shot, and takes the companion's offer on the ground. The union of those runs sets every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives, and the union of those runs sets every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice.\",\"old_line\":6,\"new_string\":\"The seeded bot walks, shoots, and drives. It boards the technical with the use key, lights the tank farm with a shot, and takes the companion's offer on the ground. The union of those runs sets every coverage flag. The ledger is the burn, read, or chair choice.\",\"new_line\":6,\"context_before\":\"Original first-person contract shooter on the shardfall engine. The playable page is `Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` in this folder. The dev folder of the same name holds the engine, the hub client, and `tests/run.sh`.\\n\\n- Title chosen from 50 riffs plus a real RNG. Notes are in the dev folder `notes/title.md`. Feedback notes are in `notes/feedback.md`.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"- Menus are a 10-foot shell on the page. Music and voices are synthesized. The hub depot round uses the unmodified session client as the first script.\\n- `tests/run.sh all` runs the sim, audio, browser, and hub checks and prints one failure count. The finished run printed `PASS 48 FAIL 0`.\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"- The `merc` scene is a headless country sim. While a contract is playing, the rendered eye follows the body and the stance, and the rifle, rag, map, GPS, and glass are props in that view. Look, hits, jams, fever, wind-driven fire, vehicles, companions, the contract list, and three endings are covered by `cargo test -p pav_core --test merc` (19 tests). \"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d95bfd55-9197-4777-977b-f286d60887ba-95","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] tanks: Earn explosion_chain and cells_500 by shooting the tanks\\n- [completed] drive: Spawn the technical nearby and board it with USE\\n- [completed] better: Set better_way only after the player takes the approach\\n- [completed] verify: Re-run playthrough, wasm pack, and verification checks\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Earn explosion_chain and cells_500 by shooting the tanks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Spawn the technical nearby and board it with USE\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Set better_way only after the player takes the approach\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Re-run playthrough, wasm pack, and verification checks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"tanks\":{\"content\":\"Earn explosion_chain and cells_500 by shooting the tanks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"drive\":{\"content\":\"Spawn the technical nearby and board it with USE\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"better\":{\"content\":\"Set better_way only after the player takes the approach\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"Re-run playthrough, wasm pack, and verification checks\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"c128ef85-3841-463b-823d-ac2f70d907a4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_682","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"At least one task must remain in progress until the goal is complete.\n\nAll tasks are complete. I will now draft the final reply with changes, test evidence, and source information. The three fixes are: shot kills a tank and blast chains neighbors, disks burn grass, explosion_chain only fires when a second tank dies, cells_500 uses the real burned count, and blow_tanks is removed.\n\nDrive now spawns 8 meters ahead, seat 0, with the bot walking and pressing USE. Better now has the companion stand ahead; the player walks and interacts, sets a flag, and done() only checks that flag. Patch, overdose, and die no longer stamp it.\n\nEvidence: merc 19 passed, playthrough 6 routes finished, human seed log shows sleep → drive → mounted after ignite11 → rain → better → patch with position change, die took ~45s, patch ~3s, wasm packed 11552939 bytes, tests/run.sh all PASS 48 FAIL 0, launches show title Jam Cry, four rows, overlook painted, CHECKS 4 each, hooks 11, webkit 2, net 4, hub 5, handin OK.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The three campaign cheats are gone, and the packed page matches that sim. A shot cooks the tank farm, the technical is boarded with the use key, and the companion's offer is taken on the ground. `tests/run.sh all` printed `PASS 48 FAIL 0`.\n\nThe tank step no longer deletes the farm. A pistol shot that kills one tank sets off the neighbours, the grass disks come from those blasts, and `explosion_chain` is set only when a second tank dies. `cells_500` still comes from the real burned-cell count. The first technical is parked 8 m ahead with an empty seat, and the bot walks up and presses the same use key the boat step uses. `better_way` is set only after the player walks to the companion and interacts. Patch, overdose, and the death timer no longer stamp it in advance.\n\nNative proof: `cargo test -p pav_core --test merc` passed 19 tests. The seeded bot reached burn, read, and chair on seeds 1 and 2, and the coverage union was complete. The human log shows the drive from the pump house to Ombe, the tank step after the cigarette, and a better-way step that moves the player before the patch. The packed page is `Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503.html` (11,552,939 bytes). Both file:// launches showed the Jam Cry title, the tagline, and the four menu rows over the dusk overlook. Browser checks were 4, 4, 11, 2, and 4. The hub harness passed all four cases.\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-05 01:35:03\n- Source: Far Cry 2\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: Shooter, first person\n- Tech: Rust 1.98, shardfall (pav_core, pav_view, pav_app, pav_audio), wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, WebGPU, one HTML page.\n- Art Direction: Sun-bleached dusk, laterite gold, dry grass, and a low sun. The overlook is flat boxes dressed in code.\n- Animation: Simulation-driven poses. The rifle and the wind rag are boxes. No skeletal clip.\n- Audio: Code-only tones. The music bus defaults to 0.10. Voices are gibberish syllables, not recorded speech. No wav, mp3, or ogg.\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1 to 4 players, plus BroadcastChannel and pasted WebRTC codes when no hub is active.\n- Testing: Native cargo tests, a seeded bot through three endings, Playwright Chromium with software WebGPU, WebKit with no WebGPU, and the hub harness.\n- Research: The engine START_HERE and MAKE_A_GAME notes, and the plan's system notes. No separate play of the source.\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch? Testing caught 26 issues. The first build reported 14 compile errors. After it compiled, the shipped tests failed 12 more times: a missing trait import, fever not latching, an attract step the clock clamps, fire crossing the road, a vehicle stage off by one, blackout health regenerating, an ignite on a cell already alight, soldiers leaving the flame, rain on the river, a gun that broke before it jammed, a long rest that skipped the post, and the last contract flag.\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 6 of those were game-breaking. The ignite step stalled, the panic step stalled, rain could not light a river cell, one seed broke the gun before the jam, the long rest never remanned the post, and the ending skipped the last contract flag.\n- What was the most helpful test you ran? The most helpful test was bot_plays_all_three_endings. It named the route, the seed, the stuck goal, the position, and the missing flags.\n- What was the least helpful test you ran? The least helpful test was the first attract check, which stepped a full second while the world clock clamps a tick to half a second, so it measured the clamp. A passing audio filter that never enters the contract was the other weak check. After the green run, 0 failures remained.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine? The headless sim, the Game trait, the seeded rng, and the single-file packer were the parts that earned their keep.\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong? The rig had no first-person camera. Hook games still drew the pavilion HUD. The wrong WebGPU flag leaves a blank canvas. Fire will not light a cell that is already burning. The world clock clamps a tick. A rest flag stuck. An ending marked finished before the last flag.\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The contract sim had to be built here: weapons, fire, fever, the shell, and the page.\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine? The hardest part was a first-person view and a two-kilometre country inside a small room, and a bot that trips every coverage flag.\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? InputFrame gained look, axes, and act, plus the buttons from reload through confirm. CameraRig gained a first-person pose. The pavilion HUD is skipped for this scene, so the page can own the menus.\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? One change worth having: a first-person camera and a game-owned UI that does not assume the pavilion.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt? The checks name the behaviour, the seeds, and the file the proof goes in.\n- What was confusing? The country lives in a simulation inside a room scene, and the WebGPU flag that actually paints is easy to miss.\n- What was the hardest thing to do? The hardest task was one seeded bot reaching three endings and every coverage flag, then a page that still paints a frame.\n- What would you change in this prompt? Name the WebGPU flags beside the screenshot check, and say the visual room is only a window onto the country."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1249,"output_tokens":1888,"cache_read_input_tokens":157312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"7237623b-cf03-45cd-8e2a-ef95ae0c29fb"}
