atrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/merc.rs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":442,\"content\":\"    w.ride.seat = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":470,\"content\":\"    w.ride.seat = 0;\"},{\"line_number\":481,\"content\":\"    dry.ride.seat = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":495,\"content\":\"    wet.ride.seat = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":510,\"content\":\"    let seat = wet.ride.seat;\"},{\"line_number\":512,\"content\":\"    assert_ne!(wet.ride.seat, seat);\"},{\"line_number\":513,\"content\":\"    wet.ride.seat = 2;\"},{\"line_number\":846,\"content\":\"    w.ride.seat = 1;\"},{\"line_number\":865,\"content\":\"    \\\"companion_died\\\", \\\"better_way\\\", \\\"ignite_flare\\\", \\\"ignite_rocket\\\", \\\"ignite_flamer\\\", \\\"ignite_mortar\\\", \\\"ignite_molotov\\\",\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"45e3a444-ee07-4c96-b826-43eefd806395"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_693","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tanks step completes in the same second.\n\nThe gap requires earning both flags by shooting tanks as a player would. chain_tanks still uses BFS to kill all neighbors within 16m of one tank death, igniting disks and marking explosion_chain if any second tank dies. cells_500 comes from burned cells. This may still be the same cheat with an extra pistol shot as a trigger.\n\nThe playthrough test only checks flags and completion. It does not verify that a shot fired before the flags appeared. If script_ignite still calls blow_tanks without a preceding shot, the tests would pass anyway. This is a missing honest test of a shipped behavior change.\n\nscript_ignite no longer calls blow_tanks. The chain now happens in shots_tick when a tank dies. The bot completes the step, so the shot path works. If it failed, the test would hang on the tanks budget.\n\nAll 19 tests finished in under two seconds, including six full playthroughs. The shot path is confirmed working and fast.\n\nThe plan explicitly requires destroying three fuel tanks by fire and producing an explosion chain that burns 500+ cells. A single shot that ignites neighboring tanks satisfies this contract. The instant BFS covering the entire farm is slightly generous but still fulfills the required explosion chain.\n\nThe drive duration of 76 seconds matches full-speed travel across roughly 1193 meters. This suggests the bot entered the vehicle immediately and drove the entire way. The code shows seat=0 with the vehicle just 8 meters ahead, so the timing is consistent with boarding quickly rather than starting unseated.\n\nThe drive test cannot prove the bot boarded the vehicle. A seat preset to 1 would still yield the same 75-second duration, and no earlier specification sets ride.kind to 1. The code change is visible: ride.kind starts at 0, so the first drive parks the vehicle and leaves seat at 0 before the bot presses USE. This appears genuine, though an earlier ignite might have altered the state.\n\nThe bus script sets seat to 0 without changing ride.kind. The second drive therefore skips the park block and does not require reboarding.\n\nAfter the bus, the vehicle is already at the player's feet with seat 0. The next drive specification skips the park block because ride.kind remains 1. The bot presses USE immediately since it is within 5 meters of the vehicle. This confirms boarding a vehicle that was already present rather than walking up to it.\n\nThe gap required the first drive to park the vehicle eight meters ahead and board it with USE. The second drive correctly uses USE on a vehicle already at the player's feet after the bus drops them, which is reasonable state rather than the original bug where seat was preset to one. The third drive after town has the bot walk because the town bot dismounts if seated.\n\nThe drive gap is fixed. The town step leaves the bot unseated and the vehicle at a distance, so the next drive correctly walks to it and boards with USE.\n\nThe companion step advances roughly two meters in one second. The bot walks about 1.8 meters to a companion four meters ahead, then interacts. No hold input is required.\n\nThe companion flag is only set on interaction within 3.2 meters. The bot walked two meters to reach the companion, which is consistent with the step. The movement occurred during the better step, not the rain step. The companion offer is spawned at the start of the step, but the flag is only stamped when the bot interacts.\n\nPatch, Overdose, and Die no longer mark better_way. The companion flag is only set after the player accepts the offered approach.\n\nI am scanning for new regressions and unmet gating criteria. I will check the patch diff, verify run.sh passes, confirm the packed HTML is fresh, and ensure prior camera, ledger, and dev fixes were not reverted.\n\nThe chain_tanks queue is O(n) but acceptable. Even if the origin tank dies, neighbors still ignite and burn within 16 meters. The 500-cell threshold depends on roughly 49 tanks being ignited, yet fuel is zero on road, water, and rock. The depot at (-520, -520) must be grass for those cells to count.\n\nThe 500-cell burn threshold is plausible because most cells carry fuel, so a single frame can jump by hundreds. The test passed, so the flag was set. It may have been set earlier by other ignite steps or panic, but the tanks step still requires explosion_chain. A potential bug was spotted: pistol damage is 22 while tank health is only 20.\n\nThe pistol damage is not a bug in practice. The ray still hits the tank despite the zone limb being smaller than the damage, because torso aim and spread jitter compensate.\n\nA drive bug was spotted: if the player is in a boat (kind 2), the drive code replaces it with a technical ride. The Boat step sets kind to 2, and the last Drive occurs after Town. I am checking whether anything resets kind back to 1 before that final drive.\n\nRepair does not reset kind from 2 to 1. It only sets seat=0 and health 35. The Drive step therefore replaces the boat with a technical ride eight meters ahead and leaves seat at zero. This confirms the final drive correctly spawns and boards a vehicle nearby.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed01a879-60c3-45b3-8298-4f235c824357-29","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fn just|fn down|struct InputFrame","glob":"**/*.rs","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed01a879-60c3-45b3-8298-4f235c824357-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/merc/world.rs","offset":1405,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed01a879-60c3-45b3-8298-4f235c824357-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"PASS|FAIL|CHECKS","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/tmp/grok-goal-8215da6fd761/implementer/run-all.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed01a879-60c3-45b3-8298-4f235c824357-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"blow_tanks|seat = 1|mark\\(\\\"better_way\\\"\\)|mark\\(\\\"explosion_chain\\\"\\)|mark\\(\\\"cells_500\\\"\\)","glob":"**/merc/**/*.rs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3685,"output_tokens":2680,"cache_read_input_tokens":86400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"940154e6-5247-454a-b163-01e5181877c2"}
