111,103,96,46,10,50,54,58,57,46,32,42,42,103,97,116,105,110,103,58,42,42,32,82,117,110,32,116,104,101,32,111,110,101,32,102,117,108,108,32,116,101,115,116,32,99,111,109,109,97,110,100,32,40,101,120,112,101,99,116,101,100,32,112,97,116,104,32,96,123,100,101,118,125,47,116,101,115,116,115,47,114,117,110,46,115,104,32,97,108,108,96,41,32,97,102,116,101,114,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,100,101,32,105,116,32,99,111,118,101,114,115,32,105,115,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,101,100,46,32,67,97,112,116,117,114,101,32,116,111,32,96,123,83,67,82,65,84,67,72,125,47,114,117,110,45,97,108,108,46,108,111,103,96,46,32,80,97,115,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,105,102,32,105,116,32,112,114,105,110,116,115,32,102,97,105,108,117,114,101,115,32,40,110,111,110,101,41,32,97,110,100,32,111,110,101,32,115,117,109,109,97,114,121,32,108,105,110,101,32,119,104,111,115,101,32,102,97,105,108,117,114,101,32,99,111,117,110,116,32,105,115,32,48,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":11,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91%2Fwork/01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"1. **gating:** Confirm the HTML path, dev subfolder, `PROGRESS.md`, and title notes. Parse `exit-interview.json` and assert TASK.md's keys, array lengths (testing 4, engine 6, prompt 4), and `usage == \\\"added on import\\\"`. Search shipped game strings for the forbidden proper names and for TODO, TBD, placeholder, and lorem. Capture the command output to `{SCRATCH}/handin.log`. Pass only if the files exist, JSON parses, and the searches are clean outside the allowed source lines.\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"2. **gating:** Run the shipped native simulation tests (the game's own test binary, starting each case from a fresh boot) for look and movement, hitscan zones and wall blocking, jam rate, jam clear, weapon break, enemy jam, syrette and wound types, fever warning, pill clear, and no-pill blackout with a diamond fee. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/sim-combat.log`. Pass only if those assertions pass and the log shows zero failures for this group.\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"3. **gating:** Run the shipped native tests for fire (8 m/s downwind ≥ 3× upwind at 60 s, breaks, regrowth, rain, chain ignition, sparse snapshot), vehicles (slope, boat shallows, repair, explode-and-ignite, NPC driver), detection (grass, night, posture, smoke, noise), and guard-post re-man rules including \\\"not while visible\\\" and town holster. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/sim-world.log`. Pass only if each of those outcomes is asserted by the run, not by a re-implementation.\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"4. **gating:** Run the shipped bot from a new game through each of the three endings on normal difficulty, then assert the PLAN.md §15 coverage-flag union, companion rescue, patch, overdose, permadeath across save and load, and a file-backed save round trip of the §5.21 fields. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/playthrough.log`. Pass only if the log shows all three endings reached and zero failures. This run must be deterministic enough that a second run of the same seeds also passes.\"},{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"5. **gating:** Run the shipped UI and offline-audio tests: focus wrap and a max of 7 rows, glyphs follow device and the Xbox setting, attract starts at 10 s of idle and not before, any input exits, dev sliders change tunables and reset restores defaults, music RMS ratio 0.10 ± 0.01, voice output non-silent and different per speaker, no NaNs. Also search the dev tree for wav, mp3, and ogg files belonging to the game. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/ui-audio.log`. Pass only if those checks pass and no game audio files are found.\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"6. **gating:** Launch the real HTML from `file://` with Playwright Chromium more than once (two separate runs), using the engine WebGPU flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader` (do not use `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`). Each run: zero page errors; the canvas drawing size equals the viewport requested for that run; the frame is substantially filled (painted fraction high or a painted bbox covering most of the surface, not a clear buffer); the visible title or the published UI state equals `{GameTitle}`; keyboard input (the Enter, Space, Enter, Space solo path) changes that state. Save screenshots and console logs to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must succeed. A readback that returns a blank image is a failure to fix. If Playwright cannot start at all, save that error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-fail.log` and treat criteria 2–5's native tests plus a static check that [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"7. **gating:** On that same page, drive the shipped browser hooks: gamepad stub flips prompts to PlayStation glyphs, the Xbox setting changes them, pointer-lock mousemove changes yaw, losing the lock opens pause, a phone profile shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and Settings with attract running and no touch controls, WebKit (no WebGPU) shows a clear message instead of a blank page, dev mode toggles a cheat and a slider visible in published status, save then Continue works from `file://`, published music gain is 0.10, and About text contains the Source Information fields and all three feedback sections. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"8. **gating:** Serve the real page with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the fetched `<title>` is this game, run PLAN.md §14.4's four harness URLs, and stop only that server PID. Pass only if `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true for each case. Then play the standalone round on two pages through BroadcastChannel and through a pasted WebRTC code to the results screen, and assert the solo page does not mark the hub client active and does not use `Math.random` for shared-world state. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"9. **gating:** Run the one full test command (expected path `{dev}/tests/run.sh all`) after the code it covers is finished. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/run-all.log`. Pass only if it prints failures (none) and one summary line whose failure count is 0.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"5085f438-2652-4eb8-aca8-daacdb1f08b6"}
