110,116,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,99,111,110,116,114,97,99,116,44,32,99,101,97,115,101,102,105,114,101,32,101,110,100,101,100,44,32,116,111,119,110,32,98,117,114,110,101,100,44,32,101,97,99,104,32,101,110,100,105,110,103,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":12,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":269,\"content\":\"| flamer | special | Flamethrower | 100/300 fuel | stream | 30/s | 14 | 0.05/s | 40 | **ignites**, wearer's tank can burst if shot |\"},{\"line_number\":319,\"content\":\"**Igniters:** molotov, flare, flamethrower, rockets, mortar, some grenades, tracer on dry grass (small chance), exploding barrels and fuel tanks, burning vehicles, burning people, cigarette from a mission script, lightning in storms.\"},{\"line_number\":325,\"content\":\"- Fuel drums and tanks explode.\"},{\"line_number\":380,\"content\":\"Roles: **Rifleman, Machine-gunner, Sniper** (glint, ridge positions), **Rocket man** (targets vehicles), **Flame trooper** (his tank explodes).\"},{\"line_number\":390,\"content\":\"Six posts on the road network (§6.3), each a stamp with 4–7 soldiers, cover nodes, a barrel or two and sometimes a technical. They fire on sight outside the ceasefire. A cleared post gets a pencil X on the map and stays clear for 24 in-game hours (slider), and never re-mans while the player can see it.\"},{\"line_number\":482,\"content\":\"| **Ombe Flats depot** | -520, -520 | Fuel tanks in a sea of grass: fire set piece, hub round |\"},{\"line_number\":514,\"content\":\"2. Destroy three fuel tanks by any means. Fire is the obvious way.\"},{\"line_number\":656,\"content\":\"- **Vehicles:** technical, jeep, truck, river boat, plus wreck variants. Wheels drawn from `VehicleView`.\"},{\"line_number\":657,\"content\":\"- **Buildings and military:** tin shack, mud-brick hut with thatch, concrete bunker, watchtower, sandbag walls, oil tanks, fuel drums, jerrycans, ammo crates, radio mast, roadside sign, hotel ruin pieces, cement silos and conveyors, church, pump machinery, cable ferry, market goods, bar interior, garage, shop shelving, tires, burnt car.\"},{\"line_number\":700,\"content\":\"| B1 | **Dry Season** (Tshala) | Burn the Hand's depot at Ombe Flats. Read the wind, approach upwind, light it, and get out as it turns. Passes GP2 and GP4 by road | Vehicle, technical, guard posts, monocular, fire, wind, diamonds | 12 min |\"},{\"line_number\":816,\"content\":\"- **Fire:** wind 8 m/s downwind reach ≥ 3× upwind after 60 s. Calm spread is roughly round. Roads and river stop it unless embers jump. Burnt cells don't re-burn, then regrow. Rain extinguishes. Barrel explodes and ignites. NPCs leave burning cells. A burning NPC spreads fire. Fuel tank cooks off. Snapshot size stays small after a big burn.\"},{\"line_number\":859,\"content\":\"**Coverage flags (each set by real play; a test passes on the union across the three playthrough runs, since no single run can both save and lose the same companion or reach every ending):** map raised, waypoint set, GPS followed, monocular tag, wind rag visible at speed > 6, jam cleared, enemy jam seen, weapon broke, weapon bought, locker used, syrette, each wound treatment type, fever warned, pill taken, black-out (bot route), player rescued, companion patched, companion overdosed, companion died, better-way taken, fire lit by each igniter class, 500+ cells burned in one fire, enemy panicked, animals fled, explosion chain, rain extinguished, stealth kill, dart kill, night contract, sleep used, safe house claimed, post cleared, post re-manned, technical driven, mounted gun fired, repair done, boat driven, bus taken, tape played, cache found by tracker, diamonds spent, each contract, ceasefire ended, town burned, each ending.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b48aaced-aa99-45c7-b