{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_725","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" in under a second means it completes within one or two ticks.\n\nA real shot could chain everything in a single tick if the player is already aimed from the previous step.\n\nThe log shows both transitions at the exact same timestamp. This suggests either two consecutive ticks within the same second, or the tanks step being marked done immediately inside begin.\n\nThe same-tick completion might occur if `done(tanks)` is true immediately inside `begin`. That would require both `cells_500` and `explosion_chain` flags to already be set. The `explosion_chain` flag is only assigned by `chain_tanks`, so it would be unexpected. However, prior ignite steps may have already burned enough cells to trigger `cells_500`.The playthrough log shows the player moved\n\nThe `begin(Tanks)` two meters from (-220,-34) function only arms the pistol and spawns to (-220,-36) before the farm. It does not set any completion  patching.flags, so `done(Tanks)` cannot be true immediately. The same-second transitions are therefore a real shot firing within a single second.\n\nThe same pattern appears in the rain-to-better transition at t=512.\n\nThe two-meter move and patch both occur at t=512. The companion sits four meters ahead, so the bot walks until the distance drops below 2.2 meters. This timing matches the prior gap requirement.\n\nThe player moved two meters during the rain-to-better step. The companion spawns four meters ahead, and the bot walks toward it. A two-meter position change in one second suggests the bot closed roughly 1.8 meters of distance, which fits within the 2.2 meter interaction threshold.\n\nThe flag is set in try_interact after walking, so the fix appears to work. The better step likely completes within the same tick as arrival because begin() does\n\nThe same-tick completion not mark it and the bot walks and interacts might o