v/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/TASK.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\"},{\"line_number\":83,\"content\":\"Design the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"Touch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"  - `keyboard.press('Escape')` does not release the lock headless, so tests call `document.exitPointerLock()`.\"},{\"line_number\":93,\"content\":\"  - Known real-browser behaviour, which I couldn't test headless: Esc releases the lock and the page may get no keydown for it, so treat `pointerlockchange` to unlocked as \\\"open the pause menu\\\". Chrome also refuses to re-lock for about a second after an Esc exit, and needs a user gesture, so show \\\"Click to resume\\\" and retry.\"},{\"line_number\":95,\"content\":\"  - `BroadcastChannel` and `storage` events work between `file://` pages in one browser context.\"},{\"line_number\":187,\"content\":\"## 4. Controls (DECIDED)\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"Controller first (DualSense, standard mapping). The keyboard and mouse use what PC FPS players expect. Prompts follow the last device used, and a Settings option swaps PlayStation glyphs for Xbox's A B X Y.\"},{\"line_number\":423,\"content\":\"- It must work from `file://`.\"},{\"line_number\":549,\"content\":\"- **This computer:** `BroadcastChannel` auto-lobby between windows or tabs (works from `file://`). This is what your tests use.\"},{\"line_number\":550,\"content\":\"- **Invite code:** WebRTC star with host-created offer, joiner answer, copy and paste codes (keyboard required for this one step; say so on screen). Use one reliable and one unordered channel per peer. STUN allowed here, never in a session.\"},{\"line_number\":576,\"content\":\"- Key caps and mouse-button icons for keyboard and mouse\"},{\"line_number\":585,\"content\":\"**Pause:** Resume, Settings, Controls, **Dev mode**, Quit to title (the confirm card says how long ago the last autosave was).\"},{\"line_number\":589,\"content\":\"- Controls: Prompts PlayStation/Xbox, Invert Y, Stick and mouse sensitivity, Aim assist, Toggle or hold for crouch and sprint\"},{\"line_number\":594,\"content\":\"- Controls: one big diagram per device (on foot, vehicle)\"},{\"line_number\":604,\"content\":\"Touch-only means `(any-pointer: fine)` false, `(pointer: coarse)` true and no controller connected. No touch controls at all (never show the engine's touch UI in this scene). Show **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a **Settings** button (tappable) over the running attract mode. Plugging in a controller or pressing a key brings the normal title.\"},{\"line_number\":834,\"content\":\"- Page opens from `file://`, title draws (screenshot past blank), no page errors. Enter, Space, Enter, Space leaves it drawing (this is what the hub's own solo check does).\"},{\"line_number\":835,\"content\":\"- **Controls:** keyboard, mouse hover and click, pad stub (§2.4). Prompts follow the device. Xbox setting changes glyphs. Synthetic mouse changes yaw under pointer lock. Lock lost opens pause.\"},{\"line_number\":837,\"content\":\"- **Touch-only:** Chromium with a phone profile (`has_touch`, `is_mobile`) shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a tappable Settings. No touch controls appear. Attract runs. Also check that WebKit (which has no WebGPU here) shows the page's clear message rather than a blank page.\"},{\"line_number\":839,\"content\":\"- **Saves:** save, reload, Continue, from `file://`.\"},{\"line_number\":875,\"content\":\"- [ ] One self-contained HTML file with the name and location TASK.md gives. Opens from `file://` in Chrome or Edge with WebGPU.\"},{\"line_number\":882,\"content\":\"- [ ] Controller first: every screen works on a DualSense (stubbed) with PlayStation glyphs, Xbox glyph option, keyboard and mouse native with their own prompts, hover moves focus, clicks work, no dense screens.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/hub/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":157,\"content\":\"And it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\"},{\"line_number\":348,\"content\":\"cases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"scripts/build-web.sh --single-file   # -> target/web/shardfall.html, runs from file://\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/CLAUDE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"  with the gzipped wasm inside; it runs from `file://` in Chrome or Edge.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/pavilion-lite/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"- a window for people to play the result (keyboard and mouse);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":168,\"content\":\"  --out out/mygame.html`: about 10 MB, runs from `file://` in Chrome or Edge (WebGPU).\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/pavilion-lite/AGENTS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"cargo run --release -- play arena            # a window, for people (keyboard + mouse)\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/docs/DESIGN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":114,\"content\":\"- **Devices:** keyboard+mouse and gamepad are always supported.\"},{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"   - keyboard+mouse and gamepad input, with the system layer;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/AGENTS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"tool family with examples, the controls and what each test suite covers: open the section you\"},{\"line_number\":142,\"content\":\"scripts/build-web.sh --single-file # -> target/web/shardfall.html: one ~10 MB page, runs from file://\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/docs/REFERENCE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"The detail behind `AGENTS.md`, read on demand: open the section you need, not the whole page.\"},{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"- [Controls](#controls): keyboard, gamepad, touch and the fixed system keys.\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"  pav_app     the game (`shardfall` binary): window, boot diagnostics, input (keyboard/mouse,\"},{\"line_number\":280,\"content\":\"## Controls\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"The scripts build `shardfall` and `pav`, then open the object workspace and the live bridge.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/engine/docs/HISTORY.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":395,\"content\":\"  batteries open the exit; three hits lose) in about an hour and 74 tool calls: 447 lines of\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6a512066-4462-48f8-94f2-fb1c9340763c-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# One test command. Prints failing lines only, then PASS n FAIL f.\\nset -u\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nLOGS=\\\"$DEV/test-logs\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$LOGS\\\"\\nmode=\\\"${1:-all}\\\"\\npass=0\\n10→fail=0\\n\\nshow_fail() {\\n  grep -E 'FAILED|^error(\\\\[|:)|panicked at|^FAIL:' \\\"$1\\\" || true\\n}\\n\\ntake_py() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  local c f\\n20→  c=\\\"$(grep -E '^CHECKS ' \\\"$log\\\" | tail -1 | awk '{print $2}')\\\"\\n  f=\\\"$(grep -c '^FAIL:' \\\"$log\\\" || true)\\\"\\n  [[ -n \\\"$c\\\" ]] || c=0\\n  pass=$((pass + c - f))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n  if [[ \\\"$c\\\" == 0 && \\\"$f\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $log produced no checks\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n  fi\\n}\\n30→\\ntake_cargo() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  if ! grep -q '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\"; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect did not finish\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    return\\n  fi\\n  # Sum every cargo result. Doc-tests often add a 0-passed line after the real suite.\\n40→  local p=0 f=0 line np nf\\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\\n    np=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) passed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    nf=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) failed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    p=$((p + ${np:-0}))\\n    f=$((f + ${nf:-0}))\\n  done < <(grep '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\")\\n  if [[ \\\"$p\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect ran 0 tests\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n50→  fi\\n  pass=$((pass + p))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n}\\n\\ncargo_tests() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  shift 2\\n  (\\n    cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n60→    CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$ENGINE/target\\\" \\\\\\n      cargo test --offline --color never \\\"$@\\\"\\n  ) >\\\"$log\\\" 2>&1 || true\\n  take_cargo \\\"$log\\\" \\\"$expect\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_sim() {\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-combat.log\\\" \\\"sim-combat\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    look_and_stick_follow_yaw hits_use_zones_and_walls_block \\\\\\n    jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear \\\\\\n70→    a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops fever_pills_blackout_and_healing\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-world.log\\\" \\\"sim-world\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks exposure_smoke_and_noise \\\\\\n    squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking \\\\\\n    vehicles_climb_break_and_float\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/playthrough.log\\\" \\\"playthrough\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    bot_plays_all_three_endings\\n}\\n\\nrun_ui() {\\n80→  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/ui-shell.log\\\" \\\"ui-shell\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\",\"content_concise\":\"1→#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# One test command. Prints failing lines only, then PASS n FAIL f.\\nset -u\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nLOGS=\\\"$DEV/test-logs\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$LOGS\\\"\\nmode=\\\"${1:-all}\\\"\\npass=0\\n10→fail=0\\n\\nshow_fail() {\\n  grep -E 'FAILED|^error(\\\\[|:)|panicked at|^FAIL:' \\\"$1\\\" || true\\n}\\n\\ntake_py() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  local c f\\n20→  c=\\\"$(grep -E '^CHECKS ' \\\"$log\\\" | tail -1 | awk '{print $2}')\\\"\\n  f=\\\"$(grep -c '^FAIL:' \\\"$log\\\" || true)\\\"\\n  [[ -n \\\"$c\\\" ]] || c=0\\n  pass=$((pass + c - f))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n  if [[ \\\"$c\\\" == 0 && \\\"$f\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $log produced no checks\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n  fi\\n}\\n30→\\ntake_cargo() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  if ! grep -q '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\"; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect did not finish\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    return\\n  fi\\n  # Sum every cargo result. Doc-tests often add a 0-passed line after the real suite.\\n40→  local p=0 f=0 line np nf\\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\\n    np=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) passed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    nf=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) failed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    p=$((p + ${np:-0}))\\n    f=$((f + ${nf:-0}))\\n  done < <(grep '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\")\\n  if [[ \\\"$p\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect ran 0 tests\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n50→  fi\\n  pass=$((pass + p))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n}\\n\\ncargo_tests() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  shift 2\\n  (\\n    cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n60→    CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$ENGINE/target\\\" \\\\\\n      cargo test --offline --color never \\\"$@\\\"\\n  ) >\\\"$log\\\" 2>&1 || true\\n  take_cargo \\\"$log\\\" \\\"$expect\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_sim() {\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-combat.log\\\" \\\"sim-combat\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    look_and_stick_follow_yaw hits_use_zones_and_walls_block \\\\\\n    jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear \\\\\\n70→    a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops fever_pills_blackout_and_healing\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-world.log\\\" \\\"sim-world\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks exposure_smoke_and_noise \\\\\\n    squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking \\\\\\n    vehicles_climb_break_and_float\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/playthrough.log\\\" \\\"playthrough\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    bot_plays_all_three_endings\\n}\\n\\nrun_ui() {\\n80→  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/ui-shell.log\\\" \\\"ui-shell\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/Jam Cry-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013503/tests/run.sh\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# One test command. Prints failing lines only, then PASS n FAIL f.\\nset -u\\nDEV=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nENGINE=\\\"$DEV/engine\\\"\\nLOGS=\\\"$DEV/test-logs\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$LOGS\\\"\\nmode=\\\"${1:-all}\\\"\\npass=0\\nfail=0\\n\\nshow_fail() {\\n  grep -E 'FAILED|^error(\\\\[|:)|panicked at|^FAIL:' \\\"$1\\\" || true\\n}\\n\\ntake_py() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  local c f\\n  c=\\\"$(grep -E '^CHECKS ' \\\"$log\\\" | tail -1 | awk '{print $2}')\\\"\\n  f=\\\"$(grep -c '^FAIL:' \\\"$log\\\" || true)\\\"\\n  [[ -n \\\"$c\\\" ]] || c=0\\n  pass=$((pass + c - f))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n  if [[ \\\"$c\\\" == 0 && \\\"$f\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $log produced no checks\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n  fi\\n}\\n\\ntake_cargo() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  show_fail \\\"$log\\\"\\n  if ! grep -q '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\"; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect did not finish\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n    return\\n  fi\\n  # Sum every cargo result. Doc-tests often add a 0-passed line after the real suite.\\n  local p=0 f=0 line np nf\\n  while IFS= read -r line; do\\n    np=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) passed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    nf=\\\"$(sed -n 's/.* \\\\([0-9][0-9]*\\\\) failed.*/\\\\1/p' <<<\\\"$line\\\")\\\"\\n    p=$((p + ${np:-0}))\\n    f=$((f + ${nf:-0}))\\n  done < <(grep '^test result:' \\\"$log\\\")\\n  if [[ \\\"$p\\\" == 0 ]]; then\\n    echo \\\"FAIL: $expect ran 0 tests\\\"\\n    fail=$((fail + 1))\\n  fi\\n  pass=$((pass + p))\\n  fail=$((fail + f))\\n}\\n\\ncargo_tests() {\\n  local log=\\\"$1\\\" expect=\\\"$2\\\"\\n  shift 2\\n  (\\n    cd \\\"$ENGINE\\\"\\n    CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=\\\"$ENGINE/target\\\" \\\\\\n      cargo test --offline --color never \\\"$@\\\"\\n  ) >\\\"$log\\\" 2>&1 || true\\n  take_cargo \\\"$log\\\" \\\"$expect\\\"\\n}\\n\\nrun_sim() {\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-combat.log\\\" \\\"sim-combat\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    look_and_stick_follow_yaw hits_use_zones_and_walls_block \\\\\\n    jams_match_the_curve_and_a_slap_shortens_the_clear \\\\\\n    a_worn_gun_breaks_and_a_jammed_soldier_stops fever_pills_blackout_and_healing\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/sim-world.log\\\" \\\"sim-world\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    fire_runs_downwind_and_respects_breaks exposure_smoke_and_noise \\\\\\n    squad_caps_shooters_and_breaks post_remans_only_when_nobody_is_looking \\\\\\n    vehicles_climb_break_and_float\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/playthrough.log\\\" \\\"playthrough\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n    bot_plays_all_three_endings\\n}\\n\\nrun_ui() {\\n  cargo_tests \\\"$LOGS/ui-shell.log\\\" \\\"ui-shell\\\" -p pav_core --test merc -- --test-threads=8 \\\\\\n\",\"total_lines\":138}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"4644339b-115f-4ae8-bb9c-907d68d9a6b1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_746","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The deliverable is Jam Cry, a single self-contained HTML first-person survival/contract shooter inspired by Far Cry 2.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f1aeb967-fc5d-415a-ba95-1af71c008b73-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md","offset":187,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f1aeb967-fc5d-415a-ba95-1af71c008b73-7","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"New Game|Continue|WASD|Enter","glob":"*.html","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6427,"output_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":16384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aad8-e6b0-7c02-9fba-a7e5c5a4c558","uuid":"4294668e-d4b4-41da-bd06-8a83500c1ce3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f1aeb967-fc5d-415a-ba95-1af71c008b73-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"187→## 4. Controls (DECIDED)\\n\\nController first (DualSense, standard mapping). The keyboard and mouse use what PC FPS players expect. Prompts follow the last device used, and a Settings option swaps PlayStation glyphs for Xbox's A B X Y.\\n190→\\nStandard mapping indices: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad up/down/left/right. gilrs names: South, East, West, North, LeftTrigger, RightTrigger, LeftTrigger2, RightTrigger2, Select, Start, LeftThumb, RightThumb, DPad*.\\n\\n| On foot | DualSense | Xbox prompt | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | LS / RS | W A S D / mouse (pointer lock) |\\n| Fire / aim down sights | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\\n| Jump, vault | ✕ | A | Space |\\n| Crouch (tap), prone (hold) | ○ | B | C or Ctrl (hold), Z prone |\\n| Reload, clear jam | □ | X | R |\\n200→| Interact (when a prompt shows; takes priority over reload) | □ | X | E, or LMB when no weapon is raised |\\n| Next weapon | △ | Y | Q, wheel, or 1 2 3 |\\n| Throw | L1 | LB | G |\\n| Machete | R1 | RB | V |\\n| Sprint | L3 | LS click | Shift |\\n| Monocular | R3 | RS click | B |\\n| Map and GPS up/down | D-pad ← | D-pad ← | M |\\n| Syrette / treat wound | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | H |\\n| Fever pills | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | P |\\n| Diamond tracker | D-pad → | D-pad → | T |\\n210→| Current contract card | Create | View | Tab |\\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\\n\\n| In a vehicle | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Steer / look | L stick / R stick | A D / mouse |\\n| Throttle / brake and reverse (analog) | R2 / L2 | W / S |\\n| Handbrake / horn | ✕ / L1 | Space / L |\\n| Get out | □ | E |\\n| Change seat (driver, mounted gun) | △ | F |\\n220→| Camera (first person, chase) | R3 | V |\\n| Mounted gun: fire / zoom | R2 / L2 | LMB / RMB |\\n| Map | D-pad ← | M |\\n\\n| Map up | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move the pencil (hover focuses a place) | R stick | mouse |\\n| Set waypoint | ✕ | LMB |\\n| Zoom | L1 / R1 | wheel |\\n| Lower map (you can keep walking or driving with it up) | ○ or D-pad ← | RMB, Esc or M |\\n230→\\n| Menus | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move focus | D-pad or L stick | Arrows or W S A D, or hover with the mouse |\\n| Confirm / back | ✕ / ○ | Enter, Space or click / Esc or RMB |\\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 | Q / E or click |\\n| Adjust slider | D-pad ← → (hold accelerates) | ← → or drag |\\n\\n**Feel settings (defaults):** stick look 140°/s at full deflection with a response curve, mouse 0.12°/count, aim assist on for controller only (slowdown near targets plus light magnetism while L2 is held), invert Y off. Rendered look uses the latest input every frame, not only tick results (§12.2).\\n\\n240→---\\n\\n## 5. Systems\\n\\nAll numbers are `Tunable` (so they appear in `pav params`, `pav set` and dev mode) or live in `engine/game/merc/*.toml`.\\n\\n### 5.1 Movement\\nUse the engine's character controller, momentum model. Walk 3.0 m/s (aiming), run 4.6, sprint 7.0 for 12 s of stamina, crouch ×0.55, prone ×0.28, jump 1.0 m, vault onto ledges (existing mantle), swim with `water_depth` (no weapon use while swimming). Eye heights: 1.58 m standing, 1.02 crouched, 0.42 prone, smoothed. Head bob has a Settings slider. Hard landings: over 6 m/s hurts, over 12 m/s can break a finger (triggers a wound treatment).\\n\\n### 5.2 Shooting\\n250→Hitscan rays from the camera with weapon spread and bullet drop past 150 m, against rapier geometry and character capsules. You write this: don't use `Projectiles` for bullets. Zones: head ×3, torso ×1, limbs ×0.6. Visible tracers on every third round, muzzle flash light, dust puffs by surface, ricochet sparks on metal, dark flecks on people. Vehicles, barrels, crates and thatch take damage as objects. Recoil is a spring on the view (pitch and yaw kick) plus the weapon root. ADS tightens spread, zooms FOV (75° to 55°), and lines up the iron sights. There is a minimal centre dot and a hit tick, with a Settings toggle.\\n\\n### 5.3 Weapons (DECIDED: three slots, plus throwables and machete)\\nThe player carries one sidearm, one primary and one special. Defined in `engine/game/merc/weapons.toml`. Starting values:\\n\\n| id | slot | name | mag / reserve | rpm | damage | range m | wear per shot % | noise m | notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| pistol | side | Service Nine | 12/60 | 300 semi | 22 | 40 | 0.10 | 120 | |\\n| revolver | side | Old Six | 6/30 | 120 | 48 | 50 | 0.05 | 140 | barely wears, slow reload |\\n| flare | side | Flare pistol | 1/8 | 40 | 10 | 60 | 0.5 | 60 | **ignites** |\\n260→| sawnoff | side | Sawn-off | 2/24 | 120 | 12 × 8 | 12 | 0.3 | 150 | |\\n| ar | primary | Forty-Seven | 30/180 | 600 | 26 | 120 | 0.14 | 160 | the country's rifle, every corpse drops one |\\n| battle | primary | Battle rifle | 20/100 | 450 | 38 | 180 | 0.12 | 180 | |\\n| smg | primary | Folding SMG | 30/180 | 800 | 16 | 50 | 0.16 | 110 | |\\n| shotgun | primary | Pump gun | 6/36 | 70 | 10 × 9 | 18 | 0.25 | 150 | |\\n| sniper | primary | Bolt rifle | 5/40 | 40 | 110 | 400 | 0.35 | 300 | scope, overlay vignette |\\n| dart | primary | Dart rifle | 1/12 | 40 | poison, kills in 3 s | 80 | 0.2 | 8 | **silent** |\",\"content_concise\":\"187→## 4. Controls (DECIDED)\\n\\nController first (DualSense, standard mapping). The keyboard and mouse use what PC FPS players expect. Prompts follow the last device used, and a Settings option swaps PlayStation glyphs for Xbox's A B X Y.\\n190→\\nStandard mapping indices: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad up/down/left/right. gilrs names: South, East, West, North, LeftTrigger, RightTrigger, LeftTrigger2, RightTrigger2, Select, Start, LeftThumb, RightThumb, DPad*.\\n\\n| On foot | DualSense | Xbox prompt | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | LS / RS | W A S D / mouse (pointer lock) |\\n| Fire / aim down sights | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\\n| Jump, vault | ✕ | A | Space |\\n| Crouch (tap), prone (hold) | ○ | B | C or Ctrl (hold), Z prone |\\n| Reload, clear jam | □ | X | R |\\n200→| Interact (when a prompt shows; takes priority over reload) | □ | X | E, or LMB when no weapon is raised |\\n| Next weapon | △ | Y | Q, wheel, or 1 2 3 |\\n| Throw | L1 | LB | G |\\n| Machete | R1 | RB | V |\\n| Sprint | L3 | LS click | Shift |\\n| Monocular | R3 | RS click | B |\\n| Map and GPS up/down | D-pad ← | D-pad ← | M |\\n| Syrette / treat wound | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | H |\\n| Fever pills | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | P |\\n| Diamond tracker | D-pad → | D-pad → | T |\\n210→| Current contract card | Create | View | Tab |\\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\\n\\n| In a vehicle | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Steer / look | L stick / R stick | A D / mouse |\\n| Throttle / brake and reverse (analog) | R2 / L2 | W / S |\\n| Handbrake / horn | ✕ / L1 | Space / L |\\n| Get out | □ | E |\\n| Change seat (driver, mounted gun) | △ | F |\\n220→| Camera (first person, chase) | R3 | V |\\n| Mounted gun: fire / zoom | R2 / L2 | LMB / RMB |\\n| Map | D-pad ← | M |\\n\\n| Map up | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move the pencil (hover focuses a place) | R stick | mouse |\\n| Set waypoint | ✕ | LMB |\\n| Zoom | L1 / R1 | wheel |\\n| Lower map (you can keep walking or driving with it up) | ○ or D-pad ← | RMB, Esc or M |\\n230→\\n| Menus | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move focus | D-pad or L stick | Arrows or W S A D, or hover with the mouse |\\n| Confirm / back | ✕ / ○ | Enter, Space or click / Esc or RMB |\\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 | Q / E or click |\\n| Adjust slider | D-pad ← → (hold accelerates) | ← → or drag |\\n\\n**Feel settings (defaults):** stick look 140°/s at full deflection with a response curve, mouse 0.12°/count, aim assist on for controller only (slowdown near targets plus light magnetism while L2 is held), invert Y off. Rendered look uses the latest input every frame, not only tick results (§12.2).\\n\\n240→---\\n\\n## 5. Systems\\n\\nAll numbers are `Tunable` (so they appear in `pav params`, `pav set` and dev mode) or live in `engine/game/merc/*.toml`.\\n\\n### 5.1 Movement\\nUse the engine's character controller, momentum model. Walk 3.0 m/s (aiming), run 4.6, sprint 7.0 for 12 s of stamina, crouch ×0.55, prone ×0.28, jump 1.0 m, vault onto ledges (existing mantle), swim with `water_depth` (no weapon use while swimming). Eye heights: 1.58 m standing, 1.02 crouched, 0.42 prone, smoothed. Head bob has a Settings slider. Hard landings: over 6 m/s hurts, over 12 m/s can break a finger (triggers a wound treatment).\\n\\n### 5.2 Shooting\\n250→Hitscan rays from the camera with weapon spread and bullet drop past 150 m, against rapier geometry and character capsules. You write this: don't use `Projectiles` for bullets. Zones: head ×3, torso ×1, limbs ×0.6. Visible tracers on every third round, muzzle flash light, dust puffs by surface, ricochet sparks on metal, dark flecks on people. Vehicles, barrels, crates and thatch take damage as objects. Recoil is a spring on the view (pitch and yaw kick) plus the weapon root. ADS tightens spread, zooms FOV (75° to 55°), and lines up the iron sights. There is a minimal centre dot and a hit tick, with a Settings toggle.\\n\\n### 5.3 Weapons (DECIDED: three slots, plus throwables and machete)\\nThe player carries one sidearm, one primary and one special. Defined in `engine/game/merc/weapons.toml`. Starting values:\\n\\n| id | slot | name | mag / reserve | rpm | damage | range m | wear per shot % | noise m | notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| pistol | side | Service Nine | 12/60 | 300 semi | 22 | 40 | 0.10 | 120 | |\\n| revolver | side | Old Six | 6/30 | 120 | 48 | 50 | 0.05 | 140 | barely wears, slow reload |\\n| flare | side | Flare pistol | 1/8 | 40 | 10 | 60 | 0.5 | 60 | **ignites** |\\n260→| sawnoff | side | Sawn-off | 2/24 | 120 | 12 × 8 | 12 | 0.3 | 150 | |\\n| ar | primary | Forty-Seven | 30/180 | 600 | 26 | 120 | 0.14 | 160 | the country's rifle, every corpse drops one |\\n| battle | primary | Battle rifle | 20/100 | 450 | 38 | 180 | 0.12 | 180 | |\\n| smg | primary | Folding SMG | 30/180 | 800 | 16 | 50 | 0.16 | 110 | |\\n| shotgun | primary | Pump gun | 6/36 | 70 | 10 × 9 | 18 | 0.25 | 150 | |\\n| sniper | primary | Bolt rifle | 5/40 | 40 | 110 | 400 | 0.35 | 300 | scope, overlay vignette |\\n| dart | primary | Dart rifle | 1/12 | 40 | poison, kills in 3 s | 80 | 0.2 | 8 | **silent** |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013503__xbd7d91/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":187,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"## 4. Controls (DECIDED)\\n\\nController first (DualSense, standard mapping). The keyboard and mouse use what PC FPS players expect. Prompts follow the last device used, and a Settings option swaps PlayStation glyphs for Xbox's A B X Y.\\n\\nStandard mapping indices: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 10 L3, 11 R3, 12–15 D-pad up/down/left/right. gilrs names: South, East, West, North, LeftTrigger, RightTrigger, LeftTrigger2, RightTrigger2, Select, Start, LeftThumb, RightThumb, DPad*.\\n\\n| On foot | DualSense | Xbox prompt | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | LS / RS | W A S D / mouse (pointer lock) |\\n| Fire / aim down sights | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\\n| Jump, vault | ✕ | A | Space |\\n| Crouch (tap), prone (hold) | ○ | B | C or Ctrl (hold), Z prone |\\n| Reload, clear jam | □ | X | R |\\n| Interact (when a prompt shows; takes priority over reload) | □ | X | E, or LMB when no weapon is raised |\\n| Next weapon | △ | Y | Q, wheel, or 1 2 3 |\\n| Throw | L1 | LB | G |\\n| Machete | R1 | RB | V |\\n| Sprint | L3 | LS click | Shift |\\n| Monocular | R3 | RS click | B |\\n| Map and GPS up/down | D-pad ← | D-pad ← | M |\\n| Syrette / treat wound | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | H |\\n| Fever pills | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | P |\\n| Diamond tracker | D-pad → | D-pad → | T |\\n| Current contract card | Create | View | Tab |\\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\\n\\n| In a vehicle | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Steer / look | L stick / R stick | A D / mouse |\\n| Throttle / brake and reverse (analog) | R2 / L2 | W / S |\\n| Handbrake / horn | ✕ / L1 | Space / L |\\n| Get out | □ | E |\\n| Change seat (driver, mounted gun) | △ | F |\\n| Camera (first person, chase) | R3 | V |\\n| Mounted gun: fire / zoom | R2 / L2 | LMB / RMB |\\n| Map | D-pad ← | M |\\n\\n| Map up | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move the pencil (hover focuses a place) | R stick | mouse |\\n| Set waypoint | ✕ | LMB |\\n| Zoom | L1 / R1 | wheel |\\n| Lower map (you can keep walking or driving with it up) | ○ or D-pad ← | RMB, Esc or M |\\n\\n| Menus | DualSense | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Move focus | D-pad or L stick | Arrows or W S A D, or hover with the mouse |\\n| Confirm / back | ✕ / ○ | Enter, Space or click / Esc or RMB |\\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 | Q / E or click |\\n| Adjust slider | D-pad ← → (hold accelerates) | ← → or drag |\\n\\n**Feel settings (defaults):** stick look 140°/s at full deflection with a response curve, mouse 0.12°/count, aim assist on for controller only (slowdown near targets plus light magnetism while L2 is held), invert Y off. Rendered look uses the latest input every frame, not only tick results (§12.2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Systems\\n\\nAll numbers are `Tunable` (so they appear in `pav params`, `pav set` and dev mode) or live in `engine/game/merc/*.toml`.\\n\\n### 5.1 Movement\\nUse the engine's character controller, momentum model. Walk 3.0 m/s (aiming), run 4.6, sprint 7.0 for 12 s of stamina, crouch ×0.55, prone ×0.28, jump 1.0 m, vault onto ledges (existing mantle), swim with `water_depth` (no weapon use while swimming). Eye heights: 1.58 m standing, 1.02 crouched, 0.42 prone, smoothed. Head bob has a Settings slider. Hard landings: over 6 m/s hurts, over 12 m/s can break a finger (triggers a wound treatment).\\n\\n### 5.2 Shooting\\nHitscan rays from the camera with weapon spread and bullet drop past 150 m, against rapier geometry and character capsules. You write this: don't use `Projectiles` for bullets. Zones: head ×3, torso ×1, limbs ×0.6. Visible tracers on every third round, muzzle flash light, dust puffs by surface, ricochet sparks on metal, dark flecks on people. Vehicles, barrels, crates and thatch take damage as objects. Recoil is a spring on the view (pitch and yaw kick) plus the weapon root. ADS tightens spread, zooms FOV (75° to 55°), and lines up the iron sights. There is a minimal centre dot and a hit tick, with a Settings toggle.\\n\\n### 5.3 Weapons (DECIDED: three slots, plus throwables and machete)\\nThe player carries one sidearm, one primary and one special. Defined in `engine/game/merc/weapons.toml`. Starting values:\\n\\n| id | slot | name | mag / reserve | rpm | damage | range m | wear per shot % | noise m | notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| pistol | side | Service Nine | 12/60 | 300 semi | 22 | 40 | 0.10 | 120 | |\\n| revolver | side | Old Six | 6/30 | 120 | 48 | 50 | 0.05 | 140 | barely wears, slow reload |\\n| flare | side | Flare pistol | 1/8 | 40 | 10 | 60 | 0.5 | 60 | **ignites** |\\n| sawnoff | side | Sawn-off | 2/24 | 120 | 12 × 8 | 12 | 0.3 | 150 | |\\n| ar | primary | Forty-Seven | 30/180 | 600 | 26 | 120 | 0.14 | 160 | the country's rifle, every corpse drops one |\\n| battle | primary | Battle rifle | 20/100 | 450 | 38 | 180 | 0.12 | 180 | |\\n| smg | primary | Folding SMG | 30/180 | 800 | 16 | 50 | 0.16 | 110 | |\\n| shotgun | primary | Pump gun | 6/36 | 70 | 10 × 9 | 18 | 0.25 | 150 | |